'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embezzlement', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T02:01:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Halbfinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b657c1b-67d8-56b9-a08f-e89886083230', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b657c1b-67d8-56b9-a08f-e89886083230'}, {'abstract': 'If a catastrophic cyberattack occurs in the United States, Americans will be justified in asking why their lawmakers failed to protect them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/opinion/cybersecurity-at-risk.html', 'snippet': 'If a catastrophic cyberattack occurs in the United States, Americans will be justified in asking why their lawmakers failed to protect them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Relentless assaults on America’s computer networks by China and other foreign governments, hackers and criminals have created an urgent need for safeguards to protect these vital systems. The question now is whether the Senate will provide them. Senator John McCain, a Republican of Arizona, and the Chamber of Commerce have already exacted compromises from sponsors of a reasonably strong bill, and are asking for more. Their demands should be resisted and the original bill approved by the Senate. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cybersecurity at Risk', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cybersecurity at Risk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare'