 Palestinian leader Yasir Arafat, petitioned the French authorities on Tuesday to investigate his death in 2004 as a homicide.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Suha Arafat, the widow of the former Palestinian leader Yasir Arafat, petitioned the French authorities on Tuesday to investigate his death in 2004 as a homicide, a judicial official said, after a Swiss laboratory found that he may have been poisoned with polonium 210, a rare radioactive isotope. Mrs. Arafat filed suit without specifying a suspect, the court’s chief investigating magistrate said. The court will determine if the allegations warrant an investigation. The Palestinian Authority has agreed to exhume the body for analysis. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Arafat’s Widow Seeks Homicide Inquiry Into His Death', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Arafat’s Widow Seeks Homicide Inquiry Into His Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poisoning and Poisons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARAFAT, YASIR', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arafat, Suha', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T05:03:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief