The offense is potent, but the defense is schematically simple, which makes it dependent on outstanding individual performances.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/detroit-lions-2012-n-f-l-season-preview/', 'snippet': 'The offense is potent, but the defense is schematically simple, which makes it dependent on outstanding individual performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chrysler isn’t the only company on the rebound in Detroit. For the first time in 12 years, the Lions – the hapless Lions – enter a season looking to build on last year’s playoff experience. O.K., so maybe the Lions still have just one playoff win since 1957. But the hope – nay, expectation – is that that will change in 2012.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Detroit Lions, 2012 N.F.L. Season Preview', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Lions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T10:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9021dba3-36bb-5965-8871-945c8654ca18', 'word_count': 2965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9021dba3-36bb-5965-8871-945c8654ca18'}, {'abstract': 'The unemployment insurance and food-stamp programs have become increasingly alike but for one important aspect, whether multiple household incomes are taken into account, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/food-stamps-married-people-need-not-apply/', 'snippet': 'The unemployment insurance and food-stamp programs have become increasingly alike but for one important aspect, whether multiple household incomes are taken into account, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Casey B. Mulligan is an economics professor at the University of Chicago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Food Stamps: Married People Need Not Apply', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T10:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Casey B. Mulligan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Casey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5134d954-e17e-5148-91c0-4a09ca63fc65', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5134d954-e17e-5148-91c0-4a09ca63fc65'}, {'abstract': 'The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration is investigating similar complaints that the Infiniti’s Intelligent Brake Assist system “inappropriately activated emergency braking.” The incidents were said to have happened at the same location, on a bridge that officials did not identify.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/two-similar-complaints-about-2013-infiniti-jx35-brakes/', 'snippet': 'The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration is investigating similar complaints that the Infiniti’s Intelligent Brake Assist system “inappropriately activated emergency braking.” The incidents were said to have happened at the same location...', 'lead_paragraph': 'After two owners of the new 2013 Infiniti JX35 complained that their automatic braking system suddenly engaged while they were driving on a bridge, then stopped the vehicles without apparent reason, the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration is investigating.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Similar Complaints About 2013 Infiniti JX35 Brakes', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Infiniti Division of Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T10:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41df23ad-7ad8-51c1-b09a-ce54a9a264ea', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41df23ad-7ad8-51c1-b09a-ce54a9a264ea'}, {'abstract': 'More colleges and universities are using YouTube to reach prospective students, allowing students opportunities to improve their college searches and strengthen their applications.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/between-cat-videos-research-colleges-on-youtube/', 'snippet': 'More colleges and universities are using YouTube to reach prospective students, allowing students opportunities to improve their college searches and strengthen their applications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a rite of passage every year — students from across the world power up their computers and begin to research the colleges of their dreams. With thousands of prospective students starting to think about preparing their applications, smart colleges are realizing that, while simple Web sites and information packets worked well enough in the past, the new generation needs new ways of access. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A YouTube Introduction to College, by Just Clicking Play', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Princeton University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tufts University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T10:01:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariha Setalvad and Tanya Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Setalvad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ae8f8b6-bf7e-5d04-ab3e-2491831fc63a', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ae8f8b6-bf7e-5d04-ab3e-2491831fc63a'}, {'abstract': "Mariel Zagunis will compete for her third-straight gold medal in fencing on Wednesday night and The Times's Mary Pilon joins Jason Stallman in London to talk about what is trending on Twitter."