-of-the-pack/', 'snippet': 'The way to keep teenagers from smoking is to make it uncool. Mandating plain packaging for cigarette brands, as Australia plans to do, will help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Remember teenage smoking? It’s been edged out by teenage obesity as the health concern of the moment. States are cutting programs to prevent the former while establishing programs to combat the latter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Teenage Smokers, Removing the Allure of the Pack', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T11:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44b45c6c-27ab-5fc8-a68a-073f3f1ca127', 'word_count': 1622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44b45c6c-27ab-5fc8-a68a-073f3f1ca127'}, {'abstract': 'I love touring factories: the layout, the materials, the machinery that’s there and the machinery that’s not there. This factory was, at first glance, very much like mine. But there were some real differences as well.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/middle-east-journal-assessing-a-factory-in-dubai/', 'snippet': 'I love touring factories: the layout, the materials, the machinery that’s there and the machinery that’s not there. This factory was, at first glance, very much like mine. But there were some real differences as well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I said in my previous post in this series, I love touring factories, particularly woodworking shops where I really know what I’m looking at. Everything is interesting: the layout, the materials, the machinery that’s there and the machinery that’s not there. The factory I got to tour in Dubai was, at first glance, very much like mine. But there were some real differences as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Middle East Journal: Can We Compete With a Factory in Dubai?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tables', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dubai (United Arab Emirates)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T11:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0959024a-0ccd-56c4-89cf-db5b47f2ce7f', 'word_count': 1689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0959024a-0ccd-56c4-89cf-db5b47f2ce7f'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Phelps and other Olympic swimmers are hearing from celebrities on Twitter.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/best-wishes-from-barack-and-justin/', 'snippet': 'Michael Phelps and other Olympic swimmers are hearing from celebrities on Twitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – It was fitting, given that the London Olympics have been designated the social media games, that President Obama avoided the old-school phone call and instead sent congratulations by Twitter to Michael Phelps on becoming the most decorated Olympian. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Best Wishes From Barack and Bieber', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bieber, Justin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franklin, Missy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lochte, Ryan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phelps, Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wade, Dwyane', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T11:22:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6611fe5-1be9-5960-9869-b1a7fd03d9f3', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6611fe5-1be9-5960-9869-b1a7fd03d9f3'}, {'abstract': 'The Master Lock 1500eDBX DialSpeed has a light-up electronic touch pad face instead of a spinning dial, unlocking with a combination of up, down, left and right clicks.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/a-padlock-people-might-want-to-steal/', 'snippet': 'The Master Lock 1500eDBX DialSpeed has a light-up electronic touch pad face instead of a spinning dial, unlocking with a combination of up, down, left and right clicks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You don’t often – or ever – see the words “combination lock” and “cool” in the same sentence, so prepare for a first: the Master Lock 1500eDBX DialSpeed is one cool combination lock.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Padlock People Might Want to Steal', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Locks and Keys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Master Lock Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T11:26:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/120edaef-3dc6-5881-a58b-1e94ff859fba', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/120edaef-3dc6-5881-a58b-1e94ff859fba'}, {'abstract': 'The company, America’s largest cable operator, also reduced its rate of loss of cable subscribers. But NBCUniversal remains a trouble spot.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/new-broadband-customers-help-drive-comcast-earnings/', 'snippet': 'The company, America’s largest cable operator, also reduced its rate of loss of cable subscribers. But NBCUniversal remains a trouble spot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Comcast added 156,000 high-speed Internet customers in the three months that ended June 30, helping to bolster its net income by 32 percent and underscoring the company’s continuing transition from cable giant to broadband provider.', 'sour