sia and other emerging markets.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/standard-chartered-profit-rises-11-in-first-half/', 'snippet': 'The British bank bucked the industry trend of weak earnings, reporting that its net income jumped 11 percent in the first half of the year on strength in Asia and other emerging markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Bucking the industry trend of weak earnings, the British bank Standard Chartered reported on Wednesday that its net income rose 11.3 percent in the first half of the year on strength in Asia and other emerging markets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Standard Chartered Profit Up 11% on Emerging-Markets Strength', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Standard Chartered Bank PLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T12:22:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61f5b414-6857-5ccf-8cb4-9c4db0e645b5', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61f5b414-6857-5ccf-8cb4-9c4db0e645b5'}, {'abstract': 'A YouTube introduction to college, a regulator rebuffs Obama on plans to reduce borrowers’ mortgage debt, complaints about the brakes in the 2013 Infiniti JX35 and other consumer-focused news in today’s Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/wednesday-reading-a-youtube-introduction-to-college/', 'snippet': 'A YouTube introduction to college, a regulator rebuffs Obama on plans to reduce borrowers’ mortgage debt, complaints about the brakes in the 2013 Infiniti JX35 and other consumer-focused news in today’s Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and on our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday Reading: A YouTube Introduction to College', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T12:41:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8d9a5c8-ad2b-5ff7-a9d1-23d9b98efb47', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8d9a5c8-ad2b-5ff7-a9d1-23d9b98efb47'}, {'abstract': 'Officials say they remain hopeful that Israel has no imminent plans to attack Iran and may be willing to let the United States take the lead in any future strike.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/world/middleeast/in-israel-panetta-warns-iran-on-nuclear-program.html', 'snippet': 'Officials say they remain hopeful that Israel has no imminent plans to attack Iran and may be willing to let the United States take the lead in any future strike.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ASHKELON, Israel — A series of public statements and private communications from the Israeli leadership in recent weeks set off renewed concerns in the Obama administration that Israel might be preparing a unilateral military strike on Iran, perhaps as early as this fall.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cr