e, Truman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitchens, Christopher', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mailer, Norman', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Solomon, Andrew', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vidal, Gore', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T13:26:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e544fe5-d293-58c7-91f3-869d7d2d1ce2', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e544fe5-d293-58c7-91f3-869d7d2d1ce2'}, {'abstract': 'Zlotys of luck.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/poles-apart-2/', 'snippet': 'Zlotys of luck.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So on the third leg of his foreign tour, Mr. Bean Mitt Romney lavished praise on the Polish economy. It wasn’t quite as big a blooper as his praise for Israel’s single-payer-plus-price controls health care system, but it wasn’t good.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poles Apart', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T13:26:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cf39330-15ae-54f8-9541-f4bce6ac704e', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cf39330-15ae-54f8-9541-f4bce6ac704e'}, {'abstract': 'On his new album “God Forgives, I Don’t,” Rick Ross delivers plenty of crowing, but it’s leavened by reflection and moments of drug-dealer shame.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/arts/music/rick-ross-tries-on-a-new-streetwise-role.html', 'snippet': 'On his new album “God Forgives, I Don’t,” Rick Ross delivers plenty of crowing, but it’s leavened by reflection and moments of drug-dealer shame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IMAGINE that Rick Ross had a heart. That beneath all the bluster, behind the imposing shades, underneath the girth and the tattoos — barriers all — there beat something urgent, a muscle carrying more weight than one man could reasonably bear.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/arts/05ROSS1_SPAN/05ROSS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/arts/05ROSS1_SPAN/05ROSS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/arts/05ROSS1_SPAN/05ROSS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/arts/05ROSS1_SPAN/05ROSS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/arts/05ROSS1_SPAN/05ROSS1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/arts/05ROSS1_SPAN/05ROSS1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank':