alth, at home and while traveling.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Page a Day', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Talmud', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T14:05:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e76e6bde-cd7f-5657-892d-b71bd667a477', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e76e6bde-cd7f-5657-892d-b71bd667a477'}, {'abstract': 'House Republican leaders say they would be willing to interrupt the August recess to address fiscal issues — but not for a deal that would raise taxes on those with high incomes.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/republicans-would-interrupt-recess-on-their-own-terms/', 'snippet': 'House Republican leaders say they would be willing to interrupt the August recess to address fiscal issues — but not for a deal that would raise taxes on those with high incomes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'House Republican leaders — on the verge of a monthlong August recess — told the Senate they stand ready to pull the House back into session to reach agreement on legislation to avert the expiration of tax cuts and the imposition of across-the-board defense cuts set to begin in January. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Would Interrupt Recess, On Their Own Terms', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T14:10:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69f6c07a-38df-5604-8289-0f1fbca6473d', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69f6c07a-38df-5604-8289-0f1fbca6473d'}, {'abstract': 'The concurrent victory of Ted Cruz in Texas and selection of Julián Castro as Democratic keynote speaker underscores the political ascendance of Hispanic Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://bruni.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/latinos-on-the-rise/', 'snippet': 'The concurrent victory of Ted Cruz in Texas and selection of Julián Castro as Democratic keynote speaker underscores the political ascendance of Hispanic Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s enormous and warranted attention in news reports this morning to Ted Cruz’s apparent double-digit victory over the Texas lieutenant governor, David Dewhurst, in that state’s Republican primary for a U.S. Senate seat. It was a headlines-grabbing, come-from-behind trouncing, and the reports focus specifically, and rightly, on what it says about the continued potency of the Tea Party and the lure of a certain sort of purism in the Republican Party, whose establishment seems unable to beat back and control insurgents from the right.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Latinos on the Rise', 'kicker': 'Frank Bruni', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castro, Julian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Ted', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T14:16:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36a37308-ecfe-5d4e-a99b-b1e74d24eb02', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36a37308-ecfe-5d4e-a99b-b1e74d24eb02'}, {'abstract': 'Louis M. Bacon’s decision to return about $2 billion to his investors is a victory of sorts for the technocrats — for now at least.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/hedge-fund-titan-plans-to-return-2-billion-to-investors/', 'snippet': 'Louis M. Bacon’s decision to return about $2 billion to his investors is a victory of sorts for the technocrats — for now at least.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:21 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Big to Profit, a Hedge Fund Plans to Get Smaller', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bacon, Louis Moore', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Draghi, Mario', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Moore Capital Management', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T14:19:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Landon Thomas Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Landon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55c65a38-93c3-5e95-b0f9-03038f43899d', 'word_count': 1346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55c65a38-93c3-5e95-b0f9-03038f43899d'}, {'abstract': 'The N.H.L. gave the players’ union thousands of pages of documents, but more have been requested in a high-stakes negotiation.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/76000-pages-at-thousands-of-dollars-per-page/', 'snippet': 'The N.H.L. gave the players’ union thousands of pages of documents, but more have been requested in a high-stakes negotiation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Commissioner Gary Bettman emerged from a negotiating session with the N.H.L. Players’ Association on Tuesday and announced that the league had supplied 76,000 pages of audited financial documents that the union had requested. And, Bettman said, “There’s more coming – lots.” Donald Fehr, the union head, said the documents represented “only a small portion” of the necessary information, “with the vast and overwhelming majority yet to come.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In N.H.L. Negotiation, 76,000 Pages, at Thousands of Dollars Per Page', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettman, Gary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fehr, Donald', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "National Hockey League Players' Assn", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T14:24:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2205e5b8-ee03-5774-8306-4fbe831ba619', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2205e5b8-ee03-5774-8306-4fbe831ba619'}, {'abstract': 'A mobile educational space will make the rounds of city schools, teaching young people how to dispose of recyclables and explaining what happens to all of the glass, metal and plastic.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/on-the-move-a-recyclarium-for-new-york/', 'snippet': 'A mobile educational space will make the rounds of city schools, teaching young people how to dispose of recyclables and explaining what happens to all of the glass, metal and plastic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a state-of-the-art recycling plant rises in Brooklyn, a mobile educational space known as the Recyclarium will be making the rounds this fall to give young New Yorkers a taste of what’s coming.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Move, a ‘Recyclarium’ for New York', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walcott, Dennis M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T14:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae42b3ad-bd59-55af-9644-0354946b95cf', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae42b3ad-bd59-55af-9644-0354946b95cf'}, {'abstract': 'Howard W. Koch Jr., known widely as “Hawk,” succeeds Tom Sherak, who stepped down on reaching a term limit as president of the Academy, which presents the Oscars.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/howard-koch-longtime-producer-named-academy-president/', 'snippet': 'Howard W. Koch Jr., known widely as “Hawk,” succeeds Tom Sherak, who stepped down on reaching a term limit as president of the Academy, which presents the Oscars.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:37 p.m. | Updated LOS ANGELES — Howard W. Koch Jr., known widely as “Hawk,” was named president of the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences at a Tuesday night meeting of its board of governors. He succeeds Tom Sherak, who stepped down on reaching a term limit after three years as president of the Academy, which presents the Oscars and oversees programs that promote film education and awareness.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Howard Koch, Longtime Producer, Named Academy President', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, Howard W Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACADEMY OF MOTION PICTURE ARTS AND SCIENCES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T14:33:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b2b475b-8cec-5682-8bb4-e76643b67647', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b2b475b-8cec-5682-8bb4-e76643b67647'}, {'abstract': 'Ted Cruz won a Republican runoff election after more than a year of street campaigning, and his victory is all but assured in November.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/us/politics/republican-senate-candidate-in-texas-is-known-as-an-intellectual-force.html', 'snippet': 'Ted Cruz won a Republican runoff election after more than a year of street campaigning, and his victory is all but assured in November.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — As a teenager, Ted Cruz was an intense and eloquent parser of free-market economics, dazzling Rotary Clubs here in Houston by reciting the Constitution. At Princeton, he was a champion debater and an intellectual leader of a band of conservative students. He was a star at Harvard Law School and clerked for the chief justice of the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/us/CRUZ/CRUZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 719, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/us/CRUZ/CRUZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1439, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/us/CRUZ/CRUZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/02/us/CRUZ/CRUZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/us/CRUZ/CRUZ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Republican Voice With Tea Party Mantle and Intellectual Heft', 'kicker': 'Man in the News| Rafael Edward Cruz', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Republican Voice With Tea Party Mantle And Intellectual Heft', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Ted', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T14:39:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b107887-094a-532c-9032-7d6718056984', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b107887-094a-532c-9032-7d6718056984'}, {'abstract': 'Watch his on-screen wrangle with William F. Buckley Jr.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/gore-vidal-r-i-p/', 'snippet': 'Watch his on-screen wrangle with William F. Buckley Jr.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gore Vidal died on Tuesday at the age of 86. The extremely prolific writer was perhaps as famous for his novels and essays as for his feuds. As Charles McGrath notes in today’s obituary, Mr. Vidal “did not lightly suffer fools” and “engaged in celebrated on-screen wrangles with Mailer, Capote and William F. Buckley Jr.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gore Vidal, R.I.P.', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buckley, William F Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vidal, Gore', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T14:46:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f14617ab-1b4f-5842-b93e-59add4abe56b', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f14617ab-1b4f-5842-b93e-59add4abe56b'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s chances of victory in the Electoral College improved, mostly because of new government data showing faster growth in personal income.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/july-31-obama-forecast-improves-on-data-showing-faster-income-growth/', 'snippet': 'The president’s chances of victory in the Electoral College improved, mostly because of new government data showing faster growth in personal income.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s chances of winning the Electoral College improved slightly on Tuesday, to 69.0 percent from 66.9 percent one day earlier, according to the FiveThirtyEight forecast model. The change was because of new government data showing faster growth in personal income, one of the seven economic data series that our forecast model uses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'July 31: Obama Forecast Improves on Data Showing Faster Income Growth', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T14:47:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a547914-4bfa-58c2-91ed-5ff4e09f63a9', 'word_count': 1094, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a547914-4bfa-58c2-91ed-5ff4e09f63a9'}, {'abstract': 'General Motors and Ford reported a drop in July sales compared with a year ago, citing lower volume to rental fleets, while Chrysler posted a 13 percent increase.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/business/as-fleet-sales-stall-automakers-report-mixed-results.html', 'snippet': 'General Motors and Ford reported a drop in July sales compared with a year ago, citing lower volume to rental fleets, while Chrysler posted a 13 percent increase.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — Auto sales in the United States cooled off in July as the two biggest American carmakers, General Motors and the Ford Motor Company, reported declines that they attributed partly to lower sales to rental car fleets.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/business/0802BIZAUTO/0802BIZAUTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/02/business/0802BIZAUTO/0802BIZAUTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/business/0802BIZAUTO/0802BIZAUTO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 632, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/business/0802BIZAUTO/0802BIZAUTO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1264, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/business/0802BIZAUTO/0802BIZAUTO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/02/business/0802BIZAUTO/0802BIZAUTO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/business/0802BIZAUTO/0802BIZAUTO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fleet Sales Stall, and Automakers Report Results That Are Mixed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fleet Sales Stall, And Automakers Report Results That Are Mixed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler Group LLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Company', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T14:52:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Vlasic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vlasic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f77c4ed-0f18-5f95-a59d-c31566b51780', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f77c4ed-0f18-5f95-a59d-c31566b51780'}, {'abstract': 'Seeking to pierce one of President Obama’s strongest arguments, Mitt Romney highlights an auto dealer who lost his business after the bailout. A new Obama spot also hits a traditional Republican strength: military spending.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/new-romney-ad-hits-obama-on-layoffs-after-auto-bailout/', 'snippet': 'Seeking to pierce one of President Obama’s strongest arguments, Mitt Romney highlights an auto dealer who lost his business after the bailout. A new Obama spot also hits a traditional Republican strength: military spending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama campaign often sums up the president’s accomplishments like this: “Osama bin Laden is dead. General Motors is alive.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Romney Ad Hits Obama on Layoffs After Auto Bailout', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T14:54:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb7384dd-1c82-5037-8f39-4b3db13ca27b', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb7384dd-1c82-5037-8f39-4b3db13ca27b'}, {'abstract': 'In a comparison of credit card networks, the Web site CardHub finds that only American Express and Discover offer extended warranties to all cardholders.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/credit-cards-with-the-best-extended-warranties/', 'snippet': 'In a comparison of credit card networks, the Web site CardHub finds that only American Express and Discover offer extended warranties to all cardholders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the benefits of shopping with a credit card is that many cards offer free, extended-warranty protection for purchases that come with an existing manufacturer’s warranty. But a new survey from the card comparison site CardHub.com finds that there are significant differences in the perk, depending on which network sponsors the card.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Credit Cards With the Best Extended Warranties', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Guarantees and Warranties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MasterCard Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Visa Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T14:54:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6f12d68-d776-599b-9d55-e2cca4ec4a68', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6f12d68-d776-599b-9d55-e2cca4ec4a68'}, {'abstract': 'The technical study is damning, too.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/more-demarco/', 'snippet': 'The technical study is damning, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, I’ve slogged through the technical appendix (pdf) from the FHFA on the proposed debt relief, and while it’s eye-glazing reading, it makes DeMarco’s stonewalling even more outrageous.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More DeMarco', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T14:54:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byli