ype_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5af77d1c-6846-5d81-8470-d9eef5ebb243', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5af77d1c-6846-5d81-8470-d9eef5ebb243'}, {'abstract': 'A new study shows less mislabeling of sturgeon caviar since regulations were tightened.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/a-caviar-crackdown-has-worked-researchers-say/', 'snippet': 'A new study shows less mislabeling of sturgeon caviar since regulations were tightened.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sturgeon caviar industry has changed drastically in the past 15 years or so. And now a study indicates that in New York, it has become more law-abiding and even ethical.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Caviar Crackdown Has Worked, Researchers Say', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caviar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T15:02:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42f0d018-de38-5a6f-a5b5-68debdc71b5a', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42f0d018-de38-5a6f-a5b5-68debdc71b5a'}, {'abstract': 'Kohei Uchimura of Japan won the gold, Marcel Nguyen of Germany the silver, Dannell Leyva of the U.S. the bronze in the men’s gymnastics individual all-around final at the 2012 Olympics in London.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/live-the-mens-individual-gymnastics-final/', 'snippet': 'Kohei Uchimura of Japan won the gold, Marcel Nguyen of Germany the silver, Dannell Leyva of the U.S. the bronze in the men’s gymnastics individual all-around final at the 2012 Olympics in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kohei Uchimura of Japan won the gold, Marcel Nguyen of Germany the silver, Dannell Leyva of the U.S. the bronze in the men’s gymnastics individual all-around final at the 2012 Olympics in London on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uchimura Wins Gold, Leyva Bronze in Men’s Gymnastics', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gymnastics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hambuechen, Fabian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leyva, Danell', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T15:03:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6b7446f-c049-5c51-af0d-934fbb8b43ee', 'word_count': 2350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6b7446f-c049-5c51-af0d-934fbb8b43ee'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama will make stops in north-central Ohio and plans to discuss “the choice in this election between two fundamentally different visions of how to grow the economy, create middle-class jobs and pay down the debt,” according to his campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/obama-heads-to-ohio-battleground-again/', 'snippet': 'President Obama will make stops in north-central Ohio and plans to discuss “the choice in this election between two fundamentally different visions of how to grow the economy, create middle-class jobs and pay down the debt,” according to his campa...', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANSFIELD, Ohio – As polls in this battleground state and nationally continue to show voters split over President Obama’s stewardship of the economy, Mr. Obama on Wednesday is making his ninth visit this year to Ohio to contrast his vision for the nation’s future with that of his Republican rival, Mitt Romney.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Heads to Ohio Battleground, Again', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T15:10:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a40680d-fdaf-5b51-a269-dd17d9e53740', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a40680d-fdaf-5b51-a269-dd17d9e53740'}, {'abstract': 'The Occupy movement is still wreaking havoc in Oakland, the world capital of anticapitalism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/magazine/oakland-occupy-movement.html', 'snippet': 'The Occupy movement is still wreaking havoc in Oakland, the world capital of anticapitalism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Anti-Capitalist Brigade started gathering early on May Day at Oakland’s Snow Park. There was free coffee, oatmeal, doughnuts, fliers with the day’s agenda and plenty of pot. A “street medic” — “I just finished a wilderness first-aid course,” he told me when I asked about his training — tended to his first case of the day, a man in his 20s whose leg had been beaten to a purple hue with a metal rod in an overnight fight in the park. Nearby, an organizer reminded protesters to take down the toll-free number for the National Lawyers Guild: “This is important. Do not put it in your cellphones, because if you get arrested, the cops will take those away. Write it on your bodies. In indelible ink. There are Sharpies on the table.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05oakland_ss-slide-UUHB/05oakland_ss-slide-UUHB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05oakland_ss-slide-UUHB/05oakland_ss-slide-UUHB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05oakland_ss-slide-UUHB/05oakland_ss-slide-UUHB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05oakland_ss-slide-UUHB/05oakland_ss-slide-UUHB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05oakland_ss-slide-UUHB/05oakland_ss-slide-UUHB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05oakland_ss-slide-UUHB/05oakland_ss-slide-UUHB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05oakland_ss-slide-UUHB/05oakland_ss-slide-UUHB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Oakland, the Last Refuge of Radical America', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The World Capital of Anti-Capitalism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oakland (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T15:11:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Mahler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/298ae756-300d-5068-b47b-2025605bd2f8', 'word_count': 6132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/298ae756-300d-5068-b47b-2025605bd2f8'}, {'abstract': 'In “Celeste and Jesse Forever,” Rashida Jones (“Parks and Recreation”) helped write a new kind of part for herself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/movies/rashida-jones-writes-a-new-part-for-herself.html', 'snippet': 'In “Celeste and Jesse Forever,” Rashida Jones (“Parks and Recreation”) helped write a new kind of part for herself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rashida Jones has a good sense of how directors see her. “I am generally cast as the dependable, affable, loving, friend-wife-girlfriend,” she said. As Ann Perkins on the NBC series “Parks and Recreation” Ms. Jones is the voice of reason among her loopier co-stars Amy Poehler, Nick Offerman and Aziz Ansari. But in her new movie, “Celeste and Jesse Forever,” coming out on Friday, she has the chance to unravel that persona, in wanton fashion. She stars as Celeste, who is in the midst of a lingering divorce from Jesse (Andy Samberg).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/02celeste-span/02celeste-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 255, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/02celeste-span/02celeste-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 255}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/02celeste-span/02celeste-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/02celeste-span/02celeste-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 816, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/02celeste-span/02celeste-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/02celeste-span/02celeste-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/02celeste-span/02celeste-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking the Mold by Writing a Part for Herself', 'kicker': 'A Word With: Rashida Jones     ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Breaking the Mold by Writing a Part for Herself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Celeste and Jesse Forever (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Rashida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T15:19:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c24fbc1-d86b-5ece-b9d1-6e723ae6f8b0', 'word_count': 1115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c24fbc1-d86b-5ece-b9d1-6e723ae6f8b0'}, {'abstract': 'In Michelle Robinson’s new book, a young boy trying to learn the rules of the jungle finds absurd adventure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/books/what-to-do-if-an-elephant-stands-on-your-foot.html', 'snippet': 'In Michelle Robinson’s new book, a young boy trying to learn the rules of the jungle finds absurd adventure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you had to choose the most popular aspect of chaos theory in children’s literature, the answer would have to be, hands down, the butterfly effect. Beginning with Dr. Seuss, who — writing under an even more colorful pseudonym, Rosetta Stone — gave us “Because a Little Bug Went Ka-Choo!,” and up through the copious “If You Give a Mouse a Cookie” franchise, children have had plenty of “this leads to that” tales to marvel over.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/01/books/01childrens-img/01childrens-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xla