pet': 'The United States field hockey team got back on track against Argentina, reprising its victory in October against Las Leonas at the Pan American Games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pam Stuper, the head field hockey coach at Yale, played on three national championship teams at Old Dominion University, and on the United States national team from 1990 to ’98, earning a bronze medal at the 1994 World Cup. She currently chairs the USA Field Hockey board of directors. She will be writing for the 2012 London Olympics blog throughout the Games.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Women Show Strength in Field Hockey Win Over Argentina', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Field', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Shannon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T16:03:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pam Stuper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stuper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/742aedd8-b478-5949-a3aa-b97a6dc70fbb', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/742aedd8-b478-5949-a3aa-b97a6dc70fbb'}, {'abstract': 'Joe Arpaio, a sheriff in Arizona, has used headline-grabbing tactics to become a hero to many Americans, but he is on trial over his treatment of Latinos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/us/an-arizona-sheriffs-fondness-for-publicity-may-bite-back.html', 'snippet': 'Joe Arpaio, a sheriff in Arizona, has used headline-grabbing tactics to become a hero to many Americans, but he is on trial over his treatment of Latinos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — In nearly 20 years as sheriff of Maricopa County, Joe Arpaio has honed his publicity skills, using headline-grabbing, often outrageous maneuvers to build a reputation as the nation’s toughest law officer and make himself a hero to many Americans. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/us/02arpaio_1/02arpaio_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/02/us/02arpaio_1/02arpaio_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/us/02arpaio_1/02arpaio_1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/us/02arpaio_1/02arpaio_1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/us/02arpaio_1/02arpaio_1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/02/us/02arpaio_1/02arpaio_1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/us/02arpaio_1/02arpaio_1-thumbLarge-v2.