nk loans. But there are several alternative, though expensive, lending sources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After years of a small-business credit crisis, conditions seem to have improved. But with the economy still struggling and new regulations meant to eliminate bad lending, bank loans continue to lag.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/business/02sbiz/02sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/02/business/02sbiz/02sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/business/02sbiz/02sbiz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/business/02sbiz/02sbiz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1356, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/business/02sbiz/02sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/02/business/02sbiz/02sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/business/02sbiz/02sbiz-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Banks Won’t Lend, There Are Alternatives, Though Often Expensive', 'kicker': 'Small-Business Guide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Banks Won’t Lend, There Are Alternatives, Though Often Expensive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T16:33:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Mount', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mount', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0c0e612-cc4f-5df3-9e25-921765697930', 'word_count': 1258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0c0e612-cc4f-5df3-9e25-921765697930'}, {'abstract': 'If a bank won’t lend you money, the good news is that there are now lots of other options. You know the bad news.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/should-a-business-ever-pay-70-percent-to-borrow-money/', 'snippet': 'If a bank won’t lend you money, the good news is that there are now lots of other options. You know the bad news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a small-business guide to alternative finance we have just published, Ian Mount runs down the list of creative alternatives to bank lending. Some have been around forever; others emerged during the crisis. Almost all are substantially more expensive than traditional bank loans, which is why they have been sources of last resort. But as demand for alternative options has increased, some prices have come down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should a Business Ever Pay 70% to Borrow Money?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T16:39:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': "By You're the Boss Editors", 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20d9521d-53f9-52af-a7ae-652a7bc70537', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20d9521d-53f9-52af-a7ae-652a7bc70537'}, {'abstract': 'Answers to readers’ questions about giving a gift, or not, if you are not invited to the wedding and other wedding-related matters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/fashion/weddings/wedding-q-and-a.html', 'snippet': 'Answers to readers’ questions about giving a gift, or not, if you are not invited to the wedding and other wedding-related matters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Feel-Good Gift From an Uninvited Guest', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/11/fashion/weddings/peggypost/peggypost-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 288, 'width': 288, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/11/fashion/weddings/peggypost/peggypost-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/11/fashion/weddings/peggypost/peggypost-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/11/fashion/weddings/peggypost/peggy