0eda2c'}, {'abstract': 'A federal appeals court rules that legal fees should be calculated under state and not federal guidelines.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/court-must-revisit-legal-fees-in-audi-vw-sludge-case/', 'snippet': 'A federal appeals court rules that legal fees should be calculated under state and not federal guidelines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal appeals court has rejected a $30 million payment to the lawyers who brought a class-action suit against Volkswagen and Audi over engines that were damaged by sludge problems.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Must Revisit Legal Fees in Audi-VW Sludge Case', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Audi Division of Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T16:59:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ba80039-c569-5a0d-8a94-117e111510b3', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ba80039-c569-5a0d-8a94-117e111510b3'}, {'abstract': 'The good news: The earth’s ability to soak up carbon has kept up with human activity that emits carbon. The bad news: There are reasons to think this pattern could change.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/the-great-disposal-service-can-it-last/', 'snippet': 'The good news: The earth’s ability to soak up carbon has kept up with human activity that emits carbon. The bad news: There are reasons to think this pattern could change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The earth is performing an enormous disposal service for the human race. About half of the carbon we are dumping into the atmosphere does not stay there and is instead taken up by the oceans and land. Were this not the case, scientists say, the earth would probably be warming far more rapidly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Great Disposal Service: Can It Last?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T17:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46af0bc8-9f85-5233-81b5-61ede2e53ac4', 'word_count': 913, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46af0bc8-9f85-5233-81b5-61ede2e53ac4'}, {'abstract': 'The sixth day of the London Olympics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/08/01/sports/olympics/20120801-OLYPOD.html', 'snippet': 'The sixth day of the London Olympics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sixth day of the London Olympics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/01/sports/olympics/20120801-OLYPOD-slide-VZA8/20120801-OLYPOD-slide-VZA8-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/01/sports/olympics/20120801-OLYPOD-slide-VZA8/20120801-OLYPOD-slide-VZA8-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1406, 'width': 2048, 'subType':