ork Times readers respond to the public editor’s most recent print column on the 2012 presidential campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/the-timess-agenda-project-for-campaign-some-readers-vote-yes-some-scoff/', 'snippet': 'New York Times readers respond to the public editor’s most recent print column on the 2012 presidential campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Included below is some reader responses to my column “Resetting the Campaign Agenda” on July 29:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Times’s Agenda Project for Campaign: Some Readers Vote Yes, Some Scoff', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T19:52:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arthur S. Brisbane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arthur', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Brisbane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f28c3c7e-19fe-5a1a-ac0e-b8f77511def7', 'word_count': 2114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f28c3c7e-19fe-5a1a-ac0e-b8f77511def7'}, {'abstract': 'In Laura Lippman’s new novel, a woman running a suburban prostitution ring learns that the father of her son, a violent pimp, may soon be released from prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/books/and-when-she-was-good-by-laura-lippman.html', 'snippet': 'In Laura Lippman’s new novel, a woman running a suburban prostitution ring learns that the father of her son, a violent pimp, may soon be released from prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heloise Lewis runs “a boutique lobbying firm whose mission statement identifies it as a nonprofit focused on income parity for all women.” It is called the Women’s Full Employment Network. “And when people hear that, they never want to know a single thing more about Heloise’s business,” Laura Lippman writes, “which is exactly as she planned it.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/02jpbook/02jpbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 718, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/02jpbook/02jpbook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1109, 'width': 778, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/02jpbook/02jpbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/02jpbook/02jpbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/02jpbook/02jpbook-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Secret Life Reinvented Once Again', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Secret Life Reinvented Once Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lippman, Laura', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T19:54:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization'