-10a42e0f6376', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b91f8a8-236c-5067-9314-10a42e0f6376'}, {'abstract': 'In her new show at Feinstein’s, Rebecca Kilgore finds her way into the essence of Garland signature hits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/arts/music/rebecca-kilgores-jazzy-side-of-judy-garland-at-feinsteins.html', 'snippet': 'In her new show at Feinstein’s, Rebecca Kilgore finds her way into the essence of Garland signature hits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s difficult to imagine two more disparate sensibilities than the singer Rebecca Kilgore and the subject of her new show, “The Jazzy Side of Judy Garland,” now playing at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency. Ms. Kilgore, who is based in Portland, Ore., has an invariably light touch. Wearing a half-smile of pure enjoyment, she sails from one number to the next like a butterfly in a field of flowers.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/sub-02kilgore/sub-02kilgore-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 941, 'width': 770, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/sub-02kilgore/sub-02kilgore-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 941, 'width': 770, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/sub-02kilgore/sub-02kilgore-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/sub-02kilgore/sub-02kilgore-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/sub-02kilgore/sub-02kilgore-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Channeling Judy Garland, Serenely', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Channeling Garland, Serenely', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kilgore, Rebecca', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T21:24:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/91cf46d5-8657-532b-ac9d-308ed8246b5b', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91cf46d5-8657-532b-ac9d-308ed8246b5b'}, {'abstract': 'Photos from the Philippines, Israel, Greece and India.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/pictures-of-the-day-philippines-and-elsewhere-3/', 'snippet': 'Photos from the Philippines, Israel, Greece and India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos from the Philippines, Israel, Greece and India.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Philippines and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T21:25:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48996d09-c504-5260-9a33-ac639054d4a8', 'word_count': 13, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48996d09-c504-5260-9a33-ac639054d4a8'}, {'abstract': 'Audiences get a taste of the future at this year’s Salzburg Festival. Newer operas are on the horizon, says its new artistic director.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/arts/music/mozart-strauss-and-friends-an-austrian-seasonal-tradition.html', 'snippet': 'Audiences get a taste of the future at this year’s Salzburg Festival. Newer operas are on the horizon, says its new artistic director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SALZBURG, Austria — Opera has long been the backbone of the Salzburg Festival. So you might have expected the festival’s new artistic director, Alexander Pereira, to treat the opera program with caution, confining himself at first to subtle shifts of emphasis. Instead Mr. Pereira, who was the director of the Zurich Opera House from 1991 to this year, is instituting major changes here, as elsewhere in the festival.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/jpoperas1/jpoperas1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/jpoperas1/jpoperas1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 309}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/jpoperas1/jpoperas1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 505, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/jpoperas1/jpoperas1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1010, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/jpoperas1/jpoperas1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/jpoperas1/jpoperas1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/jpoperas1/jpoperas1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Is a Word for Opera in Salzburg', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Summer Is a Word For Opera In Salzburg', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Salzburg (Austria)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'ARIADNE AUF NAXOS (OPERA)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salzburg Festival', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mozart, Wolfgang Amadeus', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss, Richard', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T21:29:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/63296b9c-e55e-59dd-8ff5-851705efc6a9', 'word_count': 1020, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63296b9c-e55e-59dd-8ff5-851705efc6a9'}, {'abstract': 'Confusing maps and long lines can make theme parks stressful, but several apps can keep habitual parkgoers informed and entertained.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/technology/personaltech/guides-to-legoland-disney-madame-tussauds-and-more-app-smart.html', 'snippet': 'Confusing maps and long lines can make theme parks stressful, but several apps can keep habitual parkgoers informed and entertained.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We know why we love roller coasters: it is the thrill of letting go of our normal life baggage and, for just a few minutes, feeling the physical thrill and emotional uplift of being a child again. Fully grown up as most of us are, we also know why we dislike the theme parks where many roller coasters are found: it is the hassle of hauling children around in the blazing sun while following confusing maps, only to find a long line of thrill-seekers already waiting.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/technology/02smart-web/02smart-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 286, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/02/technology/02smart-web/02smart-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 286}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/technology/02smart-web/02smart-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 286, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/technology/02smart-web/02smart-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 286, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/technology/02smart-web/02smart-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/02/technology/02smart-web/02smart-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/technology/02smart-web/02smart-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 72, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Guides to Make Park Days Smoother', 'kicker': 'App Smart', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guides To Make Park Days Smoother', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMUSEMENT AND THEME PARKS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T21:30:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kit Eaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/345e90c6-3f0a-5eda-a445-31736a7a838d', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/345e90c6-3f0a-5eda-a445-31736a7a838d'}, {'abstract': 'Until Kim Jong-un’s wife, Ri Sol-ju, began appearing with him in public, there had seldom been a woman’s face among the North’s power circles filled with Mao-suited party secretaries and military generals in olive-colored uniforms.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/in-north-korea-putting-a-female-face-front-and-center/', 'snippet': 'Until Kim Jong-un’s wife, Ri Sol-ju, began appearing with him in public, there had seldom been a woman’s face among the North’s power circles filled with Mao-suited party secretaries and military generals in olive-colored uniforms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — Ri Sol-ju, the wife of the North Korean leader, Kim Jong-un, is adding a new look to the nation’s leadership. Until she began accompanying Mr. Kim in public appearances in recent weeks, holding his arm and smiling at what appear to be adoring crowds, there had seldom been a woman’s face among the North’s power circles, which are filled with grim-faced party secretaries in Mao suits and military generals in their olive-colored uniforms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In North Korea, Putting a Female Face Front and Center', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'First Ladies (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Il', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ri Sol-ju', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Intelligence Service (South Korea)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T21:38:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/246a92cd-fd2a-5aec-bf38-96c7711e342d', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/246a92cd-fd2a-5aec-bf38-96c7711e342d'}, {'abstract': 'Airtime, the video-chat service started by the founders of Napster, does not appear to be attracting many users, despite a flashy unveiling and millions in venture funding.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/after-splashy-introduction-airtime-seems-to-deflate/', 'snippet': 'Airtime, the video-chat service started by the founders of Napster, does not appear to be attracting many users, despite a flashy unveiling and millions in venture funding.', 'lead_paragraph': ' It just goes to show. You can unleash all the star power and venture capital in your arsenal to get a new start-up off the ground, but at the end of the day, people either love your service or they don’t. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Splashy Introduction, Airtime Seems to Deflate', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Airtime Appears To Lose Ground Despite Star Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fanning, Shawn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Sean (1979- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Airtime Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T21:39:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b78544c6-0493-5efe-8679-4e29930d69f3', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b78544c6-0493-5efe-8679-4e29930d69f3'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Lochte’s custom-made stars and stripes grill offers a rare moment of fashion in these Games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/fashion/ryan-lochtes-grill-gets-a-mixed-response.html', 'snippet': 'Ryan Lochte’s custom-made stars and stripes grill offers a rare moment of fashion in these Games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THUS far, the only real fashion moment to come out of the London Olympics belongs to Ryan Lochte and his custom-made American flag dental grill (or grillz, if you prefer).