ier place, as he joins forever those whom he served in life, applauding their prejudices and fanning their hatred.”)\xa0The magazine’s interview.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vidal Speaks', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vidal, Gore', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T22:07:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheila Glaser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glaser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ce364e0-8e7a-512d-ae5c-949ba7eda4fb', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ce364e0-8e7a-512d-ae5c-949ba7eda4fb'}, {'abstract': 'Evgeny Nikitin, who withdrew from the Bayreuth Festival after he was reported to have a swastikalike tattoo on his chest, said on Tuesday that the tattoo had nothing to do with Nazis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/arts/music/opera-singer-explains-tattoo-thought-to-be-swastika.html', 'snippet': 'Evgeny Nikitin, who withdrew from the Bayreuth Festival after he was reported to have a swastikalike tattoo on his chest, said on Tuesday that the tattoo had nothing to do with Nazis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Russian bass-baritone Evgeny Nikitin, who resigned from the Bayreuth Festival over body art, wants his American audience to know his side: What appeared to be a swastika tattooed on his chest was just the first stage of a star with a heraldic crest.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/arts/sub2singer/sub2singer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 