offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/knicks-sign-j-r-smiths-brother/', 'snippet': 'Chris Smith, a 6-foot-2 guard, led Louisville to the Final Four and played on the Knicks’ summer league team in Las Vegas.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:19 p.m. | Updated Chris Smith said he experienced poor cellphone reception for most of Tuesday. When Smith was able to get a rare signal, he received a text message from his agent, Marc Cornstein, that read, “Call me ASAP.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knicks Sign J. R. Smith’s Brother', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Chris', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, J R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T23:31:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b9bbf4d-36e6-5738-a1f8-b12cb3db9dce', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b9bbf4d-36e6-5738-a1f8-b12cb3db9dce'}, {'abstract': 'Cristián Samper, the new president of the Wildlife Conservation Society, said he was motivated to take the job by a sense of urgency about the state of the world’s wildlife.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/nyregion/new-president-of-wildlife-conservation-society-says-mission-is-to-protect-species.html', 'snippet': 'Cristián Samper, the new president of the Wildlife Conservation Society, said he was motivated to take the job by a sense of urgency about the state of the world’s wildlife.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Cristián Samper told his children, ages 3 and 6, that he might leave his post as director of the Smithsonian’s National Museum of Natural History in Washington for a job in New York, they were crestfallen. After all, it is hard to top having a father who oversees dinosaur skeletons and stuffed lions, all part of one of the world’s largest collections of specimens and artifacts, 126 million in all.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/nyregion/Y-ZOO/Y-ZOO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/02/nyregion/Y-ZOO/Y-ZOO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/nyregion/Y-ZOO/Y-ZOO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/nyregion/Y-ZOO/Y-ZOO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/nyregion/Y-ZOO/Y-ZOO-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/02/nyregion/Y-ZOO/Y-ZOO-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/nyregion/Y-ZOO/Y-ZOO-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Species Vanish, Taking Up a Mission to Protect Birds and Beasts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking Up a Mission to Protect the Birds and the Beasts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zoos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samper, Cristian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wildlife Conservation Society', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T23:31:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa W. Foderaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Foderaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fd68290-6672-5714-96d9-d28f49536fcd', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fd68290-6672-5714-96d9-d28f49536fcd'}, {'abstract': 'The specter of the Sept. 11, 2001, attacks hangs over the Royal Air Force operation at the Olympics, and the lessons learned from those attacks are central to its planning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/sports/olympics/at-olympics-royal-air-force-on-terrorism-alert.html', 'snippet': 'The specter of the Sept. 11, 2001, attacks hangs over the Royal Air Force operation at the Olympics, and the lessons learned from those attacks are central to its planning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROYAL AIR FORCE STATION NORTHOLT, England — More than 70 years after squadrons of Spitfire and Hurricane fighters flew from here into an epic air battle with Hitler’s Luftwaffe, pilots flying the fastest fighter interceptors in Britain’s modern arsenal have been cast in a similar role. But instead of waves of German bombers in the Battle of Britain, these pilots are guarding against a more elusive enemy: terrorists who might seek to rain destruction on the Olympic Games from the air.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/world/flight/flight-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/02/world/flight/flight-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/world/flight/flight-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/world/flight/flight-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1294, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/world/flight/flight-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/02/world/flight/flight-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/world/flight/flight-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Olympics Vigil, From 30,000 Feet', 'kicker': 'Royal Air Force Station Northolt Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Olympics Vigil, From 30,000 Feet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Air Force', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Aircraft', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-01T23:39:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9086d73-64f1-564c-a374-b63ab7ebc6f3', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9086d73-64f1-564c-a374-b63ab7ebc6f3'}, {'abstract': 'Levi Aron, a supply store clerk accused of kidnapping and dismembering Leiby Kletzky, is expected to make a deal with prosecutors and face 40 years in prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/nyregion/levi-aron-expected-to-plead-guilty-to-killing-leiby-kletzky.html', 'snippet': 'Levi Aron, a supply store clerk accused of kidnapping and dismembering Leiby Kletzky, is expected to make a deal with prosecutors and face 40 years in prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The man accused of kidnapping, killing and dismembering Leiby Kletzky, an 8-year-old boy who had gotten lost in the Hasidic neighborhood of Borough Park, Brooklyn, is scheduled to plead guilty to the crime and face at least 40 years in prison, a state assemblyman said Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'sub