he New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/us/HEPC/HEPC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 757, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/us/HEPC/HEPC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1514, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thousands Await Testing for Hepatitis by ‘Infector’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thousands Await Testing For Hepatitis By ‘Infector’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preventive Medicine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malpractice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kwiatkowski, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hepatitis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hypodermic Needles and Syringes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T01:35:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3f5259a-6105-52cb-b413-9cbeb64e1843', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3f5259a-6105-52cb-b413-9cbeb64e1843'}, {'abstract': 'The officers, who were initially detained in May, are accused of participating in trafficking with the Beltrán Leyva gang, which had been one of the biggest suppliers of cocaine to the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/world/americas/mexico-former-defense-officials-are-accused-of-aiding-traffickers.html', 'snippet': 'The officers, who were initially detained in May, are accused of participating in trafficking with the Beltrán Leyva gang, which had been one of the biggest suppliers of cocaine to the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The former second-highest ranking secretary at the Defense Ministry and three other former officers have been formally charged with aiding drug traffickers, in the biggest military corruption case in recent years. Federal prosecutors announced the charges on Tuesday evening, confirming that the officers, who were initially detained in May, are accused of participating in trafficking with the Beltrán Leyva gang, which had been one of the biggest suppliers of cocaine to the United States. Its leader, Edgar Valdes Villareal, an American-born kingpin known as La Barbie, has been in custody since August 2010. Among the officers are Tomás Ángeles Dauahare, a retired army general who was the deputy defense secretary from 2006 to 2008 and had been seen as a rising star. His lawyer has denied the charges, and some commentators have suggested the case is politically motivated. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Former Defense Officials Are Accused of Aiding Traffickers', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Former Defense Officials Are Accused of Aiding Traffickers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beltran Leyva', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T01:41:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f73dd16e-36b2-5f37-a3d2-3aa36385e403', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f73dd16e-36b2-5f37-a3d2-3aa36385e403'}, {'abstract': 'Municipalities and institutions should leave the decision about whether to eat at Chick-fil-A to individual consumers and not to officeholders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/opinion/let-chick-fil-a-fly-free.html', 'snippet': 'Municipalities and institutions should leave the decision about whether to eat at Chick-fil-A to individual consumers and not to officeholders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Atlanta', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/opinion/0802OPEDgoodman/0802OPEDgoodman-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/opinion/0802OPEDgoodman/0802OPEDgoodman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1438, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/opinion/0802OPEDgoodman/0802OPEDgoodman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/02/opinion/0802OPEDgoodman/0802OPEDgoodman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/opinion/0802OPEDgoodman/0802OPEDgoodman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Let Chick-fil-A Fly Free', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Let Chick-fil-A Fly Free', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boycotts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cathy, Dan T', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chick-fil-A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T01:41:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Salbu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Salbu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccf2a8e8-c622-5ee0-961e-bea354e2f98e', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccf2a8e8-c622-5ee0-961e-bea354e2f98e'}, {'abstract': 'The garment district, even after the last fabric store has closed shop, should keep its name and inspire New Yorkers for years to come.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/opinion/long-live-the-garment-district.html', 'snippet': 'The garment district, even after the last fabric store has closed shop, should keep its name and inspire New Yorkers for years to come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE garment district, a roughly rectangular swatch of Manhattan between West 35th and 42nd Streets and Seventh and Ninth Avenues, was once the bustling epicenter of America’s clothing design and manufacturing industry. While its boundaries fluctuated over the decades, the garment district, as a culture and as an idea, had resonance in areas much larger than its physical size: its hundreds of thousands of workers — including my father, David Dubinsky, the long-serving president of the International Ladies’ Garment Workers’ Union — were the living embodiment of New York’s working-class economy, whose sweat and long hours draped the shoulders of the rest of the country. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Needles, Threads and New York History', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Needles, Threads and New York History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, John Fitzgerald', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Geographical', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Garment District (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T01:42:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jean Appleton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appleton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf3701a3-7488-5623-be49-3d233e45f530', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf3701a3-7488-5623-be49-3d233e45f530'}, {'abstract': 'NBC’s delayed coverage of the Olympic Games may be annoying, but there was nothing more spectacular than seeing Michael Phelps shatter a 48-year-old record by winning his 19th medal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/opinion/michael-phelps-goat.html', 'snippet': 'NBC’s delayed coverage of the Olympic Games may be annoying, but there was nothing more spectacular than seeing Michael Phelps shatter a 48-year-old record by winning his 19th medal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is always a lot of inflated drama in the televised broadcasts of the Olympic Games, the product of network executives who like to fill expensive airtime with wall-to-wall minidocumentaries about the heart, courage and personal lives of the competitors — to the frustration of those who prefer to see great athletes actually competing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Greatest Olympian', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Greatest Olympian', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phelps, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T01:43:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d8f190d-4a8b-5a54-abaf-de21c1d03b5c', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d8f190d-4a8b-5a54-abaf-de21c1d03b5c'}, {'abstract': 'The I.R.S. is finally promising to review rules governing the limits of political activity for so-called social welfare nonprofits, many of which are partisan attack dogs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/opinion/the-irs-finally-takes-on-secret-campaign-donations.html', 'snippet': 'The I.R.S. is finally promising to review rules governing the limits of political activity for so-called social welfare nonprofits, many of which are partisan attack dogs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ploy of disguising secretly financed political machines as tax-exempt “social welfare” organizations has become one of the alarming trademarks of modern, big-money politics. Under cover of the tax code, the identities of donors are kept secret while they pay for attack ads against candidates, all the while claiming their main purpose is civic and nonpartisan. Operatives from both parties have gotten deep into this shell game. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Further Review for Secret Donations', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Further Review for Secret Donations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crossroads Grassroots Policy Strategies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rove, Karl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T01:44:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f957e3d-885a-5abd-8cbb-ac4f0726d1cf', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f957e3d-885a-5abd-8cbb-ac4f0726d1cf'}, {'abstract': 'Russia is growing more rigid and intolerant by the day under President Vladimir Putin. Just look at what’s happened so far this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/opinion/russias-beleaguered-opposition.html', 'snippet': 'Russia is growing more rigid and intolerant by the day under President Vladimir Putin. Just look at what’s happened so far this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Russia is growing more rigid and intolerant by the day under President Vladimir Putin. Last month, his Parliament moved to tighten control over Internet sites, protesters and nonprofit organizations. On Monday, three singers in a punk-rock band went on trial in Moscow for the Soviet-sounding charges of “hooliganism” after they sang an anti-Putin song in a Moscow cathedral. On Tuesday, Russian prosecutors leveled what appear to be trumped-up charges of embezzlement against Aleksei Navalny, one of President Putin’s most nettlesome and charismatic critics. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia’s Beleaguered Opposition', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia’s Beleaguered Opposition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navalny, Aleksei N', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T01:44:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/143ac45a-3a11-5b91-8281-d654cb213053', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/143ac45a-3a11-5b91-8281-d654cb213053'}, {'abstract': 'While the nation is turned off by partisanship, the Republican candidates are being pushed into being more and more intractable. Just look at Tuesday’s election in Texas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/0