fessor who helped create the cognitive psychology movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Psychological research was in a kind of rut in 1955 when George A. Miller, a professor at Harvard, delivered a paper titled “The Magical Number Seven, Plus or Minus Two,” which helped set off an explosion of new thinking about thinking and opened a new field of research known as cognitive psychology.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/us/MILLER-obit/MILLER-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1441, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/us/MILLER-obit/MILLER-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1455, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/us/MILLER-obit/MILLER-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/02/us/MILLER-obit/MILLER-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/us/MILLER-obit/MILLER-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'George A. Miller, a Pioneer in Cognitive Psychology, Is Dead at 92', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'George A. Miller, a Pioneer in Cognitive Psychology, Is Dead at 92', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, George A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T02:52:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Vitello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vitello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bb1df6c-f693-5efe-8d1a-472c84c436ef', 'word_count': 1076, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bb1df6c-f693-5efe-8d1a-472c84c436ef'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands of people posted photos and updates on social media sites about their visits to Chick-fil-A restaurants on Wednesday in support of the company’s president, who has drawn criticism for statements that he made last month against same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/01/chick-fil-a-draws-huge-crowds-for-appreciation-day/', 'snippet': 'Thousands of people posted photos and updates on social media sites about their visits to Chick-fil-A restaurants on Wednesday in support of the company’s president, who has drawn criticism for statements that he made last month against same-sex m...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hundreds of thousands of people across the country headed to Chick-fil-A restaurants on Wednesday, answering a call from Mike Huckabee, the former governor of Arkansas, to show support for the fast-food chain after the company’s president drew criticism for his opposition to same-sex marriage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chick-fil-A Draws Huge Crowds for Appreciation Day', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social 