uglas of the United States won the gold medal in the women’s gymnastics all-around individual final.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Douglas Wins Gold in Women’s All-Around', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gymnastics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douglas, Gabby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raisman, Aly', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T10:59:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc06c72f-d960-5b34-a889-7a709e21045e', 'word_count': 1628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc06c72f-d960-5b34-a889-7a709e21045e'}, {'abstract': 'Discovering brilliant Mexican-American cuisine in — of all places — Mexico.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/magazine/viva-amerexico.html', 'snippet': 'Discovering brilliant Mexican-American cuisine in — of all places — Mexico.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was bound to happen: contemporary, creative, smart no-name food made by an American of Mexican extraction in Mexico. Jair Téllez’s restaurant in Mexico City, MeroToro — “mero” is grouper, “toro” is bull; it’s a made-up word, kind of a play on surf ’n’ turf — would be equally at home in L.A. or in New York, which goes to show just how “American” its neighborhood, Condesa, feels. (Condesa’s gentrification has paralleled that of Manhattan’s Lower East Side, though it is a naturally more beautiful place.)', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '46', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05eat1/05eat1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05eat1/05eat1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05eat1/05eat1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05eat1/05eat1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05eat1/05eat1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05eat1/05eat1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05eat1/05eat1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Viva Amerexico!', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Viva Amerexico!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico City (Mexico)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mexican Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbo