iness Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Goltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/baa9191b-1fc7-55e5-9626-b2e15f6567eb', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baa9191b-1fc7-55e5-9626-b2e15f6567eb'}, {'abstract': 'Android apps list their permissions on both the device and on the Web.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/qa-checking-android-app-permissions/', 'snippet': 'Android apps list their permissions on both the device and on the Web.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Checking Android App Permissions', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Google Phone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T11:01:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd434b67-a6a4-5c4a-a787-020892368742', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd434b67-a6a4-5c4a-a787-020892368742'}, {'abstract': 'Because of a lack of rain in the Midwest, far less fertilizer was flushed into rivers and far less nitrates reached the Gulf of Mexico, slowing the process that depletes oxygen there.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/big-drought-makes-for-a-small-dead-zone/', 'snippet': 'Because of a lack of rain in the Midwest, far less fertilizer was flushed into rivers and far less nitrates reached the Gulf of Mexico, slowing the process that depletes oxygen there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In yet another display of the inexorable interdependence of Earth’s ecosystems, a bad summer for Midwestern farmland has turned out to be a good one for life in the Gulf of Mexico.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Drought Makes for a Small ‘Dead Zone’', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midwestern States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi River', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T11:21:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kelly Slivka', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kelly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Slivka', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e4cdfb2-4405-5c44-ac55-f365b985a56b', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e4cdfb2-4405-5c44-ac55-f365b985a56b'}, {'abstract': 'Communities that lived and worked side by side now fear each other.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/in-assam-grim-aftermath-to-july-riots/', 'snippet': 'Communities that lived and worked side by side now fear each other.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KOKRAJHAR/CHIRANG, Assam — Almost two weeks after their village was burned by rioters, a group of Bodo men sneaked back to see the charred remains of their houses. All their livestock, except the pigs, were gone. “Right now, standing here, I am petrified,” said Kalidas Brahmo, a farmer, walking through the rubble of his home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Assam, Grim Aftermath to July Riots', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian National Congress', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T11:23:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Betwa Sharma', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Betwa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sharma', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9014007-c52e-53fa-b188-fe79ecd6382e', 'word_count': 1077, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9014007-c52e-53fa-b188-fe79ecd6382e'}, {'abstract': 'A new poll, which The Times got a first look at, suggests that voters in Maryland may well endorse its new same-sex marriage law.', 'web_url': 'https://bruni.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/hopeful-news-from-maryland/', 'snippet': 'A new poll, which The Times got a first look at, suggests that voters in Maryland may well endorse its new same-sex marriage law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new poll of Maryland voters, who will get to decide in November whether to overrule recently signed legislation establishing same-sex marriage in the state, shows that 54 percent favor the law, while 40 percent oppose it. These findings, by Hart Research Associates, will be released publicly later today; The Times was given an advance look at them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hopeful News From Maryland', 'kicker': 'Frank Bruni', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellner, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T11:45:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91401965-5e29-5514-a014-4b052c902235', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91401965-5e29-5514-a014-4b052c902235'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/morning-take-out-539/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOP STORIES ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T1