an Tyler Clary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Live: Live Coverage From Olympic Swimming', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clijsters, Kim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douglas, Gabby', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franklin, Missy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isner, John', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lochte, Ryan', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phelps, Michael', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharapova, Maria', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soni, Rebecca', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsonga, Jo-Wilfried', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whipple, Mary', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T12:38:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4275b129-dde3-5c05-a816-4c7db01c27d5', 'word_count': 4266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4275b129-dde3-5c05-a816-4c7db01c27d5'}, {'abstract': 'States like Delaware, which embraced gambling early, are allowing new types of gaming in a struggle to make up for the revenue lost to the casinos of their cash-hungry neighbors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/us/gambling-boom-leaves-states-struggling-to-catch-up.html', 'snippet': 'States like Delaware, which embraced gambling early, are allowing new types of gaming in a struggle to make up for the revenue lost to the casinos of their cash-hungry neighbors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cash-hungry states have long tried to poach business from one another. Now many are stepping up their efforts to lure gamblers from their neighbors to their growing ranks of slot machines, leaving states like Delaware, which embraced gambling early, struggling to keep up in what has become a feverish one-armed-bandit arms race.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/us/GAMBLING-2/GAMBLING-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/us/GAMBLING-2/GAMBLING-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/us/GAMBLING-2/GAMBLING-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/03/us/GAMBLING-2/GAMBLING-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/us/GAMBLING-2/GAMBLING-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'States Up the Ante in