overage, Sony reports declining profit in the quarter, and a look at branded headphones used by Olympic competitors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The F.B.I.’s hunt for leakers among the government’s national security agencies has cast a chill over media coverage of those issues, Scott Shane reports, with the agencies declining interview requests or background briefings. At the same time, the Senate is considering legislation meant to limit intelligence officials’ exchanges with reporters; that bill has been criticized by intelligence veterans and civil libertarians fear as counterproductive and raising constitutional questions. The criminal investigation was prompted by, among others, recent media disclosures on American cyberattacks on Iran and the so-called “kill list” of terrorist suspects approved for drone strikes. The reports were published by The New York Times, The Associated Press, Newsweek and other outlets, as well as in recent books by reporters for Newsweek and The Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Hunting for Leakers, and Olympic Spotlight on Headphones', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T13:08:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e51fa63-8111-5f85-97f4-c960e6ba3b82', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e51fa63-8111-5f85-97f4-c960e6ba3b82'}, {'abstract': 'The merits of dieting versus exercise when trying to lose weight, Google Wallet now works with multiple credit cards, simple home surveillance that offers peace of mind and other consumer-focused news from today’s Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/thursday-reading-dieting-vs-exercise-for-weight-loss/', 'snippet': 'The merits of dieting versus exercise when trying to lose weight, Google Wallet now works with multiple credit cards, simple home surveillance that offers peace of mind and other consumer-focused news from today’s Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and on our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday Reading: Dieting vs. Exercise for Weight Loss', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T13:09:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97dfa2fa-e8db-5c1c-adb9-eebf364fa936', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97dfa2fa-e8db-5c1c-adb9-eebf364fa936'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: Initially rejected in 1936, a story by F. Scott Fitzgerald is running in the current issue of The New Yorker.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/dismissed-as-too-fantastic-a-fitzgerald-story-gets-another-chance/', 'snippet': 'The Day: Initially rejected in 1936, a story by F. Scott Fitzgerald is running in the current issue of The New Yorker.', 'lead_paragraph': ' If you’re the sort who sees no reason to avoid clichés like the plague, you could do worse than to trot out the one about how there are no second acts in American lives. That was from F. Scott Fitzgerald. It is used and misused a lot, commonly to mean that there are no second chances, which may not be quite what Fitzgerald had in mind, especially considering that his most enduring work, “The Great Gatsby,” is about a man who reinvents himself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dismissed as ‘Too Fantastic,’ a Fitzgerald Story Gets Another Chance', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fitzgerald, F Scott', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Treisman, Deborah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorker', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T13:10:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64043607-a7db-50e4-8772-cb65b3815337', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64043607-a7db-50e4-8772-cb65b3815337'}, {'abstract': 'The ECB disappoints, big time.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/this-isnt-the-draghi-youre-looking-for/', 'snippet': 'The ECB disappoints, big time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update: Rumor is that the ECB is actually going to do more than Draghi seemed to say. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Isn’t The Draghi You’re Looking For', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T13:11:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92fdc9ee-2202-558c-97a9-e1ca719d51d4', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92fdc9ee-2202-558c-97a9-e1ca719d51d4'}, {'abstract': 'The vast numbers of ‘‘ni-nis’’ are far from undecided voters. They’ve made up their minds: They despise both President Hugo Chávez and the opposition.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/a-broad-swath-of-the-venezuelan-electorate-refuses-to-pick-a-side/', 'snippet': 'The vast numbers of ‘‘ni-nis’’ are far from undecided voters. They’ve made up their minds: They despise both President Hugo Chávez and the opposition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTREAL — “How do you imagine the voter who will decide this election?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela’s Elusive Voters', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T13:12:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francisco Toro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francisco', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0da3392-0bdf-5bd9-bc8f-14b3c8a98d82', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0da3392-0bdf-5bd9-bc8f-14b3c8a98d82'}, {'abstract': 'There have been enough horror stories about frozen PayPal accounts to make some companies think twice about using the service, Brian X. Chen reports on Thursday in The New York Times. The victims include individual sellers, start-up companies, creative artists and impromptu philanthropists.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/daily-report-paypal-measures-cause-trouble-for-start-ups/', 'snippet': 'There have been enough horror stories about frozen PayPal accounts to make some companies think twice about using the service, Brian X. Chen reports on Thursday in The New York Times. The victims include individual sellers, start-up companies, cre...', 'lead_paragraph': 'There have been enough horror stories about frozen PayPal accounts to make some companies think twice about using the service, Brian X. Chen reports on Thursday in The New York Times. The victims include individual sellers, start-up companies, creative artists and impromptu philanthropists. They all had to scramble when PayPal decided to hold on to their money longer than expected.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank