yle semifinal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking for a Different Gear in the 50 Free', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adrian, Nathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ervin, Anthony', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Gary Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Cullen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lochte, Ryan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Magnussen, James', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T13:16:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/921ac945-8baa-5451-be0e-3dfffbc6fafb', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/921ac945-8baa-5451-be0e-3dfffbc6fafb'}, {'abstract': 'Apollo Global Management said on Thursday that profit tumbled by 84 percent in the second quarter, as its core private equity business grappled with difficult markets.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/apollos-2nd-quarter-profit-falls-84/', 'snippet': 'Apollo Global Management said on Thursday that profit tumbled by 84 percent in the second quarter, as its core private equity business grappled with difficult markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apollo Global Management said Thursday that its profit tumbled by 84 percent in the second quarter, as its core private equity business grappled with difficult markets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apollo’s 2nd-Quarter Profit Falls 84%', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Black, Leon D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apollo Global Management', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T13:18:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b98dc703-d762-55fb-b2c8-82ac722ab388', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b98dc703-d762-55fb-b2c8-82ac722ab388'}, {'abstract': 'India’s English-language media pummels the government after this week’s blackouts.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/newswallah-the-government-is-broken/', 'snippet': 'India’s English-language media pummels the government after this week’s blackouts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The massive scale of this week’s blackout in India, which left 684 million without electricity, has galvanized the country’s already critical English-language media.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: The Government Is Broken', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Outages and Blackouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hazare, Anna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Policy Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Onion, The', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Open (Magazine)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Times of India', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T13:32:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b26456db-5db7-5a88-a379-9462fbd517c8', 'word_count': 584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b26456db-5db7-5a88-a379-9462fbd517c8'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s standing in the FiveThirtyEight forecast reached its strongest position to date on Tuesday as a result of favorable polls in a set of swing states.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/aug-1-obama-extends-electoral-college-advantage/', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s standing in the FiveThirtyEight forecast reached its strongest position to date on Tuesday as a result of favorable polls in a set of swing states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barack Obama’s standing in the FiveThirtyEight forecast reached its strongest position to date on Tuesday as a result of favorable polls in a set of swing states. The forecast model now gives Mr. Obama a 70.8 percent chance of winning the Electoral College, up from 69.0 percent on Monday and from 65.0 percent last Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 1: Obama Extends Electoral College Advantage', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T13:44:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15d67b59-3b9d-5df4-a9b3-ad39fcfcd97b', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15d67b59-3b9d-5df4-a9b3-ad39fcfcd97b'}, {'abstract': 'Just in time for the Democratic National Convention in Charlotte, N.C., the city starts a bicycle-sharing program, said to be the largest in the Southeast.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/for-delegates-in-a-hurry-the-bike-lane-beckons/', 'snippet': 'Just in time for the Democratic National Convention in Charlotte, N.C., the city starts a bicycle-sharing program, said to be the largest in the Southeast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just in time for the Democratic National Convention in Charlotte next month, the city has started offering a bicycle-sharing program that it says is the largest in the Southeast. Charlotte B-cycle, part of the Wisconsin-based B-cycle national network, comprises 200 commuter-style bicycles at 20 stations uptown (Charlotte’s downtown) and nearby. Most of the stops are near bus, shuttle and light-rail stops.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Delegates in a Hurry, The Bike Lane Beckons', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charlotte (NC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T13:57:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diane Daniel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Daniel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cd2d07c-df1a-5304-9387-1567ada9aa05', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cd2d07c-df1a-5304-9387-1567ada9aa05'}, {'abstract': 'Spanish officials announced the arrest of three suspects who were believed to have been planning attacks in Spain and elsewhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/world/europe/3-arrested-in-spain-are-accused-of-having-links-to-al-qaeda.html', 'snippet': 'Spanish officials announced the arrest of three suspects who were believed to have been planning attacks in Spain and elsewhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — The Spanish government said on Thursday that it had arrested three men suspected of having links to Al Qaeda and believed to have been planning attacks in Europe.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/us/03spain/03spain-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legac