rkers in Houston.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/theater/bullet-for-adolf-by-woody-harrelson-and-frankie-hyman.html', 'snippet': 'Woody Harrelson and Frankie Hyman, who together wrote the play “Bullet for Adolf,” started their friendship as construction workers in Houston.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WORKING construction in Houston one sweltering morning during the summer of 1983, Frankie Hyman overheard the site supervisor chastising another employee for arriving two hours late. When he heard an easy, drawling voice retort, “What are you talking about, I’m usually the first one in and the last to leave,” a claim that “definitely was not the case,” Mr. Hyman chuckled and decided that “I liked this guy, and I hadn’t even met him yet.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/arts/05WOODY2/05WOODY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/arts/05WOODY2/05WOODY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/arts/05WOODY2/05WOODY2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/arts/05WOODY2/05WOODY2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/arts/05WOODY2/05WOODY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/arts/05WOODY2/05WOODY2-thumbStand