splash themselves with pool water before a race; others sip it. But pre-competition rituals are common, and for various reasons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Swimmers awaiting their races on the pool deck at the Olympic aquatics center in London all have their particular routines. Michael Phelps hides behind huge headphones. Cesar Cielo of Brazil thumps his chest like Tarzan. The Australian Stephanie Rice presses on her goggles four times. A full set of shakes, rattles and rolls goes on in those tense minutes before swimmers mount the blocks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Splashing or Sipping, but Tasting the Pool Before the Swim', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitajima, Kosuke', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Larson, Breeja', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meilutyte, Ruta', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phelps, Michael', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Stephanie', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steffen, Britta', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T15:55:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lela Moore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf2451f0-f68