n', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sloan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c6dce73-289c-5b50-bfa0-fe394cd01655', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c6dce73-289c-5b50-bfa0-fe394cd01655'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time in 17 years, “GMA” last week defeated “Today” not only in total viewers, but also among viewers between the ages of 25 and 54. Lucky for “Today,” the Olympics will boost its viewership.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/just-before-olympics-good-morning-america-takes-crown-away-from-today/', 'snippet': 'For the first time in 17 years, “GMA” last week defeated “Today” not only in total viewers, but also among viewers between the ages of 25 and 54. Lucky for “Today,” the Olympics will boost its viewership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last shred of morning television dominance owned by NBC’s “Today” show came crashing down last week as ABC’s “Good Morning America” won the ratings across the board, even among the group of viewers most prized by news advertisers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just Before Olympics, ‘Good Morning America’ Takes Crown Away From ‘Today’', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curry, Ann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guthrie, Savannah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T16:15:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': 