 theater: To give audiences views of things they’ve never seen before, great actors and actresses go out on a limb.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s begin by acknowledging that all actors, especially stage actors, are brave. It takes guts as well as vanity to unpack your heart in front of a live audience.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: Guts and Glory, Onstage', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T17:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By BEN BRANTLEY', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'BRANTLEY', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fb1fd76-d04f-5c68-b432-990feebecc79', 'word_count': 1322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fb1fd76-d04f-5c68-b432-990feebecc79'}, {'abstract': 'The memories of many recent veterans cover much more ground than Post-Traumatic Stress or Traumatic Brain Injury. Even so, it can be hard to tease out a few moments of a fonder kind.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/in-war-moments-worth-remembering/', 'snippet': 'The memories of many recent veterans cover much more ground than Post-Traumatic Stress or Traumatic Brain Injury. Even so, it can be hard to tease out a few moments of a fonder kind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Iraq invaded Kuwait on Aug. 2, 1990; hard to believe there were any good days in the two decades since. How could there be? I have told my war stories both as an embedded journalist and an Army veteran of Desert Storm. When I say “Iraq,” it is only violence that is remembered.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In War, Moments Worth Remembering', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_hea