arter.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/directv-reports-its-first-drop-in-u-s-subscribers/', 'snippet': 'The company said it more than made up for the loss by adding subscribers in Latin America. Over all, DirecTV reported a 1.4 percent increase in net income, to $711 million, for the second quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DirecTV on Thursday reported its first drop in net subscribers to its service in the United States, highlighting the challenges for pay television providers in a saturated marketplace.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DirecTV Reports Its First Drop in U.S. Subscribers', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Michael D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DirecTV', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T17:14:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51b94bd4-da37-58ad-b045-4ec6f3887dac', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51b94bd4-da37-58ad-b045-4ec6f3887dac'}, {'abstract': 'Signers of a petition argued that it was inappropriate for Madonna to perform in Warsaw on the anniversary of the revolt against the Nazis.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/after-protest-madonna-shows-clip-of-warsaw-uprising-at-concert/', 'snippet': 'Signers of a petition argued that it was inappropriate for Madonna to perform in Warsaw on the anniversary of the revolt against the Nazis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Responding to critics in Poland, Madonna showed a World War II-era newsreel about the Warsaw Uprising against the Nazis during her concert on Wednesday in the city on the anniversary of that 1944 revolt, Agence France-Presse reported.\xa0 Thousands of fans applauded as the two-and-a-half minute film played.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Protest, Madonna Shows Clip of Warsaw Uprising at Concert', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Le Pen, Marine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madonna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Front (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Warsaw (Poland)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T17:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d47aede-d178-5a52-98ba-e16cb4069694', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d47aede-d178-5a52-98ba-e16cb4069694'}, {'abstract': 'The Paris-based baker Eric Kayser is best known for his breads.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/maison-kayser-a-global-baker-touches-down-in-new-york/', 'snippet': 'The Paris-based baker Eric Kayser is best known for his breads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A global chain of artisanal bakeries sounds like an oxymoron. But that’s precisely what Eric Kayser has created since he opened his little boulangerie on Rue Monge near the Sorbonne in Paris in 1996. Now his first bakery-cafe in New York is set to open on Wednesday, and leases have been signed for two more. Like his other Maison Kayser establishments, including some 20 in the Paris area, 22 in Japan and scores of others in Europe, Asia and the Middle East, the new bakery on the Upper East Side has bakers who were trained in his Paris headquarters. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maison Kayser, a Global Baker, Touches Down in New York', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Food Stuff: A Touch of Sourdough', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T17:19:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a49e83a-e4f7-5a44-a3bf-da75ba25c507', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a49e83a-e4f7-5a44-a3bf-da75ba25c507'}, {'abstract': 'A lack of new stimulus moves by the Federal Reserve and the European Central Bank this week may have a direct and painful impact on the chief source of revenue at investment banks on both sides of the Atlantic.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/for-wall-street-real-pain-when-the-fed-fails-to-act/', 'snippet': 'A lack of new stimulus moves by the Federal Reserve and the European Central Bank this week may have a direct and painful impact on the chief source of revenue at investment banks on both sides of the Atlantic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Looks like the central bankers just destroyed Wall Street’s 2012 bonus season. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Wall Street, Real Pain When the Fed Fails to Act', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quantitative Easing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T17:24:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6fb8e20-af2f-59d8-a1fb-9154f69d1dcf', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6fb8e20-af2f-59d8-a1fb-9154f69d1dcf'}, {'abstract': 'The four badminton teams that were disqualified Wednesday simply looked at the information presented to them and went in the direction that seemed to have the best chance of leading them to their goal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/sports/olympics/olympic-badminton-teams-had-right-idea-by-losing.html', 'snippet': 'The four badminton teams that were disqualified Wednesday simply looked at the information presented to them and went in the direction that seemed to have the best chance of leading them to their goal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Abby Wambach, the veteran forward on the United Sta