'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ithaca College', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northeastern States (US)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T17:29:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bc06940-d857-5e64-9823-0fc7f11424bd', 'word_count': 2717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bc06940-d857-5e64-9823-0fc7f11424bd'}, {'abstract': 'Antwerp’s outlet for exquisite footwear finds a home in one of the city’s best-loved boutiques.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/shoe-news-coccodrillo-comes-to-verso/', 'snippet': 'Antwerp’s outlet for exquisite footwear finds a home in one of the city’s best-loved boutiques.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Between the many talented designers who’ve sprung from its Royal Academy of Fine Arts and its refined retail scene, Antwerp qualifies as one of the most fashion-conscious cities in the world. That reputation has just been further corroborated with the opening of a Coccodrillo shoe salon at Verso. Coccodrillo is one of Europe’s most design-focused shoe shops (it even offers a yearly prize to a promising young student from the Academy); Verso, housed in a grand 16th-century town house, is one of the city’s most glamorous fashion boutiques. That they’ve come together makes for some of the best one-stop style shopping anywhere. “Until now Verso sold only shoes to the ready-to-wear customer to complete the outfit,” Geert Bruloot and Eddy Michiels, Coccodrillo’s founders, told The Moment via e-mail from Belgium. “We want to move towards a more independent shoe store.” Which means upping the ante on more adventurous designs: nestled among this fall’s lace pump by Dolce & Gabbana and glossy velvet slippers by Giuseppe Zanotti are curvy booties by the Turkish designer Burak Uyan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shoe News | Coccodrillo Comes to Verso', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T17:30:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy MacDonell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37ef5923-1d5d-5106-b4e9-6436264275dc', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37ef5923-1d5d-5106-b4e9-6436264275dc'}, {'abstract': 'The doctor, an expert in robotics and minimally invasive surgery, used a camera disguised as a pen to shoot the video in the Union Square station, prosecutors said.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/urologist-charged-with-shooting-video-up-skirt-in-subway/', 'snippet': 'The doctor, an expert in robotics and minimally invasive surgery, used a camera disguised as a pen to shoot the video in the Union Square station, prosecutors said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 5:56 p.m. | A urologist at Mount Sinai Medical Center was arraigned Thursday on charges of taking videos up the skirt of a woman at the Union Square subway station during the evening rush hour on Wednesday, the Manhattan district attorney’s office said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Urologist Charged With Shooting Video