eight-of-partisan-bickering/', 'snippet': 'Partisanship kills a Senate bill that would have allowed private companies to share information with the government on cybersecurity threats to critical infrastructure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No amount of death-and-destruction talk about the prospects of cyberattacks on the nation’s nuclear power plants and water systems could override the intense partisanship on Capitol Hill.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cybersecurity Bill Dies Under Weight of Partisan Bickering', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T18:41:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d4981d0-27bb-5beb-ad93-e0257800036b', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d4981d0-27bb-5beb-ad93-e0257800036b'}, {'abstract': 'Off to the seven seas.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/im-outta-here/', 'snippet': 'Off to the seven seas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Note to the Europeans: you cannot have a crisis for the next couple of weeks, because I’m going on a long-scheduled family vacation — probably without internet access most of the time. Please wait until the last week of the month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I’m Outta Here', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T18:45:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77c26f13-11b9-553a-a1de-d08739b14a4d', 'word_count': 41, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77c26f13-11b9-553a-a1de-d08739b14a4d'}, {'abstract': 'Should we just accept that when you buy a new computer, you should buy it for what it does now, and learn not to resent the fact that, inevitably, there will be better, faster, cheaper computers in the future?', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/apple-airplay-and-the-window-of-obsolescence/', 'snippet': 'Should we just accept that when you buy a new computer, you should buy it for what it does now, and learn not to resent the fact that, inevitably, there will be better, faster, cheaper computers in the future?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anytime there’s a new operating system, there’s somebody who complains. Usually, the new OS “breaks” some older piece of software. Or maybe your printer won’t work after the upgrade. Something.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple AirPlay and the Window of Obsolescence', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T18:46:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58041119-3f71-5c12-a69e-df2791dc2612', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58041119-3f71-5c12-a69e-df2791dc2612'}, {'abstract': 'About 500 residents of Needham, Mass., gathered for an “Aly Rally” in support of Aly Raisman’s effort in the women’s all-around competition.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/raismans-hometown-rallies-from-across-the-pond/', 'snippet': 'About 500 residents of Needham, Mass., gathered for an “Aly Rally” in support of Aly Raisman’s effort in the women’s all-around competition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEEDHAM, Mass. — At the “Aly Rally” in Aly Raisman’s hometown Thursday, a crowd of about 500 fans packed into a flag- and balloon-filled town hall to root her on from across the Atlantic Ocean.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Raisman’s Hometown Rallies From Across the Pond', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gymnastics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raisman, Aly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T18:51:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dina Kraft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kraft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fd1425b-5053-55bc-86c7-c915eb07256b', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fd1425b-5053-55bc-86c7-c915eb07256b'}, {'abstract': 'On view will be highlights of the Paley holdings, including Picasso’s famous 1905-6 painting “Boy Leading a Horse’’ and Gauguin’s “Seed of the Areoi” from 1892.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/paley-art-collection-heading-to-the-de-young-fine-arts-museums-in-san-francisco/', 'snippet': 'On view will be highlights of the Paley holdings, including Picasso’s famous 1905-6 painting “Boy Leading a Horse’’ and Gauguin’s “Seed of the Areoi” from 1892.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The staggering art collection put together by William S. Paley, the television impresario who founded the Columbia Broadcasting System, first went on view at the Museum of Modern Art in 1992. Paley, a longtime trustee at MoMA, had left his paintings, drawings and sculptures to the museum upon his death in 1990. After MoMA showed the collection it then traveled to museums in Indianapolis, Seattle, Los Angeles, San Diego and Baltimore. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paley Art Collection Heading to the de Young Fine Arts Museums in San Francisco', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paley, William S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fine Arts Museums of San Francisco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Portland Museum of Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T18:57:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86fb4099-a302-5d8b-bc3c-a7eb96904251', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86fb4099-a302-5d8b-bc3c-a7eb96904251'}, {'abstract': 'Rebecca Soni became the first woman ever to break the 2:20 barrier with a clocking of 2 minutes 19.59 seconds, successfully defending her gold medal in the event from the Beijing Games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/sports/olympics/soni-first-repeat-winner-in-swimming-franklin.html', 'snippet': 'Rebecca Soni became the first woman ever to break the 2:20 barrier with a clocking of 2 minutes 19.59 seconds, successfully defending her gold medal in the event from the Beijing Games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Swimming is in the world’s viewfinder for only one summer every four years, during the Olympics. For those who pour their sweat, blood and fears into the sport, the stakes and the stress can be suffocating. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/sports/olympics/02soni_olyblog/02soni_olyblog-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/02/sports/olympics/02soni_olyblog/02soni_olyblog-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/sports/olympics/02soni_olyblog/02soni_olyblog-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/02/sports/olympics/02soni_olyblog/02soni_olyblog-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'sup