d medal during the opening day of track cycling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/sports/olympics/03iht-olybritain03.html', 'snippet': 'There were cheers, boos, world records, relegations and a fifth career gold medal during the opening day of track cycling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — On the first day of track cycling, one of the Olympic diversions that the British now find most diverting, it was sometimes difficult to distinguish the faster from the slower, the triumphant from the thwarted.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/sports/olympics/03olybritain-hoy/03olybritain-hoy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/sports/olympics/03olybritain-hoy/03olybritain-hoy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1509, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Briton Emerges From Velodrome’s Chaos With a 5th Gold', 'kicker': 'Track Cycling | Team Sprint     ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Briton Emerges From Velodrome’s Chaos With a 5th Gold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Records and Achievements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cycling, Track', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoy, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T19:07:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aad778bb-383f-56c4-9c01-71552c9e85a2', 'word_count': 1192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aad778bb-383f-56c4-9c01-71552c9e85a2'}, {'abstract': 'We asked Ronen Bergman to look back on his article, “Will Israel Attack Iran?” and tell us whether he thinks an attack will still happen in 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/past-forward-on-the-possibility-of-israel-attacking-iran/', 'snippet': 'We asked Ronen Bergman to look back on his article, “Will Israel Attack Iran?” and tell us whether he thinks an attack will still happen in 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In last weekend’s issue, Ronen Bergman wrote about the mystery surrounding the Aleppo Codex: the oldest, most complete version of the Hebrew Bible, whose ownership has been in dispute since it was completed in A.D. 930. Considering the persistent tensions over Iran’s nuclear ambitions — the most recent round of sanctions against Iran imposed by the United States and the European Union was approved yesterday — it made sense that From the Archives would highlight Bergman’s previous story for the magazine, “Will Israel Attack Iran?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Past Forward: On the Possibility of Israel Attacking Iran', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T19:09:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maya Lau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df10b38a-6073-54a6-8e97-d522690fce88', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df10b38a-6073-54a6-8e97-d522690fce88'}, {'abstract': 'The show was last seen in New York in 1987.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/sondheims-marry-me-a-little-returning-to-new-york/', 'snippet': 'The show was last seen in New York in 1987.', 'lead_paragraph': ' “Marry Me a Little,” a Stephen Sondheim musical that hasn’t been performed in New York in 25 years, will begin the Keen Company’s 2012-13 season next month. The Off Broadway production, with previews beginning at the Clurman Theater on Sept. 11 and an opening night set for Oct. 2, includes songs that, producers say, have never been performed on a New York stage before, most notably “Rainbows,” from an as yet unmade film version of “Into the Woods.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sondheim’s ‘Marry Me a Little’ Returning to New York', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Sondheim Show Returns to New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lucas, Craig', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rene, Norman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silverstein, Jonathan (Theater Director)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sondheim, Stephen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Keen Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T19:09:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': No