who is remembered posthumously by former acquaintances. Possible scenes of her life are re-enacted in mostly wordless quasi-dream sequences in which Zawe Ashton portrays her as a grown-up, and Alix Luka-Cain plays her as a wistful, wide-eyed child. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03DREAMS_SPAN/03DREAMS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03DREAMS_SPAN/03DREAMS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03DREAMS_SPAN/DREAMS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03DREAMS_SPAN/DREAMS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1448, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03DREAMS_SPAN/03DREAMS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03DREAMS_SPAN/03DREAMS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03DREAMS_SPAN/03DREAMS_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lost to Her Friends, but There All the Time', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lost to Her Friends, But There All the Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morley, Carol', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T20:44:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b54f540-0790-5c52-b631-63ac43fbf7c7', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b54f540-0790-5c52-b631-63ac43fbf7c7'}, {'abstract': 'In her Olympics blog, Heather O’Reilly of the United States women’s soccer team writes about visiting Old Trafford, home of Manchester United.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/the-soccer-chronicles-between-matches-a-hallowed-english-stadium/', 'snippet': 'In her Olympics blog, Heather O’Reilly of the United States women’s soccer team writes about visiting Old Trafford, home of Manchester United.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heather O’Reilly, a midfielder on the United States women’s soccer team and a two-time gold medalist, will be writing regularly for the 2012 London Olympics blog. This is her fifth post.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Soccer Chronicles: Between Matches, a Hallowed English Stadium', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T20:48:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': "By Heather O'Reilly", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Reilly", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79864887-4385-515f-962b-d91b8774b37a', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79864887-4385-515f-962b-d91b8774b37a'}, {'abstract': 'David Pogue’s iPhone was stolen. After he let the world know on Twitter, a search ensued. Here’s his story.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/where-is-david-pogues-phone/', 'snippet': 'David Pogue’s iPhone was stolen. After he let the world know on Twitter, a search ensued. Here’s his story.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:58 p.m. | Updated  Not to ruin a good tale, but the phone was recovered.On Monday night, I was taking the Amtrak train home from a “Nova” shoot in Philadelphia — exhausted, but happy to have power and Wi-Fi for my laptop.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Is David Pogue’s iPhone?', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pogue, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': "Prince George's County (Md)", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T20:50:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26466e82-d359-5aa9-880f-2e8e3a0f3a23', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26466e82-d359-5aa9-880f-2e8e3a0f3a23'}, {'abstract': 'In “Free Radicals: A History of Experimental Film,” Pip Chodorov offers an enthusiastic, accessible look at the genre’s big names.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/movies/free-radicals-by-pip-chodorov-on-experimental-film.html', 'snippet': 'In “Free Radicals: A History of Experimental Film,” Pip Chodorov offers an enthusiastic, accessible look at the genre’s big names.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the loss of several admired avant-garde filmmakers in the past few years, “Free Radicals: A History of Experimental Film” arrives as a welcome paean to the unfettered, resourceful creativity of its subject. Despite the scope of the title, this friendly, colorful documentary from Pip Chodorov is not the last word on all the shapes, sizes and languages of experimental film, but rather an introduction brightened by a companionable enthusiasm and an apposite sense of community.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03FREEALT/FREEALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03FREEALT/FREEALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03FREEALT/FREEALT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03FREEALT/FREEALT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1535, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '