he Truth', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Freewheelin’: Bob Dylan, Jonah Lehrer and the Truth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dylan, Bob', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lehrer, Jonah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Imagine: How Creativity Works (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorker', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T20:56:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Kinney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kinney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/055e9a56-f19a-522d-8870-f4a5c08741d1', 'word_count': 1160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/055e9a56-f19a-522d-8870-f4a5c08741d1'}, {'abstract': 'A Tax Policy Center study shows that the candidate’s plan would lead to higher taxes on middle- and lower-income earners.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/romneys-tax-hike/', 'snippet': 'A Tax Policy Center study shows that the candidate’s plan would lead to higher taxes on middle- and lower-income earners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Romney campaign’s increasingly desperate attempts to dismiss a new study of its tax plan are a pretty good sign that the study is devastating. That isn’t to say the campaign is trying to counter it with actual specifics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Tax Hike', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tax Policy Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T20:58:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9e1067f-e4ad-5ed3-9a55-7534600b585b', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9e1067f-e4ad-5ed3-9a55-7534600b585b'}, {'abstract': 'Students at an education conference said it was time to tear down the wall between their digital lives outside of school and in school, where much access to technology is restricted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/08/02/students-urge-teachers-to-embrace-digital-tools/', 'snippet': 'Students at an education conference said it was time to tear down the wall between their digital lives outside of school and in school, where much access to technology is restricted.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Students Urge Teachers to Embrace Digital Tools', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T21:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By HITEN SAMTANI', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiten', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SAMTANI', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/185864cc-ba5e-5e72-b76e-1250193f0aa6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/185864cc-ba5e-5e72-b76e-1250193f0aa6'}, {'abstract': 'Last week’s opening of the store Eureka Beach on Main Street in Greenport will give the area a much-needed retail boost.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/high-style-on-the-north-fork/', 'snippet': 'Last week’s opening of the store Eureka Beach on Main Street in Greenport will give the area a much-needed retail boost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The North Fork of Long Island has many attributes — great wines, (relatively) affordable summer rentals and a lovely carousel — but shopping has never been the area’s strong suit. Last week’s opening of Eureka Beach on Main Street in Greenport will give the area a much-needed retail boost. The brainchild of the fashion designer Lucy Barnes, the television producer Heidi Kelso and the antiques dealer Fran Lombardi-Reilly, the shop reflects the trio’s personalities and specialties, with offerings ranging from new and vintage women’s clothing and accessories to children’s items and decorative accessories for the home. The opening also marks the debut of the Eureka Beach collection of caftans, tunics and dresses. “We created the line because while there are other things out there, they were just too expensive for what you’d get,” Kelso explains. “Ours are cotton, linen and silk pieces that aren’t too precious and aren’t too expensive.” The line, which ranges from $100 to $350, hangs alongside pieces by Barnes (look for the stretch denim “Miracle skirt”), jewelry by the North Fork weekender Paige Novick, Chascona bags by the stylist Karan Schijman, Riudavets summery leather slip-ons, children’s clothing by Wovenplay and textiles from Bali, Turkey and Morocco. Prices start at about $15 for a simple bangle and top out at $750 for a Moroccan blanket adorned with paillettes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'High Style on the North Fork', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T21:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31a46936-8854-5e0e-bd58-c67e85310c5d', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31a46936-8854-5e0e-bd58-c67e85310c5d'}, {'abstract': 'For a month when the economy routinely sheds a large number of jobs, seasonal adjustment is likely to provide a far different picture.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/beware-the-jobs-report-of-july/', 'snippet': 'For a month when the economy routinely sheds a large number of jobs, seasonal adjustment is likely to provide a far different picture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American economy almost certainly shed more than a million jobs last month, just as it does every July. But that’s not the “jobs number” that will get most of the attention when the Bureau of Labor Statistics speaks Friday morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beware the Jobs Report of July', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Labor Statistics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T21:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported'