sOpen 2012. As always, we’ll have four events leading up to an all-day hack day in December.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s that time of the year again! We’ve just released our schedule for TimesOpen 2012. As always, we’ll have four events leading up to an all-day hack day in December. Check out the details below and make sure to grab your ticket for this year’s first event: HTML5, Apps and JavaScript!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Announcing TimesOpen 2012', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T21:46:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Fiore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fiore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6d938d8-d59b-5127-ba78-b4972083962f', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6d938d8-d59b-5127-ba78-b4972083962f'}, {'abstract': 'At the Jacob’s Pillow Dance Festival, two premieres are part of a three-piece work, “Curtain,” choreographed by Jonah Bokaer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/arts/dance/jonah-bokaer-at-jacobs-pillow-dance-festival.html', 'snippet': 'At the Jacob’s Pillow Dance Festival, two premieres are part of a three-piece work, “Curtain,” choreographed by Jonah Bokaer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BECKET, Mass. — Jonah Bokaer is one of the mystery men of American dance. In 2000, when he joined the Merce Cunningham Dance Company in his teens (the youngest performer in its history), he made an immediate impression: both subdued and intense, alert and unfathomable, quietly graceful and utterly focused. It’s hard to forget the unnerving way he stood in the opening tableau of Cunningham’s “Way Station” (2001): fixed, like a doll, dark eyes gazing at the audience with no apparent blink. In movement, his gifts of control and changing dynamics were riveting.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03BOKAER1_SPAN/03BOKAER1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03BOKAER1_SPAN/03BOKAER1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03BOKAER1_SPAN/BOKAER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03BOKAER1_SPAN/BOKAER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03BOKAER1_SPAN/03BOKAER1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03BOKAER1_SPAN/03BOKAER1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03BOKAER1_SPAN/03BOKAER1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Exploring The Space With Stillness', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exploring The Space With Stillness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bokaer, Jonah', 'rank': 1, 'major':