rt of the lending process, the other just before closing.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/realestate/05mort-graphic/05mort-graphic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 292, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/realestate/05mort-graphic/05mort-graphic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 292}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/realestate/05mort-graphic/05mort-graphic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 577, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/realestate/05mort-graphic/05mort-graphic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1154, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/realestate/05mort-graphic/05mort-graphic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/realestate/05mort-graphic/05mort-graphic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/realestate/05mort-graphic/05mort-graphic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Simplifying Loan Documents', 'kicker': 'Mortgages', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Simplifying Loan Documents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T21:58:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vickie Elmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vickie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2594cf86-1668-5ea3-9044-928a41b23553', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2594cf86-1668-5ea3-9044-928a41b23553'}, {'abstract': 'Fernando Meirelles’s “360,” with Anthony Hopkins and Jude Law, is a multistrand narrative that follows an ensemble cast from Vienna to Phoenix, exploring the cause-and-effect nature in a string of affairs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/movies/360-with-anthony-hopkins-and-jude-law.html', 'snippet': 'Fernando Meirelles’s “360,” with Anthony Hopkins and Jude Law, is a multistrand narrative that follows an ensemble cast from Vienna to Phoenix, exploring the cause-and-effect nature in a string of affairs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A butterfly flapping its wings in Chile is a familiar culprit for all kinds of global havoc, like tornadoes in Texas. In the film “360,” though, it’s a woman taking her top off in Vienna who sets off a British man’s crisis of conscience, instigates a conjugal dispute in Paris, and obliquely stirs up funny business in Denver and some murderous business elsewhere. Here the world isn’t just small, it’s also a 360-degree metaphor that begins with a woman’s breasts, leads to the boulevard circling Vienna’s center and ends with the “O” of your slack-jawed incredulity.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag