isz, Rachel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hopkins, Anthony', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T22:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7191e979-1e08-57d7-a26d-134314d7d5a8', 'word_count': 648, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7191e979-1e08-57d7-a26d-134314d7d5a8'}, {'abstract': 'For its second season “The Franchise” shows, with an apparent lack of sugarcoating, the Miami Marlins on a losing streak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/arts/television/on-the-franchise-miami-marlins-flail-but-deliver.html', 'snippet': 'For its second season “The Franchise” shows, with an apparent lack of sugarcoating, the Miami Marlins on a losing streak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each episode of Showtime’s baseball documentary series, “The Franchise,” begins with bravado — a chorus of voices from the front office of the Miami Marlins declaring: “I’ll put this club up against anybody’s,” “When we wear this uniform we are family,” and “We are now ready to win.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03FRANCHISE1ALT_SPAN/03FRANCHISE1ALT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03FRANCHISE1ALT_SPAN/03FRANCHISE1ALT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/arts/03FRANCHISE1ALT_SPAN/FRANCHISE1ALT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 5