 are Americans still willing to make in the name of national security?', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/as-the-wars-ebb-considering-security-at-home/', 'snippet': 'More than a decade after the 9/11 attacks, what sacrifices are Americans still willing to make in the name of national security?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On At War, we mostly deal with military engagements aboard, rather than national security issues on the home front. But we want to point out a piece by At War contributor Scott Shane (@ScottShaneNYT) on The Agenda. Mr. Shane writes today about the trade-offs between security and civil liberties going into the presidential campaign. The fallout from 9/11 saw a monumental shift both in the way the government approached counterterrorism domestically, and how it executed it internationally through Iraq and Afghanistan. But the United States has, mostly, withdrawn from Iraq. And the exit from Afghanistan, though its speed will surely be an issue of debate in the campaign, is no doubt hastening. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As the Wars Ebb, Considering Security at Home', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-02T22:28:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffery DelViscio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffery', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DelViscio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d078fb3e-4bb1-5a3c-80dd-95416c01a9e4', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d078fb3e-4bb1-5a3c-80dd-95416c01a9e4'}, {'abstract': 'In summer, the city is a kaleidoscope of fractured color. Intense fluorescent shades of yellow and construction-netting orange make shoes and handbags pop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nyt