r peers hold political views that differ from ours, shouldn’t we reconsider our opinions? The author invites readers to help him make up his mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many proponents of the Affordable Care Act think there’s an overwhelming case for a government-supported expansion of medical coverage; opponents just as often think there’s an overwhelming case against.\xa0 Many people may think it’s a complicated issue on which those knowledgeable and reasonable may disagree.\xa0 But we don’t often hear from them in public debates.\xa0 The typical op-ed column or letter to the editor implies that anyone competent to judge the issue should agree with its view.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Political Disagreement', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T00:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Gutting', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gutting', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d5bc713-8b0d-5a89-b0a4-e7c76b979d53', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d5bc713-8b0d-5a89-b0a4-e7c76b979d53'}, {'abstract': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Thursday’s selection includes Facebook raising its estimate of the number of false accounts, a study showing a greater correlation between a company’s stock performance and the presence of women on its board and praise for a new note-taking app.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/02/todays-scuttlebot-a-cr