ed unprofitable routes and slashed pensions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Japan Airlines, the former flagship carrier driven to bankruptcy and a government bailout in 2010, will relist its stock here on Sept. 19 in an initial public offering that could raise $8.5 billion, the company said on Friday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JAL Plans an I.P.O. to Raise $8.5 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Airlines: Japan Airlines Plans To Relist Its Shares In Tokyo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Japan Airlines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T03:20:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/666216f4-33de-58c1-a91d-86c1b90c239e', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/666216f4-33de-58c1-a91d-86c1b90c239e'}, {'abstract': 'King Abdullah II met with Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta on Thursday to discuss the flood of refugees crossing the border from Syria and their concerns about securing Syria’s large stockpiles of chemical weapons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/world/middleeast/jordan-king-and-panetta-discuss-syria.html', 'snippet': 'King Abdullah II met with Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta on Thursday to discuss the flood of refugees crossing the border from Syria and their concerns about securing Syria’s large stockpiles of chemical weapons.', 'lead_paragraph': ' King Abdullah II met with Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta on Thursday to discuss the flood of refugees crossing the border from Syria and their concerns about securing Syria’s large stockpiles of chemical weapons. About 27,000 Syrian refugees have registered in Jordan, but the Jordanian government estimates that more than 140,000 Syrians have fled into the country in the past 10 months. American officials say that because of the escalating uprising against the government of President Bashar al-Assad, 1,000 Syrians are now crossing the border each day. Mr. Panetta pledged to continue the flow of American humanitarian aid and to work with Jordan and other countries in the region on plans to secure Syria’s weapons if the crisis worsens or the Assad government falls. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jordan: King and Panetta Discuss Syria', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jordan: King and Panetta Discuss Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panetta, Leon E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABDULLAH II, KING OF JORDAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T03:23:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Bumiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bumiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': Non