'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connell-Rodwell", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef2c325c-9245-55cb-8965-7606eea40fc1', 'word_count': 1003, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef2c325c-9245-55cb-8965-7606eea40fc1'}, {'abstract': 'Yes, there is a Cosmo for pretty much every country you can think of. Selling American friskiness has never been, like, so awesome.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/magazine/how-cosmo-conquered-the-world.html', 'snippet': 'Yes, there is a Cosmo for pretty much every country you can think of. Selling American friskiness has never been, like, so awesome.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few months ago, at the Tablao Villa Rosa, a tourist-friendly restaurant in Madrid, dozens of beautifully dressed women from all over the world were gathered around a stage taking cellphone pictures of a male flamenco dancer in tight pants. The women, whooping and clapping against the sides of their wine glasses, were editors, publishers and executives from the far-flung corners of the Cosmopolitan magazine universe — missionaries from the more established international Cosmos (Australia, France, Britain) and the newer, upstart Cosmos (Armenia, Azerbaijan, Mongolia, Vietnam and dozens of other countries). They gathered there at the biennial Cosmic Conference to soak up the Cosmo ethos (“Fun, fearless, female!”) and then went home to radiate it outward. One Cosmo staff member would tell me — in complete seriousness, having chosen her words carefully — that Cosmic was going to change my life.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05cosmo1/05cosmo1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 476, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05cosmo1/05cosmo1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 476}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05cosmo1/mag-05COSMO-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 471, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05cosmo1/mag-05COSMO-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 471, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05cosmo1/05cosmo1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05cosmo1/05cosmo1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05cosmo1/05cosmo1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 78, 'width': 78, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '99 Ways to Be Naughty in Kazakhstan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '99 Ways to be Naughty in Kazakhstan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Helen Gurley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hearst Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cosmopolitan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Kate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T11:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edith Zimmerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32fbe69c-49f0-5f6c-9efd-370a634b3eb1', 'word_count': 3990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32fbe69c-49f0-5f6c-9efd-370a634b3eb1'}, {'abstract': 'More small businesses are saving money by using Twitter and other sites to test their ideas before they invest in them.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/using-social-media-to-test-your-idea-before-you-try-to-sell-it/', 'snippet': 'More small businesses are saving money by using Twitter and other sites to test their ideas before they invest in them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When starting a business, new entrepreneurs often spend time naming the business and developing a logo and printing business cards and perfecting the look and feel of their packaging before they know whether they have a viable product or service. There’s now a better way — social media has become the ultimate tool for market research. Stephanie Clifford wrote an article for The Times this week about how big corporations are replacing focus groups with social media, but it works for small businesses, too.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Using Social Media to Test Your Idea Before You Try to Sell It', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google+', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T11:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melinda F. Emerson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melinda', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Emerson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32babee4-616c-5f6e-9b51-473b49f3ce74', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32babee4-616c-5f6e-9b51-473b49f3ce74'}, {'abstract': 'Our Summer Reading Contest is in its eighth week. Please come and post your answers to our question, and we’ll choose a favorite to feature on the blog at the end of each week.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/what-interested-you-most-in-the-times-this-week-13/', 'snippet': 'Our Summer Reading Contest is in its eighth week. Please come and post your answers to our question, and we’ll choose a favorite to feature on the blog at the end of each week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our Summer Reading Contest begins its eighth week. We’ll post the winner from week six on Aug. 6, and from week seven on Aug. 13. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Interested You Most in The Times This Week?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T11:20:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d091e89-f76d-59ea-8e0d-766fadfa8e46', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d091e89-f76d-59ea-8e0d-766fadfa8e46'}, {'abstract': 'The official and unofficial apps of the major theme parks can be very useful. Many are free.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/app-smart-extra-more-theme-parks/', 'snippet': 'The official and unofficial apps of the major theme parks can be very useful. Many are free.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s App Smart column was about theme park apps that try to give you useful information on more than one theme park at a time. These apps can be pretty useful, but there are many more theme parks than the ones listed in the apps. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'App Smart Extra: More Theme Parks', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMUSEMENT AND THEME PARKS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T11:22:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef8e3a4c-cb16-55dc-ad19-075775af4f9b', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef8e3a4c-cb16-55dc-ad19-075775af4f9b'}, {'abstract': 'Windows 7 includes a built-in tool for adding handwritten math expressions into documents.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/tip-of-the-week-doing-math-in-windows-7/', 'snippet': 'Windows 7 includes a built-in tool for adding handwritten math expressions into documents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adding mathematical equations to Microsoft Word can be an exercise in frustration, as many of the symbols used in the notation can be hard to find on the keyboard. Thanks to the Math Input Panel in Windows 7, the mathematical expressions can be written by hand with a mouse, digitizer pen or touch screen, converted to text and easily inserted into a Microsoft Word document — or any other program that supports Mathematical Markup Language.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Doing Math in Windows 7', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T11:25:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fe6eea3-3aa8-5891-b489-5a4895559aed', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fe6eea3-3aa8-5891-b489-5a4895559aed'}, {'abstract': 'Talking with the director of a film about Donald Trump’s new golf course in Scotland, constructed on dunes that local fought to protect.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/golf-course-vs-dunes-a-rebellion-that-failed/', 'snippet': 'Talking with the director of a film about Donald Trump’s new golf course in Scotland, constructed on dunes that local fought to protect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been six years since Donald Trump flew to northeastern Scotland to announce plans to build a $1 billion golf course. Permission was initially denied by the local Aberdeenshire Council but was then granted by the Scottish government on the ground that it was in the nation’s best interests. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Golf Course vs. Dunes: A Rebellion That Failed', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaches', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dunes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eminent Domain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Part-Time Employment', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T11:34:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna M. Foster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5cc4224-443c-5515-bbe1-86ea325a1d3c', 'word_count': 1607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5cc4224-443c-5515-bbe1-86ea325a1d3c'}, {'abstract': 'Less hospital noise improves patient care, a complex Wells Fargo security goes wrong for investors, why prepaid phones aren’t more popular and other consumer-focused news from today’s Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/friday-reading-less-hospital-noise-improves-patient-care/', 'snippet': 'Less hospital noise improves patient care, a complex Wells Fargo security goes wrong for investors, why prepaid phones aren’t more popular and other consumer-focused news from today’s Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and on our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Reading: Less Hospital Noise Improves Patient Care', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T11:59:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e68af0b5-bfc6-544b-b8dd-6bfc1a568a8c', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e68af0b5-bfc6-544b-b8dd-6bfc1a568a8c'}, {'abstract': 'Toyota has surged back from a downturn following the natural disasters in Japan last year and is expecting to sell 23 percent more vehicles than it did in 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/04/business/global/toyota-raises-sales-target-as-quarterly-profit-rises.html', 'snippet': 'Toyota has surged back from a downturn following the natural disasters in Japan last year and is expecting to sell 23 percent more vehicles than it did in 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Toyota roared back to a hefty profit in the first quarter and said on Friday that it intended to build a record-breaking 9.76 million cars this year, leading a recovery by Japanese automakers after a year of natural disasters and a punishingly strong currency. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'