/03/what-were-reading-493/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Washington Post: Is Michelle Obama’s better-eating crusade a nourishing feast or just a flashy appetizer that will produce little change? A thoughtful vetting of the first lady’s efforts and new book. — Patrick Farrell', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T13:38:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7608245e-962f-5f3b-a72f-dfce57137522', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7608245e-962f-5f3b-a72f-dfce57137522'}, {'abstract': 'The Dutch brewer extended its reach into Asia after it agreed to buy a stake in Asia Pacific Breweries, one the region’s biggest brewers, for around $4.1 billion', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/heineken-to-buy-stake-in-asia-pacific-breweries-for-4-1-billion/', 'snippet': 'The Dutch brewer extended its reach into Asia after it agreed to buy a stake in Asia Pacific Breweries, one the region’s biggest brewers, for around $4.1 billion', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Heineken extended its reach into Asia on Friday after the Dutch brewer agreed to buy a stake in one the region’s biggest brewers for roughly $4.1 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heineken to Buy Stake in Asia Pacific Breweries for $4.1 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': '