5, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/22/magazine/22cover/22cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/22/magazine/22cover/22cover-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The 7.22.12 Issue', 'kicker': 'Reply All | Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The 7.22.12 Issue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T14:46:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/a03157ed-ce9a-5b4c-956d-839b47c8f683', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a03157ed-ce9a-5b4c-956d-839b47c8f683'}, {'abstract': 'The Facebook racist, Mom’s dying wish, giving (too much) at the office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/magazine/hate-posts.html', 'snippet': 'The Facebook racist, Mom’s dying wish, giving (too much) at the office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I recently found the Facebook page of someone who works at a local retail establishment. He has posted terrible racist rants for all the world to see. Is it ethical to report this to his employer so that he removes the name of the establishment from his page? I find it difficult to patronize a store where such a person works. NAME WITHHELD, ARIZONA', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05ethicist/05ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05ethicist/05ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05ethicist/05ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05ethicist/05ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05ethicist/05ethicist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hate Posts', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hate Posts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T14:46:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chuck Klosterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chuck', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klosterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d4562c0-fc8c-571c-89fd-e1ce579aeb1e', 'word_count': 990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d4562c0-fc8c-571c-89fd-e1ce579aeb1e'}, {'abstract': 'When a bill was paid in maple syrup, a family tradition was born.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/magazine/how-my-grandmother-became-flush-with-syrup.html', 'snippet': 'When a bill was paid in maple syrup, a family tradition was born.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Maxwells couldn’t pay up, they settled their account with maple syrup. They were customers of my grandparents’ heating-oil service in northern Vermont. My grandfather delivered the oil, and my grandmother kept the books; when he died, she was left to close out the business. This was the North Country around Lake Memphremagog, the last exit on I-91 before the Canadian border, where plenty of farmers and people who work in the woods come up short every month. Tapping sugar maples is a common way to supplement income, and this was the case with the Maxwells, who had a sizable outstanding bill when my grandfather died. The Maxwells made a proposal: they would pay the balance over time in Vermont’s liquid gold.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '54', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05lives/mag-05Lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 517, 'width': 523, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05lives/mag-05Lives-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 517, 'width': 523, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05lives/05lives-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05lives/05lives-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/05lives/05lives-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How My Grandmother Became Flush With Syrup', 'kicker': 'Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stuck Together', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maple Syrup and Sugar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grandparents', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vermont', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T14:46:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Scribner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scribner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d610a10-1da2-5249-bf85-d4a59b10d76f', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d610a10-1da2-5249-bf85-d4a59b10d76f'}, {'abstract': 'Plus: the shady characters who made them famous.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/magazine/who-made-those-aviator-sunglasses.html', 'snippet': 'Plus: the shady characters who made them famous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early in the 20th century, as test pilots began flying higher than Mount Everest, they had to defend themselves against temperatures as low as minus-80 degrees Fahrenheit. To survive the frigid blast, aviators wore leather hoods, and they insulated their eyes with fur-lined goggles. To lift those goggles for even an instant was to risk death. In 1920, when Shorty Schroeder dared to take a biplane above 33,000 feet, his goggles fogged and he had no choice but to pull them off. Moments later, his vision blurred, and his eyes were soon frozen over.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/wmt/wmt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/wmt/wmt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/wmt/mag-05WMT-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/wmt/mag-05WMT-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 964, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/wmt/wmt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/wmt/wmt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/magazine/wmt/wmt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 96, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made Those Aviator Sunglasses?', 'kicker': 'Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Made That? (Aviator Sunglasses)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trademarks and Trade N