ula is house hunting in Mexico City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/books/review/vlad-by-carlos-fuentes.html', 'snippet': 'Carlos Fuentes’s Dracula is house hunting in Mexico City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Carlos Fuentes died in May at age 83, he left behind an impressive legacy and an eclectic body of work. Novels like the sprawling, Joycean “Terra Nostra” placed him at the center of the Latin American Boom of the 1970s, alongside such greats as Cortázar and García Márquez. But later books were often just as ambitious, returning to themes like the corruption of ideals.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/books/review/0805Vandermeer/0805Vandermeer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 230, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/books/review/0805Vandermeer/0805Vandermeer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 230}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/books/review/0805Vandermeer/0805Vandermeer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/books/review/0805Vandermeer/0805Vandermeer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1903, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/books/review/0805Vandermeer/0805Vandermeer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/books/review/0805Vandermeer/0805Vandermeer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/books/review/0805Vandermeer/0805Vandermeer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Blood', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Blood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuentes, Carlos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T14:51:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff VanderMeer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'VanderMeer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e36e276-4ea3-528a-b50f-c97f20cc412d', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e36e276-4ea3-528a-b50f-c97f20cc412d'}, {'abstract': 'Tana French’s “Broken Harbor” is a psychological suspense story about the dangers of suppressing unthinkable thoughts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/books/review/broken-harbor-by-tana-french-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Tana French’s “Broken Harbor” is a psychological suspense story about the dangers of suppressing unthinkable thoughts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Dublin murder squad has a grim case to solve in Tana French’s BROKEN HARBOR (Viking, $27.95). Four members of one family have been brutally attacked in their home in an upscale housing development that collapsed along with the real-\xadestate market. There’s a slim chance that Jennifer Spain might survive her injuries, but her husband has died of multiple stab wounds and their two children have been smothered in their beds. Detective Sgt. Mick Kennedy uses this horrific case as a training exercise for his rookie partner, and every so often the veteran cop dispenses some blunt piece of wisdom (“Nothing can trip you up like compassion”) that will come back to haunt them both.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/books/review/0805Crime/0805Crime-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 865, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/books/review/0805Crime/0805Crime-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1731, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/books/review/0805Crime/0805Crime-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/books/review/0805Crime/0805Crime-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/books/review/0805Crime/0805Crime-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leave a Light On', 'kicker': 'Crime', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leave a Light On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kellerman, Jesse', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Owen, Howard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verdon, John P (1942- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'French, Tan