', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Avenue (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T16:23:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b258ba45-c39f-5de2-baf3-ee0d649dce16', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b258ba45-c39f-5de2-baf3-ee0d649dce16'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/weekend-fare-103/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A tour of the food scene along Rockaway Beach (above) will take place on Sunday from 1 to 3 p.m. Tickets are $50 per person, online, and include food and drinks. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T16:24:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed23b618-4b7e-58ab-a97e-c1fd455053d4', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed23b618-4b7e-58ab-a97e-c1fd455053d4'}, {'abstract': 'The latest figures on jobs and unemployment have led to adjustments in The Times’s weekly election-year jobs tracker.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/a-give-and-take-on-jobs/', 'snippet': 'The latest figures on jobs and unemployment have led to adjustments in The Times’s weekly election-year jobs tracker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Friday’s monthly jobs report easily beat expectations, with the United States adding 163,000 jobs in July. Still, the unemployment rate, based on a separate survey, stayed essentially unchanged – and with rounding figured in, it even edged up to 8.3 percent from 8.2 percent a month earlier.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Give-and-Take on Jobs', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forecasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Corporation", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T16:28:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By ECONOMIX EDITORS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Economix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'EDITORS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45c324b3-0874-5290-8c00-124a70720409', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45c324b3-0874-5290-8c00-124a70720409'}, {'abstract': 'What does a president do when his general is also his enemy?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/the-mcclellan-problem/', 'snippet': 'What does a president do when his general is also his enemy?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Aug. 3, 1862, Gen. George B. McClellan received orders to begin withdrawing the Army of the Potomac from its position in front of Richmond, Va. The new Union general in chief, Henry Halleck, had given McClellan a choice: to renew his offensive against Richmond or ship his army back to Washington. McClellan resented and resisted Halleck’s authority, and stubbornly refused to advance, thinking Halleck would eventually recognize the folly of a withdrawal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The McClellan Problem', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McClellan, George B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T16:30:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Slotkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Slotkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2aefd19e-d85b-5b0f-9ec4-0ad41fd16101', 'word_count': 1483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2aefd19e-d85b-5b0f-9ec4-0ad41fd16101'}, {'abstract': 'Over the past year, destinations in Myanmar have drawn an increasing number of tourists. But the question of whether to visit a country long ruled by a brutal military dictatorship has not gone away.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/travel/visiting-myanmar-its-complicated.html', 'snippet': 'Over the past year, destinations in Myanmar have drawn an increasing number of tourists. But the question of whether to visit a country long ruled by a brutal military dictatorship has not gone away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE face towel was scented with lemon grass, and the welcome drink was fresh lemonade poured over crushed ice. Sultry breezes filtered through the open-air lobby decorated in colonial style, with wicker chairs, spinning ceiling fans, faux Southeast Asian antiques and pillars of solid teak. Footpaths wound past date palms, jasmine and frangipani; a swimming pool extended toward an artificial lake clotted with hyacinths. Beyond the lake lay one of the wonders of Southeast Asia: an arid plain speckled with 2,000 Buddhist temples.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05MYANMAR_SPAN/05MYANMAR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 460, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05MYANMAR_SPAN/05MYANMAR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 460}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05MYANMAR_SPAN/05MYANMAR_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank':