owledge of the matter. But many trading clients are still staying away.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/knight-rises-but-many-customers-fail-to-return/', 'snippet': 'Officials at the Knight Capital Group told customers that it had financing lined up for the day, according to people with knowledge of the matter. But many trading clients are still staying away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After one of the darkest days in its 17-year history, the Knight Capital Group saw its stock rise sharply on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knight Rises, but Many Customers Fail to Return', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knight Capital Group Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T16:34:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c2e9a1d-3a59-57f2-a9c7-b024dd03a5d6', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c2e9a1d-3a59-57f2-a9c7-b024dd03a5d6'}, {'abstract': 'As sisters try to find the right vacation rental properties, tensions surface and childhood grievances are revealed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/travel/with-vacation-rentals-a-little-family-drama.html', 'snippet': 'As sisters try to find the right vacation rental properties, tensions surface and childhood grievances are revealed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE calls began in January, when New York was still blanketed by the grime of city snow and ice. “Have you seen Haps Up?” my sister asked from her car in Los Angeles. If I closed my eyes, I could see the palm trees and money order joints lining La Cienega Boulevard.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05SSUMMERHOUSE/05SSUMMERHOUSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05SSUMMERHOUSE/05SSUMMERHOUSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05SSUMMERHOUSE/05SSUMMERHOUSE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05SSUMMERHOUSE/05SSUMMERHOUSE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1447, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05SSUMMERHOUSE/05SSUMMERHOUSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05SSUMMERHOUSE/05SSUMMERHOUSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05SSUMMERHOUSE/05SSUMMERHOUSE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Vacation Rentals, a Little Family Drama', 'kicker': 'Personal Journeys', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My House Is Your House (or Not)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pawleys Island (SC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T16:38:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/425a4a86-8c79-53cb-8022-5ec4d089a244', 'word_count': 1293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/425a4a86-8c79-53cb-8022-5ec4d089a244'}, {'abstract': 'The jobs report released on Friday ought to mostly reinforce pre-existing impressions about the economy: that the recovery is slow, but that the nation is probably not on the verge of a double-dip recession.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/july-jobs-report-likely-to-preserve-status-quo/', 'snippet': 'The jobs report released on Friday ought to mostly reinforce pre-existing impressions about the economy: that the recovery is slow, but that the nation is probably not on the verge of a double-dip recession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The government reported that 163,000 payroll jobs were created in July. But the unemployment rate — which is calculated through a separate survey — ticked up to 8.3 percent from 8.2 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'July Jobs Report Likely to Preserve Status Quo', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electoral College', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forecasts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T16:38:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4176a1c0-0cdd-5fbf-9dd9-03e654fa36e0', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4176a1c0-0cdd-5fbf-9dd9-03e654fa36e0'}, {'abstract': 'Next year, San Francisco will host the America’s Cup. But you don’t have to wait until then to taste the experience — and some sea spray — yourself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/travel/sailing-san-francisco-bay-like-a-pro.html', 'snippet': 'Next year, San Francisco will host the America’s Cup. But you don’t have to wait until then to taste the experience — and some sea spray — yourself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH a whoosh of water against its sleek, black hull and a thundering crack of wind-whipped sails above, USA 76 came about on San Francisco Bay. Almost immediately, the 115-foot mast — about as tall as a 10-story building — dipped 30 degrees, and I found myself riding the high side of the heeled-over sailboat as we sped under the Golden Gate Bridge. Unnerved by the sudden shift but trusting in the former America’s Cup racing yacht and its crew, I gripped the rails as we entered the towering swells just outside the Gate.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05JOURNEYS1_SPAN/05JOURNEYS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05JOURNEYS1_SPAN/05JOURNEYS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05JOURNEYS1_SPAN/05JOURNEYS1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05JOURNEYS1_SPAN/05JOURNEYS1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05JOURNEYS1_SPAN/05JOURNEYS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05JOURNEYS1_SPAN/05JOURNEYS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05JOURNEYS1_SPAN/05JOURNEYS1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sailing San Francisco Bay Like a Pro', 'kicker': 'Journeys', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sailing San Francisco Bay Like a Pro', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "AMERICA'S CUP", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sailboats and Sailing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T16:38:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Hall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdf7bdb3-d8b2-564f-a309-793cadc137cf', 'word_count': 1248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdf7bdb3-d8b2-564f-a309-793cadc137cf'}, {'abstract': 'Home to few cars, little night life and only about 18 year-round residents, Cuttyhunk Island may be an ideal destination for those who really want to escape.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/travel/tranquillity-on-cuttyhunk-island-off-cape-cod.html', 'snippet': 'Home to few cars, little night life and only about 18 year-round residents, Cuttyhunk Island may be an ideal destination for those who really want to escape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Elizabeth Islands — 16 land hops trailing southwest of Cape Cod like expertly skipped stones — are often overlooked. Fourteen of them are the property of the Forbes family and another, Penikese, is a former leper colony and now a sanctuary for roseate terns, which allows only limited access. Then there’s Cuttyhunk. Tiny and sparsely populated, to most it’s just a smear of craggy scenery viewed from the ferry to Martha’s Vineyard. But for anyone willing to forgo cars, night life and reliable Wi-Fi, it’s an ideal short getaway, just two hours from Boston.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05OVERNIGHTER3_SPAN/05OVERNIGHTER3_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05OVERNIGHTER3_SPAN/05OVERNIGHTER3_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05OVERNIGHTER3_SPAN/05OVERNIGHTER3_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05OVERNIGHTER3_SPAN/05OVERNIGHTER3_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1349, 'width': 2027, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05OVERNIGHTER3_SPAN/05OVERNIGHTER3_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05OVERNIGHTER3_SPAN/05OVERNIGHTER3_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/travel/05OVERNIGHTER3_SPAN/05OVERNIGHTER3_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tra