r of Britain’s Labour Party suggests they’re trying.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/can-the-left-capitalize-on-europes-austerity-backlash/', 'snippet': 'A meeting between François Hollande, the French president, and Ed Miliband, the leader of Britain’s Labour Party suggests they’re trying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the political surprises of the financial crash is the failure of Europe’s center-left and social democrats to capitalize on a crisis caused by reckless banks. Now a meeting between François Hollande, the French president, and the leader of Britain’s opposition Labour Party, Ed Miliband, has focused attention on moves by the left to exploit the European backlash against austerity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can the Left Capitalize on Europe’s Austerity Backlash?', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miliband, Edward S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T17:16:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/521c0e91-ae03-5fd2-acb1-4c498cf7268b', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/521c0e91-ae03-5fd2-acb1-4c498cf7268b'}, {'abstract': 'Christoph Niemann is illustrating his way through the games.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/abstract-sunday-on-the-tube/', 'snippet': 'Christoph Niemann is illustrating his way through the games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Abstract Sunday columnist, Christoph Niemann, is in London for the games. He’s going to illustrate his way through them. Today, he takes the tube to Olympic Park. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abstract Sunday on the Tube', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T17:22:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73a4327b-07fb-5200-9d1c-0e12b4f1c9b0', 'word_count': 29, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73a4327b-07fb-5200-9d1c-0e12b4f1c9b0'}, {'abstract': 'Bucks readers discuss their strategies in dealing with the uncertainty of tax increases next year.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/dealing-with-tax-uncertainties/', 'snippet': 'Bucks readers discuss their strategies in dealing with the uncertainty of tax increases next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Sullivan, in his Wealth Matters column this week, talks to wealthy investors about how they are dealing with the uncertainty about whether federal taxes will increase next year. Specifically, he looks at the 3.8 percent surtax on investment income that is in President Obama’s health care legislation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dealing With Tax Uncertainties', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T17:23:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a567a78-0873-5d48-8085-818cd7f10cc6', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a567a78-0873-5d48-8085-818cd7f10cc6'}, {'abstract': 'The eighth day of the London Olympics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/08/03/sports/olympics/20120803-OLYPOD.html', 'snippet': 'The eighth day of the London Olympics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The eighth day of the London Olympics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/sports/olympics/20120803-OLYPOD-slide-S1P4/20120803-OLYPOD-slide-S1P4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/sports/olympics/20120803-OLYPOD-slide-S1P4/20120803-OLYPOD-slide-S1P4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1510, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/sports/olympics/20120803-OLYPOD-slide-S1P4/20120803-OLYPOD-slide-S1P4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/03/sports/olympics/20120803-OLYPOD-slide-S1P4/20120803-OLYPOD-slide-S1P4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/sports/olympics/20120803-OLYPOD-slide-S1P4/20120803-OLYPOD-slide-S1P4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day From London | August 3, 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T17:26:11+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/3905c62d-1814-5c96-85a3-2ba12e93f4de', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/3905c62d-1814-5c96-85a3-2ba12e93f4de'}, {'abstract': 'The Knight Capital Group is in talks to sell its futures brokerage unit with a number of potential buyers, including the trading firm R.J. O’Brien, people briefed on the matter told DealBook on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/knight-said-to-hold-talks-to-sell-futures-brokerage-unit/', 'snippet': 'The Knight Capital Group is in talks to sell its futures brokerage unit with a number of potential buyers, including the trading firm R.J. O’Brien, people briefed on the matter told DealBook on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Knight Capital Group is in talks to sell its futures brokerage unit with potential buyers, including Chicago-based R.J. O’Brien, people briefed on the matter told DealBook on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knight Said to Hold Talks to Sell Futures Brokerage Unit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knight Capital Group Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T17:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed, Ben Protess and Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35665e0c-e653-5a9f-ac0c-b4ff28c9a019', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35665e0c-e653-5a9f-ac0c-b4ff28c9a019'}, {'abstract': 'Periodically throughout the Olympics, The Times will check in with Dennis Spurr, a sausage maker in Weymouth, England, where the sailing events are taking place.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/weymouth-journal-a-laugher-in-the-sausage-making-event/', 'snippet': 'Periodically throughout the Olympics, The Times will check in with Dennis Spurr, a sausage maker in Weymouth, England, where the sailing events are taking place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Periodically throughout the Olympics, The Times will check in with Dennis Spurr, owner of the Fantastic Sausage Factory in Weymouth, England, a pretty town on the coast where the sailing events are taking place. Spurr’s sausage business was targeted by the Olympic branding authorities in 2007 after he put up a sign featuring the Olympic five-ring logo fashioned out of sausage links. He took it down on their demands, but replaced it with a sign featuring five squares made out of sausage links.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weymouth Journal: A Laugher in the Sausage-Making Event', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spurr, Dennis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fantastic Sausage Factory (Weymouth, England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T17:34:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ada74bab-6bdb-5d46-a39b-a49982279c36', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ada74bab-6bdb-5d46-a39b-a49982279c36'}, {'abstract': 'Aleksandr Y. Lebedev, who has tweaked Vladimir V. Putin, Russia’s president, for years, said police and regulatory checks on his businesses were so intense that he would sell them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/04/world/europe/ex-kgb-banker-and-putin-critic-plans-to-sell-assets.html', 'snippet': 'Aleksandr Y. Lebedev, who has tweaked Vladimir V. Putin, Russia’s president, for years, said police and regulatory checks on his businesses were so intense that he would sell them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Aleksandr Y. Lebedev, a prominent banker and newspaper magnate who has supported the political opposition, announced on Friday that police and regulatory checks had become so intense that he would sell all of his Russia-based assets. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/world/russia/russia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 723, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/world/russia/russia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1446, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/world/russia/russia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/04/world/russia/russia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/world/russia/russia-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-K.G.B. Banker and Putin Critic Plans to Sell Assets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Putin Critic Plans to Sell His Russia-Based Assets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lebedev, Aleksandr Y', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T17:36:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/546924eb-5b5f-5778-b253-e1c76df849e6', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/546924eb-5b5f-5778-b253-e1c76df849e6'}, {'abstract': 'Eunice Johnson, of the Johnson Publishing Company, and founder of the Ebony Fashion Fair, never made the International Best Dressed List.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/eunice-johnson-and-the-best-dressed-list/', 'snippet': 'Eunice Johnson, of the Johnson Publishing Company, and founder of the Ebony Fashion Fair, never made the International Best Dressed List.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some years ago I was invited to Eleanor Lambert’s apartment on Fifth Avenue to observe the selection process for the International Best Dressed List, a publicity vehicle she drove with a keen eye to what lay ahead. Royals and socialites were always welcome on the B.D.L., and of course the odd eccentric — up to a point. Daphne Guinness secured her place as of Hall of Famer in 1994, and Anna Piaggi, the dandified Italian editor, somewhat belatedly in 2007. But Isabella Blow never made it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eunice Johnson and the Best Dressed List', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ebony (Magazine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T17:39:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f74efefe-97ae-5c94-89f9-ef249183bc18', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f74efefe-97ae-5c94-89f9-ef249183bc18'}, {'abstract': 'Food goes with shelter, right? And your very own restaurant is a great place to meet potential clients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/realestate/real-estate-agents-as-restaurateurs.html', 'snippet': 'Food goes with shelter, right? And your very own restaurant is a great place to meet potential clients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR the past seven years, Brian Morgan has had a flourishing career as a broker for Citi Habitats, specializing in apartments in Flatiron, the Village and Gramercy, especially the Gramercy Starck, where he lives. But when his younger brother Joey decided to open a string of buzzy sports-themed bars, it was no surprise that Brian was the first person to climb on board.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/realestate/05COVER1_SPAN/05COVER1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/realestate/05COVER1_SPAN/05COVER1_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/realestate/05COVER1_SPAN/cover-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 622, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/realestate/05COVER1_SPAN/cover-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 911, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/realestate/05COVER1_SPAN/05COVER1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/realestate/05COVER1_SPAN/05COVER1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumb