', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Jury’s Message for Wall Street', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelleher, Dennis M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rakoff, Jed S', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stoker, Brian H', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T21:23:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/206fbfbd-9fd5-5c6d-b501-380417965d0f', 'word_count': 1106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/206fbfbd-9fd5-5c6d-b501-380417965d0f'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s polling and economic data were mostly good news for President Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/aug-3-a-good-week-for-obama-in-forecast/', 'snippet': 'This week’s polling and economic data were mostly good news for President Obama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The past week of polling and economic data was relatively newsworthy by our forecast model’s standards, and most of the news was good for President Obama.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 3: A Good Week for Obama in Forecast', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electoral College', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forecasts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T21:34:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc3c5e66-64d3-554d-b357-0b7757f8c307', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc3c5e66-64d3-554d-b357-0b7757f8c307'}, {'abstract': 'The author of “The Aleppo Codex: A True Story of Obsession, Faith and the Pursuit of an Ancient Bible” answers questions about uncovering the history of the manuscript.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/03/matti-friedman-on-the-unsolved-mystery-of-the-aleppo-codex/', 'snippet': 'The author of “The Aleppo Codex: A True Story of Obsession, Faith and the Pursuit of an Ancient Bible” answers questions about uncovering the history of the manuscript.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ronen Bergman’s article in our July 25 issue on the Aleppo Codex was occasioned and informed by the recent publication of “The Aleppo Codex: A True Story of Obsession, Faith and the Pursuit of an Ancient Bible,” by the Israeli-Canadian journalist Matti Friedman. Several readers responded to the article with questions and theories about the whereabouts of the missing pages and the motivations of the various sources quoted. For his book, Friedman spent four years investigating the story of the codex, which he talked about in a brief Q. and A. conducted this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Matti Friedman on the Unsolved Mystery of the Aleppo Codex', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T21:38:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOEL LOVELL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LOVELL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f17bc81-8ba9-5272-89d1-5a1458524b77', 'word_count': 1469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f17bc81-8ba9-5272-89d1-5a1458524b77'}, {'abstract': 'Fin Raw Bar and Kitchen specializes in seafood, especially oysters, though meat dishes are available.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/nyregion/a-review-of-fin-raw-bar-and-kitchen-in-montclair.html', 'snippet': 'Fin Raw Bar and Kitchen specializes in seafood, especially oysters, though meat dishes are available.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A SUMMER evening may be the ideal time to get acquainted with Fin Raw Bar and Kitchen, which opened in October in downtown Montclair. With\xa0its vivacious crowds, bustling open kitchen and artful lobster-shack décor, it’s as welcoming as a neighborhood beach joint at the end of a sweltering day.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Ti