, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T22:39:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f97fc37-31d7-5a4d-9097-304d77844e0e', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f97fc37-31d7-5a4d-9097-304d77844e0e'}, {'abstract': 'In Kunar Province, a seven-hour attack stopped at 8 a.m., officials said, suggesting that the insurgents sought to limit civilian casualties to avoid alienating local residents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/04/world/asia/taliban-strike-afghan-government-buildings.html', 'snippet': 'In Kunar Province, a seven-hour attack stopped at 8 a.m., officials said, suggesting that the insurgents sought to limit civilian casualties to avoid alienating local residents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — The Taliban made a show of force across a province of northeastern Afghanistan on Friday, Afghan officials said, attacking dozens of government installations but causing relatively few deaths or injuries.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghan Strike Shows Force and Restraint of Taliban', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghan Strike Shows Force And Restraint Of Taliban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T22:40:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d35a621f-5ffe-5dde-921b-aff5c7a869a1', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d35a621f-5ffe-5dde-921b-aff5c7a869a1'}, {'abstract': '“In Paris,” a stage adaptation of a short story by the Nobel Prize-winning writer Ivan Bunin, stars Mikhail Baryshnikov as a former general in the White Russian Army.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/04/theater/reviews/in-paris-stars-mikhail-baryshnikov.html', 'snippet': '“In Paris,” a stage adaptation of a short story by the Nobel Prize-winning writer Ivan Bunin, stars Mikhail Baryshnikov as a former general in the White Russian Army.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Loneliness can make time seem to slow to a dead crawl. The most mundane tasks — the morning shave, or hanging up your hat and coat in a cafe — become drawn-out rituals that fill out the hours lying heavy in your hands. This quality of time being stretched endlessly is vividly evoked in “In Paris,” a stage adaptation of a short story by the Nobel Prize-winning writer Ivan Bunin that stars Mikhail Baryshnikov as a former general in the White Russian Army, living a life of quiet exile in the city of the title.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/arts/04INPARIS/04INPARIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'su