uments filed Friday in federal court.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cycling and Antidoping Groups Clash on Armstrong', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cycling and Antidoping Groups Clash on Armstrong', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARMSTRONG, LANCE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Anti-Doping Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Cycling Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T23:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Cycling', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Macur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5ae9029-46df-56b1-af7d-e215c1687c10', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5ae9029-46df-56b1-af7d-e215c1687c10'}, {'abstract': 'At the Blue Oar Restaurant, patrons can eat on an outside deck or at picnic tables overlooking the banks of the Connecticut River.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/nyregion/a-review-of-the-blue-oar-restaurant-in-haddam.html', 'snippet': 'At the Blue Oar Restaurant, patrons can eat on an outside deck or at picnic tables overlooking the banks of the Connecticut River.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR a summertime meal with a Caribbean vibe, it’s hard to do better than the Blue Oar, on the banks of the Connecticut River. Customers pull up in cars or dock their boats at the adjacent Midway Marina, then dig into sandwiches, hot dogs, burgers and more formal entrees at outdoor picnic tables painted in tropical hues. Some dishes seem a bit pricey, but the cash-only restaurant’s B.Y.O.B. policy keeps the bill reasonable. And the view is spectacular.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05DINECT2_SPAN/05DINECT2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05DINECT2_SPAN/05DINECT2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05DINECT2_SPAN/05DINECT2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05DINECT2_SPAN/05DINECT2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05DINECT2_SPAN/05DINECT2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05DINECT2_SPAN/05DINECT2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05DINECT2_SPAN/05DINECT2_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dock Your Boat and Dig Right In', 'kicker': 'Connecticut Dining | Haddam', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dock Your Boat And Dig Right In', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Oar (Haddam, Conn, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haddam (Conn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T23:32:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Lyness', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyness', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb3517c3-7cd9-5793-b65b-a1a4044ebadd', 'word_count': 956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb3517c3-7cd9-5793-b65b-a1a4044ebadd'}, {'abstract': 'Federal health officials reported a new outbreak of swine flu on Friday, mostly among children who appeared to have picked up the virus at county fairs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/04/science/cdc-reports-outbreak-of-swine-flu.html', 'snippet': 'Federal health officials reported a new outbreak of swine flu on Friday, mostly among children who appeared to have picked up the virus at county fairs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal health officials reported a new outbreak of swine flu on Friday, mostly among children who appeared to have picked up the virus at county fairs. Sixteen people have become infected with the H3N2 swine flu virus over the past three weeks, the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention said. There were 12 cases in 2011. The new flu has a gene from the 2009 pandemic strain that officials are monitoring because it could make the illness more contagious. So far it has only been picked up from pigs and has not been passed from person to person, said Joseph Bresee, a doctor in the influenza division at the agency. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'C.D.C. Reports Outbreak of Swine Flu ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Science', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'C.D.C. Reports Outbreak of Swine Flu', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swine Influenza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-03T23:50:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcdcab4e-2ddc-5689-afd0-3b93f96560ff', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcdcab4e-2ddc-5689-afd0-3b93f96560ff'}, {'abstract': 'Former Jet Curtis Martin, who will be inducted into the Pro Football Hall of Fame Saturday, has his eyes set on becoming a team owner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/04/sports/football/for-curtis-martin-hall-is-latest-stop-in-football-career.html', 'snippet': 'Former Jet Curtis Martin, who will be inducted into the Pro Football Hall of Fame Saturday, has his eyes set on becoming a team owner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Curtis Martin will not realize a childhood dream when he is inducted Saturday into the Pro Football Hall of Fame in Canton, Ohio.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/sports/MARTIN1/MARTIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/04/sports/MARTIN1/MARTIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth