 living room with a shag rug, an Eames bent-wire chair, a boomerang-shaped coffee table and a picture window that cleverly doubles as a film screen greets the visitor to “Long Island, America’s 1950s Frontier,” an exhibition at the Long Island Museum of American Art, History and Carriages in Stony Brook. Pop songs of the ’50s like “Blue Suede Shoes” and “Mr. Sandman” drift in from another display area, where a gaudy Wurlitzer jukebox sits amid teenagers’ memorabilia. On the picture-window screen, glimpses of Levittown from a 1952 newsreel flicker by.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI2_SPAN/05ARTSLI2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI2_SPAN/05ARTSLI2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI2_SPAN/05ARTSLI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI2_SPAN/05ARTSLI2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI2_SPAN/05ARTSLI2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI2_SPAN/05ARTSLI2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Adolescence of a Suburban Region'