Gilani, then the prime minister, after he refused to support the reopening of a corruption investigation against President Asif Ali Zardari in Switzerland. The law struck down on Friday was introduced by the Pakistan Peoples Party in July to shield Mr. Gilani’s successor, Mr. Ashraf, from a similar fate. The court gave Mr. Ashraf until Wednesday to ask Swiss authorities to reopen the case against Mr. Zardari. He has given no indication that he plans to do so.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/world/briefs-chaudhry/briefs-chaudhry-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 508, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/world/briefs-chaudhry/briefs-chaudhry-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 508, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan: Contempt Law Rejected', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: Contempt Law Rejected', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chaudhry, Iftikhar Muhammad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashraf, Raja Pervez', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-04T00:54:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/980ea0ce-c8fa-5836-a93d-b0b3aaa6debf', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/980ea0ce-c8fa-5836-a93d-b0b3aaa6debf'}, {'abstract': 'Stanley Teitel, who has led Stuyvesant High School for 13 years, said he wanted “time to devote my energy to my family and personal endeavors.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/04/education/stuyvesant-principal-announces-retirement-amid-inquiry-into-cheating.html', 'snippet': 'Stanley Teitel, who has led Stuyvesant High School for 13 years, said he wanted “time to devote my energy to my family and personal endeavors.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The principal of Stuyvesant High School abruptly announced his retirement on Friday afternoon, even as New York City continued its investigation into a cheating scandal that recently rocked the elite institution.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/nyregion/STUYVESANT/STUYVESANT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 569, 'width': 429, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/nyregion/STUYVESANT/STUYVESANT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 569, 'width': 429, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/nyregion/STUYVESANT/STUYVESANT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/04/nyregion/STUYVESANT/STUYVESANT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/nyregion/STUYVESANT/STUYVESANT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Inquiry Into Cheating, Stuyvesant Principal Will Retire', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid Inquiry Into Cheating, Stuyvesant Principal Will Retire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teitel, Stanley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheating', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stuyvesant High School', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Principals (School)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-04T00:54:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e48f65c3-9ecc-5e2c-aa5b-b5c39f88ca37', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e48f65c3-9ecc-5e2c-aa5b-b5c39f88ca37'}, {'abstract': 'Several local governments in the western region of Xinjiang have ordered Muslim restaurants to stay open during the holy month of Ramadan and are telling civil servants and students to continue to eat and drink during daylight hours.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/04/world/asia/china-muslim-fasting-discouraged.html', 'snippet': 'Several local governments in the western region of Xinjiang have ordered Muslim restaurants to stay open during the holy month of Ramadan and are telling civil servants and students to continue to eat and drink during daylight hours.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Several local governments in the western region of Xinjiang have ordered Muslim restaurants to stay open during the holy month of Ramadan and are telling civil servants and students to continue to eat and drink during daylight hours, when Muslims generally fast. Ramadan began on July 20. A notice on the Web site of the health bureau of Urumqi, the regional capital, said local officials had discussed “increasing eating and drinking during Ramadan” and were urged “to increase the monitoring of collective eating with supplied food at work units.” The goal was to “guarantee the health of the masses,” the posting said. Local governments have been putting in place such policies for several years. Southern Xinjiang and Urumqi have a large number of Uighurs, Muslims who often express discontent with ethnic Han, who dominate China. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Muslim Fasting Discouraged', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Muslim Fasting Discouraged', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Xinjiang (China)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fasting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ramadan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-04T00:57:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfb1ec8c-a904-5bf6-bfb7-6dd01510aa22', '