on’s largely unsuccessful effort to tame the rising inflation of the late 1960s and early 1970s, died on Friday in Ann Arbor, Mich. He was 96.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/us/MCCRACKEN-obit/MCCRACKEN-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 853, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/us/MCCRACKEN-obit/MCCRACKEN-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1781, 'width': 1484, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/us/MCCRACKEN-obit/MCCRACKEN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/04/us/MCCRACKEN-obit/MCCRACKEN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/04/us/MCCRACKEN-obit/MCCRACKEN-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Paul W. McCracken, Adviser to Presidents, Dies at 96', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paul W. McCracken, Adviser to Presidents, Dies at 96', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCracken, Paul W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-04T01:18:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sewell Chan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sewell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac19f6f2-2012-5491-ac09-4d700f8f1118', 'word_count': 1075, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac19f6f2-2012-5491-ac09-4d700f8f1118'}, {'abstract': 'The workers from the Transcaribe Trading Company used 30 trucks to surround the offices of La Prensa, which has published investigative articles about the company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/04/world/americas/panama-president-ends-blockade-at-la-prensa.html', 'snippet': 'The workers from the Transcaribe Trading Company used 30 trucks to surround the offices of La Prensa, which has published investigative articles about the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It took the intervention of President Ricardo Martinelli and a chief of the national police to end a blockade of the newspaper La Prensa on Friday by scores of workers from one of Panama’s largest construction companies. The workers from the Transcaribe Trading Company used 30 trucks to surround the offices of the newspaper, which has published investigative articles about the company, reporting that it had received millions of dollars in favorable government contracts. La Prensa has a long history of reporting on corruption and has clashed with the president, although his office released a statement condemning the workers’ action. A representative of the company did not respond to a request for comment, but its Web site includes videos of workers denouncing La Prensa. Lourdes de Obaldía, the editor of the newspaper, said the protest did not prevent the publication of the newspaper, but she called the blockade, which lasted several hours, part of a rising number of actions aimed at intimidating the news media in Panama. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Panama: President Ends Blockade at Newspaper', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Panama: President Ends Blockade at Newspaper', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'La Prensa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Panama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martinelli, Ricardo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-04T01:18:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/04b0f28c-955f-5b03-aeac-9cdc24b1b4df', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04b0f28c-955f-5b03-aeac-9cdc24b1b4df'}, {'abstract': 'New applications can help diners locate a meal, and make sure that certain someone pays what he owes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/nyregion/tricks-to-finding-food-and-to-paying-for-it.html', 'snippet': 'New applications can help diners locate a meal, and make sure that certain someone pays what he owes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Where to eat? It is a basic question of life in New York, and one that app developers have attempted to answer in various ways. Apps fall into a few categories: those that try to show you all the information that is out there (Yelp or Urbanspoon), those that rely on the wisdom of selected experts (Immaculate Infatuation or Chefs Feed) or apps that pick a small corner of the food world and focus on that (Tweat.it for food trucks).', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05APPCITY/05APP-CITY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05APPCITY/05APP-CITY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05APPCITY/05APP-CITY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05APPCITY/05APP-CITY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05APPCITY/05APP-CITY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tricks to Finding Food and to Paying for It', 'kicker': 'App City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tricks to Finding Food And to Paying for It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-04T01:22:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'origina