, published within a few weeks of each other, explore dalliances in wealthy school districts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/nyregion/for-a-spicier-city-turn-the-page.html', 'snippet': 'Two recent books, published within a few weeks of each other, explore dalliances in wealthy school districts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If two books, strikingly similar in manner and published within a few weeks of each other can be said to suggest a trend, then the arrival of “Motherland,” a story of midlife shenanigans in Park Slope, Brooklyn, and “Triburbia,” a story of midlife shenanigans south of Canal Street in Manhattan, signals the emergence of a new strain of pop domestic fiction. It’s one in which erotic destiny is ordained by school district — sexual dalliance facilitated by the Department of Education.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05BIGCITY1_SPAN/05BIGCITY1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05BIGCITY1_SPAN/05BIGCITY1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05BIGCITY1_SPAN/05SUBJPBIGCITY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05BIGCITY1_SPAN/05SUBJPBIGCITY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/nyregion/05BIGCITY1_SPAN/05BIGCITY1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height