ank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09367fe2-3fbd-5622-bfc3-ba2623f0a84c', 'word_count': 3576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09367fe2-3fbd-5622-bfc3-ba2623f0a84c'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney’s fate in Colorado may depend on whether his campaign can build a ground-level presence like the one that helped carry President Obama four years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/us/politics/romney-campaign-takes-to-the-ground-in-colorado.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney’s fate in Colorado may depend on whether his campaign can build a ground-level presence like the one that helped carry President Obama four years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAKEWOOD, Colo. — In an office park with clipped lawns and burbling fountains, volunteers at Mitt Romney’s new Colorado headquarters were busy working the phones. Do you approve of President Obama, they asked voters. Are you voting Democratic or Republican? Every time they tallied a new Romney supporter, they dinged a bell. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/us/05groundgame1/05groundgame1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/us/05groundgame1/05groundgame1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1405, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/us/05groundgame1/05groundgame1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/us/05groundgame1/05groundgame1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank