jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/sports/olympics/05oly-phelps/05oly-phelps-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Relay Victory in His Final Race, Phelps Claims 18th Gold', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-04T18:55:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d406407b-e01d-5e0b-a7e5-5c6977cb2d55', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d406407b-e01d-5e0b-a7e5-5c6977cb2d55'}, {'abstract': 'It’s an age-old question: Does success have more to do with talent and effort, or simply good fortune? Sociologists found some answers in an experiment with 48 songs by indie bands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/business/of-luck-and-success-economic-view.html', 'snippet': 'It’s an age-old question: Does success have more to do with talent and effort, or simply good fortune? Sociologists found some answers in an experiment with 48 songs by indie bands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE may be no topic that more reliably divides liberals and conservatives than the relationship between success and luck. Many conservatives celebrate market success as an almost inevitable consequence of talent and effort. Liberals, by contrast, like to remind us that even talented people who work hard sometimes fall on hard times through no fault of their own.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/business/05SBUVIEW/05SBUVIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/business/05SBUVIEW/05SBUVIEW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1482, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/business/05SBUVIEW/05SBUVIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/05/business/05SBUVIEW/05SBUVIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/business/05SBUVIEW/05SBUVIEW-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Luck vs. Skill: Seeking the Secret of Your Success', 'kicker': 'Economic View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Will the Skillful Win? They Should Be So Lucky', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luck', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watts, Duncan J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sociology', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-04T18:55:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'Robert H. Frank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Frank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81fd834b-1e52-56c5-989f-23ae963d0165', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81fd834b-1e52-56c5-989f-23ae963d0165'}, {'abstract': 'When my brother was murdered, I became a believer in the death penalty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/opinion/sunday/wanting-to-kill.html', 'snippet': 'When my brother was murdered, I became a believer in the death penalty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I REMEMBER the phone call from my mother distinctly. It came in February of 1980. I was 19, a high school dropout working as a tool-and-die apprentice, living in my hometown of Bridgeport, Conn. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/sunday-review/05DEATH/05DEATH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/sunday-review/05DEATH/05DEATH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/sunday-review/05DEATH/05DEATH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/sunday-review/05DEATH/05DEATH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1279, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'