alue': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Methane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-04T18:59:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/712b2010-d423-5944-af39-7fa5d4c29d9a', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/712b2010-d423-5944-af39-7fa5d4c29d9a'}, {'abstract': 'A new book by Kenneth Feinberg traces his years of work in assessing and paying victims’ claims after disasters, whether the 9/11 attacks, the Virginia Tech massacre or the Gulf of Mexico oil spill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/business/kenneth-feinbergs-new-look-at-fairnesss-price-review.html', 'snippet': 'A new book by Kenneth Feinberg traces his years of work in assessing and paying victims’ claims after disasters, whether the 9/11 attacks, the Virginia Tech massacre or the Gulf of Mexico oil spill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KENNETH R. FEINBERG, who styles himself as “a lawyer and mediator in one,” has made a career of handling hot potatoes and moving them from politicians’ plates to his own. At moments of national disaster, he has embraced the trying task of applying mere money to sustain and comfort the survivors and to bind the wounds of the afflicted. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0