ne}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce147850-ceba-5254-b3a4-e89206ff6119', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce147850-ceba-5254-b3a4-e89206ff6119'}, {'abstract': 'Massachusetts will be the first state to try to cap overall health care spending, both private and public, so that it will grow no faster than the state economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/opinion/sunday/massachusetts-takes-on-health-costs.html', 'snippet': 'Massachusetts will be the first state to try to cap overall health care spending, both private and public, so that it will grow no faster than the state economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Give Massachusetts credit for setting audacious health care goals. It took the lead in guaranteeing near-universal health insurance coverage for its residents, providing a template for the federal reforms to follow. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts Takes On Health Costs', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts Takes on Health Costs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patrick, Deval L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-04T19:19:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/54d5f758-e0f1-589c-b212-9667a14425b5', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54d5f758-e0f1-589c-b212-9667a14425b5'}, {'abstract': 'Solutions that would lower the federal prison population include repealing mandatory minimum sentences and reducing drug prosecutions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/opinion/sunday/too-many-prisoners.html', 'snippet': 'Solutions that would lower the federal prison population include repealing mandatory minimum sentences and reducing drug prosecutions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department in its recent annual report on federal sentencing issues wisely acknowledged that public safety can be maximized without maximizing prison spending. As it noted, the growing federal prison population, now more than 218,000 inmates, and a prison budget of almost $6.2 billion are “incompatible with a balanced crime policy and are unsustainable.” ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Many Prisoners', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Too Many Prisoners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mandatory Sentencing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Sentencing Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-04T19:19:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/347e5bb7-fcd0-530d-9ed6-4d7f372b0c79', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/347e5bb7-fcd0-530d-9ed6-4d7f372b0c79'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to “Taxes Needn’t Discourage Philanthropy” (Economic View, July 29).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/business/letters-when-tax-rates-touched-the-sky.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to “Taxes Needn’t Discourage Philanthropy” (Economic View, July 29).', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters: When Tax Rates Touched the Sky', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Tax Rates Touched the Sky', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-04T19:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/52d06b51-5cc8-5382-8868-032194c56945', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52d06b51-5cc8-5382-8868-032194c56945'}, {'abstract': 'Millions of Americans have to work when ill or take unpaid sick days, which can lead to financial hardship or dismissal. A national law requiring businesses to provide paid sick leave is needed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/opinion/sunday/working-while-sick.html', 'snippet': 'Millions of Americans have to work when ill or take unpaid sick days, which can lead to financial hardship or dismissal. A national law requiring businesses to provide paid sick leave is needed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 40 million American workers get no paid sick leave. They have to work when ill or take unpaid sick days, which can lead to financial hardship, or, worse, dismissal. The best way to address this workplace and public health problem is with a national law requiring businesses to provide paid sick leave — a normal benefit for workers in at least 145 countries.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Working While Sick', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Working While Sick', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paid Time Off', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brewer, Gale A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-04T19:21:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/953ecad5-f739-5a1d-b115-78e71aa0c4e2', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/953ecad5-f739-5a1d-b115-78e71aa0c4e2'}, {'abstract': 'Simply to be playing is a victory for Minnesota’s Justin Morneau, whose last season ended with a concussion, his second in 14 months.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/sports/baseball/twins-justin-morneau-bats-his-way-back-from-injuries.html', 'snippet': 'Simply to be playing is a victory for Minnesota’s Justin Morneau, whose last season ended with a concussion, his second in 14 months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Justin Morneau batted cleanup here Thursday for t