ckly than any incumbent in recent history, betting that heavy early investments in personnel, field offices and a high-tech campaign infrastructure will propel him to victory in November. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Record Spending by Obama’s Camp Shrinks Coffers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Record Spending By Obama’s Camp Shrinks Coffers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Election Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-05T00:54:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore and Jo Craven McGinty', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jo', 'middlename': 'Craven', 'lastname': 'McGinty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40643aca-9336-54ac-81ef-64e8d7b900ad', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40643aca-9336-54ac-81ef-64e8d7b900ad'}, {'abstract': 'Led by Missy Franklin, the American women won gold in the 4x100 medley relay. Sun Yang of China dethroned the defending champion Oussama Mellouli of Tunisia in the 1,500-meter freestyle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/sports/olympics/us-women-win-medley-relay-sun-yang-of-china-sets-record.html', 'snippet': 'Led by Missy Franklin, the American women won gold in the 4x100 medley relay. Sun Yang of China dethroned the defending champion Oussama Mellouli of Tunisia in the 1,500-meter freestyle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — It was going to take a lot of bling to deflect attention from the brilliance of Michael Phelps, who won his sixth medal and fourth gold of the London Games on Saturday in his fourth and final Olympics. His United States teammates on the women’s 4x100-meter medley relay had the credentials to pull it off. Missy Franklin, Rebecca Soni, Dana Vollmer and Allison Schmitt took a combined five individual golds and two silvers into the final, and they left London Aquatics Centre for the last time with a world record and a relay gold.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/sports/05oly-ws/05oly-ws-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/05/sports/05oly-ws/05oly-ws-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/sports/05oly-ws/05oly-ws-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/sports/05oly-ws/05oly-ws-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/05/sports/05oly-ws/05oly-ws-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail