Kasparov in 1990 and 2000, but ratings inflation casts a shadow on Carlsen’s accomplishment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/crosswords/chess/chess-carlsen-close-to-kasparov-record.html', 'snippet': 'Magnus Carlsen is on the verge of earning the highest rating of all time, breaking the record set by Garry Kasparov in 1990 and 2000, but ratings inflation casts a shadow on Carlsen’s accomplishment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are numbers in chess that have special significance. One of them is 2,851: the highest rating of all time, which Garry Kasparov, the former world champion, earned twice, in July 1999 and January 2000. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parsing Numbers to Choose Best Ever', 'kicker': 'Chess', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Parsing Numbers To Choose Best Ever', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carlsen, Magnus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Records and Achievements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Chess Federation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kasparov, Garry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-05T03:01:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91d24812-8049-51e7-81cc-e522ddfb3a26', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91d24812-8049-51e7-81cc-e522ddfb3a26'}, {'abstract': 'Coach Jim Calhoun, who has led the Connecticut men’s team to three N.C.A.A. titles, broke his hip in a bicycle accident and had surgery at the UConn Health Center in Farmington.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/sports/ncaabasketball/calhoun-breaks-his-hip.html', 'snippet': 'Coach Jim Calhoun, who has led the Connecticut men’s team to three N.C.A.A. titles, broke his hip in a bicycle accident and had surgery at the UConn Health Center in Farmington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Coach Jim Calhoun, who has led the Connecticut men’s team to three N.C.A.A. titles, broke his hip in a bicycle accident and had surgery at the UConn Health Center in Farmington. Calhoun, 70, slipped on sand while riding near his beach home in Madison, Conn., falling off the bike. This is the latest health complication for Calhoun, who has outlasted three bouts with cancer, missed games because of back problems last year and broke five ribs while riding his bike in 2009. The fall forced Calhoun to miss a charity game on Saturday night that featured many of his former players. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calhoun Breaks His Hip', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | College basketball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Calhoun Breaks His Hip', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calhoun, Jim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Connecticut', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-05T03:02:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/adfad4b6-9df8-561d-987c-a3b4d39364af', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adfad4b6-9df8-561d-987c-a3b4d39364af'}, {'abstract': 'Santonio Holmes had an injury scare, but X-rays on his chest came back negative, alleviating the Jets’ fears that he fractured a rib during a scrimmage in Cortland, N.Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/sports/football/sigh-of-relief-for-the-jets.html', 'snippet': 'Santonio Holmes had an injury scare, but X-rays on his chest came back negative, alleviating the Jets’ fears that he fractured a rib during a scrimmage in Cortland, N.Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Santonio Holmes had an injury scare, but X-rays on his chest came back negative, alleviating the Jets’ fears that he fractured a rib during a scrimmage in Cortland, N.Y. It was a rare dose of good news for a receiving corps that has lost several members over the last week — Jeremy Kerley and Chaz Schilens among them — to groin or hamstring pulls.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sigh of Relief for the Jets', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Pro football', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sigh of Relief for the Jets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holmes, Santonio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-05T03:04:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/32c55ea3-fcae-55e0-9