treat-plays-host-to-sailing-but-crowds-fail-to-follow/', 'snippet': 'The Olympics were supposed to fill Weymouth with record crowds, but hoteliers have had to slash prices and a festival fell victim to “dire visitor numbers.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEYMOUTH, England — The bubonic plague is said to have come ashore in this coastal town, carried by fleas infected by rats. The so-called Black Death quickly spread throughout the British Isles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weymouth Journal: Charming Retreat Plays Host to Sailing, but Crowds Do Not Follow', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sailboats and Sailing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-05T20:24:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barry Bearak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bearak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fec518c4-81eb-5d0e-b48c-7a26bea98ff8', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fec518c4-81eb-5d0e-b48c-7a26bea98ff8'}, {'abstract': 'The Knight Capital Group has secured a deal on Sunday to secure a financial lifeline from an investor group that included TD Ameritrade and the Blackstone Group, capping its efforts to stay alive, a person with direct knowledge of the matter told DealBook.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/knight-said-in-talks-to-obtain-new-capital/', 'snippet': 'The Knight Capital Group has secured a deal on Sunday to secure a financial lifeline from an investor group that included TD Ameritrade and the Blackstone Group, capping its efforts to stay alive, a person with direct knowledge of the matter told ...', 'lead_paragraph': '10:09 p.m. | Updated ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knight Capital Reaches Rescue Deal With Investor Group', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knight Capital Reaches Rescue Deal With Investor Group', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knight Capital Group Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TD Ameritrade Holding Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-05T20:27:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced and Nathaniel Popper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Popper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd747d31-ad36-5251-9a51-1965df0609e0', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd747d31-ad36-5251-9a51-1965df0609e0'}, {'abstract': 'In “Hello Goodbye Hello,” the British columnist Craig Brown weaves dozens of real-life encounters into a glittering daisy chain that reads like a mathematical proof of six degrees of separation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/books/hello-goodbye-hello-by-craig-brown.html', 'snippet': 'In “Hello Goodbye Hello,” the British columnist Craig Brown weaves dozens of real-life encounters into a glittering daisy chain that reads like a mathematical proof of six degrees of separation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'According to the captivating new book “Hello Goodbye Hello” Alexander Woollcott, the writer and Algonquin Circle wit, loved to play a game called Strange Bedfellows. One of his biggest coups took place at a Cap d’Antibes villa in the summer of 1928 when he succeeded in bringing together Harpo Marx and George Bernard Shaw (“corned beef and roses,” as he called them) at lunch. The two hit it off, and later that week Harpo drove Shaw to Cannes, where a friend of Shaw’s cast them as extras in a movie; a scene featuring them playing billiards, alas, would be left on the cutting-room floor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/jpbook/jpbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/jpbook/jpbook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1503, 'width': 1879, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Chaplin to Groucho to T. S. Eliot', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Chaplin to Groucho to T. S. Eliot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature'