tandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/bronte/bronte-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/bronte/bronte-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Loneliness and Love on the Moor', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Loneliness And Love On the Moor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luce, William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bronte, Charlotte', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alloy Theater Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-05T20:50:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cac72843-f188-5c11-b622-d49078c0a6a9', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cac72843-f188-5c11-b622-d49078c0a6a9'}, {'abstract': 'Freddy Garcia’s command was suspect, but he kept Seattle under control and had plenty of help from the Yankees’ offense, defense and bullpen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/sports/baseball/garcia-just-effective-enough-beats-mariners.html', 'snippet': 'Freddy Garcia’s command was suspect, but he kept Seattle under control and had plenty of help from the Yankees’ offense, defense and bullpen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a tepid, cloudy night in Seattle in August 1999, Freddy Garcia struck out 12 Detroit Tigers as part of a shutout, setting the Seattle Mariners’ rookie record. That night, Ken Griffey Jr. hit two home runs. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/06/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1408, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/06/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Garcia Skirts Trouble Just Enough to Beat the Mariners', 'kicker': 'Yankees 6, Mariners 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Garcia Skirts Trouble Just Enough to Beat the Mariners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Freddy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Mariners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-05T20:57:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccd7d520-9495-567d-83b8-7cfbe10a727e', 'word_count': 822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccd7d520-9495-567d-83b8-7cfbe10a727e'}, {'abstract': 'The musical “Sweet Charity” gets a Latin makeover in the director Julio Agustin’s production at the New Haarlem Arts Theater, and it’s called for.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/theater/reviews/sweet-charity-at-new-haarlem-arts-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The musical “Sweet Charity” gets a Latin makeover in the director Julio Agustin’s production at the New Haarlem Arts Theater, and it’s called for.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 1966 musical (and 1969 movie) “Sweet Charity” gets a Latin makeover in the director Julio Agustin’s production at the New Haarlem Arts Theater, and it’s called for. The original could use some salsa. With its picaresque and coincidence-filled narrative; somewhat flighty title character (a lovelorn floozy, if not a prostitute, with a heart of gold); and principal setting (a dime-dance joint, already an anachronism in mid-’60s New York), the musical, originally staged by Bob Fosse, is itself a watered-down version of Fellini’s “Nights of Cabiria,” which actually did concern a prostitute and gritty issues like physical and emotional abuse and an existential take on religion. “Sweet Charity” was never one of Fosse’s more provocative shows, and Neil Simon’s quip-packed book seems sitcom-ready in retrospect. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/sweet/sweet-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 981, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/sweet/sweet-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1962, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/sweet/sweet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/sweet/sweet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/sweet/sweet-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If This Dancer’s Amigas Could See Her Now', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If This Dancer’s Amigas Could See Her Now', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fosse, Bob', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Haarlem Arts Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Agustin, Julio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simon, Neil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-05T20:58:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7df6dd35-f167-54f4-8049-db785c94f659', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7df6dd35-f167-54f4-8049-db785c94f659'}, {'abstract': 'Phil Kline’s “dreamcitynine,” a piece commissioned by Lincoln Center Out of Doors for the composer John Cage’s centenary, had its premiere Friday at Lincoln Center’s Hearst Plaza.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/arts/music/phil-klines-dreamcitynine-at-lincoln-center-out-of-doors.html', 'snippet': 'Phil Kline’s “dreamcitynine,” a piece commissioned by Lincoln Center Out of Doors for the composer John Cage’s centenary, had its premiere Friday at Lincoln Center’s Hearst Plaza.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Never underestimate the power of serendipity; any chance encounter can have profound repercussions. Take, for example, the composer Phil Kline, who discovered “Indeterminacy,” a seminal two-LP set by John Cage, while working as a college-radio D.J. during his time at Columbia University.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/kline/kline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/kline/kline-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1310, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/kline/kline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75,