of thrill-seeking millionaires who have signed up for a military adventure in “Soldiers of Fortune.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“Soldiers of Fortune,” an execrable action thriller plopped into a few local theaters without screenings for critics, is one abortive military mission. For the cast, shooting the movie (in Ukraine) may have been a working vacation, but for viewers, watching it is an excruciating sentence of hard labor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/soldiers/soldiers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/soldiers/soldiers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/soldiers/soldiers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 542, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/soldiers/soldiers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1084, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/soldiers/soldiers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/soldiers/soldiers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/soldiers/soldiers-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Commando Mission for Millionaires', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Commando Mission for Millionaires', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slater, Christian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bean, Sean', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cromwell, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Soldiers of Fortune (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meaney, Colm', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rhames, Ving', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-05T21:33:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/15f1459e-d1ed-5566-a233-1f8240836d01', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15f1459e-d1ed-5566-a233-1f8240836d01'}, {'abstract': 'Research by a group of accounting professors shows that the revolving door actually toughens enforcement results at the S.E.C. — the opposite of what government critics have maintained.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/business/study-casts-doubt-on-how-a-revolving-door-hurts-the-sec.html', 'snippet': 'Research by a group of accounting professors shows that the revolving door actually toughens enforcement results at the S.E.C. — the opposite of what government critics have maintained.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The revolving door has long been the focus of government watchdogs here, a symbolic portal that business executives and lawyers pass through on their way to government posts and back again to the private sector. There, the thinking goes, they use their influence with former colleagues to reap benefits for themselves and their companies.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Questions Risk of S.E.C. Revolving Door', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study Questions Risk Of S.E.C. Revolving Door', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-05T21:42:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb01f011-e8bd-57ff-9ca6-d81429ef8c18', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb01f011-e8bd-57ff-9ca6-d81429ef8c18'}, {'abstract': 'Yannick Nézet-Séguin conducted two concerts in the Mostly Mozart Festival, with the Chamber Orchestra of Europe and with the Mostly Mozart Festival Orchestra.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/arts/music/yannick-nezet-seguin-at-mostly-mozart-festival.html', 'snippet': 'Yannick Nézet-Séguin conducted two concerts in the Mostly Mozart Festival, with the Chamber Orchestra of Europe and with the Mostly Mozart Festival Orchestra.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In her revitalization of the Mostly Mozart Festival over the last decade, Jane Moss, the artistic director of Lincoln Center, has shown an uncanny knack for catching conductors on the rise: not least, the festival’s current music director, Louis Langrée.', 'pri