: 960, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e08b3a2-1cf2-582e-9fc7-f397c7641d63'}, {'abstract': 'The Capitol Theater in Port Chester, N.Y. — known as a rock stage where acts like the Grateful Dead and Janis Joplin have performed — is set to reopen Sept. 4 after a $2 million renovation by Peter Shapiro.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/arts/music/capitol-theater-in-port-chester-ny-to-reopen.html', 'snippet': 'The Capitol Theater in Port Chester, N.Y. — known as a rock stage where acts like the Grateful Dead and Janis Joplin have performed — is set to reopen Sept. 4 after a $2 million renovation by Peter Shapiro.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORT CHESTER, N.Y. — Forty years ago, in its heyday, the Capitol Theater here was known as a rock stage with great acoustics, a crumbling space where the Grateful Dead, Janis Joplin, Santana and Pink Floyd played memorable concerts. So when Peter Shapiro, a founder of the Brooklyn Bowl, took over the theater last year and announced plans to reopen it as a concert hall next month, he had a heavy reputation to live up to. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/jpcapitol1/jpcapitol1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 226, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/jpcapitol1/jpcapitol1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 226}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/jpcapitol1/jpcapitol1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/arts/jpcapitol1/jpcapitol1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy