e” would not or could not survive for three full years, MTV is proving otherwise.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/mtv-sets-date-for-jersey-shore/', 'snippet': 'To those who thought “Jersey Shore” would not or could not survive for three full years, MTV is proving otherwise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To those who thought “Jersey Shore” would not or could not survive for three full years, MTV is proving otherwise. The network has set a premiere date for the sixth season of this much-mocked but also much-watched reality show and has ordered a second season of the spinoff “Snooki and JWoww,” which features these two “Jersey Shore” cast members living elsewhere in New Jersey. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'MTV Sets Date for ‘Jersey Shore’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polizzi, Nicole', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-05T21:58:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bbf0e9b-f569-5b6a-b995-b5a704737721', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bbf0e9b-f569-5b6a-b995-b5a704737721'}, {'abstract': 'A severe thunderstorm in Chicago forced organizers of the Lollapalooza music festival to suspend all activities and evacuate an estimated 100,000 people from Grant Park on Saturday, The Associated Press reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/arts/music/a-stormy-lollapalooza-sends-fans-scurrying.html', 'snippet': 'A severe thunderstorm in Chicago forced organizers of the Lollapalooza music festival to suspend all activities and evacuate an estimated 100,000 people from Grant Park on Saturday, The Associated Press reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A severe thunderstorm in Chicago forced organizers of the Lollapalooza music festival to suspend all activities and evacuate an estimated 100,000 people from Grant Park for more than two hours on Saturday afternoon, The Associated Press reported. A handful of acts had their sets cut short when concert officials announced that the park would be evacuated because the National Weather Service had issued a severe thunderstorm warning. Concertgoers took shelter in neighboring bars and restaurants and in three underground parking garages that were designated evacuation centers for the sold-out event. The gates reopened a few hours later, and a curfew was extended to accommodate the night’s scheduled headliners, which included the Red Hot Chili Peppers,  Frank Ocean and Franz Ferdinand.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Stormy Lollapalooza Sends Fans Scurrying', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Stormy Lollapalooza Sends Fans Scurrying', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lollapalooza (Music Festival)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-05T22:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a01f26a3-c755-55c4-b861-217fc7bdce7b', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a01f26a3-c755-55c4-b861-217fc7bdce7b'}, {'abstract': 'Lynn Lempel gives us quite a workout.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/things-are-going/', 'snippet': 'Lynn Lempel gives us quite a workout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONDAY’S PUZZLE — Have you been following the 2012 LONDON Olympics? Lynn Lempel has, and she offers us a nice beginning to our solving week by salting her grid with six of the sports you will find in the competition.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'General Way Things Are Going', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-05T22:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7199c0ac-94de-578c-b778-e60ee2d22d58', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7199c0ac-94de-578c-b778-e60ee2d22d58'}, {'abstract': 'Why I stubbornly continue to believe that I’m a human being — something more than other animals, and more than any computer.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/anything-but-human/', 'snippet': 'Why I stubbornly continue to believe that I’m a human being — something more than other animals, and more than any computer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wherever I turn, the popular media, scientists and even fellow philosophers are telling me that I’m a machine or a beast. My ethics can be illuminated by the behavior of termites. My brain is a sloppy computer with a flicker of consciousness and the illusion of free will. I’m anything but human.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anything But Human', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Artificial Intelligence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evolution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-05T22:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Polt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3619e53a-f0b5-53d7-8e0e-7b957cab8710', 'word_count': 1632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3619e53a-f0b5-53d7-8e0e-7b957cab8710'}, {'abstract': 'The three 80-board finals ended on Saturday at the 14th World Youth Teams Championships in China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/crosswords/bridge/bridge-14th-world-youth-teams-championships-finals.html', 'snippet': 'The three 80-board finals ended on Saturday at the 14th World Youth Teams Championships in China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAICANG, China — At the 14th World Youth Teams Championships here the three 80-board finals ended on Saturday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'World Youth Teams Championships Finals', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 