ngton is hysterically trying to close off leaks of classified information. It should not be that way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/opinion/keller-the-leak-police.html', 'snippet': 'Washington is hysterically trying to close off leaks of classified information. It should not be that way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the months leading up to the invasion of Iraq in 2003, this newspaper famously published a number of stories regurgitating the Bush administration hype about Saddam Hussein’s supposed arsenal of mass destruction. A few journalists elsewhere — notably Jonathan Landay and Warren Strobel, then of the Knight Ridder newspapers — dug deeper, discovered contrary intelligence, and challenged the official line. Later, The Times also published some excellent work on how an administration eager to justify its decision to go to war cherry-picked the intelligence to make its case.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 350, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Leak Police', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Targeted Killings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frankel, Max', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feinstein, Dianne', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T01:31:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/98586bc9-2448-5e79-85bf-d06921f30231', 'word_count': 1740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98586bc9-2448-5e79-85bf-d06921f30231'}, {'abstract': 'New and long overdue incentives are needed to reward good teachers while easing chronic low performers out of the system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/opinion/carrots-and-sticks-for-school-systems.html', 'snippet': 'New and long overdue incentives are needed to reward good teachers while easing chronic low performers out of the system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Education Secretary Arne Duncan has been pushing the states to create rigorous teacher evaluation systems that not only judge teachers by how well their students perform but also — when the results are in — reward good teachers while easing chronic low performers out of the system. More than half the states have agreed to adopt new evaluation systems in exchange for competitive grants from the federal Race to the Top program or greater flexibility under the No Child Left Behind law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carrots and Sticks for School Systems', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Carrots and Sticks for School Systems', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Evaluations (Labor)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Arne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Teacher Project', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T01:35:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/61cd7a76-fc7b-5df9-b963-6ea2bb19b201', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61cd7a76-fc7b-5df9-b963-6ea2bb19b201'}, {'abstract': 'Sources said the investigation into suspected manipulation of the Libor benchmark has led banks to cooperate by sharing information that they say implicates their rivals.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/05/banks-in-libor-inquiry-are-said-to-be-trying-to-spread-blame/', 'snippet': 'Sources said the investigation into suspected manipulation of the Libor benchmark has led banks to cooperate by sharing information that they say implicates their rivals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Major banks, which often band together when facing government scrutiny, are now turning on one another as an international investigation into the manipulation of interest rates gains momentum.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Libor Fault-Finding Grows, It Is Now Every Bank for Itself', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Libor Fault-Finding Grows, It Is Now Every Bank for Itself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libor (London Interbank Offered Rate)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays PLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HSBC Holdings PLC.', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UBS A.G', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T01:37:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed and Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78dd9e4b-1871-5300-b70b-1ac9f8e881ce', 'word_count': 1349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78dd9e4b-1871-5300-b70b-1ac9f8e881ce'}, {'abstract': 'The triumph of Usain Bolt in the men’s 100-meter sprints delighted his followers in Brixton, a London neighborhood that’s home to a large and proud Jamaican population.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/sports/olympics/usain-bolt-of-jamaica-thrills-brixton-london-with-100-meter-gold.html', 'snippet': 'The triumph of Usain Bolt in the men’s 100-meter sprints delighted his followers in Brixton, a London neighborhood that’s home to a large and proud Jamaican population.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The  Electric Brixton might have been a colonial outpost. At this cavernous nightclub nine or so miles southwest of Olympic Stadium, there were no Union Jacks, no cries for Team GB, but the closest thing to a hometown crowd a man can get 4,700 miles from home.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/sports/brixton-1344216263525/brixton-1344216263525-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/06/sports/brixton-1344216263525/brixton-1344216263525-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/sports/brixton-1344216263525/brixton-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'