reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cef3e58c-faf0-51cd-b114-88350f7d358e', 'word_count': 1172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cef3e58c-faf0-51cd-b114-88350f7d358e'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate blocked a new measure aimed at protecting America’s vulnerable computer networks from cyberattacks, leaving the nation at grave risk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/opinion/republicans-fail-a-security-test.html', 'snippet': 'The Senate blocked a new measure aimed at protecting America’s vulnerable computer networks from cyberattacks, leaving the nation at grave risk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senate Republicans regularly promote themselves as the true custodians of national security. This claim seemed particularly hollow last week when they helped block a new measure aimed at protecting America’s vulnerable computer networks from attack by, among others, potentially hostile foreign governments. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Fail a Security Test', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republicans Fail a Security Test', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lieberman, Joseph I', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Susan M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T01:38:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bac58c6-b5e1-5895-b9f0-4c5a471409b4', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bac58c6-b5e1-5895-b9f0-4c5a471409b4'}, {'abstract': 'The line of double-parked cars backs into place sinuously, expertly, as one, where the sweeper has just passed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/opinion/when-the-sweeper-comes.html', 'snippet': 'The line of double-parked cars backs into place sinuously, expertly, as one, where the sweeper has just passed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a line of cars double-parked on West 12th Street. It is Monday morning, 9:30 or so. In each car, a driver waits, some reading, some making calls, some drumming their fingers on the steering wheel. The opposite curb is empty. It is a quiet block, but the air is full of expectation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Sweeper Comes', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The City Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When the Sweeper Comes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parking', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T01:41:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verlyn Klinkenborg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verlyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klinkenborg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5e286fb-4669-597e-b197-fcfcaeb3a2c9', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5e286fb-4669-597e-b197-fcfcaeb3a2c9'}, {'abstract': 'The campaign against Senator Claire McCaskill of Missouri, fueled by tax-exempt groups backing Republican candidates, may be a precursor to such efforts on a broader scale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/us/politics/in-missouri-senate-race-ads-beset-incumbent-democrat.html', 'snippet': 'The campaign against Senator Claire McCaskill of Missouri, fueled by tax-exempt groups backing Republican candidates, may be a precursor to such efforts on a broader scale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Missouri’s long, divisive Republican Senate primary draws to a close Tuesday, but after all the intraparty fireworks, it is the incumbent Democrat, Senator Claire McCaskill, who remains in deep trouble.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/us/INCUMBENT-1/INCUMBENT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/06/us/INCUMBENT-1/INCUMBENT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/us/INCUMBENT-1/INCUMBENT-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/us/INCUMBENT-1/INCUMBENT-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1356, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/us/INCUMBENT-1/INCUMBENT-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/06/us/INCUMBENT-1/INCUMBENT-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'su