icle/9b9737e2-04f2-5884-9947-5088808fcb64', 'word_count': 1091, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b9737e2-04f2-5884-9947-5088808fcb64'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Stolarik, a freelance photographer for The New York Times, was taking photos of a fight in the Bronx and suffered injuries in an encounter with the police.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/nyregion/robert-stolarik-times-photographer-is-arrested-while-on-assignment-in-the-bronx.html', 'snippet': 'Robert Stolarik, a freelance photographer for The New York Times, was taking photos of a fight in the Bronx and suffered injuries in an encounter with the police.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A freelance photographer for The New York Times was arrested on Saturday night while on assignment with two reporters who were conducting street interviews in the Bronx. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Times Photographer Is Arrested on Assignment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Times Photographer Is Arrested on Assignment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stolarik, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freeman, George', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T01:42:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed701105-ec2b-59f0-8f2d-7b166cb03aac', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed701105-ec2b-59f0-8f2d-7b166cb03aac'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court should hear a Maryland case that raises important questions about whether the collection of DNA samples from people arrested but not yet convicted violates the Fourth Amendment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/opinion/dna-and-the-fourth-amendment.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court should hear a Maryland case that raises important questions about whether the collection of DNA samples from people arrested but not yet convicted violates the Fourth Amendment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this year, Maryland’s highest court held that collection of DNA samples from people arrested but not yet convicted violated the Fourth Amendment’s prohibition against unreasonable searches and seizures. Last week, Chief Justice John Roberts Jr. stayed that ruling while the Supreme Court decides whether to hear Maryland’s appeal of the state court decision. The Supreme Court should take up this case, but there was no good reason for the chief justice to allow the police to continue collecting DNA while the case is on appeal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DNA and the Fourth Amendment', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'DNA and the Fourth Amendment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, John G Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T01:44:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/12d2a5dd-5f97-5851-b6b5-43e48bfbf0ba', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12d2a5dd-5f97-5851-b6b5-43e48bfbf0ba'}, {'abstract': 'President Hamid Karzai said he respected Parliament’s decision to fire two senior security officials, but it was not clear how quickly he would replace them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/world/asia/karzai-says-afghan-ministers-to-be-replaced.html', 'snippet': 'President Hamid Karzai said he respected Parliament’s decision to fire two senior security officials, but it was not clear how quickly he would replace them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — President Hamid Karzai moved quickly on Sunday to confirm Parliament’s decision to dismiss two senior security ministers the day before, but he reassured the Western allies that he would avoid a vacuum in the two ministries charged with fighting the war and organizing the transition to Afghan control. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghan President Moves to Reassure Allies After Security Ministers Are Dismissed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghan President Moves to Reassure Allies After Security Ministers Are Dismissed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons