'}, {'abstract': 'A gay pride parade Sunday in Hanoi was a first for Vietnam’s socially conservative capital. Gay-rights advocates have been buoyed by the news that the National Assembly is likely to consider a proposal to legalize same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/a-coming-out-party-in-hanoi/', 'snippet': 'A gay pride parade Sunday in Hanoi was a first for Vietnam’s socially conservative capital. Gay-rights advocates have been buoyed by the news that the National Assembly is likely to consider a proposal to legalize same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — It wasn’t much of a parade, as these things go. More like a noisy bike ride with some balloons. But the gathering of about 100 gay Vietnamese in Hanoi on Sunday was still a proud declaration of sorts, a kind of political coming-out in the socially conservative country. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Coming-Out Party in Hanoi', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hanoi (Vietnam)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T04:42:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e48bcb12-2b38-5d24-82e6-68968c811254', 'word_count': 1028, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e48bcb12-2b38-5d24-82e6-68968c811254'}, {'abstract': 'How can Mitt Romney justify his alliance with the casino operator who used to back Newt Gingrich?', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/embracing-sheldon-adelson/', 'snippet': 'How can Mitt Romney justify his alliance with the casino operator who used to back Newt Gingrich?', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are two things that set Mitt Romney’s presidential campaign apart: his caution and his secretiveness.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Embracing Sheldon Adelson', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adelson, Sheldon G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Steven Craig', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Las Vegas Sands Corp', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ProPublica', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Restore Our Future', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sands China', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T04:56:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas B. Edsall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/554bf23d-c0af-5c1b-8b83-6cc6f2b2e80b', 'word_count': 1934, 'uri': 'nyt://article/554bf23d-c0af-5c1b-8b83-6cc6f2b2e80b'}, {'abstract': 'Police called it an act of domestic terrorism.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/gunman-kills-6-in-wisconsin-before-dying-in-shootout/', 'snippet': 'Police called it an act of domestic terrorism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sikh religious leaders had gathered in the lobby of the sprawling Sikh temple in suburban Milwaukee, and lunch was being prepared as congregants were arriving for Sunday services, Steven Yaccino, Michael Schwirtz and Marc Santora wrote in The New York Times. Instead of worshipers, though, an armed man stepped through the door and started firing, killing six people.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gunman Kills 6 in Wisconsin Gurdwara', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T04:59:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87df6de4-c1bb-5e8a-bf68-dc6d55a4804d', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87df6de4-c1bb-5e8a-bf68-dc6d55a4804d'}, {'abstract': 'FindTheBest, a product-and-service comparison engine, has built a sizable audience in the past year. Now it faces the challenge of trying to build a business.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/findthebest-a-comparison-engine-tries-to-build-a-business/', 'snippet': 'FindTheBest, a product-and-service comparison engine, has built a sizable audience in the past year. Now it faces the challenge of trying to build a business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kevin O’Connor recalls that he was met with mostly skepticism when he made the rounds of potential venture investors a few years ago. He wanted to build an online comparison engine, but not one for a single product or service like travel or restaurants. He wanted to cover hundreds of topics and products, from lawyers to nursing homes, smartphones to dog breeds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'FindTheBest: A Comparison Engine Tries to Build a Business', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Connor, Kevin", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FindTheBest.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T05:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e7a9e3f-d744-5587-b0e7-b85827327a69', 'word_count': 709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e7a9e3f-d744-5587-b0e7-b85827327a69'}, {'abstract': 'The alliance seeks to build on the results of an experimental treatment that trains a person’s immune system to kill cancer cells.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/business/novartis-and-penn-unite-on-anticancer-approach.html', 'snippet': 'The alliance seeks to build on the results of an experimental treatment that trains a person’s immune system to kill cancer cells.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The drugmaker Novartis and the University of Pennsylvania announced a research and licensing agreement early Monday that aims to bring to market a new approach to fighting cancer that has shown promising results in early trials.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'sour