els to Antarctica to research the limits of human physiology and psychology, moving forward the idea of the first manned mission to Mars.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/in-antarctica-dreaming-of-mars/', 'snippet': 'A scientist travels to Antarctica to research the limits of human physiology and psychology, moving forward the idea of the first manned mission to Mars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alexander Kumar, a physician and researcher at Concordia Station, writes from Antarctica, where he conducts scientific experiments for the European Space Agency’s human spaceflight program. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Antarctica, Dreaming of Mars', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mars (Planet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T11:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8386e13d-c017-55e5-b404-bf6fe0ae1337', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8386e13d-c017-55e5-b404-bf6fe0ae1337'}, {'abstract': 'Two of the most prominent London-based investment bankers of the last two decades have created a new company called Zaoui Capital, according to British regulatory documents.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/zaoui-brothers-establish-new-firm/', 'snippet': 'Two of the most prominent London-based investment bankers of the last two decades have created a new company called Zaoui