r': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Page, Wade Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oak Creek (Wis)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hate Crimes', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T14:42:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Goode and Serge F. Kovaleski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Serge', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Kovaleski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/693a6a99-d598-554e-b1fb-e2aad56e88ba', 'word_count': 1690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/693a6a99-d598-554e-b1fb-e2aad56e88ba'}, {'abstract': 'Is our model actually better for us as a country?The endpoint of our path is pretty much the elimination of people in factories.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/middle-east-journal-ill-stick-with-our-model-as-long-as-i-can/', 'snippet': 'Is our model actually better for us as a country?The endpoint of our path is pretty much the elimination of people in factories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is my last post on my trip to the Middle East. It’s going to be a while before I see any return on my investment, but the cost has not been outrageous. The trip cost about $4,100, including the two Gold Key fees. I’ll be reimbursed for about half of that by the State of Pennsylvania. We are in the process of putting together printed materials, and I’m mulling another trip in the fall to present them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Middle East Journal: I’ll Stick With Our Model (as Long as I Can)', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Productivity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tables', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dubai (United Arab Emirates)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T15:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34873635-5350-5564-9191-df8b72b393df', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34873635-5350-5564-9191-df8b72b393df'}, {'abstract': 'Live video of a news conference scheduled for 11 a.m. E.T. in Oak Creek, Wisconsin, where law enforcement officials are expected to provide more details about the shooting rampage at a Sikh temple.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/live-video-of-news-conference-about-sikh-shooting/', 'snippet': 'Live video of a news conference scheduled for 11 a.m. E.T. in Oak Creek, Wisconsin, where law enforcement officials are expected to provide more details about the shooting rampage at a Sikh temple.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a news conference on Monday from Oak Creek, Wisc., law enforcement officials provided more details on the shooting rampage at a sprawling Sikh temple in suburban Milwaukee that left six people dead and three people wounded. Our colleagues Steven Yaccino, Jennifer Preston and Marc Santora are following the investigation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of News Conference About Shooting at Sikh Temple in Wisconsin', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sikhs and Sikhism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T15:02:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6f32527-436e-5e90-886c-54a11d6326b0', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6f32527-436e-5e90-886c-54a11d6326b0'}, {'abstract': 'At the Bergdorf Goodman shoe salon, which celebrates its 111th anniversary this fall, it’s O.K. for a woman to fall for a heel.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/swept-off-her-feet/', 'snippet': 'At the Bergdorf Goodman shoe salon, which celebrates its 111th anniversary this fall, it’s O.K. for a woman to fall for a heel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When is a shoe not just a shoe? Why, when it’s a love object, a fetish or an alternate dream of self, of course. Shoes, like handbags, have grown in cultural stature over the last few decades, sending out coded and not so coded messages about the women who wear them: I am sexy, chic, kooky; I can walk without falling down in four-inch heels; I can afford to spend gobs of money on elusive brands and esoteric leathers. Manhattan department stores have, in the last few years, enlarged their shoe departments, in recognition of their allure and “recession-proof” sales potential, in many cases taking away space from what was once the main event — the clothes themselves.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '110', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Swept Off Her Feet', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Swept Off Her Feet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T15:23:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daphne Merkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daphne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Merkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53baceb9-e782-589e-89e7-8a883767d489', 'word_count': 1154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53baceb9-e782-589e-89e7-8a883767d489'}, {'abstract': 'Silence around money in your family leads to ignorance, not innocence. Carl Richards sketches it out.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/why-your-family-should-talk-about-money-more-often/', 'snippet': 'Silence around money in your family leads to ignorance, not innocence. Carl Richards sketches it out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Richards is a certified financial planner in Park City, Utah, and is the director of investor education at BAM Advisor Services. His book, “The Behavior Gap,” was published this year. His sketches are archived on the Bucks blog. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Your Family Should Talk About Money More Often', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T15:23:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'ty