sues for the military in recent years, and some service members are still resistant to gays and lesbians serving openly in the military.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/a-year-on-marines-divided-on-repeal-of-dont-ask-dont-tell/', 'snippet': 'The repeal of the policy has been one of the most controversial issues for the military in recent years, and some service members are still resistant to gays and lesbians serving openly in the military.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Marine Corps Recruit Training, Chase Davis, from Leesburg, Ga., was living a lie. He had developed a friendship with a Marine named Jackie and they had become inseparable during their first months of training. She was the only one he trusted and he confided his secret to her. He is gay. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Year on, Marines Divided on Repeal of ‘Don’t Ask, Don’t Tell’', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T15:33:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas James Brennan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'James', 'lastname': 'Brennan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/859bdde6-0e1a-5675-93d7-f3e5331ce9b5', 'word_count': 1534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/859bdde6-0e1a-5675-93d7-f3e5331ce9b5'}, {'abstract': 'Microsoft says its Bing search engine has caught up with, even surpassed, Google in search quality. It credits huge spending on computation-heavy artificial intelligence techniques. That requires getting a lot of data from diverse sources, though, and cutting a lot of deals. The costs may rise as search goes mobile.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/counting-the-mobile-costs-for-bing/', 'snippet': 'Microsoft says its Bing search engine has caught up with, even surpassed, Google in search quality. It credits huge spending on computation-heavy artificial intelligence techniques. That requires getting a lot of data from diverse sources, though,...', 'lead_paragraph': ' As search goes mobile, Microsoft could pay heavily for the ride.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/technology/03bits-bing/03bits-bing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/03/technology/03bits-bing/03bits-bing-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Counting the Mobile Costs for Bing', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T15:45:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b64eee91-2b06-5889-9a70-4c1d9ea9e21d', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b64eee91-2b06-5889-9a70-4c1d9ea9e21d'}, {'abstract': 'HCA, a for-profit hospital chain, said the inquiry centered on “medical necessity” of cardiology services at 10 of its hospitals, primarily in Florida.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/business/hca-discloses-us-inquiry-into-cardiology-services.html', 'snippet': 'HCA, a for-profit hospital chain, said the inquiry centered on “medical necessity” of cardiology services at 10 of its hospitals, primarily in Florida.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HCA Holdings’ stock fell about 4 percent Monday after the company disclosed that the cardiology practices at some of its Florida operations were under scrutiny by the Department of Justice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'HCA Discloses U.S. Inquiry Into Cardiology Services', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'HCA Discloses U.S. Inquiry Into Cardiology Services', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T15:49:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Creswell and Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Creswell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be5b994b-461f-5b0b-b55e-330017a05d8d', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be5b994b-461f-5b0b-b55e-330017a05d8d'}, {'abstract': 'Standard Chartered, motivated by the millions of dollars it reaped in fees, schemed with the Iranian government to launder $250 billion, New York’s banking regulator said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/business/standard-chartered-bank-accused-of-hiding-transactions-with-iranians.html', 'snippet': 'Standard Chartered, motivated by the millions of dollars it reaped in fees, schemed with the Iranian government to launder $250 billion, New York’s banking regulator said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Using its New York-based operations, a major British bank schemed with the Irani