proven that a former Citigroup banker, Brian H. Stoker, had violated securities laws. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Gets Encouragement, but Needs Something More', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stoker, Brian H', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tourre, Fabrice P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T16:33:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8e3f8f4-7f1a-51cb-a91c-04cee8d8725f', 'word_count': 1069, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8e3f8f4-7f1a-51cb-a91c-04cee8d8725f'}, {'abstract': 'The theater company Fishamble, the singer Wallis Bird and an exhibition of works by the painter Colette Murphy are among the fall season offerings.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/irish-arts-center-announces-new-season/', 'snippet': 'The theater company Fishamble, the singer Wallis Bird and an exhibition of works by the painter Colette Murphy are among the fall season offerings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The theater company Fishamble, the singer Wallis Bird and an exhibition of works by the painter Colette Murphy are among the fall season offerings announced by the Irish Arts Center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Irish Arts Center Announces New Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curran, Sean', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kinevane, Pat', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fishamble', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Irish Arts Center', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T16:36:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b82bced9-7331-5e69-9c82-4dcc543150bd', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b82bced9-7331-5e69-9c82-4dcc543150bd'}, {'abstract': 'The south of France lures a group of friends back again and again, but dishes celebrating the region’s summer produce can be replicated almost anywhere. Today: a grain salad with tomatoes, broad green beans and a tangy dressing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/health/nutrition/farro-salad-with-tomatoes-and-romano-beans.html', 'snippet': 'The south of France lures a group of friends back again and again, but dishes celebrating the region’s summer produce can be replicated almost anywhere. Today: a grain salad with tomatoes, broad green beans and a tangy dressing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month I had a reunion in Provence with friends who discovered this magical region of France with me more than 30 years ago. It was a true southern French vacation – we relaxed, we went to the market, we cooked. Market stalls were piled high with summer squash, tomatoes and eggplant, green beans — both regular ones and the flat ones that we call romano beans and that my Provençal market labeled cocos — onions of all kinds, braids of plump pink garlic, and leeks. Even the supermarket produce sections were inspiring. We bought short-grain rice from the Camargue, southwest of our area of Provence, for our risottos, and a local wheat berry called petit épeautre for chewy pilafs and grain salads. We ate peaches, apricots, amazing strawberries and melons for dessert and for breakfast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/science/06recipehealth/06recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/07/science/06recipehealth/06recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/science/06recipehealth/06recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/science/06recipehealth/06recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1332, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/science/06recipehealth/06recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/07/science/06recipehealth/06recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/science/06recipehealth/06recipehealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Provençal Reunion, With Vegetables at the Center of the Plate', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T16:39:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Fitness & Nutrition', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/0200de20-37e3-5f58-b4bb-4a34ff3f4d10', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0200de20-37e3-5f58-b4bb-4a34ff3f4d10'}, {'abstract': 'Two women won their respective professional categories at a national drag racing event for the first time on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/monday-motorsports-courtney-force-and-erica-enders-produce-history-at-the-dragstrip/', 'snippet': 'Two women won their respective professional categories at a national drag racing event for the first time on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having lost twice in final-round eliminator races this summer, Courtney Force, a rookie in the National Hot Rod Association’s Funny Car division and the daughter of the driver-owner John Force, was poised for a breakthrough entering the