and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T18:41:10+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/a8e8fb2e-30a0-50af-bc3c-d39ca3bb3571', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/a8e8fb2e-30a0-50af-bc3c-d39ca3bb3571'}, {'abstract': 'Jeffrey Monteiro and the rest of the women’s design team at Bill Blass were dismissed last week in the latest blow to a brand that has had more than its share of them in the last decade.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/bill-blass-fires-designer-again/', 'snippet': 'Jeffrey Monteiro and the rest of the women’s design team at Bill Blass were dismissed last week in the latest blow to a brand that has had more than its share of them in the last decade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeffrey Monteiro and the rest of the women’s design team at Bill Blass were dismissed last week in the latest blow to a brand that has had more than its share of them in the last decade. Since Mr. Blass retired in 1999, the struggling company has tried five different women’s designers (or six if you count that season in 2003 when the public relations director was ghost-designing a collection behind the scenes), but has been unable to recapture a high-end customer for its women’s wear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Blass Fires Designer. Again.', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monteiro, Jeffrey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T18:42:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b2100bf-6853-5e92-a316-70f67e07bdef', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b2100bf-6853-5e92-a316-70f67e07bdef'}, {'abstract': 'Maria Semple’s razor-sharp sendup of privileged Seattle is a novel about a fish-out-of-water mother, her Microsoft-star husband, their bright daughter and a back story shrouded in mystery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/books/whered-you-go-bernadette-a-maria-semple-novel.html', 'snippet': 'Maria Semple’s razor-sharp sendup of privileged Seattle is a novel about a fish-out-of-water mother, her Microsoft-star husband, their bright daughter and a back story shrouded in mystery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The free-range hilarity of “Where’d You Go, Bernadette” begins with Bee Branch’s report card from Galer Street School in Seattle, “a place where compassion, academics and global connectitude join together to create civic-minded citizens of a sustainable and diverse planet.” This school gives three grades: S for “Surpasses Excellence,” A for “Achieves Excellence” and W for “Working Towards Excellence.” So every kid is some kind of excellent. But Bee is a straight-S student all the way. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 609, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/arts/book/book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1218, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'capti