b7f8d-7928-57c0-ab8a-1165bc2d1cf6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/600b7f8d-7928-57c0-ab8a-1165bc2d1cf6'}, {'abstract': 'The income stagnation of the last decade stems, in simplest terms, from the economy’s overall sluggishness and the concentration of its modest gains among a small share of the population.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/a-slowdown-in-growth-an-increase-in-income-inequality/', 'snippet': 'The income stagnation of the last decade stems, in simplest terms, from the economy’s overall sluggishness and the concentration of its modest gains among a small share of the population.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The income stagnation of the last decade stems, in the simplest terms, from two factors: a slowdown in economic growth and a rise in inequality, which has concentrated the economy’s modest gains among a small share of the population. In this post, I want to look at both factors in a bit more detail.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Slowdown in Growth, an Increase in Income Inequality', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-06T19:10:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac37c39c-a00b-5090-87c5-c6788d4f70e5', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac37c39c-a00b-5090-87c5-c6788d4f70e5'}, {'abstract': 'Blacks are much more likely to elect aggressive care, and decline do-not-resuscitate orders than whites, but once given palliative care consultation, their preferences are significantly different.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/health/views/at-the-end-of-life-talk-helps-bridge-a-racial-divide.html', 'snippet': 'Blacks are much more likely to elect aggressive care, and decline do-not-resuscitate orders than whites, but once given palliative care consultation, their preferences are significantly different.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The family seated opposite me is tense. Having met at the bedside of a critically ill patient only moments earlier, we have gathered in a quiet alcove next to the intensive care unit to discuss what can only be bad news. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/science/07DNR_SPAN/07DNR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/07/science/07DNR_SPAN/07DNR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/science/07DNR_SPAN/07DNR_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/science/07DNR_SPAN/07DNR_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/science/07DNR_SPAN/07DNR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/07/science/07DNR_SPAN/07DNR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg