ue': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T00:22:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46f43e8f-6f8e-5387-b24e-542af5e2ad4a', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46f43e8f-6f8e-5387-b24e-542af5e2ad4a'}, {'abstract': 'Coming off a terrible performance in Anaheim, the Yankees starter came to Detroit determined to be more aggressive to right-handed hitters. He has been mostly effective since.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/hughess-last-start-in-detroit-marked-beginning-of-turnaround/', 'snippet': 'Coming off a terrible performance in Anaheim, the Yankees starter came to Detroit determined to be more aggressive to right-handed hitters. He has been mostly effective since.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — The last time Phil Hughes pitched against the Tigers in Detroit, he was coming off his worst outing of the season, a disastrous evening in his hometown, Anaheim, Calif., at the end of May, when he gave up seven runs in five and a third innings. The flight to Detroit was not a good one for Hughes, but once he arrived in the Midwest, he produced his best and perhaps most significant start of the season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hughes’s Last Start in Detroit Marked Beginning of Turnaround', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hughes, Phil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T00:26:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/674b15e1-b477-57b5-8c67-cf549a98e825', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/674b15e1-b477-57b5-8c67-cf549a98e825'}, {'abstract': 'The flyweight Marlen Esparza and the middleweight Claressa Shields, both of the United States women’s boxing team, won their bouts Monday to advance to the semifinals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/sports/olympics/olympic-womens-boxing-semifinals-for-esparza-and-shields.html', 'snippet': 'The flyweight Marlen Esparza and the middleweight Claressa Shields, both of the United States women’s boxing team, won their bouts Monday to advance to the semifinals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Two women on the United States boxing team — the flyweight Marlen Esparza and the middleweight Claressa Shields — are assured of winning Olympic medals after winning their bouts on Monday to advance to the semifinals.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/subBOXING/subBOXING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/subBOXING/subBOXING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/subBOXING/subBOXING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 537, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/subBOXING/subBOXING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1649, 'width': 864, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/subBOXING/subBOXING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/subBOXING/subBOXING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/subBOXING/subBOXING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Contrasting Styles Lead to Semifinals', 'kicker': 'Boxing | Women ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Contrasting Styles Lead to Semifinals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boxing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shields, Claressa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Esparza, Marlen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T00:31:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barry Bearak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bearak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a773d8ab-3642-53c6-a12e-ab0304368454', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a773d8ab-3642-53c6-a12e-ab0304368454'}, {'abstract': 'By this point in 2008, it would have been extremely unusual to not have any new state polls out on a given weekday, as happened on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/06/aug-6-pace-of-presidential-polling-slows-considerably-from-2008/', 'snippet': 'By this point in 2008, it would have been extremely unusual to not have any new state polls out on a given weekday, as happened on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As of 5 p.m. Monday, there were no new presidential polls out except for the two national tracking polls from Rasmussen Reports and Gallup. The Rasmussen numbers moved a tick toward President Obama, but it’s just not worth making much of a one-day shift in a tracking poll (a sustained shift over a week or longer would be more interesting). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 6: Pace of Presidential Polling Has Slowed Considerably From 2008', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T00:44:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e335a43-502a-5e0b-8278-d819a84ecff6', 'word_count': 916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e335a43-502a-5e0b-8278-d819a84ecff6'}, {'abstract': 'The mutual distaste between the American and Argentine men’s basketball teams manifested itself with shoves, elbows and heated exchanges, and the United States won to clinch its group’s top seed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/sports/olympics/united-states-mens-basketball-team-beats-argentina.html', 'snippet': 'The mutual distaste between the American and Argentine men’s basketball teams manifested itself with shoves, elbows and heated exchanges, and the United States won to clinch its group’s top seed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Beyond the shoves and the elbows and the mutual disdain on Monday night, the latest men’s basketball game/wrestling match between the United States and Argentina featured allegations of punches thrown. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/altHOOPS/altHOOPS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 530, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/altHOOPS/altHOOPS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 530}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/altHOOPS/altHOOPS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/altHOOPS/altHOOPS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1472, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/altHOOPS/altHOOPS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/altHOOPS/altHOOPS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/altHOOPS/altHOOPS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'th