f-5520-9be1-66b3c1640f4f', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a305a28-749f-5520-9be1-66b3c1640f4f'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on August 7, 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/pageoneplus/corrections-august-7-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on August 7, 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: August 7, 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T02:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/40cb1ae1-2674-55b6-b9a8-c1fcc2c1696f', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40cb1ae1-2674-55b6-b9a8-c1fcc2c1696f'}, {'abstract': 'An unnecessary amendment intended to clarify the status of religion in public places will only erode freedoms and create confusion in schools.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/opinion/prayer-in-missouri.html', 'snippet': 'An unnecessary amendment intended to clarify the status of religion in public places will only erode freedoms and create confusion in schools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Voters in Missouri on Tuesday will get to decide on an amendment to the State Constitution, which is supposedly intended to clarify the status of religion in Missouri’s public places. According to the amendment’s sponsor, Representative Mike McGhee, a Republican in the State House, the measure is needed to make clear that prayer is a right. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prayer in Missouri', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prayer in Missouri', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prayers and Prayer Books', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Religion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T02:01:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0a5fc65-0a6c-553d-a121-b0d854ea4be5', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0a5fc65-0a6c-553d-a121-b0d854ea4be5'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo deserves credit for stepping forward to protect 69,000 acres of timberland in the Adirondacks from commercial development.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/opinion/gov-cuomos-gift-to-nature.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo deserves credit for stepping forward to protect 69,000 acres of timberland in the Adirondacks from commercial development.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo has joined the honor role of governors and conservation groups that have stepped forward at critical moments to protect large parts of the Adirondacks from commercial development. On Sunday, Mr. Cuomo announced that the State of New York had bought 69,000 acres of timberland from the Nature Conservancy, including stretches of the upper Hudson River watershed. The purchase is the largest single addition in more than a century to the state’s “forever wild” forest preserve and will be open to hunting, fishing and recreational use but not to homebuilding and logging.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Governor’s Gift to Nature', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Governor’s Gift to Nature', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ADIRONDACK MOUNTAINS (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T02:04:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0fd8da0-0317-5776-8ab3-8cadabbb1d9a', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0fd8da0-0317-5776-8ab3-8cadabbb1d9a'}, {'abstract': 'Lt. Gen. James L. Terry, the new leader of the military joint command, said the shake-up in Afghanistan’s security leadership would not derail the transfer of authority to Afghan forces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/world/asia/us-general-sees-little-change-in-dismissal-of-afghan-ministers.html', 'snippet': 'Lt. Gen. James L. Terry, the new leader of the military joint command, said the shake-up in Afghanistan’s security leadership would not derail the transfer of authority to Afghan forces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Faced with a sudden shift in two critical Afghan security ministries after Parliament dismissed the departments’ chiefs over the weekend, the new leader of the international joint command here insisted that allied forces would not let the shake-up derail the transfer of authority to Afghan forces.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 938, 'width': 664, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumb