 Hotel in Sag Harbor doesn’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAG HARBOR, N.Y. — A lot of the talk at the American Hotel is about the American Hotel.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/nyregion/SUMMERNIGHT2/SUMMERNIGHT2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/nyregion/SUMMERNIGHT2/SUMMERNIGHT2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1352, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/nyregion/SUMMERNIGHT2/SUMMERNIGHT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/07/nyregion/SUMMERNIGHT2/SUMMERNIGHT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/nyregion/SUMMERNIGHT2/SUMMERNIGHT2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tales and Drinks Don’t Stop at the Rick’s Café of the Hamptons', 'kicker': 'Summer Nights', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tales and Drinks Don’t Stop At the Rick’s Café Of the Hamptons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamptons (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sag Harbor (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Hotel (Sag Harbor, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T02:54:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Applebome', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Applebome', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Series', '_id': 'nyt://article/31746910-2608-5a82-b8b4-c4ea501a80ca', 'word_count': 1023, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31746910-2608-5a82-b8b4-c4ea501a80ca'}, {'abstract': 'Workers striking at a Chinese-owned coal mine killed a Chinese supervisor when they hit him with a coal trolley, officials of the mine workers’ union said Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/world/africa/zambia-chinese-supervisor-dies-during-protest-at-mine.html', 'snippet': 'Workers striking at a Chinese-owned coal mine killed a Chinese supervisor when they hit him with a coal trolley, officials of the mine workers’ union said Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Workers striking at a Chinese-owned coal mine killed a Chinese supervisor when they hit him with a coal trolley, officials of the mine workers’ union said Monday. Employees at the Collum Coal Mine staged a protest over the weekend, demanding that their pay be raised to match Zambia’s new minimum wage for laborers of about $230 a month, which was announced last month. China has invested heavily in Zambia, a major producer of copper, coal and other minerals. Chinese companies in Zambia have long been accused of mistreating and underpaying their workers, and violence has broken out at the Collum mine during labor disputes in the past. President Michael Sata was elected last year on a largely anti-China platform, but has softened his position since taking office. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Zambia: Chinese Supervisor Dies During Protest at Mine', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Zambia: Chinese Supervisor Dies During Protest at Mine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zambia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T02:55:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f72b90b-4852-572a-bc63-f179bb2a722c', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f72b90b-4852-572a-bc63-f179bb2a722c'}, {'abstract': 'Suicide attacks against a military vehicle left four people dead and wounded three on Monday on the outskirts of Grozny, the capital of Chechnya, in Russia’s volatile North Caucasus region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/world/europe/russia-suicide-bombers-strike-at-military-unit-in-chechnya.html', 'snippet': 'Suicide attacks against a military vehicle left four people dead and wounded three on Monday on the outskirts of Grozny, the capital of Chechnya, in Russia’s volatile North Caucasus region.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Suicide attacks against a military vehicle left four people dead and wounded three on Monday on the outskirts of Grozny, the capital of Chechnya, in Russia’s volatile North Caucasus region. A spokesman for the Russian Interior Ministry said two suicide bombers ambushed an armored military van near a police checkpoint outside of the city. The dual explosions killed three members of a military unit and wounded three others. A fourth body, presumed to be that of one of the bombers, was also found at the scene. The bombing is the first suicide attack in Grozny in nearly a year. Moscow has been battling separatists in Chechnya since the 1990s, but a leader backed by the Kremlin has cracked down on the insurgency. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Suicide Bombers Strike at Military Unit in Chechnya', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Suicide Bombers Strike At Military Unit in Chechnya', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chechnya (Russia)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T02:57:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/714d01f1-4f2e-5568-a7f8-b8b1e3a744bb', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/714d01f1-4f2e-5568-a7f8-b8b1e3a744bb'}, {'abstract': 'The wife of Donald Suxho, the starting setter for the United States men’s volleyball team, can finally watch him at the Olympics after initially being denied a visa into London.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/sports/olympics/us-volleyball-teams-donald-suxho-has-wins-on-court-and-off.html', 'snippet': 'The wife of Donald Suxho, the starting setter for the United States men’s volleyball team, can finally watch him at the Olympics after initially being denied a visa into London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The stew of cultures served up by the Olympics is comfort food for Donald Suxho, the starting setter for the United States Olympic men’s volleyball team who immigrated from Albania in the 1990s and met his Ukrainian-born wife in 2005 while playing professionally in Greece. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/VOLLEYBALL1/VOLLEYBALL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/VOLLEYBALL1/VOLLEYBALL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/VOLLEYBALL1/VOLLEYBALL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/VOLLEYBALL1/VOLLEYBALL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1398, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/VOLLEYBALL1/VOLLEYBALL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/VOLLEYBALL1/VOLLEYBALL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/sports/VOLLEYBALL1/VOLLEYBALL1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For U.S. Volleyball Leader, Victories on Court and Of