s a white supremacist who performed in a racist rock band.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/wisconsin-killer-was-fueled-by-hate-driven-music/', 'snippet': 'Wade Michael Page, the suspect in the Sunday shooting was a white supremacist who performed in a racist rock band.', 'lead_paragraph': "“His music, Wade M. Page once said, was about ‘how the value of human life has been degraded by tyranny,'” Erica Goode and Serge F. Kovaleski wrote in The New York Times, of the music by the suspect of the Wisconsin shooting.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wisconsin Killer Was Fueled by Hate-Driven Music', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T04:54:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a15df8c2-c6c1-5286-821d-639ab2ab3638', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a15df8c2-c6c1-5286-821d-639ab2ab3638'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney and the Republican National Committee raised $25 million more in July than President Obama and his Democratic allies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/us/politics/romney-team-outpaces-obama-in-fund-raising-again.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney and the Republican National Committee raised $25 million more in July than President Obama and his Democratic allies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fund-raising machine behind Mitt Romney and the Republican Party once again outperformed President Obama and the Democrats last month, raising $25 million more in July than the president and his Democratic allies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit':