ve of silver and bronze); whether the state-sponsored sports system is both draconian and outmoded; and whether heartfelt patriotism has perhaps veered into a nationalistic fervor.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/too-much-olympic-fever-in-china/', 'snippet': 'China is vigorously debating whether it is overly obsessed with gold medals (while being somewhat dismissive of silver and bronze); whether the state-sponsored sports system is both draconian and outmoded; and whether heartfelt patriotism has perh...', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — China continues to lead the Olympic medal standings, just ahead of the United States, as the country tries to repeat its breakout performance at the 2008 Beijing Games. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/blogs/liu-rdv/liu-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/blogs/liu-rdv/liu-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1509, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Much Olympic Fever in China?', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu Xiang', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T05:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6a15155-2e7b-5711-9d42-540fc94f87fb', 'word_count': 1348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6a15155-2e7b-5711-9d42-540fc94f87fb'}, {'abstract': 'Born in Queens to Sikh immigrants, the author talks about the difficulties of maintaining a Sikh identity while living in the U.S.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/being-sikh-in-america/', 'snippet': 'Born in Queens to Sikh immigrants, the author talks about the difficulties of maintaining a Sikh identity while living in the U.S.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday, my wife and I were having a quiet brunch with friends at home in Pennsylvania when the phone started ringing. First my parents called from their home in Maryland. Then a cousin called from India. “Have you seen what’s on CNN? There’s been a shooting at a gurdwara in Wisconsin…” I felt a familiar emptiness. I had felt the same way after the morning of September 11, 2001. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Being Sikh in America', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sikhs and Sikhism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Page, Wade Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sikh Temple of Wisconsin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oak Creek (Wis)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T05:22:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amardeep Singh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amardeep', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11697fb3-0ad3-557a-be7c-76c62dd6490f', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11697fb3-0ad3-557a-be7c-76c62dd6490f'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/news-quiz-august-7-2012/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | August 7, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T05:59:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e1f3491-22c1-5bae-a76c-a55f5a22afda', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e1f3491-22c1-5bae-a76c-a55f5a22afda'}, {'abstract': 'Free-roaming dogs in India, bite millions of people annually, including vast numbers of children.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/where-streets-are-thronged-with-strays-baring-fangs/', 'snippet': 'Free-roaming dogs in India, bite millions of people annually, including vast numbers of children.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Victims of the surprise attacks limp into one of this city’s biggest public hospitals,” Gardiner Harris wrote in The New York Times, of dog bite victims in New Delhi. “Among the hundreds on a recent day were children cornered in their homes, students ambushed on their way to class and old men ambling back from work.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Streets Are Thronged With Strays Baring Fangs', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T06:56:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d557d37a-0ba8-5f3f-b324-80ba4fb6c367', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d557d37a-0ba8-5f3f-b324-80ba4fb6c367'}, {'abstract': 'A menace for a large population, dogs on Delhi streets are regularly fed by generous dog lovers.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/delhi-strays-thrive-on-affection-from-a-few/', 'snippet': 'A menace for a large population, dogs on Delhi streets are regularly fed by generous dog lovers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'India’s vast population of stray dogs mostly survives on mounds of garbage, but there are many Indians who routinely feed the dogs out of a sense of charity and love.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Delhi Strays Thrive on Affection From a Few', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T07:48:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_m