arning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/test-yourself-english-aug-7-2012/', 'snippet': 'Can you choose the best antonym for “ostentatious” as it is used in the article?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the article “For Wealthy Indian Family, Palatial House Is Not a Home.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, Aug. 7, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T08:33:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3aecc76f-d20e-5311-b6dc-54e7d80cd20a', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3aecc76f-d20e-5311-b6dc-54e7d80cd20a'}, {'abstract': 'The business of elite business schools is thriving, but they’re missing the economic opportunity of a lifetime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/magazine/is-michigan-state-really-better-than-yale.html', 'snippet': 'The business of elite business schools is thriving, but they’re missing the economic opportunity of a lifetime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the M.B.A. gold rush of the past three decades, the Yale School of Management accomplished the unthinkable. As the number of prospective business-school candidates shot up to more than 750,000 a year and tuition payments cleared $100,000, Harvard, Stanford, the University of Chicago and other schools hired star faculty members, built gleaming buildings, established themselves as global brands and brought in tens (and sometimes hundreds) of millions in profits to their universities each year. Meanwhile, Yale somehow lost money.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/16economy1_span/16economy1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 550, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/16economy1_span/16economy1_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 550}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/16economy1_span/mag-12Economy-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 892, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/16economy1_span/mag-12Economy-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1307, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/16economy1_span/16economy1_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/16economy1_span/16economy1_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/16economy1_span/16economy1_span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Michigan State Really Better Than Yale?', 'kicker': 'It’s the Economy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The $400,000 Résumé Booster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduate Schools and Students', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Davidson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davidson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d37ccab-87b1-5f7a-8444-2ffdb9c6d55b', 'word_count': 1522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d37ccab-87b1-5f7a-8444-2ffdb9c6d55b'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times staff photographer Doug Mills discusses the challenges and rewards of shooting the summer games in London this year.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/photographing-the-olympics-the-400mm-dash/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times staff photographer Doug Mills discusses the challenges and rewards of shooting the summer games in London this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times staff photographer Doug Mills is covering his fifth summer Olympics, and he has photographed seven winter games. He spoke with James Estrin by phone. The interview has been edited.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photographing the Olympics: The 400-Millimeter Dash', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phelps, Michael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T09:00:23+0000', 'document_type':