Abrupt Reversal At Standard Chartered', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Money Laundering', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Department of Financial Services (NYS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Standard Chartered Bank PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T11:36:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89ce9efd-1f79-5b92-aa6c-9e5b951aca8e', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89ce9efd-1f79-5b92-aa6c-9e5b951aca8e'}, {'abstract': 'Turkey wears its faith lightly but the demands of Ramadan can fuel tensions.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/tensions-in-turkey-during-ramadan/', 'snippet': 'Turkey wears its faith lightly but the demands of Ramadan can fuel tensions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — It is the holy month of Ramadan and, just before twilight, my Istanbul neighborhood fills with an intoxicating smell from the two wood-fire oven bakeries feverishly producing loaf after crusty loaf of seasonal bread. There’s a bustle of last-minute shopping and of people rushing to get home. When the sun finally goes down and the call to prayer comes, the streets are eerily silent except for the clink of cutlery from open apartment windows as families sit down to break the fast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Drumbeat of Ramadan', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Religion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ramadan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T11:41:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Finkel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finkel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b367c57b-8399-5695-b22e-2c06b614c5f4', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b367c57b-8399-5695-b22e-2c06b614c5f4'}, {'abstract': 'Examining earthquakes in the Barnett Shale from November 2009 to September 2011, a researcher identifies nearly eight times more quakes than had been reported, with the epicenters within two miles of drilling wells.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/near-fracking-wells-the-many-quakes-that-go-unfelt/', 'snippet': 'Examining earthquakes in the Barnett Shale from November 2009 to September 2011, a researcher identifies nearly eight times more quakes than had been reported, with the epicenters within two miles of drilling wells.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A series of small earthquakes made Halloween of 2008 an unusually scary one for people in the Dallas-Fort Worth area. While it has long been theorized that underground injections of fluids from oil and gas development operations could decrease friction and cause faults to slip, the quakes occurred in an area where people weren’t accustomed to tremors, renewing calls for research into the geological consequences of the booming natural gas industry in Texas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Near Injection Wells, Many Quakes Go Unfelt', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shale', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Academies of the United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Earthquake Information Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Texas at Austin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dallas (Tex)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T11:48:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna M. Foster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/748d6612-bf49-5cd1-ade6-9ac185d8d7a2', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/748d6612-bf49-5cd1-ade6-9ac185d8d7a2'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Schulze, the founder and owner of 20 percent of Minnesota-based Best Buy, has made a preliminary offer to take the electronics chain private. But the board holds all the cards, thanks to Minnesota law.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/minnesota-minefield-for-a-best-buy-deal/', 'snippet': 'Richard Schulze, the founder and owner of 20 percent of Minnesota-based Best Buy, has made a preliminary offer to take the electronics chain private. But the board holds all the cards, thanks to Minnesota law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before Richard Schulze can acquire and turn around Best Buy, he needs to come to terms with the State of Minnesota. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Minnesota Minefield for a Best Buy Deal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schulze, Richard M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Best BUY Company Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Credit Suisse Group A.G', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T11:55:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb976d91-9005-5564-9e9d-8dda8bd56cae', 'word_count': 1077, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb976d91-9005-5564-9e9d-8dda8bd56cae'}, {'abstract': 'The Renaissance scholars and married couple Stephen Greenblatt and Ramie Targoff are trying to renew the reputation of Thomas Browne, a 17th-century physician.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/books/thomas-browne-17th-century-author-draws-new-interest.html', 'snippet': 'The Renaissance scholars and married couple Stephen Greenblatt and Ramie Targoff are trying to renew the reputation of Thomas Browne, a 17th-century physician.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back when the English language was still young and impressionable, a London-born physician who took up the pen as a gentleman’s hobby made quite a dent, fathering a dictionary page’s worth of words we still use and tend to think of as ageless — “medical,” “suicide,” “exhaustion,” “hallucination” and “coma” among them.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/books/08browne/08browne-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 440, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/books/08browne/08browne-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 440, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/books/08browne/08browne-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/08/books/08browne/08browne-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/books/08browne/08browne-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviving Thomas Browne, an Expert on Oblivion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reviving Thomas Browne, an Expert on Oblivion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Browne, Thomas (1605-82)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Targoff, Ramie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenblatt, Stephen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T12:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78ebedcb-33aa-54dc-babd-2ad2bdaeea39', 'word_count': 1324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78ebedcb-33aa-54dc-babd-2ad2bdaeea39'}, {'abstract': '“Thus,” meaning “in this way” or “therefore,” is an adverb. “-Ly” is a suffix that turns an adjective into an adverb. Since “thus” is already an adverb, it has no need for “-ly.” So “thusly” is unnecessary — colloquial at best, illiterate in the view of many readers. Yet we’ve used “thusly” 10 times in the last year, including two days in a row last week. Let’s be careful.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/thus-just-so/', 'snippet': '“Thus,” meaning “in this way” or “therefore,” is an adverb. “-Ly” is a suffix that turns an adjective into an adverb. Since “thus” is already an adverb, it has no need for “-ly.” So “thusly” is unnecessary — colloquial at best, illiterate in the v...', 'lead_paragraph': '[PLEASE NOTE: After Deadline will be on vacation for two weeks and will return on Tuesday, Aug. 28.]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Thus,’ Just So', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T12:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip B. Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b891816a-3d12-5329-892c-65eeba159a31', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b891816a-3d12-5329-892c-65eeba159a31'}, {'abstract': 'Many say they wouldn’t be caught dead reading Cosmo outside of an airplane. But it turns out that reading Cosmo on a plane is way more challenging than reading it at home.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/10-things-i-learned-from-reading-every-last-word-of-cosmo/', 'snippet': 'Many say they wouldn’t be caught dead reading Cosmo outside of an airplane. But it turns out that reading Cosmo on a plane is way more challenging than reading it at home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I asked my friends about Cosmopolitan to prepare for my recent\xa0article in The Times Magazine, some said they wouldn’t be caught dead with a copy outside a doctor’s office or an airplane. But it turns out that reading Cosmo on an airplane — which I’m doing right now — is way, way more intense than reading it at home, because when you’re poring over an article about putting a [whatever] in or around your [whatever], and touching his [whatever] in [whatever method], while trying to lean over the magazine in such a way that hides the almost-naked people in the photographs … I don’t know. It was much easier at home! ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '10 Things I Learned From Reading Every Last Word of Cosmo', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cosmopolitan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T12:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edith Zimmerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17286e32-0f63-5c19-86b8-76ab6b9cb239', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17286e32-0f63-5c19-86b8-76ab6b9cb239'}, {'abstract': 'Abdul Rahim Wardak’s announcement on Tuesday came just three days after Parliament voted to dismiss him and another minister as part of an effort to end corruption.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/world/asia/afghan-defense-minister-announces-resignation.html', 'snippet': 'Abdul Rahim Wardak’s announcement on Tuesday came just three days after Parliament voted to dismiss him and another minister as part of an effort to end corruption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Afghanistan’s defense minister announced his resignation on Tuesday, just three days after Parliament voted to dismiss him and another minister as part of an effort to end corruption.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/world/asia/08kabul-cnd-1/08kabul-cnd-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/world/asia/08kabul-cnd-1/08kabul-cnd-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1483, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/world/asia/08kabul-cnd-1/08kabul-cnd-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/08/world/asia/08kabul-cnd-1/08kabul-cnd-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/world/asia/08kabul-cnd-1/08kabul-cnd-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghan Defense Minister Announces Resignation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghan Defense Minister Announces Resignation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wardak, Abdul Rahim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T12:06:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d236eae5-c2f9-54a5-b07f-339a1036274b', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d236eae5-c2f9-54a5-b07f-339a1036274b'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/opinion-report-the-right-to-pray/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: The Right to Pray', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T12:13:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fa1816d-c2c6-5d40-ae2a-0842593b457c', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fa1816d-c2c6-5d40-ae2a-0842593b457c'}, {'abstract': 'The $3.1 billion Dream Center, a riverfront complex that is expected to cover six large city blocks, has ambitions to rival the Broadway theater district and the West End in London.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/business/global/08iht-park08.html', 'snippet': 'The $3.1 billion Dream Center, a riverfront complex that is expected to cover six large city blocks, has ambitions to rival the Broadway theater district and the West End in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI — DreamWorks Animation SKG, the Hollywood studio behind hits like “Shrek,” “Kung Fu Panda” and “Madagascar,” said on Tuesday that it planned to develop a $3.1 billion cultural and entertainment district in Shanghai with a group of Chinese partners.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/business/STUDIO/STUDIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/08/business/STUDIO/STUDIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 289}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/business/STUDIO/STUDIO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 494, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/business/STUDIO/STUDIO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 988, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/business/STUDIO/STUDIO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/08/business/STUDIO/STUDIO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/business/STUDIO/STUDIO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'DreamWorks Animation Plans Shanghai Entertainment District', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'DreamWorks Animation Pushes Further Into China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Katzenberg, Jeffrey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DreamWorks Animation SKG Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T12:14:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza and Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7179392-56d1-54f3-9397-482c472feea9', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7179392-56d1-54f3-9397-482c472feea9'}, {'abstract': 'Live blogging Tuesday’s action at the Olympics, including track and field, soccer, gymnastics and beach volleyball.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/london-live-follow-tuesdays-action-at-the-olympics/', 'snippet': 'Live blogging Tuesday’s action at the Olympics, including track and field, soccer, gymnastics and beach volleyball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The track and field action kicked off on Tuesday and started with a crash: Liu Xiang of China tumbling out of the heats of the 110-meter hurdles, taking the 2004 gold medalist out of the competition and flashing back to his similar flameout in Beijing. The women’s hurdles provided legitimate excitement, with Sally Pearson of Australia just holding off American Dawn Harper, the 2008 gold medalist, by .02 seconds. Kellie Wells of the United States finished third and Lolo Jones was fourth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Live: Follow Tuesday’s Action at the Olympics', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T12:28:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/105bf426-9386-5f11-ae40-03c9a66e3e85', 'word_count': 7859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/105bf426-9386-5f11-ae40-03c9a66e3e85'}, {'abstract': 'Jeffrey Ross, a veteran performer at Comedy Central’s celebrity roasts, discusses the cable channel’s decision not to broadcast jokes he told at a tribute to Roseanne Barr that invoked the deadly shootings at a movie theater in Aurora, Colo.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/comedian-explains-his-act-after-comedy-central-cuts-jokes-on-colorado-shootings/', 'snippet': 'Jeffrey Ross, a veteran performer at Comedy Central’s celebrity roasts, discusses the cable channel’s decision not to broadcast jokes he told at a tribute to Roseanne Barr that invoked the deadly shootings at a movie theater in Aurora, Colo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The comedian Jeffrey Ross says that the tradition of the celebrity roast is “one of the last bastions of free speech.” But he’s not looking to go to battle over a bit he performed at a recent tribute to Roseanne Barr that invoked the deadly shootings in an Aurora, Colo., movie theater — material that Comedy Central will not show when the tribute event is broadcast on Sunday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comedian Explains His Act After Comedy Central Cuts Jokes on Colorado Shootings', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aurora, Colo, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barr, Roseanne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paterno, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ross, Jeffrey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comedy Central', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Aurora (Colo)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T12:59:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3573abbc-0601-59c1-a353-5156eccea16c', 'word_count': 914, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3573abbc-0601-59c1-a353-5156eccea16c'}, {'abstract': 'A digital photo can come in different color modes, and the that works best depends on what you want to do with the image.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07