, the men’s team sat in business class on the flight to Europe while the women’s team sat in economy class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Japan’s national soccer teams made waves on their way to the Olympics last month when the men’s team, which is made up mostly of under-23 players, sat in business class on the flight to Europe while the women’s team, which won last year’s World Cup, sat in economy class.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Japan’s Soccer Teams, a Question of Equality', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T14:28:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82f61d08-85c5-57f2-9e40-0cc5c843b385', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82f61d08-85c5-57f2-9e40-0cc5c843b385'}, {'abstract': 'Seemingly out of nowhere, Knight Capital made a huge amount of trades last week that ended up saddling the firm with $440 million of losses. The episode tests the limits of what a market can possibly know. And that’s why it’s uniquely unnerving.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/knight-of-the-living-dread/', 'snippet': 'Seemingly out of nowhere, Knight Capital made a huge amount of trades last week that ended up saddling the firm with $440 million of losses. The episode tests the limits of what a market can possibly know. And that’s why it’s u