 of the weird weather so much of the world is experiencing can be attributed to global warming, and how much to the natural variability of climate? The question has political implications as well as scientific ones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James E. Hansen, the irrepressible NASA scientist who was among the first to sound the alarm about human-caused global warming, has roiled the scientific community again with a new scientific paper explicitly linking high concentrations of carbon dioxide and other heat-trapping gases to recent severe heat waves and drought.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Parse Climate Change and Extreme Weather?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temperature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hansen, James E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T14:55:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a870369c-76f5-5b38-9aa8-ccf5f1f48c19', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a870369c-76f5-5b38-9aa8-ccf5f1f48c19'}, {'abstract': 'The highest rates are among black children with disabilities, which can include learning difficulties.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/education/analysis-examines-disabled-students-suspensions.html', 'snippet': 'The highest rates are among black children with disabilities, which can include learning difficulties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Students with disabilities are almost twice as likely to be suspended from school as nondisabled students, with the highest rates among black children with disabilities.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspensions Are Higher for Disabled Students, Federal Data Indicate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suspensions Are Higher For Disabled Students, Federal Data Indicate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Discipline (Students)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Los Angeles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T14:59:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Motoko Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a6390b9-e2c7-5d5d-8b1b-aec13118b0eb', 'word_count': 1021, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a6390b9-e2c7-5d5d-8b1b-aec13118b0eb'}, {'abstract': 'Designer Markus Lupfer and Asos.com have collaborated on a 10-piece, all leather, kaleidoscope-patterned collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/the-new-black/', 'snippet': 'Designer Markus Lupfer and Asos.com have collaborated on a 10-piece, all leather, kaleidoscope-patterned collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years the London-based designer Markus Lupfer and the British retailer Asos.com have made cool and quirky clothes for women — at very different price points (Lupfer, high; Asos, low). Now they’ve gone into business together and are meeting in the middle, offering a 10-piece, all leather, kaleidoscope-patterned collection for the Asos Black label (available in October). “I love the cutout skater dress,” Lupfer says. “It is so cute and fun.” Along the lines of Lupfer’s own ready-to-wear brand — which features glitter-bombed cocktail dresses and loudmouthed graphic tops — Asos Black includes tailored track pants, boxy shell tops, hot-shorts and pencil skirts, as well as pouchettes and utilitarian heels to complete the look. The collaboration hits what Lupfer calls the “nonintimidating” (read: cost-effective) side of high fashion, which is probably why he can comfortably add, “The girls in my office want it all.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '92', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New Black', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The New Black', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T15:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd6e03e6-75ae-54da-ad97-741f94b49585', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd6e03e6-75ae-54da-ad97-741f94b49585'}, {'abstract': 'An erroneous notice informed some voters on the Upper West Side that their polling place had moved a couple miles away.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/to-the-polls-ye-sons-of-freedom-and-bring-a-metrocard/', 'snippet': 'An erroneous notice informed some voters on the Upper West Side that their polling place had moved a couple miles away.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Your Pollsite May Have Changed,” said the glossy mailer from the Board of Elections that arrived last week at the homes of nearly 1,200 active registered voters (including this reporter) who live in the West 60s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To the Polls, Ye Sons of Freedom! And Bring a MetroCard.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Board of Elections (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T15:05:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9318aa41-6c03-5662-975c-0e2c953c29b9', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9318aa41-6c03-5662-975c-0e2c953c29b9'}, {'abstract': 'Dispatching the personal representative of its paramount leader to Damascus, Iran moved to reframe the conflict as part of a battle with the United States and others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/world/middleeast/fighting-grows-more-intense-in-aleppo-syria.html', 'snippet': 'Dispatching the personal representative of its paramount leader to Damascus, Iran moved to reframe the conflict as part of a battle with the United States and others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT — Iran moved on Tuesday to reframe the Syrian conflict as part of a wider battle with the United States and other hostile world powers, dispatching the personal representative of its paramount leader, Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, to Damascus for a televised display of solidarity with Syria’s president as battles raged and dozens of Iranian hostages in rebel custody were threatened with death.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1298, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/08/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/world/SYRIA/SYRIA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Envoy Casts Syria as Part of Wider Conflict', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran Envoy Casts Syria as Part of Wider Conflict', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'p