r-capita basis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grenada Moves to the Top of This List', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Grenada', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T15:55:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b4b3ad0-1602-5f5b-8df2-34ca9d869976', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b4b3ad0-1602-5f5b-8df2-34ca9d869976'}, {'abstract': 'The sophisticated flavors and textures that this dish offers may convert those who think they don’t like leeks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/health/nutrition/elizabeths-braised-leeks-with-parmesan-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'The sophisticated flavors and textures that this dish offers may convert those who think they don’t like leeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My friend Elizabeth tells me that even people who think they don’t like leeks like this dish. The leeks are braised in wine and water or stock until soft and golden, then topped with Parmesan and run under a broiler, so you get a crunchy layer on top of soft cooked leeks. One of the tricks here is to discard the outer layers that become papery when you cook them, so that the whole leek will be soft and easy to cut through.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/07/science/07recipehealth/07recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'hei