io', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/150595aa-d425-57f3-a67a-8806c84439e6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/150595aa-d425-57f3-a67a-8806c84439e6'}, {'abstract': 'Jan Ebeling rode Rafalca in the Grand Prix Special portion of the Olympic dressage finals but did not qualify for the Grand Prix Freestyle.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/rafalca-does-not-advance-in-olympic-dressage/', 'snippet': 'Jan Ebeling rode Rafalca in the Grand Prix Special portion of the Olympic dressage finals but did not qualify for the Grand Prix Freestyle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — As he rode into the ring on his horse, Rafalca, the equestrian Jan Ebeling blew a kiss to a few women in the stands he calls the three amigos: his wife, Amy Ebeling; Beth Meyer; and Ann Romney, whose husband, Mitt, is the presumptive presidential candidate for the Republican Party.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rafalca Does Not Advance in Olympic Dressage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Ann', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T16:49:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d42a933f-3c36-510f-b10e-c680a546ba71', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d42a933f-3c36-510f-b10e-c680a546ba71'}, {'abstract': 'Kevin Hart, Bill Maher, Robin Williams and Aziz Ansari are among the funnymen who will be featured at this year’s New York Comedy Festival, which runs from Nov. 7 through 11.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/new-york-comedy-festival-unveils-2012-lineup/', 'snippet': 'Kevin Hart, Bill Maher, Robin Williams and Aziz Ansari are among the funnymen who will be featured at this year’s New York Comedy Festival, which runs from Nov. 7 through 11.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kevin Hart, Bill Maher, Robin Williams and Aziz Ansari are among the funnymen who will be featured at this year’s New York Comedy Festival, its organizers announced on Tuesday. The five-day festival, which is produced by Carolines on Broadway in association with Comedy Central, will kick off its ninth year on Nov. 7, beginning with a Next Big Thing event at the Paley Center for Media and an interview with Ricky Gervais, in conversation with John Hodgman, at Town Hall.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Comedy Festival Unveils 2012 Lineup', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Comedy Festival Unveils Lineup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ansari, Aziz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gervais, Ricky', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hart, Kevin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maher, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oswalt, Patton', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Robin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APOLLO THEATER', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ninety-Second Street Y', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T17:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01719f2f-dbea-538f-8c69-f6124f3480d7', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01719f2f-dbea-538f-8c69-f6124f3480d7'}, {'abstract': 'In honor of Bergdorf Goodman’s 111th anniversary, T’s Jane Herman delivers The Daily Shoe from the store’s famous shoe salon.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/the-daily-shoe-ysl/', 'snippet': 'In honor of Bergdorf Goodman’s 111th anniversary, T’s Jane Herman delivers The Daily Shoe from the store’s famous shoe salon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In honor of Bergdorf Goodman’s 111th anniversary, T’s Jane Herman delivers The Daily Shoe from the store’s famous shoe salon. Today’s pick: A gold-toed flat from YSL.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Daily Shoe | YSL', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bergdorf Goodman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T17:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ca952bd-0ab2-537e-9a42-d1603ec3a55c', 'word_count': 40, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ca952bd-0ab2-537e-9a42-d1603ec3a55c'}, {'abstract': 'For a fee, American Airlines will deliver baggage to the address of a passenger’s choosing.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/americans-bag-delivery-lets-you-skip-the-carousel/', 'snippet': 'For a fee, American Airlines will deliver baggage to the address of a passenger’s choosing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First there were fees for checked bags. Then for carry-ons. Now, American Airlines is adding a fee, but this time it’s for a perk that had not been previously included in the price of a ticket: baggage delivery to the address of a passenger’s choosing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American’s Bag Delivery Lets You Skip the Carousel', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luggage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN AIRLINES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T17:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Drake', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drake', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a24849be-5c25-5971-b7a7-a22516882195', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a24849be-5c25-5971-b7a7-a22516882195'}, {'abstract': 'Small-business owners are receiving millions of dollars in rebates thanks to the health care overhaul. What these owners can do with the money is not entirely clear.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/the-affordable-care-act-rebate-checks-are-in-the-mail-now-what/', 'snippet': 'Small-business owners are receiving millions of dollars in rebates thanks to the health care overhaul. What these owners can do with the money is not entirely clear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some small businesses were among the most strident opponents of the Affordable Care Act, but by Wednesday, many of these businesses will have received checks totaling $321 million from their health insurance providers, courtesy of the health care overhaul that became law in 2010. The checks are rebates from insurers that did not spend at least 80 percent of the premiums they collected from small group plans on either actual health care expenses or improving the quality of health care, a provision known as the medical loss ratio rule.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Affordable Care Act Rebate Checks Are in the Mail: Now What?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labor Department (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T17:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/648b3622-4b83-50b6-8324-5862d20e3009', 'word_count': 1227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/648b3622-4b83-50b6-8324-5862d20e3009'}, {'abstract': 'The Iranian government said it would hold the United States responsible for the fate of a group of Iranians held by Syrian rebels following an artillery attack that reportedly killed three of them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/world/middleeast/iran-warns-united-states-on-fate-of-hostages-in-syria.html', 'snippet': 'The Iranian government said it would hold the United States responsible for the fate of a group of Iranians held by Syrian rebels following an artillery attack that reportedly killed three of them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Iran said Tuesday that it was holding the United States responsible for the fate of a group of Iranians held by Syrian rebels, as the highest-ranking Iranian official to visit Syria since the antigovernment uprising began there arrived in Damascus to show support for President Bashar al-Assad and attempt to secure the release of the hostages.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Warns U.S. on Fate of Hostages in Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran Warns U.S. on Fate of Hostages in Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Larijani, Ali', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jalili, Saeed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T17:06:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article