2/08/08/business/pfizer-settles-us-charges-of-overseas-bribery.html', 'snippet': 'The pharmaceutical company and a subsidiary will pay a total of $60 million to resolve accusations that it paid doctors in several countries to prescribe its drugs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission announced on Tuesday that it had reached a $45 million settlement with Pfizer to resolve charges that subsidiaries of Pfizer and Wyeth, which it acquired in 2009, bribed overseas doctors and other health care workers to increase sales of their drugs.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pfizer Settles U.S. Charges of Bribing Doctors Abroad', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pfizer Settles U.S. Charges Of Bribing Doctors Abroad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pfizer Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T17:31:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Thomas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c997cd0-609c-5938-9b7c-4fb942a42641', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c997cd0-609c-5938-9b7c-4fb942a42641'}, {'abstract': 'Is prenatal depression common knowledge, or does the myth of the perpetually glowing, happy expectant mother still prevail?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/pregnant-depressed-and-surprised/', 'snippet': 'Is prenatal depression common knowledge, or does the myth of the perpetually glowing, happy expectant mother still prevail?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A pregnancy (especially a first pregnancy) is in so many ways a rabbit hole.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pregnant, Depressed and Surprised', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T17:33:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fa94b19-a286-5555-be70-44e1e5322abd', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fa94b19-a286-5555-be70-44e1e5322abd'}, {'abstract': 'Alistair Brownlee won the men’s triathlon and his brother Jonathan finished third, giving Britain its first medals in the event.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/sports/olympics/brownlee-brothers-give-britain-first-medals-in-triathlon.html', 'snippet': 'Alistair Brownlee won the men’s triathlon and his brother Jonathan finished third, giving Britain its first medals in the event.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — To win a medal at the men’s Olympic triathlon Tuesday, it took a band of brothers, not all of them related. Alistair Brownlee, the prohibitive favorite, delivered Britain its 19th gold medal of these Games with an 11-second victory over Javier Gómez of Spain. Brownlee’s younger brother, Jonathan, was 31 seconds back, in third.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/sports/08triathlon-brownlee-brothers/08triathlon-brownlee-brothers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/sports/08triathlon-brownlee-brothers/08triathlon-brownlee-brothers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1521, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/sports/08triathlon-brownlee-brothers/08triathlon-brownlee-brothers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/08/sports/08triathlon-brownlee-brothers/08triathlon-brownlee-brothers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/sports/08triathlon-brownlee-brothers/08triathlon-brownlee-brothers-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'British Brothers Are Again Atop an Increasingly Popular Sport', 'kicker': 'Triathlon | Men', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Brothers Are Again Atop an Ever-Escalating Sport', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brownlee, Alistair', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triathlon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brownlee, Jonathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gomez, Javier', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T17:37:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e31e74f-c63b-5014-a67e-e4eea47c7162', 'word_count': 1033, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e31e74f-c63b-5014-a67e-e4eea47c7162'}, {'abstract': 'Our second post on using theater techniques to help students work with Times content. This one highlights a technique called Tableau.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/scenes-in-tableau-drama-strategies-to-use-with-any-days-times-part-2/', 'snippet': 'Our second post on using theater techniques to help students work with Times content. This one highlights a technique called Tableau.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week is Drama Week on The Learning Network, and we’ve teamed with David Kener, a teacher and former executive director of the American Place Theater Literature to Life Program, to bring you different strategies daily for using theater techniques in classes across the curriculum. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scenes in Tableau: Drama Strategies to Use With Any Day’s Times (Part 2)', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T17:53:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Kener and Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae61ab9c-06cc-57c5-bda8-95722236504c', 'word_count': 1031, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae61ab9c-06cc-57c5-bda8-95722236504c'}, {'abstract': 'New York Historical Society announces a major exhibition this fall on World War ii.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/fall-exhibit-to-focus-on-world-war-ii-and-new-york-city/', 'snippet': 'New York Historical Society announces a major exhibition this fall on World War ii.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Helping to fill the seemingly endless appetite for information about World War II, the New-York Historical Society is planning a major exhibition on the conflict’s effect on the homefront this fall.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Historical Society Exhibit to Focus on World War II and New York City', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Historical Society Plans World War II Exhibition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T17:53:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb98e182-c180-59f7-93c9-6c684123bff9', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb98e182-c180-59f7-93c9-6c684123bff9'}, {'abstract': 'The news program has left its competitors behind during its broadcasts from London during the Games. It soared to an enormous total viewer number: 10.85 million, about three million more than its recent average.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/nbc-nightly-news-adds-three-million-viewers-from-olympics/', 'snippet': 'The news program has left its competitors behind during its broadcasts from London during the Games. It soared to an enormous total viewer number: 10.85 million, about three million more than its recent average.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nothing has helped the recently flagging fortunes of NBC News like the injection of large audiences after coverage of the Olympics on the network this summer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘NBC Nightly News’ Adds Three Million Viewers From Olympics', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelley, Scott', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sawyer, Diane', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Brian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC News', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T17:55:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73426ffb-b648-5e15-9919-5fece2365c9f', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73426