rimaries-in-missouri-and-michigan-among-those-to-watch/', 'snippet': 'On Tuesday, voters in Missouri, Michigan, Washington and Kansas will pick their candidates for the House and Senate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nope, sorry. The Congressional primaries are not over yet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congressional Primaries in Missouri and Michigan Among Those to Watch', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akin, Todd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burner, Darcy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carnahan, Russ', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cassis, Nancy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarke, Hansen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clay, Bill', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clay, William Lacy Jr', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conyers, John Jr', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Durant, W Clark', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCaskill, Claire', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCotter, Thaddeus G', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peters, Gary', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruderman, Laura', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stabenow, Debbie', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steelman, Sarah', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T18:11:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e06f97f-2a0a-55d6-93b3-301f219082f1', 'word_count': 1090, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e06f97f-2a0a-55d6-93b3-301f219082f1'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Mann is considered by many to be the world’s first cyborg. Mr. Mann sits down to discuss augmented reality, wearable Apple and Google products, and the idea of connecting computers to the brain.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/one-on-one-steve-mann-wearable-computing-pioneer/', 'snippet': 'Steve Mann is considered by many to be the world’s first cyborg. Mr. Mann sits down to discuss augmented reality, wearable Apple and Google products, and the idea of connecting computers to the brain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steve Mann is considered by many to be the world’s first cyborg. He has been using wearable computers that assist his vision since the 1970s. Now he wears a display screen over his right eye and is connected to a computer and the Internet. In this edited interview, he discusses “mediated reality”; the coming wearable-computing wars among Apple, Google and RIM; and the\xa0brain-computer interface.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One on One: Steve Mann, Wearable Computing Pioneer', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wearable Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mann, Steve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T18:15:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fedf2d4-1538-55b2-8f5a-920286c6f35b', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fedf2d4-1538-55b2-8f5a-920286c6f35b'}, {'abstract': 'Deutsche Grammophon is about to release Robert Lepage’s gigantic production of of Wagner’s “Ring” cycle at the Metropolitan Opera on eight DVDs or five Blu-ray discs.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/an-outsize-ring-on-a-living-room-scale/', 'snippet': 'Deutsche Grammophon is about to release Robert Lepage’s gigantic production of of Wagner’s “Ring” cycle at the Metropolitan Opera on eight DVDs or five Blu-ray discs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have seen segments of the Metropolitan Opera’s latest production of Wagner’s “Ring” cycle, directed by Robert Lepage, from various perspectives in addition to performances in the house: “Das Rheingold” projected onto large screens in Times Square (in a deluge) and in an HD screening at a movie theater in Ellsworth, Me.; “Die Walküre” in HD at a theater in Manhattan. Soon I will be able to view it in the intimacy of my living room, and you will too, on eight DVDS or five Blu-ray discs, to be released by Deutsche Grammophon on Sept. 11.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Outsize ‘Ring’ on a Living-Room Scale', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', '