e has announced the nine finalists, one in each of those categories, for its “2012 Manliest Restaurants in America” competition.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'So Where do Guys Eat, After All?', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T18:28:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e332e8c3-9d0a-5861-92fc-75b29525604f', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e332e8c3-9d0a-5861-92fc-75b29525604f'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Deary, a motor pacer for keirin races, dynamic events run at blazing speed with many crashes, follows custom by riding slowly on purpose.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/sports/olympics/olympic-track-cycling-pacer-has-no-need-for-speed.html', 'snippet': 'Peter Deary, a motor pacer for keirin races, dynamic events run at blazing speed with many crashes, follows custom by riding slowly on purpose.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The capacity crowd at the Olympic Velodrome on Tuesday roars in anticipation. Six highly trained and fit cyclists set off on a race for gold.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/sports/MOTORBIKE/MOTORBIKE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/08/sports/MOTORBIKE/MOTORBIKE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'cre