b35-aa9c7ddc617b'}, {'abstract': 'As rescue workers raced to help after the worst flooding in Manila since 2009, residents turned to social media to pinpoint the locations of those trapped.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/filipinos-turn-to-twitter-as-a-lifeline-after-severe-flooding/', 'snippet': 'As rescue workers raced to help after the worst flooding in Manila since 2009, residents turned to social media to pinpoint the locations of those trapped.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The worst flooding since 2009 has swamped major streets in Manila and nine provincial areas around the city, as rescue workers used rafts and boats to try to rescue people trapped on rooftops or in buildings. As my colleague Floyd Whaley writes, more than 50 people have been killed and at least 250,000 have been evacuated in the last week in the flooding, which was set off by a series of storms and monsoon rains', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Filipinos Turn to Twitter as a Lifeline After Severe Flooding', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manila (Philippines)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T20:03:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a13287e-eb58-5514-ace3-03ba49ecd585', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a13287e-eb58-5514-ace3-03ba49ecd585'}, {'abstract': 'Debate the virtues of a thicker, sturdier crust, which has fallen out of style in Neapolitan-mad New York in recent years.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/thick-crust-or-thin-whats-your-slice/', 'snippet': 'Debate the virtues of a thicker, sturdier crust, which has fallen out of style in Neapolitan-mad New York in recent years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week Pete Wells reviews Nicoletta, the East Village pizzeria where the chef Michael White had hoped, he said, to conjure the Wisconsin pizza of his youth, a pie with a crust that’s not too thick or too thin, cut into squares. What he is serving instead has a crust that, while not deep-dish, approaches that heft, sliced into the usual triangles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thick Crust or Thin: What’s Your Slice?', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T20:04:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/465ed443-0412-5f7e-ad99-07bd653efe59', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/465ed443-0412-5f7e-ad99-07bd653efe59'}, {'abstract': 'Oliver Peoples has paired up with Parabellum, the leather goods company, for a limited line of two unisex sunglasses, resulting in a curious intersection of rugged and polish.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/sunglasses-from-oliver-peoples-and-parabellum/', 'snippet': 'Oliver Peoples has paired up with Parabellum, the leather goods company, for a limited line of two unisex sunglasses, resulting in a curious intersection of rugged and polish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oliver Peoples has paired up with Parabellum, the leather goods company, for a limited line of two unisex sunglasses, resulting in a curious intersection of rugged and polish.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunglasses From Oliver Peoples and Parabellum', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunglasses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oliver Peoples', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T20:13:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corbin Chamberlin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corbin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chamberlin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8cccc6e-8a0f-522c-929c-73ff3991f0bb', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8cccc6e-8a0f-522c-929c-73ff3991f0bb'}, {'abstract': 'Sally Pearson of Australia, the 100-meter hurdles silver medalist in 2008, won gold. The Americans Dawn Harper, Kellie Wells and Lolo Jones swept the next three places.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/sports/olympics/sally-pearson-wins-hurdles-lolo-jones-track-and-field.html', 'snippet': 'Sally Pearson of Australia, the 100-meter hurdles silver medalist in 2008, won gold. The Americans Dawn Harper, Kellie Wells and Lolo Jones swept the next three places.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — As Australia’s Sally Pearson sailed over hurdle after hurdle Tuesday, a crowd of 80,000 at Olympic Stadium erupted in a roar, but she said she could not hear a thing.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '