how up to the Olympics, find some pins and start trading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – For Olympic athletes, glory comes wrapped in gold, silver and bronze. For some of the rest of us, it comes in the form of an enamel pin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Beginner’s Guide to Olympic Pin Collecting', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memorabilia and Souvenirs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T21:44:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab4f4bfe-0a61-505d-8371-3ae9677fb349', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab4f4bfe-0a61-505d-8371-3ae9677fb349'}, {'abstract': 'The Public Theater said that its production of “Into the Woods” at the Delacorte Theater in Central Park would run through Sept. 1.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/theater/footnotes.html', 'snippet': 'The Public Theater said that its production of “Into the Woods” at the Delacorte Theater in Central Park would run through Sept. 1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Public Theater said that its production of “Into the Woods” at the Delacorte Theater in Central Park would run through Sept. 1, a week longer than originally scheduled. The Stephen Sondheim-James Lapine musical began previews on July 24 and officially opens Thursday. ... In other fairy tale news, “Rodgers & Hammerstein’s Cinderella,” already announced for Broadway with Laura Osnes as Cinderella and Santino Fontana as the Prince, has a theater and an opening date. The musical will start previews at the Broadway Theater on Jan. 21 with an official opening night of Feb. 21, according to a release.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Footnotes', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Footnotes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T21:45:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/badf30cd-8285-5fac-aa7d-03ba0b10468e', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/badf30cd-8285-5fac-aa7d-03ba0b10468e'}, {'abstract': 'The Chamber Orchestra of Europe, led by Yannick Nézet-Séguin, gave a vibrant performance on Sunday in the Mostly Mozart Festival at Alice Tully Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/arts/music/mostly-mozart-and-chamber-orchestra-of-europe.html', 'snippet': 'The Chamber Orchestra of Europe, led by Yannick Nézet-Séguin, gave a vibrant performance on Sunday in the Mostly Mozart Festival at Alice Tully Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Chamber Orchestra of Europe took its first steps into the spotlight, it left a mixed impression. This was an ensemble of young musicians, mostly alumni of the European Union Youth Orchestra, who wanted to continue working together as a professional group, and you wanted to root for them. They gave you plenty to work with: on their early recordings and tours the playing was energetic and trim, but it could also be cautious and prim, as if only the most finely polished performances were acceptable. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/08mozart/08mozart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/08mozart/08mozart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/08mozart/08mozart-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/08mozart/08mozart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1437, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/08mozart/08mozart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/08mozart/08mozart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/08mozart/08mozart-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Highlighting Contrasts and Not Holding Back', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Highlighting Contrasts and Not Holding Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mostly Mozart Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'},