. One of these governors was, as the mayor of London once put it, a guy called Mitt Romney.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gutting Welfare', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Welfare (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T21:56:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7982651e-07c5-5dd2-a2ef-affab80f6bf8', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7982651e-07c5-5dd2-a2ef-affab80f6bf8'}, {'abstract': 'Vail International Dance Festival commissions works, and Monday’s program in Colorado featured world premieres by Brian Brooks, Matthew Neenan, Doug Varone and Christopher Wheeldon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/arts/dance/vail-international-dance-festival-presents-4-premieres.html', 'snippet': 'Vail International Dance Festival commissions works, and Monday’s program in Colorado featured world premieres by Brian Brooks, Matthew Neenan, Doug Varone and Christopher Wheeldon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VAIL, Colo. — Even on a rainy evening here, the walk from the center of this town to the Gerald R. Ford Amphitheater, where most performances of the Vail International Dance Festival take place, is a thrill for the senses: you pass through pine trees beside a rushing mountain stream amid the Rockies. And after several performances, the walk home features a sky full of unusually bright stars.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/DIRECTIONS/DIRECTIONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/DIRECTIONS/DIRECTIONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/DIRECTIONS/DIRECTIONS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 585, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/DIRECTIONS/DIRECTIONS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1170, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/DIRECTIONS/DIRECTIONS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/DIRECTIONS/DIRECTIONS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/DIRECTIONS/DIRECTIONS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gulping the Heady, Thin Air of Creativity', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gulping the Heady, Thin Air of Creativity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neenan, Matthew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Varone, Doug', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Brian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheeldon, Christopher', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T21:57:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f350f76c-92a6-5adc-99f6-829aa192ccdf', 'word_count': 1033, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f350f76c-92a6-5adc-99f6-829aa192ccdf'}, {'abstract': 'To get every member of my family sitting down in one place and looking at each other every day, I compromised on dinner and created the ‘Family Breakfast’.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/the-family-breakfast/', 'snippet': 'To get every member of my family sitting down in one place and looking at each other every day, I compromised on dinner and created the ‘Family Breakfast’.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a mother, I daydream about the ideal family dinner, a sort of mini-Thanksgiving with a Norman Rockwell haze to it. I love the idea of a family seated around the table, talking over the events of the day, learning table manners, conversational skills and good nutritional habits. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Family Breakfast', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T21:57:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Alice Teti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Alice', 'lastname': 'Teti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a79f17c-a86b-54b4-9d4b-4595c4b37a3b', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a79f17c-a86b-54b4-9d4b-4595c4b37a3b'}, {'abstract': 'Shannon Eastin will become the first woman to officiate an N.F.L. game when the San Diego Chargers host the Green Bay Packers on Thursday night.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/woman-prepares-to-officiate-and-make-n-f-l-history/', 'snippet': 'Shannon Eastin will become the first woman to officiate an N.F.L. game when the San Diego Chargers host the Green Bay Packers on Thursday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shannon Eastin, who was overruled by her mother when she wanted to play youth football, will make it to the N.F.L. on Thursday night. Eastin will become the first woman to officiate an N.F.L. game when the San Diego Chargers host the Green Bay Packers in a preseason game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woman Prepares to Officiate and Make N.F.L. History', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T21:57:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Pedulla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pedulla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_m