he Democratic Party, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo is skipping most of the Democratic National Convention next month because, he said, he is too busy with his day job in New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo to Attend Only Last  Day of Democratic National Convention', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T22:35:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f488a2e0-f18c-598b-aa1f-ca0d67b667e4', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f488a2e0-f18c-598b-aa1f-ca0d67b667e4'}, {'abstract': 'In 1972, Olga Korbut displayed balletic moves for 20 seconds of her floor routine. Today’s female gymnasts have no time to waste on dancing around.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/artistry-fades-as-gymnasts-push-boundaries/', 'snippet': 'In 1972, Olga Korbut displayed balletic moves for 20 seconds of her floor routine. Today’s female gymnasts have no time to waste on dancing around.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American gymnast Aly Raisman won an Olympic gold medal in the floor exercise Tuesday with a score of 15.6, well above the silver medalist Catalina Ponor’s 15.2 (a huge margin in the fractional point differences of gymnastics) and the bronze medalist Aliya Mustafina’s14.9. The difference in the scores reflects the difficulty of these women’s routines.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Artistry Fades as Gymnasts Push Boundaries', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gymnastics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Korbut, Olga', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T22:36:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91fa20ba-87d2-5937-9de3-40f5b0cea9f7', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91fa20ba-87d2-5937-9de3-40f5b0cea9f7'}, {'abstract': 'Escorted by summer visitors from Ireland, a cardboard cutout of Michael Collins has been touring New York and other American cities.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/an-irish-revolutionary-checks-out-the-sights-90-years-after-his-death/', 'snippet': 'Escorted by summer visitors from Ireland, a cardboard cutout of Michael Collins has been touring New York and other American cities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The other day, Richard Teahan was strolling down Fifth Avenue with Michael Collins under his arm when a woman covered fully by a burqa approached him near 65th Street and asked for directions to the Port Authority Bus Terminal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Irish Revolutionary Checks Out the Sights 90 Years After His Death', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Irish Revolutionary Visits 90 Years After His Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'COLLINS, MICHAEL', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T22:36:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd539359-e9f6-5cb3-a544-f41ad0140565', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd539359-e9f6-5cb3-a544-f41ad0140565'}, {'abstract': 'The Iranian weight lifter Behdad Salimikordasiabi won gold with a 545-pound lift. Mark Cannella, a former United States coach, explains how he did it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/08/07/sports/olympics/weighlighting.html', 'snippet': 'The Iranian weight lifter Behdad Salimikordasiabi won gold with a 545-pound lift. Mark Cannella, a former United States coach, explains how he did it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Iranian weight lifter Behdad Salimikordasiabi won gold with a 545-pound lift. Mark Cannella, a former United States coach, explains how he did it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lifting 545 Pounds Over His Head for Olympic Gold', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight Lifting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-07T22:37:22+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news