y Egypt’s new Islamist leader has to establish control over the lawless Sinai and work with Israel to do so.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/opinion/egypts-sinai-problem.html', 'snippet': 'The border attack in the Sinai Peninsula is why Egypt’s new Islamist leader has to establish control over the lawless Sinai and work with Israel to do so.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update: On Wednesday, after this editorial was published, Egypt was reported to have launched its first airstrikes in decades in the Sinai Peninsula, deploying attack helicopters to strike at gunmen after the shootings of 16 Egyptian soldiers on Sunday. Few details are known, but it appeared to be a retaliatory action to defend Egypt against an upsurge in attacks by militants. The strikes will add to tensions between the new government of President Mohamed Morsi, an Islamist, and the largely secular Egyptian army.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Sinai Problem', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt’s Sinai Problem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sinai Peninsula (Egypt)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T01:07:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/df872f78-65f1-57bf-98d9-fa196020fcf8', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df872f78-65f1-57bf-98d9-fa196020fcf8'}, {'abs