e their families for years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — When Liu Xiang, China’s track and field superstar, crashed to the ground at the London Olympic Games on Tuesday after stumbling over the first hurdle in his 110-meter men’s hurdles heat, an announcer on the state broadcaster openly wept and subway riders thronging platform television screens gasped in horror. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heavy Burden on Athletes Takes Joy Away From China’s Olympic Success', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heavy Burden on Athletes Takes Joy Away From China’s Olympic Success', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu Xiang', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T01:46:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/445691fd-3352-58a8-a4f7-421d54601521', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/445691fd-3352-58a8-a4f7-421d54601521'}, {'abstract': 'Investigators are looking at Wade M. Page’s involvement in the white supremacist music scene, where he played with a number of bands.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/myspace-page-gunman-belonged-to-white-supremacist-band/', 'snippet': 'Investigators are looking at Wade M. Page’s involvement in the white supremacist music scene, where he played with a number of bands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a teenager, Wade M. Page, the 40-year-old gunman who killed six people and wounded three others at the Wisconsin Sikh Temple on Sunday, developed a passion for music. His stepmother, Laura Page, 67, recalled that he worshiped the guitarist Stevie Ray Vaughan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Shooting, Searching for Clues in the Music of Hate', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oak Creek, Wis, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sikhs and Sikhism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Page, Wade Michael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANTI-DEFAMATION LEAGUE', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern Poverty Law Center', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oak Creek (Wis)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T01:47:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston and Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79582ec2-1598-5869-962b-f0c48b2327b5', 'word_count': 1622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79582ec2-1598-5869-962b-f0c48b2327b5'}, {'abstract': 'It’s not impossible to make North Carolina a true tipping-point state, but it’s just not all that likely.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/aug-7-north-carolina-isnt-central-to-electoral-math/', 'snippet': 'It’s not impossible to make North Carolina a true tipping-point state, but it’s just not all that likely.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were two polls out in Colorado on Tuesday showing apparently contradictory results. One survey, from Rasmussen Reports, had an exact tie there. Another, from Public Policy Polling, put President Obama ahead by six points, or by four points with Gary Johnson, a Libertarian, included in the survey. (In cases where pollsters ask questions both with and without Mr. Johnson on the ballot, we simply average the numbers, so our forecast model treats the poll as showing a five-point lead for Mr. Obama.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 7: North Carolina Isn’t Central to Electoral Math', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T01:47:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23b24e9a-0636-58e3-ad17-702501c20f43', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23b24e9a-0636-58e3-ad17-702501c20f43'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time since the conflict in Syria began last year, an activist opposed to President Bashar al-Assad has publicly presented possible evidence that the antigovernment forces have obtained a heat-seeking, shoulder-fired anti-aircraft missile.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/07/in-syria-potential-threat-to-government-air-power-emerges/', 'snippet': 'For the first time since the conflict in Syria began last year, an activist opposed to President Bashar al-Assad has publicly presented possible evidence that the antigovernment forces have obtained a heat-seeking, shoulder-fired anti-aircraft mis...', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time since the conflict in Syria began last year, an activist opposed to President Bashar al-Assad has publicly presented possible evidence that the antigovernment forces have obtained a heat-seeking, shoulder-fired anti-aircraft missile.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Syria, Potential Threat to Government Air Power Emerges', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War and Guerrilla Warfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEPPO (SYRIA)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T01:49:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c543d6c-ff2d-5f9d-8208-4ed066a77068', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c543d6c-ff2d-5f9d-8208-4ed066a77068'}, {'abstract': 'A new mosque that has faced arson, vandalism and a court battle has passed inspection and will be allowed to open by Friday, in time for the final week of Ramadan, its leaders said Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/us/tennessee-mosque-is-expected-to-open-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'A new mosque that has faced arson, vandalism and a court battle has passed inspection and will be allowed to open by Friday, in time for the final week of Ramadan, its leaders said Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new mosque that has faced arson, vandalism and a court battle has passed inspection and will be allowed to open by Friday, in time for the final week of Ramadan, its leaders said Tuesday. The State Fire Marshal’s Office said it had issued a temporary certificate of occupancy for 30 days to the Islamic Center of Murfreesboro. For two years, the center’s expansion has faced legal challenges and threats of violence. Vandals painted “not welcome” on construction signs at the mosque and set fire to construction equipment. A Texas man was indicted in June on charges that he left messages threatening to detonate a bomb at the center on Sept. 11. In May, a county judge ruled that the construction plans had not received sufficient comment from the public and that an occupancy permit could not be granted. Federal prosecutors filed a discrimination lawsuit, and a federal judge ruled in the mosque’s favor last month. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tennessee: Mosque Is Expected To Open This Week ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tennessee: Mosque Is Expected To Open This Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic Center of Murfreesboro', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mosques', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Murfreesboro (Tenn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tennessee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T01:53:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robbie Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robbie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc41d95a-61e3-588d-813f-7fa38cb72559', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc41d95a-61e3-588d-813f-7fa38cb72559'}, {'abstract': 'In a promising twist for the city’s survival as a place where things are made, an old factory in Brooklyn has avoided being converted to condos, the fate of many old industrial buildings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/nyregion/small-factories-thrive-in-brooklyn-replacing-industrial-giants.html', 'snippet': 'In a promising twist for the city’s survival as a place where things are made, an old factory in Brooklyn has avoided being converted to condos, the fate of many old industrial buildings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hulking five-story brick factory, complete with an emblematic smokestack, once braided rope for New York’s shipbuilding industry and employed hundreds of blue-collar workers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/nyregion/MANUFACTURING1/MANUFACTURING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/08/nyregion/MANUFACTURING1/MANUFACTURING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/nyregion/MANUFACTURING1/MANUFACTURING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cred