ugh/', 'snippet': 'Media scouring of political ads can be helpful, but we have to count on voters’ common sense too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The speaker is a Midwestern Everyman: White, balding, deep in middle age, with hollows around his eyes. He sits at a kitchen table, nursing a cup of coffee, talking about what happened after Bain Capital closed down his steel plant in 2001. He lost his job; his family lost its health insurance. His wife felt lousy but didn’t go to the doctor, to spare the family worry and expense. When she finally ended up in the hospital, the diagnosis was cancer. She had 22 days to live.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fact-Checking Is Not Enough', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ayers, William C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horton, Willie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Priorities USA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T04:32:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39614147-e652-5913-9142-b7e9301433c1', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39614147-e652-5913-9142-b7e9301433c1'}, {'abstract': 'Communist Party veteran blames top leadership for the party’s poor performance.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/a-conversation-with-former-lok-sabha-speaker-somnath-chatterjee/', 'snippet': 'Communist Party veteran blames top leadership for the party’s poor performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Somnath Chatterjee was the speaker of the Lok Sabha, India’s lower house of Parliament, from 2004 to 2009. A widely admired parliamentarian from West Bengal, Mr. Chatterjee had joined the Communist Party of India (Marxist) in 1968. In 2008, he was expelled from the party for refusing to step down as speaker during a no-confidence vote against the government on the issue of the India-U.S. civilian nuclear deal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With: Former Lok Sabha Speaker Somnath Chatterjee', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bengal (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T05:03:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sambuddha Mitra Mustafi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sambuddha', 'middlename': 'Mitra', 'lastname': 'Mustafi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1091f54f-ba1a-565f-aa42-19feb97cf7a9', 'word_count': 1139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1091f54f-ba1a-565f-aa42-19feb97cf7a9'}, {'abstract': 'White power music, a powerful tool for keeping the supremacist movement alive.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/wisconsin-shooting-exposes-the-angry-music-of-hatecore/', 'snippet': 'White power music, a powerful tool for keeping the supremacist movement alive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The shooting rampage by an “avowed white supremacist” that killed six people at a suburban Sikh Temple near Milwaukee “came at a time of both growth and disarray in the supremacist movement,” James Dao and Serge F. Kovaleski wrote in The New York Times. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wisconsin Attack Exposes the Angry Music of ‘Hatecore’', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T06:24:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7faa4bc4-1647-5efc-8671-de2a185cf774', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7faa4bc4-1647-5efc-8671-de2a185cf774'}, {'abstract': 'Mohamed Morsi, Egypt’s president, upended the country’s security apparatus after the deadliest attack on the Egyptian military in years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/world/middleeast/egypt-sinai-attacks.html', 'snippet': 'Mohamed Morsi, Egypt’s president, upended the country’s security apparatus after the deadliest attack on the Egyptian military in years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EL ARISH, Egypt — President Mohamed Morsi fired his intelligence chief and other top security officials on Wednesday in a sweeping response by his new government to the killings of 16 soldiers in the Sinai Peninsula. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/world/09egypt-span/09egypt-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/09/world/09egypt-span/09egypt-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08