}, {'abstract': 'A new poll shows that Mitt Romney maintains a sizable advantage among white, working-class voters and President Obama leading with women in Wisconsin, Colorado and Virginia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/08/08/us/politics/08poll-results-documents.html', 'snippet': 'A new poll shows that Mitt Romney maintains a sizable advantage among white, working-class voters and President Obama leading with women in Wisconsin, Colorado and Virginia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new poll shows that Mitt Romney maintains a sizable advantage among white, working-class voters and President Obama leading with women in Wisconsin, Colorado and Virginia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quinnipiac University/New York Times/CBS Poll on Swing States', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T07:02:58+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/c1499548-4600-596d-9f56-e36f1aa6d641', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/c1499548-4600-596d-9f56-e36f1aa6d641'}, {'abstract': 'The U.S. Justice Department does not draw a distinction between Sikhs and Muslims, report says.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/mourning-victims-sikhs-lament-being-mistaken-for-radicals-or-militants/', 'snippet': 'The U.S. Justice Department does not draw a distinction between Sikhs and Muslims, report says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sikhs across the United States mourned the deaths in the Wisconsin shooting, and some said that the incident “revived bitter memories of the period just after the Sept. 11 attacks” when their “distinctive turbans and beards” seemed to trigger violence by people who mistook them for Muslims militants, Ethan Bronner wrote in The New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mourning Victims, Sikhs Lament Being Mistaken for Radicals or Militants', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T07:10:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20a813af-4ab2-5562-aabf-5e31dfc82444', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20a813af-4ab2-5562-aabf-5e31dfc82444'}, {'abstract': 'The question is about the per-guard cost of security for the Summer Olympics.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/test-yourself-math-aug-8-2012/', 'snippet': 'The question is about the per-guard cost of security for the Summer Olympics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Test your math skills with this question created by Scott Matthews at Math for America from the article “Amid Reports of Ineptitude, Concerns Over Security at London Olympics.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | Math, Aug. 8, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T08:32:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92a1b443-dfe7-5b71-91b3-8ca2fe955bc7', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92a1b443-dfe7-5b71-91b3-8ca2fe955bc7'}, {'abstract': 'In a conversation with James Estrin, the New York Times staff photographer Chang W. Lee discusses his methods applied at the London Olympics.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/you-have-to-see-it-before-it-happens/', 'snippet': 'In a conversation with James Estrin, the New York Times staff photographer Chang W. Lee discusses his methods applied at the London Olympics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chang W. Lee, a staff photographer for The New York Times, is photographing the Olympics. He spoke with James Estrin from London on Sunday night. The interview has been edited.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘You Have to See It Before It Happens’', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T09:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08f146ed-bcb6-5950-978b-c9c1273be343', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08f146ed-bcb6-5950-978b-c9c1273be343'}, {'abstract': 'To wipe away our history, would be to forget our own mothers and fathers, the daughter of Sikh immigrants, born and raised in California writes in an op-ed.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/recollections-of-the-first-gurdwara-in-the-u-s/', 'snippet': 'To wipe away our history, would be to forget our own mothers and fathers, the daughter of Sikh immigrants, born and raised in California writes in an op-ed.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Stockton Gurdwara in California — the first Sikh temple in the United States — is celebrating its 100th anniversary this year,” Bhira Backhaus wrote in an op-ed in the New York Times. Immigrants from Punjab, “purchased the lot on Grant Street in early 1912.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recollections of the First Gurdwara in the U.S.', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T09:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b3b5809-f447-5018-b1f6-b19739d287d5', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b3b5809-f447-5018-b1f6-b19739d287d5'}, {'abstract': 'Why have “shred-a-thons,” like the recent Shred Day in Cambridge, Mass., become popular around the country in recent years?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/the-joys-of-shred-day/', 'snippet': 'Why have “shred-a-thons,” like the recent Shred Day in Cambridge, Mass., become popular around the country in recent years?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHAT is Shred Day? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Joys of ‘Shred Day’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T09:05:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Murray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/795fde57-36ef-52e4-b417-2c72f2d3b7c8', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/795fde57-36ef-52e4-b417-2c72f2d3b7c8'}, {'abstract': 'Pakistan’s Supreme Court issued a contempt-of-court notice against Prime Minister Raja Pervez Ashraf on Wednesday, signaling a rerun of judicial proceedings that saw his predecessor ousted from office in June.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/world/asia/raja-pervez-ashraf-faces-contempt-charges-in-pakistan.html', 'snippet': 'Pakistan’s Supreme Court issued a contempt-of-court notice against Prime Minister Raja Pervez Ashraf on Wednesday, signaling a rerun of judicial proceedings that saw his predecessor ousted from office in June.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — The Supreme Court issued a contempt-of-court notice against Prime Minister Raja Pervez Ashraf on Wednesday, signaling what appeared to be a rerun of judicial proceedings in which his predecessor was ousted from office in June. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/world/PAKISTAN/PAKISTAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 801, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/world/PAKISTAN/PAKISTAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1603, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/world/PAKISTAN/PAKISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/09/world/PAKISTAN/PAKISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image