8T11:01:41+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Movies', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/9c0b23d3-ef69-5dad-a66d-5a9cfef45507', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/9c0b23d3-ef69-5dad-a66d-5a9cfef45507'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists travel to the islands of Oceania to study dolphin communities and the genetic relationships among them.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/a-pattern-of-dolphins/', 'snippet': 'Scientists travel to the islands of Oceania to study dolphin communities and the genetic relationships among them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scott Baker, associate director of the Marine Mammal Institute at Oregon State University, writes from Samoa, where he studies the formation of local communities among dolphins, and their genetic isolation from one another. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pattern of Dolphins', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dolphins and Porpoises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Samoa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T11:15:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cad05234-b1f3-5547-b900-4625f2ade83c', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cad05234-b1f3-5547-b900-4625f2ade83c'}, {'abstract': 'When they broadcast religious conversions live, Pakistani television channels cross the line between the sensational and the exploitative.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/pakistani-television-goes-for-sensational-coverage-of-religious-issues/', 'snippet': 'When they broadcast religious conversions live, Pakistani television channels cross the line between the sensational and the exploitative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KARACHI — With more than 90 cash-strapped channels competing for the attention of 40 million viewers daily, it’s not surprising that Pakistan’s independent media producers resort to sensationalism to boost ratings. During the holy Muslim month of Ramadan, channel owners and advertisers try to cash in on religious sentiment by hiring celebrities to host ever more elaborate, though only marginally religious, shows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conversion Ratings', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T11:25:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Huma Yusuf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Huma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yusuf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d78fc1c2-6fe0-536f-b0aa-9ba0e9329f79', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d78fc1c2-6fe0-536f-b0aa-9ba0e9329f79'}, {'abstract': '“Hope Springs” brings Meryl Streep and Tommy Lee Jones together as a couple in a longtime marriage that’s gone dry. Enter a therapist, Steve Carell.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/movies/movie-review-hope-springs-with-meryl-streep-and-tommy-lee-jones.html', 'snippet': '“Hope Springs” brings Meryl Streep and Tommy Lee Jones together as a couple in a longtime marriage that’s gone dry. Enter a therapist, Steve Carell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chance to watch Meryl Streep or Tommy Lee Jones is often all the encouragement the otherwise reluctant moviegoer needs to risk the kitsch pleasures of “Mamma Mia!”and the familiar genre beats of “Men in Black 3.” The new film “Hope Springs” holds out the delectable promise of watching them work on screen together for the first time, and in a story about a longtime marriage that’s gone dry. It’s a subject that’s as unusual in mainstream American cinema as the sight of major stars letting it all hang out on camera, wrinkles and possibly dignity included, though perhaps not for long, given the movie industry’s growing interest in the country’s aging population. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/HOPE/HOPE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/HOPE/HOPE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/HOPE/HOPE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/HOPE/HOPE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1398, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/HOPE/HOPE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/HOPE/HOPE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/arts/HOPE/HOPE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Together, in Separate Beds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still Together, in Separate Beds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carell, Steve', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Tommy Lee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streep, Meryl', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hope Springs (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frankel, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T11:38:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b1d58ea-3c1f-5aa3-a268-48e1a6769b98', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b1d58ea-3c1f-5aa3-a268-48e1a6769b98'}, {'abstract': 'During Ramadan old parts of Delhi are abuzz with vendors serving mouth-watering food until wee hours of the morning.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/feasting-after-fasts-in-the-streets-of-old-delhi/', 'snippet': 'During Ramadan old parts of Delhi are abuzz with vendors serving mouth-watering food until wee hours of the morning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During this holy month of Ramadan (or Ramzan, as it is called in India), when the sun sets, Old Delhi awakens to a slew of delectable aromas and crowded markets as excited Muslim families break their fast with a feast known as iftar. A majority of the families prepare traditional delicacies in their homes and head out to the Jama Masjid, the principal mosque of the area, to eat in its gigantic courtyard. Many others throng the narrow lanes to feast after their fast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feasting After Fasts in the Streets of Old Delhi', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fasting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ramadan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mughlai', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T11:41:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raksha Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raksha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/175a6e67-a288-5e42-978b-78cec183ca9d', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/175a6e67-a288-5e42-978b-78cec183ca9d'}, {'abstract': 'Heroic blockbusters like “Marvel’s the Avengers” and “The Dark Knight Rises” are draws this summer, but so are smaller films like “Moonrise Kingdom” and “Magic Mike.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/movies/audiences-are-finding-diversity-at-summer-movies.html', 'snippet': 'Heroic blockbusters like “Marvel’s the Avengers” and “The Dark Knight Rises” are draws this summer, but so are smaller films like “Moonrise Kingdom” and “Magic Mike.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN “Jaws” landed in June 1975, it thrilled so many moviegoers week after hot sticky week that within months it had made box office history. As the critic Tom Shone put it in his book “Blockbuster,” “That’s what America did in the summer of 1975: It watched ‘Jaws.’\xa0” These days, though, Americans are rarely unified by one must-see movie for long, even when school’s out. When “Marvel’s The Avengers” opened in May, it topped the box office for three weeks until it was toppled by “Men in Black 3,” which held the top spot for two, until it was bested by “Snow White and the Huntsman,” which held on for one. And so it goes as each studio behemoth is bumped by the next in what has become a faster cycle of planned obsolescence.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blockbusters Yield to Magic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blockbusters Yield To Magic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Magic Mike (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Marvel's The Avengers (Movie)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Moonrise Kingdom (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Brave (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Dark Knight Rises (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Best Exotic Marigold Hotel (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Prometheus (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hope Springs (Movie)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Amazing Spider-Man (Movie)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 