cle/f82923fa-b64b-5011-8cf9-1aad38ac1300', 'word_count': 1552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f82923fa-b64b-5011-8cf9-1aad38ac1300'}, {'abstract': 'Whenever analysts and arms researchers scrutinize infantry weapons circulating through a conflict they encounter predictable finds. But sometimes there are surprises.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/taliban-gun-locker-the-frankengun-of-wardak-province/', 'snippet': 'Whenever analysts and arms researchers scrutinize infantry weapons circulating through a conflict they encounter predictable finds. But sometimes there are surprises.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost no matter the place or the year, whenever analysts and arms researchers scrutinize infantry weapons circulating through a conflict, they encounter predictable finds. Time and again, the same items turn up: AK assault rifles, PK machine guns, RPG-7 shoulder-fired anti-armor weapons, and, depending on the region, a smattering of M-16 variants, Fabrique Nationale and Heckler & Koch weapons, and bolt-action or lever-action rifles from yesteryear. There are oddities, including homemade jobs. Often there are also stray vestigial arms from previous wars in the same region or from particular arms transfers to a government on the same soil. But most of these are outliers. Usually a researcher can write up a list of likely candidates, then check them off while working the beat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taliban Gun Locker: The Frankengun of Wardak Province', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T12:03:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85d2c242-fd66-5827-9c5e-71afce255957', 'word_count': 1723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85d2c242-fd66-5827-9c5e-71afce255957'}, {'abstract': 'The Carlyle Group swung to a second-quarter loss of $57 million, as it struggled to show growth in its core private equity investments.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/carlyle-swings-to-a-loss-in-2nd-quarter/', 'snippet': 'The Carlyle Group swung to a second-quarter loss of $57 million, as it struggled to show growth in its core private equity investments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Carlyle Group swung to a loss in its second quarter, the firm said on Wednesday, as it struggled to show growth in its core private equity investments.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carlyle Swings to a Loss in 2nd Quarter', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubenstein, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carlyle Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T12:09:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/919aa9f8-b628-52a7-be22-d08ac30c771f', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/919aa9f8-b628-52a7-be22-d08ac30c771f'}, {'abstract': 'James Cameron, director of the global hit films “Titanic” and “Avatar,” cut the ribbon on the new office of the Cameron Pace Group China in the port city of Tianjin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/business/media/tianjin-draws-in-an-a-list-hollywood-director.html', 'snippet': 'James Cameron, director of the global hit films “Titanic” and “Avatar,” cut the ribbon on the new office of the Cameron Pace Group China in the port city of Tianjin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — James Cameron, director of the global hit films “Titanic” and “Avatar,” said Wednesday he was setting up shop in the Chinese city of Tianjin to bring his cutting-edge 3-D technologies and production services to a high-technology industrial park aimed at aiding China’s booming moviemaking industry.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/business/Chinafilm/Chinafilm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/business/Chinafilm/Chinafilm-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China Draws In an A-List Hollywood Director', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China’s Thirst for 3-D Draws an A-List Hollywood Director', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T12:14:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsec