fying for the women’s Olympic high jump final begins on Thursday morning. In this year’s competition, at least three of the medal contenders have given birth in the last year or two, including the gold medal favorite, Anna Chicherova of Russia, and the American Olympic trials champion Chaunté Lowe. And that does not include the defending Olympic champion, Tia Hellebaut of Belgium, who is in the midst of a second comeback to the sport after having had two children since she won the gold medal four years ago. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Baby, a Gold?', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Acuff, Amy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joy, Elizabeth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stones, Dwight', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T12:32:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gendelman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gendelman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6678485-d454-5e2f-a9c9-8e7f10b889fc', 'word_count': 1081, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6678485-d454-5e2f-a9c9-8e7f10b889fc'}, {'abstract': 'The premium cable business Starz will become a separate publicly traded company in a spinoff later this year.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/liberty-media-to-split-off-starz/', 'snippet': 'The premium cable business Starz will become a separate publicly traded company in a spinoff later this y