 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff1a6299-c56f-5e3a-8501-157d00c29e8c', 'word_count': 575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff1a6299-c56f-5e3a-8501-157d00c29e8c'}, {'abstract': 'Though lacking the pedigree of their better-known teammates on the United States taekwondo team, Terrence Jennings and Paige McPherson say they believe medals are within their reach.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/2-u-s-athletes-look-to-first-olympic-taekwondo-action/', 'snippet': 'Though lacking the pedigree of their better-known teammates on the United States taekwondo team, Terrence Jennings and Paige McPherson say they believe medals are within their reach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Half of the United States Olympic taekwondo team is not like the other. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 U.S. Athletes Look to First Olympic Taekwondo Action', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taekwondo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Diana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Steven', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T13:40:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Otis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24391e3a-1b3e-59b9-b0a0-de5af1a5a3cc', 'word_count': 863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24391e3a-1b3e-59b9-b0a0-de5af1a5a3cc'}, {'abstract': 'Democrats’ preferred candidates, among their own and Republicans, won some contested primaries. Kansas, Michigan, Missouri and Washington held primaries Tuesday, and in all but Kansas, Democrats can claim success.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/in-primaries-democrats-preferred-candidates-including-republicans-are-winners/', 'snippet': 'Democrats’ preferred candidates, among their own and Republicans, won some contested primaries. Kansas, Michigan, Missouri and Washington held primaries Tuesday, and in all but Kansas, Democrats can claim success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — So, to recap: In a group of primaries Tuesday night, an endangered Senate incumbent helped pick her Republican opponent, a spouse’s imprisonment failed to impede a landslide victory for a veteran House member in Michigan and a reindeer farmer/Santa impersonator is now the Republican candidate for another seat in that state.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Primaries, Democrats’ Preferred Candidates (Including Republicans) Are Winners', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T13:43:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/584e67dd-8b96-5017-86b7-639bf6778587', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/584e67dd-8b96-5017-86b7-639bf6778587'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s ads are leaving an impression with one group that can’t help him.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/an-obama-message-that-really-sticks/', 'snippet': 'The president’s ads are leaving an impression with one group that can’t help him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s only August and the campaign hasn’t really sunk in with the public yet, right? Wrong. Even the children are listening, probably too much.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Obama Message That Really Sticks', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Younger Set: It’s the Message That Sticks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Messina, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westport (Conn)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T13:48:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51fdfee2-38b0-59d5-a7fa-5c2df8535c95', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51fdfee2-38b0-59d5-a7fa-5c2df8535c95'}, {'abstract': 'The commission suspends decisions on license renewals for nuclear plants until the commission reassesses the nagging issue of storing spent nuclear fuel.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/on-our-radar-n-r-c-puts-off-licensing-decisions/', 'snippet': 'The commission suspends decisions on license renewals for nuclear plants until the commission reassesses the nagging issue of storing spent nuclear fuel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Nuclear Regulatory Commission suspends final decisions on licenses for power plants pending a court-ordered reassessment of the issue of storing spent nuclear fuel. That won’t prevent the agency from continuing to review license applications, a spokesman says, adding that no final licensing decisions had been expected this year. [Bloomberg News]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: N.R.C. Puts Off Licensing Decisions', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T13:53:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25f69b63-d48f-505e-8fab-53a240de1d58', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25f69b63-d48f-505e-8fab-53a240de1d58'}, {'abstract': 'The Edinburgh Airport and the National Galleries of Scotland agreed to put a white cover over a poster depicting Picasso’s “Nude Woman in a Red Armchair” – though not without a rejoinder from gallery officials – and then they reversed the decision.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/after-complaints-picasso-nude-is-covered-up-at-edinburgh-airport/', 'snippet': 'The Edinburgh Airport and the National Galleries of Scotland agreed to put a white cover over a poster depicting Picasso’s “Nude Woman in a Red Armchair” – though not without a rejoinder from gallery officials – and then they reversed the decision...', 'lead_paragraph': '11:45 a.m. | Updated ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Complaints, Picasso Nude at Airport Is Covered Up, Then Uncovered', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Airport Plays Peekaboo With a Picasso Nude', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Posters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picasso, Pablo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Galleries of Scotland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scottish National Gallery of Modern Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Edinburgh (Scotland)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T13:54:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/991f37d0-038f-5138-834c-a699990a5dfa', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/991f37d0-038f-5138-834c-a699990a5dfa'}, {'abstract': 'A hologram-like display, known as an airport virtual assistant, answers international travelers’ questions at Newark Liberty International Airport.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/that-newark-airport-greeter-sure-can-project/', 'snippet': 'A hologram-like display, known as an airport virtual assistant, answers international travelers’ questions at Newark Liberty International Airport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the woman answering international travelers’ questions as they arrive at Newark Liberty International Airport’s Terminal B seems a little repetitive, she should be forgiven. She is an airport virtual assistant, otherwise known as AVA, a hologram-like display that was installed there late last month as part of a six-month trial run. La Guardia and Kennedy Airports were scheduled to get trial avatars of their own last week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'That Newark Airport Greeter Sure Can Project', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Newark Liberty International Airport (NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T14:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Drake', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drake', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef6b0af6-1abb-52b8-b758-f2accba09c95', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef6b0af6-1abb-52b8-b758-f2accba09c95'}, {'abstract': 'Also, the judge in the Google-Oracle case wants to know about payments to journalists, bloggers and commentators for favorable coverage; and Hollywood is building bridges to China.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/the-breakfast-meeting-obama-on-the-news-media-and-madonna-speaks-out-in-russia/', 'snippet': 'Also, the judge in the Google-Oracle case wants to know about payments to journalists, bloggers and commentators for favorable coverage; and Hollywood is building bridges to China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barack Obama has more than a spectator’s interest in how the news media does its job, Amy Chozick notes as she describes the president’s typical news diet. Press coverage helped propel him to the national stage when he was a state legislator, and three and a half years into his presidential term he sees news coverage as frustrating his ambitions to change the tone of political debate. His most persistent complaint is what he calls the news media’s belief in a “false balance,” in which two opposing sides are given equal weight regardless of the facts. (A note of caution from Tom Rosenstiel, director of the Project for Excellence in Journalism: “I think we’ve learned through history to beware of presidents playing press critic. They’re not press critics — they’re people trying to advance a political agenda.”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Obama on the News Media, and Madonna Speaks Out in Russia', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T14:08:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7be7bdc-febf-5d4b-af4b-709a177c801a', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7be7bdc-febf-5d4b-af4b-709a177c801a'}, {'abstract': 'The champion’s defeat in the Olympic semifinal is a heartbreak for Indian fans.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/indias-boxing-hero-mary-kom-settles-for-bronze/', 'snippet': 'The champion’s defeat in the Olympic semifinal is a heartbreak for Indian fans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mary Kom’s gold medal quest ended on Wednesday when she lost in the semifinals of the Olympic women’s flyweight boxing competition to Britain’s Nicola Adams, the second-ranked fighter in the world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India’s Boxing Hero Mary Kom Settles for Bronze', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boxing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kom, Mary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T14:13:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38222c53-1cfa-532b-8e84-adfe55c20c6f', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38222c53-1cfa-532b-8e84-adfe55c20c6f'}, {'abstract': 'The TimesTalks series is hosting a panel discussion on Wednesday with current and former Olympians about how women’s participation in the Games has changed and about their personal experiences. Moderated by Juliet Macur of The Times.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/timestalks-wome-of-the-summer-games/', 'snippet': 'The TimesTalks series is hosting a panel discussion on Wednesday with current and former Olympians about how women’s participation in the Games has changed and about their personal experiences. Moderated by Juliet Macur of The Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time, the United States has sent more women than men to compete on its Olympic teams in London, reflecting the evolution of women’s participation in the modern Games. The TimesTalks series hosted a panel discussion on Wednesday with Olympic athletes past and present about participating in the Games, how they have prepared and what they have discovered. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesTalks: Women of the Summer Games', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Shawn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rhode, Kim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zagunis, Mariel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T14:20:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ac148a1-6dff-563b-8c93-6e2da9b5fb6d', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ac148a1-6dff-563b-8c93-6e2da9b5fb6d'}, {'abstract': 'What the Starbucks partnership with Square will mean for cash. | Ultrarich in France consider exodus over tax proposal. | Charging companies with fraud, but sparing individuals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/business/100000001709681/business-day-live-august-8-2012.html', 'snippet': 'What the Starbucks partnership with Square will mean for cash. | Ultrarich in France consider exodus over tax proposal. | Charging companies with fraud, but sparing individuals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What the Starbucks partnership with Square will mean for cash. | Ultrarich in France consider exodus over tax proposal. | Charging companies with fraud, but sparing individuals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/bu