person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/848c55cd-aad1-50b2-9e70-5b111a664da0', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/848c55cd-aad1-50b2-9e70-5b111a664da0'}, {'abstract': 'The United States women’s soccer team demonstrated resilience against the Canadians in a nail-biter of a semifinal, and the Americans will need all their guile against a tough Japanese team in the gold medal match.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/breaking-it-down-a-soccer-match-for-the-ages/', 'snippet': 'The United States women’s soccer team demonstrated resilience against the Canadians in a nail-biter of a semifinal, and the Americans will need all their guile against a tough Japanese team in the gold medal match.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ali Krieger is a defender for the United States women’s national soccer team and plays for FFC Frankfurt. Because of an injury, she is not playing for the team in the 2012 Games. She was an alternate on the 2008 United States Olympic team and started for the Americans in last summer’s World Cup. She has been writing for the 2012 London Olympics blog, and this is her third post.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking It Down: A Soccer Match for the Ages', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krieger, Ali', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lloyd, Carli', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgan, Alex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rapinoe, Megan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wambach, Abby', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T15:34:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ali Krieger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ali', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krieger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35972dfa-b630-5318-a289-ba8d63590fd9', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35972dfa-b630-5318-a289-ba8d63590fd9'}, {'abstract': 'Or is it too favorable to the credit card companies?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/would-the-credit-card-settlement-help-merchants/', 'snippet': 'Or is it too favorable to the credit card companies?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times has published an article exploring the dissatisfaction brewing among some retailer advocates with a recently proposed settlement to a lawsuit that pitted merchants against Visa, MasterCard and the leading banks. Among the grievances: for the first time, merchants would gain the right to charge customers more for paying with a credit card — unless they accept American Express cards. As the article explains, American Express, which is not party to the settlement, has rules that can make it difficult or impossible for merchants to institute surcharges.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will the Credit Card Settlement Help Merchants?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Mallory', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hanft, Noah 