, 'lead_paragraph': 'MILWAUKEE — Around the middle of June, Wade M. Page split with his girlfriend, moving out of the home they shared in South Milwaukee. In mid-July, he suddenly stopped showing up to his job as a machine operator. About two weeks later, he bought a 9-millimeter handgun, testing it by firing 50 rounds at a target in the gun shop’s basement.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/us/06shooter2_cnd/06shooter2_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 850, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/us/06shooter2_cnd/06shooter2_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1699, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/06/us/06shooter2_cnd/06shooter2_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/06/us/06shooter2_cnd/06shooter2_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Investigators Seek Clues in Gunman’s Last Weeks Before Temple Murders', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Investigators Seek Clues In Gunman’s Last Weeks Before Temple Murders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sikhs and Sikhism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sikh Temple of Wisconsin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oak Creek, Wis, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Page, Wade Michael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oak Creek (Wis)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T16:34:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18a5d662-930d-506d-8ff4-d08ca4f7cd46', 'word_count': 1038, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18a5d662-930d-506d-8ff4-d08ca4f7cd46'}, {'abstract': 'When asked last month about a potential spinoff of the pay-TV company, Liberty’s chairman, John Malone said: “There are no plans on Starz at this time other than to grow it.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/libertys-spinoff-of-starz-was-firmly-denied-only-a-month-ago/', 'snippet': 'When asked last month about a potential spinoff of the pay-TV company, Liberty’s chairman, John Malone said: “There are no plans on Starz at this time other than to grow it.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“There are no plans on Starz at this time other than to grow it.” That’s what the chairman of Liberty Media, John Malone, told a New York Times reporter last month at the Sun Valley, Idaho, media conference.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liberty’s Spinoff of Starz Was Firmly Denied Only a Month Ago', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALBRECHT, CHRIS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malone, John C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Liberty Media Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sun Valley (Idaho)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T16:37:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5732768-8022-5b80-9fb9-75ff9fd35057', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5732768-8022-5b80-9fb9-75ff9fd35057'}, {'abstract': 'Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac, the two mortgage finance giants, reported some of their best quarterly results since the real estate collapse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/business/economy/fannie-and-freddie-reports-offer-positive-sign-for-housing.html', 'snippet': 'Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac, the two mortgage finance giants, reported some of their best quarterly results since the real estate collapse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In the latest sign that the worst might be over for the battered American housing market, the two government-controlled mortgage finance giants, Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac, this week reported some of their best quarterly results since the real estate collapse. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Twin Reports Stoke Cautious Optimism for Rebound in the Housing Market', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Twin Reports Stoke Cautious Optimism for Rebound in the Housing Market', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Assn (Fannie Mae)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T16:38:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55a9e723-d6ef-52b4-a371-2ec01f122376', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55a9e723-d6ef-52b4-a371-2ec01f122376'}, {'abstract': 'Meet Todd Akin, the Missouri Republican trying to unseat Claire McCaskill.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/too-conservative-or-just-extremely-conservative/', 'snippet': 'Meet Todd Akin, the Missouri Republican trying to unseat Claire McCaskill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ahead of Tuesday’s G.O.P. primary in Missouri, Senator Claire McCaskill and her Democratic supporters spent around $2 million on ads describing one candidate, Representative Todd Akin, as too conservative for the state. Ms. McCaskill’s hope was that Missouri Republicans would think “too conservative, sounds good!” and support Mr. Akin—in her estimation a relatively weak challenger. That strategy seems to have worked: Mr. Akin won last night’s race with 36 percent of the vote.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Conservative, or Just Extremely Conservative?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akin, Todd', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCaskill, Claire', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T16:40:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/590b1729-2bd4-5138-8e91-9a985adbbb29', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/590b1729-2bd4-5138-8e91-9a985adbbb29'}, {'abstract': 'Three new picture books celebrate Brooklyn, Times Square and the Cathedral of St. John the Divine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/books/selina-alkos-b-is-for-brooklyn-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Three new picture books celebrate Brooklyn, Times Square and the Cathedral of St. John the Divine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a moment when crowded public schools, escalating rents, competitive hyperparenting and a flagging economy may drive wavering New York parents out to the suburbs, three newly published and gloriously illustrated books for city offspring could persuade them to stay put.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/books/08bforbrooklyn/08bforbrooklyn-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 299, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/08/books/08bforbrooklyn/08bforbrooklyn-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 299}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/books/08bforbrooklyn/08bforbrooklyn-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 511, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/books/08bforbrooklyn/08bforbrooklyn-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1460, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/books/08bforbrooklyn/08bforbrooklyn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/08/books/08bforbrooklyn/08bforbrooklyn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/books/08bforbrooklyn/08bforbrooklyn-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Kids’ Stories', 'kicker': "Children's Books", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rockliff, Mara', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alko, Selina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKendry, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Low, William', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T16:42:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamela Paul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fdc5f81-3ed6-516c-8347-b6144182ed5e', 'word_count': 1007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fdc5f81-3ed6-516c-8347-b6144182ed5e'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Stott’s new book traces the roots of evolutionary theory, from Aristotle to Alfred Russel Wallace.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/natural-selections-evolution-rebecca-stott-talks-about-darwins-ghosts/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Stott’s new book traces the roots of evolutionary theory, from Aristotle to Alfred Russel Wallace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Soon after he published “On the Origin of Species,” Charles Darwin was accused of neglecting to mention the thinkers who had helped to shape evolutionary theory before him. He scrambled to put together a list of predecessors that would be added to future editions of his book. In “Darwin’s Ghosts,” Rebecca Stott tells the story of those predecessors’ work, from the empirical research of Aristotle to the studies of Alfred Russel Wallace, who was piecing together the science around the same time as Darwin. In The New York Times Book Review, Hugh Raffles called the book an “absorbing account” with a narrative that “flows easily across continents and centuries.” In a recent e-mail interview, Ms. Stott discussed the roots of her interest in Darwin, the reasons Wallace played second fiddle without complaint and more. Below are edited excerpts from the conversation:', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Natural Selection’s Evolution: Rebecca Stott Talks About ‘Darwin’s Ghosts’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Origin Of Darwinism: A Theory Evolved', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Darwin's Ghosts (Book)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evolution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Darwin, Charles Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stott, Rebecca', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wallace, Alfred Russel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T16:44:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b13fffd-3983-5dc5-aa82-de28631350c7', 'word_count': 1119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b13fffd-3983-5dc5-aa82-de28631350c7'}, {'abstract': 'Three specimens unearthed in Kenya are the most compelling evidence yet for multiple lines of evolution in our own genus, Homo, scientists said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/science/new-fossils-indicate-offshoots-in-human-family-tree.html', 'snippet': 'Three specimens unearthed in Kenya are the most compelling evidence yet for multiple lines of evolution in our own genus, Homo, scientists said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fossil by fossil, scientists over the last 40 years have suspected that their models for the more immediate human family tree — the single trunk, straight as a Ponderosa pine, up from Homo habilis to Homo erectus to Homo sapiens — were oversimplified. The day for that serious revision may be at hand.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/science/09leakey_span/09leakey_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/09/science/09leakey_span/09leakey_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/science/09leakey_span/09leakey_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/science/09leakey_span/09leakey_span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2