or/', 'snippet': 'Stung by criticism of its leadership, the museum’s board has decided the institution needs a curatorial leader in addition to a director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Museum of Contemporary Art, Los Angeles, stung by criticism of its leadership, has reversed course and decided to conduct a search for a chief curator, after initially saying that it would leave the position unfilled.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reversing Course,  Los Angeles Art Museum Will Look for Chief Curator', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Los Angeles Museum, in Switch, to Seek Curator', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deitch, Jeffrey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schimmel, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T17:20:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd1be927-1449-5cae-ae35-71341206edda', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd1be927-1449-5cae-ae35-71341206edda'}, {'abstract': 'A picture of the North Korean first lady, Ri Sol-ju, published on Tuesday shows her with a Christian Dior handbag, something most North Korean women have never heard of, much less owned.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/in-a-starving-nation-luxury-for-a-few/', 'snippet': 'A picture of the North Korean first lady, Ri Sol-ju, published on Tuesday shows her with a Christian Dior handbag, something most North Korean women have never heard of, much less owned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — The South Korean news media, which scrutinizes every photo of the North Korean leader, Kim Jong-un, zeroed in this week on one particular photo released by the North’s state-run news agency on Tuesday. It shows Mr. Kim watching an art performance by soldiers during a military visit, the first reported in the North Korean media since he fired the top army leader, Vice Marshal Ri Yong-ho, on July 15.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Starving Nation, Luxury for a Few', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Famine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Handbags and Purses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luxury Goods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ri Sol-ju', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T17:21:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7092738d-0397-5e62-b961-75a8d5f3f358', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7092738d-0397-5e62-b961-75a8d5f3f358'}, {'abstract': 'Seth Numrich will portray the “Golden Boy” protagonist Joe Bonaparte, a young man torn between careers as a violinist and a boxer, alongside an ensemble cast that includes Tony Shalhoub (of TV’s “Monk” and Broadway’s “Lend Me a Tenor”) and Danny Burstein (a recent Tony Award nominee for “Follies”).', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/golden-boy-cast-features-tony-shalhoub-yvonne-strahovski-and-danny-burstein/', 'snippet': 'Seth Numrich will portray the “Golden Boy” protagonist Joe Bonaparte, a young man torn between careers as a violinist and a boxer, alongside an ensemble cast that includes Tony Shalhoub (of TV’s “Monk” and Broadway’s “Lend Me a Tenor”) and Danny B...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seth Numrich will play the lead character in Bartlett Sher’s coming production of Clifford Odets’s “Golden Boy” for Lincoln Center Theater, alongside an ensemble cast including Yvonne Strahovski, Tony Shalhoub, Danny Burstein and Dagmara Dominczyk among several others, press representatives for the theater company said on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Golden Boy’ Cast Features Tony Shalhoub, Yvonne Strahovski and Danny Burstein', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Casting Announced For ‘Golden Boy’ Revival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Golden Boy (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Camp, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cullen, Sean', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eisenberg, Ned', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jenkins, Daniel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Numrich, Seth', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Odets, Clifford', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shalhoub, Tony', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sher, Bartlett', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Belasco Theater', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Theater', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T17:22:34+0000'