 is hinged at the top. And that makes all the difference.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/a-critical-design-change-for-a-bag-to-carry-your-tech-stuff/', 'snippet': 'The Command Messenger bag by Timbuk2, for carrying a laptop, is hinged at the top. And that makes all the difference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few months back, I wrote about what tech stuff I own — and what I carry it in. I noted that I had a Timbuk2 messenger bag. It’s a Transportation Security Administration-approved model that unzips to open like a butterfly’s wings, so that the laptop compartment can lie flat for airport scanning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Critical Design Change for a Bag to Carry Your Tech Stuff', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laptop Computers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T19:06:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c1159de-4820-51fe-88ac-28e968ba765d', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c1159de-4820-51fe-88ac-28e968ba765d'}, {'abstract': 'Slow release of ingredients provides lasting benefits, companies say, and more consumers are willing to wait for results.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/fashion/time-release-products-prove-popularskin-deep.html', 'snippet': 'Slow release of ingredients provides lasting benefits, companies say, and more consumers are willing to wait for results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE beauty industry, long promising to stop or at least stave off time, is finding a way to market it. Over the last year or so, store shelves have become packed with so-called time-release products, which promise staggered benefits the longer they sink in. \xa0 ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09SKIN1/09zSKIN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 956, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09SKIN1/09zSKIN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1911, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09SKIN1/09zSKIN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09SKIN1/09zSKIN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09SKIN1/09zSKIN1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marketing Time in a Bottle Pays Off', 'kicker': 'Skin Deep', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marketing Time in a Bottle Pays Off', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clinique', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joey New York', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T19:07:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b1301a3-112a-5b23-89a2-4a782e003205', 'word_count': 892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b1301a3-112a-5b23-89a2-4a782e003205'}, {'abstract': 'Why the Ohio River Valley mattered so much to the Union – and why the Confederacy wanted it.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/the-breadbasket-of-the-union/', 'snippet': 'Why the Ohio River Valley mattered so much to the Union – and why the Confederacy wanted it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The summer of 1862 saw the Civil War’s two fronts as a mirror image. In the West, Federal troops had harnessed long stretches of the Cumberland, Tennessee and Mississippi Rivers to drive deep into the Confederacy. Fort Henry, Fort Donelson, Nashville and Memphis had all fallen, leaving Union forces largely in control of Kentucky, middle and western Tennessee, northern Mississippi and northern Alabama. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breadbasket of the Union', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio River', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T19:07:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Phillips', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Phillips', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a5be8cf-b512-5f3a-88c5-f4c7ef4e5eaf', 'word_count': 1868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a5be8cf-b512-5f3a-88c5-f4c7ef4e5eaf'}, {'abstract': 'Members of the kibbutz, on Israel’s border with Egypt and the Gaza Strip, recalled Sunday’s attack on Egyptian soldiers and why they continue to live near the dangerous border.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/world/middleeast/near-miss-for-kibbutz-in-path-of-sinai-incursion.html', 'snippet': 'Members of the kibbutz, on Israel’s border with Egypt and the Gaza Strip, recalled Sunday’s attack on Egyptian soldiers and why they continue to live near the dangerous border.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KEREM SHALOM, Israel — The members of the tiny kibbutz here on Israel’s troubled border with Egypt and the Gaza Strip were just finishing a light supper in their dining hall on Sunday evening when text messages warned them to take cover. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Near Miss for Kibbutz in Path of Sinai Incursion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Residents Of Kibbutz, A Near Miss Is Unsettling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kibbutz Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sinai Peninsula (Egypt)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T19:15:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c453c9b-236d-5b60-8148-dd392d9f61c5', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c453c9b-236d-5b60-8148-dd392d9f61c5'}, {'abstract': 'Real Madrid Coach Jose Mourinho, in New York for an international friendly against A.C. Milan at Yankee Stadium, said he would be interested in coaching in the United States in the future.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/mourinho-has-eyes-on-u-s/', 'snippet': 'Real Madrid Coach Jose Mourinho, in New York for an international friendly against A.C. Milan at Yankee Stadium, said he would be interested in coaching in the United States in the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Word is, he no longer cares to be called the Special One.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mourinho Has Eyes on U.S.', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mourinho, Jose', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Real Madrid (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T19:17:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f346a604-1c0f-57a0-b11b-261ac56b54db', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f346a604-1c0f-57a0-b11b-261ac56b54db'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of towering, sinuous sculptures by John Chamberlain will be displayed in the plaza of the Seagram Building.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/chamberlain-works-to-be-displayed-at-seagram-plaza/', 'snippet': 'A collection of towering, sinuous sculptures by John Chamberlain will be displayed in the plaza of the Seagram Building.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The plaza of the Seagram Building, which has been the stage for a procession of supersized contemporary art installations over the last few years, is about to sprout a forest of tinfoil tentacles. Or at least a bunch of towering, sinuous things that appear to be made of foil, created by the sculptor John Chamberlain, who died in 2011.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chamberlain Works to Be Displayed at Plaza of Seagram Building', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chamberlain Sculptures at Seagram Building', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chamberlain, John (1927-2011)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gagosian Gallery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T19:20:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca66511c-b74c-5529-9bfe-0c39acde08ae', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca66511c-b74c-5529-9bfe-0c39acde08ae'}, {'abstract': 'For the luxury consumer who is excited to hear about what’s going on in a range of categories, the first issue of Du Jour, a new print-digital hybrid, will be released this month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/fashion/du-jour-a-new-magazine-for-the-wealthy.html', 'snippet': 'For the luxury consumer who is excited to hear about what’s going on in a range of categories, the first issue of Du Jour, a new print-digital hybrid, will be released this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS the textbook-thick September issues of fashion magazines begin clogging mailboxes and newsstands this week, there will be some new faces competing for your attention, especially if you are part of that vastly underserved population known as rich people.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09zFRONTROW/09zFRONTROW-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 864, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09zFRONTROW/09zFRONTROW-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1727, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09zFRONTROW/09zFRONTROW-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09zFRONTROW/09zFRONTROW-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09zFRONTROW/09zFRONTROW-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType':