eral Reserve and the Justice Department are now in the uncomfortable position of deciding what to do with their i...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The  order issued to Standard Chartered by Benjamin M. Lawsky, the superintendent of the New York State Department of Financial Services, creates a problem for the federal government in its own investigations of the bank. Mr. Lawsky accused the bank of operating “as a rogue institution” in its dealings with Iranian customers in violation of federal law, and seeks to revoke its license to do business in New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Next in the Standard Chartered Case', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iranian-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawsky, Benjamin M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spitzer, Eliot L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Department of Financial Services (NYS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Standard Chartered Bank PLC', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T20:43:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cd59efa-d09c-513c-b403-167615a6146b', 'word_count': 939, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cd59efa-d09c-513c-b403-167615a6146b'}, {'abstract': 'The mobile wallet just became more hip with the news that Starbucks has teamed up with Square, the mobile payments start-up. Competitors, analysts and others weighed in on the news of the deal.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/starbucks-square-reactions/', 'snippet': 'The mobile wallet just became more hip with the news that Starbucks has teamed up with Square, the mobile payments start-up. Competitors, analysts and others weighed in on the news of the deal.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The mobile wallet just became more hip with the news that Starbucks has teamed up with Square, the mobile payment start-up. Beginning this fall, you’ll be able to pay for a cup of joe at Starbucks by showing a Square barcode on your smartphone to a cashier.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Starbucks-Square Deal: Visionary or Risky?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Commerce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Square Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starbucks Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T20:44:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fe0488c-1f7f-5f7d-8109-0370859ffd44', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fe0488c-1f7f-5f7d-8109-0370859ffd44'}, {'abstract': 'Fashion is in the midst of a serious affair with tennis, as editors, designers and models hit the courts to play or cheer. Now serving and rooting: Anna Wintour.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/fashion/tennis-and-fashion-its-a-love-match.html', 'snippet': 'Fashion is in the midst of a serious affair with tennis, as editors, designers and models hit the courts to play or cheer. Now serving and rooting: Anna Wintour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WANT to rub shoulders with a high-powered fashion editor? How about a designer? Arguably the best place these days isn’t the Top of the Standard hotel or even Amy Sacco’s new boîte, No. 8, but a nondescript slab of a building at 27th Street and Eighth Avenue, a neighbor to Chelsea housing projects and a Gristede’s grocery store, and the home of the misleadingly titled Midtown Tennis Club. (It’s not in Midtown, and membership isn’t required to play there.)', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09TENNIS/09zTENNIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 520, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09TENNIS/09zTENNIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 520}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09TENNIS/09zTENNIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 887, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09TENNIS/09zTENNIS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1773, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/