nesday, upgrading her previous two Olympic silver medals to gold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Allyson Felix of the United States won the women’s 200 meters at the London Games in 21.88 seconds on Wednesday, upgrading her previous two Olympic silver medals to gold.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/sports/olympics/20120809_FELIX-slide-BGO5/20120809_FELIX-slide-BGO5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/sports/olympics/20120809_FELIX-slide-BGO5/20120809_FELIX-slide-BGO5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/sports/olympics/20120809_FELIX-slide-BGO5/20120809_FELIX-slide-BGO5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/08/sports/olympics/20120809_FELIX-slide-BGO5/20120809_FELIX-slide-BGO5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/08/sports/olympics/20120809_FELIX-slide-BGO5/20120809_FELIX-slide-BGO5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Felix Wins Gold', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T20:52:03+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/1df45655-786d-575a-b6d0-7880fdff57d3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/1df45655-786d-575a-b6d0-7880fdff57d3'}, {'abstract': 'Grand Band, a group of six new-music pianists who first played together at the Bang on the Can Marathon in June, gave its second performance Tuesday night at Le Poisson Rouge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/arts/music/grand-band-at-le-poisson-rouge.html', 'snippet': 'Grand Band, a group of six new-music pianists who first played together at the Bang on the Can Marathon in June, gave its second performance Tuesday night at Le Poisson Rouge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When people refer to piano quartets or piano trios, they generally mean a piano and some other stuff — a violin and a cello, say. But the new ensemble Grand Band is a piano sextet in the purest sense: six pianos, and only six pianos.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Flock of Keyboards, Gathered in the Round', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Flock of Keyboards, Gathered in the Round', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Poisson Rouge', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grand Band', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T20:53:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/03510e68-7985-507d-98dc-1dbcccddf462', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03510e68-7985-507d-98dc-1dbcccddf462'}, {'abstract': 'Dennis Spurr, owner of the Fantastic Sausage Factory in Weymouth, England, likes to mix unusual ingredients in his products.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/weymouth-journal-beer-in-sausage-rather-than-beer-and-sausage/', 'snippet': 'Dennis Spurr, owner of the Fantastic Sausage Factory in Weymouth, England, likes to mix unusual ingredients in his products.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Periodically throughout the Olympics we will check in with Dennis Spurr, owner of the Fantastic Sausage Factory in Weymouth, a pretty town on the English coast where the sailing events are taking place. Mr. Spurr’s sausage business was a target of the Olympic branding authorities in 2007 after he put up a sign featuring the Olympic five-ring logo fashioned out of sausage links. He took it down on their demands, but replaced it with a sign featuring five squares made out of sausage links.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weymouth Journal: Beer in Sausage, Rather Than Beer and Sausage', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weymouth Journal: Strawberries and Sausage?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sausages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spurr, Dennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fantastic Sausage Factory (Weymouth, England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Weymouth (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T20:56:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02fc5d7c-072d-5c86-a102-699a9b8c5390', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02fc5d7c-072d-5c86-a102-699a9b8c5390'}, {'abstract': 'As apparel sales lag, accessories — footwear, handbags, glasses and hats — are booming. Fashion students are interested.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/fashion/accessories-are-hot-for-retailers-and-fashion-students.html', 'snippet': 'As apparel sales lag, accessories — footwear, handbags, glasses and hats — are booming. Fashion students are interested.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A YEAR before Paula Cheng graduated from Parsons the New School for Design with an M.F.A. in fashion design in May, she won a contest organized by the Metropolitan Museum of Art to create designs inspired by the Alexander McQueen exhibition at the museum. Ms. Cheng focused not on bumster pants nor showstopper gowns, but on black platform-heeled shoes and sandals with winged tiers of fur that have already been pictured on Italian Vogue’s Web site.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09ACCESS2_SPAN/09ACCESS2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09ACCESS2_SPAN/09ACCESS2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09ACCESS2_SPAN/09ACCESS2_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09ACCESS2_SPAN/09ACCESS2_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09ACCESS2_SPAN/09ACCESS2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/09/fashion/09ACCESS2_SPAN/09ACCESS2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'All the Trimmings Are the Main Course', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All the Trimmings Are the Main Course', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Handbags and Purses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hats and Caps', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parsons the New School for Design', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunglasses', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T20:57:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simone S. Oliver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simone', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Oliver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ecad5cc-b202-52b4-b41b-d12b7536b98c', 'word_count': 1411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ecad5cc-b202-52b4-b41b-d12b7536b98c'}, {'abstract': 'Any moment not shrouded in gold, silv