oduction of “Coriolanus,” Shakespeare’s drama about an election that pits disdainful elites against the 99 percent, would seem to be a perfect fit for both our time and the inherently populist theater series to which it belongs, Shakespeare in the Park(ing) Lot. (Yes, this Elizabethan tragedy is performed gratis on the pavement of a functioning municipal parking lot, amid cars, trucks and pedestrians ferrying home Chinese takeout.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/arts/coriolanus/coriolanus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/arts/coriolanus/coriolanus-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1276, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Angry Romans Occupy Ludlow Street', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Angry Romans Occupy Ludlow Street', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-08T21:50:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/28a8c1c7-0cac-5374-a6c2-40ed669f6544', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28a8c1c7-0cac-5374-a6c2-40ed669f6544'}, {'abstract': 'Unlike R-rated movies or a learner’s permit, there are no clear rules that dictate when a child can or should have a phone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/technology/personaltech/weighing-when-a-child-is-old-enough-for-a-cellphone.html', 'snippet': 'Unlike R-rated movies or a learner’s permit, there are no clear rules that dictate when a child can or should have a phone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wendy Sue Swanson, a pediatrician in Seattle, knows that a 9-month-old baby can perform some basic acts of imitation. You might expect smiling, blinking and some other facial expressions and gestures. But you know what she’s seeing a lot of?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/business/9-TOOLKIT/9-TOOLKIT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/business/9-TOOLKIT/9-TOOLKIT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/business/9-TOOLKIT/9-TOOLKIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/09/business/9-TOOLKIT/9-TOOLKIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/business/9-TOOLKIT/9-TOOLKIT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Johnny’s First Phone: A Guide for Parents', 'kicker': 'To