gainst Iranian Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Persian Gulf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T00:59:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10bd7ae2-c010-597c-807f-54394bd11df4', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10bd7ae2-c010-597c-807f-54394bd11df4'}, {'abstract': 'By broadly interpreting Title IX, the Supreme Court has made the law a powerful force for the advancement of women. But the recent direction of the court’s jurisprudence makes it highly unlikely the court would play a similar role if another rights-creating statute came along.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/the-court-at-the-olympics/', 'snippet': 'By broadly interpreting Title IX, the Supreme Court has made the law a powerful force for the advancement of women. But the recent direction of the court’s jurisprudence makes it highly unlikely the court would play a similar role if another right...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many people are celebrating the achievements of American women at the London Olympics, where women exceed men in the number of athletes on the United States team and have walked away with an impressive number of gold medals. And many have noted the connection between the women’s historic success and the 40th anniversary of Title IX, which President Richard M. Nixon signed into law on June 23, 1972.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Court at the Olympics', 'kicker': 'Opinionator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Title IX (Gender Discrimination Legislation)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalia, Antonin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T01:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c55fb16c-c03a-5049-bee8-39ee49a418e7', 'word_count': 1443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c55fb16c-c03a-5049-bee8-39ee49a418e7'}, {'abstract': 'What the artist saw in Michigan and New York.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/things-i-saw-no-25/', 'snippet': 'What the artist saw in Michigan and New York.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Suggestions for what you’d like Jason to see and draw may be sent to thingsisaw@nytimes.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Things I Saw — No. 25', 'kicker': 'Things I Saw', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T01:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Polan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb2ecb4d-63af-5ede-b9cf-92b616adcf67', 'word_count': 21, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb2ecb4d-63af-5ede-b9cf-92b616adcf67'}, {'abstract': 'A projected life-size image of a woman explains where to find taxi stands and baggage claim every time someone comes within 30 feet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/nyregion/la-guardias-digital-avatar-gives-passengers-airport-information.html', 'snippet': 'A projected life-size image of a woman explains where to find taxi stands and baggage claim every time someone comes within 30 feet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'La Guardia Airport’s newest employee, a young woman named Marie, made quite an impression during her first day on the job Wednesday. Airport managers smiled as they watched the blue-eyed, 6-foot-tall blonde with apple-red cheeks stand in front of new arrivals and pleasantly explain where they could find the baggage claim and the taxi stands. Her bosses did not even mind when she twiddled her thumbs and rolled her eyes when no one was around.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/nyregion/AVATAR/AVATAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/09/nyregion/AVATAR/AVATAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty