': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Schweber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b351e7f8-a4a3-54ab-aec7-cc21e4a5a5dc', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b351e7f8-a4a3-54ab-aec7-cc21e4a5a5dc'}, {'abstract': 'Bundling mortgages and selling them to investors is helping banks make big profits even as they charge lower interest rates.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/with-rate-twist-banks-increase-mortgage-profit/', 'snippet': 'Bundling mortgages and selling them to investors is helping banks make big profits even as they charge lower interest rates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Interest rates on mortgages and refinancing are at record lows, giving borrowers plenty to celebrate. But the bigger winners are the banks making the loans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Rates Low, Banks Increase Mortgage Profit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Rates Low For Home Loans, Bankers Cash In', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'US Bancorp (Del)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wells Fargo & Company', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T01:03:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/215116c3-66d4-5d0f-a892-062892ef3bbf', 'word_count': 1191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/215116c3-66d4-5d0f-a892-062892ef3bbf'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Chris Christie demanded that existing contracts and their renewals be exempt from the audits approved by the New Jersey Legislature.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/nyregion/christie-seeks-to-weaken-new-oversight-of-halfway-houses.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Chris Christie demanded that existing contracts and their renewals be exempt from the audits approved by the New Jersey Legislature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie’s administration came under heavy criticism from legislators last month at hearings on New Jersey’s privately run halfway houses, which handle thousands of inmates each year. On Wednesday, Mr. Christie fired back, saying he would significantly weaken a measure approved by the legislators to increase their oversight of the system.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Christie Seeks to Weaken Oversight of Halfway Houses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Christie Seeks to Weaken Halfway Houses’ Oversight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Community Education Centers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palatucci, William J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T01:06:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dolnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dolnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce1e6d85-2c6f-538f-9d1b-3024e7ea93f8', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce1e6d85-2c6f-538f-9d1b-3024e7ea93f8'}, {'abstract': 'Ri Sol-ju, the wife of Kim Jong-un, was pictured with what appeared to be a Christian Dior handbag. The bag’s going price in Seoul is $1,600, about 16 times the monthly wage of some of the country’s best-paid workers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/world/asia/north-korea-is-that-a-dior-comrade.html', 'snippet': 'Ri Sol-ju, the wife of Kim Jong-un, was pictured with what appeared to be a Christian Dior handbag. The bag’s going price in Seoul is $1,600, about 16 times the monthly wage of some of the country’s best-paid workers.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In a country that still has trouble feeding all its people, Ri Sol-ju, the wife of the country’s young leader, was pictured this week with what appears to be a luxury many North Korean women have probably never heard of, much less owned: a Christian Dior handbag. If it is not a knockoff, the bag’s going price in Seoul is the equivalent of $1,600, about 16 times the monthly wage of some of North Korea’s best-paid workers. The family of Ms. Ri’s husband, Kim Jong-un, has long been said to live in style. A former Russian presidential envoy who traveled with his father on a private train in 2001 reported that it was stocked with cases of French wine and that live lobsters were delivered. But it has been unusual for Pyongyang’s elite to show wealth so publicly. In a recent speech to party leaders, Mr. Kim lovingly remembered how his father insisted on wearing a threadbare gray parka to remind himself of the famine of the 1990s. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korea: Is That a Dior, Comrade?', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Korea: Is That a Dior, Comrade?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ri Sol-ju', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Handbags and Purses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Dior SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T01:09:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d88b368-e6cf-51cb-867d-b69907429051', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d88b368-e6cf-51cb-867d-b69907429051'}, {'abstract': 'Misty May-Treanor and Kerri Walsh Jennings defeated another American team in two sets to win their third consecutive gold medal in beach volleyball.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/sports/olympics/in-beach-volleyball-third-gold-medal-for-americans.html', 'snippet': 'Misty May-Treanor and Kerri Walsh Jennings defeated another American team in two sets to win their third consecutive gold medal in beach volleyball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Misty May-Treanor said she wanted Wednesday night’s gold medal match to be the best of her and her American beach volleyball teammate Kerri Walsh Jennings’s lives. And by most accounts, it was. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/sports/BEACH1/BEACH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 723, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/sports/BEACH1/BEACH1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1446, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/sports/BEACH1/BEACH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/09/sports/BEACH1/BEACH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/sports/BEACH1/BEACH1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'All-American Ending for Beach Volleyball Team', 'kicker': "Beach Volleyball | Women's Final", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All-American Match, All-American Ending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'May-Treanor, Misty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walsh Jennings, Kerri', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ross, April', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beach Volleyball', 'rank': 6, 'major'