ething is true.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/08/hear-all-ye-people-hearken-o-earth/', 'snippet': 'While truth might not be dependent on typeface, a typeface can subtly influence us to believe something is true.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is the first installment in a two-part series. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hear, All Ye People;  Hearken, O Earth (Part 1)', 'kicker': 'Errol Morris', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T01:15:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Errol Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Errol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d85533c-910f-54de-b285-22c193aa26ad', 'word_count': 4361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d85533c-910f-54de-b285-22c193aa26ad'}, {'abstract': 'Landing near Shanghai, a typhoon forced more than a million people were forced to evacuate and the city’s two major airports delayed or canceled hundreds of flights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/world/asia/china-typhoon-leads-to-evacuation.html', 'snippet': 'Landing near Shanghai, a typhoon forced more than a million people were forced to evacuate and the city’s two major airports delayed or canceled hundreds of flights.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A typhoon struck the eastern coast of China on Wednesday, landing near Shanghai and creating torrential rain and powerful winds that knocked out power and forced the evacuation of more than a million people. There were no reports of deaths, but many businesses were closed and Shanghai’s two major airports delayed or canceled hundreds of flights. Shanghai’s ports, among the world’s busiest by container volume, were also closed Wednesday, according to Reuters. Local governments in the region were on high alert following flooding in Beijing in late July that caused the deaths of at least 77 people and led to a public outcry over the city’s poor preparedness. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Typhoon Leads to Evacuation', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Typhoon Leads to Evacuation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T01:18:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bf438c0-3b61-5e9c-8bcf-4664517ff351', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bf438c0-3b61-5e9c-8bcf-4664517ff351'}, {'abstract': 'The results focused renewed attention on Rupert Murdoch’s decision in June to approve a spinoff of his company’s newspapers into a new company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/business/media/news-corp-posts-loss-on-publishing-write-down.html', 'snippet': 'The results focused renewed attention on Rupert Murdoch’s decision in June to approve a spinoff of his company’s newspapers into a new company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A write-down on News Corporation’s underperforming publishing unit contributed to the company’s loss of $1.6 billion, or 64 cents a share, in the quarter that ended June 30.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/business/Newscorp/Newscorp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/09/business/Newscorp/Newscorp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1310, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Publishing Losses Hurt Results at News Corp.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Publishing Losses Hurt Results at News Corp.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dow Jones & Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX (TV Network)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wall Street Journal', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T01:21:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'midd