None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T01:47:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85cede8f-1aa0-54a5-8f82-89fd0839b36f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85cede8f-1aa0-54a5-8f82-89fd0839b36f'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney’s charge that President Obama is encouraging welfare dependency by ending federal work requirements is false and divisive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/opinion/mr-romney-hits-bottom-on-welfare.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney’s charge that President Obama is encouraging welfare dependency by ending federal work requirements is false and divisive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney’s campaign has hit new depths of truth-twisting with its accusation that President Obama plans to “gut welfare reform” by ending federal work requirements. The claim is blatantly false, but it says a great deal about Mr. Romney’s increasingly desperate desire to define the president as something he is not.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Romney Hits Bottom on Welfare', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Romney Hits Bottom on Welfare', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Welfare (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T01:47:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/336efe06-64b5-520a-8ccf-5de976e17ab8', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/336efe06-64b5-520a-8ccf-5de976e17ab8'}, {'abstract': 'After its successful landing on Mars, the rover Curiosity will give us a flood of data from its sensors and cameras, in something close to real time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/opinion/news-from-mars.html', 'snippet': 'After its successful landing on Mars, the rover Curiosity will give us a flood of data from its sensors and cameras, in something close to real time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mars never gets old. Every time we get a new look at the planet we see it in higher resolution. The earliest images shot from a dedicated spacecraft, taken by Mariner 4 in July 1965, look more like images from an abdominal ultrasound than photographs of a planet. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News From Our Neighboring Planet', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'News From Our Neighboring Planet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mars (Planet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Curiosity (Mars Rover)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T01:47:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/39284ce7-ec98-5280-be61-f003e3c498f1', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39284ce7-ec98-5280-be61-f003e3c498f1'}, {'abstract': 'An appeals court convincingly ruled that an inmate could sue the warden for endangering his health and for cruel and unusual punishment when the heat index in his unit reached “extreme danger.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/opinion/heat-exhaustion-in-a-texas-prison.html', 'snippet': 'An appeals court convincingly ruled that an inmate could sue the warden for endangering his health and for cruel and unusual punishment when the heat index in his unit reached “extreme danger.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'For much of the summer of 2008, temperatures in Beeville, Tex., soared above 90 degrees. For almost two weeks, the heat index was 130 degrees or higher, in what scientists consider the “extreme danger” range, when the risk of heat stroke is imminent. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heat Exhaustion in a Texas Prison', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heat Exhaustion in a Texas Prison', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blackmon, Eugene', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T01:47:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bde8682-c7fa-5c3d-8dfc-691888f36e87', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bde8682-c7fa-5c3d-8dfc-691888f36e87'}, {'abstract': 'Why is Obama passive as thousands of Syrians are dying? Top strategists want him to act now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/opinion/kristof-obama-awol-in-syria.html', 'snippet': 'Why is Obama passive as thousands of Syrians are dying? Top strategists want him to act now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ASPEN, Colo.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': 