le/3760d9b4-04d5-5197-8436-5da4f317ba4f', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3760d9b4-04d5-5197-8436-5da4f317ba4f'}, {'abstract': 'A new whistle-blower lawsuit has been filed against Infosys, the giant Indian outsourcing company, by a man who says he was harassed into quitting after he reported visa fraud by managers there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/us/california-infosys-faces-2nd-suit-over-visas.html', 'snippet': 'A new whistle-blower lawsuit has been filed against Infosys, the giant Indian outsourcing company, by a man who says he was harassed into quitting after he reported visa fraud by managers there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new whistle-blower lawsuit has been filed against Infosys, the giant Indian outsourcing company, by a man who says he was harassed into quitting after he reported visa fraud by managers there. Satya Dev Tripuraneni, an American who worked for Infosys for five years in California, says the company billed fraudulently for workers brought from India on short-term visitor visas and also evaded taxes. After he reported his concerns, he was threatened and demoted, Mr. Tripuraneni claims in the lawsuit filed in federal court for the Northern District of California. Danielle D’Angelo, an Infosys spokeswoman, said the company had started an internal investigation of the claims. A trial in the case of Jay Palmer, another whistle-blower who reported suspected visa fraud at Infosys, begins Aug. 20 in Montgomery, Ala. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Company Faces 2nd Suit Over Visas', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Company Faces 2nd Suit Over Visas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tripuraneni, Satya Dev', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whistle-Blowers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Visas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Infosys Technologies Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T04:14:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/38c54aee-cca3-5729-bd4e-88e89da8688c', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38c54aee-cca3-5729-bd4e-88e89da8688c'}, {'abstract': 'José Mourinho of Real Madrid said he would be interested in coaching in the United States in the future, although not as the national coach.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/sports/soccer/real-madrids-mourinho-sees-a-future-coaching-in-the-us.html', 'snippet': 'José Mourinho of Real Madrid said he would be interested in coaching in the United States in the future, although not as the national coach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'José Mourinho of Real Madrid said he would be interested in coaching in the United States in the future, although not as the national coach. “The quality of the game is good,” he said in New York. “They have a positive approach to the game, they want to win, want to play well, want to express good qualities. Step by step it is coming, and one day I want to give a little bit of a help.” More at nytimes.com/goal.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Real Madrid’s Mourinho Sees a Future Coaching in the U.S.', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Soccer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Real Madrid’s Mourinho Sees A Future Coaching in the U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Real Madrid (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mourinho, Jose', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T04:15:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a56ccb9c-3836-5f65-b0d7-2925c1f9434e', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a56ccb9c-3836-5f65-b0d7-2925c1f9434e'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Defense has identified 2,059 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/us/names-of-the-dead.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense has identified 2,059 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense has identified 2,059 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations. It confirmed the death of the following American recently:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}]