e_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a09b1534-5825-5aa4-928c-dc5cb7b22b5f', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a09b1534-5825-5aa4-928c-dc5cb7b22b5f'}, {'abstract': 'Key areas are expanding far less than expected compared with the same period a year ago, although inflation has decreased dramatically.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/business/global/economic-growth-flagging-in-china.html', 'snippet': 'Key areas are expanding far less than expected compared with the same period a year ago, although inflation has decreased dramatically.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Hopes dimmed for an imminent pickup in China, the world’s growth engine, as a batch of disappointing economic data released Thursday showed industrial production and retail sales falling well short of expectations in July.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Growth Flagging in China, Government Data Show', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Growth Flagging in China, Government Data Show', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross National Product (GNP)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T07:16:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bettina Wassener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bettina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wassener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d56a1dac-5afa-5ef3-ae26-92a4561c2602', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d56a1dac-5afa-5ef3-ae26-92a4561c2602'}, {'abstract': 'Can you choose the adverb that best completes the sentence from the article?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/test-yourself-english-aug-9-2012/', 'snippet': 'Can you choose the adverb that best completes the sentence from the article?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the article “Why Can’t the Bronx Be More Like Brooklyn?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, Aug. 9, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T08:34:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7bf72ab-65c4-5725-bd45-4dddd92c3cce', 'word_count': 48, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7bf72ab-65c4-5725-bd45-4dddd92c3cce'}, {'abstract': 'The future of solar belongs to whoever can convince consumers that it’s not just for tree-huggers and rich people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/magazine/the-secret-to-solar-power.html', 'snippet': 'The future of solar belongs to whoever can convince consumers that it’s not just for tree-huggers and rich people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most mornings, Danny Kennedy hops on a bike with orange saddlebags and rides half an hour from his home to Oakland’s Jack London Square. He makes for quite a picture cruising down Telegraph Avenue, decked out as he often is in an orange helmet, orange jacket and orange leather Adidas shoes. When he arrives at his office, he often makes his rounds on an orange indoor bike. (He’s not joking around with the orange thing.) Though Kennedy was once a young environmental activist documenting the horrors of the oil and mining industries, he’s now a 41-year-old company man. The orange that he wears daily — which extends even to the checks on his shirts, and which drives his wife crazy — is the brand color for his rapidly growing residential solar company, Sungevity, whose revenues grew by a factor of eight in 2010 and doubled again in 2011, and whose employees have grown to 260 from 3 since the company’s inception five years ago.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12Solar1/12Solar1-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 455, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12Solar1/12Solar1-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 455}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12Solar1/mag-12Solar-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 776, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12Solar1/mag-12Solar-t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1448, 'width': 1098, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12Solar1/12Solar1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12Solar1/12Solar1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12Solar1/12Solar1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Secret to Solar Po