t': 'If Chinese officials hoped the trial of Bo Xilai’s wife would show off a more transparent legal system, they are likely to be disappointed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/world/asia/murder-trial-of-bo-xilais-wife-concludes.html', 'snippet': 'If Chinese officials hoped the trial of Bo Xilai’s wife would show off a more transparent legal system, they are likely to be disappointed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HEFEI, China — Worried that a longtime friend and business associate might harm her only child, Gu Kailai lured him to a rented villa in southwest China, plied him with alcohol until he could take no more and then, when he began to vomit and requested a drink of water, poured a poisonous concoction into his mouth.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/global-home/10china-image3/10china-image3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/global-home/10china-image3/10china-image3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1534, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/global-home/10china-image3/10china-image3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/10/global-home/10china-image3/10china-image3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/global-home/10china-image3/10china-image3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fast-Paced Trial in China Murder Leaves Shadows', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fast-Paced Trial In China Murder Leaves Shadows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heywood, Neil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gu Kailai', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bo Xilai', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T10:22:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1761491-405b-587a-bc0e-1b536be23d9b', 'word_count': 1417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1761491-405b-587a-bc0e-1b536be23d9b'}, {'abstract': 'The Israeli protest movement is dead. Israelis have moved on, the government has moved on — to tax hikes and budget cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/the-israeli-protest-movement-is-dead/', 'snippet': 'The Israeli protest movement is dead. Israelis have moved on, the government has moved on — to tax hikes and budget cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEL AVIV\xa0— Last summer was the summer of tents and hope. This summer is the summer of no free lunches and tough economic measures. Last summer, a surprisingly vigorous social justice movement sent hundreds of thousands of Israelis to the town square. This summer, its dregs are attracting meager participation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer of No Discontent', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T10:33:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea111e60-be0e-51ae-b8fa-b9e5b027546c', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea111e60-be0e-51ae-b8fa-b9e5b027546c'}, {'abstract': 'The United States women’s soccer team will play Japan in a rematch of last year’s World Cup final, and Usain Bolt of Jamaica looks to win his second gold of these Games. Soccer reporter Sam Borden joins Victor Mather in London to preview the women’s final.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/what-were-watching-u-s-soccer-seeking-revenge-and-gold/', 'snippet': 'The United States women’s soccer team will play Japan in a rematch of last year’s World Cup final, and Usain Bolt of Jamaica looks to win his second gold of these Games. Soccer reporter Sam Borden joins Victor Mather in London to preview the women...', 'lead_paragraph': "(function($){var data = chameleonData;var ticker = new NYTD.NYTMM.NewsTicker($('#nytmm_embed_223'), data);})(jQuery||NYTD.jQuery);", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Watching: U.S. Soccer Seeking Revenge, and Gold', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolt, Usain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Women's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T10:40:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92193b22-47da-50ae-b7c3-8a69fecdce23', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92193b22-47da-50ae-b7c3-8a69fecdce23'}, {'abstract': 'Where in the world should Mark Bittman go eat? He wants to hear your suggestions.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/go-ahead-send-me-packing/', 'snippet': 'Where in the world should Mark Bittman go eat? He wants to hear your suggestions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The (Times) Magazine’s food and drink issue will appear on Oct. 14, and the editors (of which I’m one) have agreed that I should travel somewhere and write about the food. That, in itself, is not that unusual of an idea, but maybe this is: we’ve decided to solicit your input to determine where I’ll go. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Go Ahead, Send Me Packing', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ab7ab36-4e6d-59cc-b079-566b9096fd58', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ab7ab36-4e6d-59cc-b079-566b9096fd58'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t sweat the recipes. Cook what looks good and prepare for happy accidents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/magazine/go-fish.html', 'snippet': 'Don’t sweat the recipes. Cook what looks good and prepare for happy accidents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I used to say that I never invented a dish in my life, but now that would be disingenuous. I know I’m not creative in the same sense that a talented chef is, but I also know that my experience has taken me from a place where I would slavishly follow recipes to one where I rarely look at them. Now almost every meal begins with a fantasy. I then buy what looks as if it has the potential to fulfill that fantasy — or simply open the refrigerator and see what’s already there. At that point I improvise on an already established theme from I guess what you’d call my repertoire. In this regard, cooking is like music, but easier: the basic skills are not difficult to attain, and the creativity comes not in reinventing them but in imagining new ways in which to combine them.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12eat1/12eat1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 419, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12eat1/12eat1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 419}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12eat1/mag-12Eat-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12eat1/mag-12Eat-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12eat1/12eat1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12eat1/12eat1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12eat1/12eat1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Go Fish', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Go Fish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pasta', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T11:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51ac1992-bc72-5f78-8bc4-0247425ae6b0', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51ac1992-bc72-5f78-8bc4-0247425ae6b0'}, {'abstract': 'Embracing cheap tequila.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/magazine/punch-drunk-love.html', 'snippet': 'Embracing cheap tequila.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a good day, the train ride from New York to Burlington, Vt., takes about nine hours. (Train? As I’ve confessed before, I’m one of those hopeless nondriving New Yorkers. Besides, I love trains. Usually.) But an unseasonably hot Wednesday in late May was not a good day. Forty minutes out of Penn Station, the engine broke down. Off went the lights and the air-conditioning. A “rescue engine” was on its way, but after half an hour slipped by without any sign of deliverance, I began to despair. Then we changed trains. Again. And again.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '40', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12drink/12drink-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 615, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12drink/12drink-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 615}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12drink/12drink-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 898, 'width': 876, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12drink/12drink-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 898, 'width': 876, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12drink/12drink-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12drink/12drink-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/magazine/12drink/12drink-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Punch-Drunk Love', 'kicker': 'Drink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Punch-Drunk Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tequila', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T11:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosie Schaap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc3ac805-c349-5a1a-9ec0-e13bc8954a6f', 'word_count': 575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc3ac805-c349-5a1a-9ec0-e13bc8954a6f'}, {'abstract': 'At TerraCycle, we believe that someone who isn’t performing well needs to know about it in real time, and someone who is doing great deserves immediate recognition.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/the-problem-with-performance-reviews/', 'snippet': 'At TerraCycle, we believe that someone who isn’t performing well needs to know about it in real time, and someone who is doing great deserves immediate recognition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Performance reviews are standard protocol in corporate America. The objective seems to be for the company to give formal and direct feedback to employees, who are assumed to understand that the reviews represent an opportunity to get a status check (like a report card) that can help them improve their performance and in the end further their careers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Problem With Performance Reviews', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance 