of-crows-at-park-avenue-armory.html', 'snippet': 'With violent dream sequences, dark symbolism and references to fascism, this 29-minute sound installation explores the repercussions of spatial-aural illusionism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The installations of Janet Cardiff and George Bures Miller have always had a poltergeist quality; they disrupt space while being more or less invisible. Using ambisonic recording technology they engulf listeners in a constantly shifting three-dimensional field — a complete soundscape, as the artists call it. Submitting to one of these works is a deeply uncanny experience, even when the sounds are derived from glorious 16th-century choral music (as in their 2001 masterwork, “The Forty Part Motet”).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/0810CROWS/0810CROWS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/0810CROWS/0810CROWS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/0810CROWS/0810CROWS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/0810CROWS/0810CROWS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1285, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/0810CROWS/0810CROWS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/0810CROWS/0810CROWS-thumbStandard.jpg', 't