: 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/sports/10bolt-span3/10bolt-span3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bolt Is First to Repeat as Winner of 100 and 200 Meters', 'kicker': 'Track and Field | Finals', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Double Repeat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Carl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolt, Usain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudisha, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jamaica (West Indies)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blake, Yohan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T16:08:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4de62479-5a5b-582e-b319-8cde71a1768d', 'word_count': 1475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4de62479-5a5b-582e-b319-8cde71a1768d'}, {'abstract': 'A writer sees, in the search engine phrases soldiers and their spouses use to find her blog, the story of war.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/search-engines-log-the-fearsome-journeys-of-war-families/', 'snippet': 'A writer sees, in the search engine phrases soldiers and their spouses use to find her blog, the story of war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A wife just found out her husband is going to war. Her husband stands in a doorway. She backs down a hallway away from the news of a deployment that keeps coming closer. She locks herself in a room, sits in front of a computer, and types into a search engine the phrase “husband off to Afghanistan soon.” She knows Afghanistan is not a word but a place. It is a country made of mountains, men, and machine guns where her husband will go to war and live or die. But she is searching for more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Search Engines Log the Fearsome Journeys of War Families', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T16:11:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amalie Flynn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amalie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flynn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6509c944-c474-5526-ab62-2c9140744ba9', 'word_count': 1386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6509c944-c474-5526-ab62-2c9140744ba9'}, {'abstract': 'The public editor provides the e-mail he has been sending to readers regarding The Times recent article on American Olympic athlete Lolo Jones.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/lolo-jones-article-is-too-harsh/', 'snippet': 'The public editor provides the e-mail he has been sending to readers regarding The Times recent article on American Olympic athlete Lolo Jones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers have weighed in to complain about The New York Times’s Aug. 5 piece on U.S. Olympics hurdler Lolo Jones. Below is the response I have sent to those who e-mailed me about this:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lolo Jones Article Is Too Harsh', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T16:12:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arthur S. Brisbane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arthur', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Brisbane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e90aa93b-5ebd-5f13-9138-b38530340caa', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e90aa93b-5ebd-5f13-9138-b38530340caa'}, {'abstract': 'In honor of “The Expendables 2,” five haikus on the glory of Sylvester Stallone.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/five-ku-short-poems-on-sylvester-stallone-in-advance-of-the-expendables-2/', 'snippet': 'In honor of “The Expendables 2,” five haikus on the glory of Sylvester Stallone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oscar nomineesFor both acting and writing:Chaplin. Welles. Stallone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Five-Ku: Short Poems on Sylvester Stallone in Advance of ‘The Expendables 2’', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stallone, Sylvester', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T16:18:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Sternbergh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sternbergh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca2aeb57-39e0-582f-ac38-44dba7fc85f5', 'word_count': 39, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca2aeb57-39e0-582f-ac38-44dba7fc85f5'}, {'abstract': 'The owner of the Crepes du Nord cafe in New York’s financial district has started cloning the French- and Scandinavian-inspired creperie in shopping mall kiosks.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/crepes-du-nord-heads-for-the-malls/', 'snippet': 'The owner of the Crepes du Nord cafe in New York’s financial district has started cloning the French- and Scandinavian-inspired creperie in shopping mall kiosks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Morten Sohlberg, the owner of the Smorgas Chef restaurants in New York and the Crepes du Nord cafe in the financial district, has started cloning the French- and Scandinavian-inspired creperie in shopping mall kiosks. As in his other restaurants, he will emphasize sustainable and organic foods, with some ingredients grown on his upstate farm. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crepes du Nord Heads for the Malls', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T16:25:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a79778e-a1f4-58ab-8eae-c8fe0b9ca383', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a79778e-a1f4-58ab-8eae-c8fe0b9ca383'}, {'abstract': 'The conflict was two very different experiences: the one on the battlefield, and the one seen from home.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/the-two-civil-wars/', 'snippet': 'The conflict was two very different experiences: the one on the battlefield, and the one seen from home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Josiah Williams was 23 years old when he saw his Uncle Whit’s head blown apart at the Battle of Cedar Mountain, which took place in north central Virginia on Aug. 9, 1862. But even his account as witness wasn’t enough to convince his parents, back in Indiana, of Whit’s death. They simply refused to believe him and, without a body to bring back, he had no more proof to offer. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Two Civil Wars', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T16:30:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Etcheson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Etcheson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15e7e093-aad8-5ff2-a211-c6dff1ef7f47', 'word_count': 1521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15e7e093-aad8-5ff2-a211-c6dff1ef7f47'}, {'abstract': 'The shows will now play through January 20th and September 30th, respectively.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/bring-it-on-and-closer-than-ever-extend-runs/', 'snippet': 'The shows will now play through January 20th and September 30th, respectively.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gimme an E! Gimme an X! Gimme … Well let’s cut to the chase: The Broadway production of “Bring It On: The Musical” will continue through Jan. 20 at the St. James Theater, the show’s producers announced on Thursday. It had been scheduled to close on Oct. 7.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Bring It On’ and ‘Closer Than Ever’ Extend Runs', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Bring It On’ Extends Run', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blankenbuehler, Andy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Amanda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitt, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maltby, Richard Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miranda, Lin-Manuel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shire, David', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitty, Jeff', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St James Theater', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'York Theater Co', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T16:32:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27b6294a-4de5-5c00-b1e4-142dded98f46', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27b6294a-4de5-5c00-b1e4-142dded98f46'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Harding, whose political influence was felt for decades from New York City to Albany as the state’s Liberal Party leader, fell from grace in 2009 after a corruption investigation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/nyregion/raymond-b-harding-ex-liberal-party-leader-dies-at-77.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Harding, whose political influence was felt for decades from New York City to Albany as the state’s Liberal Party leader, fell from grace in 2009 after a corruption investigation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Raymond B. Harding, the former leader of New York State’s Liberal Party, who advanced the careers of mayors and governors but was disgraced in the corruption scandal that brought down State Comptroller Alan G. Hevesi, died on Thursday in the Bronx. He was 77.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/nyregion/HARDING1-obit/HARDING1-obit-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 826, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/nyregion/HARDING1-obit/HARDING1-obit-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 857, 'width': 1063, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/nyregion/HARDING1-obit/HARDING1-obit-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/10/nyregion/HARDING1-obit/HARDING1-obit-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/nyregion/HARDING1-obit/HARDING1-obit-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Raymond Harding, 77, Dies; Liberal Party Power Broker', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Raymond B. Harding, 77, Liberal Party Power Broker, Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harding, Raymond B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T16:32:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert D. McFadden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d7c70c5-8370-54d7-9688-de86f7d344ef', 'word_count': 1211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d7c70c5-8370-54d7-9688-de86f7d344ef'}, {'abstract': 'The choices facing the Leadership Conference of Women Religious are the choices facing liberal Christianity as a whole.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/american-nuns-and-the-fate-of-liberal-christianity/', 'snippet': 'The choices facing the Leadership Conference of Women Religious are the choices facing liberal Christianity as a whole.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a passage from\xa0my colleague Laurie Goodstein’s dispatch from this year’s assembly of the Leadership Conference of Women Religious, the American nuns’ organization that was criticized by the Vatican earlier this year:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Nuns and the Fate of Liberal Christianity', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T16:32:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be8ada14-3c73-54e8-abda-db7520d7f5f3', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be8ada14-3c73-54e8-abda-db7520d7f5f3'}, {'abstract': 'The fourth installment in this franchise is less a thrilling reboot than a salvage mission, with Jeremy Renner taking over from Matt Damon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/movies/movie-review-the-bourne-legacy.html', 'snippet': 'The fourth installment in this franchise is less a thrilling reboot than a salvage mission, with Jeremy Renner taking over from Matt Damon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just before “The Bourne Legacy” gets its game on, the franchise’s new face, played by Jeremy Renner, comes out of the Alaskan wilderness to take refuge in a cabin. There he meets another of his kind, a superspy with a scowl and enough artillery to invade a small country. By the time they’ve grudgingly warmed up to each other an unmanned drone is blasting everything to bits. It’s an effectively blunt opener for a series that from its start has tracked a different military drone, this one a man fighting to recover first his identity and then his humanity. That you may not remember the name of Mr. Renner’s agent, Aaron Cross, after all the dust finally settles, suggests that the fight goes on.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10BOURNE_SPAN/10BOURNE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10BOURNE_SPAN/10BOURNE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image