 'Today’s pick: a graphic, black and gold platform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jane Herman delivers The Daily Shoe from the Bergdorf Goodman shoe salon in honor of the store’s 111th anniversary. Today’s pick: a graphic, black and gold platform from Giuseppe Zanotti. $775.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Daily Shoe | Giuseppe Zanotti', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T17:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e81367b4-ee2e-546e-ae13-d1883e36e587', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e81367b4-ee2e-546e-ae13-d1883e36e587'}, {'abstract': 'In a settlement announced Thursday, the Federal Trade Commission fined Google $22.5 million for privacy violations related to showing personalized ads to users of Apple’s Safari browser. It is the latest settlement in a crackdown on tech companies by the commission, though critics say regulators are not doing enough.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/f-t-c-fines-google-22-5-million-for-safari-privacy-violations/', 'snippet': 'In a settlement announced Thursday, the Federal Trade Commission fined Google $22.5 million for privacy violations related to showing personalized ads to users of Apple’s Safari browser. It is the latest settlement in a crackdown on tech companies...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Boris Roessler/European Pressphoto Agency', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/blogs/bitpix-google-logo2/bitpix-google-logo2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/blogs/bitpix-google-logo2/bitpix-google-logo2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/10/blogs/bitpix-google-logo2/bitpix-google-logo2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'F.T.C. Fines Google $22.5 Million for Safari Privacy Violations', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Google, Accused of Skirting Privacy Provision, Is to Pay $22.5 Million to Settle Charges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T17:03:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88359eda-8b17-527d-93ee-111cb9c4ae1a', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88359eda-8b17-527d-93ee-111cb9c4ae1a'}, {'abstract': 'The new FX drama “The Americans” will star Keri Russell and Matthew Rhys as a suburban Washington couple who are secretly KGB spies.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/fx-orders-cold-war-spy-drama-the-americans/', 'snippet': 'The new FX drama “The Americans” will star Keri Russell and Matthew Rhys as a suburban Washington couple who are secretly KGB spies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 1980s were a time of Reaganomics, Rubik’s Cubes and the possibility that your seemingly straitlaced neighbors were actually undercover Soviet spies. That’s the premise of the new television drama “The Americans,” which will star Keri Russell, Matthew Rhys and Noah Emmerich, and which FX said on Thursday it had ordered\xa0 for next year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'FX Orders Cold War Spy Drama ‘The Americans’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cold War Era', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emmerich, Noah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rhys, Matthew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Russell, Keri', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'KGB', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T17:04:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb381595-0bdd-5fc0-abfb-bb0c8579cbfd', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb381595-0bdd-5fc0-abfb-bb0c8579cbfd'}, {'abstract': 'A summer day in one Brooklyn neighborhood. Part-time classes, short-term jobs, handball and the Olympics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/08/09/summer-snapshot-from-sunset-park/', 'snippet': 'A summer day in one Brooklyn neighborhood. Part-time classes, short-term jobs, handball and the Olympics.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Snapshot From Sunset Park', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T17:10:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By HITEN SAMTANI', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiten', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SAMTANI', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8616dafc-302a-57cf-bece-269ee394a343', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8616dafc-302a-57cf-bece-269ee394a343'}, {'abstract': 'Haley Anderson of the United States overtook two swimmers in the final 1,000 meters of the 6.2-mile open-water race, which lasted nearly two hours and in which four seconds separated the top four finishers.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/haley-anderson-wins-silver-in-10k-swim/', 'snippet': 'Haley Anderson of the United States overtook two swimmers in the final 1,000 meters of the 6.2-mile open-water race, which lasted nearly two hours and in which four seconds separated the top four finishers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Call Haley Anderson the Flying Fish. Her range in the water calls to mind the versatility of Paavo Nurmi on the track, where in the 1920s he earned the nickname the Flying Finn on his way to Olympic victories in distances ranging from 1,500 to 10,000 meters. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Haley Anderson Wins Silver in 10K Swim', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, Haley', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T17:11:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifi