eaders in Colorado and Iowa, both election battlegrounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PUEBLO, Colo. – Speaking not far from a wind turbine manufacturing plant here on the hot plains, President Obama on Thursday contrasted his support for keeping alive an expiring tax credit for wind energy producers with the opposition of Mitt Romney to that subsidy and others for clean energy alternatives to oil.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Draws Contrast With Romney on Wind Energy Tax Credit', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T17:50:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c3a260c-11eb-558d-8079-45ce3a78470c', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c3a260c-11eb-558d-8079-45ce3a78470c'}, {'abstract': 'A disappointing exit from the Olympics by the men’s team after its semifinal loss to Mexico on Tuesday meant Japan’s women carried the hopes of the nation.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/japanese-soccer-fans-prepare-for-womens-gold-medal-game/', 'snippet': 'A disappointing exit from the Olympics by the men’s team after its semifinal loss to Mexico on Tuesday meant Japan’s women carried the hopes of the nation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Soccer fans were napping to prepare for what the local news media were calling the battle of the century, the women’s Olympic gold medal match Thursday between Japan and the United States, which was scheduled to kick off at a ghastly 3:45 a.m. here. “It’s national sleepiness day!” says Miki, who tweets at @Mikilin999.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tokyo Rises Early for Women’s Gold Medal Game', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T17:52:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/106b7d57-0b9b-5d60-a0ca-2de28617cb43', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/106b7d57-0b9b-5d60-a0ca-2de28617cb43'}, {'abstract': 'There were no conclusions or declarations by the 30 participating nations, including Russia and China, according to diplomats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/world/middleeast/iran-hosts-its-own-meetings-on-syria-conflict.html', 'snippet': 'There were no conclusions or declarations by the 30 participating nations, including Russia and China, according to diplomats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Shut out of diplomatic meetings on the Syria conflict, Iran convened emergency consultations of its own on Thursday, with participants from nearly 30 countries, including Russia and China, discussing ways to reach a solution. It was the first such gathering since the special representative Kofi Annan resigned as a United Nati