 success.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/how-to-make-your-lost-phone-findable/', 'snippet': 'There are apps that help you find your lost phone. They may not work perfectly, but using them increases the odds of success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, I lost my iPhone on a train. I used Apple’s Find My iPhone feature to track it to a house in suburban Maryland, and the local police were able to return it to me. Because I’d tweeted about these developments, the quest for the phone became, much to my surprise, an Internet-wide, minute-by-minute real-life thriller. (You can read the whole story here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Make Your Lost Phone Findable', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T18:23:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3dc3998-51b1-5701-932d-3e1280ccba79', 'word_count': 980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3dc3998-51b1-5701-932d-3e1280ccba79'}, {'abstract': 'By selecting David Walker, a former top official at the Bank of England, Barclays is seeking to draw a line under the interest rate manipulation scandal, which has raised questions about the governance and the culture at the Bri