uri': 'nyt://article/6be50a04-ba5c-536c-ae8b-e86b36d5ac94'}, {'abstract': 'Luis Rios went for a run in Prospect Park one morning in 1977, and he never really stopped.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/after-a-jog-35-years-ago-hes-still-running-in-circles/', 'snippet': 'Luis Rios went for a run in Prospect Park one morning in 1977, and he never really stopped.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At 11 a.m. on Sunday two things will happen: in London, around 100 of the world’s fastest men will launch themselves onto the 26.2-mile Olympic marathon course, dashing from Buckingham Palace to the Tower of London in front of hundreds of thousands of excited spectators. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Jog 35 Years Ago, He’s Still Running in Circles', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After 35 Years of Running in Circles, No Sign of Straying', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marathon Running', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prospect Park (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T19:23:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9de20b8-b211-5836-8cca-3fb1dd1df259', 'word_count': 936, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9de20b8-b211-5836-8cca-3fb1dd1df259'}, {'abstract': 'N.Y. See: Working under an impromptu parasol on the dome of a new transit and retail hub.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/broadway-and-fulton-street-1218-p-m/', 'snippet': 'N.Y. See: Worki