riginal': 'By Mosi Secret', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mosi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Secret', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36336a12-82c5-5e71-a195-a05e7ea71b52', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36336a12-82c5-5e71-a195-a05e7ea71b52'}, {'abstract': 'Generic creams routinely prescribed by doctors have been undergoing rapid price increases, an example of the murky and often illogical world of drug pricing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/business/prescription-skin-creams-jump-in-price.html', 'snippet': 'Generic creams routinely prescribed by doctors have been undergoing rapid price increases, an example of the murky and often illogical world of drug pricing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They are the staples of most dermatology practices: generic creams and ointments that treat everything from skin rashes to athlete’s foot to scabies. Many doctors prescribe the drugs without a second thought. But increasingly, some dermatologists say, patients are complaining about a recent, mysterious and rapid rise in price.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/business/10dermatology-pic/10dermatology-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 557, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/business/10dermatology-pic/10dermatology-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1113, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Soaring Ointment Prices Are a Dermatologic Mystery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Generic, but Not Cheap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keyw