ika Rudelius’s “Rituals of Capitalism,” a video at Leo Koenig, shows young adults in moments of self-consciousness and vulnerability that are less personal than they are symptomatic of larger cultural growing pains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leo Koenig 541 and 545 West 23rd Street, Chelsea', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Julika Rudelius: ‘Rituals of Capitalism’', 'kicker': 'Art In Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Julika Rudelius: ‘Rituals of Capitalism’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T20:27:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb214b38-7174-5148-9701-2ff0c2c00479', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb214b38-7174-5148-9701-2ff0c2c00479'}, {'abstract': 'On our reading list: Shinji Turner-Yamamoto’s “Global Tree Project,” Davy Rothbart’s “My Heart Is an Idiot” and Judith Clark’s “Handbags.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/bookshelf-22/', 'snippet': 'On our reading list: Shinji Turner-Yamamoto’s “Global Tree Project,” Davy Rothbart’s “My Heart Is an Idiot” and Judith Clark’s “Handbags.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Global Tree Project” (Damiani, $40) shows off Shinji Turner-Yamamoto’s enchanting site-specific installations, including the birch trees he suspended in the nave of an abandoned 19th-century chapel in Cincinnati. Davy Rothbart falls in love instantly, often with the wrong people, which explains the title of his achingly funny essay collection: “My Heart Is an Idiot” (Farrar, Straus and Giroux, $25). From a 300-year-old silk Limoges bridal purse to a Céline tote, Judith Clark’s “Handbags” (Yale University Press, $50) assembles standout pieces from the Simone Handbag Museum, which opened last month in Seoul, South Korea. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bookshelf', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Judith', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T20:28:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dadaa9a-5708-5bfc-9966-81894c3b9fb3', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dadaa9a-5708-5bfc-9966-81894c3b9fb3'}, {'abstract': '“Tête-à-Tête,” at Yancey Richardson Gallery, was organized by Mickalene Thomas and focuses on portraiture, a genre that bridges both African and American photography.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/arts/design/tete-a-tete.html', 'snippet': '“Tête-à-Tête,” at Yancey Richardson Gallery, was organized by Mickalene Thomas and focuses on portraiture, a genre that bridges both African and American photography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yancey Richardson Gallery ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘TêTE-à-TêTE’', 'kicker': 'Art In Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Tête-à-Tête’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T20:28:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d562a84-d27c-515c-a2df-8c9d1f63eb76', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d562a84-d27c-515c-a2df-8c9d1f63eb76'}, {'abstract': 'Everything around and within me is partly because of his fatherly advice, his example and even the fact that he could get impatient and stubborn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/fashion/sad-news-like-a-warm-hug-goodbye.html', 'snippet': 'Everything around and within me is partly because of his fatherly advice, his example and even the fact that he could get impatient and stubborn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN friends and colleagues heard that my father had died in an unexpected drowning — on Father’s Day, no less — they couldn’t believe I was at work the next day, that I went swimming in the morning, that I was not at home weeping.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/fashion/12MODERNLOVE/12MODERNLOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 622, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/fashion/12MODERNLOVE/12MODERNLOVE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1244, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/fashion/12MODERNLOVE/12MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/fashion/12MODERNLOVE/12MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/fashion/12MODERNLOVE/12MODERNLOVE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sad News Like a Warm Hug Goodbye', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sad News Like a Warm Hug Goodbye', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T20:29:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lucy Schulte Danziger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lucy', 'middlename': 'Schulte', 'lastname': 'Danziger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c65a9760-2468-5e2b-bf38-26ca9060373f', 'word_count': 1525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c65a9760-2468-5e2b-bf38-26ca9060373f'}, {'abstract': 'A global food price index jumped 6 percent in July, with the drought afflicting grain crops in the United States the leading factor.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/another-jolt-to-global-food-prices/', 'snippet': 'A global food price index jumped 6 percent in July, with the drought afflicting grain crops in the United States the leading factor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For anyone doubting the importance of American agriculture to world markets, the latest price report from the United Nations Food and Agriculture Organization will be revealing. The agency reported on Thursday that its food price index jumped by 6 percent in July. That was largely because of rising grain prices, with the drought in the United States and its expected impact on the corn harvest being the biggest factor. The cereals component of the index jumped 17 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Jolt to Global Food Prices', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T20:31:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3be152e-c887-5f89-8876-4c427b35df5f', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3be152e-c887-5f89-8876-4c427b35df5f'}, {'abstract': 'At the Broadway Dance Center in Manhattan, students learn grooving and popping and other hip-hop moves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/arts/dance/hip-hop-lessons-at-broadway-dance-center.html', 'snippet': 'At the Broadway Dance Center in Manhattan, students learn grooving and popping and other hip-hop moves.', 'lead_paragraph': '“IT’S not about the move, it’s the groove,” Val Ho, a k a Ms. Vee, said to her hip-hop class at the Broadway Dance Center in Manhattan. I tried to take this advice to heart as I warmed up alongside nine fellow students on a recent afternoon. Most of them were women in their 20s with dance backgrounds and perfect posture. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10URBAN1_SPAN/10URBAN1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10URBAN1_SPAN/10URBAN1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10URBAN1_SPAN/10URBAN1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10URBAN1_SPAN/10URBAN1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10URBAN1_SPAN/10URBAN1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10URBAN1_SPAN/10URBAN1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10URBAN1_SPAN/10URBAN1