, 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/748ffeee-9f5e-548d-bc6a-b262d619b1e7'}, {'abstract': 'Three parts of a 14th-century altarpiece are reunited for the first time in 200 years in “The Adoration of the Magi by Bartolo di Fredi,” at the Museum of Biblical Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/arts/design/the-adoration-of-the-magi-at-museum-of-biblical-art.html', 'snippet': 'Three parts of a 14th-century altarpiece are reunited for the first time in 200 years in “The Adoration of the Magi by Bartolo di Fredi,” at the Museum of Biblical Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The baby’s feet must smell sweet to the rapt old king who kneels and cups them to his face like flowers. One of three sages and seekers, he’s come a long way to find this child, who sits upright, grave and alert, on his mother’s lap, though he’s only 2 weeks old.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10MAGI2/10MAGI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 224, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10MAGI2/10MAGI2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 224}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10MAGI2/10MAGI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10MAGI2/10MAGI2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10MAGI2/10MAGI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10MAGI2/10MAGI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10MAGI2/10MAGI2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 149, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Come Let Us Adore Him', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Come Let Us Adore Him', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reviews', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Biblical Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T21:25:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/59140512-3b32-5556-990a-82c2ec1e19e4', 'word_count': 1306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59140512-3b32-5556-990a-82c2ec1e19e4'}, {'abstract': 'Can’t afford Sancerre’s prices? Four of its neighbors — Pouilly-Fumé, Menetou-Salon, Quincy and Reuilly — also do wonderful things with the sauvignon blanc grape.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/dining/reviews/in-the-orbit-of-sancerre-wines-of-the-times.html', 'snippet': 'Can’t afford Sancerre’s prices? Four of its neighbors — Pouilly-Fumé, Menetou-Salon, Quincy and Reuilly — also do wonderful things with the sauvignon blanc grape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVERYBODY knows Sancerre. That’s a problem among some in the wine avant-garde, for whom familiarity breeds contempt. I have heard Sancerre sneered at as a sort of comfort food, signaling timidity in a cliquish world that sizes up personality and status by choice of beverage. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/dining/15WINE_SPAN/15WINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/15/dining/15WINE_SPAN/15WINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/dining/15WINE_SPAN/15WINE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/dining/15WINE_SPAN/15WINE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/dining/15WINE_SPAN/15WINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/15/dining/15WINE_SPAN/15WINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Orbit of Sancerre', 'kicker': 'Wines of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Orbit of Sancerre', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T21:26:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Dining & Wine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ea5556b-6ef7-5251-9e10-76a817ecefb4', 'word_count': 1086, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ea5556b-6ef7-5251-9e10-76a817ecefb4'}, {'abstract': 'Plaintiffs say that wolves will get the upper hand and maul hunting dogs unless the rules are tightened.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/wisconsin-sued-over-rules-on-dogs-in-wolf-hunts/', 'snippet': 'Plaintiffs say that wolves will get the upper hand and maul hunting dogs unless the rules are tightened.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The wildlife agency in Wisconsin, the only state that allows people to use dogs while hunting wolves, faces a lawsuit contending that it is permitting state-sanctioned animal fighting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wisconsin Is Sued Over Dogs in Wolf Hunts', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunting and Trapping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wolves', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Advocates', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T21:28:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adeshina Emmanuel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adeshina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Emmanuel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ca6847c-7d86-5efa-9a10-1766662b1ba7', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ca6847c-7d86-5efa-9a10-1766662b1ba7'}, {'abstract': 'The family band Haim shares its favorite songs, old and new, of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/sisters-of-summer-haim/', 'snippet': 'The family band Haim shares its favorite songs, old and new, of the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Los Angeles sisters Alana, Este and Danielle Haim, of the girl group Haim, started their musical careers in a band with their parents. “We did covers of KEarth 101 songs, bands like the Eagles, Billy Joel and Santana,” explains Danielle, 23, the middle sister. It wasn’t until years later — Aug. 7, 2007, to be exact — that Danielle, her younger sister, Alana, now 20, and her older sister, Este, now 26, played their first show sans their parents. After taking a break to finish high school (Alana), finish college (Este) and tour with Jenny Lewis and Julian Casablancas (Danielle), the girls of Haim are now releasing demos, and their summer anthem “Forever” landed them on tour with Mumford & Sons. Here are Haim’s picks for their favorite jams of the season:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sisters of Summer | Haim', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T21:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Moonves', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moonves', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36c60eaa-6d08-584b-935b-fc5845ff66fc', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36c60eaa-6d08-584b-935b-fc5845ff66fc'}, {'abstract': 'The pianist Garrick Ohlsson was the soloist in Wednesday night’s performance at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/arts/music/garrick-ohlsson-at-mostly-mozart-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The pianist Garrick Ohlsson was the soloist in Wednesday night’s performance at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There seem to be odd little pockets of convergence in the musical cosmos. One involves the pianist Garrick Ohlsson, the composer Luciano Berio and Beethoven’s “Emperor” Concerto. The last time I heard Mr. Ohlsson play the “Emperor” was with the Philadelphia Orchestra in 1993, in a program with “Epiphanies,” a major work by Berio: a concert that because of a cancellation ended up also being conducted by Berio.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10MOSTLY_SPAN/10MOSTLY_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10MOSTLY_SPAN/10MOSTLY_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10MOSTLY_SPAN/0810MOSTLY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10MOSTLY_SPAN/0810MOSTLY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10MOSTLY_SPAN/10MOSTLY_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Varied, Colorful Elements, United in Performance', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Varied, Colorful Elements, United in Performance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reviews', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mostly Mozart Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ohlsson, Garrick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T21:31:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a7332fa-b875-5dad-bffd-910509dc865e', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a7332fa-b875-5dad-bffd-910509dc865e'}, {'abstract': 'Willem van Aelst’s still lifes, while manifestly objects of extraordinary artifice, are experienced as uncannily present, as if they were hallucinated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/arts/design/willem-van-aelst-still-life-paintings-at-national-gallery.html', 'snippet': 'Willem van Aelst’s still lifes, while manifestly objects of extraordinary artifice, are experienced as uncannily present, as if they were hallucinated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Still-life painting bloomed as never before in the Netherlands in the 17th century, and among its most vibrant and coveted blossoms were those of Willem van Aelst (1627-83). He is the subject of “Elegance and Refinement: The Still-Life Paintings of Willem van Aelst,” a small, intense exhibition of 28 paintings at the National Gallery of Art here. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multi