d933169de7', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/087d2498-bf59-5e4f-b38b-d1d933169de7'}, {'abstract': 'Under the health care law, insurers must issue refunds if less than 85 percent of premiums pay for care. But people on employer plans may have to wait for the cash, if they see it at all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/nyregion/health-insurance-refunds-may-stall-in-employers-hands.html', 'snippet': 'Under the health care law, insurers must issue refunds if less than 85 percent of premiums pay for care. But people on employer plans may have to wait for the cash, if they see it at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the great health insurance giveback: $1.1 billion in premiums returned to policyholders under the Affordable Care Act. But while many people who buy their own insurance found a check in the mail last week, millions insured through employers are still wondering what is happening with the money. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/nyregion/Y-REBATE/Y-REBATE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/nyregion/Y-REBATE/Y-REBATE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Insurer Refunds May Stall in Employers’ Hands', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Delay in Insurance Refund May Lie With Employers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rebates and Refunds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-09T23:51:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nina Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3042c5f-516a-583f-a6e6-a0ba18da0d37', 'word_count': 1243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3042c5f-516a-583f-a6e6-a0ba18da0d37'}, {'abstract': 'Marikina is famed for its cobblers, but after severe storms struck the Philippines last month, it has become famous for its flooding.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/world/asia/city-in-philippines-known-for-shoes-is-up-to-its-knees-in-water.html', 'snippet': 'Marikina is famed for its cobblers, but after severe storms struck the Philippines last month, it has become famous for its flooding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MARIKINA, the Philippines — Marikina is famed for its cobblers, whose handmade shoes are a source of local pride. Its Shoe Museum is home to a pair of shoes from each president of the Philippines, including 800 of the more than 3,000 pairs in the collection of Imelda R. Marcos. A barge in the Marikina River sports statues of two giant shoes, and what the city fathers claim is the world’s largest functional shoe — more than 15 feet long — is on display in a local mall.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/world/MANILA-1/MANILA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/10/world/MANI