tage, background and interviews, tells the story of Leo Zisman, an 81-year-old survivor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/movies/the-lion-of-judah-holocaust-documentary.html', 'snippet': '“The Lion of Judah,” a Holocaust documentary with travel footage, background and interviews, tells the story of Leo Zisman, an 81-year-old survivor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barely 60 minutes long, the Holocaust documentary “The Lion of Judah” feels less like a feature film than a well-executed school project pulling together certain required elements: travel footage, reaction interviews, archival background and licks of music. The director Matt Mindell divides time between reporting on his tour of the Warsaw Ghetto and camps (Majdanek, Auschwitz, Terezin) with a group, and ceding the stage to an 81-year-old survivor, Leo Zisman, who recounts to visitors his experiences facing down Nazis.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10RDP_LIONSPAN/0810LION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10RDP_LIONSPAN/0810LION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 309}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10RDP_LIONSPAN/0810LION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 528, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10RDP_LIONSPAN/0810LION-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1055, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/arts/10RDP_LIONSPAN/0810LION-thumbStand