joy under federal labor law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rights for Domestic Workers', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rights for Domestic Workers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T01:08:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/700c9a0a-3a7e-5855-b5c7-e4585910ca2d', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/700c9a0a-3a7e-5855-b5c7-e4585910ca2d'}, {'abstract': 'Nine New Yorkers recounted their frustrations with the city, with a small-business owner saying his bill jumped to $10,000 from $1,000.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/nyregion/at-hearing-customers-complain-of-unfair-and-inaccurate-water-bills.html', 'snippet': 'Nine New Yorkers recounted their frustrations with the city, with a small-business owner saying his bill jumped to $10,000 from $1,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A woman from Queens said her quarterly water bill jumped by more than $500. A small-business owner said his bill for the quarter rose to $10,000 from about $1,000.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/nyregion/WATER/WATER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 