e, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6453a85f-1196-5e49-9e5a-c7d9efcb84ca', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6453a85f-1196-5e49-9e5a-c7d9efcb84ca'}, {'abstract': 'The rowdy politics of 19th-century America offer a hint about where we’re headed now.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/09/riling-up-the-shrewd-wild-boys/', 'snippet': 'The rowdy politics of 19th-century America offer a hint about where we’re headed now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today we would consider Edmund Keyser, who kept a saloon in Philadelphia during the 1860s, a compulsive gambler. But at the time he was known as a “sporting man.” Keyser enjoyed all of the era’s brutal entertainments. He bet on bare-knuckle boxing. He bet on rat-baiting. He played the horses. And come October of each election year, he would scrawl “busy canvassing” in his meticulous wager book and entertain himself hustling for the Democratic Party.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Riling Up the ‘Shrewd, Wild Boys’', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T01:12:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Grinspan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grinspan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c14f2d5-2b26-5c0b-a86d-85909f565058', 'word_count': 1887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c14f2d5-2b26-5c0b-a86d-85909f565058'}, {'abstract': 'A deal on oil pipeline fees is a good step and should be implemented quickly, but the countries face many other volatile issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/opinion/sudan-and-south-sudan-make-progress.html', 'snippet': 'A deal on oil pipeline fees is a good step and should be implemented quickly, but the countries face many other volatile issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sudan and South Sudan ended a dangerous stalemate when they finally reached an agreement on oil pipeline fees last week. The elements of the deal should be carried out as quickly as possible given the severe financial stress on both nations. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sudan and South Sudan Make Progress', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sudan and South Sudan Make Progress', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T01:16:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4916c53f-d643-500f-a206-7b29de943b03', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4916c53f-d643-500f-a206-7b29de943b03'}, {'abstract': 'A government lawsuit against a background check company is a good start and puts the industry on notice. But a growing trade needs even closer scrutiny.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/opinion/accuracy-in-criminal-background-checks.html', 'snippet': 'A government lawsuit against a background check company is a good start and puts the industry on notice. But a growing trade needs even closer scrutiny.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For far too long, the federal government has neglected its responsibility for regulating the companies that provide criminal background checks used by 9 in 10 companies to screen job applicants. The damage done to job seekers by flawed and unreliable data — a common problem with such services — can be devastating. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accuracy in Criminal Background Checks', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Accuracy in Criminal Background Checks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HireRight Solutions Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Trade Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Scores', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T01:19:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/04627ebd-93ec-541b-aa9e-bd44b1bfa867', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04627ebd-93ec-541b-aa9e-bd44b1bfa867'}, {'abstract': 'The series on typography concludes with an account of John