dropped a provision that asserted an exclusive license to users’ posts, Adam Yauch’s will, and the Mars rover has nearly a million Twitter followers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The online classified site Craigslist dropped a provision that asserted an exclusive license to users’ posts just two weeks after implementing it, CNET reported. The effort was intended to fend off third parties trying to repurpose the site’s listings, but a sympathetic note from the Electronic Frontier Foundation explained that after meeting with Craigslist, the company agreed to change its policy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Craiglist Relents on Owning Posts, and a Chatty Mars Rover', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T13:05:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dca2a093-b6b7-50c0-85c6-f58081111096', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dca2a093-b6b7-50c0-85c6-f58081111096'}, {'abstract': 'Live blogging Friday’s action at the Olympics, including swimming, track and field, and taekwondo.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/london-live-follow-fridays-action-at-the-olympics/', 'snippet': 'Live blogging Friday’s action at the Olympics, including swimming, track and field, and taekwondo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent Olympics, the United States 4×100 meter relay teams have struggled just to pass the baton all the way around the track, but this time, the women’s team put together the dream race: clean passes and a world record time.', 'source'