(NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T13:14:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Pedersen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pedersen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01576051-50b6-54a8-824d-7ab8d29d2ad4', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01576051-50b6-54a8-824d-7ab8d29d2ad4'}, {'abstract': 'The TimesTalks series hosted a panel discussion with several of the young American breakout stars of the 2012 Games today in London. Juliet Macur of The Times served as moderator.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/timestalks-faces-of-the-2012-summer-games/', 'snippet': 'The TimesTalks series hosted a panel discussion with several of the young American breakout stars of the 2012 Games today in London. Juliet Macur of The Times served as moderator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As some veterans exit the Olympic scene, several young American athletes have the future of their sports in their hands. The TimesTalks series hosted a panel discussion with several of those new stars on Friday in London. Scheduled to attend were the gymnast Aly Raisman, beach volleyball’s Jen Kessy and April Ross, and the swimmers Conor Dwyer and Nathan Adrian. Juliet Macur of The Times moderated.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesTalks: Faces of the 2012 Summer Games', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adrian, Nathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raisman, Aly', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ross, April', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T13:18:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e929b4d-5287-5623-b2a1-3411f94673b4', 'word_count': 66, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e929b4d-5287-5623-b2a1-3411f94673b4'}, {'abstract': 'During the three-day convention in Charlotte, N.C., Democrats will focus on the choice for middle-class voters in November by using “real people” to highlight the differences between Barack Obama and Mitt Romney, according to a news report Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/memo-outlines-democrats-convention-plans/', 'snippet': 'During the three-day convention in Charlotte, N.C., Democrats will focus on the choice for middle-class voters in November by using “real people” to highlight the differences between Barack Obama and Mitt Romney, according to a news report Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Democrats will use the three-day Democratic National Convention next month to contrast President Obama with a portrayal of Mitt Romney as someone who would “devastate the American middle class,” according to a news report Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Memo Outlines Democrats’ Convention Plans', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charlotte (NC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T13:27:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db024731-c501-536b-973b-adfd4c177db7', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db024731-c501-536b-973b-adfd4c177db7'}, {'abstract': 'Tax rates for the wealthiest are lower than they used to be and many of them pay less than 15 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/08/10/business/the-wealthiest-400-taxpayers.html', 'snippet': 'Tax rates for the wealthiest are lower than they used to be and many of them pay less than 15 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tax rates for the wealthiest are lower than they used to be and many of them pay less than 15 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Top 400: Lower Taxes and More Capital Gains and Dividends', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T13:27:29+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/92b33e19-24bd-5aa3-bf37-87505a218b44', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/92b33e19-24bd-5aa3-bf37-87505a218b44'}, {'abstract': 'Based on experts’ analysis of data on the wealthiest taxpayers, Mitt Romney has almost certainly been paying income taxes, but perhaps at a very low rate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/business/in-the-superrich-clues-to-romneys-tax-returns-common-sense.html', 'snippet': 'Based on experts’ analysis of data on the wealthiest taxpayers, Mitt Romney has almost certainly been paying income taxes, but perhaps at a very low rate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the face of it, Senator Harry Reid’s explosive but flimsily sourced claim that Mitt Romney paid no income tax seems preposterous. Mr. Romney has denied it, and without his returns no one can say for sure. But for someone who makes millions of dollars a year, would it even be possible?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption'