, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1479, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Laid Off More Than Once, and Seeking a Career', 'kicker': 'Shortcuts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Laid Off More Than Once, And Seeking a Career', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T14:55:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alina Tugend', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tugend', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33ced0fd-e5cc-55d7-a02a-13e81a1d99f4', 'word_count': 1276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33ced0fd-e5cc-55d7-a02a-13e81a1d99f4'}, {'abstract': 'Dealing with some antsy kids? One solution is quality children’s apps. Not only are they perfect for rainy day fun, but they can extend your school’s curriculum into the vacation.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/childrens-apps-that-inject-a-little-learning-into-vacation/', 'snippet': 'Dealing with some antsy kids? One solution is quality children’s apps. Not only are they perfect for rainy day fun, but they can extend your school’s curriculum into the vacation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dealing with some antsy kids? One solution is quality children’s apps. Not only are they perfect for rainy day fun, but they can extend your school’s curriculum into the vacation, a point you might not want to mention to your child. They are listed here by age, from young to old.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Children’s Apps That Inject a Little Learning Into Vacation', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T15:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Warren Buckleitner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Warren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckleitner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a654589-3c35-509d-ba3d-6ca530f6102d', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a654589-3c35-509d-ba3d-6ca530f6102d'}, {'abstract': 'The British classic, as reimagined by Katie Hillier.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/the-get-aspreys-wiltshire-clutch/', 'snippet': 'The British classic, as reimagined by Katie Hillier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The London designer Katie Hillier virtually eats, breathes and sleeps accessories working at the helm of her fine jewelry line, Hillier, and as a consultant for Marc by Marc Jacobs and Victoria Beckham. Most recently she’s designed a 10-piece collection of handbags in collaboration with the British heritage brand Asprey (prices starting at $1,200). “I didn’t want to reinvent the wheel,” says Hillier, who studied up on Asprey classics like the Belgravia Darcy bag and the Mayfair clutch before putting pen to paper on the designs. “There are so many wonderful Asprey bags that are just perfect as they are,” she explains. So instead of updating or reinterpreting those, Hillier turned to archival gentlemen’s document holders for inspiration. Warm, sybaritic shades of sapphire, hazel and shiny licorice make the bags feel especially luxurious and modern. “For the palette I was very inspired by a walk through the woods in autumn,” Hillier says. A standout: this accordion clutch in bramble crocodile, part of the Wiltshire group that also features shoulder bags in skins like ostrich and python.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Asprey’s Wiltshire Clutch', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T15:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd712576-7db1-5aab-8d37-6f0b2274fdcc', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd712576-7db1-5aab-8d37-6f0b2274fdcc'}, {'abstract': 'Mourners from all over the world traveled to Oak Creek, Wisc. to pay tribute to the six people killed in the Sikh Temple of Wisconsin on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/memorial-service-for-victims-of-the-sikh-temple-shooting/', 'snippet': 'Mourners from all over the world traveled to Oak Creek, Wisc. to pay tribute to the six people killed in the Sikh Temple of Wisconsin on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, 7:53 p.m. Thousands of mourners from around the world crowded into a gymnasium at Oak Creek High School in Oak Creek, Wis. to attend a wake and a memorial service for the six worshipers who were shot and killed on Sunday at the Sikh Temple of Wisconsin in suburban Milwaukee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Memorial Service for Victims of the Sikh Temple Shooting', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oak Creek, Wis, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sikhs and Sikhism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T15:06:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Yaccino and Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/034cf5c7-9dcc-52c1-b28e-cd1dbd3824ca', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/034cf5c7-9dcc-52c1-b28e-cd1dbd3824ca'}, {'abstract': 'Gu Kailai, the wife of an ambitious Chinese leader, plotted to protect her son from demands for money by the Briton she is accused of killing, according to reports of the prosecutors’ case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/world/asia/blackmail-emerges-as-gu-kailai-motive-for-heywood-killing-in-china.html', 'snippet': 'Gu Kailai, the wife of an ambitious Chinese leader, plotted to protect her son from demands for money by the Briton she is accused of killing, according to reports of the prosecutors’ case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Gu Kailai, the wife of one of China’s most ambitious leaders, plotted with allies, including the local police chief, to protect her son from what she saw as the blackmail demands of the British business associate she confessed in court to killing, according to accounts of the trial that emerged on Friday, including one from the state-run Xinhua news agency. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/world/asia/10china-videothumb/10china-videothumb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/world/asia/10china-videothumb/10china-videothumb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1528, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/world/asia/10china-videothumb/10china-videothumb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/10/world/asia/10china-videothumb/10china-videothumb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/world/asia/10china-videothumb/10china-videothumb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blackmail Cited as Motive in a Killing That Shook China', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Murder Case Weaves Blackmail and a Mother’s Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heywood, Neil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'valu