ument_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/147e7905-1525-5ef5-8343-c11a857de080', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/147e7905-1525-5ef5-8343-c11a857de080'}, {'abstract': 'To mark World Elephant Day, an environmental group fills in some gaps in information about the slaughter of some 300 elephants in Cameroon early this year.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/mourning-the-elephants/', 'snippet': 'To mark World Elephant Day, an environmental group fills in some gaps in information about the slaughter of some 300 elephants in Cameroon early this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In March I wrote about the coordinated slaughter of elephants early this year by poachers in Cameroon. The scale of the killings is hard to absorb: well over 300 are thought to have been killed within the span of a few months, wiping out a significant portion of the country’s elephant population.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mourning the Elephants', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elephants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ivory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poaching (Wildlife)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smuggling', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cameroon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T15:17:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'su