Krishna, celebrated in Bhopal, Madhya Pradesh.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: August 10', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T15:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e1eb07c-c68d-511a-ac6e-c8163dea0c58', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e1eb07c-c68d-511a-ac6e-c8163dea0c58'}, {'abstract': 'A piece of the hearth before which Edgar Allan Poe composed his most celebrated poem languished in obscurity at Columbia University for a century.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/mystery-of-a-poe-relic-the-raven-mantels-curious-journey/', 'snippet': 'A piece of the hearth before which Edgar Allan Poe composed his most celebrated poem languished in obscurity at Columbia University for a century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One hundred and sixty-eight bleak Decembers ago or thereabouts, Edgar Allan Poe sat before a fireplace in a farmhouse on a high bluff on what would someday be called the Upper West Side, composing a poem. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/nyregion/cityroom-poe3/cityroom-poe3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 829, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/nyregion/cityroom-poe3/cityroom-poe3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1659, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype