e23-beef5595f0c9'}, {'abstract': 'The necessary steps to fix a financial crisis in the United States were painful and unpopular, according to the writer, who was the head of the Obama administration’s financial crisis response team. But in Europe, the consequences of a delayed or inadequate response are far worse.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/swift-rescue-in-u-s-provides-lessons-for-europe/', 'snippet': 'The necessary steps to fix a financial crisis in the United States were painful and unpopular, according to the writer, who was the head of the Obama administration’s financial crisis response team. But in Europe, the consequences of a delayed or ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lee Sachs, chief executive of Alliance Partners, is former counselor to the secretary of the Treasury and was head of the financial crisis response team in the Obama administration. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Swift Rescue in U.S. Provides Lessons for Europe', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T15:36:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lee Sachs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sachs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fec242e3-e44e-5ae3-965d-7a9e71222841', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fec242e3-e44e-5ae3-965d-7a9e71222841'}, {'abstract': 'Spain defeated Russia on Thursday, 67-59, to advance to the gold medal game at the London Olympics..', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/live-coverage-of-spain-russia-basketball-semifinal/', 'snippet': 'Spain defeated Russia on Thursday, 67-59, to advance to the gold medal game at the London Olympics..', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time around, Spain’s men’s basketball team didn’t take Russia as seriously as it should have in the London Olympics. Russia won, 77-74, in group play.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live: Spain Defeats Russia to Advance to Basketball Final', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gasol, Pau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T15:41:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/764083e4-a7a1-5753-9b7f-01ebd6021322', 'word_count': 1427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/764083e4-a7a1-5753-9b7f-01ebd6021322'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Rakoff, a humorist and essayist, was known for his incisive wit and keen eye for the preposterous.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/books/david-rakoff-award-winning-humorist-dies-at-47.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Rakoff, a humorist and essayist, was known for his incisive wit and keen eye for the preposterous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Rakoff, a prizewinning humorist whose mordant, neurotic essays examined everything from his surreal stint portraying Sigmund Freud in a Christmastime shop window display to his all-too-real battles with cancer, died on Thursday in Manhattan. He was 47.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/RAKOFF-obit/RAKOFF-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/RAKOFF-obit/RAKOFF-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/RAKOFF-obit/RAKOFF-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/RAKOFF-obit/RAKOFF-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/RAKOFF-obit/RAKOFF-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'David Rakoff, 47, Comic Essayist, Dies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'David Rakoff, 47, Comic Essayist, Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rakoff, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T15:41:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/85950692-5c84-5f1d-85ff-9345cda6db5c', 'word_count': 921, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85950692-5c84-5f1d-85ff-9345cda6db5c'}, {'abstract': 'Many of us have “our” summer spot. What makes yours special? Does it restore a sense of balance, or renew your sense of priorities? For me, it’s ours Russian dacha.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/how-to-tune-out-the-euro-crisis/', 'snippet': 'Many of us have “our” summer spot. What makes yours special? Does it restore a sense of balance, or renew your sense of priorities? For me, it’s ours Russian dacha.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each year, I retire to our Russian dacha for as many days as we can manage, to savor the quiet, soak up the sun and the simpler life, albeit one complicated by a lack of running water, occasional power outages and a wide variety of insects ready to inflict irritation. As I write in my latest column, the dacha is much more than a place; it is a mindset, and a keepstone, “our” spot on this Earth where very little changes each year, where the constancy of Russia bats back its equally eternal uncertainties. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Tune Out the Euro Crisis', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T15:42:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7a3379f-0807-5eb1-b51b-89d05d2daeda', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7a3379f-0807-5eb1-b51b-89d05d2daeda'}, {'abstract': 'In Marie NDiaye’s novel, women draw on reserves of love, common sense and even self-mockery to counteract the damage being done to them by narcissistic family members.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/books/review/three-strong-women-by-marie-ndiaye.html', 'snippet': 'In Marie NDiaye’s novel, women draw on reserves of love, common sense and even self-mockery to counteract the damage being done to them by narcissistic family members.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans have a curiously limited vision of France. We may be wild about Chanel sunglasses, Vuitton handbags, Champagne or Paris in the spring, but when it comes to the kinds of contemporary French culture that can’t be bought in a duty-free shop, most of us draw a blank. Luckily, this veil of benign ignorance is being lifted as publishers in the United States introduce American readers to a new generation of hugely gifted French writers who are reworking the boundaries of fiction, memoir and history (Emmanuel Carrère, Laurent Binet, the American-born Jonathan Littell) or of high art and snuff lit (Michel Houelle\xadbecq). Among the recent crop of writers just reaching the top of their game, Marie NDiaye, born in 1967 and now living in Berlin, is pre-eminent.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/books/review/12eberstadt-img/12eberstadt-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 743, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'captio