 world of high school cheerleading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/books/review/dare-me-by-megan-abbott.html', 'snippet': 'Megan Abbott’s latest thriller finds power, desire and revenge in the insular world of high school cheerleading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fiction has not been kind to cheerleaders. Maybe this has something to do with the fact that future writers are more likely to be found scowling on the bleachers than doing back handsprings across the gymnasium floor. But now Megan Abbott has put her spirit fingers to the task of writing the Great American Cheerleader Novel, and — stop scowling — it’s spectacular.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/books/review/0812CAIN/0812CAIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 888, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/books/review/0812CAIN/0812CAIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1549, 'width': 1787, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/books/review/0812CAIN/0812CAIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/books/review/0812CAIN/0812CAIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/books/review/0812CAIN/0812CAIN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bring It On', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bring It On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abbott, Megan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T15:52:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Cain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/986c9e50-462f-54fe-812f-27399fb4122f', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/986c9e50-462f-54fe-812f-27399fb4122f'}, {'abstract': 'Looking like a camping flashlight, the ShoqBox from Philips is rugged, splash-proof and comes with a carabiner to fasten to a backpack. It doesn’t have a lot of fancy features that would detract from its simple design.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/a-rugged-speaker-for-the-outdoors/', 'snippet': 'Looking like a camping flashlight, the ShoqBox from Philips is rugged, splash-proof and comes with a carabiner to fasten to a backpack. It doesn’t have a lot of fancy features that would detract from its simple design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the world of portable speakers, simplicity is a big selling point. Their design has been streamlined by adding rechargeable internal batteries and removing cables in favor of streaming Bluetooth technology.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rugged Speaker for the Outdoors', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Simple Portable Speaker. Maybe a Bit Too Simple.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koninklijke Philips Electronics N.V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T15:52:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0a12fc3-59a3-5172-bf48-7b3b535bc893', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0a12fc3-59a3-5172-bf48-7b3b535bc893'}, {'abstract': 'In Dale Peck’s novel, a Midwesterner arrives in New York to claim his inheritance, a brownstone that may contain buried treasure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/books/review/the-garden-of-lost-and-found-by-dale-peck.html', 'snippet': 'In Dale Peck’s novel, a Midwesterner arrives in New York to claim his inheritance, a brownstone that may contain buried treasure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The problem is not that Dale Peck can’t write. Far from it. The problem is that Dale Peck can’t stop writing.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/books/review/0812Powers/0812Powers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 327, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/books/review/0812Powers/0812Powers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 327}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/books/review/0812Powers/0812Powers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 559, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/books/review/0812Powers/0812Powers-superJumbo.jpg', 'heigh