enya last August with Me to We, a company that offers what its Web site calls “transformative trips.” At a cost of $4,195 per person (excluding international airfare), guests spend 10 days immersed in African culture while participating in community development programs and living in “rustic, luxury cottages.”', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/travel/12DOGOOD1/12DOGOOD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/travel/12DOGOOD1/12DOGOOD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/travel/12DOGOOD1/12DOGOOD1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/travel/12DOGOOD1/12DOGOOD1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 959, 'width': 1273, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/travel/12DOGOOD1/12DOGOOD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/travel/12DOGOOD1/12DOGOOD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Volunteer Trips: Is Your Family Ready?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can Travel Make the Child?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volunteers and Community Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T17:43:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Conlin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Conlin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/702efba1-2153-527a-b677-a789760421ae', 'word_count': 2552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/702efba1-2153-527a-b677-a789760421ae'}, {'abstract': 'A look at three restaurants that are infusing their offerings with flavors from across the Atlantic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/travel/in-london-a-taste-of-america.html', 'snippet': 'A look at three restaurants that are infusing their offerings with flavors from across the Atlantic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUST steps from Carnaby Street, patrons line up to sample pulled pork and beef ribs and wash them down with bourbon and Pabst Blue Ribbon in a dining room that would not seem out of place in Lexington, Ky. The restaurant, Pitt Cue, though, is actually about 4,000 miles east of Lexington, in London.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/travel/12HEADSUP_SPAN/12HEADSUP_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/travel/12HEADSUP_SPAN/12HEADSUP_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/travel/12HEADSUP_SPAN/12HEADSUP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'sup