and visiting Myanmar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: Regarding “Easing the Pain of Workouts on the Road” (Getaway, Aug. 5), why not let guests clean the hotel? Sweeping the stairs, vacuuming carpets and carrying laundered sheets are a great workout. Lift the bed while other people vacuum underneath. Squeeze 100 oranges for juice and carry other people’s heavy bags upstairs. Steven Ira MarcusMurcia, Spain', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Editor', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Workouts on the Road', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T17:47:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/853c6f74-9edc-5fcb-b8e2-40e96ef75442', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/853c6f74-9edc-5fcb-b8e2-40e96ef75442'}, {'abstract': 'A. O. Scott and David Carr discuss the success, or failure, of actors and musicians who multitask.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/the-sweet-spot-aug-10/', 'snippet': 'A. O. Scott and David Carr discuss the success, or failure, of actors and musicians who multitask.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, A. O. Scott and David Carr discuss the success, or failure, of actors and musicians who multitask, like Woody Harrelson working as a playwright and stage director.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sweet Spot: Aug. 10', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrelson, Woody', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T17:48:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1efd6a6-4fa4-57f8-9fd6-4edcd726ee0d', 'word_count': 29, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1efd6a6-4fa4-57f8-9fd6-4edcd726ee0d'}, {'abstract': 'In 1978 had the Pacers retained Dan Roundfield, who left as a free agent and recently died, then Indiana planned to draft Larry Bird before the Celtics could.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/roundfields-impact-on-a-team-he-never-played-for/', 'snippet': 'In 1978 had the Pacers retained Dan Roundfield, who left as a free agent and recently died, then Indiana planned to draft Larry Bird before the Celtics could.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dan Roundfield, who drowned Monday in Aruba, played in 746 N.B.A. games over 11 seasons for four teams. But the one team he probably affected the most is a club for which he never played: the Boston Celtics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Roundfield’s Impact on a Team He Never Played For', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bird, Larry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roundfield, Dan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Hawks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indiana Pacers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T17:50:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter May', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'May', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73fc2c9d-2025-5b68-85c8-b07452877982', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73fc2c9d-2025-5b68-85c8-b07452877982'}, {'abstract': 'Determined to avoid perceptions that Mr. Romney’s support is slipping, a senior adviser said there was no legitimate explanation for the swing in recent polls.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/romney-advisers-dismiss-recent-dip-in-polls/', 'snippet': 'Determined to avoid perceptions that Mr. Romney’s support is slipping, a senior adviser said there was no legitimate explanation for the swing in recent polls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Advisers to Mitt Romney on Friday dismissed a series of new national polls that showed their candidate’s standing had weakened against President Obama, but they conceded that they could not explain what they called a “huge shift” in the numbers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Advisers Dismiss Recent Dip in Polls', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T17:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro and Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9127d20e-8f9e-5d64-8e0d-7d9482793d57', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9127d20e-8f9e-5d64-8e0d-7d9482793d57'}, {'abstract': 'See the records that fell at the London Olympics and explore the history of the records in each event.', 'web_u