h': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/realestate/12HUNT4_SPAN/HUNT-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1001, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/realestate/12HUNT4_SPAN/HUNT-4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2001, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/realestate/12HUNT4_SPAN/12HUNT4_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/realestate/12HUNT4_SPAN/12HUNT4_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/realestate/12HUNT4_SPAN/12HUNT4_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Folding Up the Murphy Bed for Good', 'kicker': 'The Hunt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Folding Up the Murphy Bed for Good', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T17:58:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b9f103b-6377-530e-b606-54c65e243c23', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b9f103b-6377-530e-b606-54c65e243c23'}, {'abstract': 'Support for same-sex couples now increasingly includes the expectation that they will have children.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/gay-couples-face-pressure-to-become-parents/', 'snippet': 'Support for same-sex couples now increasingly includes the expectation that they will have children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Support for same-sex couples is growing exponentially. So is the pressure on those couples from their friends and families: When are you going to have kids? A Motherlode contributor,\xa0 Marcus Mabry, feels lucky to have had the choice. Others have learned to ward off the questioners. Read more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gay Couples Face Pressure to Become Parents', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T18:04:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c2107fb-9146-5d5b-a079-892cc5bee857', 'word_count': 48, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c2107fb-9146-5d5b-a079-892cc5bee857'}, {'abstract': 'When you’re summering in Provence, it’s easy to put vegetables seasoned with the thyme, rosemary and savory that grows everywhere at the center of your plate every day.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/cooking-with-the-flavors-of-provence/', 'snippet': 'When you’re summering in Provence, it’s easy to put vegetables seasoned with the thyme, rosemary and savory that grows everywhere at the center of your plate every day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you can’t spend your summer in Provence, you can at least capture the flavors of a summer meal. This week Martha Rose Shulman offers five new recipes with a Provençal flair. She writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cooking With the Flavors of Provence', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T18:04:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5ea7357-7024-50da-9888-003b6d91d4d5', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5ea7357-7024-50da-9888-003b6d91d4d5'}, {'abstract': 'David Rakoff, the brilliant writer and actor and artist and friend to many people here at the magazine, died last night at the age of 47 from a long bout with cancer', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/david-rakoff-we-will-miss-you/', 'snippet': 'David Rakoff, the brilliant writer and actor and artist and friend to many people here at the magazine, died last night at the age of 47 from a long bout with cancer', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Rakoff, the brilliant writer and actor and artist and friend to many people here at the magazine, died last night at 47 following a long bout with cancer. There are expressions of love and admiration all over the place today — at The New Yorker and at The Awl and in this amazing outpouring at #DavidRakoff on Twitter — and they are all worth reading. In addition to being unfathomably funny in his work, David also confronted his illness in his writing with startling and bracing honesty. The final lines in the final essay, “Another Shoe,” of his final book, “Half Empty,” are these:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'David Rakoff, We Will Miss You', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rakoff, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T18:07:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joel Lovell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aec49c16-4ee1-5c78-a0b7-256152eebb5f', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aec49c16-4ee1-5c78-a0b7-256152eebb5f'}, {'abstract': 'Face it, Mom and Dad, you can’t control your child’s erotic life. But you can offer an adult perspective on the pornography that’s all too easy to find.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/approaching-carefully-the-subject-of-teens-and-porn/', 'snippet': 'Face it, Mom and Dad, you can’t control your child’s erotic life. But you can offer an adult perspective on the pornography that’s all too easy to find.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week’s parental quandary: How Do You Steer a Teenager Away from the Worst Porn? morphed, in the comments, into a multitude of spin-off questions. What’s “porn?” Does the swimsuit issue of Sports Illustrated count, or not? Does placing the lesser evils of pornography, however you define it, within a teenager’s sphere constitute endorsing it, or is such an interest in your child’s sex life “horrifying” and “helicopter parenting at its worst?” “What is wrong,” as Mouse writes, “with leaving your kids alone to find their own way (with the help of their friends) through adolescence?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Approaching (Carefully) the Subject of Teenagers and Porn', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pornography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Dan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T18:15:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57d198b7-707c-5976-a043-634d3e57eede', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57d198b7-707c-5976-a043-634d3e57eede'}, {'abstract': 'Embee, a longstanding Brooklyn manufacturer, makes the sunshades seen on food carts all over New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/garden/the-city-reliquary-salutes-the-embee-sunshade-company.html', 'snippet': 'Embee, a longstanding Brooklyn manufacturer, makes the sunshades seen on food carts all over New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Embee umbrellas are all over New York, punctuating the streetscape with wedges of color. They shade hot-dog stands and roasted nut carts and provide cover for sidewalk cafes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/garden/10CURRENTS/10CURRENTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}},