ant and his seemingly endless supply of 3-pointers, overwhelmed Argentina by 29 points. The 3-pointer was again in evidence on Friday when the United States defeated Argentina, 109-83, in an Olympic semifinal in London.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Men’s Basketball Team Advances to Gold Medal Game', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T19:47:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By NATE TAYLOR', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'TAYLOR', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c66741e6-6d61-5468-9742-b0cdd6457486', 'word_count': 1027, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c66741e6-6d61-5468-9742-b0cdd6457486'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge in New York rules that libel case filed by forensic art expert Peter Paul Biro can go forward but he dismisses part of the complaint.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/judge-rules-libel-case-against-the-new-yorker-can-go-forward/', 'snippet': 'A federal judge in New York rules that libel case filed by forensic art expert Peter Paul Biro can go forward but he dismisses part of the complaint.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A federal judge in New York has dismissed part of a libel suit filed by Peter Paul Biro, a forensic art expert, against The New Yorker but declined the magazine’s request to dismiss the entire complaint.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Rules Libel Case Against The New Yorker Can Go Forward', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'r