window into the history of soul music past and present. The original, released in 1976 and the new version, due Friday, both tell the story of a family of female singers in the ’60s embroiled in a melodramatic struggle to make it in the legendarily treacherous record business. In both “Sparkle” films the title character is a good girl with a fine voice (Irene Cara in the original, “American Idol” winner Jordin Sparks now) who has to mature as a performer and a woman when her older, wilder sibling, Sister (Lonette McKee then, Carmen Ejogo now), falls Billie Holiday-like victim to both abuse by men and drug addiction.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/arts/12SPARKLE1_SPAN/12SPARKLE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/arts/12SPARKLE1_SPAN/12SPARKLE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/arts/12SPARKLE1_SPAN/12SPARKLE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/arts/12SPARKLE1_SPAN/12SPARKLE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/arts/12SPARKLE1_SPAN/12SPARKLE1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/arts/12SPARKLE1_SPAN/12SPARKLE1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Soul Fable, Reimagined for a New Era', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Soul Fable, Reimagined For a New Era', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sparks, Jordin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sparkle (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franklin, Aretha', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gospel Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Houston, Whitney', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayfield, Curtis', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T21:09:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson George', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'George', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a28d313-86cd-5263-b69f-7dff433b1611', 'word_count': 1128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a28d313-86cd-5263-b69f-7dff433b1611'}, {'abstract': 'Economists debasing their reputations.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/culture-of-fraud/', 'snippet': 'Economists debasing their reputations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Still on vacation, but I have internet access for a bit, and have checked in on a few matters. The big story of the week among the dismal science set is the Romney campaign’s white paper on economic policy, which represents a concerted effort by three economists — Glenn Hubbard, Greg Mankiw, and John Taylor — to destroy their own reputations. (Yes, there was a fourth author, Kevin Hassett. But the co-au