 moderate, and who could reposition the Republican ticket toward the center.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/another-way-for-romney-to-go-bold-pick-a-moderate/', 'snippet': 'The case for picking someone who has credentials as a moderate, and who could reposition the Republican ticket toward the center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lot of vice-presidential chatter has been framed around the question of whether Mitt Romney will make a “bold” choice for a running mate — like Representative Paul D. Ryan of Wisconsin — or a “safe” one, like Senator Rob Portman of Ohio.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Way for Romney to ‘Go Bold’? Pick a Moderate', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vice Presidents and Vice Presidency (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T21:48:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03d1a729-9d0d-574c-8a58-ea4bb2740653', 'word_count': 1202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03d1a729-9d0d-574c-8a58-ea4bb2740653'}, {'abstract': 'For the past 100 years, competitors have tested their mettle in this five-part series of contests — fencing, swimming, riding, running and shooting — designed to identify a well-rounded athlete.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/last-but-not-least-modern-pentathlon/', 'snippet': 'For the past 100 years, competitors have tested their mettle in this five-part series of contests — fencing, swimming, riding, running and shooting — designed to identify a well-rounded athlete.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — With only two days left in the London Games, most sports have handed out some medals by now. But for modern pentathlon, perhaps the most unusual sport on the Olympic program, not so fast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Last but Not Least, Modern Pentathlon', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pentathlon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T21:50:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By JACQUI MAHER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacqui', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MAHER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f552826-aa5c-57c4-8346-972818d333da', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f552826-aa5c-57c4-8346-972818d333da'}, {'abstract': 'Once the wind kicked up at the Ocean Course on Friday, so did the scores at the P.G.A. Championship.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/tough-course-lives-up-to-its-reputation/', 'snippet': 'Once the wind kicked up at the Ocean Course on Friday, so did the scores at the P.G.A. Championship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIAWAH ISLAND, S.C. — Pete Dye’s house of horrors is having its revenge in the second round of the 94th P.G.A. Championship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tough Course Lives Up to Its Reputation', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf