ea1dcd88e'}, {'abstract': 'M. and her husband have a “good divorce” but after the monthly dinners they have together with their 4-year-old, their daughter seems sad and confused.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/when-divorced-parents-get-along-is-it-confusing-for-kids/', 'snippet': 'M. and her husband have a “good divorce” but after the monthly dinners they have together with their 4-year-old, their daughter seems sad and confused.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s quandary, in M.’s own words:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Divorced Parents Get Along, Is It Confusing for the Children?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T22:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7692cd69-606d-57b6-ba69-aeaaf0429e29', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7692cd69-606d-57b6-ba69-aeaaf0429e29'}, {'abstract': 'The Web series “Up to Speed,” on Hulu, follows Timothy Levitch as a tour guide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/arts/television/up-to-speed-with-timothy-levitch-on-hulu.html', 'snippet': 'The Web series “Up to Speed,” on Hulu, follows Timothy Levitch as a tour guide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We were introduced to the tour guide Timothy Levitch, known as Speed, 14 years ago in the documentary “The Cruise,” which depicted him as the Walt Whitman of the double-decker bus, a New York original with a touch of poetry and a large reservoir of hot air. Riffing about sincerity, nonconformity, the evils of work and the “lascivious voyeurism” of the bus tour, sleeping on friends’ couches and arguing with his bosses, he was like a Bartleby who preferred not to shut up.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/SPEED/SPEED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/SPEED/SPEED-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/SPEED/SPEED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/SPEED/SPEED-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/SPEED/SPEED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/SPEED/SPEED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/SPEED/SPEED-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Guide Who Talks to Statues and Trees', 'kick