ddlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06461f53-c95c-576a-86c3-c890f2017003', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06461f53-c95c-576a-86c3-c890f2017003'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Nelson’s production of “A Month in the Country,” at the Williamstown Theater Festival, features a younger leading lady than is traditionally cast in the play.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/theater/reviews/a-month-in-the-country-at-williamstown-theater-festival.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Nelson’s production of “A Month in the Country,” at the Williamstown Theater Festival, features a younger leading lady than is traditionally cast in the play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WILLIAMSTOWN, Mass. — Early in Richard Nelson’s clinical new production of Turgenev’s “Month in the Country,” one character says waspishly to her platonic lover, “You love observing people, picking them apart, rummaging around in them ...” It’s a fair definition of everybody else onstage: These folks just can’t stop dissecting one another’s behavior and motives and affectations.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/MONTH-jp/MONTH-jp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/MONTH-jp/MONTH-jp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/MONTH-jp/MONTH-jp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/MONTH-jp/MONTH-jp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1231, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/MONTH-jp/MONTH-jp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/MONTH-jp/MONTH-jp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/MONTH-jp/MONTH-jp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Group Psychoanalysis on a Russian Estate', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Group Psychoanalysis On a Russian Estate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turgenev, Ivan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Williamstown Theater Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T22:07:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d4cae23-8aca-556d-a5a4-479dccf18ff6', 'word_count': 1102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d4cae23-8aca-556d-a5a4-479dccf18ff6'}, {'abstract': 'The United States women’s soccer team’s victory against Japan at the Olympics was the most-watched event in the history of the NBC Sports Network.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/with-womens-soccer-final-nbc-sports-network-sets-a-record/', 'snippet': 'The United States women’s soccer team’s victory against Japan at the Olympics was the most-watched event in the history of the NBC Sports Network.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States women’s soccer team’s victory over Japan in the gold medal final of the London Games on Thursday was seen by an average of 4.35 million viewers — the most-watched event in the NBC Sports Network’s history. The 2-1 win eclipsed viewership of Stanley Cup finals games played in 2009 and 2010 when NBCSN was called Versus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Women’s Soccer Final, NBC Sports Network Sets a Record', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC Sports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC Sports Network', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T22:12:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/192874b3-605c-56ee-a119-f21a403c275c', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/192874b3-605c-56ee-a119-f21a403c275c'}, {'abstract': 'The Festival of Contemporary Music, a staple at Tanglewood, began on Thursday with works by Elliott Carter, Harrison Birtwistle, Niccolò Castiglioni, Luke Bedford and Sean Shepherd.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/arts/music/festival-of-contemporary-music-at-tanglewood.html', 'snippet': 'The Festival of Contemporary Music, a staple at Tanglewood, began on Thursday with works by Elliott Carter, Harrison Birtwistle, Niccolò Castiglioni, Luke Bedford and Sean Shepherd.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LENOX, Mass. — The Boston Symphony Orchestra is throwing itself a summer-long party to celebrate the 75th anniversary of Tanglewood, its off-season home here in the Berkshires, and the student performers at its educational arm, the Tanglewood Music Center, are taking part as well. Yet at the center’s annual Festival of Contemporary Music, which opened on Thursday evening and runs through Monday, it seems to be pretty much business as usual. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/CONTEMP/CONTEMP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/CONTEMP/CONTEMP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/CONTEMP/CONTEMP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/CONTEMP/CONTEMP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/CONTEMP/CONTEMP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/CONTEMP/CONTEMP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth'