s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Colorful World of Synchronized Swimming', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Synchronized Swimming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T22:19:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samantha Storey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Storey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea787233-317c-5eba-ad80-fae243781c75', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea787233-317c-5eba-ad80-fae243781c75'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees closer, and baseball’s career saves leader, said he would love to be able to pitch now, but that he knew he could not rush his recovery from knee surgery.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/rivera-preaches-patience-as-he-works-toward-a-return/', 'snippet': 'The Yankees closer, and baseball’s career saves leader, said he would love to be able to pitch now, but that he knew he could not rush his recovery from knee surgery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SARATOGA SPRINGS, N.Y. − Although Yankees Manager Joe Girardi has left open the remote possibility that closer Mariano Rivera might return this season from a torn anterior cruciate ligament in his right knee, the pitcher emphasized the need for patience during an appearance at Saratoga Race Course.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rivera Preaches Patience as He Works Toward a Return', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Mariano', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T22:46:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Pedulla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pedulla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18d7d5bc-64fa-56c0-8327-bab7a61aaad9', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18d7d5bc-64fa-56c0-8327-bab7a61aaad9'}, {'abstract': 'David Joyce, a county prosecutor, will replace Representative Steven C. LaTourette as the Republican nominee in Ohio’s 14th Congressional District, entering the race as the favored candidate.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/republicans-pick-ballot-replacement-for-ohio-congressman/', 'snippet': 'David Joyce, a county prosecutor, will replace Representative Steven C. LaTourette as the Republican nominee in Ohio’s 14th Congressional District, entering the race as the favored candidate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Joyce will replace Representative Steven C. LaTourette as the Republican nominee in Ohio’s 14th Congressional District, local party leaders said on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Pick Ballot Replacement for Ohio Congressman', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaTourette, Steven C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T22:57:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c709c81-4c3c-5e5d-a762-2a7bfb4b6935', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c709c81-4c3c-5e5d-a762-2a7bfb4b6935'}, {'abstract': 'Rather than offering Tex-Mex- or California-style fare, Vega offers dishes that are authentically Mexican.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/nyregion/a-review-of-vega-in-hartsdale.html', 'snippet': 'Rather than offering Tex-Mex- or California-style fare, Vega offers dishes that are authentically Mexican.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE first place I had a sopaipilla — that puffy pillow of fried dough popular in New Mexico — was in a restaurant in a nondescript strip mall outside Santa Fe. Served warm and drizzled with honey, it was delicious — and incredibly popular with the Spanish-speaking diners, nearly all of whom had a few for dessert. But it is not an item seen on New York menus very often.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12DINEWE1/12DINEWE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12DINEWE1/12DINEWE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 998, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12DINEWE1/12DINEWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75,