ns', 'value': 'Oak Creek (Wis)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T23:48:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Yaccino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62a2e838-f953-569c-ac33-4f6b8972eb4b', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62a2e838-f953-569c-ac33-4f6b8972eb4b'}, {'abstract': 'Visitors to the National Mall have been confronted with an empty Reflecting Pool and a closed Washington Monument as construction crews make repairs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/us/national-mall-dotted-with-construction-projects.html', 'snippet': 'Visitors to the National Mall have been confronted with an empty Reflecting Pool and a closed Washington Monument as construction crews make repairs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The nation’s capital is under construction.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/us/MALL/MALL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 660, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/us/MALL/MALL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1319, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bulldozers Join Tourists as Fixtures in Capital', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bulldozers Join Tourists As Fixtures in Capital', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trust for the National Mall', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Mall (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Park Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-10T23:53:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Berg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa159424-2244-53c0-9304-2e53b4975349', 'word_count': 898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa159424-2244-53c0-9304-2e53b4975349'}, {'abstract': 'For high-level athletes, it’s a perennial struggle to balance focus and family.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/alone-in-the-zone/', 'snippet': 'For high-level athletes, it’s a perennial struggle to balance focus and family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have been trying to imagine how I would have felt if, after having performed at a level that made me the best in the world, I only then learned from my parents that my grandparents were dead and my mother had cancer. The news last week that the multiple gold medals of the Chinese diver Wu Minxia had, in a way, come at a price made me think about the tug of war between the hyper-focus required to excel and the yearning for connection. That tension often makes athletes feel as if these forces are mutually exclusive or, at the very least, that they linger in the realm of the imbalanced and unhealthy. Death, it would appear, is inconvenient. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alone in the Zone', 'kicker': 'Opinionator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords':