yt://article/8dbc0a15-a59c-541c-a459-b4a1301b31de'}, {'abstract': 'The northern Sinai Peninsula has seen a buildup of troops and military hardware since a fatal attack Sunday on Egyptian soldiers who were about to break their Ramadan fast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/world/middleeast/egypt-tightens-grip-on-sinai.html', 'snippet': 'The northern Sinai Peninsula has seen a buildup of troops and military hardware since a fatal attack Sunday on Egyptian soldiers who were about to break their Ramadan fast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EL-ARISH, Egypt — The new police chief peered through the black grill of a holding cell and asked a baby-faced prisoner inside when he had gotten there. The young man — he might have been a teenager — had been detained in the previous day or two as Egypt’s military swept through the Sinai in pursuit this week of the killers of 16 of its soldiers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/world/SINAI/SINAI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/11/world/SINAI/SINAI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/world/SINAI/SINAI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/world/SINAI/SINAI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1425, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/world/SINAI/SINAI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnai