state/', 'snippet': 'We know much less about what’s going on in Iowa than in the other swing states, but there was a new poll there on Friday, and it had pretty good news for Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some swing states get more polling love than others. In Florida, the matchup between President Obama and Mitt Romney has been tested 29 times by pollsters since last November. In Ohio, there have been 25 polls, and in Virginia, 27. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 10: Iowa, the Forgotten Swing State', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rasmussen Reports', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T01:04:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/443061fa-342b-5080-9b91-512f8e848598', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/443061fa-342b-5080-9b91-512f8e848598'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney’s biggest challenge at the moment is not President Obama. It’s himself. He begins a four-state bus tour on Saturday to try to strengthen his relationship with voters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/us/politics/romney-renews-focus-on-empathy-gap-with-obama.html', 'snipp