r New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aug. 10, 2012', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lottery Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T01:43:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/13b6ba59-d181-54c8-8fdf-ee3c184597e8', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13b6ba59-d181-54c8-8fdf-ee3c184597e8'}, {'abstract': 'The manager will still incur an automatic fine for being ejected in the fifth inning of Thursday’s game in Detroit for arguing a call.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/10/girardi-avoids-suspension/', 'snippet': 'The manager will still incur an automatic fine for being ejected in the fifth inning of Thursday’s game in Detroit for arguing a call.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Manager Joe Girardi was not given a suspension for his vehement argument with umpires that got him ejected from the Yankees’ 4-3 win on Thursday in Detroit. Joe Torre, Girardi’s predecessor and former manager when he played for the Yankees, spoke to Girardi and umpire Tim Welke on the phone to get their positions on the incident. Torre said that even though there may have been contact between Girardi and Bob Davidson, who intervened, it did not warrant a suspension. Girardi claimed that any contact was initiated by Davidson as he tried to separate him and Welke.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia':