ad lost 9 of their previous 11 games and had dropped three in a row. The Yankees happily added to their woes with a 10-4 victory Friday.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/sports/yankees-floater/yankees-floater-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1006, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/sports/yankees-floater/yankees-floater-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1987, 'width': 1953, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/sports/yankees-floater/yankees-floater-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/11/sports/yankees-floater/yankees-floater-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/sports/yankees-floater/yankees-floater-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Use Blue Jays to Continue Turnaround', 'kicker': 'Yankees 10, Blue Jays 4', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yanks Use Blue Jays To Continue Turnaround', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Blue Jays', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Freddy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T03:22:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87f5c618-c3c4-5a74-bcb4-24efac25405b', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87f5c618-c3c4-5a74-bcb4-24efac25405b'}, {'abstract': 'On the Street: The Newport Vintage Dance Week took place July 29 to Aug. 3 in Rhode Island, drawing 200 participants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/fashion/100000001716260/bill-cunningham-last-dance.html', 'snippet': 'On the Street: The Newport Vintage Dance Week took place July 29 to Aug. 3 in Rhode Island, drawing 200 participants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the Street: The Newport Vintage Dance Week took place July 29 to Aug. 3 in Rhode Island, drawing 200 participants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/fashion/video-0812billcunningham/video-0812billcunningham-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/10/fashion/video-0812billcunningham/video-0812billcunningham-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/fashion/video-0812billcunningham/video-0812billcunningham-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/10/fashion/video-0812billcunningham/video-0812billcunningham-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Cunningham | Last Dance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T03:22:10+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'Joanna Nikas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nikas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/b4b8ce79-89ec-51bd-b246-90ef80fc852b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/b4b8ce79-89ec-51bd-b246-90ef80fc852b'}, {'abstract': 'Dora B. Schriro, the correction commissioner, tends her garden at this time of year, devours the Sunday newspapers and keeps her BlackBerry close by for any news from Rikers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/nyregion/dora-b-schriro-correction-commissioner-tends-to-her-garden-on-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'Dora B. Schriro, the correction commissioner, tends her garden at this time of year, devours the Sunday newspapers and keeps her BlackBerry close by for any news from Rikers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City’s commissioner of correction, Dora B. Schriro, developed a template to reform the nation’s immigrant detention system while working at the United States Department of Homeland Security; she has also headed the Corrections Departments of Missouri and Arizona. Ms. Schriro, 62, began her career in New York in 1984 and was appointed to her current job by Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg in 2009. Born on Staten Island, she focuses on Rikers Island these days, with a goal of making jails safer for those who work in them and for those who are incarcerated. A widow, she lives in a 99-year-old Dutch colonial on City Island in the Bronx with her calico cat, Annie Annie. Sundays at this time of year find Ms. Schriro in her garden, where she recently planted eight new rosebushes.\xa0', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1_SPAN/12ROUTINE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1_SPAN/12ROUTINE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1_SPAN/12ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1_SPAN/12ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1_SPAN/12ROUTINE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1_SPAN/12ROUTINE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1_SPAN/12ROUTINE1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Roses, Pasta and Police Shows', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Roses, Pasta and Police Shows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rikers Island Prison Complex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schriro, Dora B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'City Island (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T03:23:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e34a40db-d0fb-5caf-b5b2-0c5382a923ae', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e34a40db-d0fb-5caf-b5b2-0c5382a923ae'}, {'abstract': 'After you get off the ferry, subway fare is all you’ll need to get to Tottenville, the southernmost town on Staten Island and in the State of New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/nyregion/on-staten-island-many-ways-to-travel-to-the-past.html', 'snippet': 'After you get off the ferry, subway fare is all you’ll need to get to Tottenville, the southernmost town on Staten Island and in the State of New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If, like Edna St. Vincent Millay in her poem “Recuerdo,” you get off the ferry with only subway fare in your pocket, that’s as much as you’ll need to get to Tottenville, the southernmost town on Staten Island — and in the State of New York. It’s surely one of the longer journeys you can take for a single MetroCard swipe: a little over 20 miles from Manhattan, 5 of them over water and 16 on the Staten Island Railway. Named for a family of landowners and shipyard founders, Tottenville is a colonial-era relic amid energetic recent development. Several of the oldest buildings sit within Conference House Park, whose wild, beautiful woods are crisscrossed with paths leading to the shore.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12LOCAL1_SPAN/12LOCAL1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12LOCAL1_SPAN/12LOCAL1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12LOCAL1_SPAN/12LOCAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12LOCAL1_SPAN/12LOCAL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12LOCAL1_SPAN/12LOCAL1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/nyregion/12LOCAL1_SPAN/12LOCAL1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Boat and a Train to the Colonial Past', 'kicker': 'Local Stop | Tottenville', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Boat and a Train to the Colonial Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tottenville (Staten Island, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'val