n in Afghanistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — When she refused to prostitute herself or have sex with the man she was forced to marry when she was about 13, officials said, Sahar Gul’s in-laws tortured her and threw her into a dirty, windowless cellar for months until the police discovered her lying in hay and animal dung.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/world/SAHAR-BULLDOG/SAHAR-BULLDOG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/world/SAHAR-BULLDOG/SAHAR-BULLDOG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/world/SAHAR-BULLDOG/SAHAR-BULLDOG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/world/SAHAR-BULLDOG/SAHAR-BULLDOG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/world/SAHAR-BULLDOG/SAHAR-BULLDOG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/world/SAHAR-BULLDOG/SAHAR-BULLDOG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/world/SAHAR-BULLDOG/SAHAR-BULLDOG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wed and Tortured at 13, Afghan Girl Finds Rare Justice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wed and Tortured at 13, Afghan Girl Finds Rare Justice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gul, Sahar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T15:04:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb5892e3-594a-57a1-bd23-4c18f531aeb6', 'word_count': 1701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb5892e3-594a-57a1-bd23-4c18f531aeb6'}, {'abstract': 'A poem by Dorothy Margaret Stuart of Britain that won a 1924 Olympic bronze portrays fencing as “the clashing of the thin grey swords.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/sports/olympics/when-poetry-was-an-olympic-event.html', 'snippet': 'A poem by Dorothy Margaret Stuart of Britain that won a 1924 Olympic bronze portrays fencing as “the clashing of the thin grey swords.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The torrent of sports poetry inspired by the London Olympics continues unabated: NPR even hosted Poetry Games, in which listeners voted on a selection of verse with an athletic theme by celebrated poets from various countries. But few people today recall that poetry, just like the 100 meters, was an official Olympic competition from 1912 to 1948. Sadly, the names of the medal winners are not listed on the International Olympic Committee’s rosters. And many of the winning poems in the so-called Pentathlon of the Muses — which had to be “inspired by the idea of sport” — have mysteriously vanished as well, perhaps, as critics have suggested, because of their dubious literary quality.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medals That Were Won Not in Pentathlon or 100 Meters, but in Iambic Pentameter', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Medals That Were Won Not In Pentathlon or 100 Meters, But in Iambic Pentameter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T15:08:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tony Perrottet', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perrottet', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fff88e9-5b55-5e5a-acda-f2e6309fff29', 'word_count': 881, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fff88e9-5b55-5e5a-acda-f2e6309fff29'}, {'abstract': 'The Jets hope that the veteran safety Yeremiah Bell, who was recommended by offensive coordinator Tony Sparano, can bring some stability to the team’s defense.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/sports/football/yeremiah-bell-new-jets-leader-in-middle-of-defense-proves-a-quick-study.html', 'snippet': 'The Jets hope that the veteran safety Yeremiah Bell, who was recommended by offensive coordinator Tony Sparano, can bring some stability to the team’s defense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CORTLAND, N.Y. — The Jets needed a safety, and not merely any safety. They were, of course, looking for a safety who could blanket opposing receivers and wallop them when they caught the ball, but they really were seeking a maestro, someone who could run the secondary. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/dog-jets/dog-jets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 706, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/dog-jets/dog-jets-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1412, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/dog-jets/dog-jets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/dog-jets/dog-jets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/dog-jets/dog-jets-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Offensive Coach Gives Defense a Lift', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Offensive Coordinator Gives the Defense a Lift', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sparano, Tony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bell, Yeremiah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Dolphins', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T15:18:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8d7ec8b-731b-5d93-94d7-03e7544a3c4c', 'word_count': 991, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8d7ec8b-731b-5d93-94d7-03e7544a3c4c'}, {'abstract': 'Prime farmland in the Sacramento River’s delta would be affected in the diversion of fresh water to the state’s more economically vital areas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/us/california-farmers-fear-impact-of-water-distribution-plan.html', 'snippet': 'Prime farmland in the Sacramento River’s delta would be affected in the diversion of fresh water to the state’s more economically vital areas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COURTLAND, Calif. — On the last Sunday of July, this small town in the Sacramento River’s delta takes a pause from the peak of the pear harvest season by holding its annual pear fair. A pear run, a pear parade, a pear pie eating contest and a pear fair queen are as much a part of life’s rhythm here as the pruning, picking and packing of pears.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/ALT-DELTA-1/ALT-DELTA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/us/ALT-DELTA-1/ALT-DELTA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/ALT-DELTA-1/ALT-DELTA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'super