': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/77fde4a8-5b92-5d1e-905f-2ac8c397a10b', 'word_count': 2172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77fde4a8-5b92-5d1e-905f-2ac8c397a10b'}, {'abstract': 'The killings heightened worries about how the coalition troops can protect themselves while working at close quarters with their Afghan counterparts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/world/asia/forces-killed-were-shot-in-company-of-afghans.html', 'snippet': 'The killings heightened worries about how the coalition troops can protect themselves while working at close quarters with their Afghan counterparts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Six of the eight American, British and coalition service members killed since Thursday in southern Afghanistan were shot in the company of their Afghan allies, officials of the NATO-led coalition here said Saturday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coalition Soldiers Killed Were Shot in Company of Afghans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Afghans Kill Allies, Force’s Trust Is Shaken', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T17:13:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9eedd7a-c3ec-55a0-a59b-e84fb1be1229', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9eedd7a-c3ec-55a0-a59b-e84fb1be1229'}, {'abstract': 'I’m beginning to worry that the Democrats are now controlled by an extremist fringe — of e-mail writers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/opinion/sunday/al-and-joe-lead-the-spam-squad.html', 'snippet': 'I’m beginning to worry that the Democrats are now controlled by an extremist fringe — of e-mail writers.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:25 a.m. Received an urgent e-mail from Al Gore with an unsettling subject line: “Disaster.” Turns out the former vice president wanted to tell me that the Republican Party had been “hijacked by an extremist fringe,” and I should send “$3 or more” a.s.a.p. Now, I’m a fan of the former vice president and, considering some of the blather I’ve heard recently from the Tea Party, it didn’t surprise me to learn that the G.O.P. had been hijacked. But I’m beginning to worry that it’s the Democrats who are now controlled by an extremist fringe — of e-mail writers. These are some of the genuine campaign e-mails I received over just two days recently:', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sunday-review/12LOOSEENDS/12LOOSEENDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sunday-review/12LOOSEENDS/12LOOSEENDS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sunday-review/12LOOSEENDS/12LOOSEENDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'hei