it left town for summer recess. That did not happen, and American companies that do business in Russia, or want to, may find themselves at a disadvantage with foreign competitors once Russia joins the World Trade Organization on Aug. 22. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trade Relations With Russia', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trade Relations With Russia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jackson-Vanik Amendment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Magnitsky, Sergei L', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T17:23:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff15d1d4-aeda-53b2-b840-8129379d4513', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff15d1d4-aeda-53b2-b840-8129379d4513'}, {'abstract': 'Ann Romney said that Mitt Romney would pick a candidate who shared her husband’s values. Take a look at how Mr. Romney and his running mate, Paul D. Ryan, match up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/08/12/us/politics/20120812-ryan-romney.html', 'snippet': 'Ann Romney said that Mitt Romney would pick a candidate who shared her husband’s values. Take a look at how Mr. Romney and his running mate, Paul D. Ryan, match up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ann Romney said that Mitt Romney would pick a candidate who shared her husband’s values. Take a look at how Mr. Romney and his running mate, Paul D. Ryan, match up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Romney’s Image', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vice Presidents and Vice Presidency (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T17:25:49+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/858b5897-807b-5a4a-aa17-fc2d9b4280a7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/858b5897-807b-5a4a-aa17-fc2d9b4280a7'}, {'abstract': 'Two Florida courts take different views of a Supreme Court ruling against life sentences without parole for juveniles not convicted of homicide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/opinion/sunday/de-facto-life-without-parole.html', 'snippet': 'Two Florida courts take different views of a Supreme Court ruling against life sentences without parole for juveniles not convicted of homicide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, an appeals court in Florida overturned a 60-year sentence for a young defendant who shot someone when he was almost 17 years old and was convicted of attempted murder, armed robbery and armed burglary. He would not have been released from prison until he was 76, exceeding his life expectancy according to National Vital Statistics Reports. The court found his sentence was unconstitutional. On the same day, a Florida state trial judge, without any hesitation, sentenced another defendant to 100 years for crimes he committed as a juvenile.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'De Facto Life Without Parole', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'De Facto Life Without Parole', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T17:26:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/17f6e6a2-1a62-592d-a6ca-688f7008b4e7', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17f6e6a2-1a62-592d-a6ca-688f7008b4e7'}, {'abstract': 'Mike Trout has had an incredible rookie season for the Los Angeles Angels.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/one-of-a-kind-stats-for-angels-rookie/', 'snippet': 'Mike Trout has had an incredible rookie season for the Los Angeles Angels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mike Trout turned 21 on Tuesday, and naturally, he celebrated by hitting a home run. It gave Trout, the Los Angeles Angels’ incomparable rookie, 20 homers for the season. He hit his 21st on Friday, and he entered Saturday with a .345 average and 36 stolen bases, leading the American League in both categories.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One-of-a-Kind Stats for Angels’ Rookie', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Extra Bases: One-of-a-Kind Stats', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trout, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Angels of Anaheim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T17:27:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56cac87e-3590-56a7-ade7-23b8ac3a63c1', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56cac87e-3590-56a7-ade7-23b8ac3a63c1'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney’s economic plan makes vague promises about deep tax cuts, with no details about how he would pay for them. His choice of Paul Ryan as a running mate, however, suggests that the costs would be harsh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/opinion/sunday/romneys-tax-plan-defies-the-rules-of-math.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney’s economic plan makes vague promises about deep tax cuts, with no details about how he would pay for them. His choice of Paul Ryan as a running mate, however, suggests that the costs would be harsh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN May of 2000, when George W. Bush was running for president on a platform of extravagant tax cuts for all, his campaign did something that would be considered remarkable today: it submitted his tax plan to the Congressional Joint Committee on Taxation, to see how much all those tax cuts would cost the Treasury.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0,