', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bc0dc6a-743d-5032-852d-00c19589e1f1', 'word_count': 1031, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bc0dc6a-743d-5032-852d-00c19589e1f1'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Ryan’s appeal to the right isn’t just about his fiscal approach.', 'web_url': 'https://bruni.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/a-social-conservative-too/', 'snippet': 'Paul Ryan’s appeal to the right isn’t just about his fiscal approach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Ryan’s conservatism is almost always described in terms of his approach to budgetary matters and his desire to cut federal spending significantly. And that has been the focus of the discussion about him today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Social Conservative, Too', 'kicker': 'Frank Bruni', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T17:59:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_