, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Defense of Single Motherhood', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Defense of Single Motherhood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Single Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McLanahan, Sara S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Single Mothers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Amato, Paul R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T18:01:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Roiphe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roiphe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f014919-66f1-5135-a45d-18e10eb5a57e', 'word_count': 1232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f014919-66f1-5135-a45d-18e10eb5a57e'}, {'abstract': 'America should never refight the last war, especially when we don’t understand it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/opinion/sunday/what-we-dont-know-about-vietnam-can-still-hurt-us.html', 'snippet': 'America should never refight the last war, especially when we don’t understand it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS the war in Afghanistan drags on with no definitive victory in sight for the United States and American troops begin to withdraw, comparisons to the Vietnam War are once again in the air, 50 years after both Washington and Hanoi decided to beef up their forces in South Vietnam. “Just take a run through the essential Vietnam War checklist,” wrote Tom Engelhardt in Mother Jones magazine, noting “there’s ‘quagmire’\xa0” and “the idea of winning ‘hearts and minds’\xa0” as well as “bomb-able, or in our era drone-able, ‘sanctuaries’ across the border” and even “a one-man version of My Lai.” Although these analogies are particularly attractive to critics — who see America’s battle in Afghanistan as even more futile than Vietnam and advocate a quick exit — they are deeply flawed.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sunday-review/12VIETNAM/12VIETNAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 835, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sunday-review/12VIETNAM/12VIETNAM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1670, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sunday-review/12VIETNAM/12VIETNAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/sunday-review/12VIETNAM/12VIETNAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sunday-review/12VIETNAM/12VIETNAM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Exploding the Myths About Vietnam', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exploding the Myths About Vietnam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duan, Le', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T18:01:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lien-Hang Nguyen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lien-hang', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nguyen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b54c3983-da06-5774-a8d4-73117bdebb25', 'word_count': 1303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b54c3983-da06-5774-a8d4-73117bdebb25'}, {'abstract': 'Delays of new important regulations call into question the Obama administration’s commitment to reforms that are needed to make government work better.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/opinion/sunday/rules-delayed-governing-denied.html', 'snippet': 'Delays of new important regulations call into question the Obama administration’s commitment to reforms that are needed to make government work better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been 19 months since President Obama signed into law the Food Safety Modernization Act, the first overhaul of the Food and Drug Administration’s food safety laws since the 1930s. But if you think the food supply has become markedly safer since then, think again. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source