s.com/2012/08/12/sports/olympics/rhythmic-gymnastics-remains-women-only-at-olympics.html', 'snippet': 'Rhythmic gymnastics is one of only two Olympic sports — synchronized swimming is the other — in which both sexes do not participate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Around and around they went, gracefully shimmying and passing balls, hoops and batons to and fro. The crowd roared as the rhythmic gymnasts, five to a team or competing as individuals, made their way through elaborately choreographed routines. They seemed to have it all: gallons of product in their hair, makeup caked on their smiling faces, and uniforms adorned with enough reflective matter to make a Vegas showgirl blush.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/gymnastics/gymnastics-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/gymnastics/gymnastics-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/gymnastics/gymnastics-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/gymnastics/gymnastics-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/gymnastics/gymnastics-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Men, Sport’s Stigma Dampens Appeal', 'kicker': 'Gymnastics | Rhythmic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Men, Sport’s Stigma Dampens Appeal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Synchronized Swimming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rhythmic Gymnastics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gymnastics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T18:09:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Pilon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pilon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4234cb7c-c7fa-56a2-8976-22b0a06a748c', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4234cb7c-c7fa-56a2-8976-22b0a06a748c'}, {'abstract': 'The London Games showcased the very best of us.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/opinion/sunday/bruni-the-soul-of-the-olympics.html', 'snippet': 'The London Games showcased the very best of us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S easy to be cynical about the Olympics: about the runaway commercialism; about the jingoism that so many countries bring to the games; about NBC. Definitely about NBC. Its breathless degree of fake suspense during prime time broadcasts has been a silly mockery of our wired ways, and too many on-the-spot interviews with athletes redefined dippy. How do you feel? Jubilant if you’ve medaled, crushed if you haven’t and really, really tired. Fill in the blanks.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Soul of the Olympics', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Soul of the Olympics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douglas, Gabby', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phelps, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zonderland, Epke', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'May-Treanor, Misty', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walsh Jennings, Kerri', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Attar, Sarah', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franklin, Missy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pistorius, Oscar', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Kirani', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T18:10:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/174ab4fc-7cca-5c74-9813-557e97ffd7e1', 'word_count': 1121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/174ab4fc-7cca-5c74-9813-557e97ffd7e1'}, {'abstract': 'What happens if you’re in love with a young woman and, with age, her beauty fades?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/opinion/sunday/old-love.html', 'snippet': 'What happens if you’re in love with a young woman and, with age, her beauty fades?', 'lead_paragraph': 'YEARS ago, when I was a callow 39, I had lunch with a college friend whose intellectual authority over me was considerable; we lunched together often, at least once a month. On that particular occasion I put to him a question that embarrassed me: what if one is deeply in love with a young woman — which was my case — and with age her beauty fades. Will her attraction fatally diminish? Might it be displaced by a sort of repulsion? For instance, when her skin withers and wrinkles, will I still want to kiss the crook of her arms, those arms that I so admire, and, if gallantry pushes me to do so, will I have to avert my eyes? ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sunday-review/12LOVE/12LOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 731, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sunday-review/12LOVE/12LOVE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1463, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sunday-review/12LOVE/12LOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/sunday-review/12LOVE/12LOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sunday-review/12LOVE/12LOVE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Old Love', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Old Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T18:12:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Louis Begley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Louis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Begley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaf32edb-182d-5f19-809f-0146e97e5d49', 'word_count': 961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaf32edb-182d-5f19-809f-0146e97e5d49'}, {'abstract': 'Cleveland, which held first place as late as June 23, lost 11 in a row from July 27 through last Tuesday, falling out of the race in the American League Central.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/indians-fade-away-in-a-l-central/', 'snippet': 'Cleveland, which held first place as late as June 23, lost 11 in a row from July 27 through last Tuesday, falling out of the race in the American League Central.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Travis Hafner signed a $57 million contract extension in 2007, he had just turned 30 and was on his way to his fourth season in a row with at least 100 runs batted in. The Cleveland Indians, who were on their way to a division title, had Hafner locked up through 2012.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indians Fade Away in A.L. Central', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Extra Bases: Indians Fade Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hafner, Travis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sizemore, Grady', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Indians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T18:20:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37f05081-233e-5297-8711-9c63759353ee',