/39b0dd29-6d92-5e83-a461-831bae448af7'}, {'abstract': 'The United States women’s basketball team won its fifth straight gold medal with an 86-50 victory in the final, behind 21 points from Candace Parker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/sports/olympics/us-women-rout-france-for-olympic-title.html', 'snippet': 'The United States women’s basketball team won its fifth straight gold medal with an 86-50 victory in the final, behind 21 points from Candace Parker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The most dominant team in basketball, men’s or women’s, college or professional, domestic or international, won another gold medal Saturday. It felt like 2008 all over again. Or 2004. Or 2000. Or 1996.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/12basketball/12basketball-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/12basketball/12basketball-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/12basketball/12basketball-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/12basketball/12basketball-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/12basketball/12basketball-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/12basketball/12basketball-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/12basketball/12basketball-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Women Run Away With 5th Straight Gold', 'kicker': "Basketball | Women's Final", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Women Run Away With 5th Straight Gold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Candace', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T21:53:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe67cc4e-ffc4-5cee-bc05-7dc223937462', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe67cc4e-ffc4-5cee-bc05-7dc223937462'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama signed legislation exempting scores of government positions from Senate confirmation, which may ease a backlog that has left many government agencies without presidential appointees for months at a time.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/obama-signs-law-exempting-many-appointees-from-senate-approval/', 'snippet': 'President Obama signed legislation exempting scores of government positions from Senate confirmation, which may ease a backlog that has left many government agencies without presidential appointees for months at a time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A backlog that has left many government agencies without presidential appointees for months at a time may ease a bit because President Obama signed legislation on Friday exempting scores of government positions from Senate confirmation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Signs Law Exempting Many Appointees From Senate Approval', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T21:59:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a67eab71-a47f-5885-994b-77de23c443d6', 'word_count': 622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a67eab71-a47f-5885-994b-77de23c443d6'}, {'abstract': 'The dancer-choreographer Kyle Abraham is taking August easy, but he’s planning a busy fall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/arts/dance/kyle-abraham-on-pittsburgh-and-pavement.html', 'snippet': 'The dancer-choreographer Kyle Abraham is taking August easy, but he’s planning a busy fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN it comes to cities that fuel the creative fire, Pittsburgh isn’t usually the first to spring to mind. But don’t tell Kyle Abraham. This dancer and choreographer has been mining that town for material his entire career. Born there into the hip-hop culture of the late 1970s, Mr. Abraham, 34, mixes that influence with classical music and movement training. In 2010 he caught the eye of the dance world with “The Radio Show,” which was inspired by a Pittsburgh station and earned him a Bessie Award. It dealt with race and identity, issues he’s explored throughout his work. Then came “Live! The Realest MC,” loosely based on the story of Pinocchio and an autobiographical look at coming out in a hip-hop world.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/arts/12SNAPSHOT/12SNAPSHOT-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1604, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/arts/12SNAPSHOT/12SNAPSHOT-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1872, 'width': 1195, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/arts/12SNAPSHOT/12SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/arts/12SNAPSHOT/12SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/arts/12SNAPSHOT/12SNAPSHOT-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Pittsburgh and the Peace Sign', 'kicker': 'Snapshot | Kyle Abraham', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Pittsburgh And the Peace Sign', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abraham, Kyle (1977- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh (Pa)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T21:59:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4e3c9a0-d2c4-53c3-a5e9-fcab5c939cf7', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4e3c9a0-d2c4-53c3-a5e9-fcab5c939cf7'}, {'abstract': 'It is not what it seems. Or is it?', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/meaning-of-it/', 'snippet': 'It is not what it seems. Or is it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — IT took me a while, but I think I’ve finally gotten over my “What have you done for me since the October, 2011, puzzle contest, Patrick Berry?” thing. Today’s Sunday puzzle is the kind of jokey, strong, wordplay-filled grid I like to see from him. And clean. This is no stunt grid, but even when he makes a showy puzzle, Mr. Berry can be counted on to fill his puzzle well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Meaning of It', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-11T22:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4718ea95-ab49-52bb-a212-9806fa428339', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4718ea95-ab49-52bb-a212-9806fa428339'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Fleischmann believed he had achieved cold fusion in a lab, but his announcement proved premature and he was discredited.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/science/martin-fleischmann-cold-fusion-seeker-dies-at-85.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Fleischmann believed he had achieved cold fusion in a lab, but his announcement proved premature and he was discredited.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martin Fleischmann made the greatest discovery since fire: replicating the furnace of the sun at room temperature in a jar of water, essentially solving the world’s energy needs forever.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/world/dog-FLEISCHMANN-obit/dog-FLEISCHMANN-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 809, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/world/dog-FLEISCHMANN-obit/dog-FLEISCHMANN-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1617, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/world/dog-FLEISCHMANN-obit/dog-FLEISCHMANN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/world/dog-FLEISCHMANN-obit/dog-FLEISCHMANN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbn