son': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pilon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f47022a3-5a0e-57c0-88be-343d90b023d2', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f47022a3-5a0e-57c0-88be-343d90b023d2'}, {'abstract': 'Dan Zevin, the dude dad with the minivan, offers advice for full-time fathers. Get out your soup ladles.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/meditations-from-the-dad-in-the-minivan/', 'snippet': 'Dan Zevin, the dude dad with the minivan, offers advice for full-time fathers. Get out your soup ladles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dan Zevin, author of “Dan Gets a Minivan: Life at the Intersection of Dude and Dad” and “The Day I Turned Uncool,” may be a humorist, but like the dads profiled in the Sunday Styles piece “Just Wait Until Your Mother Gets Home,” he has also been a full-time father, squeezing in a sentence or two during nap time. Now, when the babysitter doesn’t show, or the school calls to turn in the child with a fever he dropped off moments before, he’s the guy who takes the fall. His musings on fatherhood, in appropriately short, new-parent appropriate bursts, follow. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meditations from the Dad in the Minivan', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zevin, Dan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T01:27:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Zevin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zevin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f60ef31c-3aa3-5acf-829c-30f7f0c5645a', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f60ef31c-3aa3-5acf-829c-30f7f0c5645a'}, {'abstract': 'Rory McIlroy and Vijay Singh shared a six-under-par lead when Saturday’s third round of the P.G.A. Championship was postponed because of heavy rain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/sports/golf/pga-championship-mcilroy-and-singh-lead-when-play-stops.html', 'snippet': 'Rory McIlroy and Vijay Singh shared a six-under-par lead when Saturday’s third round of the P.G.A. Championship was postponed because of heavy rain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIAWAH ISLAND, S.C. — If you build a golf course on the ocean, there is always the chance a storm will roll in from the sea. And throughout the week at the 2012 P.G.A. Championship, thunderstorms have been in the forecast every day for the Ocean Course on Kiawah Island. But the rain has been infrequent, with little impact on play — until Saturday.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/GOLF1/GOLF1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/GOLF1/GOLF1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/GOLF1/GOLF1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/GOLF1/GOLF1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/GOLF1/GOLF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/GOLF1/GOLF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/GOLF1/GOLF1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'McIlroy and Singh Share Lead as Heavy Rain Stops Play', 'kicker': 'P.G.A. Championship', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heavy Rain Arrives, Play Stops, and McIlroy and Singh Share the Lead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIlroy, Rory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PGA Championship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singh, Vijay', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T01:33:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3765526f-a20e-5a2c-b6bf-cb4b6b522c2c', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3765526f-a20e-5a2c-b6bf-cb4b6b522c2c'}, {'abstract': 'Abortion providers have noticed more and more women crossing the border to buy misoprostol, to be used as abortion pills, at Mexican pharmacies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/us/looking-to-mexico-for-an-alternative-to-the-abortion-clinic.html', 'snippet': 'Abortion providers have noticed more and more women crossing the border to buy misoprostol, to be used as abortion pills, at Mexican pharmacies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MCALLEN — In this Roman Catholic stronghold, where abortion is deeply stigmatized, reproductive health providers tell stories of women going to pharmacies across the border in Mexico, in search of a drug they hope will terminate unwanted pregnancies. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/TTPILL-01/TTPILL-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/us/TTPILL-01/TTPILL-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/TTPILL-01/TTPILL-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/TTPILL-01/TTPILL-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1295, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/TTPILL-01/TTPILL-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/us/TTPILL-01/TTPILL-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/TTPILL-01/TTPILL-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking to Mexico for an Alternative to Abortion Clinics', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking to Mexico for an Alternative to Abortion Clinics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T02:17:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thanh Tan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thanh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6848d535-d9af-5ddf-952a-ef338c14e9ee', 'word_count': 1052, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6848d535-d9af-5ddf-952a-ef338c14e9ee'}, {'abstract': 'Jets safety Eric Smith could miss the rest of the preseason after spraining a ligament in his left knee while covering a punt during the team’s 17-6 loss to Cincinnati on Friday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/sports/football/knee-injury-sidelines-jets-safety-eric-smith.html', 'snippet': 'Jets safety Eric Smith could miss the rest of the preseason after spraining a ligament in his left knee while covering a punt during the team’s 17-6 loss to Cincinnati on Friday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Safety Eric Smith, an integral member of the Jets’ secondary and a valuable contributor on special teams, could miss the rest of the preseason after spraining the medial collateral ligament in his left knee while covering a punt during the team’s 17-6 loss to Cincinnati on Friday night. The extent of Smith’s injury has not been announced by the team, but a football official with knowledge of his magnetic resonance imaging results confirmed it. Smith could return for the Sept. 9 season opener against Buffalo. ¶ The police in Davie, Fla., said that Dolphins receiver Chad Johnson had been arrested on a domestic violence charge, accused of head-butting his newlywed wife during an argument in front of their home. Johnson’s wife, Evelyn Lozada, is on the reality show “Basketball Wives.” Johnson changed his last name back from Ochocinco after his wedding to Lozada. (AP)', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knee Injury Sidelines Jets Safety', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Pro Football', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knee Injury Sidelines Jets Safety', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Eric', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T02:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/39c5a492-7f60-5983-89c3-222003142cba', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39c5a492-7f60-5983-89c3-222003142cba'}, {'abstract': 'As throngs of police officers drew their weapons and pursued a man with a large knife down 7th Avenue and then shot him to death, many bystanders stopped to watch, record video and take photos.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/police-shoot-man-near-times-square-and-tourists-reach-for-cameras/', 'snippet': 'As throngs of police officers drew their weapons and pursued a man with a large knife down 7th Avenue and then shot him to death, many bystanders stopped to watch, record video and take photos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The typical afternoon furor in Times Square became something more menacing on Saturday as throngs of police officers drew their weapons and pursued a man with a large knife down Seventh Avenue and then shot him to death. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Shoot Man in Midtown, and Tourists Reach for Cameras', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Times Square and 42nd Street (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T02:31:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz and Aaron Edwards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Edwards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8072286f-9586-57ff-90f4-079f2a99a469', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8072286f-9586-57ff-90f4-079f2a99a469'}, {'abstract': 'The Dwyer, which has attracted 75,000 visitors to visual art exhibitions, writers’ workshops, and music and theater performances — all free or low-cost — has run into major financial problems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/11/arts/dwyer-cultural-center-in-harlem-tries-to-stay-afloat.html', 'snippet': 'The Dwyer, which has attracted 75,000 visitors to visual art exhibitions, writers’ workshops, and music and theater performances — all free or low-cost — has run into major financial problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stomping and twisting, homeless mothers and children and young professionals were all part of the mix at the Dwyer Cultural Center in Harlem one recent Saturday, as they tried to master the intricacies of swing dancing. But scenes like this have been few and far between lately. The Dwyer, which since opening three years ago has attracted 75,000 visitors to visual art exhibitions, readings, writers’ workshops, children’s educational programs and music and theater performances — all free or low-cost — has run into major financial problems. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/11DWYER/11DWYER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/11DWYER/11DWYER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/11DWYER/11DWYER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/11DWYER/11DWYER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/11/arts/11DWYER/11DWYER-thumbLarge.jpg',