ge': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/JP-DYING/JP-DYING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/us/JP-DYING/JP-DYING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/JP-DYING/JP-DYING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/JP-DYING/JP-DYING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1405, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/JP-DYING/JP-DYING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/us/JP-DYING/JP-DYING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/JP-DYING/JP-DYING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Ill Doctor, a Surprise Reflection of Who Picks Assisted Suicide', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Ill Doctor, a Surprise Reflection of Who Picks Assisted Suicide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euthanasia and Assisted Suicide', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T02:47:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Hafner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hafner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c393d0d-ab6b-5887-8e08-cedb8e4d9f71', 'word_count': 1450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c393d0d-ab6b-5887-8e08-cedb8e4d9f71'}, {'abstract': 'For school officials and policy makers grappling with rising enrollment and decreased state revenue, the primary target is the cost of personnel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/us/texas-schools-zero-in-on-employee-numbers.html', 'snippet': 'For school officials and policy makers grappling with rising enrollment and decreased state revenue, the primary target is the cost of personnel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Texas lawmakers took up the issue of how to make fewer dollars stretch further in public schools during the 2011 legislative session, “efficiency” was a commonly uttered word. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Hard Times, Schools Zero In on Employees', 'kicker': 'Texas Tribune | Inside the Numbers', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Hard Times, Schools Zero In On Employees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T02:55:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Morgan Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Morgan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16f70af4-a4f7-599f-a92c-458dcce13275', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16f70af4-a4f7-599f-a92c-458dcce13275'}, {'abstract': 'The cards may be stacked against Democrats, but it’s only a matter of when, not if, the political pendulum will swing back.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/us/in-gop-dominated-texas-democrats-wait-for-their-opening.html', 'snippet': 'The cards may be stacked against Democrats, but it’s only a matter of when, not if, the political pendulum will swing back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Being a Democrat in a Texas election is like being the fastest sprinter outside of Jamaica or the best beach volleyball team outside of the United States. Unless something odd happens, your medal will be silver or bronze.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a G.O.P.-Dominated State, Democrats Wait for Their Opening', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a G.O.P.-Dominated State, Democrats Wait for Their Opening', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T02:59:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Ramsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/428698b1-020e-52ec-af01-c4c796514410', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/428698b1-020e-52ec-af01-c4c796514410'}, {'abstract': 'Some of Houston’s best-known chefs are regulars in the city’s Chinatown restaurants and offer their recommendations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/us/star-houston-chefs-favorite-chinatown-restaurants-and-dishes.html', 'snippet': 'Some of Houston’s best-known chefs are regulars in the city’s Chinatown restaurants and offer their recommendations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mention Chinatown to Texans, and many will think first of New York or San Francisco, where traditional Chinese street signs, bumpy durian fruits and bamboo baskets filled with dumplings have inspired countless Instagrams. While the Chinatowns in those cities have long been tourist destinations, a similar corridor in Houston receives less recognition, even from local residents, a surprising fact considering that Houston’s New Chinatown is large (almost six square miles) and centered on a busy stretch of Bellaire Boulevard. “Many people have lived in Houston all of their lives and have never been here,” said Christy Chang, who gives weekly tours of the area with her company, Asian Heritage Discovery. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/TTCULTURE/TTCULTURE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/12/us/TTCULTURE/TTCULTURE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/TTCULTURE/TTCULTURE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/TTCULTURE/TTCULTURE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/TTCULTURE/TTCULTURE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/us/TTCULTURE/TTCULTURE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/us/TTCULTURE/TTCULTURE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What the Star Chefs Love in Houston’s Chinatown', 'kicker': 'Texas Monthly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What the Star Chefs Love in Houston’s Chinatown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T03:04:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stirling Kelso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stirling', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kelso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ace55ec-e283-5b5e-ad5f-975e7f2c6c89', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ace55ec-e283-5b5e-ad5f-975e7f2c6c89'}, {'abstract': 'Left-handed pitcher Johan Santana allowed eight runs in one and a third innings in his return from three weeks on the disabled list. The Mets’ loss at Citi Field was its sixth in eight games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/sports/baseball/braves-shell-mets-as-johan-santana-makes-early-exit.html', 'snippet': 'Left-handed pitcher Johan Santana allowed eight runs in one and a third innings in his return from three weeks on the disabled list. The Mets’ loss at Citi Field was its sixth in eight games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The much-anticipated return of Johan Santana began with the expectation that three weeks on the disabled list with a sprained ankle had helped rest his fatigued left arm.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/mets/mets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 823, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/mets/mets-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1952, 'width': 1569, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/mets/mets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/mets/mets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/sports/mets/mets-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'About as Bad as It Gets for Santana in His Return', 'kicker': 'Braves 9, Mets 3', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'About as Bad as It Gets for Santana in His Return', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santana, Johan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', '