arly reaction to Representative Paul Ryan’s selection as Mitt Romney’s running mate was muted. One commentator said Mr. Ryan “ticks most boxes” for the Republican candidate, while...', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The official Chinese news agency and state-run media outlets on the mainland offered little commentary on the selection of Representative Paul D. Ryan as the running mate of Mitt Romney, the presumptive Republican presidential nominee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Asia, So Far, Paul Ryan Remains Out of Focus', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xinhua', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T04:19:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7736d1e-a5d6-5b13-bcc1-60b9c6cae035', 'word_count': 1052, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7736d1e-a5d6-5b13-bcc1-60b9c6cae035'}, {'abstract': 'After he found out he had cancer, the groom asked the bride if she would stay with him. She said, “Why would I leave?”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/fashion/weddings/angela-sclafani-and-michael-olexa-vows.html', 'snippet': 'After he found out he had cancer, the groom asked the bri