ich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/04b6fc18-ac67-5e5b-9f46-6c777b2ece99', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/04b6fc18-ac67-5e5b-9f46-6c777b2ece99'}, {'abstract': 'Drugs and drama, world records, an eccentric opening, historic breakthroughs, women boxers, a man with no legs. Quite an Olympics. What thrilled you? Made you weepy? What was rubbish? Let us know.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/london-2012-a-gold-medal-or-an-also-ran/', 'snippet': 'Drugs and drama, world records, an eccentric opening, historic breakthroughs, women boxers, a man with no legs. Quite an Olympics. What thrilled you? Made you weepy? What was rubbish? Let us know.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were drugs, of course there were — a slew of positive tests and expulsions, in weight lifting and race walking, in gymnastics and judo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/blogs/jess-rdv/jess-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/12/blogs/jess-rdv/jess-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'London 2012: A Gold Medal, or An Also-Ran?', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaherkani, Wojdan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Olympic Committee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T08:20:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f2d56a0-e4f2-5370-b605-795678e42048', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f2d56a0-e4f2-5370-b605-795678e42048'}, {'abstract': 'While there are still some big events on Sunday, the final day of competition, it is also time to look back on the London Olympics. Members of The Times staff select their favorite athletes and stories of the Summer Games.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/what-were-watching-on-final-day-time-to-reflect/', 'snippet': 'While there are still some big events on Sunday, the final day of competition, it is also time to look back on the London Olympics. Members of The Times staff select their favorite athletes and stories of the Summer Games.', 'lead_paragraph': "(function($){var data = chameleonData;var ticker = new NYTD.NYTMM.NewsTicker($('#nytmm_embed_875'), data);})(jQuery||NYTD.jQuery);", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Watching: On Final Day, Time to Reflect', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolt, Usain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T09:40:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87ed47fb-6f74-595a-9962-7d3327fae259', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87ed47fb-6f74-595a-9962-7d3327fae259'}, {'abstract': 'The Browns are easily the least-talented team in the A.F.C. North. The endless rebuilding continues in Cleveland.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/cleveland-browns-2012-n-f-l-season-preview/', 'snippet': 'The Browns are easily the least-talented team in the A.F.C. North. The endless rebuilding continues in Cleveland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s Year 14 of the Cleveland Browns’ rebuilding project. Or Year 3 of their third or fourth rebuilding project – however you want to look at it (averting your gaze would be understandable). The Browns finished 4-12 last season, the third straight year, and ninth time since their reinstatement in 1999, that they have lost at least 11 games. They did it primarily with bad offense (13.6 points per game, ranked third worst), though their defense was nowhere near as good as its No. 5 scoring ranking suggested.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cleveland Browns, 2012 N.F.L. Season Preview', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Browns', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T10:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f1a20d3-b439-5a3b-9525-b0000a28f7ba', 'word_count': 2834, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f1a20d3-b439-5a3b-9525-b0000a28f7ba'}, {'abstract': 'Equality in the sports arena means an equal opportunity and a level playing field. But ultimately, sports are competitive and the pecking order should be reflected on the podium.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/silver-and-bronze-are-not-equal/', 'snippet': 'Equality in the sports arena means an equal opportunity and a level playing field. But ultimately, sports are competitive and the pecking order should be reflected on the podium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Watching the Olympics over the past two weeks, I noticed something odd about the heights of the podiums during the awards ceremonies. While the podium on which the gold medal winner stands is — as expected — the highest, the heights of the silver and bronze podiums are the same. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Silver and Bronze Are Not Equal', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T10:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ranjani Iyer Mohanty', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ranjani', 'middlename': 'Iyer', 'lastname': 'Mohanty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d960fde3-c99d-5bd8-b529-3a725e04d7ef', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d960fde3-c99d-5bd8-b529-3a725e04d7ef'}, {'abstract': 'What happened after I convinced myself that staying home to badger my child 24/7 would improve his chances in life: I realized my energies could be better spent in not driving him nuts.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/how-not-to-be-a-helicopter-parent-volunteer/', 'snippet': 'What happened after I convinced myself that staying home to badger my child 24/7 would improve his chances in life: I realized my energies could be better spent in not driving him nuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Years ago, when one of my children was partying too much in high school, and college applications were looming, I quit my job teaching at a university and began working full time at home. In truth, I had been teaching college students on and off for 25 years, and I was at the end of my pedagogical rope. But I also convinced myself that staying home to badger my child 24/7 would improve his chances in life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Not to Be a Helicopter Parent: Volunteer', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levine, Madeline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Children's Defense Fund", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T11:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Blake', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blake', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5b00fc7-f9ee-5d47-9397-0c175cf6ffd0', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5b00fc7-f9ee-5d47-9397-0c175cf6ffd0'}, {'abstract': 'Top magazine and long-form articles this week.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/newswallah-long-reads-edition-38/', 'snippet': 'Top magazine and long-form articles this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Open magazine ran an Independence Day special on “Radical Indians” this week. Particularly interesting is a dissection of the work of Arundhati Roy, the writer and activist, whom the magazine labels “the Queen of Exaggeration.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Long Reads Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T11:25:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sruthi Gottipati', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sruthi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gottipati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a9ecb55-ee04-5ec4-90e4-0012614c347b', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a9ecb55-ee04-5ec4-90e4-0012614c347b'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen Kiprotich’s victory in the marathon gave Uganda its first gold medal at the London Games and its second ever. Abel Kirui of Kenya won silver and his countryman Wilson Kipsang took bronze.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/sports/olympics/ugandan-kiprotich-surges-past-2-kenyans-to-win-marathon-gold.html', 'snippet': 'Stephen Kiprotich’s victory in the marathon gave Uganda its first gold medal at the London Games and its second ever. Abel Kirui of Kenya won silver and his countryman Wilson Kipsang took bronze.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The East Africans were heavily favored to win the Olympic marathon Sunday, but they happened to be Kenyans and Ethiopians, not a Ugandan named Stephen Kiprotich. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/sports/13marathon1/13marathon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'artic