ch, Stephen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T13:01:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88d7fbd0-2ae2-5eef-951f-8ff6f13cad22', 'word_count': 881, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88d7fbd0-2ae2-5eef-951f-8ff6f13cad22'}, {'abstract': 'The United States men’s basketball defeated Spain to win the gold medal at the London Olympics.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/live-coverage-of-the-u-s-spain-mens-basketball-game/', 'snippet': 'The United States men’s basketball defeated Spain to win the gold medal at the London Olympics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The journey to the gold medal game for the United States men’s national basketball team started with a simple question to Kobe Bryant about whether the current team could beat the Dream Team from 1992.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Highlights and Analysis From the Men’s Basketball Title Game', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryant, Kobe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chandler, Tyson', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gasol, Marc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gasol, Pau', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibaka, Serge', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T13:32:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8f6dd4e-7ece-5228-bd79-46ce82b80efa', 'word_count': 2675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8f6dd4e-7ece-5228-bd79-46ce82b80efa'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Ryan’s ascendency to No. 2 spot on the Republican ticket is a signal event for a movement that counts him as one of their own. If Mitt Romney wins in November, a Tea Party favorite will be a heartbeat from the Oval Office.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/ryan-brings-the-tea-party-to-the-ticket/', 'snippet': 'Paul Ryan’s ascendency to No. 2 spot on the Republican ticket is a signal event for a movement that counts him as one of their own. If Mitt Romney wins in November, a Tea Party favorite will be a heartbeat from the Oval Office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For two years, Tea Party lawmakers in the House have been the stubborn barbarians at the gate, strong-arming their often reluctant Republican colleagues by refusing to compromise on spending, taxes, debt or social policy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryan Brings the Tea Party to the Ticket', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Club for Growth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T13:36:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41d3024c-4c4d-57c7-bd82-d66f4c8c8a47', 'word_count': 930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41d3024c-4c4d-57c7-bd82-d66f4c8c8a47'}, {'abstract': 'Some Yoga studio operators say they are feeling under siege from government agencies trying to apply regulations on their businesses.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/government-agencies-are-taking-aim-at-yoga-studios-operators-say/', 'snippet': 'Some Yoga studio operators say they are feeling under siege from government agencies trying to apply regulations on their businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three years ago, yoga studios in New York waged a spirited and successful campaign to fend off a proposed state government regulation that some studios said would have led to their demise.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Government Agencies Targeting Yoga Studios, Some Owners Say', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yoga Studios Preparing For New Fight With City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yoga', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'West, Alison', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buildings Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labor Department (NYS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T14:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fcc56f9-83dc-5030-af48-cdb2587922bf', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fcc56f9-83dc-5030-af48-cdb2587922bf'}, {'abstract': 'Relief workers saved more than 200 people from the rubble of dozens of villages that were destroyed after two earthquakes struck Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/world/middleeast/scores-dead-in-iran-quake.html', 'snippet': 'Relief workers saved more than 200 people from the rubble of dozens of villages that were destroyed after two earthquakes struck Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Iranian relief workers saved more than 200 people from the rubble of dozens of villages destroyed when two powerful earthquakes struck Saturday in a wide area north of the city of Tabriz, an Iranian official said Sunday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/world/IRAN-1/IRAN-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/world/IRAN-1/IRAN-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '200 Rescued in Iran After Quakes; Death Toll Rises to 300', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '200 Rescued in Iran Aft