nd in a circular motion, followed by the index and middle fingers.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/sports/13yankees-2/13yankees-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/sports/13yankees-2/13yankees-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1623, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/sports/13yankees-2/13yankees-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/13/sports/13yankees-2/13yankees-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/sports/13yankees-2/13yankees-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yanks’ Rally Falls Short as Hughes Loses Grip', 'kicker': 'Blue Jays 10, Yankees 7', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yanks’ Rally Falls Short As Hughes Loses Grip', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Blue Jays', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Rajai', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T20:18:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39466324-83fb-557c-8e15-48695509b3f3', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39466324-83fb-557c-8e15-48695509b3f3'}, {'abstract': 'The Public Theater’s Mobile Shakespeare Unit is back home with its abbreviated production of “Richard III,” with a nine-person cast that stars Ron Cephas Jones.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/theater/reviews/richard-iii-with-ron-cephas-jones-at-the-public-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The Public Theater’s Mobile Shakespeare Unit is back home with its abbreviated production of “Richard III,” with a nine-person cast that stars Ron Cephas Jones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No character in Shakespeare is as hungry for power as Richard III. And it’s hard to think of an actor with a naturally hungrier look than Ron Cephas Jones, the tall, beanpole-thin, snakelike actor who portrays the title character in the production of “Richard III” from the Public Theater’s new Mobile Shakespeare Unit. This scaled-down staging has been presented at prisons, homeless shelters and other sites in underserved neighborhoods before returning to the company’s home base on Astor Place.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/arts/richard/richard-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 708, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/arts/richard/richard-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1415, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/arts/richard/richard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/13/arts/richard/richard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/arts/richard/richard-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Royal Power Player Who Sprints to the Throne', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Royal Power Player Who Sprints to the Throne', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Ron Cephas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T20:24:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a91a4cf3-52e2-51bc-bca4-5a90cdb48829', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a91a4cf3-52e2-51bc-bca4-5a90cdb48829'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Way the World Works,” a collection of essays from the last 15 years, Nicholson Baker caroms among topics as diverse as video games and World War II pacifism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/books/nicholson-baker-the-way-the-world-works.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Way the World Works,” a collection of essays from the last 15 years, Nicholson Baker caroms among topics as diverse as video games and World War II pacifism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the final essay of this hodge-podgy collection, Nicholson Baker — best known for his microscopically detailed accounts of daily life, his love of the minute, the specific, the Seinfeld-ian small — notes that he’d like to write a book for children and adults called “The Way the World Works,” a book that would explain “everything about history, beauty, wickedness, invention, the meaning of life,” the “whole unseemly, bulging ball of wax.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/arts/jpbook/jpbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1002, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/arts/jpbook/jpbook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2003, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/13/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pick a Topic, Any Topic. He Did.', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pick a Topic, Any Topic. He Did.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Nicholson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T20:34:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dc83e2f-57b9-5eba-ad08-d68bc5880d9a', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dc83e2f-57b9-5eba-ad08-d68bc5880d9a'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney sought to capitalize on conservative enthusiasm for his vice-presidential choice without having to defend all of Representative Paul D. Ryan’s positions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/us/politics/with-gop-ticket-complete-crowds-swell.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney sought to capitalize on conservative enthusiasm for his vice-presidential choice without having to defend all of Representative Paul D. Ryan’s positions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WAUKESHA, Wis. — Democrats moved aggressively on Sunday to wrap Mitt Romney in the politically charged details of budget-cutting proposals championed by his new running mate, Representative Paul D. Ryan, as Mr. Romney sought to capitalize on conservative enthusiasm for his choice without having to defend every element of Mr. Ryan’s positions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/us/13campaign-1/13campaign-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/13/us/13campaign-1/13campaign-1-arti