 'The Civilians theater company will assemble an evening of performance material inspired by more than 150 interviews with activists associated with the Occupy movement.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/12/occupy-wall-street-inspires-a-show/', 'snippet': 'The Civilians theater company will assemble an evening of performance material inspired by more than 150 interviews with activists associated with the Occupy movement.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In commemoration of the one-year anniversary of the Occupy Wall Street movement, the Civilians theater company will assemble an evening of performance material inspired by more than 150 interviews with activists associated with the Occupy movement that have been conducted over the last year. A cabaret, called “Let Me Ascertain You: Occupy #S17,” is to feature monologues and songs created by Civilians artists from their interviews. It will run for one night, Sept. 17, at Joe’s Pub at the Public Theater. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Occupy Wall Street Inspires a Show', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Occupy Wall Street Inspires a Show', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cosson, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Civilians, The (Theater Co)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T21:38:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b393f15-d5b6-571a-b199-ba1509a99459', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b393f15-d5b6-571a-b199-ba1509a99459'}, {'abstract': 'The comedian has reached an agreement with Henry Holt & Company to publish a memoir covering over four decades of his life and featuring his thoughts on growing older, The Associated Press reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/books/a-memoir-to-come-from-billy-crystal.html', 'snippet': 'The comedian has reached an agreement with Henry Holt & Company to publish a memoir covering over four decades of his life and featuring his thoughts on growing older, The Associated Press reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The comedian Billy Crystal has reached an agreement with Henry Holt & Company to publish a memoir covering over four decades of his life and featuring his thoughts on growing older, The Associated Press reported. Financial terms for the book were not disclosed, but it was reported that the deal could be worth about $4 million. Mr. Crystal, who will turn 65 next year, also hopes the book will translate to the stage in a similar fashion to his previous memoir, “700 Sundays,” which was adapted into a one-man play in 2004 and won a Tony Award in 2005 for Special Theatrical Event.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Memoir to Come From Billy Crystal', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Memoir to Come From Billy Crystal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crystal, Billy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-12T21:40:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'r