more will lose their homes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The One Housing Solution Left: Mass Mortgage Refinancing', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The One Housing Solution Left: Mass Mortgage Refinancing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeowner Affordability and Stability Plan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkley, Jeffrey A (1956- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Housing Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeMarco, Edward J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-13T01:01:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph E. Stiglitz and Mark Zandi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Stiglitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zandi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1d1a613-bc4b-5400-9c00-7e855110be3f', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1d1a613-bc4b-5400-9c00-7e855110be3f'}, {'abstract': 'While it is not uncommon for a presidential candidate to know his opponent’s No. 2 better, the history between President Obama and Paul Ryan sets up an especially intriguing showdown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/