'nyt://article/841f71c5-f151-56d7-9a52-a9055d931cea'}, {'abstract': 'A string of fatal attacks by great white sharks has Australian officials considering removing the “apex predator” from the country’s list of protected species. Could shark hunting make a comeback? If so, Australia might need a bigger boat.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/should-great-white-sharks-remain-protected/', 'snippet': 'A string of fatal attacks by great white sharks has Australian officials considering removing the “apex predator” from the country’s list of protected species. Could shark hunting make a comeback? If so, Australia might need a bigger boat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — It has been a month since the shark took Ben Linden.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/blogs/shark-rdv/shark-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/blogs/shark-rdv/shark-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1354, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Should Great White Sharks Remain Protected?', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sharks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-13T04:44:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/193ccaf4-65d8-5ab8-9887-6cb621b64b7a', 'word_count': 1050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/193ccaf4-65d8-5ab8-9887-6cb621b64b7a'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Paul D. Ryan’s first outing alone as the Republican vice-presidential candidate he has chosen a particularly exposed high-wire appearance: a political soapbox at the Iowa State Fair.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/for-ryans-first-solo-outing-as-candidate-a-soapbox-appearance-at-the-iowa-state-fair/', 'snippet': 'Representative Paul D. Ryan’s first outing alone as the Republican vice-presidential candidate he has chosen a particularly exposed high-wire appearance: a political soapbox at the Iowa State Fair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — Representative Paul D. Ryan is going solo, and for his first outing alone as the Republican vice-presidential candidate he has chosen a particularly exposed high-wire appearance: a political soapbox at the Iowa State Fair.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Ryan’s First Solo Outing as Candidate, a Soapbox Appearance at the Iowa State Fair', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State and County Fairs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-13T04:57:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/542f5903-8e4f-591d-b62e-0304bdc1309c', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/542f5903-8e4f-591d-b62e-0304bdc1309c'}, {'abstract': 'After his father died, Paul D. Ryan formed a self-reliance that would shape his worldview and one day capture the imagination of Mitt Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/us/politics/family-faith-and-politics-describe-life-of-paul-ryan.html', 'snippet': 'After his father died, Paul D. Ryan formed a self-reliance that would shape his worldview and one day capture the imagination of Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JANESVILLE, Wis. — Representative Paul D. Ryan’s childhood home here was not overtly partisan. His parents were enthusiastic supporters of Representative Les Aspin, a Democrat, yet adored President Ronald Reagan from their glimpses of him on the evening news. But the death of his father when Mr. Ryan was only 16 punctured his life of math tests and bike riding, and in that fissure, the seeds of his worldview were planted.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/us/politics/13ryan_cnd/13ryan_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/13/us/politics/13ryan_cnd/13ryan_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/us/politics/13ryan_cnd/13ryan_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/13/us/politics/13ryan_cnd/13ryan_cnd-superJum