one of the authors of a study on women’s political representation and its effect on crime in India. As the government reserves for women a third of all seats in local government institutions like the village council, the researchers sought to find out whether having female political leaders at the local level would have a positive effect on women. Instead, they found that the reported number of crimes against women rose. Ms. Mani explained in an e-mail interview with India Ink why that’s not bad news.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With: Social Scientist Anandi Mani', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-13T08:20:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sruthi Gottipati', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sruthi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gottipati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a0e9781-0979-525b-a7e2-bc63c40ff2de', 'word_count': 1127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a0e9781-0979-525b-a7e2-bc63c40ff2de'}, {'abstract': 'Today’s question is about Derek Jeter and the number of games he will need to play for the Yankees to surpass the record held by Carl Yastrzemski for most games played for one team.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/test-yourself-math-aug-13-2012/', 'snippet': 'Today’s question is about Derek Jeter and the number of games he will need to play for the Yankees to surpass the record held by Carl Yastrzemski for most games played for one team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Test your math skills with this question created by Scott Matthews at Math for America from the article “Another Landmark for Jeter.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': []