0', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87b53b76-1df3-5bc7-8702-49311047bb5a', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87b53b76-1df3-5bc7-8702-49311047bb5a'}, {'abstract': 'At least two Ugandan military helicopters, key assets in a push against militants in Somalia, “lost communication” somewhere in Kenyan airspace and may have crashed, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/world/africa/ugandan-copters-en-route-to-battle-shabab-disappear-over-kenya.html', 'snippet': 'At least two Ugandan military helicopters, key assets in a push against militants in Somalia, “lost communication” somewhere in Kenyan airspace and may have crashed, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — At least two Ugandan military helicopters, crucial assets in a push against militants in Somalia, have vanished over Kenya, officials in Nairobi said on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ugandan Copters, en Route to Battle Shabab, Disappear Over Kenya', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ugandan Copters, En Route to Battle Shabab, Disappear Over Kenya', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Helicopters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-13T09:39:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69bd68cb-eee9-5172-b370-74ca0bb57402', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69bd68cb-eee9-5172-b370-74ca0bb57402'}, {'abstract': 'It’s hard to see the Bengals’ offense taking the type of leap that’s needed to overtake the Ravens or the Steelers in the A.F.C. North.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/cincinnati-bengals-2012-n-f-l-season-preview/', 'snippet': 'It’s hard to see the Bengals’ offense taking the type of leap that’s needed to overtake the Ravens or the Steelers in the A.F.C. North.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Temper any optimism you might have for the Cincinnati Bengals with a healthy sprinkle of caution. Yes, this is a relatively young team coming off a surprising postseason appearance. But we’ve seen this before. In 2005 the Bengals made the postseason only to lose in the wild-card round and then finish 8-8, 7-9 and 4-11-1 the next three years. In 2009, they surprisingly broke through with another wild-card appearance, only to lose that game and 12 more the following season. The Bengals have not had back-to-back playoff seasons in 30 years. They have not won a playoff game in 22 years — the N.F.L.’s longest current drought.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cincinnati Bengals, 2012 N.F.L. Season Preview', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cincinnati Bengals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-13T10:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_na