tigations of Wall Street for potential wrongdoing that contributed to the financial crisis in 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/is-that-it-for-financial-crisis-cases/', 'snippet': 'The disclosures that the Justice Department has closed an investigation of Goldman Sachs and that the Securities and Exchange Commission has decided not to pursue a civil fraud case may turn out to be the denouement of the government’s investigati...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week turned out to be a good one for Goldman Sachs. The Justice Department closed a criminal investigation of the firm and its chief executive, Lloyd C. Blankfein, and the firm disclosed that the Securities and Exchange Commission had decided not to pursue a civil fraud case related to a subprime mortgage deal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is That It for Financial Crisis Cases?', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collateralized Debt Obligations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levin, Carl M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Permanent Subcommittee on Investigations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-13T15:22:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Hennin