', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2baf01a1-4e33-5c1a-9f36-f9737dc14419', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2baf01a1-4e33-5c1a-9f36-f9737dc14419'}, {'abstract': 'Can you save three sheep from a pack of wolves?', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/numberplay-wolves/', 'snippet': 'Can you save three sheep from a pack of wolves?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Special announcement! Numberplay’s Gary Antonick will be on vacation for several weeks. The next Numberplay post will appear on Monday, Sept. 10.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay: Wolves and Sheep', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-13T16:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4acc20a0-fc62-5d0a-be04-d544a19da979', 'word_count': 1706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4acc20a0-fc62-5d0a-be04-d544a19da979'}, {'abstract': 'A new study suggests that under natural conditions, the climate in the earth’s two hemispheres were out of step in past eras. Today, mountain ice is retreating worldwide, suggesting that human-produced greenhouse gases could be at work.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/climate-insight-from-a-magical-mountain-range/', 'snippet': 'A new study suggests that under natural conditions, the climate in the earth’s two hemispheres were out of step in past eras. Today, mountain ice is retreating worldwide, suggesting that human-produced greenhouse gases could be at work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As many people know, human civilization arose during a particularly stable period in the history of the earth – the Holocene, encompassing the 12,000 years since the end of the last ice age. It may have been no accident that civilization burst forth during an era when ice had retreated from some of the most favorable land and when climate, sea level and other conditions had settled down after the turbulence of the ice age. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Climate Insight From a Magical Mountain Range', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glaciers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mountains', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putnam, Aaron E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature Geoscience (Journal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Zealand', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-13T16:05:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1f6c390-5bd9-54d3-ac07-5c06a7e090f5', 'word_count': 1084, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1f6c390-5bd9-54d3-ac07-5c06a7e090f5'}, {'abstract': 'Paolo Gabriele, the butler, is charged with aggravated theft and accused of taking and then leaking documents from the pope’s private apartment that raised allegations of corruption at the Vatican.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/world/europe/vatican-judge-indicts-popes-butler-in-leak-case.html', 'snippet': 'Paolo Gabriele, the butler, is charged with aggravated theft and accused of taking and then leaking documents from the pope’s private apartment that raised allegations of corruption at the Vatican.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A judge at the Vatican on Monday ordered the former butler of Pope Benedict XVI to stand trial on charges of taking and then leaking documents from the pope’s private apartment that raised allegations of corruption at the Vatican. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/22/world/vatican/vatican-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/22/world/vatican/vatican-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1201, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/22/world/vatican/vatican-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/22/world/vatican/vatican-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/22/world/vatican/vatican-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pope’s Butler Indicted in Vatican Leak Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pope’s Butler Indicted in Vatican Leak Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gabriele, Paolo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vatican City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-13T16:06:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell and Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae60ad66-f727-5e06-a0b0-7ca955f1debf', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae60ad66-f727-5e06-a0b0-7ca955f1debf'}, {'abstract': 'The HuffPost Live online network is one of the most ambitious attempts yet to rethink what TV should look and feel like when streamed over the Internet. For starters, viewers are encouraged to join in using their webcams.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/huffington-post-begins-an-online-tv-network/', 'snippet': 'The HuffPost Live online network is one of the most ambitious attempts yet to rethink what TV should look and feel like when streamed over the Internet. For starters, viewers are encouraged to join in using their webcams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Huffington Post on Monday began what it hopes will be a never-ending news talk show on the Internet, HuffPost Live.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': []