t': 'President Gurbanguly Berdymukhammedov has ordered the release of 1,327 convicts to observe the end of the Muslim holy month of Ramadan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/world/asia/turkmenistan-convicts-pardoned.html', 'snippet': 'President Gurbanguly Berdymukhammedov has ordered the release of 1,327 convicts to observe the end of the Muslim holy month of Ramadan.', 'lead_paragraph': ' President Gurbanguly Berdymukhammedov has ordered the release of 1,327 convicts to observe the end of the Muslim holy month of Ramadan. It is the latest in a series of mass pardons set to coincide with national holidays in the isolated former Soviet republic. Turkmen state media reported on Monday that 44 foreigners would be among those pardoned. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkmenistan: Convicts Pardoned', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turkmenistan: Convicts Pardoned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berdymukhammedov, Gurbanguly', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkmenistan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T00:49:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b701ba1-6e00-55d5-84b2-99f67fdcfd72', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b701b