': {'main': 'Fatal Fall From Palisades Raises Concerns on Safety', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fatal Fall From Palisades Raises Concerns on Safety', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Palisades Interstate Park', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Falls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T02:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Zernike', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zernike', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7af06f0d-2612-5fb7-9504-f552d5feb230', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7af06f0d-2612-5fb7-9504-f552d5feb230'}, {'abstract': 'A chance for some mid-summer traveling with Ian Livengood.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/summer-hideaways/', 'snippet': 'A chance for some mid-summer traveling with Ian Livengood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY’S PUZZLE — The epitaph that Thomas Jefferson wrote for himself lists precisely three accomplishments: that he authored the Declaration of Independence and the Virginia Statute of Religious Freedom and that he founded the University of Virginia. (Not one to pad a résumé, Jefferson refrained from mentioning, you know, his presidency.) If you knew this, you probably had no trouble filling in 46 Across, which referred to the establishment of UVA. It’s just one of many clues in today’s Ian Livengood-constructed puzzle that seems perfectly suited for mid-August: tossed in alongside vacation destinations in the theme, there are a couple of nagging reminders of school.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Hideaways', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T02:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Gaffney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gaffney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f11f72b8-1be7-58f9-8e9c-88e96393b0be', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f11f72b8-1be7-58f9-8e9c-88e96393b0be'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on August 14, 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/pageoneplus/corrections-august-14-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on August 14, 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: August 14, 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T02:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/c799465d-ab54-524a-8011-7056ed01259e', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c799465d-ab54-524a-8011-7056ed01259e'}, {'abstract': 'Thomas Caffall opened fire on police officers after a constable tried to serve an eviction notice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/us/3-including-gunman-are-killed-in-shooting-near-texas-am.html', 'snippet': 'Thomas Caffall opened fire on police officers after a constable tried to serve an eviction notice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLLEGE STATION, Tex. — A gunman opened fire on police officers near the Texas A&M University campus shortly after noon on Monday, killing at least two people, including a local constable, and wounding four others, the police said. The gunman, who was shot by officers, died after he was taken into custody.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/14/us/14shooting_span/14shooting_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/14/us/14shooting_span/14shooting_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/14/us/14shooting_span/14shooting_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/14/us/14shooting_span/14shooting_span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1417, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '3 Dead, Including Gunman, in Shooting Near Texas A&M', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '3, Including Gunman, Are Killed in Shooting Near Texas A&M', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caffall, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas A&M University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'College Station (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T02:01:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez and Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18951e17-37c2-5955-9f62-098de5899a99', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18951e17-37c2-5955-9f62-098de5899a99'}, {'abstract': 'A consultant’s analysis of the New York City Housing Authority says the authority is not organized to spend federal dollars wisely or efficiently. It needs to be fixed as much as leaky plumbing does.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/opinion/repair-new-york-citys-housing-issues.html', 'snippet': 'A consultant’s analysis of the New York City Housing Authority says the authority is not organized to spend federal dollars wisely or efficiently. It needs to be fixed as much as leaky plumbing does.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 650,000 people live in housing that is controlled or subsidized by the New York City Housing Authority. Too many have to wait for months for needed repairs to leaking plumbing and other problems. In an estimated 10,000 apartments, repairs are not scheduled until 2014. This is clearly unacceptable. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Repair New York City’s Housing Issues', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Repair New York City’s Ho