', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1ac9d50-2791-583b-bcad-5bc63635e60a', 'word_count': 1195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1ac9d50-2791-583b-bcad-5bc63635e60a'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Ryan, who voted for the Glass-Steagall repeal in 1999, today says banks should not be too big to fail. And he differs with Wall Street on some other points as well.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/13/paul-ryan-and-what-wall-street-should-know/', 'snippet': 'Paul Ryan, who voted for the Glass-Steagall repeal in 1999, today says banks should not be too big to fail. And he differs with Wall Street on some other points as well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He could be mistaken for a Wall Street banker. Or perhaps a hedge fund manager. Or even a managing director at a private equity firm, like Bain Capital.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Everything Wall St. Should Know About Ryan', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Everything Wall St. Should Know About Ryan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T02:26:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ross Sorkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/170d19f4-a166-51d9-bc50-03eb6f4bf4fa', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/170d19f4-a166-51d9-bc50-03eb6f4bf4fa'}, {'abstract': 'The Mexican Navy announced Monday that a suspected member of a drug gang was captured while carrying the identification cards of a recently slain newspaper employee in the state of Veracruz.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/world/americas/suspected-drug-gang-member-linked-to-veracruz-killings.html', 'snippet': 'The Mexican Navy announced Monday that a suspected member of a drug gang was captured while carrying the identification cards of a recently slain newspaper employee in the state of Veracruz.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Mexican Navy announced Monday that a man suspected of being a member of a drug gang had been captured while carrying the identification cards of a recently slain newspaper employee in the state of Veracruz. The authorities link the suspect, Juan Carlos Hernández Pulido, whom they captured Friday, to the killing of the newspaper employee, Irasema Becerra. Her dismembered remains were found in May along with those of three photojournalists. Six journalists have been killed in Mexico so far this year; five of them in Veracruz. None of the crimes have been solved yet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Suspect Linked to Veracruz Killings, Officials Say', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Suspect Linked to Veracruz Killings, Officials Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Veracruz (Mexico)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T02:26:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Zabludovsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'las