14/the-other-running-mates/', 'snippet': 'What do the roles played by Michelle Obama and Ann Romney in the presidential campaign tell us about the state of feminism?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The argument over whether American feminism is really dead — or just beaten back into a corner — never fails to get a conversation going.\xa0Indeed, it’s fair to say we can’t stop talking, writing or reading the chatter about it, in private or in public. In the late summer stretch from now into September, this topic is bound to heat up as Michelle Obama and Ann Romney make their own campaign stops — though 2012 is no 2008 when it comes to up-ending age-old paradigms for women in politics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Other Running Mates', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Ann', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T04:02:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jamie Stiehm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jamie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stiehm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb1f027e-4d47-58bb-a0c0-013b84d4cbdc', 'word_count': 2601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb1f027e-4d47-58bb-a0c0-013b84d4cbdc'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 86 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https