ointing out stains that looked like dried blood.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Paan’ Stains Dot the Sidewalks of Queens', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T07:17:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a04ba77-7ecb-56a1-88ad-f3e5effaca00', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a04ba77-7ecb-56a1-88ad-f3e5effaca00'}, {'abstract': 'Can you choose the best synonym for “moxie” as it is used in the article?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/test-yourself-english-aug-14-2012/', 'snippet': 'Can you choose the best synonym for “moxie” as it is used in the article?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the On the Runway blog post “At Pratt, Seeking a Sophisticated Eye.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, Aug. 14, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T08:33:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8470536f-1070-524e-a111-ef8893fdae54', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8470536f-1070-524e-a111-ef8893fdae54'}, {'abstract': 'Indian classical dancer, Malini Srinivasan, performs at the New York International Fringe Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/indian-danseuse/', 'snippet': 'Indian classical dancer, Malini Srinivasan, performs at the New York International Fringe Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Near the beginning of her show ‘Being Becoming,’ the Bharata Natyam dancer Malini Srinivasan sits behind translucent red fabric and adorns herself,” Brian Seibert of The New York Times wrote in a review of the dancer’s show, part of the New York International Fringe Festival.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian Gods Begging Devotion', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T08:57:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8013bb68-9de5-5150-846d-323d4667d156', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8013bb68-9de5-5150-846d-323d4667d156'}, {'abstract': 'In a conversation with James Estrin, Mickey H. Osterreicher, a lawyer for the National Press Photographers Association, discusses a troubling trend of arrests for photography in public spaces.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/criminalizing-photography/', 'snippet': 'In a conversation with James Estrin, Mickey H. Osterreicher, a lawyer for the National Press Photographers Association, discusses a troubling trend of arrests for photography in public spaces.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Mickey H. Osterreicher is the general counsel for the National Press Photographers Association and edits the organization’s Advocacy Committee blog. He spoke with James Estrin. Their conversation has been edited.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Criminalizing Photography', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New