econd-and-1. Quarterback Joe Flacco is dropping back to pass. He has completed five of his last seven throws on what’s turning out to be a brilliant 56-yard drive. Flacco calmly pump-fakes and then slings a laser between two defenders in the front corner of the end zone. The ball lands in the hands of wide receiver Lee Evans. It’s an incredible throw – the type of throw that exhibits why the Ravens took Flacco in the first round, the type of throw that makes fans forget about Flacco’s middling 57.6 percent accuracy in the\xa0 regular season or his four-year reputation as the young quarterback who isn’t ready to push a great Ravens club over the top.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Baltimore Ravens, 2012 N.F.L. Season Preview', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Ravens', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T10:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/746e829a-a311-5c53-bf92-a3791a70de8a', 'word_count': 2767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/746e829a-a311-5c53-bf92-a3791a70de8a'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney’s economic team ignores the record in blaming President Obama for ills created by George W. Bush’s policies, particularly his tax cuts, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/blaming-obama-for-george-w-bushs-policies/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney’s economic team ignores the record in blaming President Obama for ills created by George W. Bush’s policies, particularly his tax cuts, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul. He is the author of “The Benefit and the Burden: Tax Reform – Why We Need It and What It Will Take.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blaming Obama for George W. Bush’s Policies', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T10:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77619b87-11a2-5629-b20b-0a859c15a58f', 'word_count': 1130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77619b87-11a2-5629-b20b-0a859c15a58f'}, {'abstract': 'If you have at least two of these players on your fantasy team, you are probably in the running.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/fantasy-focus-the-top-10-in-profit/', 'snippet': 'If you have at least two of these players on your fantasy team, you are probably in the running.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Remember when Matt Kemp was tearing up the league in April, and everyone who didn’t have a top-three pick was upset about missing out him? And then it was Josh Hamilton, on pace for 100 home runs and 1,000 runs batted in through the end of May.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedi