fety', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mount Kenya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T10:51:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman and Josh Kron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/731e73dc-8f33-5f2b-bc5d-9b6e4dbd61ba', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/731e73dc-8f33-5f2b-bc5d-9b6e4dbd61ba'}, {'abstract': 'Alli Kobrick wore oversize black pants from Urban Outfitters, a black short-sleeved vest from Beacon’s Closet over a black tee shirt with brightly printed sneakers she bought out West.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/intersection-menswear-inspired-prospect-heights-streetstyle/', 'snippet': 'Alli Kobrick wore oversize black pants from Urban Outfitters, a black short-sleeved vest from Beacon’s Closet over a black tee shirt with brightly printed sneakers she bought out West.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prospect Heights, Brooklyn, is a small neighborhood with a lot of style. This part of Brooklyn lies between Grand Army Plaza and Atlantic Avenue, and Flatbush and Washington Avenues; and borders Park Slope, Crown Heights, Clinton Hill and Fort Greene. Its mix of tree-lined streets, brick-face houses, sidewalk cafes, bars, boutiques and yoga studios make for a model urban epicenter. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Intersection: Borrowing From the Boys', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prospect Heights (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T11:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simone S. Oliver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simone', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Oliver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8cff9c4-c9f7-597a-bbf9-346ca9912f52', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8cff9c4-c9f7-597a-bbf9-346ca9912f52'}, {'abstract': 'While Jay Goltz has become quite adept at delegating almost everything else, the combination of vehicles and stickers has long been a surprising source of grief.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/the-one-task-i-cant-seem-to-delegate/', 'snippet': 'While Jay Goltz has become quite adept at delegating almost everything else, the combination of vehicles and stickers has long been a surprising source of grief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The other day, three yearly license plate renewal stickers arrived in the mail for three of my company vehicles. This meant someone would have to put the stickers on and replace the registration card in each of the cars. Normally, that someone would be me. While I have become quite adept at delegating almost everything else, the combination of vehicles and stickers has long been a surprising source of grief, education and humor for me. I have given speeches about my failures to manage this process.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The One Task I Can’t Seem to Delegate', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T11:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Goltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbf3c62c-4339-5fcd-a053-4d1a4f63b9ca', 'word_count': 1233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbf3c62c-4339-5fcd-a053-4d1a4f63b9ca'}, {'abstract': 'Some of the nondescript eateries cook up the best Ramadan dishes.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/from-nalli-nihari-to-malpau-mumbai-offers-hearty-ramadan-fare/', 'snippet': 'Some of the nondescript eateries cook up the best Ramadan dishes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is never a better time to be a meat eater in Mumbai than the month of Ramadan, when streets come alive with delectable aromas in the evening as Muslims prepare to break their fast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Nalli Nihari to Malpua, Mumbai Offers Hearty Ramadan Fare', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ramadan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T11:04:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc7d85a0-e22e-5ae1-9534-76476d20db28', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc7d85a0-e22e-5ae1-9534-76476d20db28'}, {'abstract': 'What do the changes at the top in the Egyptian military mean for the U.S. relationship with Egypt? A research project by the country’s new Chief of Staff, written as part of his war studies in the U.S., provides some insights.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/what-egypts-new-guard-thinks-about-america/', 'snippet': 'What do the changes at the top in the Egyptian military mean for the U.S. relationship with Egypt? A research project by the country’s new Chief of Staff, written as part of his war studies in the U.S., provides some insights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — As analysts grapple with the implications of a purge of the senior echelons of the Egyptian military by Mohamed Morsi, the country’s Muslim Brotherhood president, the inevitable question in Washington is where the new guard stands in relation to the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/14/blogs/rdv-egypt/rdv-egypt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/14/blogs/rdv-egypt/rdv-egypt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1095, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Egypt’s New Guard Thinks About America', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Council of the Armed Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T11:18:30+0000', 'documen