3a1a', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d78bd189-c992-55a6-8ea4-3435e0483a1a'}, {'abstract': 'As a writer, I watched the Olympics with something like awe at the perfect narrative arc of it all.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/a-not-insubstantial-pageant/', 'snippet': 'As a writer, I watched the Olympics with something like awe at the perfect narrative arc of it all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — In the end, nothing went terribly wrong, and more went right than anyone could have anticipated. If this sounds like faint praise, it isn’t. For seven years, the Olympics have been bearing down on London filling it with anxiety and an anticipation that were scarcely articulated — at least until the Olympic torch landed on this island and all along the length and breadth of the country, often in driving rain, people lined the streets to watch it go past.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Not Insubstantial Pageant', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ennis, Jessica', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farah, Mo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Daily Mail', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T13:32:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kamila Shamsie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kamila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shamsie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47004877-911e-54e5-9292-6c087c3616fb', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47004877-911e-54e5-9292-6c087c3616fb'}, {'abstract': 'Acknowledging the extent of the contamination is just the first challenge in tackling a project as big as detoxifying a river, especially one that was as abused as the Passaic.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/cleaning-a-river-that-was-given-up-for-dead/', 'snippet': 'Acknowledging the extent of the contamination is just the first challenge in tackling a project as big as detoxifying a river, especially one that was as abused as the Passaic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1984, when the Environmental Protection Agency put the old Diamond Alkali factory in Newark on its list of the most heavily polluted places in the country, the agency was not thinking about the Passaic River, which runs right in front of the plant. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cleaning a River That Was Given Up for Dead', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diamonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dioxin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Superfund', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Company', 'rank': 9, 'maj