cleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/14/business/video-bdl-120814/video-bdl-120814-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/14/business/video-bdl-120814/video-bdl-120814-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/14/business/video-bdl-120814/video-bdl-120814-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Business Day Live | August 14, 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Canadian Auto Workers Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Stock Exchange', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nasdaq Stock Market', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Municipal Bonds', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T14:50:03+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'Mac William Bishop, Channon Hodge, Nadia Sussman and Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mac', 'middlename': 'William', 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Channon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Nadia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sussman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/88af01be-e317-5104-8b59-fb910643b742', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/88af01be-e317-5104-8b59-fb910643b742'}, {'abstract': 'Aïda Ruilova’s compact, psychologically charged videos, which have been shown everywhere from the Venice Biennale to a Jumbotron in Times Square, don’t so much draw you in as snare you in a relentless loop with no hope of climax or resolution.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/camera-sly/', 'snippet': 'Aïda Ruilova’s compact, psychologically charged videos, which have been shown everywhere from the Venice Biennale to a Jumbotron in Times Square, don’t so much draw you in as snare you in a relentless loop with no hope of climax or resolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aïda Ruilova’s compact, psychologically charged videos, which have been shown everywhere from the Venice Biennale to a Jumbotron in Times Square, don’t so much draw you in as snare you in a relentless loop with no hope of climax or resolution. Her latest, a collaboration with the director Abel Ferrara, begins with a conversation about Pier Paolo Pasolini’s death and veers into a wholly tangential discourse on love, hustlers, desire, drugs, conspiracy, film scripts and the actress Zoë Lund. It will be shown at the New Museum in New York this fall and at Kayne Griffin Corcoran in Los Angeles next spring. And then there is Ruilova’s continuing collaboration with her husband, the artist Raymond Pettibon. “Having a baby is the ultimate ready-made,” she says of their infant son. “We make videos with him every day.” ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '228', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Timely | Camera Sly', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Camera Sly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T15:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a94d4ad5-f2d8-57de-a7e4-8eb92c029e30', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a94d4ad5-f2d8-57de-a7e4-8eb92c029e30'}, {'abstract': 'Behind the Bollywood dream of the Great Indian Wedding, complete with white horse and brass bands, the reality for many Indian women is stark: there isn’t much alternative to marriage. Does it have to be this way for the next generation?', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/will-indian-women-ever-have-the-freedom-not-to-marry/', 'snippet': 'Behind the Bollywood dream of the Great Indian Wedding, complete with white horse and brass bands, the reality for many Indian women is stark: there isn’t much alternative to marriage. Does it have to be this way for the next generation?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Behind the Bollywood dream of the Great Indian Wedding, complete with white horse and brass bands, the reality for many Indian women is stark: there isn’t much alternative to marriage. Does it have to be this way for the next generation? How long can tradition be used to justify marrying off women before they’re old enough to make good choices — or to pressure women into marriage, because being single is not a culturally acceptable choice?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Indian Women Ever Have the Freedom Not to Marry?', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T15:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nilanjana S. Roy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nilanjana', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Roy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fb98863-1ee9-5bc0-b915-57ed79d7518a', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fb98863-1ee9-5bc0-b915-57ed79d7518a'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama basking in the glow of a campaign stop in Iowa.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/shining-a-light-on-obama/', 'snippet': 'President Obama basking in the glow of a campaign stop in Iowa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This photograph from The Associated Press is creating a fair amount of chatter this morning, and is naturally prompting some caption-writing contests. No, it is not doctored, and it captured President Obama speaking at Bayliss Park in Council Bluffs, Iowa, on Monday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shining a Light on Obama', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T15:04:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7fb288e-86f0-5b9f-bf54-d72c70f09cd9', 'word_count': 45, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7fb288e-86f0-5b9f-bf54-d72c70f09cd9'}, {'abstract': 'Ballet, music, dance, theater and more will be part of the Guggenheim’s Works & Process lineup.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/guggenheim-announces-works-process-performance-season/', 'snippet': 'Ballet, music, dance, theater and more will be part of the Guggenheim’s Works & Process lineup.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Royal Danish Ballet, the director Robert Lepage and an expert on the neuroscience of taste will be featured in the fall season of the Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum’s Works & Process series, which begins Sept. 9. The performances, aimed at giving audiences insight into the creative process, will take place in the museum’s Peter B. Lewis Theater. Most events will also be livestreamed. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guggenheim Announces ‘Works & Process’ Performance Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guggenheim Lineup For Works & Process', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ades, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lepage, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maliphant, Russell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mizrahi, Isaac', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picasso, Pablo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevens, Sufjan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Danish Ballet', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T15:04:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a80387d8-ff36-5680-955f-afbd0fc195d3', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a80387d8-ff36-5680-955f-afbd0fc195d3'}, {'abstract': 'An artist installs sculptures in tropical shallows with an eye to saving reefs.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/the-art-of-reef-conservation/', 'snippet': 'An artist installs sculptures in tropical shallows with an eye to saving reefs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s not to like about the\xa0work of Jason deCaires Taylor? The 37-year-old sculptor, raised in England, Spain and Malaysia, has found a way to blend a love of diving and coral reefs with his art — which he crafts on dry land and then lowers into the seas, where, he says, it diverts divers who might otherwise spend too much time poking at fragile reefs. The sculptures themselves, with time, end up as homes for corals, sponges and other marine life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Art of Reef Conservation', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diving and Divers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'MEXICO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reefs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museo Subacuatico de Arte', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cancun (Mexico)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Puerto Morelos (Mexico)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T15:04:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49b5ce43-ccec-5a1e-8005-0a7f32ce59c6', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49b5ce43-ccec-5a1e-8005-0a7f32ce59c6'}, {'abstract': 'Mixed-case signs, mandated by the Federal Highway Administration, are the wave of the future.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/throughout-the-city-a-new-generation-of-street-signs/', 'snippet': 'Mixed-case signs, mandated by the Federal Highway Administration, are the wave of the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This message is addressed to New Yorkers who were more surprised to see a street sign with uppercase and lowercase letters than they were to learn that an intersection in Harlem had been named for Judge Bruce McM. Wright:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Throughout the City, a New Generation of Street Signs', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Like Spelling, Capitalization Now Counts on Street Signs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Signals and Signs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sadik-Khan, Janette', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Highway Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T15:11:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dff97dc3-b118-50be-8e02-6418d2ec21db', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dff97dc3-b118-50be-8e02-6418d2ec21db'}, {'abstract': 'The United States men’s national team faces a daunting task when it plays an international friendly against Mexico at Aztec Stadium.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/estadio-azteca-into-the-lions-den/', 'snippet': 'The United States men’s national team faces a daunting task when it plays an international friendly against Mexico at Aztec Stadium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday, when the United States plays Mexico in a friendly in Mexico City, the Americans will try to earn their first victory on the home soil of their greatest rival: they are 0-23-1 in Mexico since the first game in 1937, a 7-2 drubbing. To win, they will need to beat Mexico in the Estadio Azteca, one of the most famed stadiums in the world: a 105,000-seat caldron perched at an elevation of 7,200 feet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Estadio Azteca: Into the Lion’s Den', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donovan, Landon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Tim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maradona, Diego', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_dat