jor': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T15:14:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5d7c823-d8d4-50d4-892c-c1ec33612b79', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5d7c823-d8d4-50d4-892c-c1ec33612b79'}, {'abstract': 'The R&B singer offered no explanation for the cancellations.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/frank-ocean-cancels-european-performances/', 'snippet': 'The R&B singer offered no explanation for the cancellations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frank Ocean has abruptly canceled his European tour, including several festival appearances and a series of high-profile concerts with Coldplay. Mr. Ocean, an R&B singer who drew international attention when he revealed last month that his first true love was with a man, did not give a reason for his decision.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Frank Ocean Cancels European Performances', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Frank Ocean Cancels European Tour', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ocean, Frank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T15:17:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb0aa46b-bf57-55b6-9a4c-1818aeb68668', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb0aa46b-bf57-55b6-9a4c-1818aeb68668'}, {'abstract': 'A survey gauging whether candidates should talk about taking action on global warming.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/should-candidates-talk-about-climate-change/', 'snippet': 'A survey gauging whether candidates should talk about taking action on global warming.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:16 p.m. | Updates below | Anthony Leiserowitz, the\xa0director of the\xa0Yale Project on Climate Change Communication, just sent the note below about a new analysis of climate attitudes. I’m posting it here as part of a continuing effort to point to notable news and analysis out there in the firehose flood  of information:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should Candidates Talk About Climate Change?', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T15:23:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/594c3335-4d08-54e7-ad60-1a9e58ccf32e', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/594c3335-4d08-54e7-ad60-1a9e58ccf32e'}, {'abstract': 'Vermont Rolling Pins are hand turned, in eight styles, and can be ordered in a choice of woods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/dining/rolling-pins-from-vermont-make-for-smooth-pastry.html', 'snippet': 'Vermont Rolling Pins are hand turned, in eight styles, and can be ordered in a choice of woods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though the job of fashioning the dough for fresh fruit pies, tarts, cobblers and such can be improvised with a wine bottle, it really calls for a well-made rolling pin that’s sleek and balanced. Vermont Rolling Pins are hand turned, in eight styles, including a hefty classic Shaker model (top); a simple column; a lighter, sharply tapered French style (center) that is a dream to use for delicate pastry; and several finished with handsome carved finials and handles. They can be ordered in a choice of woods, including cherry, maple and walnut. The Shaker, French and column styles also come in child’s versions (bottom). ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/dining/15STUFF_PINSSPAN/15STUFF_PINSSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/15/dining/15STUFF_PINSSPAN/15STUFF_PINSSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/dining/15STUFF_PINSSPAN/15STUFF_PINSSPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/dining/15STUFF_PINSSPAN/15STUFF_PINSSPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/