ions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T15:33:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/acf37af7-b662-54be-93d8-42f4426fb577', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acf37af7-b662-54be-93d8-42f4426fb577'}, {'abstract': 'A new version of lobster mac and cheese is made with quinoa pasta and a topping of corn, rice and grated cheese.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/dining/gluten-free-lobster-mac-and-cheese-to-order.html', 'snippet': 'A new version of lobster mac and cheese is made with quinoa pasta and a topping of corn, rice and grated cheese.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gluten-free with no compromise describes the new version of lobster mac and cheese from Hancock Gourmet Lobster in Cundy’s Harbor, Me. Gluten-free? Really? The macaroni is a quinoa pasta, its lush mascarpone cream sauce is thickened with a little gluten-free flour, and the breadcrumb topping is made from corn, rice and grated cheese. The serving is liberally studded with chunks of lobster.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/dining/15STUFF_MACSPAN/15STUFF_MACSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/15/dining/15STUFF_MACSPAN/15STUFF_MACSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/dining/15STUFF_MACSPAN/15STUFF_MACSPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, '