of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu from a rival political party, will resign his seat in Parliament to join Mr. Netanyahu’s government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/world/middleeast/avi-dichter-named-israeli-home-front-minister.html', 'snippet': 'Avi Dichter, an old army friend of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu from a rival political party, will resign his seat in Parliament to join Mr. Netanyahu’s government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel on Tuesday named an old army friend from a rival political party as his new home front minister, amid growing concern here about preparedness for the response to a potential attack on Iran this fall.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Names New Home Front Minister', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Names New Minister To Oversee Home Front', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dichter, Avi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T15:44:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33ec0c25-58c4-5208-86f6-368cc3b2f2d1', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33ec0c25-58c4-5208-86f6-368cc3b2f2d1'}, {'abstract': 'Cooked in packets, this savory fish dish can be assembled well ahead of time and baked at the last minute.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/health/nutrition/rainbow-trout-baked-with-tomatoes-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'Cooked in packets, this savory fish dish can be assembled well ahead of time and baked at the last minute.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My friend Christine always makes salmon prepared this way when I arrive at her home in Provence after my long trip from California. It’s a great dish to make when you don’t know exactly when guests are going to arrive, as everything can be prepared in advance and the fish can be baked at the last minute. I’ve adapted Christine’s salmon recipe to rainbow trout, which are farmed in a sustainable way and less expensive than wild salmon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/14/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/14/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/14/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/14/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/14/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/14/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/14/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rainbow Trout Baked in Foil With Tomatoes, Garlic and Thyme', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T15:46:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Fitness & Nutrition', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/66de7e31-2814-5efb-9222-fc39e75999d2', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66de7e31-2814-5efb-9222-fc39e75999d2'}, {'abstract': 'Under private equity ownership, HCA made an aggressive push for more revenue that sometimes led to conflicts with doctors and nurses over patient care.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/business/hca-giant-hospital-chain-creates-a-windfall-for-private-equity.html', 'snippet': 'Under private equity ownership, HCA made an aggressive push for more revenue that sometimes led to conflicts with doctors and nurses over patient care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the Great Recession, when many hospitals across the country were nearly brought to their knees by growing numbers of uninsured patients, one hospital system not only survived — it thrived.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/business/15hca-span/15hca-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/15/business/15hca-span/15hca-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/business/15hca-span/15hca-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/business/15hca-span/15hca-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Giant Hospital Chain Is Blazing a Profit Trail', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Giant Hospital Chain Is Blazing a Profit Trail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bain Capital', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HCA Holdings Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T15:54:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Creswell and Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Creswell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ffb4fac-2d30-5ed2-83ff-22aad140971f', 'word_count': 4116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ffb4fac-2d30-5ed2-83ff-22aad140971f'}, {'abstract': 'How a has-been officer became a Civil War naval hero.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/the-making-of-rear-admiral-farragut/', 'snippet': 'How a has-been officer became a Civil War naval hero.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Yesterday I hoisted my flag at the main, and the whole fleet cheered, which I returned with a most dignified salute,” wrote David Glasgow Farragut, commander of the Union’s Western Gulf Blockading Squadron, to his family on Aug. 12, 1862. “I called all hands, and read the act of Congress complimentary of their achievements. I got under way, and stood down the river, leaving a general order to be read to the fleet. I stopped at the forts, to let the men see what they had done to deserve the resolutions.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Making of Rear Admiral Farragut', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farragut, David Glasgow', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Welles, Gideon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T16:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Meredith Hindley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Meredith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hindley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68a51446-b432-5acc-bc1f-4fe1ff54a475', 'word_count': 2045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68a51446-b432-5acc-bc1f-4fe1ff54a475'}, {'abstract': 'The material was assembled by Joseph Schildkraut, the actor who played Mr. Frank in the stage and film versions of “The Diary of Anne Frank.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/rare-otto-frank-archive-to-be-auctioned-in-new-york/', 'snippet': 'The material was assembled by Joseph Schildkraut, the actor who played Mr. Frank in the stage and film versions of “The Diary of Anne Frank.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'An archive of documents and artifacts relating to Otto Frank, the father of Anne Frank, will be auctioned off on Nov. 5 at Doyle New York, the auction house has announced. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rare Otto Frank Archive to Be Auctioned in New York', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frank, Anne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frank, Otto', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schildkraut, Joseph', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Doyle New York', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yivo Institute for Jewish Research', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T16:03:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06accf2d-4668-5ac0-8ac4-8390a73b9c57', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06accf2d-4668-5ac0-8ac4-8390a73b9c57'}, {'abstract': 'The United States Preventive Services Task Force declined on Monday to recommend hearing tests for older adults without symptoms of hearing loss.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/in-testing-for-hearing-loss-how-often-is-too-often/', 'snippet': 'The United States Preventive Services Task Force declined on Monday to recommend hearing tests for older adults without symptoms of hearing loss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hearing tests are cheap and effective. There are no known health harms. And they can identify older adults with compromised hearing who might benefit from using a hearing aid.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Insufficient’ Evidence for Routine Hearing Tests, Experts Say', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ears and Hearing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preventive Medicine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Preventive Services Task Force', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T16:03:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judith Graham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Graham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e41a3c18-ce38-5cbc-a63f-838b0aa4b9e3', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e41a3c18-ce38-5cbc-a63f-838b0aa4b9e3'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Deshmukh died of multiple organ failure in Chennai on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/science-minister-vilasrao-deshmukh-dies-at-67/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Deshmukh died of multiple organ failure in Chennai on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vilasrao Deshmukh, the minister for science and technology and a former Maharashtra chief minister, died of multiple organ failure in Chennai on Tuesday afternoon. Mr. Deshmukh, 67, had been suffering from liver cancer over the past six months.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Science Minister Vilasrao Deshmukh Dies at 67', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deshmukh, Vilasrao', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T16:08:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a52ded0-4d14-5c02-a803-1af9f975d61f', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a52ded0-4d14-5c02-a803-1af9f975d61f'}, {'abstract': 'Natasha Trethewey, Amiri Baraka and Jorie Graham are among those participating in the events in October.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/fall-poetry-festival-lineups-announced/', 'snippet': 'Natasha Trethewey, Amiri Baraka and Jorie Graham are among those participating in the events in October.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Poetry may make nothing happen, as W. H. Auden once wrote. But in October it will bring an unusual number of poets and poetry mavens to the greater New York area. The United States poet laureate Natasha Trethewey, the Pulitzer Prize winner C. K. Williams, the former New Jersey poet laureate Amiri Baraka and dozens of others will gather in Newark on Oct. 11-14 for the 14th Geraldine R. Dodge Poetry Festival, a biennial event that bills itself as North America’s largest poetry event. And Oct. 18-20, the American Academy of Poets will present its sixth annual Poets Forum, which will feature readings and discussions on issues like poetry and social media (the subject of a lecture by Jorie Graham), and poetry-themed walking tours of Harlem, the West Village, the Museum of Modern Art and SoHo. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fall Poetry Festival Lineups Announced', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lots of Poetry Fests Coming in October', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baraka, Amiri', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Jorie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trethewey, Natasha', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Academy of Poets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T16:14:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46c8e89c-bb4d-5d34-b23f-8390165fc310', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46c8e89c-bb4d-5d34-b23f-8390165fc310'}, {'abstract': 'It’s far from his hometown in Switzerland, but Roger Federer is comfortable (and successful) at the Western & Southern Open in Cincinnati.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/cincinnati-is-federers-kind-of-town/', 'snippet': 'It’s far from his hometown in Switzerland, but Roger Federer is comfortable (and successful) at the Western & Southern Open in Cincinnati.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MASON, Ohio — “You know why we like Stan Wawrinka here?” a fan said as he watched Wawrinka, the Swiss professional player, play a first-round match at the Western & Southern Open in Cincinnati last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cincinnati Is Federer’s Kind of Town', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T16:15:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b21a44ad-eba2-5d1b-8e8c-60c5ccab5683', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b21a44ad-eba2-5d1b-8e8c-60c5ccab5683'}, {'abstract': 'The new release, called “The Price of Politics,” will be Mr. Woodward’s 17th book and will examine efforts by government leaders to restore the American economy, the publisher said.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/new-woodward-book-due-in-september/', 'snippet': 'The new release, called “The Price of Politics,” will be Mr. Woodward’s 17th book and will examine efforts by government leaders to restore the American economy, the publisher said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fall books season just got a little more crowded. Bob Woodward’s 17th book, “The Price of Politics,” will be published on Sept. 11, his publisher said on Tuesday, in the splashy, embargoed style that has been a trademark of a Woodward release. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Woodward Book Due in September', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Book From Bob Woodward', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodward, Bob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC News', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Simon & Schuster Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T16:16:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/814bdb10-1438-54f5-ae3e-8dba9ae10780', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/814bdb10-1438-54f5-ae3e-8dba9ae10780'}, {'abstract': 'Russia isn’t too happy about the latest U.S. sanctions on Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/undisguised-blackmail/', 'snippet': 'Russia isn’t too happy about the latest U.S. sanctions on Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there is any chance of a diplomatic solution on Iran’s nuclear program – admittedly a long shot – the major powers have to stand united on sanctions, incentives and negotiating strategy. The United States and its partners (Britain, France, Germany, Russia and China) have managed that pretty well since President Obama took office, despite what Mitt Romney \xa0might say on the campaign trail. But the Russians are getting anxious.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Undisguised Blackmail’', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T16:26:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Giacomo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Giacomo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d49bcc0f-c34d-5803-a340-df86a2fcfc5d', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d49bcc0f-c34d-5803-a340-df86a2fcfc5d'}, {'abstract': 'In an opinion article in response to a recent New York Times essay, a parent writes: "Before dropping algebra in favor of more ‘useful’ mathematics, we would do well to first examine how we deliver and assess the most fundamental aspects of math education."', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/08/14/before-dropping-algebra-fix-math-education/', 'snippet': 'In an opinion article in response to a recent New York Times essay, a parent writes: "Before dropping algebra in favor of more ‘useful’ mathematics, we would do well to first examine how we deliver and assess the most fundamental aspects of math e...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before Dropping Algebra, Fix Math Education', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T16:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By MATTHEW LEVEY', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LEVEY', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3937dbe7-720e-5e2a-9ae4-0923f14e71ee', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3937dbe7-720e-5e2a-9ae4-0923f14e71ee'}, {'abstract': 'Bank of America’s new check deposit app balked at a hand-written, personal check.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/trying-to-deposit-checks-with-my-new-iphone/', 'snippet': 'Bank of America’s new check deposit app balked at a hand-written, personal check.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bank of America has (finally) begun offering a check deposit feature on its mobile banking app for smartphones and tablets. The addition gave me the push I needed to try mobile banking on my new iPhone. So I tested it, with varying results.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trying to Deposit Checks With My New iPhone', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Deposit By iPhone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer 