eform/', 'snippet': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg appeared with William M. Daley, a former White House chief of staff, in Chicago, and with media mogul Rupert Murdoch in Boston to promote proposals on immigration reform and urge a more vigorous discussion of the topic i...', 'lead_paragraph': '9:50 p.m. | Updated  BOSTON — Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg joined Rupert Murdoch, the chief of the News Corp. media company, in Boston on Tuesday night, appearing in the same city as Mitt Romney’s campaign headquarters to make an economic argument for immigration reform and call for a more substantial discussion of the issue in the presidential campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg Urges Campaigns to Discuss Immigration Reform', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T17:33:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Ann Cullotta and Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': 'Ann', 'lastname': 'Cullotta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe4f5bba-e374-5c92-b114-4c462c73f038', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe4f5bba-e374-5c92-b114-4c462c73f038'}, {'abstract': 'The joy of Shakespeare in the Park is a summer ritual that can be connected to milestones in a New Yorker’s life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/theater/shakespeare-in-the-park-delacorte-theater-a-summer-ritual.html', 'snippet': 'The joy of Shakespeare in the Park is a summer ritual that can be connected to milestones in a New Yorker’s life.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Into the woods, each time you go,/There’s more to learn of what you know.” It was hard not to be reminded of those Sondheim lyrics last week when I went to Central Park, which is as close as many New Yorkers get to the woods, for the latest Shakespeare in the Park production. Dodging bikers and runners, walking up the gentle slope and through one of the wooden pathways to arrive at the Delacorte Theater, I was reminded of my first visit years ago. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/arts/LIFE-jp2/LIFE-jp2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/15/arts/LIFE-jp2/LIFE-jp2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/arts/LIFE-jp2/LIFE-jp2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/arts/LIFE-jp2/LIFE-jp2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1386, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/arts/LIFE-jp2/LIFE-jp2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/15/arts/LIFE-jp2/LIFE-jp2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/arts/LIFE-jp2/LIFE-jp2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Park’s Starring Role in a Yearly Ritual', 'kicker': 'Still Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Park’s Starring Role in a Yearly Ritual', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shakespeare in the Park', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Delacorte Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T17:34:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7dc2114-7289-5f5d-b25c-3484a2f92831', 'word_count': 1059, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7dc2114-7289-5f5d-b25c-3484a2f92831'}, {'abstract': 'The Alberleen Group provides seasoned investment bankers with the infrastructure and working capital to start their own firms.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/can-a-banker-think-like-an-entrepreneur/', 'snippet': 'The Alberleen Group provides seasoned investment bankers with the infrastructure and working capital to start their own firms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a just-published New York Times article, I write about Jolyne Caruso, a Wall Street veteran who founded the Alberleen Group, a company that applies the incubator concept — ubiquitous in the world of tech start-ups — to investment banking. The Alberleen Group provides seasoned investment bankers with the infrastructure and working capital to start their own firms. In exchange, it takes a revenue share.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can a Banker Think Like an Entrepreneur?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caruso, Jolyne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neal, E Stanley", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alberleen Group LLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T17:35:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6347f21-6304-5ed6-b5b4-01e749fea54e', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6347f21-6304-5ed6-b5b4-01e749fea54e'}, {'abstract': 'Feeding or petting a dolphin is illegal, but many who love them seem blissfully unaware.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/the-dolphin-lovers-conundrum/', 'snippet': 'Feeding or petting a dolphin is illegal, but many who love them seem blissfully unaware.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People who express the greatest concern about protecting Florida’s wild dolphins are often the same ones who break laws about feeding, petting or swimming with the charismatic species, according to a new study commissioned by the National Marine Fisheries Service. And the report suggests that dolphin harassment is on the rise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dolphin Lover’s Conundrum', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T17:50:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deborah Weisberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deborah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4330d2fa-5467-5537-b9a7-f5e353e93136', 'word_count': 789, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4330d2fa-5467-5537-b9a7-f5e353e93136'}, {'abstract': 'A Renaissance woman, this model — who designs bikes, acts in feature films and dances on prime-time T.V. — is well-diversified.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/profile-in-style-hannelore-knuts/', 'snippet': 'A Renaissance woman, this model — who designs bikes, acts in feature films and dances on prime-time T.V. — is well-diversified.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps the worst thing you could call Hannelore Knuts  is a model-turned-fill-in-the-blank. Fortunately, the title doesn’t really apply. After 14 years in the business, the 34-year-old Belgian is still modeling — and does five hours of boxing workouts a week to keep it that way. She is also taking photographs: she shot her first campaign, for the French men’s brand Arnys. She acts: she’s in the first feature by her boyfriend, the artist Nicolas Provost, and she will play David Bowie in a Radio Soulwax video. She designs bags for Delvaux and just put the finishing touches on a bike for Marniek Kint, which she describes as having a slightly off-white frame, a fluorescent pink brake cable, classic racing handlebars and a hot pink basket. “Yep! The perfect man race bike for women,” she says. And not least, this fall she will appear on the Belgian version of “Dancing With the Stars.” So what do you call Knuts? Busy comes to mind.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Profile in Style | Hannelore Knuts', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T18:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba07f2f4-bd3a-5988-a5ae-ebbf8cf845bb', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba07f2f4-bd3a-5988-a5ae-ebbf8cf845bb'}, {'abstract': 'New York’s top banking regulator had accused Standard Chartered of laundering $250 billion for Iranian clients and lying about it to authorities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/business/standard-chartered-settles-with-new-york-for-340-million.html', 'snippet': 'New York’s top banking regulator had accused Standard Chartered of laundering $250 billion for Iranian clients and lying about it to authorities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Standard Chartered, the British bank, has agreed to pay New York’s top banking regulator $340 million to settle claims that it laundered hundreds of billions of dollars in tainted money for Iran and lied to regulators.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/business/BANK/BANK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/business/BANK/BANK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'British Bank in $340 Million Settlement for Laundering', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Laundering Case Settled by Bank For $340 Million', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub'