.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/court-to-hear-googles-challenge-to-class-action-lawsuit-on-book-scanning/', 'snippet': 'A federal judge earlier had allowed the Authors Guild to represent all authors affected by Google’s ambitious digitalization project. A higher court has agreed to consider the company’s objections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In May, the Authors Guild celebrated a decision in the long-running case over Google’s book-scanning project when a federal judge granted its authors class-action status.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court to Hear Google’s Challenge to Class-Action Lawsuit on Book Scanning', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chin, Denny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Authors Guild', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Book Search', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T18:35:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36f9b6d7-271d-5683-9cbe-adb9358652ed', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36f9b6d7-271d-5683-9cbe-adb9358652ed'}, {'abstract': 'Audience interest in the Stephen Sondheim-James Lapine musical is high and problems are fixable, the producers say.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/despite-mixed-reviews-producers-eyeing-woods-move-to-broadway/', 'snippet': 'Audience interest in the Stephen Sondheim-James Lapine musical is high and problems are fixable, the producers say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Theater producers are pursuing a possible Broadway transfer of the Central Park staging of “Into the Woods” in spite of several negative reviews last week that would usually put a damper on such plans.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Mixed Reviews, Producers Eyeing ‘Woods’ Move to Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Into the Woods’ Eyeing Broadway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lapine, James', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parnes, Joey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sondheim, Stephen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Delacorte Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CENTRAL PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T18:37:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/277905aa-6a35-5d11-b9a1-233bddcef763', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/277905aa-6a35-5d11-b9a1-233bddcef763'}, {'abstract': 'The Tigers thought they had the pitching and hitting to be one of the best teams in baseball. So far, the potential hasn’t translated into consistent wins.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/tigers-stuck-in-neutral/', 'snippet': 'The Tigers thought they had the pitching and hitting to be one of the best teams in baseball. So far, the potential hasn’t translated into consistent wins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Things seemed so perfect in spring training for the Detroit Tigers. The team, on paper, had it all: ace pitchers in Justin Verlander and Doug Fister, a can’t-miss closer in Jose Valverde, a slugger in Miguel Cabrera and an off-season, big-money acquisition in Prince Fielder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tigers Stuck in Neutral', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cabrera, Miguel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fielder, Prince', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fister, Doug', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leyland, Jim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Anibal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valverde, Jose', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verlander, Justin', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago White Sox', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oakland Athletics', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T18:40:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d54b41f-2d8b-5f87-83d5-12f0b54ecca2', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d54b41f-2d8b-5f87-83d5-12f0b54ecca2'}, {'abstract': 'The multimedia musical show based on work by Langston H