ack, Kotter,” provides a moment to reminisce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First Robert Hegyes. Now, alas, Ron Palillo has left the classroom, dead of a heart attack at 63.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'So Soon, Another Sweathog Is Gone', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T19:03:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae6ac19d-902c-5c3b-9ea2-09bef416019a', 'word_count': 69, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae6ac19d-902c-5c3b-9ea2-09bef416019a'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney’s campaign is embracing a potentially explosive debate over the future of Medicare with a new television ad that accuses President Obama of cutting $700 billion from the health care program for the elderly.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/new-ad-attacks-obama-on-medicare/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney’s campaign is embracing a potentially explosive debate over the future of Medicare with a new television ad that accuses President Obama of cutting $700 billion from the health care program for the elderly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney‘s campaign signaled that it intended to fight rather than run from Democratic attacks over Republican Medicare policies, unveiling a new ad that stresses that President Obama cut $700 billion from the program.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Ad Attacks Obama on Medicare', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mica, John L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T19:04:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear and Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/605b32d5-c27e-52aa-b5ea-49061bd7cd72', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/605b32d5-c27e-52aa-b5ea-49061bd7cd72'}, {'abstract': 'Does Mitt Romney support Paul Ryan’s Medicare plan, or not?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/medicare-confusion/', 'snippet': 'Does Mitt Romney support Paul Ryan’s Medicare plan, or not?', 'lead_paragraph': 'An unnamed Republican operative told Politico this week that if Mitt Romney and Paul Ryan “win the battle to define Medicare” they will win the election, but “if they lose it, then they lose big in the fall.” Whether that’s accurate or not, the Romney campaign doesn’t seem to have figured out its Medicare messaging.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicare Confusion', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T19:28:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bce9ebda-33c2-55c1-be61-907c4c789d8a', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bce9ebda-33c2-55c1-be61-907c4c789d8a'}, {'abstract': 'Ole-Martin Hansen moved from Norway to London 10 years ago to study sound art, but he soon found a very different calling: smoking salmon, the Norwegian way.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/edible-selby-live-stream/', 'snippet': 'Ole-Martin Hansen moved from Norway to London 10 years ago to study sound art, but he soon found a very different calling: smoking salmon, the Norwegian way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ole-Martin Hansen moved from Norway to London 10 years ago to study sound art, but he soon found a very different calling: smoking salmon, the Norwegian way. At his North London shop, Hansen & Lydersen, he recreated his grandfather’s special smoking chamber in a 1950s boiler room, where he flavors fresh salmon from Denmark’s Faroe Islands with beechwood and juniper, and uses small fans to blow air on the fish. “The salmon needs to move,” he explains. After curing the fish with salt from Guérande, France, Hansen sends it to some of London’s finest restaurants and markets. Lest there be any doubt about his dedication to the fish, Hansen adds that the chamber is equipped with a piano, on which he plays them Edvard Grieg’s “In the Hall of the Mountain King.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '116', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Edible Selby | Live Stream', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Live Stream', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T19:30:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Todd Selby and Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Todd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Selby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d6a8aa4-ecd0-5945-b09e-dc2c579fd595', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d6a8aa4-ecd0-5945-b09e-dc2c579fd595'}, {'abstract': 'Andrea Lynn Green, left, and Hallie Foote in one of the one-act plays in "Harrison, TX: Three Plays by Horton Foote."', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/theater/100000001721676/excerpt-blind-date.html', 'snippet': 'Andrea Lynn Green, left, and Hallie Foote in one of the one-act plays in "Harrison, TX: Three Plays by Horton Foote."', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrea Lynn Green, left, and Hallie Foote in one of the one-act plays in "Harrison, TX: Three Plays by Horton Foote."', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/14/arts/video-harrison/video-harrison-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/14/arts/video-harrison/video-harrison-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/14/arts/video-harrison/video-harrison-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 