1-b173-a640c5c3689b', 'word_count': 1281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/042d5cf8-bc5b-5061-b173-a640c5c3689b'}, {'abstract': 'The district attorney, Cyrus R. Vance Jr., says a new lab costing $4.2 million to build will help his office continue its efforts to keep up with tech-savvy criminals.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/manhattan-prosecutor-to-centralize-efforts-against-cybercrime/', 'snippet': 'The district attorney, Cyrus R. Vance Jr., says a new lab costing $4.2 million to build will help his office continue its efforts to keep up with tech-savvy criminals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many criminals in the city are becoming more sophisticated, like using high-tech tools for identity theft and other forms of computer crimes. The city’s response? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Manhattan Prosecutor to Centralize Efforts Against Cybercrime', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identity Fraud', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vance, Cyrus R Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T20:14:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aaron Edwards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Edwards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12cf50e5-d2d0-5db9-8595-210831a7f13b', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12cf50e5-d2d0-5db9-8595-210831a7f13b'}, {'abstract': 'However does Lady Mary Crawley upkeep her baroque costumes?', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/the-dirt-on-clean-laundering-fashions-most-elaborate-creations/', 'snippet': 'However does Lady Mary Crawley upkeep her baroque costumes?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though “Downton Abbey” is currently between seasons — Season 3, which will take the fictional Crawley family into the Jazz Age, will have its debut next month in Britain but not until January on this side of the Atlantic — its sumptuous costumes remain firmly planted in our imaginations; for many, they’re reason enough to tune in. So while watching the the Balmain fall 2012 collection unfurl it was easy to embroider a line between the elaborate, mosaic-style beading that the designer Olivier Rousteing dreamed up and the exquisitely embellished clothes worn by Lady Mary and company. The obvious parallels, of course, lie in the richness of the workmanship. But there are less evident similarities between the “Downton” costumes and Rousteing’s clothes, as well as those of Erdem Moralioglu, who embroidered lace onto rubber; Marios Schwab, who layered sequined gowns with chiffon; and Gucci, where the designer Frida Giannini sent out a cocktail dress dripping with coq feathers. These creations (and many others, every season) beg the inevitable question: How are they to be cleaned? Once these individual testaments to the skills of seamstresses, embroiderers, featherers and beaders have been worn, perspired in and spilled on, what’s the wearer to do?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dirt on Clean | Laundering Fashion’s Most Elaborate Creations', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T20:25:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy MacDonell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24e0a0d1-65cf-5616-a752-9da741af0ee1', 'word_count': 1494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24e0a0d1-65cf-5616-a752-9da741af0ee1'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Dennis Cardoza of California had already announced that he would not run for re-election and retire after this year. But on Tuesday, he issued a statement surprising many saying that he would, in fact, step down immediately.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/representative-cardoza-throws-in-the-towel/', 'snippet': 'Representative Dennis Cardoza of California had already announced that he would not run for re-election and retire after this year. But on Tuesday, he issued a statement surprising many saying that he would, in fact, step down immediately.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So much for a long goodbye.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawmaker Literally Can’t Wait to Leave Congress', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Early Retirement: Forgoing the Next Five Months', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cardoza, Dennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costa, Jim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Blue Dog Coalition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T20:28:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adeshina Emmanuel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adeshina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Emmanuel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eae83bf6-4dfa-578c-bf88-5caed8c2522c', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eae83bf6-4dfa-578c-bf88-5caed8c2522c'}, {'abstract': 'Josh Mandel, a candidate for the Senate in Ohio, railed against “radical organizations” like the Sierra Club and the League of Conservation Voters.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/a-fiery-introduction-for-romney-in-ohio-coal-country/', 'snippet': 'Josh Mandel, a candidate for the Senate in Ohio, railed against “radical organizations” like the Sierra Club and the League of Conservation Voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEALLSVILLE, Ohio — A Senate candidate, introducing Mitt Romney at a rally here on Tuesday, railed against “radical organizations” like the Sierra Club and the League of Conservation Voters, and he said he had a message for those, like President Obama, who stood in the way of the coal industry: “Over our dead bodies.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fiery Introduction for Romney in Ohio Coal Country', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-14T20:30:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cfad36d-d9f2-59c5-b785-a2170cdcad68', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cfad36d-d9f2-59c5-b785-a2170cdcad68'}, {'abstract': 'Collaborating with a marine biologist, VW created an ocean-going observa