ant-that-i-wish-could.html', 'snippet': 'Ming Du, a restaurant in the garment district, has had trouble with its report card from the city’s Health Department. Here’s to hoping it gets an A and keeps it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a tiny restaurant in the garment district that I keep rooting for. It’s like a dear but troubled friend who has issues. It’s 38th Street Restaurant and Bakery, also known as Ming Du, a simple, steam-table Chinese place where neighborhood workers get tasty food cheap.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/opinion/18edsall-chartimg/18edsall-chartimg-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 627, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/opinion/18edsall-chartimg/18edsall-chartimg-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1061, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Little Restaurant That (I Wish) Could', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The City Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Little Restaurant That (I Wish) Could', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hygiene and Cleanliness', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'City Life', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T01:01:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c832ea8-37a5-56cd-b72b-528c5ea129d6', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c832ea8-37a5-56cd-b72b-528c5ea129d6'}, {'abstract': 'The murders at the Sikh temple in Wisconsin are a reminder of our hate crimes problem. States and cities need to increase the enforcement against bias-motivated violence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/opinion/unprosecuted-hate-crimes.html', 'snippet': 'The murders at the Sikh temple in Wisconsin are a reminder of our hate crimes problem. States and cities need to increase the enforcement against bias-motivated violence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Attorney General Eric Holder Jr. told the Senate in 2009 that “we have a significant hate crimes problem in this country.” The recent murders at the Sikh temple in Wisconsin have raised this issue in the public consciousness. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unprosecuted Hate Crimes', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unprosecuted Hate Crimes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hate Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oak Creek (Wis)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sikhs and Sikhism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T01:02:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_nam