/opinion/remedying-the-effects-of-agent-orange-in-vietnam.html', 'snippet': 'Readers praise American plans to address damage from a defoliant used during the Vietnam War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remedying the Effects of Agent Orange', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Remedying the Effects of Agent Orange', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AGENT ORANGE (DEFOLIANT)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Defects', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T01:07:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/eec1f786-7dd1-560f-a04b-ced078a4750c', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eec1f786-7dd1-560f-a04b-ced078a4750c'}, {'abstract': 'Africa Israel Properties and Developments USA will retain an ownership stake in the Upper West Side building, but the condo board and sales sponsor will be managed by another investor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/nyregion/a-major-investor-in-apthorp-cedes-day-to-day-control.html', 'snippet': 'Africa Israel Properties and Developments USA will retain an ownership stake in the Upper West Side building, but the condo board and sales sponsor will be managed by another investor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Apthorp apartment building has long been one of New York City’s most famous structures, a heavy limestone behemoth built by the Astors in 1908, once home to Nora Ephron and Al Pacino. In recent years, however, it has developed a decidedly less glamorous reputation as one of the city’s most troubled condominium conversions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Major Investor in the Apthorp Cedes Its Day-to-Day Control', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Major Investor in the Apthorp Cedes Its Day-to-Day Control', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condominiums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apthorp (Manhattan, NY, Apartments)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Arefin US Investments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Africa Israel Properties and Developments USA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T01:12:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/852ac871-cd12-5c84-91e7-2ba052da3d59', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/852ac871-cd12-5c84-91e7-2ba052da3d59'}, {'abstract': 'Republican elections officials curtail early voting in Democratic counties, but not in theirs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/opinion/overt-discrimination-in-ohio.html', 'snippet': 'Republican elections officials curtail early voting in Democratic counties, but not in theirs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update: On Wednesday afternoon, Jon Husted, the Ohio Secretary of State, announced that all Ohio counties would follow a uniform early-voting policy. The policy would extend early-voting hours to 7 p.m. on weekdays during the last two weeks before the election, though all early voting is banned during the final three days of the campaign.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Overt Discrimination in Ohio', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Overt Discrimination in Ohio', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Husted, Jon', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T01:12:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/04eb4861-51e7-5343-aaf7-ad12c8ca4a1d', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04eb4861-51e7-5343-aaf7-ad12c8ca4a1d'}, {'abstract': 'On another day, the polls conducted partly or wholly after the vice-presidential announcement would constitute some decent numbers for the Republicans — but so far, also, they suggest a below-average bounce.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/aug-14-the-fog-of-polling-and-ryans-bounce-so-far/', 'snippet': 'On another day, the polls conducted partly or wholly after the vice-presidential announcement would constitute some decent numbers for the Republicans — but so far, also, they suggest a below-average bounce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I noted on Saturday, past vice-presidential announcements have typically been greeted with a small “bounce” in the polls. Harry J. Enten, at The Guardian, has run the numbers on this for vice-presidential announcements dating back to 1984. He finds a net gain of four percentage points in the polls — and a mean of six — for the party that just named its new running mate. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 14: The Fog of Polling — and Ryan’s ‘Bounce’ So Far', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T01:14:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79f38cdf-7349-52b5-9aaa-173f2136111c', 'word_count': 1698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79f38cdf-7349-52b5-9aaa-173f2136111c'}, {'abstract': 'Investigators can legally confiscate a cellphone and review video only after obtaining a court order, which is not required if the owner consents, a law professor said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/nyregion/the-police-sought-cellphones-pictures-of-times-square-shooting.html', 'snippet': 'Investigators can legally confiscate a cellphone and review video only after obtaining a court order, which is not required if the owner consents, a law professor said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dozens of bystanders grabbed their cellphones and hit the record button as a knife-wielding man skipped backward through Times Square on Saturday. Some witnesses, holding their cellphones above their heads to capture the action, ran alongside police officers as they pursued the man down Seventh Avenue with guns drawn.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/nyregion/PHONE1/PHONE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/15/nyregion/PHONE1/PHONE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/nyregion/PHONE1/PHONE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/nyregion/PHONE1/PHONE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Sought Cellphones for Video of Times Square Shooting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Police Sought Cellphones for Times Sq. Shooting Video', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Darius H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Times Square and 42nd Street (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T01:19:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wendy Ruderman and Aaron Edwards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wendy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Edwards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9af1dbd-e3b3-5e6a-a74d-615b5fa8aa47', 'word_count': 992, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9af1dbd-e3b3-5e6a-a74d-615b5fa8aa47'}, {'abstract': 'The storied restaurant moved a step closer to winning interior landmark designation when the city’s Landmarks Preservation Commission agreed to schedule a hearing to review it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/nyregion/rainbow-room-shut-by-feud-has-fading-wish.html', 'snippet': 'The storied restaurant moved a step closer to winning interior landmark designation when the city’s Landmarks Preservation Commission agreed to schedule a hearing to review it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was probably the most cinematically perfect space in New York. It had that stylishly streamlined modern look — elegant crystal chandeliers here, a revolving dance floor there, long velvety draperies beyond. And it had those magical views that made the Empire State Building and the Chrysler Building seem small enough to reach out and touch.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/nyregion/RAINBOW/RAINBOW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag