 effect.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parking Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Parking Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parking', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T03:03:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2be6e72-b4cc-5f1a-86c4-fe7feb1ba93a', 'word_count': 26, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2be6e72-b4cc-5f1a-86c4-fe7feb1ba93a'}, {'abstract': 'A day after lashing out at attacks that he called “wild and reckless,” Mitt Romney rebuked President Obama for running a campaign of “enmity and jealousy and anger” during a network interview.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/14/romney-delivers-a-harsh-rebuke-of-obama-at-final-stop-on-bus-tour/', 'snippet': 'A day after lashing out at attacks that he called “wild and reckless,” Mitt Romney rebuked President Obama for running a campaign of “enmity and jealousy and anger” during a network interview.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:14 a.m. | Updated In a CBS interview on Wednesday, Mitt Romney continued his harsh rebuke of the Obama administration, charging that President Obama is running a campaign of “enmity and jealousy and anger and this is not in my view what the American people want to see.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Delivers a Harsh Rebuke of Obama at Final Stop on Bus Tour', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T03:10:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45d23f23-d300-50a8-868c-dd59664ec5a2', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45d23f23-d300-50a8-868c-dd59664ec5a2'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Paul D. Ryan traveled to Las Vegas to meet with Sheldon Adelson in what Mitt Romney’s camp called a “finance event.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/us/politics/paul-ryan-meets-sheldon-adelson-in-las-vegas.html', 'snippet': 'Representative Paul D. Ryan traveled to Las Vegas to meet with Sheldon Adelson in what Mitt Romney’s camp called a “finance event.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Four days after his announcement as Mitt Romney’s running mate, Representative Paul D. Ryan was not in Florida talking Medicare with elderly voters or in drought-ridden Iowa talking about a farm bill. He traveled to the Venetian hotel here for a meeting hosted by Sheldon Adelson, the billionaire casino mogul who has pledged to spend as much as $100 million this year to defeat President Obama.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryan Meets Casino Mogul and Major G.O.P. Donor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ryan Meets Casino Mogul and Major G.O.P. Donor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adelson, Shel