59-5fbe-891e-d199e1db728a', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f84b4248-4c59-5fbe-891e-d199e1db728a'}, {'abstract': 'While the Mars rover Curiosity beams back its first images from the Red Planet, some advocates of planetary exploration couldn’t wait to start exploring, and got started — on Earth.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/finding-mars-in-familiar-places/', 'snippet': 'While the Mars rover Curiosity beams back its first images from the Red Planet, some advocates of planetary exploration couldn’t wait to start exploring, and got started — on Earth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rover Curiosity survived its famed “seven minutes of terror” and has touched down on the surface of Mars, and the world cheered.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding Mars in Familiar Places', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Curiosity (Mars Rover)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mars (Planet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zubrin, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mars Society', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yediot Aharonot', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T09:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b051b6b-48b3-52d9-939e-a4980df4d1d6', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b051b6b-48b3-52d9-939e-a4980df4d1d6'}, {'abstract': 'Changing a strongly held belief has little to do with actual facts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/magazine/the-mind-of-a-flip-flopper.html', 'snippet': 'Changing a strongly held belief has little to do with actual facts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forget for a minute everything you know about politics. Barack Obama now openly supports gay marriage. Mitt Romney now opposes roughly the same kind of health care reform he fought for as governor of Massachusetts. What if they weren’t two politicians calculating how to win an election but instead just two guys who changed their minds? They didn’t “flip-flop”; they experienced, as social scientists say, an attitude change, the way any of us do when we become a vegetarian or befriend a neighbor we used to hate or even just choose to buy a new brand of toothpaste.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/magazine/19eureka2/19eureka2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/19/magazine/19eureka2/19eureka2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/magazine/19eureka2/19eureka2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/magazine/19eureka2/19eureka2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/magazine/19eureka2/19eureka2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnai