: 'If you’re thinking about selling your iPhone so you can use the money to buy Apple’s new smartphone when it comes out, better act fast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/22/technology/bits/bitpix-apple-iphone1/bitpix-apple-iphone1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/22/technology/bits/bitpix-apple-iphone1/bitpix-apple-iphone1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/22/technology/bits/bitpix-apple-iphone1/bitpix-apple-iphone1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/04/22/technology/bits/bitpix-apple-iphone1/bitpix-apple-iphone1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/22/technology/bits/bitpix-apple-iphone1/bitpix-apple-iphone1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting a Jump on iPhone Upgraders', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T14:56:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c6ffc5c-1f67-5065-92c6-fd8fdb4c4eee', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c6ffc5c-1f67-5065-92c6-fd8fdb4c4eee'}, {'abstract': 'To reduce evaporation, a start-up venture proposes to cover reservoirs with a layer of vegetable oil made from palm and coconut.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/a-different-approach-to-coping-with-drought/', 'snippet': 'To reduce evaporation, a start-up venture proposes to cover reservoirs with a layer of vegetable oil made from palm and coconut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Water levels are low in reservoirs all over the parched West, but in many areas, the amount of water being used is no greater than the amount that evaporates, according to Moshe Alamaro, a scientist and inventor affiliated with M.I.T. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Different Approach to Coping With Drought', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reservoirs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T14:57:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a18d479d-c825-56ba-aac5-ed4494828b76', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a18d479d-c825-56ba-aac5-ed4494828b76'}, {'abstract': 'The Democrats’ war on Representative Paul D. Ryan has moved into the Upper Chamber, and it is extending beyond the battle over Medicare.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/senate-democrats-shift-strategy-on-ryan/', 'snippet': 'The Democrats’ war on Representative Paul D. Ryan has moved into the Upper Chamber, and it is extending beyond the battle over Medicare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Democrats’ war on Representative Paul D. Ryan has moved into the Upper Chamber, and it is extending beyond the battle over Medicare.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Democrats’ Strategy for Ryan Includes the Deficit', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vice Presidents and Vice Presidency (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumer, Charles E', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T14:58:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbb6c0fb-48c1-5f21-b72d-a1cc5938ea6f', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbb6c0fb-48c1-5f21-b72d-a1cc5938ea6f'}, {'abstract': 'Claressa Shields pays homage to the coach that got her to the Olympics.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/claressa-shields-shares-gold/', 'snippet': 'Claressa Shields pays homage to the coach that got her to the Olympics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two months ago, Claressa Shields packed a strapless purple dress to wear in London if she became one of the first women boxers to win an Olympic medal. When the 17-year-old boxer from Flint, Mich. (who was included in our multimedia feature on America’s boxing women aiming for the Olympics this past winter), finally got to wear that dress, she had more than one historical achievement to celebrate: the first woman middleweight gold medalist, the youngest since 1924, the only American boxer to stand on top of the podium this year and the second-most-trending name on Yahoo! on the day of her victory.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Claressa Shields Shares Gold', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shields, Claressa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T15:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By SUE JAYE JOHNSON', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sue', 'middlename': 'Jaye', 'lastname': 'JOHNSON', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d720e98f-7168-5379-89b9-b5313f1eeeb3', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d720e98f-7168-5379-89b9-b5313f1eeeb3'}, {'abstract': 'Fifty-five thousand pieces of fashion history under one roof in Paris — now that’s a killer closet.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/this-old-thing/', 'snippet': 'Fifty-five thousand pieces of fashion history under one roof in Paris — now that’s a killer closet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '143', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Old Thing?', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Old Thing?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Versace, Gianni', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watanabe, Junya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BALENCIAGA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T15:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Yaeger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaeger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0666e58-30d8-5e13-9019-2a81ee787c00', 'word_count': 1155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0666e58-30d8-5e13-9019-2a81ee787c00'}, {'abstract': 'Samsung’s new iPad rival, the Galaxy Note 10.1, is loaded with features, but not all are well organized or practical.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/technology/personaltech/samsungs-rival-for-the-ipad-loads-on-the-features.html', 'snippet': 'Samsung’s new iPad rival, the Galaxy Note 10.1, is loaded with features, but not all are well organized or practical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hot news in Silicon Valley legal circles these days is Apple’s titanic lawsuit against Samsung. Apple maintains that Samsung pilfered some of its iPhone and iPad designs when creating the Samsung Galaxy series of phones and tablets. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/pogue-75/pogue-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/pogue-75/pogue-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tablet Straining to Do It All', 'kicker': 'State of the Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tablet Straining To Do It All', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T15:03:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03a87760-0fb4-5241-824e-65c8a84c4551', 'word_count': 1299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03a87760-0fb4-5241-824e-65c8a84c4551'}, {'abstract': 'When the Key Food in Windsor Terrace closed, many residents were unhappy. News that the space was to become a Walgreens has made many of them angry.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/a-lament-for-a-supermarket-and-outrage-over-its-replacement/', 'snippet': 'When the Key Food in Windsor Terrace closed, many residents were unhappy. News that the space was to become a Walgreens has made many of them angry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was an unlovely place and its customers had many complaints: a chronic damp and musty smell, a poor selection unless one harbored a passion for Campbell’s soups, exorbitant prices, a fresh deli that could be anything but and bored workers with little interest in helping shoppers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lament for a Supermarket, and Outrage Over Its Replacement', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Outrage Over a Supermarket’s Unfresh Replacement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets and Grocery Stores', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walgreen Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Windsor Terrace (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T15:13:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Farmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ba9b888-85ad-566d-a81f-e15acc8f431d', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ba9b888-85ad-566d-a81f-e15acc8f431d'}, {'abstract': 'Answers to readers’ questions about inviting noisy babies to a small ceremony and other wedding-related matters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/fashion/weddings/wedding-q-and-a.html', 'snippet': 'Answers to readers’ questions about inviting noisy babies to a small ceremony and other wedding-related matters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My fiancé and I are planning a small wedding for family and close friends. It is important to us that the sanctity and beauty of the ceremony be respected. Several of our guests have babies and young children. We are happy to have them at our wedding under their parents’ supervision, but are concerned that this might lead to disruptions during the religious ceremony, which will be about 30 to 45 minutes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/11/fashion/weddings/peggypost/peggypost-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 288, 'width': 288, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/11/fashion/weddings/peggypost/peggypost-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/02/11/fashion/weddings/peggypost/peggypost-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/02/11/fashion/weddings/peggypost/peggypost-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wedding Q. and A.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T15:19:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peggy Post', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peggy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Post', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0871b0f-f7c7-5c4b-b309-33478407b2ca', 'word_count': 958, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0871b0f-f7c7-5c4b-b309-33478407b2ca'}, {'abstract': 'And so it must not be acknowledged.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/the-truth-has-a-well-known-demagogic-bias/', 'snippet': 'And so it must not be acknowledged.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The other day I picked up on something William Saletan wrote to illustrate the conventional wisdom that has let the essentially ridiculous Paul Ryan go so far. Today let me pick on William Galston – again not a household name, but a good representative of the Beltway gone bad.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Truth Has A Well-Known Demagogic Bias', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T15:27:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00983a1e-ec94-5c3e-b21e-0fb1f2bca78b', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00983a1e-ec94-5c3e-b21e-0fb1f2bca78b'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Ringwald’s “When It Happens to You” follows the troubles of a married couple.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/leaning-toward-the-light-molly-ringwald-talks-about-her-new-novel/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Ringwald’s “When It Happens to You” follows the troubles of a married couple.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Molly Ringwald became a star for her roles in a beloved triumvirate of mid-’80s teenage movies: “Sixteen Candles,” “The Breakfast Club” and “Pretty in Pink.” Now 44, she continues to act and is also focused on a career as an author. In 2010, she published “Getting the Pretty Back.” She called that effort “a kind of entertaining, anecdotal style guide.” Her new book is “When It Happens to You,” a novel told in stories centered around Phillip and Greta, a couple whose marriage is foundering. In a recent e-mail interview, Ms. Ringwald discussed the appeal of flawed characters, advice she got from Bret Easton Ellis and more. Below are edited excerpts from the conversation:', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leaning Toward the Light: Molly Ringwald Talks About Her New Novel', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Word With: Molly Ringwald: From ‘Breakfast Club’ to Movie-Star-Turned-Novelist Club', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ringwald, Molly', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T15:27:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d4d4c8e-7e8e-5949-9a74-4ef5d6808c64', 'word_count': 1208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d4d4c8e-7e8e-5949-9a74-4ef5d6808c64'}, {'abstract': 'Tired of being tired when you travel across time zones? Here’s some advice for fighting jet lag, straight from a team at NASA.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/travel/a-battle-plan-for-jet-lag.html', 'snippet': 'Tired of being tired when you travel across time zones? Here’s some advice for fighting jet lag, straight from a team at NASA.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE are more so-called remedies for jet lag than there are time zones, from long-standing antidotes like No-Jet-Lag’s homeopathic tablets to new innovations like the Valkee Brain Stimulation Headset, which was tested earlier this year by Finnair and purports to alleviate jet lag by channeling bright light into the brain through the ear canal. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/travel/19GETAWAY1/19JPGETAWAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 842, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/travel/19GETAWAY1/19JPGETAWAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1683, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/travel/19GETAWAY1/19GETAWAY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/19/travel/19GETAWAY1/19GETAWAY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/travel/19GETAWAY1/19GETAWAY1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Battle Plan for Jet Lag', 'kicker': 'The Getaway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Battle Plan for Jet Lag', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jet Lag', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T15:36:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Rosenbloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenbloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a26a6d0c-b655-52cc-bf20-a79b0ea6ae60', 'word_count': 1452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a26a6d0c-b655-52cc-bf20-a79b0ea6ae60'}, {'abstract': 'After Yahoo reported on the Red Sox players’ revolt, there was some backtracking in Boston but little sympathy for Bobby Valentine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/sports/baseball/red-sox-latest-turmoil-centers-on-valentine-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'After Yahoo reported on the Red Sox players’ revolt, there was some backtracking in Boston but little sympathy for Bobby Valentine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With everything that changes each season in baseball, it is nice to have a constant, a touchstone that reminds you what era one is in. To that end, the Red Sox are performing a public service, their dysfunction so consistent that it is almost comforting. Only the details change, from booing Nomar Garciaparra out of town to Manny being Manny to fried chicken and beer to whatever has popped out of Bobby Valentine’s mouth today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/sports/16leading/16leading-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/sports/16leading/16leading-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1520, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/sports/16leading/16leading-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/16/sports/16leading/16leading-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/sports/16leading/16leading-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Just Red Sox Being Red Sox', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valentine, Bobby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Chad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Gregg', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Philbin, Joe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strasburg, Stephen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Nationals', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T15:39:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/950e03e8-42a0-59e1-84b7-544793efea7b', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/950e03e8-42a0-59e1-84b7-544793efea7b'}, {'abstract': 'Cadillac will show two V-16-powered Fleetwood roadsters built from sketches from the 1930s at Pebble Beach this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/wheelies-the-32-pack-edition/', 'snippet': 'Cadillac will show two V-16-powered Fleetwood roadsters built from sketches from the 1930s at Pebble Beach this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which we bring you motoring news from around the Web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheelies: The 32-Pack Edition', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Pebble Beach Concours D'Elegance (Car Show)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cadillac Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pebble Beach (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T15:41:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c44c378-7083-57e0-ba39-16b4be9d62dd', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c44c378-7083-57e0-ba39-16b4be9d62dd'}, {'abstract': 'In her four seasons at “Saturday Night Live,” Abby Elliott provided impersonations of famous figures like Angelina Jolie, Meryl Streep, Zooey Deschanel and Rachel Maddow.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/abby-elliott-not-returning-to-saturday-night-live/', 'snippet': 'In her four seasons at “Saturday Night Live,” Abby Elliott provided impersonations of famous figures like Angelina Jolie, Meryl Streep, Zooey Deschanel and Rachel Maddow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Abby Elliott has joined the ranks of performers like Kristen Wiig and Andy Samberg who are leaving the cast of “Saturday Night Live.” Ms. Elliott, who joined “SNL” as a featured performer during its 2008-9 season, told the Web site Splitsider.com that she would not be returning to that long-running late-night comedy series. NBC declined to comment on Wednesday but a person with direct knowledge of plans at the show confirmed the report.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abby Elliott Not Returning to ‘Saturday Night Live’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Abby Elliott Leaving ‘Saturday Night Live’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elliott, Abby', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T15:48:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7bbf0e4-1ac9-5c5a-b044-f7d50cbab86d', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7bbf0e4-1ac9-5c5a-b044-f7d50cbab86d'}, {'abstract': 'A new collection includes established favorites like “Little Miss Muffett” along with less celebrated nursery folk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/books/the-mcelderry-book-of-mother-goose.html', 'snippet': 'A new collection includes established favorites like “Little Miss Muffett” along with less celebrated nursery folk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The renowned children’s book editor Margaret McElderry died last year, but the imprint bearing her name carries on, as does the publisher’s “McElderry Book of...”\xa0series of anthologies. “The McElderry Book of Mother Goose,” the fourth volume (earlier collections were of Greek myths, Aesop’s fables and Grimms’ fairy tales) does much to continue her storied tradition — and give it a fresh little tweak, especially for those who’ve had enough of Little Jack Horner and his over-recited ilk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/books/15muffett/15muffett-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/15/books/15muffett/15muffett-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/books/15muffett/15muffett-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 618, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/books/15muffett/15muffett-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1236, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/books/15muffett/15muffett-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/15/books/15muffett/15muffett-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/books/15muffett/15muffett-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rare Mother Goose, Indeed', 'kicker': "Children's Books", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mathers, Petra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T15:49:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamela Paul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/db98b1f2-d152-5cbf-8f0d-187070f23163', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db98b1f2-d152-5cbf-8f0d-187070f23163'}, {'abstract': '“There’s nothing we’re hiding,” Ann Romney tells NBC.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/ann-romney-refuses-to-release-more-tax-returns/', 'snippet': '“There’s nothing we’re hiding,” Ann Romney tells NBC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an interview scheduled to be broadcast Thursday evening on NBC’s “Rock Center,” Ann Romney, the wife of the Republican nominee, Mitt Romney, found herself facing some of the same questions that have dogged her husband’s campaign in recent weeks — namely, about the Romney family’s tax returns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ann Romney Refuses to Release More Tax Returns', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mormons (Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Ann', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T15:49:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/414dbf30-35f4-5734-888f-5a5c584a07f3', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/414dbf30-35f4-5734-888f-5a5c584a07f3'}, {'abstract': 'The science editor of Boing Boing kicks off her new column for the magazine, called “Eureka.”', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/introducing-maggie-koerth-baker/', 'snippet': 'The science editor of Boing Boing kicks off her new column for the magazine, called “Eureka.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers of Boing Boing will know what I mean when I say that very few people can write about science like Maggie Koerth-Baker. She is the site’s longtime science editor and also the author of the excellent book Before the Lights Go Out: Conquering the Energy Crisis Before It Conquers Us. And starting this month, she’ll be contributing a regular column to the magazine that we’re calling Eureka. Her terrific first column is about the mind of a flip-flopper. Maggie will be writing frequently about the intersection of science and culture, about studies she finds to be especially revealing or provocative, about human behavior and technological innovation and natural phenomena. In short, she’ll be bringing us in closer, smarter, more exciting contact with the scientific world. We’re very happy to have her joining the magazine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Introducing Maggie Koerth-Baker', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T15:54:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugo Lindgren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindgren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94d09933-d323-5622-810c-9b6681f51b8a', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94d09933-d323-5622-810c-9b6681f51b8a'}, {'abstract': 'A new report should prod people to think more seriously about America’s role in the country we invaded.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/remember-iraq/', 'snippet': 'A new report should prod people to think more seriously about America’s role in the country we invaded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since troops withdrew at the end of 2011, Iraq has receded from the American public consciousness. Just consider the U.S. presidential campaign where the economy – understandably – predominates. President Obama and Mitt Romney rarely even mention the country we invaded.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remember Iraq?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council on Foreign Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T15:55:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Giacomo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Giacomo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec354a8d-2bb9-5e2b-8360-ba0f7a59f8e8', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec354a8d-2bb9-5e2b-8360-ba0f7a59f8e8'}, {'abstract': 'In a balancing act, the Interior Department rules out drilling in some sections of the National Petroleum Reserve but green-lights it in others.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/energy-security-vs-environment-in-alaska/', 'snippet': 'In a balancing act, the Interior Department rules out drilling in some sections of the National Petroleum Reserve but green-lights it in others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the Marcellus Shale in New York and Pennsylvania and the Bakken Shale in North Dakota are trigger points in the world of fossil-fuel extraction these days, Alaska has been the lodestar for oil and gas development in the United States for the last half-century. And as befits a state dominated more by wild lands than humankind, it has been home to some of the fiercest political battles pitting energy interests against environmental concerns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Energy Security vs. Environment in Alaska', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Migration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reserves (Natural Resources)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murkowski, Lisa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC NATIONAL WILDLIFE REFUGE', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marcellus Shale', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'National Petroleum Reserve (Alaska)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T16:04:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d5e3ed1-2ac5-507e-83d6-9dee7b5b1061', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d5e3ed1-2ac5-507e-83d6-9dee7b5b1061'}, {'abstract': 'Konno’s sleek timepiece is his first foray into the world of watch design.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/the-get-skagen-denmark-and-hiromichi-konno-watch/', 'snippet': 'Konno’s sleek timepiece is his first foray into the world of watch design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It could be said that Hiromichi Konno has a thing for Danish design. Four years ago, he enjoyed a certain degree of acclaim when he created the futuristic-looking Rin chair for the venerable Danish furniture collective Fritz Hansen. More recently, Konno approached the watch company Skagen Denmark about a collaboration. “I was so impressed by their design philosophy,” Konno said, which he defines as “simple and beautiful.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Skagen Denmark and Hiromichi Konno Watch', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T16:07:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Felsenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Felsenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/508eb1ef-9bfa-52db-a560-a101dbaf3bd3', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/508eb1ef-9bfa-52db-a560-a101dbaf3bd3'}, {'abstract': 'The recent trading debacle at Knight Capital has highlighted the issues associated with automated and high-speed trading. Yet today’s technological challenges are not unlike those faced by traders in the 19th century, whose jobs were revolutionized by the advent of ticker machines.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/wall-streets-race-to-the-48-millisecond-trade/', 'snippet': 'The recent trading debacle at Knight Capital has highlighted the issues associated with automated and high-speed trading. Yet today’s technological challenges are not unlike those faced by traders in the 19th century, whose jobs were revolutionize...', 'lead_paragraph': 'It took just 45 minutes this month for one of Wall Street’s top trading firms to lose $440 million, a loss that has focused attention on the potential problems associated with high-speed trading. Yet today’s technological challenges are not unlike those faced by traders in the 19th century, whose jobs were revolutionized by the advent of ticker machines.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wall Street’s Race to the 48-Millisecond Trade', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edison, Thomas A', 'rank': 