ial': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/63c58f15-261c-52be-b8b6-a118980dafee', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63c58f15-261c-52be-b8b6-a118980dafee'}, {'abstract': 'No, by definition — the GOP’s definition.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/reasonable-republicans/', 'snippet': 'No, by definition — the GOP’s definition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several commenters have asked that I provide examples of Republicans making reasonable economic arguments; some of them seem to be saying that I’m proving my bias if I don’t provide such examples.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reasonable Republicans?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T16:12:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bdd1b16-8cac-5a37-ac17-ab488873bce5', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bdd1b16-8cac-5a37-ac17-ab488873bce5'}, {'abstract': 'A look at how the second-tier business schools are challenging the Harvards and Whartons for relevance and outreach.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/forget-harvard-real-economic-change-will-come-from-the-bottom/', 'snippet': 'A look at how the second-tier business schools are challenging the Harvards and Whartons for relevance and outreach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Sunday’s magazine, Adam Davidson finds a reason to cheer for second-rate business schools. They may lack Nobel laureate professors and ivy-covered buildings, but they have managed to drive down the cost of a business degree. Some schools, like the University of California, Irvine, even offer online classes for free. ‘‘There are hundreds of millions of small farmers, shopkeepers and potential entrepreneurs,’’ Davidson writes, ‘‘for whom mass business-educational tools could be transformational in ways that make a handful of top schools seem utterly irrelevant.’’ According to Larry Cooperman, director of U.C. Irvine’s OpenCourseWare program, the transformation has already begun.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Forget Harvard; Real Economic Change Will Come From the Bottom', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Schools', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davidson, Adam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Irvine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T16:16:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Kedmey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kedmey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0801b8a1-4dc9-5676-824a-cf59cd3ffedb', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0801b8a1-4dc9-5676-824a-cf59cd3ffedb'}, {'abstract': 'Rafael Nadal, who has not played a match since June 28 at Wimbledon, withdrew from the Olympics and two Open warm-up events because of chronic knee problems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/sports/tennis/rafael-nadal-withdraws-from-us-open.html', 'snippet': 'Rafael Nadal, who has not played a match since June 28 at Wimbledon, withdrew from the Olympics and two Open warm-up events because of chronic knee problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rafael Nadal withdrew from the United States Open on Wednesday, saying he was not ready to return to competition because of chronic knee problems that forced him out of the Olympics and two warm-up tournaments for the Open.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/sports/NADALfloater/NADALfloater-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 956, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/sports/NADALfloater/NADALfloater-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1912, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/sports/NADALfloater/NADALfloater-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/16/sports/NADALfloater/NADALfloater-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/sports/NADALfloater/NADALfloater-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Recovering From Knee Problems, Nadal Will Miss United States Open', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knee Problems to Keep Nadal Out of U.S. Open', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T16:32:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'orig