e': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "National Hockey League Players' Assn", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T16:53:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53d78ad8-792a-5e67-ad48-70d99ce713c1', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53d78ad8-792a-5e67-ad48-70d99ce713c1'}, {'abstract': 'There is no sign yet of a wave breaking toward either party, but some individual races look a little different from a couple of months ago.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/in-senate-races-politics-are-local-again/', 'snippet': 'There is no sign yet of a wave breaking toward either party, but some individual races look a little different from a couple of months ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We will soon be unveiling our forecast model for United States Senate races. But as a point of comparison and because there have been a number of important primaries for the Senate in recent weeks, I first wanted to give you my view of the contests. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Senate Races, Politics Are Local Again', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T16:56:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b7bf3bb-11bb-5247-a9b3-6b341039bbb8', 'word_count': 2245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b7bf3bb-11bb-5247-a9b3-6b341039bbb8'}, {'abstract': 'Comparing different parts of the world’s oceans, the index weighs whether the human activity there is sustainable or in need of better management.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/introducing-the-ocean-health-index/', 'snippet': 'Comparing different parts of the world’s oceans, the index weighs whether the human activity there is sustainable or in need of better management.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a potential milestone for ocean management, a team of collaborators has produced the first Ocean Health Index, a tool for appraising the state of the world’s oceans. The index takes into account the major factors that influence the quality of regional marine ecosystems like fisheries, biodiversity, tourism and carbon storage and then assigns a score from zero to 100 for each place.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Introducing the Ocean Health Index', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Santa Barbara', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T17:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kelly Slivka', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kelly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Slivka', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1356fccd-1379-510a-88c7-646eaeede2ae', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1356fccd-1379-510a-88c7-646eaeede2ae'}, {'abstract': 'The Delano hotel, managed by Morgans Hotel Group, is getting an outpost in Moscow. It is the latest new hotel for the company, which is also expanding two other brands.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/an-outpost-of-miami-chic-will-open-in-moscow/', 'snippet': 'The Delano hotel, managed by Morgans Hotel Group, is getting an outpost in Moscow. It is the latest new hotel for the company, which is also expanding two other brands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Delano hotel is getting an outpost in Moscow, according to executives with the Morgans Hotel Group. The 160-room hotel, scheduled to open in 2015, will be run by Morgans and developed with the Capital Group.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Delano, This Time in Moscow', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgans Hotel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Istanbul (Turkey)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marrakesh (Morocco)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T17:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Drake', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drake', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e7e76e3-26c6-519d-bf6b-3228a80b18d0', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e7e76e3-26c6-519d-bf6b-3228a80b18d0'}, {'abstract': 'Ohio doesn’t treat all voters the same. Will the secretary of state fix that?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/equal-voting-consideration/', 'snippet': 'Ohio doesn’t treat all voters the same. Will the secretary of state fix that?', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the board mentioned on the editorial page today, Ohio doesn’t treat all voters the same. Depending on where you live, your polling place may close promptly 5 p.m., or stay open in the evenings and on weekends. More specifically, if you live in a county likely to favor President Obama, you’ll have to get to the polls before the end of the traditional work day; if you live in a county likely to swing Republican, you can take your time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Equal (Voting) Consideration', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Husted, Jon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T17:01:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9bed495-ad57-55e2-b0b7-b96b3194320f', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9bed495-ad57-55e2-b0b7-b96b3194320f'}, {'abstract': 'Vows made by President François Hollande to spur economic growth and shrink a budget deficit in France have clashed as an iconic carmaker prepares to lay off thousands of workers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/world/europe/peugeots-troubles-test-francois-hollandes-contradictory-campaign-promises.html', 'snippet': 'Vows made by President François Hollande to spur economic growth and shrink a budget deficit in France have clashed as an iconic carmaker prepares to lay off thousands of workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOCHAUX, France — Peugeot, one of France’s iconic companies, is in trouble, presenting President François Hollande with an early, telling crisis that is displaying the contradictions at the heart of his campaign promises to spur economic growth while shrinking the budget deficit with tax increases.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/world/europe/16France/16France-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/world/europe/16France/16France-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/world/europe/16France/16France-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/16/world/europe/16France/16France-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/world/europe/16France/16France-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Peugeot’s Troubles, a Test of Contradictory Campaign Promises for Hollande', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peugeot’s Troubles Expose Contradictions in Hollande’s Campaign Promises', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Socialism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Peugeot SA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T17:05:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87b3dfe9-2a1a-5bc7-9758-3ee66e3bbead', 'word_count': 1324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87b3dfe9-2a1a-5bc7-9758-3ee66e3bbead'}, {'abstract': 'A proposed change to S.E.C. disclosure rules could unduly discourage activism of outside shareholders to the detriment of companies and investors, the author writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/dont-discourage-outside-shareholders/', 'snippet': 'A proposed change to S.E.C. disclosure rules could unduly discourage activism of outside shareholders to the detriment of companies and investors, the author writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission is currently considering a rule-making petition that advocates tightening the rules governing how quickly shareholders must disclose when they hold 5 percent or more of a company’s shares. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Discourage Outside Shareholders', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Harrison A Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T17:06:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lucian A. Bebchuk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lucian', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Bebchuk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bea0d88-18f6-5d63-9472-03a4b11a54d6', 'word_count': 900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bea0d88-18f6-5d63-9472-03a4b11a54d6'}, {'abstract': 'The president, aides said, will use the last day of a three-day bus tour of Iowa to take on Mitt Romney and his running mate, Paul D. Ryan, over the health care program for older Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/on-medicare-obama-plays-offense/', 'snippet': 'The president, aides said, will use the last day of a three-day bus tour of Iowa to take on Mitt Romney and his running mate, Paul D. Ryan, over the health care program for older Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBUQUE, Iowa — With Mitt Romney on the attack over Medicare, President Obama entered the fight on Wednesday, catapulting the popular entitlements program to the top of the presidential campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Medicare, Obama Plays Offense', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T17:09:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bb13304-306b-537b-b1ea-03af97b6dcfe', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bb13304-306b-537b-b1ea-03af97b6dcfe'}, {'abstract': 'While the prosecution of three members of the Russian protest band Pussy Riot has raised human rights concerns, the American actress Alicia Silverstone has identified another “urgent matter” exposed by the case: Russian prisons do not serve vegan meals.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/actress-writes-to-putin-to-demand-vegan-meals-for-jailed-punk-protesters/', 'snippet': 'While the prosecution of three members of the Russian protest band Pussy Riot has raised human rights concerns, the American actress Alicia Silverstone has identified another “urgent matter” exposed by the case: Russian prisons do not serve vegan ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, 5:23 p.m. While the prosecution of three members of a Russian protest band called Pussy Riot has raised concerns about freedom of speech and the growing influence of the Orthodox Church in Russia, an American actress has identified another “urgent matter” about the case: Russian prisons do not serve vegan meals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Actress Writes to Putin to Demand Vegan Meals for Jailed Punk Protesters', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Orthodox Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veganism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silverstone, Alicia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'People for the Ethical Treatment of Animals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pussy Riot', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T17:12:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39d9bf5d-4cb1-5d83-a617-d32c23c0bc9e', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39d9bf5d-4cb1-5d83-a617-d32c23c0bc9e'}, {'abstract': "Jane Herman delivers The Daily Shoe from the Berg