.Follow me here: I was moved by seeing a man in the role of a young woman being kissed by a second guy, playing a teenage boy, who minutes earlier portrayed an old lady. And that wasn’t the only instance of unexpected emotion in “2 Households, 2 ________: Shakespeare’s R&J,” a pretty good show despite a fairly bad (and unprintable) title. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Fringe Festival Report:  ‘2 Households…’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York International Fringe Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T17:43:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Jaworowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jaworowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1707b1c-192e-5f73-8230-e3fce814be02', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1707b1c-192e-5f73-8230-e3fce814be02'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Volstad of the Cubs has lost 23 games in a row, but is still in the starting rotation.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/for-cubs-volstad-another-start-another-loss/', 'snippet': 'Chris Volstad of the Cubs has lost 23 games in a row, but is still in the starting rotation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the surface, it would seem logical to question the employment of a starting pitcher who has an 0-9 record and a 6.96 earned run average this season. Throw in a losing streak of 23 games, and one can start to question why the Cubs right-hander Ch