s of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Wednesday’s selection includes a Curiosity Rover app and song parodies from fans of the game Minecraft.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently. See more here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Mars on View, and Odes to Minecraft', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T19:33:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c59605c-b658-5013-afeb-ca981548b4fe', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c59605c-b658-5013-afeb-ca981548b4fe'}, {'abstract': 'The 43rd installment of “Now That’s What I Call Music!” tops the Billboard album chart.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/now-43-compilation-tops-album-chart/', 'snippet': 'The 43rd installment of “Now That’s What I Call Music!” tops the Billboard album chart.', 'lead_paragraph': ' After a nine-week run at No. 1, Carly Rae Jepsen’s song “Call Me Maybe” has finally been bumped from the top spot, by Flo Rida’s “Whistle.” But Ms. Jepsen’s song is now part of a different No. 1. It is the first track on the latest installment — Vol. 43 — of “Now That’s What I Call Music!” — the long-running pop compilation series, which opens atop Billboard’s album chart this week.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Now 43’ Compilation Tops Album Chart', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Carly Rae Jepsen: From No. 1 to No. 1', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flo Rida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jepsen, Carly Rae', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T19:43:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b012a1d-2a35-559b-a86d-11cb4be62d6b', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b012a1d-2a35-559b-a86d-11cb4be62d6b'}, {'abstract': 'There is already a lot of amorous language for Paul Ryan, but his suits could use an adjustment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/fashion/a-look-at-paul-ryans-fashion-sense.html', 'snippet': 'There is already a lot of amorous language for Paul Ryan, but his suits could use an adjustment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SO far, the Mitt Romney-Paul Ryan ticket has been given the approval rating typically reserved for a