documented in the film “Inocente.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Inocente Izucar wants to join the circus someday and learn sign language. She paints her face every morning with colors and designs as bold as those on her sprawling canvases. She sometimes orders dessert before dinner because she emphatically believes “you can never go wrong with a root-beer float.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/jpinocente1/jpinocente1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/jpinocente1/jpinocente1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/jpinocente1/jpinocente1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/jpinocente1/jpinocente1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1472, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/jpinocente1/jpinocente1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/jpinocente1/jpinocente1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/jpinocente1/jpinocente1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dreaming of a Life as Vivid as Her Art', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dreaming Of a Life As Vivid As Her Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Izucar, Inocente', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nix Fine, Andrea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fine, Sean', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T22:21:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d472ee68-a0c3-5c66-bed7-de220bd69dff', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d472ee68-a0c3-5c66-bed7-de220bd69dff'}, {'abstract': 'The hosts of “Noticiero Univision,” Jorge Ramos and María Elena Salinas, will urge Mitt Romney and President Obama to participate in a debate or forum for its Hispanic viewers.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/on-univisions-nightly-news-a-plea-for-presidential-debate-on-latino-issues/', 'snippet': 'The hosts of “Noticiero Univision,” Jorge Ramos and María Elena Salinas, will urge Mitt Romney and President Obama to participate in a debate or forum for its Hispanic viewers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Univision will use its nightly news broadcast on Wednesday to plead with both presidential campaigns to accommodate an additional debate, on Univision, directed at the issues of concern to Latino viewers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Univision’s Nightly News, a Plea for Presidential Debate on Latino Issues', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T22:22:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac986270-29ef-518b-a4b2-18587bebc74e', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac986270-29ef-518b-a4b2-18587bebc74e'}, {'abstract': 'Thanks to help from his friends, 2 Chainz is hip-hop’s rising star.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/arts/music/2-chainz-is-hip-hops-rising-star.html', 'snippet': 'Thanks to help from his friends, 2 Chainz is hip-hop’s rising star.', 'lead_paragraph': '2 Chainz is 35, tall and gangly, all awkward angles. A working-class-minded interloper into a hip-hop era that has largely shelved self-presentations that are less than 110 percent polished, he juts out, tough to miss. His luxury restaurant is Benihana, not Philippe. His luxury brand is Polo, not Margiela. He rapped for more than a decade with little to no acclaim. He is nobody’s sex symbol.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/CHAINZ/CHAINZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/CHAINZ/CHAINZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1523, 'width': 2014, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/CHAINZ/CHAINZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/CHAINZ/CHAINZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/CHAINZ/CHAINZ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hip-Hop’s Loyal Mascot Now Cheers Himself On', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hip-Hop’s Loyal Mascot Now Cheers Himself On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': '2 Chainz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T22:26:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/815f0c0e-3de2-512b-a634-daca95346ff9', 'word_count': 931, 'uri': 'nyt://article/815f0c0e-3de2-512b-a634-daca95346ff9'}, {'abstract': 'The Smuin Ballet presented Trey McIntyre’s “Oh, Inverted World” at the Joyce Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/arts/dance/smuin-ballet-performs-oh-inverted-world-at-the-joyce.html', 'snippet': 'The Smuin Ballet presented Trey McIntyre’s “Oh, Inverted World” at the Joyce Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The opening work of the Smuin Ballet’s triple bill at the Joyce Theater on Monday provides evidence of one of the most singular choreographic minds working in ballet today. Trey McIntyre’s “Oh, Inverted World” — set to songs by the Shins — is a pop ballet, reminiscent of some of the best pop ballets of Twyla Tharp. Its subject, though, is one that I don’t remember Ms. Tharp tackling: the perplexity of young individuals amid the group. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/SMUIN/SMUIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/SMUIN/SMUIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1315, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/SMUIN/SMUIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/SMUIN/SMUIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/arts/SMUIN/SMUIN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Perplexity of Youths in a Group', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Perplexity Of Youths In a Group', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smuin Ballets/SF', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIntyre, Trey', 'ra