that made clear the impunity granted to public officials by Russia’s criminal justice system: The editor of a local newspaper was beaten nearly to death in 2008 after criticizing the mayor of a Moscow suburb, and the police barely feigned an investigation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russian Mayor at Center of Protests Resigns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russian Mayor at Center of Protests Resigns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strelchenko, Vladimir', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T22:41:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8fcc77a-bdd7-5b1a-a990-58da2f34535b', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8fcc77a-bdd7-5b1a-a990-58da2f34535b'}, {'abstract': 'At the Second World Mind Sports Games at the Lille, France, all three United States teams qualified for the round of 16.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/crosswords/bridge/bridge-play-at-the-second-world-mind-sports-games.html', 'snippet': 'At the Second World Mind Sports Games at the Lille, France, all three United States teams qualified for the round of 16.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LILLE, France — At the Second World Mind Sports Games here all three United States teams qualified for the round of 16, which started on Wednesday and will end on Thursday at 1:20 p.m. Eastern time. The results are at worldbridge.org.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/arts/card/card-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/arts/card/card-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bridge Play at the Second World Mind Sports Games', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T22:45:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3ac4208-3f94-5718-a67f-1b6132bbd61f', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3ac4208-3f94-5718-a67f-1b6132bbd61f'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands of Tunisian women marched in the capital, Tunis, Monday night, to protest a provision in the new Islamist government’s draft constitution describing women as “complementary to men.”', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/tunisian-women-march-to-defend-equality/', 'snippet': 'Thousands of Tunisian women marched in the capital, Tunis, Monday night, to protest a provision in the new Islamist government’s draft constitution describing women as “complementary to men.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Reuters reported, thousands of Tunisian women marched in the capital, Tunis, on Monday night to protest a provision in the new Islamist government’s draft constitution describing women as “complementary to men.” The 6,000 protesters pledged to defend the equality under the law they have enjoyed since Tunisia adopted its Code of Personal Status on Aug. 13, 1956.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tunisian Women March to Defend Equality', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T22:50:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18ffeaff-9779-51f4-8c74-3354a7ebaf33', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18ffeaff-9779-51f4-8c74-3354a7ebaf33'}, {'abstract': 'The Pelican brand of protective cases for electronics overhauled its marketing strategy to reach more consumers by adding a Web presence and print and television ads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/business/media/pelican-products-maneuvers-to-add-customers-without-losing-any-advertising.html', 'snippet': 'The Pelican brand of protective cases for electronics overhauled its marketing strategy to reach more consumers by adding a Web presence and print and television ads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Pelican brand of protective cases for electronics is well known, but only among users in fields like the oil industry, the military and aerospace. For years, the company’s primary form of marketing consisted of expos and trade publications.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/business/Adco1/Adco1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/16/business/Adco1/Adco1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/business/Adco1/Adco1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 555, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/business/Adco1/Adco1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1109, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/business/Adco1/Adco1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/16/business/Adco1/Adco1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/business/Adco1/Adco1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Product With Devotees Tries to Widen Its Niche', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Product With Devotees Tries to Widen Its Niche', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pelican Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T22:53:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2396e1c6-a417-5e64-b28e-2e3d82de2162', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2396e1c6-a417-5e64-b28e-2e3d82de2162'}, {'abstract': 'The announcement extended the company’s program to remove certain ingredients from baby products to include adult products.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/business/johnson-johnson-to-remove-formaldehyde-from-products.html', 'snippet': 'The announcement extended the company’s program to remove certain ingredients from baby products to include adult products.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Johnson & Johnson, which makes a range of personal care products like baby shampoo, acne cream and antiwrinkle lotion, announced plans Wednesday to remove a host of potentially harmful chemicals, like formaldehyde, from its line of consumer products by the end of 2015, becoming the first major consumer products company to make such a widespread commitment.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/business/