, '_id': 'nyt://article/19e7d237-e68c-5f8e-94c5-d469aa010b71', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19e7d237-e68c-5f8e-94c5-d469aa010b71'}, {'abstract': 'Two researchers focused on fungi, frogs and climate change explain their work and the challenges in communicating complicated science in today’s online environment.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/on-frogs-fungi-climate-and-headlines/', 'snippet': 'Two researchers focused on fungi, frogs and climate change explain their work and the challenges in communicating complicated science in today’s online environment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday, the University of South Florida press office put out a release to draw attention to an important new study finding amplified disease risk in frogs when exposure to a dangerous fungus coincides with increasingly varied temperatures. The headline was “Frogs Getting Sick from Climate Change.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Frogs, Fungi, Climate and the New News Process', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T23:09:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d2186e1-e1f9-51f5-8fc0-753f1564a905', 'word_count': 1359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d2186e1-e1f9-51f5-8fc0-753f1564a905'}, {'abstract': 'Cloud-based applications feed off new data, check into different machines and deal with servers around the world. A start-up, Boundary, hopes to make a Big Data play out of mapping all this near chaos, improving performance and eventually predicting where there might be trouble.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/boundary-keeping-cloud-software-in-shape/', 'snippet': 'Cloud-based applications feed off new data, check into different machines and deal with servers around the world. A start-up, Boundary, hopes to make a Big Data play out of mapping all this near chaos, improving performance and eventually predicti...', 'lead_paragraph': ' With thousands of different software applications flying around the cloud of a data center’s computer servers and storage devices, things can get complex. There might be a business in explaining the story of their travels to overtaxed system managers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/technology/15bits-boundary-pic/15bits-boundary-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 857, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/technology/15bits-boundary-pic/15bits-boundary-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1146, 'width': 1369, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Boundary: Keeping Cloud Software in Shape', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boundary Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T23:11:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '',