, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9df222af-3b83-5778-a4b0-ef62dd77a6c2', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9df222af-3b83-5778-a4b0-ef62dd77a6c2'}, {'abstract': 'Would a fully equipped outdoor kitchen with appliances increase the resale value of my house?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/garden/do-outdoor-kitchens-increase-home-values-market-ready.html', 'snippet': 'Would a fully equipped outdoor kitchen with appliances increase the resale value of my house?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. Would a fully equipped outdoor kitchen with appliances increase the resale value of my house?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/garden/16MARKET/16MARKET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/garden/16MARKET/16MARKET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Market Ready', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Market Ready', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kitchens', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T23:44:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/731696c5-8819-559e-8d5d-b2d919d244db', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/731696c5-8819-559e-8d5d-b2d919d244db'}, {'abstract': 'So, big whoop, it turns out that some iPad designer at New York Magazine hit a home run in the bottom of the ninth to beat The New York Times Magazine. Winning isn’t everything.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/15/new-york-times-magazine-plays-new-york-magazine-in-softball-everyone-gets-confused-about-whos-on-which-team/', 'snippet': 'So, big whoop, it turns out that some iPad designer at New York Magazine hit a home run in the bottom of the ninth to beat The New York Times Magazine. Winning isn’t everything.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Where we left off, on the fertile lowlands of Central Park’s public softball fields, our heroes from The New York Times Magazine were celebrating their first softball victory of the season (and maybe the last few years) against their archrival, The New Yorker. The score was around 9-1, some said. If only that were the only score of the summer we had to recall.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Times Magazine Plays New York Magazine in Softball, Everyone Gets Confused About Who’s On Which Team', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T23:48:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Kelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1156d6a-2514-59a9-bf06-72e16922828a', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1156d6a-2514-59a9-bf06-72e16922828a'}, {'abstract': 'The Food and Drug Administration issued a warning on Wednesday after three children died from respiratory arrest caused by regular doses of codeine after surgery to treat sleep apnea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/health/warning-issued-on-codeine-for-children.html', 'snippet': 'The Food and Drug Administration issued a warning on Wednesday after three children died from respiratory arrest caused by regular doses of codeine after surgery to treat sleep apnea.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Food and Drug Administration issued a warning on Wednesday after three children died from respiratory arrest caused by regular doses of codeine after surgery to treat sleep apnea. The agency cautioned parents and health workers to watch for symptoms of overdose, like unusual sleepiness, difficulty being aroused or awakened, confusion or noisy and difficult breathing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Warning Issued on Codeine for Children', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Warning Issued On Codeine for Children', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Codeine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APNEA (SLEEP DISORDER)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T23:50:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5152ca61-bb89-582b-8e2d-727c52be835e', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5152ca61-bb89-582b-8e2d-727c52be835e'}, {'abstract': 'Running back David Wilson, a 2012 first-round draft pick from Virginia Tech, expects to be a starter at some point, though he realizes it will take time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/sports/football/giants-top-draft-pick-david-wilson-is-eager-to-contribute.html', 'snippet': 'Running back David Wilson, a 2012 first-round draft pick from Virginia Tech, expects to be a starter at some point, though he realizes it will take time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — David Wilson jogged close to the sideline, his right hand gripping a ball. In that moment at Monday’s practice, Wilson could hear the fans just 10 feet away.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/sports/Y-GIANTS/Y-GIANTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/sports/Y-GIANTS/Y-GIANTS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1581, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/sports/Y-GIANTS/Y-GIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/16/sports/Y-GIANTS/Y-GIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/sports/Y-GIANTS/Y-GIANTS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Giants’ Top Pick Shows Grit and Speed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Giants’ Top Pick Shows Grit And Speed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-15T23:56:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89fe25a1-f67b-5b49-9872-0706ea73637c', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89fe25a1-f67b-5b49-9872-0706ea73637c'}, {'abstract': 'A turtle pond installed by the popular children’s book author Jan Brett has apparently attracted at least one resident, not to mention a giant bullfrog.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/garden/even-turtles-need-a-place-to-call-home-a-conversation-with-the-author-jan-brett-qa.html', 'snippet': 'A turtle pond installed by the popular children’s book author Jan Brett has apparently attracted at least one resident, not to mention a giant bullfrog.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two years ago, the children’s-book author and illustrator Jan Brett and her husband, Joseph Hearne, a bassist with the Boston Symphony Orchestra, installed a turtle pond on the grounds of their two-acre home in Norwell, Mass. It was inspired by her plan to write a book about an Eastern box turtle with wildflowers and ferns sprouting from its shell. In “Mossy,” due out next month (G. P. Putnam’s Sons; $17.99), the turtle spends some unhappy months on display at a natural-history museum until a penitent biologist restores it to its habitat.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 