r Joke Tied To Shootings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aurora, Colo, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Merchant Marine Academy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Gregory F', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T00:21:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariel Kaminer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaminer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22eca2eb-1b6e-57df-88ea-589753f67d59', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22eca2eb-1b6e-57df-88ea-589753f67d59'}, {'abstract': 'The legislation would allow for a casino to be built in Prince George’s County and permit table games in casinos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/us/maryland-casino-bill-goes-to-voters.html', 'snippet': 'The legislation would allow for a casino to be built in Prince George’s County and permit table games in casinos.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Maryland will get another casino and expand table games statewide if voters approve a measure signed by Gov. Martin O’Malley on Wednesday. The legislation would allow for a casino to be built in Prince George’s County and permit table games in casinos. It also would enable the state’s casinos to stay open all day and lower taxes at some of them. Mr. O’Malley said it would create 2,300 jobs and generate $200 million for education. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maryland: Casino Bill Goes to Voters',