/15/espnfc-press-pass-debuts/', 'snippet': 'A new global soccer show, “ESPNFC Press Pass” debuted worldwide on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ESPN’s English-language global soccer show — “ESPNFC Press Pass” — debuted Wednesday in the United States and will be carried throughout the coming European season. The 30-minute show will be carried on the ESPNEWS channel six nights a week, Monday through Saturday at 2 a.m. Eastern (Sunday through Friday at 11 p.m. Pacific).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘ESPNFC Press Pass’ Debuts', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T02:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oliver Tse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oliver', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6683bd18-e9b9-57be-9c00-15c8e0de0dfe', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6683bd18-e9b9-57be-9c00-15c8e0de0dfe'}, {'abstract': 'Two and a half years after the earthquake, the pressing need for safe, stable housing for all displaced people in Haiti remains unmet, despite billions of dollars in reconstruction aid.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/world/americas/years-after-haiti-quake-safe-housing-is-dream-for-multitudes.html', 'snippet': 'Two and a half years after the earthquake, the pressing need for safe, stable housing for all displaced people in Haiti remains unmet, despite billions of dollars in reconstruction aid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORT-AU-PRINCE, Haiti — Since the earthquake of Jan. 12, 2010, a scrappy 12-year-old boy named Givenson Fanfan has been sleeping on the rock-hard floor of a tent pitched in a fetid camp dominated by a 50-foot tower of trash. He dreams of a bed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/world/JP-HAITI-2/JP-HAITI-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/16/world/JP-HAITI-2/JP-HAITI-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/world/JP-HAITI-2/JP-HAITI-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/world/JP-HAITI-2/JP-HAITI-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/world/JP-HAITI-2/JP-HAITI-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/16/world/JP-HAITI-2/JP-HAITI-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/world/JP-HAITI-2/JP-HAITI-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Years After Haiti Quake, Safe Housing Is a Dream for Many', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': Non