ganizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T11:41:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f783f10-2d9a-51dd-aecf-1eb31e0b780d', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f783f10-2d9a-51dd-aecf-1eb31e0b780d'}, {'abstract': 'Bared flesh is common in experimental modern dance. And sometimes — infrequently — it succeeds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/arts/dance/nakedness-in-dance-taken-to-extremes.html', 'snippet': 'Bared flesh is common in experimental modern dance. And sometimes — infrequently — it succeeds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOW do you react to the look of a naked body onstage? Thirty-four years ago, as part of a friend’s bachelor party, I went to a London strip club with a group of seven other men. We were all in our early 20s; most of them were distinctly upper-crust; some qualified as what the English call chinless wonders and Hooray Henrys. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/arts/19NAKED1_SPAN/19JPNAKED1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/19/arts/19NAKED1_SPAN/19JPNAKED1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url