ne even though he knew it would invite comparison with one of the greatest chase scenes of all time, the one in “The French Connection” with Gene Hackman in a car going after a bad guy in a train on the tracks overhead. As Mr. Koepp explained in this article about the difficulties of getting a pursuit right: “Shooting a chase scene in New York City, you’re standing on the shoulders of that giant. I almost didn’t do it, but I love the trestles.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Your Favorite Movie Chase Scene?', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Thrill of the Chase, Post-‘French Connection’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Damon, Matt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedkin, William', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hackman, Gene', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keaton, Buster', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koepp, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McQueen, Steve', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T16:20:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed1c1064-90bd-5d5f-84dd-12149f878af3', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed1c1064-90bd-5d5f-84dd-12149f878af3'}, {'abstract': 'A young communicator uses song and graphics to deconstruct the fight over GMO foods.', 'web_url': 