er-with-a-twist-as-actresses-trade-off-old-times-roles/', 'snippet': 'In Ian Rickson’s forthcoming production, Kristin Scott Thomas and Lia Williams will alternate in the lead female roles, opposite Rufus Sewell.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Most actors have enough layers to explore with just one character in “Old Times,” an enigmatic 1971 play about identity and fractured memories by Harold Pinter, the Nobel Prize winner best known for psychological chillers like the “The Homecoming” and “The Caretaker.” But the theater director Ian Rickson has thrown down a challenge to leading ladies Kristin Scott Thomas and Lia Williams for an coming London revival of “Old Times” – they will alternate in the female roles of Kate and Anna, old friends who have not seen each other in 20 years. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Director Plans Pinter With a Twist, as Actresses Trade Off ‘Old Times’ Roles', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Director Plans Pinter With a Nightly Twist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Sonia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pinter, Harold', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rickson, Ian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott Thomas, Kristin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sewell, Rufus', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Lia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T16:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb3d073b-be4a-5ada-9e63-56a3cd41fd9c', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb3d073b-be4a-5ada-9e63-56a3cd41fd9c'}, {'abstract': 'Even as he crafted the Emancipation Proclamation, the president was making plans to ship freed slaves to Central America.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/lincolns-panama-plan/', 'snippet': 'Even as he crafted the Emancipation Proclamation, the president was making plans to ship freed slaves to Central America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Aug. 14 1862, Abraham Lincoln hosted a “Deputation of Free Negroes” at the White House, led by the Rev. Joseph Mitchell, commissioner of emigration for the Interior Department. It was the first time African Americans had been invited to the White House on a policy matter. The five men were there to discuss a scheme that even a contemporary described as a “simply absurd” piece of “charlatanism”: resettling emancipated slaves on a 10,000-acre parcel of land in present-day Panama. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lincoln’s Panama Plan', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Panama', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T16:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Beard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://articl