quare Offers Flat-Rate Plan for Small Businesses', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Commerce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Square Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T17:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08426bc6-3154-5a9a-bd17-f1a0cd8fe357', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08426bc6-3154-5a9a-bd17-f1a0cd8fe357'}, {'abstract': 'Fewer teenagers than one might have expected report having oral sex before intercourse.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/the-slightly-surprising-sex-lives-of-teenagers/', 'snippet': 'Fewer teenagers than one might have expected report having oral sex before intercourse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New numbers show fewer teenagers than you might expect report having oral sex before vaginal sex. The myth of teenagers experimenting with oral sex, and not really considering it “sex,” has been around for a while, but this new data, from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention’s National Survey of Family Growth and reported in The Times’s Health section, shows that teenagers themselves tell researchers something different.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Slightly Surprising Sex Lives of Teenagers', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 