tist Jonathan Horowitz thinks that contemporary art should be more engaged with the issues being raised by the election.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Art Out of November’s Election', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making Art Out of Presidential Politics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horowitz, Jonathan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CONTEMPORARY ARTS MUSEUM', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hammer Museum', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T18:38:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9c03d5f-1023-5cfe-bc1d-9ff766dc1935', 'word_count': 330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9c03d5f-1023-5cfe-bc1d-9ff766dc1935'}, {'abstract': 'David Coulthard drove a Red Bull Formula One demonstration vehicle up to 190 miles per hour through the Lincoln Tunnel, Red Bull claimed.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/wheelies-the-federal-speed-edition/', 'snippet': 'David Coulthard drove a Red Bull Formula One demonstration vehicle up to 190 miles per hour through the Lincoln Tunnel, Red Bull claimed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which we bring you motoring news from around the Web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheelies: The Federal Speed Edition', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coulthard, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bentley Motors Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Endowment for International Peace', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fisker Automotive', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T18:39:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c826e193-0f94-510f-91cc-a1540416243c', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c826e193-0f94-510f-91cc-a1540416243c'}, {'abstract': 'The creative director of Dior fine jewelry is the latest to brilliantly re-imagine our signature initial.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/fleur-show/', 'snippet': 'The creative director of Dior fine jewelry is the latest to brilliantly re-imagine our signature initial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T asked the Paris-based creative director of Dior fine jewelry, Victoire de Castellane, to redesign the magazine’s signature initial for the fall women’s issue knowing she’d create something wild and completely wonderful. Translating her elaborate three-dimensional jewels into a flat, two-dimensional illustration for our magazine was no easy task. To do so de Castellane looked to her home city, Paris, for inspiration. “I very much like to stroll around le jardin des Bagatelles, in particular the iris garden,” she explains. Below, de Castellane talks about the T that’s 