ames New Director', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indianapolis Museum Names New Director', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, MAXWELL L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Museum of Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indianapolis (Ind)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T19:24:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b816d5db-d003-51cb-9da3-3baf0e51bcf9', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b816d5db-d003-51cb-9da3-3baf0e51bcf9'}, {'abstract': 'In theory, customer property at a brokerage firm should be even more secure than money deposited in a bank. Somehow, it never quite seems to work out that way.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/after-mf-global-a-need-to-find-new-ways-to-protect-customers/', 'snippet': 'In theory, customer property at a brokerage firm should be even more secure than money deposited in a bank. Somehow, it never quite seems to work out that way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The MF Global story still lingers as an insolvency matter, but now we hear rumblings that there will be no criminal charges. It may well be that no crimes were committed, but if this is so, it is time to seriously rethink how broker-dealers handle customer property.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After MF Global, a Need to Find New Ways to Protect Customers', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commodities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Deposit Insurance Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MF Global', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities Investor Protection Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T19:25:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen J. Lubben', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Lubben', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71e7ca02-d212-5b88-90c7-e452fafcc0ef', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71e7ca02-d212-5b88-90c7-e452fafcc0ef'}, {'abstract': 'Rental car insurance is available for luxury cars for an extra fee, under American Express’s premium option.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/getting-rental-car-coverage-for-luxury-vehicles/', 'snippet': 'Rental car insurance is available for luxury cars for an extra fee, under American Express’s premium option.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bucks recently reported on the differences in rental car insurance that consumers get, depending on which credit card they use to pay for the rental. The report noted that for basic coverage, available to cardholders at no charge, the major card networks generally exclude luxury vehicles and that American Express also excludes some popular sport utility vehicles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Rental Car Coverage for Luxury Vehicles', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Insurance and Liability', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami (Fla)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T19:29:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c79bdd12-6f7f-5e2c-91b7-8451c01af76f', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c79bdd12-6f7f-5e2c-91b7-8451c01af76f'}, {'abstract': 'Gentlemen’s clubs in Tampa, Fla., and Charlotte, N.C., are extending a friendly welcome to conventiongoers — even as officials in both parties warn against partaking.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/at-conventions-strip-clubs-are-eager-for-business/', 'snippet': 'Gentlemen’s clubs in Tampa, Fla., and Charlotte, N.C., are extending a friendly welcome to conventiongoers — even as officials in both parties warn against partaking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The convention organizers say no, no, no. But the gentlemen’s clubs of Tampa, Fla., and Charlotte, N.C., are saying yes, yes, yes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Conventions, Strip Clubs Are Eager for Business', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NIGHTCLUBS AND CABARETS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strip Clubs and Strippers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Penthouse', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican National Committee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T19:33:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3eb1f38c-cc9e-5f43-a224-7ebd24338a93', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3eb1f38c-cc9e-5f43-a224-7ebd24338a93'}, {'abstract': 'Cole Haan’s first limited-edition women’s collaboration features shoes by Olivia Kim of Opening Ceremony and Jen Brill, a brand ambassador for Chanel.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/sole-sisters/', 'snippet': 'Cole Haan’s first limited-edition women’s collaboration features shoes by Olivia Kim of Opening Ceremony and Jen Brill, a brand ambassador for Chanel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cole Haan’s recent collaborations — with the musician Theophilus London on a pair of blue suede bucks and with the recording artist and designer Hiroshi Fujiwara on neon-accented wingtips — have offered men of style a new view of the venerable footwear brand. This fall, the company is giving its women’s line a similar treatment. For the first limited-edition women’s collaboration, Olivia Kim, Opening Ceremony’s vice president of creative, and her pal Jen Brill, a brand ambassador for Chanel and creative consultant, have created a collection of shoes that can be worn from day to night. “Being able to run around the city comfortably and still look cute is always a challenge,” Brill says. “That was the starting point of the design process.” Both women grew up wearing Cole Haan shoes, and for inspiration they turned to looks from the company’s archive, like a leather fisherman sandal from the mid-1990s and a 1970s clog. The twist? “We wanted to use colors that were different from what you may expect traditionally from Cole Haan,” Kim says of their collection’s three styles: a strappy sandal ($528), an ankle-strap pump ($528) and an ankle boot ($548), all rendered in jewel-toned Italian suede. “We personally love rich, saturated colors,” added Kim, whose hair is sometimes frosted pink. (Brill’s signature is red lips.) The Chelsea collection will be available Sept. 10 at the Cole Haan SoHo store (128 Prince Street; 212-219-8240). Kim and Brill, meanwhile, are hard at work on their holiday line; they say to expect metallic pastels and plenty of flash.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '92', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sole Sisters', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sole Sisters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T19:38:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bea1e35-565a-528e-ad83-377ce4e9955f', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bea1e35-565a-528e-ad83-377ce4e9955f'}, {'abstract': 'In a city that offers a window into South Africa’s past, Johannesburgers are working to create a vibrant future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/travel/36-hours-in-johannesburg.html', 'snippet': 'In a city that offers a window into South Africa’s past, Johannesburgers are working to create a vibrant future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOURISTS who bypass Johannesburg and head straight to Cape Town or out on safari are missing one of Africa’s most thrilling metropolises. This former gold-rush town suffered in the aftermath of apartheid, but the revitalization that came with South Africa’s hosting of the soccer World Cup in 2010 has blossomed. With a major face-lift of the city’s infrastructure — including the two-year-old mass transit rail system, the Gautrain, which was completed in June — Johannesburg is showing off its virtues and overcoming its vices. Although crime in some precincts remains stubbornly high and a bit of caution is recommended, downtown Johannesburg is in the midst of a revival. Nowadays, young Johannesburgers from different backgrounds are working together to remake their city for the next generation, tapping into a wellspring of creative energy and entrepreneurial spirit. Parts of Johannesburg’s once-decrepit inner city have turned into a vital gathering place, including an old parking garage that now houses a food and fashion market, and a one-time alcohol warehouse that is today stocked with galleries and restaurants. New enticements seem to pop up every few months in this fast-changing dynamo of a city.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/travel/19HOURS_SPAN/19HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/19/travel/19HOURS_SPAN/19HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 342}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'imag