, 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/685a03e2-b404-5ca5-9d17-6043d30f2147', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/685a03e2-b404-5ca5-9d17-6043d30f2147'}, {'abstract': 'The military reaches out into the civilian crowd for new ideas on combat vehicles.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/darpa-to-the-people-you-think-it-up-we-make-sure-it-shoots/', 'snippet': 'The military reaches out into the civilian crowd for new ideas on combat vehicles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most of us know what the term “crowdsourcing” means. It’s been around for more than five years now, and it’s been used to tackle big, complex tasks ranging from finding many people (after natural disasters) to finding one (after a plane crash). It’s been used for everyday problems like traffic and to answer scientific research questions. Crowdsourcing has even been used to make things, from books to videos.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Darpa to the People: You Think It Up, We Make Sure It Shoots', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crowdsourcing (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Advanced Research Projects Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T20:11:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffery DelViscio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffery', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DelViscio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99885830-98c8-5149-873c-172316d6ba52', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99885830-98c8-5149-873c-172316d6ba52'}, {'abstract': 'The victims were mostly young men returning to their villages for Id al-Fitr, the Islamic festival that marks the end of Ramadan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/world/asia/pakistani-taliban-kill-22-shiites-in-bus-attack.html', 'snippet': 'The victims were mostly young men returning to their villages for Id al-Fitr, the Islamic festival that marks the end of Ramadan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — Pakistani Taliban militants pulled 22 Shiites off buses and gunned them down in a remote northern mountain pass on Thursday, in the latest iteration of a pattern of attacks targeting religious minorities.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistani Taliban Kill 22 Shiites in Bus Attack', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taliban Gun Down 22 Shiites Pulled Off Buses in Remote Northern Pakistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T20:12:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/925c13de-4df4-51ca-8a0b-6731f99444c5', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/925c13de-4df4-51ca-8a0b-6731f99444c5'}, {'abstract': 'The promoters of the CBGB music festival have joined with Amnesty International to raise funds for the members of Pussy Riot, who are on trial in Moscow.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/cbgb-joins-efforts-to-support-russian-punk-band/', 'snippet': 'The promoters of the CBGB music festival have joined with Amnesty International to raise funds for the members of Pussy Riot, who are on trial in Moscow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The promoters of the CBGB music festival in New York say they plan to sell special T-shirts and other merchandise online to raise money for the jailed members of the Russian punk rock band Pussy Riot, who face a prison term for singing a protest song in a church. On Friday in Moscow a judge declared them guilty of hooliganism. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'CBGB Joins Efforts to Support Russian Punk Band', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMNESTY INTERNATIONAL', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBGB', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pussy Riot', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T20:24:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'org