icker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robots and Robotics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Robot & Frank (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T20:28:25+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Movies', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/8a8614cf-683f-5201-8638-6ef7d24429c7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/8a8614cf-683f-5201-8638-6ef7d24429c7'}, {'abstract': 'Are you on board with exorbitantly priced skincare products? That’s the $64,000 question. Plus tax.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/samurai-shopper-dream-creams/', 'snippet': 'Are you on board with exorbitantly priced skincare products? That’s the $64,000 question. Plus tax.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Samurai recently went to see the newish movie “The Queen of Versailles,” a documentary about people with beer tastes and Champagne pocketbooks. But for the Samurai Shopper, that’s backward; my luxurious taste is often adulterated by a Pabst Blue Ribbon budget. Through the tricky economic stratagem of robbing Peter to pay Paul, I can occasionally spring for super-expensive skin care products that lighten, brighten and tighten. Why would I do this? Superman had kryptonite; I have Cle de Peau’s La Creme ($775 for 1.7 ounces).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Samurai Shopper | Dream Creams', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T20:29:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By S.S. Fair', 'person': [{'firstname': 'S.', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastn