nt_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f741172d-a0ac-53ae-89b6-cfad2caa7cf6', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f741172d-a0ac-53ae-89b6-cfad2caa7cf6'}, {'abstract': 'The spooked animal bolted near Columbus Circle, dumped its driver and toppled its carriage containing passengers, running into two cars. The horse escaped serious injury.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/carriage-horse-collides-with-car/', 'snippet': 'The spooked animal bolted near Columbus Circle, dumped its driver and toppled its carriage containing passengers, running into two cars. The horse escaped serious injury.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A spooked carriage horse burst out of line near Central Park on Thursday, thundered into the busy traffic on Columbus Circle, dumped his driver and two passengers, struck two cars, shed the wreckage of his carriage and ran free for four blocks before being captured on Ninth Avenue, the authorities and witnesses said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '3 Are Injured When Horse Sheds Coach in Manhattan', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '3 Are Injured When Horse Sheds Coach In Manhattan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CENTRAL PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'COLUMBUS CIRCLE (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T20:47:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/573e5106-a23d-532c-b0ab-e7ee19f29143', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/573e5106-a23d-532c-b0ab-e7ee19f29143'}, {'abstract': 'In the United States, unlike in the Old World, the wine industry did not evolve to make intriguing, inexpensive wines. But they do exist for $20 or less.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/dining/12-values-in-american-wines-the-pour.html', 'snippet': 'In the United States, unlike in the Old World, the wine industry did not evolve to make intriguing, inexpensive wines. But they do exist for $20 or less.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A FEW weeks ago, I wrote about wines at the coveted intersection of high value and low price. I suggested that the greatest concentration of value, where you could find wines that were not merely palatable, but exciting, was in the $15 to $25 range. And I recommended 20 bottles at $20 that were the kinds of wines I would look forward to drinking any day of the week.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/dining/22POUR_SPAN/22POUR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/22/dining/22POUR_SPAN/22POUR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/dining/22POUR_SPAN/22POUR_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/dining/22POUR_SPAN/22POUR_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height'