_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1ea3008-63ab-5299-97ca-47979352584c', 'word_count': 990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1ea3008-63ab-5299-97ca-47979352584c'}, {'abstract': '“Cosmopolis,” directed by David Cronenberg and based on a novel by Don DeLillo, follows a young man with plenty of money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/movies/movie-review-cosmopolis-directed-by-david-cronenberg.html', 'snippet': '“Cosmopolis,” directed by David Cronenberg and based on a novel by Don DeLillo, follows a young man with plenty of money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first image in David Cronenberg’s “Cosmopolis,” a cold, funny number about the erotics of money and the seduction of death, is that of a chrome grille on a white stretch limousine. The shot is a close-up that’s so tightly framed that the grille, with its U shape and vertical bars, looks as if it were smiling. It also looks like a shark, a perfect starting point for a story about a master of the universe who, over one long day and night, lives, eats, evacuates and fornicates in the limo. A master who, like some kind of millennial Jonah, has taken up residence in the belly of a new beast.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17COSMO_SPAN/17COSMO_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17COSMO_SPAN/17COSMO_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17COSMO_SPAN/17COSMO_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17CO