ord_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14e0942a-c636-5dc2-a120-409f084b3cc2'}, {'abstract': 'Vice magazine’s annual photo issue, showcasing a selection of projects by some of the magazine’s favorite photographers, is equal parts weird, beautiful and grotesque.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/taking-a-look-at-vice/', 'snippet': 'Vice magazine’s annual photo issue, showcasing a selection of projects by some of the magazine’s favorite photographers, is equal parts weird, beautiful and grotesque.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vice magazine’s annual photo issue, showcasing a selection of projects by some of the magazine’s favorite photographers, is equal parts weird, beautiful and grotesque. The issue was originally produced by photographer (and former Vice photo editor) Ryan McGinley in 2001, and has become something of an institution for new photography. This year’s selection of pictures, on display last week at Brooklyn’s Black and White Gallery, was as intriguing as always, featuring images from more established artists like the South African photographer Roger Ballen (who photographed the band Die Antwoord for the Times magazine earlier this year) and younger artists like Elizabeth Renstrom (who is straight out of photography school) and 17-year-old Olivia Bee (who took the photographs for the Times magazine’s story on teaching teens about sex).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Grotesque, Weird Beauty of Vice’s Photo Issue', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGinley, Ryan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vice (Magazine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T21:28:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Cwynar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cwynar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c8cdc38-2c32-5c6a-8bc7-8dcafe53e3dd', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c8cdc38-2c32-5c6a-8bc7-8dcafe53e3dd'}, {'abstract': 'Photos from South Africa, Malta, Syria and India.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/pictures-of-the-day-south-africa-and-elsewhere-3/', 'snippet': 'Photos from South Africa, Malta, Syria and India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos from South Africa, Malta, Syria and India.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: South Africa and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malta', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T21:31:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d55d9e0a-15eb-5c11-b515-5468821f64a6', 'word_count': 13, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d55d9e0a-15eb-5c11-b515-5468821f64a6'}, {'abstract': 'The N.H.L. players’ union has some interesting proposals, but the owners have the upper hand in the labor dispute and their primary goal is cutting salaries.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/in-n-h-l-negotiation-the-unions-good-ideas-may-not-matter/', 'snippet': 'The N.H.L. players’ union has some interesting proposals, but the owners have the upper hand in the labor dispute and their primary goal is cutting salaries.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:59 a.m. | Updated Commissioner Gary Bettman and the owners may be coming off as the villains in the eyes of the public in the N.H.L. labor negotiations, but that won’t matter to them one bit, not while they have the chance to save hundreds of millions of dollars each year with a new collective bargaining agreement, and certainly not while they have the upper hand in these negotiations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In N.H.L. Negotiations, Union’s Good Ideas May Not Matter', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettman, Gary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fehr, Donald', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T21:32:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bf06762-a610-5f70-9495-e44383882bd9', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bf06762-a610-5f70-9495-e44383882bd9'}, {'abstract': 'Both President Obama and Mitt Romney have agreed to suspend their campaign commercials on Sept. 11, in honor of the 2001 terrorist attacks.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/obama-and-romney-to-suspend-ads-on-911/', 'snippet': 'Both President Obama and Mitt Romney have agreed to suspend their campaign commercials on Sept. 11, in honor of the 2001 terrorist attacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is quite likely the only reprieve Americans will get from what is expected to be an especially heavy and sustained barrage of political advertising this fall. But on Sept. 11, President Obama and Mitt Romney have agreed to suspend their campaign commercials.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama and Romney to Suspend Ads on 9/11', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Advertising Break: Pausing to Commemorate 9/11', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanksville (PA)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T21:33:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1586a496-0626-5ae3-bfda-14170b5e4246', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1586a496-0626-5ae3-bfda-14170b5e4246'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine says it is “entirely satisfied that the language in question in his recent column was an unintentional error.” His column will return to the magazine on Sept. 7. CNN likewise announced Mr. Zakaria’s return from suspension.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/after-review-time-says-fareed-zakarias-plagiarism-was-isolated-incident/', 'snippet': 'The magazine says it is “entirely satisfied that the language in question in his recent column was an unintentional error.” His column will return to the magazine on Sept. 7. CNN likewise announced Mr. Zakaria’s return from suspension.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Time magazine and CNN are reinstating the commentator Fareed Zakaria after a review of his work in light of his admission that he plagiarized parts of a New Yorker article in a recent column for Time.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Time and CNN Reinstate Journalist After Review', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Time and CNN Reinstate Journalist After Review', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zakaria, Fareed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time (Magazine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T21:34:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b805e5e8-89df-515a-b638-b94b03c5a7a9', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b805e5e8-89df-515a-b638-b94b03c5a7a9'}, {'abstract': 'The common American idea of opera — as the most solemn kind of date night — has profoundly damaged it in this country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/arts/music/how-hollywood-films-are-killing-opera.html', 'snippet': 'The common American idea of opera — as the most solemn kind of date night — has profoundly damaged it in this country.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The opera?” the main character of Kenneth Lonergan’s recent film, “Margaret,” sourly asks her mother. “Why are you going to the opera?”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17MARGARET_SPAN/17MARGARET_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17MARGARET_SPAN/17MARGARET_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17MARGARET_SPAN/0817MARGARETjp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17MARGARET_SPAN/0817MARGARETjp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 977, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17MARGARET_SPAN/17MARGARET_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17MARGARET_SPAN/17MARGARET_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17MARGARET_SPAN/17MARGARET_SPAN-thumbLarge-v3.jp