itz.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/books/review/batter-up.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to a recent sketchbook by Rick Meyerowitz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Batter Up', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Batter Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T21:40:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/c13b3caf-4851-5a60-923e-6fe17c2d7333', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c13b3caf-4851-5a60-923e-6fe17c2d7333'}, {'abstract': 'For “A Living Man Declared Dead and Other Chapters I-XVIII,” the artist spent years chasing down stories and people to photograph.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/arts/design/taryn-simon-exhibition-at-moma.html', 'snippet': 'For “A Living Man Declared Dead and Other Chapters I-XVIII,” the artist spent years chasing down stories and people to photograph.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Along with everything else that’s been deflated, downsized or drained of its power in our millennial lives, the image, formerly worth 1,000 words is now worth about 200 — maybe 250 on a good day. Now we rely on captions to convey meaning. These texts were already becoming obligatory in the 1930s, according to Walter Benjamin, but are now virtually a medium of their own.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17SIMON_SPAN/17SIMON_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 