t & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Schwendener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ea79fbc-3ffe-5e77-8d6b-7da560c1289e', 'word_count': 937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ea79fbc-3ffe-5e77-8d6b-7da560c1289e'}, {'abstract': 'As his wedding day loomed, the actor Andrew McCarthy braved more than just the snows of Kilimanjaro.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/t-magazine/cold-feat-andrew-mccarthy-climbs-kilimanjaro.html', 'snippet': 'As his wedding day loomed, the actor Andrew McCarthy braved more than just the snows of Kilimanjaro.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My pack is by the door; I leave in the morning. I am standing with my fiancée, D, in the kitchen. The sight of my waiting backpack has triggered her anxiety. She’s a different person than she was just a few minutes ago. “You’re always coming and going, leaving and coming, you have no time to love me,” she blurts out. We have just returned from a long, romantic dinner, after having spent the afternoon together. And now the tears come.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '154', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/t-magazine/19talk-mccarthy-slide-EZL2/19talk-mccarthy-slide-EZL2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/15/t-magazine/19talk-mccarthy-slide-EZL2/19talk-mccarthy-slide-EZL2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/t-magazine/19talk-mccarthy-slide-EZL2/19talk-mccarthy-slide-EZL2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_nam