: 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/33ea9864-de12-565a-85a2-3cd9c5cd59e1', 'word_count': 1505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33ea9864-de12-565a-85a2-3cd9c5cd59e1'}, {'abstract': 'When it comes to his tax returns, Mitt Romney expects the public to accept his word.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/just-trust-me/', 'snippet': 'When it comes to his tax returns, Mitt Romney expects the public to accept his word.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney deigned to answer questions about his tax returns today, assuring reporters at a news conference that he had never paid less than 13 percent of his income in taxes in the last decade. That’s considerably lower than the rate many middle-class families pay, but what’s really remarkable is that Mr. Romney now expects the public to accept his word and move on.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just Trust Me', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T21:59:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9009cbb2-303d-5c98-9c16-17e1e668b404', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9009cbb2-303d-5c98-9c16-17e1e668b404'}, {'abstract': 'If your old network router is acting up, there are some troublesho