ract': 'Bahrain sentenced a leading rights activist to three years in prison on Thursday for “inciting” anti-government protests in speeches and Twitter updates.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/bahrain-sentences-activist-to-3-years-in-prison-for-inciting-protests/', 'snippet': 'Bahrain sentenced a leading rights activist to three years in prison on Thursday for “inciting” anti-government protests in speeches and Twitter updates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bahrain sentenced a leading rights activist to three years in prison on Thursday for “inciting” antigovernment protests in speeches and Twitter updates, the state news agency reports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bahrain Sentences Activist to 3 Years in Prison for ‘Inciting’ Protests', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Assembly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khalifa, Hamad Bin Isa al-', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khawaja, Abdulhadi al-', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajab, Nabeel', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahrain', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manama (Bahrain)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T22:59:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey and Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a109a9e-b9ee-5e08-a538-c89eb396e4c3', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a109a9e-b9ee-5e08-a538-c89eb396e4c3'}, {'abstract': 'Jordin Sparks has the title role in “Sparkle,” a Cinderella tale out of Motown that features the last screen performance by Whitney Houston.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/movies/movie-review-sparkle-with-whitney-houston-and-jordin-sparks.html', 'snippet': 'Jordin Sparks has the title role in “Sparkle,” a Cinderella tale out of Motown that features the last screen performance by Whitney Houston.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is impossible to watch “Sparkle” and not relate its story to the life of Whitney Houston, one of its executive producers. She portrays Emma, a former entertainer turned prim, disapproving church lady in late-1960s Detroit. Emma forsook show business after nearly succumbing to the same excesses that caught up with Houston, who died in February, not long after “Sparkle” was completed. If the film is a sudsy show-business Cinderella story in which Emma’s youngest daughter, Sparkle (Jordin Sparks), ascends to glory, Houston’s presence makes it a cautionary tale.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17SPARKLE_SPAN/17SPARKLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17SPARKLE_SPAN/17SPARKLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17SPARKLE_SPAN/0817SPARKLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17SPARKLE_SPAN/0817SPARKLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17SPARKLE_SPAN/17SPARKLE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17SPARKLE_SPAN/17SPARKLE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/17SPARKLE_SPAN/17SPARKLE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Woman Who Knows the Music Industry, and a Few Who Don’t (Yet)', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Woman Who Knows the Music Industry, and a Few Who Don’t (Yet)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luke, Derek', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sparks, Jordin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Houston, Whitney', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sparkle (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-16T23:08:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1012b8f6-0e3d-5d4c-8e27-25905e439046', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1012b8f6-0e3d-5d4c-8e27-25905e439046'}, {'abstract': '“The Awakening,” directed by Nick Murphy and starring Rebecca Hall and Dominic West, is a ghost story set in an England paralyzed with grief after the traumas of World War I.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/movies/the-awakening-with-rebecca-hall-and-dominic-west.html', 'snippet': '“The Awakening,” directed by Nick Murphy and starring Rebecca Hall and Dominic West, is a ghost story set in an England paralyzed with grief after the traumas of World War I.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sherlock Holmes meets “The Others” in “The Awakening,” a supernatural thriller with a chilly “Masterpiece Theater” gloss and a pretentious, post-Freudian subtext. Ghosts are not merely the restless undead in this sleek first feature directed by Nick Murphy from a screenplay he wrote with Stephen Volk. They are also repressed memories in the subconscious of its luscious female Sherlock, Florence Cathcart (Rebecca Hall, from “Vicky Cristina Barcelona”). More broadly they are the unquiet spirits of the dead in a country paralyzed with grief after the traumas of World War I and the 1918 influenza pandemic. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/arts/0817AWAKENING_SPAN/0817AWAKENING_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'su