an League, the Yankees and the Rangers seem destined to meet in a couple of months, and the players are not afraid to say it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/sports/baseball/yankees-and-rangers-are-possible-preview-of-playoffs.html', 'snippet': 'With the the two best records in the American League, the Yankees and the Rangers seem destined to meet in a couple of months, and the players are not afraid to say it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Boston Red Sox straggle into New York on Friday, but the truth is that the show has left town. The uniforms of the Yankees and the Red Sox evoke a time gone by, when the teams were close in talent. The Red Sox are bickering and stale and going nowhere now. The real rivalry is the one we just saw.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/sports/17kepner-1/17kepner-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/sports/17kepner-1/17kepner-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1455, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/sports/17kepner-1/17kepner-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/17/sports/17kepner-1/17kepner-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/sports/17kepner-1/17kepner-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees and Rangers: See You in October', 'kicker': 'On Baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yankees and Rangers: See You in October', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Josh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T00:35:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7594bf82-1c63-585d-8c8d-b1310eebd09f', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7594bf82-1c63-585d-8c8d-b1310eebd09f'}, {'abstract': 'The drought represents an opportunity to reimagine how we manage, use and even think about water.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/opinion/dont-waste-this-drought.html', 'snippet': 'The drought represents an opportunity to reimagine how we manage, use and even think about water.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WE’RE in the worst drought in the United States since the 1950s, and we’re wasting it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Waste the Drought', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Waste The Drought', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T00:37:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Fishman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fishman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/90293c16-74c1-5519-981a-2d94aabc57fd', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90293c16-74c1-5519-981a-2d94aabc57fd'}, {'abstract': 'In losing the soap opera, the Syrian government has lost one of its most powerful means of spreading ideas and political messages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/opinion/in-syria-the-soap-opera-is-a-casualty-of-war.html', 'snippet': 'In losing the soap opera, the Syrian government has lost one of its most powerful means of spreading ideas and political messages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the Syrian town my family comes from, every afternoon during the holy month of Ramadan the streets were jammed with people. They were rushing home not only to escape the heat and to prepare the iftar, the evening meal that breaks the fast, but also to catch the latest episodes of their favorite soap operas — the musalsals. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Casualty of War: Soap Operas', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Casualty of War: Soap Operas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ramadan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soap Operas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'ran