y, Bloomberg Decides to Revamp Its Board', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rhea, John B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing Authority (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T01:49:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/964e8567-fcfb-543a-a38a-fb9cf009c161', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/964e8567-fcfb-543a-a38a-fb9cf009c161'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s new rules restricting access to counsel for prisoners not actively challenging their detention are being challenged. The rules are neither fair nor constitutional.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/opinion/the-right-to-counsel-at-guantanamo-bay.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s new rules restricting access to counsel for prisoners not actively challenging their detention are being challenged. The rules are neither fair nor constitutional.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawyers for the government and for detainees in Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, are scheduled to square off in federal court in Washington on Friday over new rules imposed this spring by the Obama administration restricting access to counsel for prisoners not actively challenging their detention. They are neither fair nor constitutional. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Right to Counsel at Guantánamo Bay', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Right to Counsel at Guant&aacute;namo Bay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T01:50:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/090cef4c-d318-51aa-8d6e-48db8a7a724d', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/090cef4c-d318-51aa-8d6e-48db8a7a724d'}, {'abstract': 'While American politicians refuse to enact gun control laws, American gun enthusiasts are buying up Russian-made Kalashnikov rifles and shotguns by the tens of thousands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/opinion/that-hot-new-rifle-from-russia.html', 'snippet': 'While American politicians refuse to enact gun control laws, American gun enthusiasts are buying up Russian-made Kalashnikov rifles and shotguns by the tens of thousands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an eerie postscript to the cold war, American gun enthusiasts have been buying Kalashnikov rifles and shotguns by the tens of thousands, helping the Russian arms manufacturer stay afloat in a global market oversaturated with its AK-47s, long the weapon of choice among the world’s insurgents and armies. American sales of single-shot civilian versions of the Kalashnikov rose by 50 percent last year among buyers impressed with the automatic model’s lethal accuracy in the world’s trouble spots.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'That Hot New Rifle From Russia', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That Hot New Rifle From Russia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arms Trade', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Rifle Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aurora, Colo, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T01:53:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf7d9b23-5b21-59a2-87d0-4f28c5567a67', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf7d9b23-5b21-59a2-87d0-4f28c5567a67'}, {'abstract': 'Despite its almost sacred place in baseball, there is one little secret about batting practice: many players think it is a mind-numbing, flaw-producing, strategically empty exercise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/sports/baseball/batting-practice-cherished-tradition-or-colossal-waste-of-time.html', 'snippet': 'Despite its almost sacred place in baseball, there is one little secret about batting practice: many players think it is a mind-numbing, flaw-producing, strategically empty exercise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Baseball is a sport defined by routines and traditions, and there are few more entrenched than batting practice, a pregame ritual that is far older than most teams that engage in it. For two hours before almost every game, each team dutifully rolls out the batting cage and hits slowly pitched balls to outfields across North America.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source':