rnational Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T02:06:18+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/80a6e16f-aace-5820-9e86-5e9ef5954a92', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/80a6e16f-aace-5820-9e86-5e9ef5954a92'}, {'abstract': 'The Peel Regional Police were unable to immediately confirm whether the remains came from one person.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/world/americas/canada-police-find-human-head-in-an-ontario-river.html', 'snippet': 'The Peel Regional Police were unable to immediately confirm whether the remains came from one person.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The police in Mississauga, Ontario, a Toronto suburb, found a human head in a river on Thursday, a day after they were alerted to a human foot in the same area. The Peel Regional Police were unable to immediately confirm whether the remains came from one person. Detective Randy Cowan said it was unclear whether there had been a murder, but added, “There’s definitely something amiss.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Police Find Human Head in an Ontario River', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Police Find Human Head in an Ontario River', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ontario (Canada)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T02:09:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/22eee826-4b0c-535d-998f-612fec71a7f3', 'word_count': 68, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22eee826-4b0c-535d-998f-612fec71a7f3'}, {'abstract': 'After losing the first three games in the series, the Rangers avoided a sweep by scoring six runs off Yankees relief pitchers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/sports/baseball/yankees-fall-a-bullpen-collapse-short-of-sweeping-the-rangers.html', 'snippet': 'After losing the first three games in the series, the Rangers avoided a sweep by scoring six runs off Yankees relief pitchers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees had beaten the Texas Rangers in three straight games and all was well. The team banners high atop the white facade of their stadium — arranged by record and flittering like lures in a stream — gracefully attested that they were secure in first place, with Baltimore a big, fat six games behind. And so, perhaps the Yankees could ease up just a bit as they went for the sweep.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 671, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1341, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/17/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/sports/KEPNER/KEPNER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Fall a Bullpen Collapse Short of Sweeping the Rangers', 'kicker': 'Rangers 10, Yankees 6', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yanks Fall a Bullpen Collapse Short of Sweeping the Rangers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chamberlain, Joba', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T02:09:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Prager', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prager', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbc72949-c4b1-5183-a411-f735bde1b5b1', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbc72949-c4b1-5183-a411-f735bde1b5b1'}, {'abstract': 'The history of vice-presidential candidates drawn from the House, like Paul Ryan, is entertaining and revealing.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/from-the-house-to-the-white-house/', 'snippet': 'The history of vice-presidential candidates drawn from the House, like Paul Ryan, is entertaining and revealing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In all the media excitement over Mitt Romney’s selection of Representative Paul D. Ryan as his running mate on the Republican ticket, little attention has been focused on the rarity of an incumbent member of the House of Representatives holding second place on a national ticket. Each party has done it twice since 1900, with one success and one failure for both Republicans and Democrats so far. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From the House to the White House', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vice Presidents and Vice Presidency (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bentsen, Lloyd M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferraro, Geraldine A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T02:13:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lewis L. Gould', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lewis', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Gould', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecc233e1-2277-58eb-b9a2-665e05a2c998', 'word_count': 899, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecc233e1-2277-58eb-b9a2-665e05a2c998'}, {'abstract': 'While much is obscure about Egyptian politics, the new president seems to be seeking a fine line between an Army accustomed to power and Islamists hungry for it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/opinion/president-morsis-rebalancing-act-in-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'While much is obscure about Egyptian politics, the new president seems to be seeking a fine line between an Army accustomed to power and Islamists hungry for it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The stunning events in Egypt over the past week have been at least as significant for what didn’t happen as what did. After President Mohamed Morsi replaced the country’s top two generals on Sunday, there were no street protests condemning his actions, no real alarms from Israel and no Army retaliation. In fact, the generals accepted medals of commendation from Mr. Morsi and will serve as his advisers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'President Morsi’s Rebalancing Act', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President Morsi&#8217;s Rebalancing Act', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sinai Peninsula (Egypt)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T02:14:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8ab1cc5-aca5-5b5e-a9d0-5680ddeb5d11', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8ab1cc5-aca5-5b5e-a9d0-5680ddeb5d11'}, {'abstract': 'As many as 1,000 people demonstrated against mining operations in an environmentally fragile part of Tibet on Wednesday, Radio Free Asia reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/world/asia/china-protester-killed-as-police-fire-on-demonstration.html', 'snippet': 'As many as 1,000 people demonstrated against mining operations in an environmentally fragile part of Tibet on Wednesday, Radio Free Asia reported.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The police shot and killed a protester on Wednesday after as many as 1,000 people demonstrated against mining operations in an environmentally fragile part of Tibet, Radio Free Asia reported Thursday. The broadcaster, which quoted an India-based Tibetan exile with contacts in the region, said security forces detained six people and used tear gas and live fire to disperse locals who were protesting against the mine. Government officials claim that the site, in Markham County in the Tibetan Autonomous Region, is being prepared for a power plant. In another matter, the Tibetan Center for Human Rights and Democracy said that two men who this week had set themselves on fire to protest Chinese rule had died of their injuries. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Protester Killed as Police Fire on Demonstration', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Protester Killed as Police Fire on Demonstration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T02:24:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://