ks’ decision to let Jeremy Lin leave for Houston rather than match a three-year, $25 million contract.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/month-later-still-waiting-for-answers-on-lin-move/', 'snippet': 'Not a single team official has stepped forward to explain the Knicks’ decision to let Jeremy Lin leave for Houston rather than match a three-year, $25 million contract.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a touching scene that instantly went viral, Jeremy Lin peered through his computer screen and, across thousands of miles, tried his best to console a heartbroken young Knicks fan. The video chat has been viewed nearly 167,000 times since it was posted to YouTube on Aug. 6. It lasts 9 minutes 18 seconds.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Month Later, Still Waiting for Answers on Lin Move', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Month Later, Still Waiting For Answers On Lin Move', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lin, Jeremy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Rockets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T02:29:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28ce6e6c-5d2b-5d40-9acb-7c15fb681d82', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28ce6e6c-5d2b-5d40-9acb-7c15fb681d82'}, {'abstract': 'Gatherings of a group of California professionals in the depths of unemployment reveal a post-recession landscape where grim frustration battles with the simple desire to find a way out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/us/unemployment-depths-seen-in-california-peer-group.html', 'snippet': 'Gatherings of a group of California professionals in the depths of unemployment reveal a post-recession landscape where grim frustration battles with the simple desire to find a way out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CORONA, Calif. — The analysts pore over the numbers every month, the full menagerie of economic indicators. President Obama and Mitt Romney trade barbs over who is at fault for a sluggish recovery. But here, in a region with one of the highest unemployment rates in the country, other numbers often loom larger. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/us/JP-LONGTERM-1/JP-LONGTERM-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/17/us/JP-LONGTERM-1/JP-LONGTERM-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/us/JP-LONGTERM-1/JP-LONGTERM-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/us/JP-LONGTERM-1/JP-LONGTERM-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/us/JP-LONGTERM-1/JP-LONGTERM-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/17/us/JP-LONGTERM-1/JP-LONGTERM-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/us/JP-LONGTERM-1/JP-LONGTERM-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Long-Term Jobless Regroup to Fight the Odds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Long-Term Jobless Regroup to Fight the Odds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T02:31:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9624038-bfba-5f3e-b743-cac4137e93ae', 'word_count': 1191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9624038-bfba-5f3e-b743-cac4137e93ae'}, {'abstract': 'Democratic candidates running to fill Representative Barney Frank’s seat debated in Massachusetts on Thursday evening.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/democrats-vying-for-barney-franks-seat-go-easy-on-biden-gaffe/', 'snippet': 'Democratic candidates running to fill Representative Barney Frank’s seat debated in Massachusetts on Thursday evening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Joseph Kennedy III, who is hoping to succeed Representative Barney Frank in his suburban Boston district, avoided saying Thursday whether Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. had gone too far when he said that Republicans would “put y’all back in chains.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Vying for Barney Frank’s Seat Go Easy on Biden Gaffe', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frank, Barney', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T02:34:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fd8b456-8296-551b-bf92-d4ca42aa3c7d', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fd8b456-8296-551b-bf92-d4ca42aa3c7d'}, {'abstract': 'Matt Harvey had eight strikeouts in seven and two-thirds innings to produce the finest work of his still-brief career and help the Mets escape Cincinnati with a victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/sports/baseball/matt-harvey-pitches-mets-past-reds.html', 'snippet': 'Matt Harvey had eight strikeouts in seven and two-thirds innings to produce the finest work of his still-brief career and help the Mets escape Cincinnati with a victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CINCINNATI — Manager Terry Collins often marvels at the maturity and makeup of Matt Harvey, the Mets’ precocious rookie right-hander, and he was at it again Thursday afternoon. As he sat in his office with reporters, Collins responded to a question about how successfully Harvey, 23, was blending into his big-league surroundings.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/sports/METS/METS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 789, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/sports/METS/METS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1579, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/sports/METS/METS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/17/sports/METS/METS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/sports/METS/METS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Harvey Pitches to Beat the Rain and the Reds', 'kicker': 'Mets 8, Reds 4', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Harvey Pitches to Beat The Rain and the Reds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Terry L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cincinnati Reds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harvey, Matt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T02:42:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4ea1e0c-9eae-5735-a18c-561fb0d03268', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4ea1e0c-9eae-5735-a18c-561fb0d03268'}, {'abstract': 'Gen. Sedky Sobhi argued that America’s presence in the Middle East and its “one sided” support of Israel had mired it in an unwinnable war with Islamist militants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/world/middleeast/in-paper-chief-of-egypt-army-criticized-us.html', 'snippet': 'Gen. Sedky Sobhi argued that America’s presence in the Middle East and its “one sided” support of Israel had mired it in an unwinnable war with Islamist militants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a student at the United States Army War College in Pennsylvania, the chief of staff of Egypt’s armed forces argued in a paper that the American military presence in the Middle East and its “one sided” support of Israel were fueling hatred toward the United States and miring it in an unwinnable global war with Islamist militants.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Paper, Chief of Egypt’s Army Criticized U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S.-Egypt Tie: Glimpse of Ire By Army Chief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sobhi, Sedky', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Telhami, Shibley', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T02:42:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick and Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/525cd9e1-fbf5-5b22-af85-fb289779188e', 'word_count': 1207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/525cd9e1-fbf5-5b22-af85-fb289779188e'}, {'abstract': 'Our forecast model now gives Mitt Romney a 31.3 percent chance of winning the Electoral College, up from 26.7 percent late last week.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/16/aug-16-why-im-not-buying-the-romney-rally/', 'snippet': 'Our forecast model now gives Mitt Romney a 31.3 percent chance of winning the Electoral College, up from 26.7 percent late last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the political futures market Intrade, shares in Mitt Romney have been a hot commodity this week. As of early Thursday evening, the bettors there gave Mr. Romney a 43.5 percent chance of winning November’s election. That’s up from about 39 percent late last week, before Mr. Romney’s announcement that Representative Paul D. Ryan of Wisconsin would be his running mate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 16: Why I’m Not Buying the Romney Rally', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywo