e’s online anger in China about the dispute over islands claimed by China, Japan and Taiwan. But what was drawing more of the mainland’s attention on the Internet? The tale of a killer’s girlfriend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Perhaps topics like the beautiful moll of a multiple-murdering hoodlum just shot dead by police will always fascinate more than politics — even issues that bristle with anger like territorial sovereignty.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/blogs/flag-rdv/flag-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/blogs/flag-rdv/flag-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1412, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Anger Diverted by the Saga of a Hoodlum’s Girlfriend', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Senkaku Islands', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T03:12:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa031fad-c377-5d41-ba21-39eea80249e8', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa031fad-c377-5d41-ba21-39eea80249e8'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney’s transition team has been working since June, offering a glimpse into what his approach to governing might be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/us/politics/mitt-romneys-transition-team-is-hard-at-work.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney’s transition team has been working since June, offering a glimpse into what his approach to governing might be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As Mitt Romney and Paul D. Ryan fanned out across the country this week, glad-handing voters and donors, a smaller but no less important gathering was taking place on Capitol Hill: Mr. Romney’s transition team met on Tuesday with more than a dozen loyalists from the private and public sectors in space borrowed from a law office.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/us/17transition/17transition-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 580, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/us/17transition/17transition-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 580, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Campaigning Aside, Team Plans a Romney Presidency', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Campaigning Aside, Team Plans a Romney Presidency', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leavitt, Michael O', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Myers, Beth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T03:37:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03a3ceb0-e879-53f1-b821-386002890706', 'word_count': 936, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03a3ceb0-e879-53f1-b821-386002890706'}, {'abstract': 'Running at the beach can cause extra aches and pains for those who aren’t used to it, but sand running can translate into faster times and serve as a form of speed training in areas where hills are scarce.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/the-challenges-of-beach-running/', 'snippet': 'Running at the beach can cause extra aches and pains for those who aren’t used to it, but sand running can translate into faster times and serve as a form of speed training in areas where hills are scarce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mike Musso doesn’t know of a time when he wasn’t running on the beach. “I’d run from my house to the surf beach to hang out,” said Mr. Musso, 20, who grew up at the Jersey Shore and now works there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Challenges of Beach Running', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaches', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muscles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sand and Gravel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T04:01:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jen A. Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jen', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'ra