— an urgent matter as it is soon to be displaced for the park’s renovation.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/could-the-sphere-go-here/', 'snippet': 'Fritz Koenig’s “Sphere for Plaza Fountain,” which was damaged in the Sept. 11 attack and has now been in Battery Park for 10 years, still has no permanent home — an urgent matter as it is soon to be displaced for the park’s renovation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is to become of Fritz Koenig’s “Sphere for Plaza Fountain”? The colossal bronze sculpture was the centerpiece of the World Trade Center plaza. It survived the Sept. 11 attack and has stood for more than 10 years in Battery Park, damaged but instantly recognizable as a “memorial to those we lost,” in Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s words.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Could the ‘Sphere’ Go Here?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foye, Patrick J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National September 11 Memorial and Museum', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parks and Recreation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'BATTERY PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 12, 'm