nytimes.com/2012/08/17/on-our-radar-rating-the-oil-and-gas-sector/', 'snippet': 'The oil and natural gas industry and the federal government have the least positive images, as they did in polling last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans rate the oil and natural gas industry their least favorite sector in a Gallup poll. [Gallup]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Rating the Oil and Gas Sector', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T11:47:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/639a3380-855d-521c-88a8-92f4e0a68dd3', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/639a3380-855d-521c-88a8-92f4e0a68dd3'}, {'abstract': 'After a decade of Harry Potter movies, Emma Watson traded Hogwarts for Oxford and Brown. Now the former child star is back on the big screen with a whole new bag of tricks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/t-magazine/emma-watson-the-graduate.html', 'snippet': 'After a decade of Harry Potter movies, Emma Watson traded Hogwarts for Oxford and Brown. Now the former child star is back on the big screen with a whole new bag of tricks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Emma Watson, the onetime co-star of the most successful movie franchise ever, is a very grateful and a very lucky person. How do I know that? Because I sat down with the 22-year-old in a gastropub in a trendy neighborhood of North London, and in the course of an hour’s conversation she said “grateful” five times and “lucky” eight. True, of those five “grateful”s two were of the “ungrateful” form — yet these were embedded in clauses like “I felt guilty because I felt like that meant I was ungrateful. . . .” So, as you can see, Watson is a young woman who wants it put firmly on the record that she understands human lives are shaken up in the snow globe of uncertainty, and that simply because she’s ended up being covered in golden flakes, she doesn’t take it as her due, oh, no.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '200', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/t-magazine/19well-emma-2/19well-emma-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 775, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/t-magazine/19well-emma-2/19well-emma-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1504, 'width': 1139, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/t-magazine/19well-emma-2/19well-emma-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/19/t-magazine/19well-emma-2/19well-emma-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/t-magazine/19well-emma-2/19well-emma-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Graduate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Graduate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Perks of Being a Wallflower (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watson, Emma', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T11:50:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Will Self', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Will', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Self', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5017b868-29a7-5954-aaee-675e0ece33b6', 'word_count': 2210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5017b868-29a7-5954-aaee-675e0ece33b6'}, {'abstract': 'Mario’s adventures continue to look like kids’ stuff, but the new edition still offers amusing surprises.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/18/arts/video-games/new-super-mario-bros-2-for-the-nintendo-3ds.html', 'snippet': 'Mario’s adventures continue to look like kids’ stuff, but the new edition still offers amusing surprises.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of gaming’s greatest heroes, Super Mario, must rescue Princess Peach for the umpteenth time in New Super Mario Bros. 2, a fresh game from the Japanese developers at Nintendo who have been creating interactive adventures for their plumber protagonist for more than a generation.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/arts/18supermario-2/18supermario-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 240, 'width': 400, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/arts/18supermario-2/18supermario-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 240, 'width': 400, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/arts/18supermario-2/18supermario-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail',