mble printed book decide to st...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Devotees of the old-fashioned printed book who are distressed by the onrushing digital future — and there are more of them out there than you might think — cherish William H. Gass’s 1999 essay, “A Defense of the Book.” Personally, I own multiple copies, including its original appearance in Harper’s magazine, its reappearance in Mr. Gass’s collection “A Temple of Texts,” even a slightly strange limited edition done in cardboard. Nothing has ever summed up so well the book’s virtues as an object.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/technology/16bits-book-pic/16bits-book-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/16/technology/16bits-book-pic/16bits-book-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Champion of the Book Takes to the iPad', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gass, William H', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T12:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec445b38-f64c-5e20-a7b0-a39a7a7f5623', 'word_count': 909, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec445b38-f64c-5e20-a7b0-a39a7a7f5623'}, {'abstract': 'The great 16th-century painter Raphael (1483-1520) is being honored with a rare exhibition focusing on the last period of his life. “Late Raphael” is on display at the Prado through Sept. 16 and moves on to the Louvre from Oct. 8 through Jan. 14.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/rare-survey-of-late-raphael-masterpieces-at-the-prado/', 'snippet': 'The great 16th-century painter Raphael (1483-1520) is being honored with a rare exhibition focusing on the last period of his life. “Late Raphael” is on display at the Prado through Sept. 16 and moves on to the Louvre from Oct. 8 through Jan. 14.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The great 16th-century painter Raphael (1483-1520) became one of the most influential Western artists during the last phase of his brief life. But though often celebrated, he has not been honored with a full-scale exhibition focusing on this period.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rare Survey of Late Raphael Masterpieces at the Prado', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louvre', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louvre Museum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prado Museum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madrid (Spain)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T12:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valerie Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valerie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/646400a1-1663-5e70-81ad-edb8e176b2e5', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/646400a1-1663-5e70-81ad-edb8e176b2e5'}, {'abstract': 'Recent developments in Egypt have brought United States policy makers closer than ever to a confronting a situation that has haunted American relations with Egypt for more than 30 years: a government truly controlled by the Islamists of the Muslim Brotherhood.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/changes-atop-egypts-government-create-uncertain-path-for-united-states/', 'snippet': 'Recent developments in Egypt have brought United States policy makers closer than ever to a confronting a situation that has haunted American relations with Egypt for more than 30 years: a government truly controlled by the Islamists of the Muslim...', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the first months of Barack Obama’s stint in the United States Senate and the beginning of President George W. Bush’s second term, an Egyptian general wrote a thesis for the Army War College in Carlisle Barracks, Pa., offering American policy makers advice about how to manage relations with the Middle East.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Changes Atop Egypt’s Government Create Uncertain Path for United States', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Eg