 or a grunge kid working in an indie record shop that suddenly got a film deal, there’s a degree of affluence all of a sudden.” Do those people even exist anymore?  Those people are still out there. They might have landed at different gigs. I’m constantly amazed by people who still get extraordinary tech deals for concepts and businesses which don’t have any hope of returning anything to their investors.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/magazine/19talk/mag-19Talk-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 553, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/magazine/19talk/mag-19Talk-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1332, 'width': 719, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/magazine/19talk/19talk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/19/magazine/19talk/19talk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Case Against Purple', 'kicker': 'Talk | Tyler Brûlé', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Case Against Purple', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brule, Tyler', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T14:42:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Andrew Goldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Andrew', 'lastname': 'Goldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/1eb2b8a8-159f-5e78-881e-59324560ef9e', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1eb2b8a8-159f-5e78-881e-59324560ef9e'}, {'abstract': 'How I painted and broke a masterpiece.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/magazine/i-was-jeff-koonss-studio-serf.html', 'snippet': 'How I painted and broke a masterpiece.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a 21-year-old art student, I answered a help-wanted ad at the SoHo studio of Jeff Koons. During the interview, the studio manager set my slides on a light box and leaned over them with a loupe, inspecting each one like a jeweler with a tray of semiprecious stones. The head painter was consulted, a tall and taciturn man who eventually came over to shake my hand. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/magazine/19lives/mag-19Lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 964, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/magazine/19lives/mag-19Lives-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1017, 'width': 1080, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/magazine/19lives/19lives-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/19/magazine/19lives/19lives-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/magazine/19lives/19lives-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Was Jeff Koons’s Studio Serf', 'kicker': 'Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reflections of a Studio Serf', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koons, Jeff', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T14:42:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Powers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Powers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a76165e-2c2c-593a-9f40-5220ee147f9e', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a76165e-2c2c-593a-9f40-5220ee147f9e'}, {'abstract': 'The previous tenant; the ex-girlfriend; the front-runner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/magazine/last-known-address.html', 'snippet': 'The previous tenant; the ex-girlfriend; the front-runner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shortly after renting a house, I found out from neighbors that the previous tenant died of an overdose. This didn’t create any major inconveniences, although early on we did find a few remnants (like police tape). But it did feel unsettling and slightly disturbing. Did our landlord have any ethical obligation to tell us what had happened before we signed the lease?\xa0WILLIAM, NEW YORK', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/magazine/19ethicist/19ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/