’s pick: Roger Vivier’s latest, a tri-colored pump with the brand’s signature buckle at the toe.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/the-daily-shoe-roger-vivier-2/', 'snippet': 'Today’s pick: Roger Vivier’s latest, a tri-colored pump with the brand’s signature buckle at the toe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jane Herman delivers The Daily Shoe from the Bergdorf Goodman shoe salon in honor of the store’s 111th anniversary. Today’s pick: Roger Vivier’s latest, a tri-colored pump with the brand’s signature buckle at the toe. $795.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Daily Shoe | Roger Vivier', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T17:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd94d134-969a-58d7-8466-4d424c989cfd', 'word_count': 43, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd94d134-969a-58d7-8466-4d424c989cfd'}, {'abstract': 'A. O. Scott and David Carr discuss the lingering influence of the baby-boom generation.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/the-sweet-spot-august-17/', 'snippet': 'A. O. Scott and David Carr discuss the lingering influence of the baby-boom generation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, A. O. Scott and David Carr discuss the success of artists from the baby-boom generation, like Meryl Streep and Bruce Springsteen, and what sells when it comes to age.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sweet Spot | Aug. 17', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T17:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32c2a78c-7eb5-5e6d-a289-7ff6aa5236f2', 'word_count': 31, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32c2a78c-7eb5-5e6d-a289-7ff6aa5236f2'}, {'abstract': 'A closer look at the issues that arise when sharks are lured, for science or sport, with tasty chum.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/chumming-around-with-great-white-sharks/', 'snippet': 'A closer look at the issues that arise when sharks are lured, for science or sport, with tasty chum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of my Pace University communication students, Martin Totlandt, spent much of the summer in South Africa and filed this “Your Dot” dispatch about the controversy over the process of chumming — luring sharks with a fishy, bloody brew spooned overboard — something done both for science and for adventure tourism cage diving operations. The video above was shot by Totland of a shark encounter in June (the camera was on a pole). Here is his post:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chumming Around With Great White Sharks', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boats and Boating', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eco-Tourism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Sport', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sharks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'sub