: None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24e98149-cb8b-51d0-91d3-c0d4a04ca8c1', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24e98149-cb8b-51d0-91d3-c0d4a04ca8c1'}, {'abstract': 'Bucks readers tell their tales about dealing with their lenders on force-placed insurance.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/a-lesson-for-homeowners/', 'snippet': 'Bucks readers tell their tales about dealing with their lenders on force-placed insurance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Sullivan writes this week in his Wealth Matters column about force-placed insurance — insurance that a lender buys when it concludes that a homeowner does not have adequate hazard, flood or wind coverage. But the problem is that this insurance is almost always more expensive than the homeowner could buy in the open market. In addition, the coverage may be redundant or not needed at all. But homeowners have been reporting that they have a difficult time getting their lenders to remove the insurance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lesson for Homeowners', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T17:13:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57ac3616-4644-5e78-ac8c-43f0ebe2d859', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57ac3616-4644-5e78-ac8c-43f0ebe2d859'}, {'abstract': 'What good is a fishing spot if it’s on private land? A club in Colorado solves this problem, offering access to dozens of properties while keeping costs — and crowds — small.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/travel/casting-in-colorado-away-from-the-crowds.html', 'snippet': 'What good is a fishing spot if it’s on private land? A club in Colorado solves this problem, offering access to dozens of properties while keeping costs — and crowds — small.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NORTHERN Colorado was still rubbing the previous night’s Independence Day parties from its eyes as I parked beside the rancher’s fence, pulled on waders and strung my fly rod. In the valley the drowsy river was a silver twist among green willows. The air smelled of wet sage, and black cattle stood like chess pieces in the distant fields. Beyond them the 12,000-foot peaks of the Mount Zirkel Wilderness had lined up for morning’s roll call, their summits lighted up like match tips.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/travel/19-cover-span/19-cover-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/19/travel/19-cover-span/19-cover-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/travel/19-cover-span/19-cover-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/travel/19-cover-span/19-cover-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 1250, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/travel/19-cover-span/19-cover-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/19/travel/19-cover-span/19-cover-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/travel/19-cover-span/19-cover-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Casting in Colorado, Away From the Crowds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Your Own Piece of River', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trout', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Sport', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T17:17:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/029ab03b-3485-596d-a9d0-50c6c5ada881', 'word_count': 3414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/029ab03b-3485-596d-a9d0-50c6c5ada881'}, {'abstract': 'Have you ever thought about the data trail you leave as you go about the ordinary business of living in an age of information? If so, let us know.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/share-the-tale-of-your-data-trail/', 'snippet': 'Have you ever thought about the data trail you leave as you go about the ordinary business of living in an age of information? If so, let us know.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week I wrote about how improvements in technology and the capacity to store huge amounts of data cheaply now allow both the government and the private sector to collect and retain vast amounts of personal information. The laws and regulations that govern such collection, in the view of many experts, are outdated and inconsistent. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Share the Tale of Your Data Trail', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T17:20:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6a135ee-1aeb-5bc2-8f85-d5298d96cf33', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6a135ee-1aeb-5bc2-8f85-d5298d96cf33'}, {'abstract': '“The Underwater Welder,” by Jeff Lemire, entered the graphic books paperback best-seller list at No. 6.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/graphic-books-best-sellers-talking-about-the-underwater-welder/', 'snippet': '“The Underwater Welder,” by Jeff Lemire, entered the graphic books paperback best-seller list at No. 6.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Underwater Welder,” by Jeff Lemire, enters our graphic books paperback best-seller list at No. 6 this week. It’s about Jack Joseph, a man feeling pressure because of his deep sea welding gig and the fact that he’s going to become a father. The introduction to the book, by Damon Lindelof, one of the creators of “Lost,” compares it to “The Twilight Zone.” The book starts out innocently enough, seemingly a story about Jack, his pregnant wife, their life struggles and Jack’s relationship with his own father. Things get a bit eerie after Jack emerges from one of his dives to a changed world. Mr. Lemire’s characters, even when they’re happy, have a melancholy look to them. They create an almost instant rapport with the reader.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: Talking About ‘The Underwater Welder’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graphic Novels', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T17:30:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04a3704e-d43a-5eab-a1b5-b82518efb91e', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04a3704e-d43a-5eab-a1b5-b82518efb91e'}, {'abstract': 'Chipper Jones’s 19th year with the Braves — he has said it will be his last — is offering plenty of highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/for-chipper-jones-a-salute-and-two-home-runs/', 'snippet': 'Chipper Jones’s 19th year with the Braves — he has said it will be his last — is offering plenty of highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It would be perfectly understandable if Chipper Jones slowed down a bit — he is 40 and in the final weeks of h