consolable tears, I took him for a walk. I strapped him to my chest in a nylon baby carrier, kissed Mommy good-bye and ventured into the cool evening. Together we walked. Well, I walked. He rode.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before Adoption, 79 Lost Days', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADOPTIONS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T17:52:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Otto', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otto', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6532db84-5643-52a1-96c0-8c10aa7f7fbd', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6532db84-5643-52a1-96c0-8c10aa7f7fbd'}, {'abstract': 'The former Algerian foreign minister, Lakhdar Brahimi, will replace Kofi Annan, who resigned in frustration two weeks ago over his inability to advance his plan to halt the Syrian conflict.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/18/world/middleeast/lakhdar-brahimi-algerian-statesman-to-succeed-kofi-annan-as-special-syrian-envoy.html', 'snippet': 'The former Algerian foreign minister, Lakhdar Brahimi, will replace Kofi Annan, who resigned in frustration two weeks ago over his inability to advance his plan to halt the Syrian conflict.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lakhdar Brahimi, a former Algerian foreign minister and widely respected statesman, was appointed Friday as the new special envoy to Syria from the United Nations and Arab League to replace Kofi Annan, who resigned in frustration two weeks ago over his inability to advance his plan to halt the Syrian conflict.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Veteran Algerian Statesman to Succeed Annan as Special Syrian Envoy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Veteran Algerian Statesman to Succeed Annan as Special Syrian Envoy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brahimi, Lakhdar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANNAN, KOFI', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALGERIA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban Ki-moon', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T17:52:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d6a9241-6e10-5d2d-b922-1f515899eea6', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d6a9241-6e10-5d2d-b922-1f515899eea6'}, {'abstract': 'Smudgy shadow, bold liner, inky brows — makeup artist Mark Carrasquillo sharpens our gaze.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/eye-intensity/', 'snippet': 'Smudgy shadow, bold liner, inky brows — makeup artist Mark Carrasquillo sharpens our gaze.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘I don’t have a signature style,” says Mark Carrasquillo, the makeup artist who created the dramatic eyes on these pages. “But I like to think I can do many things, from full drag to ‘scrubbed clean,’ and somehow make it look like my hand.” He may be versatile, but one thing that carries through all his work is sex appeal. “I’ve been accused of making girls look oversexed,” he admits. The sultry makeup he did here has a tough-girl edge. “I wanted to play with the idea of youth, which for me means a bare face with one statement, like a drawn-on eyebrow or a matte black eye. No foundation, no blush — just lots of attitude.” While lipstick is optional (“I don’t believe in the rule that says you shouldn’t wear a strong eye with a strong lip — it’s a good-taste trap”), great skin is imperative. Carrasquillo’s trade secret? A special arnica oil-based luminizer he whips up in his East Village kitchen. “Every model I use it on asks me to make some for them,” he says. “I won’t reveal all the ingredients, but it’s healing and leaves skin with a beautiful, glowing finish.” Maquillage magic can only do so much, though, he adds. “A woman can have incredible skin, but if she’s not happy in it, all the makeup in the world won’t help. I’m so tired of seeing beautiful young girls with Botox, etc. I want to tell them to just simmer down and enjoy who they are.” More…', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eye Intensity', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T18:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandra Ballentine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ballentine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60d18f51-a1c4-54f6-9c83-9c496a3f1525', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60d18f51-a1c4-54f6-9c83-9c496a3f1525'}, {'abstract': 'The showdown was a test case in American labor relations, partly because Caterpillar was driving such a hard bargain when its business was thriving.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/18/business/striking-caterpillar-workers-ratify-contract-offer.html', 'snippet': 'The showdown was a test case in American labor relations, partly because Caterpillar was driving such a hard bargain when its business was thriving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Workers who had been striking at a Caterpillar hydraulic parts factory in Joliet, Ill., voted on Friday to ratify a proposed six-year contract that contained almost all of the concessions the company had demanded.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/business/Cat-1345245522968/Cat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/business/Cat-1345245522968/Cat-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1420, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Caterpillar Workers Ratify Deal They Dislike', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Caterpillar Workers Ratify Deal They Dislike', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Assn of Machinists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Caterpillar Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T18:13:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f10e7f1d-4ec7-59f8-a926-992dfac41a45', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f10e7f1d-4ec7-59f8-a926-992dfac41a45'}, {'abstract': 'William H. Gass has written an essay that can be read only on an iPad equipped with iBooks 2.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/a-champion-of-the-book-takes-to-the-ipad/', 'snippet': 'William H. Gass has written an essay that can be read only on an iPad equipped with iBooks 2.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The author William H. Gass has written a 15,000-word essay called “Abstractions Arrive: Having Been There All the Time,” a collaboration with the noted photographer Michael Eastman, that can be read only on an iPad equipped with iBooks 2. It’s a surprising move by Mr. Gass, whose 1999 essay “A Defense of the Book” is cherished by devotees of the old-fashioned printed book who are distressed by the onrushing digital future. On our sister blog Bits, David Streitfeld recently spoke to Mr. Gass to learn more about the project.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Champion of the Book Takes to the iPad', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gass, William H', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streitfeld, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T18:13:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fdd47bd-53f5-56d3-870e-d8d3dcbad6b1', 'word_count': 89, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fdd47bd-53f5-56d3-870e-d8d3dcbad6b1'}, {'abstract': 'A nine-room apartment in a building designed by James E.R. Carpenter encompasses the entire ninth floor, with views of Central Park and the Metropolitan Museum of Art.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/big-ticket-sold-for-19-5-million-3/', 'snippet': 'A nine-room apartment in a building designed by James E.R. Carpenter encompasses the entire ninth floor, with views of Central Park and the Metropolitan Museum of Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In prime position on Fifth Avenue’s Museum Mile, a nine-room condominium that encompasses the entire ninth floor of 988 Fifth Avenue and offers stunning views of Central Park and the Metropolitan Museum of Art sold for $19.5 million, the biggest sale of the week, according to city records.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Ticket | Sold for $19.5 Million', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T18:14:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48cf5029-13f5-524a-b752-c8db1a599a9e', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48cf5029-13f5-524a-b752-c8db1a599a9e'}, {'abstract': 'A study of its archives shows that CCTV America, an outpost of the Chinese state-controlled broadcaster, tends to avoid news of dissidents or disgraced officials.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/on-cctv-america-some-china-stories-recede-from-view/', 'snippet': 'A study of its archives shows that CCTV America, an outpost of the Chinese state-controlled broadcaster, tends to avoid news of dissidents or disgraced officials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although they come from opposite ends of the Chinese political spectrum, for two months this spring Bo Xilai, a Communist Party official who was dismissed from his post, and Chen Guangcheng, a blind, activist lawyer who fled house arrest in his village, shared one important trait: they were the most closely watched Chinese men in the world. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On CCTV America, Some China Stories Recede From View', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bo Xilai', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen Guangcheng', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China Central Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T18:15:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacob Fromer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fromer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36a9faf8-7751-5160-8e85-76a31cbe78b7', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36a9faf8-7751-5160-8e85-76a31cbe78b7'}, {'abstract': 'As the National Republican Congressional Committee starts its first wave of advertisements, get ready for the debate over the health care law to be reignited.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/in-new-ads-republicans-attack-over-medicare/', 'snippet': 'As the National Republican Congressional Committee starts its first wave of advertisements, get ready for the debate over the health care law to be reignited.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Get ready for the debate over the 2010 health care law – its Medicare component especially – to be reignited on the airwaves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In New Ads, Republicans Attack Over Medicare', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T18:17:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76b90f47-dace-54b3-8c3c-4b768d51ebf1', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76b90f47-dace-54b3-8c3c-4b768d51ebf1'}, {'abstract': 'Food news you can use.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/relevant-links/', 'snippet': 'Food news you can use.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple of links that didn’t make it into today’s column: How unequal, for example, is income in America? (A more difficult question is, Why do we say unequal but inequality?) You might check out the charts and figures here. There are a dozen charts right here that tell the story nicely. Be careful: it’s brain-wrenching material.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Relevant Links', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': Non