2dd0dbd7-4802-5e62-809c-0695980258b3'}, {'abstract': 'Russell Wasendorf Sr., the former chief executive of the failed brokerage firm Peregrine Financial Group, pleaded not guilty on Friday to lying to federal regulators. He has been charged with 31 counts of deceiving regulators about the value of his customers’ accounts.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/peregrine-founder-pleads-not-guilty/', 'snippet': 'Russell Wasendorf Sr., the former chief executive of the failed brokerage firm Peregrine Financial Group, pleaded not guilty on Friday to lying to federal regulators. He has been charged with 31 counts of deceiving regulators about the value of hi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The former chief executive of the failed brokerage firm Peregrine Financial Group, who last month wrote a note admitting that he had committed a long-ranging investment fraud, pleaded not guilty on Friday to lying to federal regulators.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Chief of Peregrine Pleads Not Guilty to Fraud', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Chief of Peregrine Pleads Not Guilty to Fraud', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commodities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embezzlement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Futures and Options Trading', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wasendorf, Russell R Sr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Peregrine Financial Group Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cedar Rapids (Iowa)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T19:23:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de947c1b-1442-51c4-82ab-2f2bf05a09cc', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de947c1b-1442-51c4-82ab-2f2bf05a09cc'}, {'abstract': 'The auto insurer Progressive may have done everything wrong in a lawsuit that became a cause célèbre on social media this week, but there’s a lesson for us all in the details.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/18/your-money/progressives-side-of-the-insurance-case-that-blew-up-on-the-internet.html', 'snippet': 'The auto insurer Progressive may have done everything wrong in a lawsuit that became a cause célèbre on social media this week, but there’s a lesson for us all in the details.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It isn’t often that automobile insurance becomes the subject of nationwide outrage. So when it does happen, it’s worth a peek inside all our policies to figure out how they actually work and what the insurance companies are up to behind the scenes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/business/18money-span/18money-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/18/business/18money-span/18money-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/business/18money-span/18money-span-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024,