ion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca R. Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9270b491-7538-5d29-b82c-b08cd47c45f2', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9270b491-7538-5d29-b82c-b08cd47c45f2'}, {'abstract': 'I am hugely grateful to work with a team of fashion editors who bring their taste and super-refined antennae for what’s new and really interesting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/t-magazine/editors-letter.html', 'snippet': 'I am hugely grateful to work with a team of fashion editors who bring their taste and super-refined antennae for what’s new and really interesting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More and more, when I sit in the front row or speak to students, I am asked to comment on the relevance of magazines and editors in the age of live streamed fashion shows and immediate news from the catwalks. It’s a timely and good question, one that deserves not to be brushed aside; and something I thought about as we reviewed the final pages for this issue, which is devoted to the fall women’s collections.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '76', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/t-magazine/19edletter/19edletter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/t-magazine/19edletter/19edletter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/t-magazine/19edletter/19edletter-thumbStand