: 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voice Recognition Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-17T23:18:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c587366-c693-5cab-8540-f669e953d81a', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c587366-c693-5cab-8540-f669e953d81a'}, {'abstract': 'Rraci’s, an Italian restaurant in Brewster, N.Y., has sturdy appetizers and worthy salads, but its menu hews to an older era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/nyregion/a-review-of-rracis-in-brewster.html', 'snippet': 'Rraci’s, an Italian restaurant in Brewster, N.Y., has sturdy appetizers and worthy salads, but its menu hews to an older era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S been seven years since I last reviewed Rraci’s, and I can report that history pretty much repeats itself, but at a higher price. A charming back dining patio has been added, but inside, the pallor of age hangs over the restaurant. Ocher walls are almost hidden by a clutter of pretty mirrors reflecting the small spaces, window swags, wine bottles and dusty bouquets of silk flowers. The dim lighting, the dark wainscoting and a deep plum ceiling can feel cozy or claustrophobic, like being at the back of a cave. The menu, too, is dated, a near copy of that offered years ago. Dishes reflect the taste of those times — a preference for the rich and the heavy with less interest in the subtle and the seasonal. When is the last time anyone had calf’s liver as an appetizer?', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 