York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recycling Plant Fire Unnerves a New York Town', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T00:22:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5ac7985-9a50-55e9-959e-de6e68adabaa', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5ac7985-9a50-55e9-959e-de6e68adabaa'}, {'abstract': 'Karoline Leach’s “Tryst,” playing at TheaterWorks Hartford, City Arts on Pearl, is a story of a con man and a spinster that delivers psychological twists and turns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/nyregion/a-review-of-tryst-at-theaterworks-hartford.html', 'snippet': 'Karoline Leach’s “Tryst,” playing at TheaterWorks Hartford, City Arts on Pearl, is a story of a con man and a spinster that delivers psychological twists and turns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'She is a mousy millinery assistant, consigned to the back room because she is not considered attractive enough to deal with customers. He is a small-time con man, looking for his next mark. He swiftly marries the women he woos, beds them (just to be polite), takes control of their bank accounts (this is 1910 London, after all, and young ladies need protecting) and runs for the hills.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/nyregion/19ARTSCT1_SPAN/19ARTSCT1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge':