dropping her first match since May, while her sister Venus advanced to the semifinals at the Western & Southern Open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/18/sports/tennis/serena-williams-is-upset-at-western-southern-open.html', 'snippet': 'Serena Williams lost in straight sets to Angelique Kerber, dropping her first match since May, while her sister Venus advanced to the semifinals at the Western & Southern Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MASON, Ohio — Serena Williams, the Olympic gold medalist and Wimbledon champion, lost her first match since May on Friday, falling to the German Angelique Kerber, 6-4, 6-4, in the quarterfinals at the Western & Southern Open in this suburb of Cincinnati.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/sports/TENNIS/TENNIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/sports/TENNIS/TENNIS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1639, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/sports/TENNIS/TENNIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/18/sports/TENNIS/TENNIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/sports/TENNIS/TENNIS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Williams Sisters, a Split in Cincinnati', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Williams Sisters Split in Cincinnati, Ending One Streak and Another Drought', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerber, Angelique', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Serena', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Venus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T00:48:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f1f3e23-923e-579e-bbfe-8e174cc45707', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f1f3e23-923e-579e-bbfe-8e174cc45707'}, {'abstract': 'The education reform movement, slow economies and federal grant competitions have led lawmakers to tighten the requirements for earning and keeping tenure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/18/nyregion/nearly-half-of-new-york-city-teachers-are-denied-tenure-in-2012.html', 'snippet': 'The education reform movement, slow economies and federal grant competitions have led lawmakers to tighten the requirements for earning and keeping tenure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly half of New York City teachers reaching the end of their probations were denied tenure this year, the Education Department said on Friday, marking the culmination of years of efforts toward Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s goal to end “tenure as we know it.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Many New York City Teachers Denied Tenure in Policy Shift', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Policy Shift, Fewer Teachers Are Given Tenure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Evaluations (Labor)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tenure', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T00:53:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40b0a118-8359-5450-8cfb-9c18133e86ba', 'word_count': 1177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40b0a118-8359-5450-8cfb-9c18133e86ba'}, {'abstract': 'Formula One was fortunate to find that its annual August break of five weeks between races coincided with the greatest sporting circus on earth, at the Olympics in London. While the racing series hibernated, the Olympics nevertheless gave time – and a reason – for Formula One fans and journalists to brainstorm about their sporting series by comparison.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/watching-the-olympics-seeing-formula-one/', 'snippet': 'Formula One was fortunate to find that its annual August break of five weeks between races coincided with the greatest sporting circus on earth, at the Olympics in London. While the racing series hibernated, the Olympics nevertheless gave time – a...', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — I kept an eye on the Olympics, and since it is the summer break in Formula One, I tried to keep my mind off Formula One. But, inevitably, comparisons of the two spectacles kept entering my thoughts — especially since Formula One has for many years hyped itself as the world’s third most popular sporting spectacle, behind the Olympics and World Cup soccer. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/blogs/15formulaone-olympics/15formulaone-olympics-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 354, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/15/blogs/15formulaone-olympics/15formulaone-olympics-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 354, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Watching the Olympics, Seeing Formula One', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T01:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b075ab4b-50ed-5439-b010-58615d144291', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b075ab4b-50ed-5439-b010-58615d144291'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Teixeira was out of the lineup Friday night against the Boston Red Sox for what he called inflammation in his left wrist.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/17/ailing-yankees-give-teixeira-a-break-to-rest-injured-wrist/', 'snippet': 'Mark Teixeira was out of the lineup Friday night against the Boston Red Sox for what he called inflammation in his left wrist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees look more brittle with each passing day. C. C. Sabathia, Andy Pettitte and Alex Rodriguez are on the disabled list, and now Mark Teixeira’s sore left wrist will most likely keep him sidelined for a couple of games.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ailing Yankees Give Teixeira Chance to Rest Injured Wrist', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabathia, C C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teixeira, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T01:05:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c5256b3-2556-5424-9b57-56b90604f765', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c5256b3-2556-5424-9b57-56b90604f765'}, {'abstract': 'After an initial flush of enthusiasm, merchants have grown wary of daily deal Web sites like Groupon and LivingSocial. Now consumers are starting to follow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/18/technology/merchants-and-shoppers-sour-on-daily-deal-sites-like-groupon.html', 'snippet': 'After an initial flush of enthusiasm, merchants have grown wary of daily deal Web sites like Groupon and LivingSocial. Now consumers are starting to follow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As their e-mail in-boxes filled with daily deal offers from Web sites like Groupon, Lea Pische and Edwin Hermawan, a pizzeria waitress and a former lawyer living on the Lower East Side, finally decided to buy one: a discounted Skillshare class on how to start a business.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/business/Dealsjp1/Dealsjp1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/18/business/Dealsjp1/Dealsjp1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/business/Dealsjp1/Dealsjp1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/business/Dealsjp1/Dealsjp1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1420, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Merchants and Shoppers Sour on Daily Deal Sites', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ready To Ditch The Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coupons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Groupon Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LivingSocial.com', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T01:07:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford and Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3346118b-ac89-5e7c-bfa2-670808c536ef', 'word_count': 1158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3346118b-ac89-5e7c-bfa2-670808c536ef'}, {'abstract': 'A Shakespeare work that has been performed only twice on Broadway is at the F. M. Kirby Shakespeare Theater at Drew University in Madison, N.J.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/nyregion/a-review-of-measure-for-measure-in-madison.html', 'snippet': 'A Shakespeare work that has been performed only twice on Broadway is at the F. M. Kirby Shakespeare Theater at Drew University in Madison, N.J.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Isabella’s quandary in the Shakespeare play “Measure for Measure” is a little like Joan’s in the 2012 season of “Mad Men.” Should a woman sleep with a man she finds repellent if by doing so she serves a greater good? And how much greater does that good have to be? On “Mad Men,” it was a matter of crass commerce, an advertising agency getting its first big auto account. In “Measure for Measure,” it is a question of the woman’s saving her brother from execution. But this story being a product of Elizabethan England, when notions of immortal damnation were taken more personally, the playwright cannot let her fall into bed with just anybody. He cannot let her fall into bed at all.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/nyregion/19ARTSNJ2/19ARTSNJ2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1442, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/nyregion/19ARTSNJ2/19ARTSNJ2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1454, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/nyregion/19ARTSNJ2/19ARTSNJ2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/19/nyregion/19ARTSNJ2/19ARTSNJ2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/nyregion/19ARTSNJ2/19ARTSNJ2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Indecent Proposal and a Moral Dilemma', 'kicker': 'Arts | New Jersey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Indecent Proposal And a Moral Dilemma', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shakespeare Theater of New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'F M Kirby Shakespeare Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monte, Bonnie J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T01:09:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/58eda513-a071-5d22-8ebf-5c22b377407e', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58eda513-a071-5d22-8ebf-5c22b377407e'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican vice-presidential candidate Paul D. Ryan and his wife also paid 15.9 percent in federal income taxes in 2010, according to tax returns he released Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/18/us/politics/ryan-tax-returns-show-20-percent-rate-in-2011.html', 'snippet': 'The Republican vice-presidential candidate Paul D. Ryan and his wife also paid 15.9 percent in federal income taxes in 2010, according to tax returns he released Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republican vice-presidential candidate Paul D. Ryan and his wife, Janna, paid 20 percent of their adjusted gross income in federal income taxes in 2011 and 15.9 percent in 2010, according to tax returns he released Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryan Tax Returns Show 20 Percent Rate in 2011', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ryan Tax Returns Show 20 Percent Rate in 2011', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Janna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vice Presidents and Vice Presidency (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T01:12:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Kocieniewski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kocieniewski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99e81552-e8e3-5992-a482-6