0e789c'}, {'abstract': 'Surveillance cameras are omnipresent in the post 9/11 world, but they have been focused least on where they are needed most: high-crime areas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/nyregion/the-watchmens-misdirected-gaze.html', 'snippet': 'Surveillance cameras are omnipresent in the post 9/11 world, but they have been focused least on where they are needed most: high-crime areas.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Person of Interest,” the CBS television drama developed as if to risk the collective cardiovascular failure of the New York Civil Liberties Union, delivers a vision of the city in which technological innovation, boundless private capital and an outlaw disposition collude to render a fantasia of sixth-sense policing. At the center sits an obsessive billionaire computer savant who deploys his own pattern-recognition software, advanced surveillance gadgetry and the acrobatics of a former spy to identify those about to perpetrate or fall prey to violence, and pre-empt their fate. Murder and malfeasance are nipped virtually at conception. Pass the cupcakes!', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/nyregion/19BIGCITY1/19JPBIGCITY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/nyregion/19BIGCITY1/19JPBIGCITY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/nyregion/19BIGCITY1/19BIGCITY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/19/nyregion/19BIGCITY1/