', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/18/latin-america-sees-hand-of-colonialism-in-assange-standoff/', 'snippet': 'The case of Julian Assange, the Wikileaks founder stranded in London despite a grant of asylum in Ecuador, has rekindled suspicions in Latin America about perceived neo-colonialism on the part of the British.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Ecuador was this past weekend seeking support from its Latin American partners to confront what officials described as threats by Britain over Quito’s decision to grant asylum to Julian Assange, the WikiLeaks founder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/blogs/rdv-ecuador/rdv-ecuador-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/18/blogs/rdv-ecuador/rdv-ecuador-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1280, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Latin America Sees Hand of Colonialism in Assange Standoff', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asylum, Right of', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extradition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assange, Julian P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ecuador', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T12:04:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ad1dfa5-2ae0-5469-af0d-b5fd683ee589', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ad1dfa5-2ae0-5469-af0d-b5fd683ee589'}, {'abstract': 'The most interesting number of Friday was 13,275.20. That was the closing price of the Dow Jones industrial average, which left it just a few points shy of its highest close since the financial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/18/aug-17-does-a-bullish-stock-market-predict-a-faster-recovery/', 'snippet': 'The most interesting number of Friday was 13,275.20. That was the closing price of the Dow Jones industrial average, which left it just a few points shy of its highest close since the financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There wasn’t much in the way of polling data on Friday. The national tracking polls were released — Mitt Romney and Paul D. Ryan got a comparatively poor number in the Rasmussen Reports tracking poll, which had President Obama pulling into a one-point lead after having trailed in that survey for much of the past few weeks. And there was a new national survey from the firm Angus Reid, which conducts online polls. It had Mr. Romney ahead by four points — up from a tie in its poll last month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 17: Does a Bullish Stock Market Predict a Faster Recovery?', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T13:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24ca80a1-ac8f-54a3-8303-201788975cb4', 'word_count': 1145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24ca80a1-ac8f-54a3-8303-201788975cb4'}, {'abstract': 'The final pick: a blinding ankle boot from Manolo Blahnik that’s covered in crystals and was designed exclusively for Bergdorf Goodman.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/18/the-daily-shoe-manolo-blahnik-boot/', 'snippet': 'The final pick: a blinding ankle boot from Manolo Blahnik that’s covered in crystals and was designed exclusively for Bergdorf Goodman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jane Herman delivers The Daily Shoe from the Bergdorf Goodman shoe salon in honor of the store’s 111th anniversary. Today’s pick (and the last in this series): a blinding ankle boot from Manolo Blahnik that’s covered in crystals and was designed exclusively for Bergdorf Goodman. $7,800.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Daily Shoe | Manolo Blahnik Boot', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blahnik, Manolo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bergdorf Goodman', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T13:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3becb5f0-863b-5ba0-9114-06df1a71b2da', 'word_count': 46, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3becb5f0-863b-5ba0-9114-06df1a71b2da'}, {'abstract': 'A computer simulation played in the EA Sports game FIFA 13 predicts that Manchester City will repeat as champions of England’s Premier League.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/18/premier-league-and-the-winner-is/', 'snippet': 'A computer simulation played in the EA Sports game FIFA 13 predicts that Manchester City will repeat as champions of England’s Premier League.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let the games begin. No, not those Games. The games on the field and on the screen, TV and video. England’s Premier League and EA’s FIFA Soccer 13.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Premier League: And the Winner Is …', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Electronic Arts Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'English Premier League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T14:17:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0942f5bf-0516-5249-b740-f4db0f206f3e', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0942f5bf-0516-5249-b740-f4db0f206f3e'}, {'abstract': 'Sauvignon blanc from Burgundy? Isn’t Burgundy chardonnay country, at least as far as its white wines are concerned? Yes, mostly it is. But there are a few exceptions, and one is Saint-Bris, part of a small cluster of wine-making villages that produce wines similar to those of Sancerre and its satellites.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/18/further-notes-for-the-sancerre-inclined/', 'snippet': 'Sauvignon blanc from Burgundy? Isn’t Burgundy chardonnay country, at least as far as its white wines are concerned? Yes, mostly it is. But there are a few exceptions, and one is Saint-Bris, part of a small cluster of wine-making villages that prod...', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — In his most recent Wines of The Times column, Eric Asimov tastes the so-called Sancerre satellites — appellations that produce white wine in a similar style to their better-known Loire Valley neighbor, from the same grape variety, sauvignon blanc. Indeed, wine from these appellations, which include Pouilly-Fumé, Menetou-Salon, Reuilly and Quincy, can be a good bet. Pouilly-Fumé sometimes matches or surpasses Sancerre in quality (and, unfortunately, in price) but all of the others are bargains. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/blogs/ihtrdvwine17/ihtrdvwine17-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1023, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/17/blogs/ihtrdvwine17/ihtrdvwine17-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2046, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Further Notes for the Sancerre-Inclined', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asimov, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Loire Valley (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T15:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_