, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0dbddca-681a-5c4a-8ce3-fa53e5d8ae39', 'word_count': 1215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0dbddca-681a-5c4a-8ce3-fa53e5d8ae39'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Volstad of the Cubs has gone 23 starts in a row without a victory and is 0-9 with a 6.96 earned run average in 12 starts this season.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/18/volstead-struggling-with-the-cubs/', 'snippet': 'Chris Volstad of the Cubs has gone 23 starts in a row without a victory and is 0-9 with a 6.96 earned run average in 12 starts this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No player sums up the futility of the 2012 Chicago Cubs better than starter Chris Volstad. The Cubs acquired Volstad from the Miami Marlins in January for Carlos Zambrano, an expensive and volatile starter the team was eager to shed. But while Volstad may be quieter than Zambrano, his results have been discouraging.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Volstead Struggling with the Cubs', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Volstad, Chris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Cubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T15:58:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03d976ad-5112-58b7-9331-7fe6adb0e1ea', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03d976ad-5112-58b7-9331-7fe6adb0e1ea'}, {'abstract': 'Get lost in this diagramless from Fred Piscop.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/18/blanking-out/', 'snippet': 'Get lost in this diagramless from Fred Piscop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SECOND SUNDAY PUZZLE — The variety puzzle from Fred Piscop this week is a diagramless, so brace yourself for the sheer terror of seeing 289 white squares blankly staring at you. Warning: There is some assembly required. You have to figure out the puzzle’s geometry, and that is the hardest part. You have to determine which squares are to be filled in and which should be black squares. Adding to the difficulty is that you have to add the numbers to the grid.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blanking Out', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T16:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Gaffney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gaffney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cec34cb-55c7-51df-9d98-b94a1dd03660', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cec34cb-55c7-51df-9d98-b94a1dd03660'}, {'abstract': 'We too often deny the importance of our possessions and don’t spend enough time thinking about how they can boost happiness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/opinion/sunday/clutter-storage-and-happiness.html', 'snippet': 'We too often deny the importance of our possessions and don’t spend enough time thinking about how they can boost happiness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH all the supply lists, school clothes and emergency contact sheets required before September begins, I can barely keep track of everything I have to buy, fill out or turn in. The new school year means that a bunch of new stuff will pour into our apartment — and I still haven’t figured out what to do with all the stuff from last year. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/sunday-review/19STUFF/19STUFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/sunday-review/19STUFF/19STUFF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1639, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/sunday-review/19STUFF/19STUFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/19/sunday-review/19STUFF/19STUFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/sunday-review/19STUFF/19STUFF-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 116, 'width': 116, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Stuff', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Good Stuff', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Storage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T16:01:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': 