'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/opinion/sunday/asias-roiling-sea.html', 'snippet': 'Washington should keep nudging China and its rivals to settle their South China Sea claims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The South China Sea, one of the world’s most important waterways, has been contested off and on for centuries. These days, with the sea bounded by some of Asia’s most vibrant economies — China, Vietnam, the Philippines, Taiwan and Malaysia — the competition has become a virtual free-for-all. Confrontations over territorial control are alarmingly frequent and could get out of hand, with dangerous consequences.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asia’s Roiling Sea', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Asia’s Roiling Sea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South China Sea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Assn of Southeast Asian Nations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T17:19:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e03f825-4321-5017-923b-604555979ad3', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e03f825-4321-5017-923b-604555979ad3'}, {'abstract': 'Gregg Olson, the 1989 American League Rookie of the Year for Baltim