0935-5c28-8679-f4a3347eb96c'}, {'abstract': 'Cantaloupes from a farm in southwestern Indiana appear to be the source of the infections, state and federal authorities say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/us/salmonella-outbreak-in-20-states-kills-2-and-sickens-141.html', 'snippet': 'Cantaloupes from a farm in southwestern Indiana appear to be the source of the infections, state and federal authorities say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An outbreak of salmonella infections across 20 states has resulted in two deaths and sickened 141 people in recent weeks, state and federal authorities said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Salmonella Outbreak in 20 States Kills 2 and Sickens 141', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Salmonella Outbreak in 20 States Kills 2 and Sickens 141', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salmonella (Bacteria)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T18:37:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af8f02ac-8fb0-5567-a003-4001555e80a2', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af8f02ac-8fb0-5567-a003-4001555e80a2'}, {'abstract': 'Soon after Dan Dakich took the head basketball coaching job at West Virginia in 2002, he realized he made a mistake and decided to return to his old job at Bowling Green.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/sports/ncaabasketball/landing-in-west-virginia-dan-dakich-checked-the-exits.html', 'snippet': 'Soon after Dan Dakich took the head basketball coaching job at West Virginia in 2002, he realized he made a mistake and decided to return to his old job at Bowling Green.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Soon after Dan Dakich took the basketball head coaching job at West Virginia in 2002, he sat down with a yellow legal pad and wrote a list of the issues facing the Mountaineers. It became so long and daunting that he decided it was too much. Eight days after he was hired, he walked away from what he said was a seven-year contract offer worth $3.5 million to return to his old job at Bowling Green, which pays $125,000 a year. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/sports/Dakich/Dakich-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/19/sports/Dakich/Dakich-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/sports/Dakich/Dakich-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 619, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/sports/Dakich/Dakich-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1239, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/sports/Dakich/Dakich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/19/sports/Dakich/Dakich-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'