all of Fame right-hander, had to watch.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In This Feast of Perfection, as Always, a Famine Lurks', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Extra Bases: In This Feast of Perfection, as Always, a Famine Lurks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'HERNANDEZ, FELIX', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Jim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Mariners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T18:53:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1164e070-099a-5c0d-97fc-baa6d6939f8d', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1164e070-099a-5c0d-97fc-baa6d6939f8d'}, {'abstract': 'Utility and telecommunications stocks are the traditional dividend payers, but investors now have other places to turn for income, including technology stocks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/your-money/dividend-paying-stocks-found-in-unusual-places.html', 'snippet': 'Utility and telecommunications stocks are the traditional dividend payers, but investors now have other places to turn for income, including technology stocks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DIVIDEND seekers are in a bit of a quandary. As frightened investors have raced into defensive equities lately, traditional income-producing areas of the stock market have become fairly frothy. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/business/19-FUND1/19-FUND1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/business/19-FUND1/19-FUND1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1183, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding Dividends in Unusual Places', 'kicker': 'Fundamentally', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding Dividends In Unusual Places', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intel Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-18T18:57:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul J. Lim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Lim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/022ee7d6-27dc-55d5-be08-511784494a07', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/022ee7d6-27dc-55d5-be08-511784494a07'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Ryan spoke of his care for a relative with Alzheimer’s, seeking to counter President Obama’s charge that Republicans would “end Medicare as we know it.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/us/politics/in-defending-medicare-plan-ryan-speaks-on-caregiver-role.html', 'snippet': 'Paul Ryan spoke of his care for a relative with Alzheimer’s, seeking to counter President Obama’s charge that Republicans would “end Medicare as we know it.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE VILLAGES, Fla. — After several days in which he mentioned only generalities on the campaign trail, Representative Paul D. Ryan sought on Saturday to play offense on Medicare, attacking in detail President Obama’s health care plan, seizing an issue that has the potential to be one of Mr. Ryan’s biggest liabilities in joining the Republican presidential ticket. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/us/politics/19ryan2-span/sub-ryan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/19/us/politics/19ryan2-span/sub-ryan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/us/politics/19ryan2-span/sub-ryan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/us/politics/19ryan2-span/sub-ryan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1405, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/us/politics/19ryan2-span/sub-ryan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/19/us/politics/19ryan2-span/sub-ryan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/19/us/politics/19ryan2-span/sub-ryan-thu