are disinformation, on the cover.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/unethical-commentary-newsweek-edition/', 'snippet': 'Obamacare disinformation, on the cover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are multiple errors and misrepresentations in Niall Ferguson’s cover story in Newsweek — I guess they don’t do fact-checking — but this is the one that jumped out at me. Ferguson says:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unethical Commentary, Newsweek Edition', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-19T20:31:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93e8f732-ef45-5a26-8557-fa4294d8e2b3', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93e8f732-ef45-5a26-8557-fa4294d8e2b3'}, {'abstract': 'On the last day of the Downtown Dance Festival on Friday, the Erasing Borders program of Indian dance offered Bollywood and classical genres.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/arts/dance/indian-dance-at-downtown-dance-festival.html', 'snippet': 'On the last day of the Downtown Dance Festival on Friday, the Erasing Borders program of Indian dance offered Bollywood and classical genres.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In February, as I stood in line to collect my visa to go to India, the man next to me said: “You’re interested in Indian dance? But then you have to go to Bombay.” He was referring to dance in Bollywood movies.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/20/arts/erasing/erasing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/20/arts/erasing/erasing-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1314, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/20/arts/erasing/erasing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/20/arts/erasing/erasing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/20/arts/erasing/erasing-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian Dance via Bollywood, by Way of Russia, Near Wall Street', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indian Dance via Bollywood, by Way of Russia, Near Wall Street', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Downtown Dance Festival (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indo-American Arts Council', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-19T20:31:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d38ea8a7-d4ba-5540-a3d3-dc9d0e7d8ea8', 'word_count': 950, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d38ea8a7-d4ba-5540-a3d3-dc9d0e7d8ea8'}, {'abstract': '“Henry V,” “Much Ado About Nothing” and “Cymbeline” mix comedy and history at the Stratford Shakespeare Festival in Ontario.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/theater/stratford-shakespeare-festival-henry-v-and-cymbeline.html', 'snippet': '“Henry V,” “Much Ado About Nothing” and “Cymbeline” mix comedy and history at the Stratford Shakespeare Festival in Ontario.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STRATFORD, Ontario — One of the signal pleasures of attending the Stratford Shakespeare Festival here is the opportunity it affords to sample the breadth and depth of Shakespeare’s work in just a few days: a history play on Wednesday, a comedy on Thursday, a late romance on Friday. To survey Shakespeare’s plays in such proximity is sometimes to be reminded how unsatisfying — or at least how limiting — these traditional classifications can be. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/20/arts/jpstratford1/jpstratford1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/20/arts/jpstratford1/jpstratford1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/20/arts/jpstratford1/jpstratford1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 488, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/20/arts/jpstratford1/jpstratford1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 975, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'cred