nt filmmaker Ira Sachs, whose works have explored the lives of gay men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Museum of the Moving Image in Astoria, Queens, will host “Looking for Love,” the first major New York retrospective of the independent filmmaker Ira Sachs, whose works have explored the lives of gay men. The program is to include a selection of shorts and all of Mr. Sach’s feature films, including “The Delta,” “Forty Shades of Blue” and “Married Life.” His latest film, “Keep the Lights On,” about a man and his drug-addicted boyfriend (with Thure Lindhardt, above left, and Zachary Booth), had its premiere at the Sundance Film Festival in January and opens theatrically on Sept. 7. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum to Hold Sachs Retrospective', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Museum to Hold Sachs Retrospective', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sachs, Ira', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of the Moving Image', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-19T22:08:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d5a1450-cc47-5265-aecf-b047cdde26e6', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d5a1450-cc47-5265-aecf-b047cdde26e6'}, {'abstract': 'The celebrity blogger and gossip columnist Perez Hilton will make his New York theater debut in “Newsical the Musical: End of the World Edition.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/theater/from-gossip-to-musical-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The celebrity blogger and gossip columnist Perez Hilton will make his New York theater debut in “Newsical the Musical: End of the World Edition.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The celebrity blogger and gossip columnist Perez Hilton will make his New York theater debut next month when he joins the cast of the Off Broadway revue “Newsical the Musical: End of the World Edition,” a show that riffs on headlines. During his four-week engagement Mr. Hilton will perform a number written about him by Rick Crom, the show’s composer and lyricist. Mr. Hilton is to begin performances on Sept. 8 at the Kirk Theater in Clinton, with his opening night set for Sept. 17.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Gossip to Musical Theater', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Gossip To Musical Theater', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hilton, Perez', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-19T22:12:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/113eb982-55d2-58b0-a37f-7da3c52da310', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/113eb982-55d2-58b0-a37f-7da3c52da310'}, {'abstract': 'The following tax-exempt fixed-income issues are scheduled for pricing this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/business/treasury-auctions-set-for-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'The following tax-exempt fixed-income issues are scheduled for pricing this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Treasury’s schedule of financing this week includes Monday’s regular weekly auction of new three- and six-month bills and an auction of four-week bills on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Auctions Set for This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasury Auctions Set for This Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-19T22:16:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b58bb4c-e489-5a08-9912-6fba9189e32c', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b58bb4c-e489-5a08-9912-6fba9189e32c'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of $20 cash-only tickets are being available for more than 30 Off Broadway plays and musicals starting 20 minutes before curtain.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/theater-tickets-on-a-budget/', 'snippet': 'A selection of $20 cash-only tickets are being available for more than 30 Off Broadway plays and musicals starting 20 minutes before curtain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Starting on Sept. 4 the Off Broadway Alliance will sponsor 20at20, a biannual event now in its sixth year, in which $20 cash-only tickets are made available for more than 30 Off Broadway plays and musicals starting 20 minutes before curtain. According to the alliance, a nonprofit group that supports Off Broadway theater, budget-conscious theatergoers with stamina and an empty Saturday calendar could spend $100 — less than one Broadway ticket — to see five shows: “Gazillion Bubble Show,” at 11 a.m.; “Avenue Q,” at 2:30 p.m.; “Sistas: The Musical,” at 4:30 p.m.; “Silence! The Musical,” at 8 p.m.; and “Fuerzabruta,” at 10. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Tickets on a Budget', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Budget Theater Tickets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Off Broadway Alliance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-19T22:21:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52e7a2ea-61d8-52e4-a1ba-63971cbb9e21', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52e7a2ea-61d8-52e4-a1ba-63971cbb9e21'}, {'abstract': 'The victims were attending the funeral of a slain colleague in Ingushetia, a predominately Muslim republic in the volatile North Caucasus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/world/europe/bomber-kills-7-police-officers-in-russian-republic.html', 'snippet': 'The victims were attending the funeral of a slain colleague in Ingushetia, a predominately Muslim republic in the volatile North Caucasus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — A suicide bomber killed seven police officers who were attending the funeral of a slain colleague on Sunday morning in Ingushetia, a predominantly Muslim republic in the North Caucasus where Russia has long struggled to suppress a separatist insurgency. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bomber Kills 7 Officers in Russian Republic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bomber Kills 7 Officers in Russian Republic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attemp