 Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/c0a53161-a08f-594b-978f-18c5ce6a59de', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/c0a53161-a08f-594b-978f-18c5ce6a59de'}, {'abstract': 'Condé Nast, the magazine publisher, will go from being a client of the digital advertising company Flite to owning about 11 percent of it.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/19/conde-nast-invests-in-digital-advertising-company-flite/', 'snippet': 'Condé Nast, the magazine publisher, will go from being a client of the digital advertising company Flite to owning about 11 percent of it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Condé Nast, the high-end magazine publisher, will announce on Monday that it is joining the cloud.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Condé Nast Invests in Digital Advertising Company Flite', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Condé Nast to Buy Stake In Cloud-Based Ad Company', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conde Nast Publications Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Flite Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T01:21:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d98e512-6f2c-531f-9276-3405250102c3', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d98e512-6f2c-531f-9276-3405250102c3'}, {'abstract': 'A timetable set by a federal magistrate judge for the F.D.A. to follow in withdrawing the use of antibiotics in farm animals is too long.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/opinion/get-antibiotics-off-the-farm.html', 'snippet': 'A timetable set by a federal magistrate judge for the F.D.A. to follow in withdrawing the use of antibiotics in farm animals is too long.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this month, a federal magistrate judge in New York told the Food and Drug Administration to quit dillydallying on its three-decade effort to curb indiscriminate use of antibiotics in farm animals to spur their growth. He set a timetable for the agency to follow in withdrawing two important drugs — penicillin and two forms of tetracycline — from widespread use in animals. The trouble is, that timetable will give the F.D.A. five more years to complete the process. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Get Antibiotics Off the Farm', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Get Antibiotics Off the Farm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factory Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Livestock', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T01:23:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e4f142f-7da8-5351-a302-2b2196986ff2', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e4f142f-7da8-5351-a302-2b2196986ff2'}, {'abstract': 'Special-interest spending tilts state courts toward business interests, not independence. Top state judges should be appointed through merit selection, not elected.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/opinion/judicial-elections-and-the-bottom-line.html', 'snippet': 'Special-interest spending tilts state courts toward business interests, not independence. Top state judges should be appointed through merit selection, not elected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year, 32 states will be holding contested elections or retention votes for judges on their highest courts. An ideological battle in Florida, an expensive and partisan one in North Carolina and others are providing uncomfortable lessons about why judges on the highest courts should be appointed rather than elected. Elections turn judges into politicians, and the need to raise money to finance ever more expensive campaigns makes the judiciary more vulnerable to improper influence by donors. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judicial Elections and the Bottom Line', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judicial Elections and the Bottom Line', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for American Progress', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T01:23:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/af55b80c-8582-5838-9f77-6d0ef1b48351', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af55b80c-8582-5838-9f77-6d0ef1b48351'}, {'abstract': 'More than 2,000 people descended on Dieppe, France, on Sunday to commemorate one of the bloodiest days of World War II.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/08/20/world/europe/20120820DIEPPE.html', 'snippet': 'More than 2,000 people descended on Dieppe, France, on Sunday to commemorate one of the bloodiest days of World War II.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 2,000 people descended on Dieppe, France, on Sunday to commemorate one of the bloodiest days of World War II.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/20/world/europe/20120820DIEPPE-slide-CLAY/20120820DIEPPE-slide-CLAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/20/world/europe/20120820DIEPPE-slide-CLAY/20120820DIEPPE-slide-CLAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/20/world/europe/20120820DIEPPE-slide-CLAY/20120820DIEPPE-slide-CLAY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/20/world/europe/20120820DIEPPE-slide-CLAY/20120820DIEPPE-slide-CLAY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption