0/india-asks-pakistan-to-investigate-panic-tied-to-northeast/', 'snippet': 'Government officials in India blame “elements based in Pakistan” for triggering panic that led to the exodus of northeastern migrants to their native states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'India’s top security official on Sunday “called on the Pakistani government to investigate Indian claims that ‘elements based in Pakistan’ had orchestrated a fear-mongering misinformation campaign that helped set off last week’s nationwide panic among migrants from India’s northeastern states,” Jim Yardley wrote in The New York Times. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India Asks Pakistan to Investigate Panic Tied to Northeast', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T05:38:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1aef0af-67df-5e18-a346-c481ce43adb5', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1aef0af-67df-5e18-a346-c481ce43adb5'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Scott was known for visceral action films, including “Top Gun.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/director-tony-scott-jumps-to-his-death-from-los-angeles-bridge/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Scott was known for visceral action films, including “Top Gun.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Tony Scott, the director of exuberant action films including “Top Gun” and “Unstoppable” and a prolific producer of television shows and commercials in partnership with his older brother, Ridley Scott, died on Sunday after jumping from the Vincent Thomas Bridge into the Los Angeles Harbor. He was 68.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline':