irstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Folbre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f688f853-5ae0-549b-9ef6-bf199cbead36', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f688f853-5ae0-549b-9ef6-bf199cbead36'}, {'abstract': 'Is it the essential oil? Well, the dove that advised Noah he could finally park the Ark carried with it an olive sprig. Olive oil lit the lamp that miraculously burned for eight days, which Jews celebrate at Hanukkah. And the first Olympic competitors wore only a coating of it.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/in-tuscany-a-mad-celebrant-of-olive-oil/', 'snippet': 'Is it the essential oil? Well, the dove that advised Noah he could finally park the Ark carried with it an olive sprig. Olive oil lit the lamp that miraculously burned for eight days, which Jews celebrate at Hanukkah. And the first Olympic competi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'VICCHIO, Italy — When the Renaissance started around here on Giotto’s palette, back around 1300, olives had been oiling the works of Mediterranean civilizations for millennia. They symbolized peace, and a pleasant lunch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Tuscany, a Mad Celebrant of Olive Oil', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olive Oil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tuscany (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T10:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mort Rosenblum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mort', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenblum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa59c8fe-7840-5582-b2b5-9f21b3dc82fd', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa59c8fe-7840-5582-b2b5-9f21b3dc82fd'}, {'abstract': 'Park Geun-hye, a daughter of President Park Chung-hee, was the first woman to become the presidential candidate of a major political party in South Korea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/world/asia/park-geun-hye-nominated-for-south-korean-presidency.html', 'snippet': 'Park Geun-hye, a daughter of President Park Chung-hee, was the first woman to become the presidential candidate of a major political party in South Korea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — A former dictator’s daughter who cited Queen Elizabeth I of Britain as her role model became the first serious female contender for South Korea’s presidency on Monday when she was chosen as the governing party’s candidate for the election in December.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/world/asia/21korea_1/21korea_1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/world/asia/21korea_1/21korea_1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1464, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/world/asia/21korea_1/21korea_1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/21/world/asia/21korea_1/21korea_1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/world/asia/2