 'A Senate candidate’s comments on abortion may be the topic of the day, but there’s little chance the Romney-Ryan ticket will address it at a campaign event in New Hampshire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GOFFSTOWN, N.H. — Mitt Romney’s campaign is expecting several thousand people to attend the town-hall-style meeting he’s holding with his running mate, Paul D. Ryan, here today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Akin Comments Unlikely to Come Up at Romney-Ryan Event', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T13:16:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25f9fe5e-5e3f-5ce0-b00d-0b18b82f39f6', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25f9fe5e-5e3f-5ce0-b00d-0b18b82f39f6'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/what-were-reading-504/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Skirt Steak Files: Charlotte Druckman, whose book on women chefs, “Skirt Steak,” will be published in November, examines the lineup for the Grand Fooding festival next month in Brooklyn and runs some gender math: Of the 29 food industry participants in the dinners and other events taking place over five days, only two are women. Neither of those women is a chef. The festival is put together by Le Fooding, a French group that claims to offer a younger, fresher perspective on the restaurant scene. — Pete Wells', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T13:20:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5dea4ec-6760-5383-81a8-e93749ee4225', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5dea4ec-6760-5383-81a8-e93749ee4225'}, {'abstract': 'The British airport operator BAA has agreed to sell Stansted Airport, a base for many of Europe’s low-cost airlines. Potential buyers include the British firm Manchester Airports Group and the Incheon International Airport Corporation.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/baa-to-sell-a-london-airport-after-an-antitrust-ruling/', 'snippet': 'The British airport operator BAA has agreed to sell Stansted Airport, a base for many of Europe’s low-cost airlines. Potential buyers include the British firm Manchester Airports Group and the Incheon International Airport Corporation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The British airport operator BAA agreed on Monday to sell Stansted Airport in London after the company decided not to challenge a court ruling on antitrust grounds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Antitrust Ruling, BAA to Sell a London Airport', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BAA Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stansted International Airport (London)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T13:21:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fab97f94-524a-58c8-b5b0-df661d8e499e', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fab97f94-524a-58c8-b5b0-df661d8e499e'}, {'abstract': 'Kinder Morgan Energy Partners has agreed to sell some pipeline and processing properties to Tallgrass Energy Partners for about $1.8 billion in cash, in the latest asset sale by the company in the wake of its takeover of the El Paso Corporation.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/kinder-morgan-to-sell-assets-to-tallgrass-for-1-8-billion/', 'snippet': 'Kinder Morgan Energy Partners has agreed to sell some pipeline and processing properties to Tallgrass Energy Partners for about $1.8 billion in cash, in the latest asset sale by the company in the wake of its takeover of the El Paso Corporation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kinder Morgan Energy Partners said on Monday that it had agreed to sell some pipeline and processing properties to Tallgrass Energy Partners for about $1.8 billion in cash, in the latest asset sale by the company in the wake of its takeover of the El Paso Corporation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kinder Morgan to Sell Assets to Tallgrass for $1.8 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kinder Morgan Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T13:31:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0ce295d-062e-567c-a81f-45ee919462f5', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0ce295d-062e-567c-a81f-45ee919462f5'}, {'abstract': 'Two decades after the Board of Estimate, a powerful city body, was terminated, it still exists — at least in the pages of the city’s manual of rules and regulations.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/years-after-it-was-abolished-a-city-board-lives-on/', 'snippet': 'Two decades after the Board of Estimate, a powerful city body, was terminated, it still exists — at least in the pages of the city’s manual of rules and regulations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The city’s Board of Estimate, an omnipotent body composed of the five borough presidents and three citywide elected officials, was gaveled to order for the last time on Aug. 27, 1990. But anybody who spends time delving into the city’s administrative code — there are people like this — knows that the board lives on in scores of references in the directory. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Years After It Was Abolished, a City Board Lives On', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vallone, Peter F Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T13:42:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30ef0a3d-2b05-56d7-a3c8-9c9d107f5e9c', 'word_count': 941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30ef0a3d-2b05-56d7-a3c8-9c9d107f5e9c'}, {'abstract': 'Why has median household income endured its worst 12-year stretch since the Great Depression? Experts and readers respond to some of the potential causes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/the-14-potential-causes-of-the-income-slump/', 'snippet': 'Why has median household income endured its worst 12-year stretch since the Great Depression? Experts and readers respond to some of the potential causes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Why has median household income just endured its worst 12-year stretch since the Great Depression?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 14 Potential Causes of the Income Slump', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T13:50:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7647923-9030-55ca-a060-bd5b69088865', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7647923-9030-55ca-a060-bd5b69088865'}, {'abstract': 'Also, David Carr on why some journalists make things up, and movie theater chains decide they can make films, too.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/the-breakfast-meeting-restoring-the-zakaria-brand-and-profiting-in-textbooks/', 'snippet': 'Also, David Carr on why some journalists make things up, and movie theater chains decide they can make films, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The multimedia career of Fareed Zakaria — CNN host, Time magazine and Washington Post columnist, public speaker — took a hit this month when he was found to have lifted entire passages from a New Yorker article for his Time magazine column. After a brief suspension, he will return to those outlets. But he tells Christine Haughney that he has been chastened by the experience: “Other things will have to go away. There’s got to be some stripping down.” To media critics, Mr. Zakaria is an example of how the personal brand now trumps the institutional brand, even of important outlets like Time and CNN. Still, even a widely successful personal brand can be overextended.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Restoring the Zakaria Brand, and Profiting in Textbooks', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T13:51:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fac56397-af03-5955-bdcd-c11d3e01595f', 'word_count': 669, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fac56397-af03-5955-bdcd-c11d3e01595f'}, {'abstract': 'When negotiating a sale, Instagram’s founders could have protected themselves from a decline in Faceook’s share value if they had used some common merger tools.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/how-instagram-could-have-cut-a-better-deal/', 'snippet': 'When negotiating a sale, Instagram’s founders could have protected themselves from a decline in Faceook’s share value if they had used some common merger tools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In hindsight, perhaps Instagram should have cut a different deal with Facebook. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Instagram Could Have Cut a Better Deal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T13:55:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ee0fc66-718d-5195-b05b-31ecfecc814f', 'word_count': 1290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ee0fc66-718d-5195-b05b-31ecfecc814f'}, {'abstract': 'Writers continued to look at the Melky Cabrera suspension after a report that an associate of his purchased a Web site in a scheme to support the player’s claim that his positive drug test was an accident.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/leading-off-get-a-web-site-for-that/', 'snippet': 'Writers continued to look at the Melky Cabrera suspension after a report that an associate of his purchased a Web site in a scheme to support the player’s claim that his positive drug test was an accident.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the heels of a report that an associate of the Giants’ Melky Cabrera tried to concoct a fake Web site so the outfielder could wiggle out of punishment for his positive test for performance-enhancing drugs, it is tempting to roll your eyes and toss him on the pile of sports’ most dismal cheaters. But he might really be on to something. Wouldn’t we all like to create a Web site to explain away a late car insurance payment or a forgotten anniversary. (Look, honey, cosmic-excuses.com says the Earth’s slowed rotation combined with global warming and the obesity epidemic means it’s really May 3. I’m not late!)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off: Get a Web Site for That!', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryant, Kobe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cabrera, Melky', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunn, Adam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Deion', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Giants', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T14:02:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f91abb29-e33d-5760-84ff-fe9046c0c9e7', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f91abb29-e33d-5760-84ff-fe9046c0c9e7'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican presidential candidate Mitt Romney’s image makers know he has been perceived as stiff and distant. They are determined to use the convention to display his warmer side, on prime time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000001729498/bui