le to make a return call — resulting in big phone fees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple of weeks ago I started getting persistent phone calls from an overseas number. The calls repeated in groups of five or so over a roughly 15-minute period before stopping. Then they would resume hours or days later. When I checked the number, I found it was from Ukraine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Twist on an Old Phone Swindle', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T14:22:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/404d63f9-e245-5ff3-9847-07f63c7f52fa', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/404d63f9-e245-5ff3-9847-07f63c7f52fa'}, {'abstract': 'A writer is of the opinion that we’re teaching a generation of children to reach for a pill instead of learning to cope.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/criticizing-the-ritalin-generation/', 'snippet': 'A writer is of the opinion that we’re teaching a generation of children to reach for a pill instead of learning to cope.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much has been written about the Ritalin Generation, to the point where many parents of children with attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, and people with A.D.H.D themselves, feel more than a little condemned