ogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/a-low-water-tour-of-the-mississippi-river/', 'snippet': 'The Mississippi River Commission’s annual low-water inspection tour is two weeks of travel and talk in which the panel that advises the Army Corps of Engineers on managing the mighty river speaks directly with the American people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABOARD THE MOTOR VESSEL MISSISSIPPI, at Alton, Illinois — The big room was crowded on Friday with people who had gathered mainly to complain. It’s the annual low-water inspection tour, a summer ritual of the Mississippi River Commission, two weeks of travel and talk in which the panel that advises the Army Corps of Engineers on managing the mighty river and its tributaries speaks directly with the American people in their own towns, on their rivers. The tour was immortalized in a 1987 essay in The New Yorker by John McPhee titled “Atchafalaya.” That essay appeared in his wonderful 1990 book, “The Control of Nature.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Low-Water Tour of the Mississippi River', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Levees and Dams', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARMY CORPS OF ENGINEERS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi River', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T14:58:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9534e1ce-f867-52e2-b93e-1c5d732f1af7', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9534e1ce-f867-52e2-b93e-1c5d732f1af7'}, {'abstract': 'Josh Wald’s Greenpoint property, offered for $2.5 million, immediately became the object of some derision on Curbed and Brownstoner, but experts say the attention won’t hurt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/nyregion/listing-of-models-brooklyn-home-ignites-blog-readers.html', 'snippet': 'Josh Wald’s Greenpoint property, offered for $2.5 million, immediately became the object of some derision on Curbed and Brownstoner, but experts say the attention won’t hurt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pictures of Josh Wald’s three-story, cedar-shingled home in Greenpoint, Brooklyn, seemed perfectly nice. They showed a leafy garden, a bright, open kitchen, the sleek retro finishes one might find in a Restoration Hardware catalog and a closet larger than many New York apartments. All those touches were drawn together with an asking price of $2.499 million.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/nyregion/21APPRAISAL/21APPRAISAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/21/nyregion/21APPRAISAL/21APPRAISAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/nyregion/21APPRAISAL/21APPRAISAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/nyregion/21APPRAISAL/21APPRAISAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'r