hool’s Borden Auditorium. Other musicians, including several of Manhattan’s staff members, will also take part. Two pieces will have their first performances: “Constellation,” for two violas, celeste and piano (that would be Mr. Sirota’s contribution) and “Twelve Days,” for six violas (as if there weren’t enough violas in Mr. Sirota’s life). Mr. Sirota has been president of Manhattan since 2005.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Concert for the Exiting Manhattan School of Music President', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Goodbye Concert For Robert Sirota', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manhattan School of Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T19:48:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/202093ca-edbb-501a-beb0-862947aa9b03', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/202093ca-edbb-501a-beb0-862947aa9b03'}, {'abstract': 'Breaking an 80-year-old ban against admitting female members, the Augusta National Golf Club turned to two women with distinguished careers. One is Darla Moore, a former banker turned financier whose negotiating toughness is the stuff of legend.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/financier-gets-nod-as-one-of-2-women-admitted-to-augusta-national/', 'snippet': 'Breaking an 80-year-old ban against admitting female members, the Augusta National Golf Club turned to two women with distinguished careers. One is Darla Moore, a former banker turned financier whose negotiating toughness is the stuff of legend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fo