an Orthodox Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T20:30:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62781fb2-cbbb-58ca-9d45-1804811121b9', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62781fb2-cbbb-58ca-9d45-1804811121b9'}, {'abstract': 'The author of this week’s cover article describes Roseland, the area of Chicago where Obama worked as a community organizer, and the challenge in turning political speech into action.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/behind-the-cover-story-paul-tough-on-how-obamas-stance-on-poverty-has-changed/', 'snippet': 'The author of this week’s cover article describes Roseland, the area of Chicago where Obama worked as a community organizer, and the challenge in turning political speech into action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Tough, a contributing writer for the magazine, wrote\xa0this week’s cover article\xa0on Roseland, a struggling section in Chicago where Barack Obama worked as a community organizer. Tough is the author of “Whatever It Takes: Geoffrey Canada’s Quest to Change Harlem and America.” His\xa0last article\xa0for the magazine was about schools focusing on students’ character as well as academic subjects like math or science. His new book, “How Children Succeed: Grit, Curiosity, and the Hidden Power of Character,” will come out on Sept. 4.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Cover Story: Paul Tough on How Obama’s Stance on Poverty Has Changed', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo