web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/the-making-of-a-thriller-writer/', 'snippet': 'A faux encounter with a Ludlum character and my father’s imagination were one of the many ways my parents set me on a thriller writer’s path.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was one of those arid summer days where you can see heat rippling from the pavement. Air-conditioning in the cranky Chevrolet up full blast. Kermit and the Muppets on the stereo singing about a rainbow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Making of a Thriller Writer', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ludlum, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T21:35:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Richtel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richtel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db1b9a80-071f-5763-a9e7-4e749e7239dc', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db1b9a80-071f-5763-a9e7-4e749e7239dc'}, {'abstract': 'Despite the facts, the ancient idea that women have some natural defense against being impregnated by rapists has been endorsed several times in recent years by elected officials who oppose abortion.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/myth-about-rape-and-pregnancy-is-not-new/', 'snippet': 'Despite the facts, the ancient idea that women have some natural defense against being impregnated by rapists has been endorsed several times in recent years by elected officials who oppose abortion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, 12:22 a.m. Representative Todd Akin, the Republican Senate nominee from Missouri, gave new prominence to an old myth this past weekend when he downplayed the need for rape victims to have access to abortions. He claimed  that pregnancies from rape are “really rare,” because, “If it’s a legitimate rape, the female body has ways to try to shut that whole thing down.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Myth About Rape and Pregnancy Is Not New', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akin, Todd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boozman, Fay', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huckabee, Mike', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARKANSAS', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T21:40:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39af3c5d-8321-52ba-a7d0-bd97f9ae619a', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39af3c5d-8321-52ba-a7d0-bd97f9ae619a'}, {'abstract': 'Eight of the ten N.B.A. owners who have made contributions to the candidates’ campaigns so far have donated to Mr. Romney’s campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/for-n-b-a-owners-the-moneys-on-romney/', 'snippet': 'Eight of the ten N.B.A. owners who have made contributions to the candidates’ campaigns so far have donated to Mr. Romney’s campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama may have a better jump shot than his Republican rival for president, but N.B.A. owners seem more eager to offer Mitt Romney the bigger contract.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For N.B.A. Owners, the Money’s on Romney', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Team Play: For N.B.A. Team Owners, Romney Is Their First Pick', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T21:42:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a97fb6e-4dcd-56d7-9eed-08f6bc99a850', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a97fb6e-4dcd-56d7-9eed-08f6bc99a850'}, {'abstract': 'Somalia swore in a new government to replace the internationally-backed transitional federal government that has tried in recent years to assert control over the embattled country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/world/africa/new-parliament-is-convened-in-somalia.html', 'snippet': 'Somalia swore in a new government to replace the internationally-backed transitional federal government that has tried in recent years to assert control over the embattled country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOGADISHU, Somalia — Somalia convened a new federal Parliament on Monday, swearing in a new government to replace the internationally backed transitional federal government that has tried, with varying degrees of success, to assert control over the embattled country in recent years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/global-home/21somalia-image2/21somalia-image2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/global-home/21somalia-image2/21somalia-image2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1346, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Parliament Is Convened in Somalia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mogadishu (Somalia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T21:42:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mohamed Ibrahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mohamed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ibrahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4bc6044-fde7-5eea-8b68-851a11c0179d', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4bc6044-fde7-5eea-8b68-851a11c0179d'}, {'abstract': 'Chugging behind a whale in an inflatable vessel, researchers may have only a precious second or two to affix an electronic tag to its glistening back. The tag precisely tracks the animal’s movements.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/a-whale-a-tag-a-mission/', 'snippet': 'Chugging behind a whale in an inflatable vessel, researchers may have only a precious second or two to affix an electronic tag to its glistening back. The tag precisely tracks the animal’s movements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I note in my article for Tuesday’s Times, humpback whales spend summer after summer just a stone’s throw from the coast of Massachusetts, yet scientists are still only beginning to learn fairly basic things about them. In our modern world of satellites and chips, it’s amazing how little we know about whales.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Whale, a Tag, a Mission', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-20T21:47:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kelly Slivka', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kelly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Slivka', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04741791-1fe3-53bb-94a2-96f2377f5d4d', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04741791-1fe3-53bb-94a2-96f2377f5d4d'}, {'abstract': 'The Bard Music Festival’s grand finale was a concert performance of Camille Saint-Saëns’s stately, largely unheard 1883 opera, “Henry VIII,” conducted by Leon Botstein.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/arts/music/leon-botstein-conducts-henry-viii-at-bard-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The Bard Music Festival’s grand finale was a concert performance of Camille Saint-Sa