lue': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T00:13:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Moore and Oliver Stone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Oliver', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9af1a80f-81e0-5a21-b160-6c72b81bcd7c', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9af1a80f-81e0-5a21-b160-6c72b81bcd7c'}, {'abstract': 'The nation’s pipeline network is governed by laws and regulations that were written long before the unique risks and hazards associated with dilbit began to emerge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/opinion/the-dangers-of-diluted-bitumen-oil.html', 'snippet': 'The nation’s pipeline network is governed by laws and regulations that were written long before the unique risks and hazards associated with dilbit began to emerge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVERY day more than one million barrels of oil flow to refineries in the United States from western Canada’s oil sands region. Producers hope to quadruple that amount in the next decade, arguing that oil from a friendly neighbor will deliver an extra degree of national security. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crude, Dirty and Dangerous', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crude, Dirty and Dangerous', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Spills', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Enb