w require small restaurants and cafes to have just one bathroom, not two.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They are gently lighted and spacious and lined with pristine tiles. They are as cramped as Port-O-Lets, splashed with graffiti and redolent with urine. They can be found behind sliding barnlike doors, down rickety staircases, through fry cooks’ kitchens or, just as often, not at all.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/nyregion/SUB-BATHROOM/SUB-BATHROOM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/nyregion/SUB-BATHROOM/SUB-BATHROOM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1531, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Rule Shift, Restroom Hunt May Get Tougher', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Rule Shift, Restroom Hunt May Get Tougher', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Mental Hygiene Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starbucks Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bathrooms and Toilets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T00:46:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'or