ing electronics retailer aiming to turn around its fortunes, announced Monday that it had hired the chief executive of the hospitality company Carlson as its new leader — a move that is likely to be the first of several disclosures the company plans to make to reassure investors.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With New Chief, Best Buy Tries to Set Its Own Turnaround', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Best Buy Names a Hospitality Executive as Its Chief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Best BUY Company Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T01:03:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77423a57-a677-55f2-892a-1f21ceed7eea', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77423a57-a677-55f2-892a-1f21ceed7eea'}, {'abstract': 'The Public Company Accounting Oversight Board said that it had found deficiencies in every audit of brokerage firms that it had reviewed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/business/accounting-board-faults-audits-of-brokerage-firms.html', 'snippet': 'The Public Company Accounting Oversight Board said that it had found deficiencies in every audit of brokerage firms that it had reviewed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The many auditors who inspect the financial statements of brokerage firms appear to be cutting corners and not doing all the work they should do, a worrisome sign after the collapse of the Peregrine Financial Group, a leading commodities brokerage firm, where a fraud had gone undetected for many years.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/business/Audit/Audit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/business/Audit/Audit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Regulator Says Broker Audits Fail to Include Required Work', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Regulator Says Broker Audits Fail to Include Required Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Company Accounting Oversight Board', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Brokers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T01:05:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ed80669-5a75-5f0e-a38a-576445e854b5', 'word_count': 991, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ed80669-5a75-5f0e-a38a-576445e854b5'}, {'abstract': 'Darla Moore has made her mark as one of Wall Street’s most powerful and wealthy female executives, known for taking defunct companies and making them profitable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/sports/golf/darla-moore-new-augusta-member-knows-about-barriers.html', 'snippet': 'Darla Moore has made her mark as one of Wall Street’s most powerful and wealthy female executives, known for taking defunct companies and making them profitable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After years of working her way to the highest levels of Wall Street, Darla Moore was still thinking about a dilapidated building known as the bean market in her hometown, Lake City, S.C. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/sports/subYGOLF/subYGOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/sports/subYGOLF/subYGOLF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1378, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/sports/subYGOLF/subYGOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/21/sports/subYGOLF/subYGOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/sports/subYGOLF/subYGOLF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In World of Finance, One New Member Has Already Driven the Green', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In World of Finance, She Has Already Driven the Green', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Masters Golf Tournament', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Augusta National Golf Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Condoleezza', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Darla', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T01:06:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Pilon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pilon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/396f1cca-3727-5038-8484-9be7655272cf', 'word_count': 976, 'uri': 'nyt://article/396f1cca-3727-5038-8484-9be7655272cf'}, {'abstract': 'A judge nullified an important plan to increase taxi service in the outer boroughs. It is now up to the City Council to fix this problem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/opinion/new-york-citys-taxi-plan.html', 'snippet': 'A judge nullified an important plan to increase taxi service in the outer boroughs. It is now up to the City Council to fix this problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a sweeping ruling last week, Justice Arthur Engoron of State Supreme Court in Manhattan nullified New York City’s important plan to increase taxi service in the outer boroughs and northern Manhattan. By doing so, he knocked a $635 million hole in the city’s $68.5 billion budget. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York City’s Taxi Plan', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York City’s Taxi Plan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vacca, James', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Engoron, Arthur F', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T01:07:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/56367074-3a5a-5888-aee3-a530234063dd', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56367074-3a5a-5888-aee3-a530234063dd'}, {'abstract': 'With the decision by the Augusta National Golf Club to welcome two women into its fold, another bastion of male authority has gotten with the times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/opinion/women-at-the-augusta-golf-club.html', 'snippet': 'With the decision by the Augusta National Golf Club to welcome two women into its fold, another bastion of male authority has gotten with the times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What a year this has been for women breaking barriers. Daw Aung San Suu Kyi took a seat in Myanmar’s Parliament. Saudi Arabia, Brunei and Qatar let women compete on their Olympic teams for the first time. And now another bastion of male authority and rigorous devotion to antiquated laws has heeded the call of equality.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Women at Augusta', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Women at Augusta', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Augusta National Golf Club', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Payne, Billy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T01:07:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b6b86e8-c965-5f32-b037-0c0caa304929', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b6b86e8-c965-5f32-b037-0c0caa304929'}, {'abstract': 'American troops are increasingly at risk from attacks from their supposed Afghan allies. More must be done to protect American forces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/opinion/the-enemy-within.html', 'snippet': 'American troops are increasingly at risk from attacks from their supposed Afghan allies. More must be done to protect American forces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s bad enough when American and coalition troops in Afghanistan meet death at the hands of the Taliban. Now they are increasingly vulnerable to members of the Afghan Army and police — the very forces they are training to secure the country’s future. At least 40 NATO troops have been killed by their Afghan counterparts this year, including 10 American service members in one horrendous two-week stretch. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Enemy Within', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Enemy Within', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T01:07:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a981927-9af9-57f8-95e2-e8b0caf49062', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a981927-9af9-57f8-95e2-e8b0caf49062'}, {'abstract': 'Industry and government officials along the East Coast and the Gulf of Mexico believe their ports, too, can gain from the expansion of the Panama Canal to allow much larger ships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/us/us-ports-seek-to-lure-big-ships-after-panama-canal-expands.html', 'snippet': 'Industry and government officials along the East Coast and the Gulf of Mexico believe their ports, too, can gain from the expansion of the Panama Canal to allow much larger ships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — The four cranes rise grandly over the port here, 14 stories high. Just off the boat from China and now being prepared for operations, the $40 million machines are part of this city’s gamble that when supersize container ships start coming through the expanded Panama Canal in 2015, Baltimore will be one of the few ports on the East Coast ready for their business. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/us/PORTS-1/PORTS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/21/us/PORTS-1/PORTS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/us/PORTS-1/PORTS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/us/PORTS-1/PORTS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/us/PORTS-1/PORTS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/21/us/PORTS-1/PORTS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/21/us/PORTS-1/PORTS-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Panama Canal’s Growth Prompts U.S. Ports to Expand', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Ports Expand, With an Eye On Panama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'va