on': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cd47ef0-0155-5ea8-be38-71a418c27d20', 'word_count': 1233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cd47ef0-0155-5ea8-be38-71a418c27d20'}, {'abstract': 'If you’re a moderate voter, it’s important to think through what really matters this year. How we go about entitlement spending should be a top priority.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/opinion/brooks-guide-for-the-perplexed.html', 'snippet': 'If you’re a moderate voter, it’s important to think through what really matters this year. How we go about entitlement spending should be a top priority.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s say you’re generally a moderate voter. You look at the Romney-Ryan ticket and see that they are much more conservative than you. They don’t believe in tax increases ever. You think tax increases have to be a part of a budget deal. They want to slash social spending to the bone. You think that would be harsh on the vulnerable and bad for social cohesion.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Guide for the Perplexed', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guide For the Perplexed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T01:23:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/daa2015e-8157-5794-bb0c-fcf5ddfde875', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daa2015e-8157-5794-bb0c-fcf5ddfde875'}, {'abstract': 'Once in a great while, a poll comes along with methodology that is so implausible that it deserves some further comment. The Foster McCollum White Baydoun poll of Florida is one such survey.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/20/aug-20-when-the-polling-gets-weird/', 'snippet': 'Once in a great while, a poll comes along with methodology that is so implausible that it deserves some further comment. The Foster McCollum White Baydoun poll of Florida is one such survey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Monday brought a Monmouth University poll showing President Obama ahead by one point in the national race — the same margin that he had in the last poll they conducted in June. Mitt Romney held onto a 2-point lead in the Gallup national tracking poll, and pulled ahead of Mr. Obama again by one point in the Rasmussen national tracker, which has fluctuated a bit recently but usually has a steady number like that. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 20: When the Polling Gets Weird', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T01:25:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67dc495c-b087-5e9b-b073-c9bd82d89c8c', 'word_count': 1246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67dc495c-b087-5e9b-b073-c9bd82d89c8c'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama warned Syria on Monday that it would face American military intervention if there were signs that its arsenal of unconventional weapons was being moved or prepared for use.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/world/middleeast/obama-threatens-force-against-syria.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama warned Syria on Monday that it would face American military intervention if there were signs that its arsenal of unconventional weapons was being moved or prepared for use.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama warned Syria on Monday that it would face American military intervention if there were signs that its arsenal of unconventional weapons was being moved or prepared for use. It was Mr. Obama’s first direct threat of force against Syria, as he has resisted being drawn into the bloody 18-month rebellion.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Threatens Force Against Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Threatens Force Against Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T01:26:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d4ccc0b-2c3a-5720-bedb-bba9a8d2f2b0', 'word_count': 960, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d4ccc0b-2c3a-5720-bedb-bba9a8d2f2b0'}, {'abstract': 'The views articulated by Representative Todd Akin are far from new in anti-abortion circles, but leading experts on reproductive health said there is no solid data to support his clai