-straight-into-the-voting-booth/', 'snippet': 'Why are young people enthusiastic volunteers and organizers but tepid voters?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It strikes me as funny that we call our political organizations “parties.” For most of us, elections and political parties are the antithesis of fun. It’s no wonder that many young people avoid them. As colleges around the country welcome hordes of students, and politicians feebly attempt to spark interest in the fall election, we should ask why.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scared Straight — Into the Voting Booth', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T03:13:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By ANN BEESON', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'BEESON', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c0a4f03-e0c1-5dc9-8a9f-d020b39143a7', 'word_count': 1366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c0a4f03-e0c1-5dc9-8a9f-d020b39143a7'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Coughlin and players were not happy that the video of second-year cornerback Prince Amukamara being tossed in an ice tub was released. Some viewers described the video content as bullying.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/sports/football/giants-upset-over-release-of-prank-video-of-player-being-tossed-in-ice-tub.html', 'snippet': 'Tom Coughlin and players were not happy that the video of second-year cornerback Prince Amukamara being tossed in an ice tub was released. Some viewers described the video content as bullying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — The sign above the entrance to the Giants’ locker room reads “NY Giants Championship Culture,” indicating that members of the defending Super Bowl 