am Davidson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davidson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a19c9629-0bbb-5038-8fee-eb6e56fbd2d1', 'word_count': 1255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a19c9629-0bbb-5038-8fee-eb6e56fbd2d1'}, {'abstract': 'In the fifth installment of his series, “Smoke-Filled Rooms,” New York Times staff photographer Stephen Crowley examines the candidates’ foreign policies.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/smoke-filled-rooms-over-there/', 'snippet': 'In the fifth installment of his series, “Smoke-Filled Rooms,” New York Times staff photographer Stephen Crowley examines the candidates’ foreign policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While pundits agree that this presidential election will likely turn on economic issues, the candidates have been busy demonstrating that they are capable in foreign policy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shaping Foreign Policy', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crowley, Stephen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T09:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58afb577-42a2-5ba6-bbec-3e4fa175b19c', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58afb577-42a2-5ba6-bbec-3e4fa175b19c'}, {'abstract': 'Some northeastern students are staying put in their colleges, feeling insecure going back to their rented accommodations.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/in-bangalore-classrooms-turn-into-makeshift-homes/', 'snippet': 'Some northeastern students are staying put in their colleges, feeling insecure going back to their rented accommodations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A classroom on the third floor of the humanities block of St. Joseph’s College in Bangalore now serves as a makeshift dormitory. Mattresses have been rolled out atop benches laid side by side and on the professors’ wooden podium, surrounded by duffel bags packed for an indefinite stay. Since Thursday, five girls from India’s northeastern states have made this space their home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Bangalore, Classrooms Turn Into Makeshift Homes', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangalore (India)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T09:49:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niharika Mandhana', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niharika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandhana', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32837291-8e4b-5357-9d03-37c0f1e96ad5', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32837291-8e4b-5357-9d03-37c0f1e96ad5'}, {'abstract': 'Insurgents fired at the plane of Gen. Martin E. Dempsey as it was parked at the heavily fortified Bagram Airfield in Afghanistan, American and NATO officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/world/asia/top-us-commanders-plane-damaged-in-afghan-attack.html', 'snippet': 'Insurgents fired at the plane of Gen. Martin E. Dempsey as it was parked at the heavily fortified Bagram Airfield in Afghanistan, American and NATO officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Insurgents hiding outside the heavily fortified Bagram Air Base fired a pair of rockets early Tuesday that damaged the parked C-17 transport plane used by Gen. Martin E. Dempsey, the chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, American and Afghan officials said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rocket Fire Damages Plane Used by Joint Chiefs Chairman', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plane Used by Joint Chiefs Chairman Is Damaged by Rocket Fire in Afghanistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Martin E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bagram Air Base (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Aircraft', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T09:59:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr. and Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr.', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cf3ef52-2739-5965-99d0-ea2d9a1ef3da', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cf3ef52-2739-5965-99d0-ea2d9a1ef3da'}, {'abstract': 'Unsurprising, Mitt Romney supports provision of the tax code that benefits people in his own financial circumstances, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/exploring-mitt-romneys-taxes-and-tax-plan/', 'snippet': 'Unsurprising, Mitt Romney supports provision of the tax code that benefits people in his own financial circumstances, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul. He is the author of “The Benefit and the Burden: Tax Reform – Why We Need It and What It Will Take.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exploring Mitt Romney’s Taxes and Tax Plan', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tax Policy Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T10:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f21ebf41-b229-5386-9018-ca708da4c496', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f21ebf41-b229-5386-9018-ca708da4c496'}, {'abstract': 'The event, which was threatened with extinction in 2009, put on a show of strength last weekend in metro Detroit.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/the-woodward-dream-cruise-rediscovers-its-strut/', 'snippet': 'The event, which was threatened with extinction in 2009, put on a show of strength last weekend in metro Detroit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROYAL OAK, Mich. — As the 18th annual Woodward Dream Cruise got under way on Saturday morning, I drove south on Woodward Avenue accompanied by my wife, Marlene, and son, Erik, in our 1955 Chevrolet Bel Air. Our immediate goal was a breakfast of sliders at the venerable Hunter House in Birmingham, a nutritionally suspect Dream Cruise tradition for the Stenquist clan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Woodward Dream Cruise Rediscovers Its Strut', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cadillac Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Studebaker Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T10:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fa59332-d84c-5c83-a786-7826f9fbb66f', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fa59332-d84c-5c83-a786-7826f9fbb66f'}, {'abstract': 'There’s no need to wait until the bitter or glorious end to start looking ahead to next season.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/fantasy-focus-keeper-possibilities/', 'snippet': 'There’s no need to wait until the bitter or glorious end to start looking ahead to next season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m far from alone in playing in multiple fantasy leagues. I like all formats: A.L./N.L.-only, keeper, redraft, mixed, head-to-head, roto, Scoresheet and Strat-O-Matic. I’ve succeeded in most formats, and failed in the same, with this year being no different. In at least two of my keeper leagues, I’m already looking toward 2013, speculating on potential closers and looking to acquire guys that could be undervalued in next year’s drafts. Here’s a look at a handful (with statistics through Sunday’s games unless noted):', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantasy Focus: Keeper Possibilities', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Domonic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Wade', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Espinosa, Danny', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jennings, Desmond', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T10:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Regan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Regan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/126f4513-77d3-5d83-85bb-643fd8ed764c', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/126f4513-77d3-5d83-85bb-643fd8ed764c'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/the-early-word-uproar/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Today’s Times', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Uproar', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T10:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f309994e-67f4-51a8-b149-f52668037490', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f309994e-67f4-51a8-b149-f52668037490'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Meles oversaw substantial economic growth as prime minister and made Ethiopia a staunch American counterterrorism ally but drew criticism for harsh treatment of dissidents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/world/africa/meles-zenawi-ethiopian-leader-dies-at-57.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Meles oversaw substantial economic growth as prime minister and made Ethiopia a staunch American counterterrorism ally but drew criticism for harsh treatment of dissidents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Meles Zenawi, Ethiopia’s repressive prime minister, who lifted his country from the ruins of civil war and transformed it into one of Africa’s fastest-growing economies and one of the United States government’s closest African allies, died on Monday, state television reported. He was 57.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/world/22zenawi_3/22zenawi_3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'ju