l Qaeda is doing in Syria has recently moved to the forefront of the West’s debate over how to respond to the uprising against President Bashar al-Assad.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/concerns-about-al-qaeda-in-syria-underscore-questions-about-rebels/', 'snippet': 'The question of what Al Qaeda is doing in Syria has recently moved to the forefront of the West’s debate over how to respond to the uprising against President Bashar al-Assad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is Al Qaeda doing in Syria?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Concerns About Al Qaeda in Syria Underscore Questions About Rebels', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T10:40:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fff30b8-7496-5bcc-a2d6-8018aa14a11b', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fff30b8-7496-5bcc-a2d6-8018aa14a11b'}, {'abstract': '‘Real Sports With Bryant Gumbel’ will feature Steve Gleason, who lifted New Orleans’s spirits after Hurricane Katrina and who is now dealing with Lou Gehrig’s disease.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/steve-gleasons-story/', 'snippet': '‘Real Sports With Bryant Gumbel’ will feature Steve Gleason, who lifted New Orleans’s spirits after Hurricane Katrina and who is now dealing with Lou Gehrig’s disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A game is just a game, but every once in a while, it transcends that. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steve Gleason’s Story', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Orleans Saints', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T10:45:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9a8397f-d28e-5e91-bb9e-f10346fac8e5', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9a8397f-d28e-5e91-bb9e-f10346fac8e5'}, {'abstract': 'The Bucs are on the right track after last season’s disaster, but another last-place finish in the division looms.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/tampa-bay-bucs-2012-season-preview/', 'snippet': 'The Bucs are on the right track after last season’s disaster, but another last-place finish in the division looms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy Benoit, who is previewing all 32 teams, turns his attention to the N.F.C. South this week, starting with the Tampa Bay Buccaneers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tampa Bay Bucs, 2012 Season Preview', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Buccaneers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T11:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28dd5074-3aed-58f0-b75e-7cc71d665018', 'word_count': 2816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28dd5074-3aed-58f0-b75e-7cc71d665018'}, {'abstract': 'If you take these steps, you may have a crowd in place when equity crowdfunding gets final approval.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/its-not-too-soon-to-think-about-crowdfunding/', 'snippet': 'If you take these steps, you may have a crowd in place when equity crowdfunding gets final approval.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have taken a real interest in equity crowdfunding and its potential impact on social entrepreneurs. One reason: I would have loved to have been able to take advantage of it when I was doing my initial financing of TerraCycle.\xa0 Had crowdfunding existed then, I would have been able to raise money faster, on better terms, and from a wider range of investors — all good things when it comes to financing a small business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Not Too Soon to Think About Crowdfunding', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crowdfunding (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organi