ng students to complete part of their studies in their own country and the rest abroad, are making inroads into India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/indian-and-western-colleges-set-up-joint-study/', 'snippet': 'Twinning programs, allowing students to complete part of their studies in their own country and the rest abroad, are making inroads into India.', 'lead_paragraph': '“As colleges and universities worldwide wait for India’s lawmakers to approve a bill granting full access to the country’s vast education market,” Vir Singh wrote in The International Herald Tribune, “some institutions are reaching Indian students through twinning programs.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian and Western Colleges Set Up Joint Study Programs', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T12:16:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efd066e0-8bed-5042-a39f-a2840a75796b', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efd066e0-8bed-5042-a39f-a2840a75796b'}, {'abstract': 'The changing face of Europe’s cities has sharpened a debate over housing policies that are seen as driving growing numbers of poor and jobless to the margins.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/europes-cities-gentrification-or-ghettoization/', 'snippet': 'The changing face of Europe’s cities has sharpened a debate over housing policies that are seen as driving growing numbers of poor and jobless to the margins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The widening gap between haves and have-nots in debt-saddled Europe has sharpened a debate over whether the accelerating gentrification of its major cities is l