: {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0fc9f6b-81cb-5d31-baa0-14c6ca2c11bd', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0fc9f6b-81cb-5d31-baa0-14c6ca2c11bd'}, {'abstract': 'The new e-commerce site is turning luxury resale into easy impulse buys with the added confidence of authenticity checks.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/site-to-be-seen-hello-la-mode/', 'snippet': 'The new e-commerce site is turning luxury resale into easy impulse buys with the added confidence of authenticity checks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Start-ups, by nature, are something of a gamble. But the French entrepreneurs Eric Gagnaire, Thierry Sebba and Mathieu Bidart based their business model on eliminating one big risk. Customers of their new luxury e-commerce marketplace, Hello La Mode, won’t have to worry about clicking to buy that Chanel bag or Hermès tie because these items, and all that sell on the site, will have to pass a rigorous check for authenticity and quality by the site’s team of fashion experts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Site to Be Seen | Hello La Mode', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T15:29:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Dishman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dishman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4578a9a5-4378-503a-91bd-e1349c04884d', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4578a9a5-4378-503a-91bd-e1349c048