ticle/4bd8a54b-07b7-5459-993b-fd0efeefc3f8', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bd8a54b-07b7-5459-993b-fd0efeefc3f8'}, {'abstract': 'The chief minister of Gujarat is claiming success for a new dam in defiance of the facts, illustrating a politics based more on hype than substance.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/politics-be-dammed/', 'snippet': 'The chief minister of Gujarat is claiming success for a new dam in defiance of the facts, illustrating a politics based more on hype than substance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DELHI — Last week an unlikely new tourist destination opened in Gujarat, western India. Since Narendra Modi, the state’s chief minister, proclaimed in a blog post, “Fantastic visual treat awaits you as Narmada Dam overflows!” nearly 150,000 people have gathered to watch the accumulated water flow over the partially completed Sardar Sarovar Dam on the Narmada River.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Politics Be Dammed', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Irrigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Levees and Dams', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gandhi, Rajiv', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Bank', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gujarat State (India)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T16:08:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hartosh Singh Bal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hartosh', 'middlename': 'Singh', 'lastname': 'Bal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a1fb9ca-3c9e-5864-b46a-ad55cc9fed13', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a1fb9ca-3c9e-5864-b46a-ad55cc9fed13'}, {'abstract': 'Some new whiskey distillers are speeding up whiskey aging to get bottles on the shelves faster with techniques that still make the whiskey interesting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/dining/whiskey-start-ups-are-rolling-out-a-smaller-barrel-sooner.html', 'snippet': 'Some new whiskey distillers are speeding up whiskey aging to get bottles on the shelves faster with techniques that still make the whiskey interesting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE indispensable ingredient in great whiskey is time: years of aging and mellowing in casks. But in the world of craft whiskey, a growing number of distillers are unwilling to wait that long.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/dining/22AGED1_SPAN/22AGED1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/22/dining/22AGED1_SPAN/22AGED1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/dining/22AGED1_SPAN/22AGED1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/dining/22AGED1_SPAN/22AGED1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'sup