ival Adds ‘Paperboy’ to Schedule', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York Film Festival Adds ‘The Paperboy’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Film Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kidman, Nicole', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pena, Richard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Film Society of Lincoln Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T16:22:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99a6b4d9-7f15-5466-9694-92b9e6fa2f45', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99a6b4d9-7f15-5466-9694-92b9e6fa2f45'}, {'abstract': 'Giving up possible savings in exchange for less clutter.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/my-coffee-my-clutter/', 'snippet': 'Giving up possible savings in exchange for less clutter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Richards’ recent column on throwing away unnecessary stuff got me thinking of what items I could get rid of to declutter my house. I got an easy answer while searching through a kitchen drawer for some dog biscuits — and finding instead a bag overflowing with empty Starbucks coffee sacks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Coffee, My Clutter', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dunkin Donuts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starbucks Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T16:23:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d840b49-d1d1-5b41-abdb-b688ef059a61', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d840b49-d1d1-5b41-abdb-b688ef059a61'}, {'abstract': 'Hot dogs, bowls of buttered pasta and other child-friendly foods can wreak havoc on parents’ health. How do you accommodate their tastes without compromising your diet?', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/how-has-your-childs-diet-changed-your-own/', 'snippet': 'Hot dogs, bowls of buttered pasta and other child-friendly foods can wreak havoc on parents’ health. How do you accommodate their tastes without compromising your diet?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Matt Richtel writes this week about how fatherhood has led to his dietary woes. He gathers tips from bloggers and nutrition experts about the best ways to keep healthy while making meals that include the occasional hot dog or bowl of buttered pasta — foods that are not cholesterol-friendly, but are beloved by children. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Has Your Child’s Diet Changed Your Own?', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T16:24:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ef8e7c9-193f-5305-8373-cf5209f6af1a', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ef8e7c9-193f-5305-8373-cf5209f6af1a'}, {'abstract': 'An Indiana man uses Lincoln’s 1862 call for Army volunteer as a chance for redemption.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/andy-milices-second-chance/', 'snippet': 'An Indiana man uses Lincoln’s 1862 call for Army volunteer as a chance for redemption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By the summer of 1862, the Union Army was wearing thin, worn down by death, disease and the need to occupy extensive tracts of rebel territory. To make things worse, the Army’s one-year enlistments were about to expire, sending thousands of men home. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Andy Milice’s Second Chance', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T16:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc104212-4ac6-525f-a6dd-5fa0f5d9e0a8', 'word_count': 1288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc104212-4ac6-525f-a6dd-5fa0f5d9e0a8'}, {'abstract': 'Stencil art — one of the oldest art forms — seems a perfect fit for the military, a subculture focused on uniformity and limits.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/stenciled-relief-for-forward-operating-base-monotony/', 'snippet': 'Stencil art — one of the oldest art forms — seems a perfect fit for the military, a subculture focused on uniformity and limits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While cruising a main drag in southern Afghanistan one night in late May, I spied a silhouetted Eazy-E eyeballing me from one of the Jersey barriers lining the sidewalk. I tried not to stare at his ball cap, shades, and twin-crossed pistols. About 20 feet later, there he was peering from another wall, and again 20 feet after that. He was everywhere. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stenciled Relief for Forward Operating Base Monotony', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graffiti', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banksy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kandahar (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T16:35:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brandon Lingle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brandon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lingle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/977ce1b4-cd89-5266-88fd-d5f985218dd5', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/977ce1b4-cd89-5266-88fd-d5f985218dd5'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican platform committee approved language on Tuesday calling for a constitutional amendment outlawing abortion with no explicit exceptions for cases of rape or incest.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/g-o-p-approves-strict-anti-abortion-language-in-party-platform/', 'snippet': 'The Republican platform committee approved language on Tuesday calling for a constitutional amendment outlawing abortion with no explicit exceptions for cases of rape or incest.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:35 p.m. | Updated Even as the Republican establishment continued to call for Representative Todd Akin of Missouri to drop out of his Senate race because of his comments on rape and abortion, Republicans approved platform language on Tuesday calling for a constitutional amendment outlawing abortion with no explicit exceptions for cases of rape or incest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Approves Strict Anti-abortion Language in Party Platform', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T16:36:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab0348cd-2fa5-5bb0-adf7-c61c2f72cf05', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab0348cd-2fa5-5bb0-adf7-c61c2f72cf05'}, {'abstract': 'Federal securities regulators say they have handed out the first reward under a new whistle-blower program, paying nearly $50,000 to an unnamed person who helped the agency shut down an investment fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/s-e-c-pays-out-first-whistle-blower-reward/', 'snippet': 'Federal securities regulators say they have handed out the first reward under a new whistle-blower program, paying nearly $50,000 to an unnamed person who helped the agency shut down an investment fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal securities regulators said on Tuesday that they had handed out the first reward under a new whistle-blower program, paying nearly $50,000 to a person who helped the agency shut down an investment fraud. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Pays Out First Whistle-Blower Reward', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whistle-Blowers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T16:38:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da5cb4dc-30d3-5924-acf8-f3365cbc8c29', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da5cb4dc-30d3-5924-acf8-f3365cbc8c29'}, {'abstract': 'Through a smoke cloud caused by faulty pyrotechnics, a 1928 Mercedes-Benz emerged at Pebble Beach with the award for Best of Show.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/wheelies-the-smoke-on-the-water-edition/', 'snippet': 'Through a smoke cloud caused by faulty pyrotechnics, a 1928 Mercedes-Benz emerged at Pebble Beach with the award for Best of Show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which we bring you motoring news from around the Web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheelies: The Smoke on the Water Edition', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Pebble Beach Concours D'Elegance (Car Show)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bentley Motors Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Peugeot SA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pebble Beach (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T16:49:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a263af13-6324-5ca3-b34d-3e97e0e04e22', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a263af13-6324-5ca3-b34d-3e97e0e04e22'}, {'abstract': 'President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad said Iran needed new weapons and navigation systems in order to defend itself against foreign threats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/world/middleeast/iran-unveils-more-defense-projects.html', 'snippet': 'President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad said Iran needed new weapons and navigation systems in order to defend itself against foreign threats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Iran’s president unveiled an upgraded short-range missile and several new defense projects on Tuesday, saying the Islamic Republic needed new weapons and navigation systems in order to defend itself against foreign threats.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Unveils More Defense Projects', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran: Upgraded Missile Introduced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AHMADINEJAD, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T16:51:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2246bf91-e041-57b5-9c87-ab412610c3c1', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2246bf91-e041-57b5-9c87-ab412610c3c1'}, {'abstract': 'One of Mr. Leno’s jokes: “As you may have heard, our parent company has downsized ‘The Tonight Show.’ And we’ve consistently been No. 1 in the ratings. And if you know anything about our network, that kind of thing is frowned upon.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/jay-leno-snipes-at-comcast-over-tonight-show-cutbacks/', 'snippet': 'One of Mr. Leno’s jokes: “As you may have heard, our parent company has downsized ‘The Tonight Show.’ And we’ve consistently been No. 1 in the ratings. And if you know anything about our network, that kind of thing is frowned upon.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday, the NBC network, part of Comcast, imposed budget cuts at “The Tonight Show,” which included layoffs of between 20 and 25 staff members. The host, Jay Leno, took a pay cut, according to a person with direct knowledge of the cuts, in order to limit the number of layoffs. On Monday, Mr. Leno joined the long line of late-night hosts who use the monologue to take aim at the boss: “As you may have heard, our parent company has downsized ‘The Tonight Show.’ And we’ve consistently been No. 1 in the ratings. And if you know anything about our network, that kind of thing is frowned upon.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jay Leno Snipes at Comcast Over ‘Tonight Show’ Cutbacks', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T16:56:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f04433d6-913f-5095-97ec-6b4d207673f9', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f04433d6-913f-5095-97ec-6b4d207673f9'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Todd Akin said definitively Tuesday that he would not step aside. After his comments on rape, fellow Republicans, including Mitt Romney, asked him to drop out of the Missouri Senate race.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/us/politics/ignoring-calls-to-quit-akin-appeals-to-voters-in-ad.html', 'snippet': 'Representative Todd Akin said definitively Tuesday that he would not step aside. After his comments on rape, fellow Republicans, including Mitt Romney, asked him to drop out of the Missouri Senate race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Representative Todd Akin on Tuesday ignored a deadline to abandon Missouri’s Senate race and vowed to remain the Republican nominee in defiance of his party’s leaders, including the presidential standard-bearer, Mitt Romney.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cre