anizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T16:57:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c8f4694-4d77-56c3-8c89-cd1a54c1ee1d', 'word_count': 1300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c8f4694-4d77-56c3-8c89-cd1a54c1ee1d'}, {'abstract': 'The announcement on Tuesday that Mr. Kimmel’s show will move up a half-hour sets up a direct competition with Jay Leno and David Letterman.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/jimmy-kimmel-to-move-to-1130-in-january-abc-announces/', 'snippet': 'The announcement on Tuesday that Mr. Kimmel’s show will move up a half-hour sets up a direct competition with Jay Leno and David Letterman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2002, ABC pulled out every stop to lure David Letterman away from CBS, offering him the time period occupied by its news program “Nightline.” The network failed, and soon after inserted a new late-night host, Jimmy Kimmel, in the hour after “Nightline.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ABC Sees a Contender in Jimmy Kimmel', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ABC Sees A Contender In Kimmel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fallon, Jimmy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kimmel, Jimmy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leno, Jay', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Letterman, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sweeney, Anne', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T17:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d5ff99d-29bd-5ab0-aee6-bb4381bd730f', 'word_count': 964, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d5ff99d-29bd-5ab0-aee6-bb4381bd730f'}, {'abstract': 'Fixing the confidence gap does not require a wholesale restructuring of the regulatory system, argue the authors. Instead, they say, what is needed is new thinking, a commitment to ethics education and clarification of the laws already on the books.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/restoring-trust-in-the-futures-market/', 'snippet': 'Fixing the confidence gap does not require a wholesale restructuring of the regulatory system, argue the authors. Instead, they say, what is needed is new thinking, a commitment to ethics education and clarification of the laws already on the book...', 'lead_paragraph': 'James E. Oliff is a member of the board of FFastFill and of the CME Group, where he previously served as vice chairman. Neal L. Wolkoff was formerly the chairman and chief executive of the American Stock Exchange, chief operating officer of the New York Mercantile Exchange and chief executive of ELX Futures.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Restoring Trust in the Futures Market', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Futures and Options Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CME Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MF Global', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T17:06:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By James E. Oliff and Neal L. Wolkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Oliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Neal', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wolkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0114ecc8-95e5-5113-8361-1cf395cc2422', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0114ecc8-95e5-5113-8361-1cf395cc2422'}, {'abstract': 'A draft of the platform circulating this week calls for constitutional bans on abortion and same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/the-g-o-p-platform/', 'snippet': 'A draft of the platform circulating this week calls for constitutional bans on abortion and same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every four years the two parties draft new platforms ahead of their presidential nominating conventions. These don’t necessarily indicate immediate legislative priorities, but they do indicate general direction. Since the 1980s, the Republican platform has been a test of how far the mainstream of the party is willing to move toward the right-wing fringe. Judging from the draft circulating this week, the answer is, pretty much all the way over.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'ma