has taken center stage and remains up for grabs.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/in-missouris-move-to-the-right-a-question-of-how-far/', 'snippet': 'While Missouri, with 10 electoral votes, appears likely to wind up in the Mitt Romney column in November, the Senate race has taken center stage and remains up for grabs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We continue our Presidential Geography series, a one-by-one examination of the peculiarities that drive the politics in all 50 states and the District of Columbia. Here, a look at Missouri, the Show Me State. FiveThirtyEight spoke with David Robertson, a professor in the political science department at the University of Missouri-St.\xa0Louis, and Brian R. Calfano, an associate professor of political science at Missouri State University.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Missouri’s Move to the Right, a Question of How Far', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T17:28:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micah Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c78864e3-3262-5ef0-a5e4-78b883f3ab68', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c78864e3-3262-5ef0-a5e4-78b883f3ab68'}, {'abstract': 'The line, which is staying away from gendered pale blues and pinks, is all about fun hues and textured fabrics.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/knocking-kids-socks-off-hansel-from-basel/', 'snippet': 'The line, which is staying away from gendered pale blues and pinks, is all about fun hues and textured fabrics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best thing about making accessories for children: “Not worrying about how the customer will integrate the pieces into her wardrobe,” says Hannah Byun, the Los Angeles-based designer of the stockings and sock line Hansel From Basel. “There’s nothing holding you back. It’s a free-for-all.” It’s true. A little girl could get away with mixing Byun’s mustache-print tights, or socks that resemble strawberries with leaves around the ankles — styles from her first collection for children, available this fall — with anything she owns and look cute, not cuckoo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knocking Kids’ Socks Off | Hansel From Basel', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T17:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Kane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9eb0525-415b-5bf2-8400-42a1d3c6703d', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9eb0525-415b-5bf2-8400-42a1d3c6703d'}, {'abstract': 'The story of an American’s dream to build a luxury Himalayan ski resort shows the particular difficulties faced by foreign companies who want to do business in India.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/08/21/business/global/ski-ss.html', 'snippet': 'The story of an American’s dream to build a luxury Himalayan ski resort shows the particular difficulties faced by foreign companies who want to do business in India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The story of an American’s dream to build a luxury Himalayan ski resort shows the particular difficulties faced by foreign companies who want to do business in India.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia