468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c613a79-e4a7-5eee-8b00-224f72db49ab'}, {'abstract': 'Exposure to antibiotics before 6 months correlates with a later weight gain in childhood — another argument against their indiscriminate use.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/early-antibiotic-use-linked-to-childhood-obesity/', 'snippet': 'Exposure to antibiotics before 6 months correlates with a later weight gain in childhood — another argument against their indiscriminate use.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before you accept antibiotics for your infant, you may want to consider the results of a study published in the International Journal of Obesity showing a correlation between antibiotic exposure before 6 months and an increased body mass later in childhood, between 10 months and 3 years of age.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Early Antibiotic Use Linked to Childhood Obesity', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T18:24:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5bc4ced-041e-5f92-a01a-ee9cfbc855e8', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5bc4ced-041e-5f92-a01a-ee9cfbc855e8'}, {'abstract': 'A simple step with butter makes the summer pie a less tedious experience for the baker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/dining/summer-fruit-pies-with-a-simple-twist.html', 'snippet': 'A simple step with butter makes the summer pie a less tedious experience for the baker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOST summer stone fruit — peaches, plums, nectarines, apricots — are candidates for a pretty tart. Fresh figs qualify, too. I cut the fruit into quarters or eighths, depending on their size, then crowd the wedges so that they stand at attention in tight concentric circles on a pastry shell. I dust the fruit with sugar and, as a typical recipe demands, I would dot the top with butter.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/dining/22PIE/22PIE-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/22/dining/22PIE/22PIE-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/dining/22PIE/22PIE-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/dining/22PIE/22PIE-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1315, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/dining/22PIE/22PIE-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/22/dining/22PIE/22PIE-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/dining/22PIE/22PIE-t