 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/winding-down-the-elephant-season/', 'snippet': 'A researcher reflects on her 20th season studying elephants in Namibia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Caitlin O’Connell-Rodwell, who teaches at the Stanford University School of Medicine, writes from Etosha National Park in Namibia, where she is studying elephant societies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winding Down the Elephant Season', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elephants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Testosterone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Namibia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T19:09:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': "By Caitlin O'Connell-Rodwell", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connell-Rodwell", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/030f4a2b-16e8-51b1-a22d-46179ef485e9', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/030f4a2b-16e8-51b1-a22d-46179ef485e9'}, {'abstract': 'Yael Farber’s adaptation of the Strindberg play sets the story in post-apartheid South Africa.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/a-south-african-miss-julie-captivates-edinburgh-festival/', 'snippet': 'Yael Farber’s adaptation of the Strindberg play sets the story in post-apartheid South Africa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EDINBURGH\xa0 — With 2,695 events in 279 locations to choose from, the process of deciding what to see here at the Edinburgh Festival Fringe can be a logistical nightmare. “I don’t want to miss anything really fantastic,” you think. Then:\xa0 “Can I possibly make it from Assembly on the Mount to Underbelly in Bristo Square in 15 minutes?” (Doubtful.) Planning anxiety kicks in.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A South African ‘Miss Julie’ Captivates Edinburgh Festival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Edinburgh Festival Fringe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farber, Yael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mda, Zakes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Edinburgh (Scotland)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T19:25:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41643516-3452-57e7-875f-b6040529f1e4', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41643516-3452-57e7-875f-b6040529f1e4'}, {'abstract': 'Next week, Arctic sea ice may melt to its smallest size since data collection began in 1979, according to the lead scientist at the National Snow and Ice Data Center.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/on-the-radar-arctic-sea-ice-melt/', 'snippet': 'Next week, Arctic sea ice may melt to its smallest size since data collection began in 1979, according to the lead scientist at the National Snow and Ice Data Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Next week, Arctic sea ice may melt to its smallest size since data collection began in 1979, according to the lead scientist at the National Snow and Ice Data Center. The summer of 2007 holds the record for sea ice melt, when the minimum area of the Arctic sea ice recorded was 39 percent smaller than the average minimum from 1979 to 2000. [Reuters]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Radar: Arctic Sea Ice Melt', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T19:28:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52a43e08-b2c6-5503-84d3-0baa51a5ad5f', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52a43e08-b2c6-5503-84d3-0baa51a5ad5f'}, {'abstract': 'The British supercar producer usurped the role of automotive consultancies like Pininfarina and Bertone, showing a one-off vehicle designed in house for a client.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/with-x-1-mclaren-plays-custom-coachbuilder/', 'snippet': 'The British supercar producer usurped the role of automotive consultancies like Pininfarina and Bertone, showing a one-off vehicle designed in house for a client.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The term “special operations” conjures images of furtive, masked figures in black, emerging like ninjas from stealthy vehicles to infiltrate a target. Those evocations are amply reflected by a one-of-a-kind supercar, the McLaren X-1, the first full product from the British marque’s Special Operations program.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With X-1, McLaren Plays Custom Coachbuilder', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 's