ract': 'Almost all substantial new sources of electricity in the United States in recent years have been powered by natural gas or wind.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/a-valuable-view-of-trends-in-new-u-s-electric-power-sources/', 'snippet': 'Almost all substantial new sources of electricity in the United States in recent years have been powered by natural gas or wind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is a valuable long-view chart from the Energy Information Administration showing how natural gas plants and wind turbines have been the dominant sources of new electricity generation capacity in the United States in recent years. Click here for more background from the Energy Department. There’s plenty of additional discussion of “the gas age” on Dot Earth. I found this via a Climate Progress post focused on new capacity built in the first half of this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Valuable View of Trends in New U.S. Electric Power Sources', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T19:57:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94f3db58-20c2-54be-a6b2-6fe367c11490', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94f3db58-20c2-54be-a6b2-6fe367c11490'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney is once again being forced to carefully navigate between the uncompromising antiabortion positions of his party’s base and the more moderate politics of the swing voters he needs to win over.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/with-abortion-in-the-spotlight-a-challenge-for-romney/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney is once again being forced to carefully navigate between the uncompromising antiabortion positions of his party’s base and the more moderate politics of the swing voters he needs to win over.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:07 p.m. | Updated HOUSTON — The decision by Republican convention delegates to oppose abortion without explicit exceptions for rape and incest poses a tricky political challenge for Mitt Romney as he prepares to accept the presidential nomination in Tampa, Fla., next week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Abortion in the Spotlight, a Challenge for Romney', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akin, Todd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Priebus, Reince R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T20:03:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0c49831-b7de-5818-a961-7cdb7e23d72f', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0c49831-b7de-5818-a961-7cdb7e23d72f'}, {'abstract': 'The lawsuit, brought by the union representing corrections officers, contends Delaney Hall lacks authority under state law to house inmates awaiting trial.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/nyregion/suit-says-newark-halfway-houses-operation-is-illegal.html', 'snippet': 'The lawsuit, brought by the union representing corrections officers, contends Delaney Hall lacks authority under state law to house inmates awaiting trial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Jersey’s largest private halfway house has operated for over a decade without legal authority and should be shut down, a union representing corrections officers claims in a lawsuit. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1,200-Bed Halfway House in Newark Is Operating Illegally, Suit Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '1,200-Bed Halfway House in Newark Is Operating Illegally, Suit Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Delaney Hall (Newark, NJ)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Community Education Centers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Essex County (NJ)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Guards', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T20:06:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dolnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dolnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34653edd-b4af-5fe0-945f-ed6e7e2786aa', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34653edd-b4af-5fe0-945f-ed6e7e2786aa'}, {'abstract': 'In more than six years of spying on Muslims, the N.Y.P.D.’s secret surveillance program never generated a lead.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/surveillance-civil-liberties-and-inefficiency/', 'snippet': 'In more than six years of spying on Muslims, the N.Y.P.D.’s secret surveillance program never generated a lead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the Associated Press disclosed the N.Y.P.D.’s Muslim surveillance program, the Times board editorialized against it from a civil liberties perspective. It seemed the police were spying on Muslims—sending plainclothes officers to monitor Muslims at mosques, on college campuses, taking photographs of Muslim-owned businesses, listening to conversations—with no “reason to think anything wrong was going on.” The board acknowledged that “under a federal court decree, it is permissible to collect information from public sources” but argued that “going to public places apparently selected on the basis of religion” was “another matter.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Surveillance, Civil Liberties and Inefficiency', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Raymond W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T20:08:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 