f2a8040bde4'}, {'abstract': 'Years after wondering, “Can sick people be funny?,” Michael J. Fox is returning to series television.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/arts/television/michael-j-fox-returning-to-nbc-with-sitcom-in-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Years after wondering, “Can sick people be funny?,” Michael J. Fox is returning to series television.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Michael J. Fox learned he had Parkinson’s disease, but before he publicly disclosed his diagnosis in 1998, he worried that his career as a comedic actor would be ruined if viewers knew that he was, as he put it in his memoir, “battling an incurable neurological disease.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/arts/FOX/FOX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/arts/FOX/FOX-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1428, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/arts/FOX/FOX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/22/arts/FOX/FOX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/arts/FOX/FOX-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Parkinson’s in Check, Fox to Star in Sitcom', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Parkinson’s In Check, Fox to Star In Sitcom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Parkinson's Disease", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fox, Michael J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T21:54:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1b448c8-5499-5134-b542-6ce423b2fe09', 'word_count': 916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1b448c8-5499-5134-b542-6ce423b2fe09'}, {'abstract': 'Chuck Thompson’s new book is a tour of the Confederate States of America, the country he says should be created by the South’s secession from the North.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/books/better-off-without-em-by-chuck-thompson.html', 'snippet': 'Chuck Thompson’s new book is a tour of the Confederate States of America, the country he says should be created by the South’s secession from the North.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chuck Thompson is a travel writer who has worked on assignment in more than 50 countries. Real countries. The kinds that have recognizable borders and appear on maps. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/arts/book/book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1849, 'width': 1664, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/22/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/arts/book/book-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Northern (or Maybe Bronx?) Cheer for the South’s Independence', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Northern (or Maybe Bronx?) Cheer for the South’s Independence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Chuck', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T22:05:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfe345fa-28f7-5c7e-97ff-2b524aea4444', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfe345fa-28f7-5c7e-97ff-2b524aea4444'}, {'abstract': 'The mean-spirited platform circulating ahead of the convention shows that Republican politics has moved so far to the right that the extreme is now the mainstream.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/opinion/what-the-gop-platform-represents.html', 'snippet': 'The mean-spirited platform circulating ahead of the convention shows that Republican politics has moved so far to the right that the extreme is now the mainstream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the years, the major parties’ election-year platforms have been regarded as Kabuki theater scripts for convention week. The presidential candidates blithely ignored them or openly dismissed the most extreme planks with a knowing wink as merely a gesture to pacify the noisiest activists in the party.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What the G.O.P. Platform Represents', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What the G.O.P. Platform Represents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T22:08:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7705c36e-1e5d-5571-98cc-04e7a8de94de', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7705c36e-1e5d-5571-98cc-04e7a8de94de'}, {'abstract': 'A whole class of restaurants encourages groups to share dishes. But very few small plates actually lend themselves to sharing.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/the-big-problem-with-small-plates/', 'snippet': 'A whole class of restaurants encourages groups to share dishes. But very few small plates actually lend themselves to sharing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week I review La Vara, a new restaurant in Brooklyn with a menu that explores the contribution that Jews and Muslims made to Spain’s cuisine. Have you been? If you have, I’d love to know what you thought. I admired a great deal of the dishes that the owners and co-chefs, Alex Raij and Eder Montero, have put on their menu (those artichokes! That tuna salad! Those red shrimp, served with their heads!). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Big Problem With Small Plates', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T22:12:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fccf0b7-cecd-50c4-966d-056820be3306', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fccf0b7-cecd-50c4-966d-056820be3306'}, {'abstract': 'At 90 minutes, “Fantasy Artists” is rather good. But you can’t help thinking that at 75 minutes it would be even better.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/new-york-fringe-festival-report-fantasy-artists/', 'snippet': 'At 90 minutes, “Fantasy Artists” is rather good. But you can’t help thinking that at 75 minutes it would be even better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reviews of shows from the New York International Fringe Festival will appear on ArtsBeat through the festival’s close on Aug. 26. For more information, go to fringenyc.org.James Ryan Caldwell knows how to write. All he needs now is to learn when to quit. At 90 minutes, his expertly acted comedy-drama “Fantasy Artists” is rather good. But you can’t help thinking that at 75 minutes it would be even better.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Fringe Festival Report: ‘Fantasy Artists’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fantasy Artists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York International Fringe Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caldwell, James Ryan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T22:25:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Jaworowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jaworowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/143fdd02-eb14-5e18-b35f-be0eb3e42462', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/143fdd02-eb14-5e18-b35f-be0eb3e42462'}, {'abstract': 'Carl C. Icahn, who owns 82 percent of CVR Energy, said on Tuesday that he was dropping an offer to take the Texas refiner private, citing changing market conditions.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/icahn-withdraws-offer-to-take-refining-company-private/', 'snippet': 'Carl C. Icahn, who owns 82 percent of CVR Energy, said on Tuesday that he was dropping an offer to take the Texas refiner private, citing changing market conditions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl C. Icahn, who owns 82 percent of CVR Energy, said on Tuesday that he was dropping an offer to take the Texas refiner private, citing changing market conditions. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Icahn Withdraws Offer to Take Refining Company Private', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizati