ion permits American charities to transfer up to $300,000 each to relief and rebuilding efforts, bypassing restrictions on financial transactions that are enforced under the sanctions imposed on Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States cleared the way on Tuesday for American charities to expedite relief to the victims of the double earthquake that struck Iran more than two weeks ago, issuing the charities a temporary but broad exemption to the regimen of economic sanctions imposed on that country over its disputed nuclear energy program.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'United States Grants Broad Sanctions Exemption for Iran Quake Aid', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iranian-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonough, Denis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of Foreign Assets Control (United States Treasury)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-21T23:35:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad3cf459-c115-516a-bee6-8424fabb7b20', 'word_count': 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad3cf459-c115-516a-bee6-8424fabb7b20'}, {'abstract': 'An anti-Islam blogger’s ads in support of Israel have been reworked by critics in San Francisco and New York.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/anti-islam-ads-remixed-in-san-francisco-and-new-york/', 'snippet': 'An anti-Islam blogger’s ads in support of Israel have been reworked by critics in San Francisco and New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Benjamin Weiser reported last month, a federal judge in Manhattan ruled that the Metropolitan Transportation Authority had violated the First Amendment rights of a pro-Israel group by refusing to run an ad that refers to Arabs as “savage” on 318 city buses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anti-Islam Ads Remixed in San Francisco and New York', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geller, Pamela', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rand, Ayn', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Freedom Defense Initiative', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metro-North Commuter Railroad', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 14