et': 'Hakeem Nicks is eager to see action in the preseason games, but the Giants would rather be cautious with their star receiver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Hakeem Nicks snared a pass in the left flat from Eli Manning during Tuesday’s practice and looked as if he wanted to simply run all day.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1948, 'width': 1403, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/GIANTS/GIANTS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Recovery for the Speedy Nicks Is Deliberately Slow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recovery for Nicks Is Deliberately Slow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicks, Hakeem', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T00:28:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Pedulla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pedulla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fecb2a7d-7512-5013-87e1-2927c254faec', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fecb2a7d-7512-5013-87e1-2927c254faec'}, {'abstract': 'To give more people access to our bounty of fresh food, we need to support real farmers, not businessmen riding half-million-dollar combines.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/celebrate-the-farmer/', 'snippet': 'To give more people access to our bounty of fresh food, we need to support real farmers, not businessmen riding half-million-dollar combines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was at a farm dinner in Maine the other night, a long table of 60 people eating corn, chicken, salad, a spectacular herb sorbet and other goodies. When one of the hosts arose to ask someone to describe the first course on the table – huge marrow bones from the farm’s cattle– she introduced not the chef but the farmers. Similarly, at a fund-raiser on Cape Cod a week or so earlier, the talk was all about the provenance of the produce and meat rather than the cooking technique. The most popular guy was the oyster grower.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrate the Farmer!', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Local Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T00:30:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17afa178-b3b5-5807-8ddc-776ef3bbfb4d', 'word_count': 1125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17afa178-b3b5-5807-8ddc-776ef3bbfb4d'}, {'abstract': 'Withdrawal from Afghanistan threatens to enmesh the United States and NATO in a minefield of regional rivalries and domestic strongman politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/opinion/after-afghanistan-a-new-great-game.html', 'snippet': 'Withdrawal from Afghanistan threatens to enmesh the United States and NATO in a minefield of regional rivalries and domestic strongman politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SINCE 9/11, America’s priority in Central Asia has been to defeat the Taliban in Afghanistan. But as the United States and NATO pull out, there is a new danger: that the West could become entangled in regional rivalries, local strongman politics and competition with Russia and China.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Afghanistan, a New Great Game', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Afghanistan, a New Great Game', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Bases and Installations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Asia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T00:42:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Cooley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/41f95005-ceda-5337-8c4e-03d3d7cda3f0', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41f95005-ceda-5337-8c4e-03d3d7cda3f0'}, {'abstract': 'How the provisions in the president’s health care law differ from the plans of Mitt Romney and Paul Ryan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/08/21/us/politics/Comparing-the-Candidates-on-Medicare.html', 'snippet': 'How the provisions in the president’s health care law differ from the plans of Mitt Romney and Paul Ryan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How the provisions in the president’s health care law differ from the plans of Mitt Romney and Paul Ryan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comparing the Candidates on Medicare', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T00:44:20+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/1f4ca4d5-8c9a-57b4-8ca8-e8dca6c4f561', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/1f4ca4d5-8c9a-57b4-8ca8-e8dca6c4f561'}, {'abstract': 'More rulings make it clear that states cannot bypass federal authority and create their own schemes to harass and expel illegal immigrants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/opinion/setback-for-rogue-immigration-laws-in-georgia-and-alabama.html', 'snippet': 'More rulings make it clear that states cannot bypass federal authority and create their own schemes to harass and expel illegal immigrants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal appeals court in Atlanta on Monday properly blocked several provisions of immigration laws in Alabama and Georgia, saying they violated constitutional rights and undermined federal law. The rulings were huge setbacks for the repellent idea that states can bypass federal authority over immigration and create their own schemes to harass and expel undocumented residents.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Setback for Rogue Immigration Laws', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Setback for Rogue Immigration Laws', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal-State Relations (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T00:45:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8406812f-0eb3-5c70-87fa-d06afa16c4d3', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8406812f-0eb3-5c70-87fa-d06afa16c4d3'}, {'abstract': 'A Wi-Fi-like technology to warn drivers of hazards is being tested in a yearlong program in Michigan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/201