orted', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eed4e750-f49e-5ebe-9f0d-632fd1c3f1f4', 'word_count': 1232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eed4e750-f49e-5ebe-9f0d-632fd1c3f1f4'}, {'abstract': 'Armed with a scholar’s knowledge, Mr. Lindenbaum helped his clients bend the city’s zoning rules without breaking them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/nyregion/samuel-h-lindenbaum-lawyer-to-major-new-york-developers-dies-at-77.html', 'snippet': 'Armed with a scholar’s knowledge, Mr. Lindenbaum helped his clients bend the city’s zoning rules without breaking them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Samuel H. Lindenbaum, who was widely considered New York City’s top zoning lawyer and who was credited with doing as much as any of the powerful developers among his clients to shape the modern skyline of Manhattan, died on Friday at his home in East Hampton, N.Y. He was 77. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/nyregion/LINDENBAUM-obit/LINDENBAUM-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/22/nyregion/LINDENBAUM-obit/LINDENBAUM-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/nyregion/LINDENBAUM-obit/LINDENBAUM-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/nyregion/LINDENBAUM-obit/LINDENBAUM-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1283, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/nyregion/LINDENBAUM-obit/LINDENBAUM-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/22/nyregion/LINDENBAUM-obit/LINDENBAUM-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/nyregion/LINDENBAUM-obit/LINDENBAUM-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Samuel H. Lindenbaum, ‘Dean’ of New York Zoning Lawyers, Dies at 77', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Samuel H. Lindenbaum, 77, Zoning Lawyer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zoning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lindenbaum, Samuel H', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T00:48:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/2aabb659-5710-5a75-ab50-a7d3aba20fc7', 'word_count': 967, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2aabb659-5710-5a75-ab50-a7d3aba20fc7'}, {'abstract': 'The High Line has become a tourist-clogged catwalk and a catalyst for some of the most rapid gentrification in the city’s history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/opinion/in-the-shadows-of-the-high-line.html', 'snippet': 'The High Line has become a tourist-clogged catwalk and a catalyst for some of the most rapid gentrification in the city’s history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN the first segment of the High Line, the now-famous park built atop an old elevated railway on the West Side of Manhattan, opened in 2009, I experienced a moment of excitement. I had often wondered what it would be like to climb that graffiti-marked trestle with its wild urban meadow. Of course, I’d seen the architectural renderings and knew not to expect a wilderness. Still, the idea was enticing: a public park above the hubbub, a contemplative space where nature softens the city’s abrasiveness. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/opinion/0822OPEDbenaroya/0822OPEDbenaroya-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 284, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/22/opinion/0822OPEDbenaroya/0822OPEDbenaroya-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 284}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/opinion/0822OPEDbenaroya/0822OPEDbenaroya-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 485, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/opinion/0822OPEDbenaroya/0822OPEDbenaroya-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 970, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/opinion/0822OPEDbenaroya/0822OPEDbenaroya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/22/opinion/0822OPEDbenaroya/0822OPEDbenaroya-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/opinion/0822OPEDbenaroya/0822OPEDbenaroya-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disney World on the Hudson', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Disney World on the Hudson', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gentrification', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Line (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T00:49:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremiah Moss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremiah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfc64f98-ade2-5820-9665-22501c327a7a', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfc64f98-ade2-5820-9665-22501c327a7a'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court should take a case for review to reaffirm the Hyde Amendment, a federal law that checks against gross misconduct by federal prosecutors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/opinion/prosecutorial-abuse.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court should take a case for review to reaffirm the Hyde Amendment, a federal law that checks against gross misconduct by federal prosecutors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal law allows federal courts to award attorneys’ fees and other expenses to criminal defendants who prove gross misconduct on the part of federal prosecutors. The law — a 1997 amendment sponsored by Representative Henry Hyde, a Republican — is a valuable deterrent to prosecutorial abuse, providing compensation in cases where a court finds the government’s position to be “vexatious, frivolous or in bad faith.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prosecutorial Abuse', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prosecutorial Abuse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hyde, Henry J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T00:51:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/67751f3a-fdbb-5269-88dd-da06e0a703d3', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67751f3a-fdbb-5269-88dd-da06e0a703d3'}, {'abstract': 'The federal government is about to strike a wolf management plan with Wyoming. But whether it’s enough to guarantee a sustainable population is far from clear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/opinion/uncertain-future-for-the-gray-wolf.html', 'snippet': 'The federal government is about to strike a wolf management plan with Wyoming. But whether it’s enough to guarantee a sustainable population is far from clear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The recovery of the gray wolf in the Rocky Mountain West is one of the Endangered Species Act’s great success stories. Hunted nearly to extinction, wolves were reintroduced to the region in the 1990s and have since staged a remarkable comeback, thanks to federal protections. But whether this story has a happy ending will depend on the federal government’s willingness to monitor, and revise if necessary, wolf management plans it has agreed to in Idaho and Montana and is about to strike with Wyoming. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uncertain Future for the Gray Wolf', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Uncertain Future for the Gray Wolf', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wyoming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wolves', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunting and Trapping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T01:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f0a06da-507a-5061-a7fd-70199958f554', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f0a06da-507a-5061-a7fd-70199958f554'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Pettitte, eager to get back in the Yankees rotation after a leg injury, answered questions about the news that Roger Clemens was scheduled to start for a minor league team in Texas on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/21/pettitte-talks-about-return-his-and-clemenss/', 'snippet': 'Andy Pettitte, eager to get back in the Yankees rotation after a leg injury, answered questions about the news that Roger Clemens was scheduled to start for a minor league team in Texas on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — After a light catch with C.C. Sabathia in the outfield Tuesday afternoon, Andy Pettitte returned to the clubhouse and was asked, among other things, about his old friend 