/us/appeals-court-limits-alabamas-immigration-law.html', 'snippet': 'The appeals court struck down many of the state’s measures that had gone furthest in making the everyday lives of illegal immigrants so difficult.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Alabama’s immigration law was passed in the spring of 2011, it was the boldest test yet of the doctrine of self-deportation. If the state put up legal obstacles to nearly every aspect of illegal immigrants’ lives, as a chief sponsor of the law put it at the time, it would “make their lives difficult and they will deport themselves.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Appeals Court Draws Boundaries on Alabama’s Immigration Law', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Appeals Court Draws Boundaries on Alabama’s Immigration Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T02:54:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson and Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organizatio