agraph': 'New York, a city of subcultures, has a gem on Manhattan’s West Side. Bordered by 94th and 96th Streets, between the Onassis Reservoir and the West Drive of one of the world’s most famous public spaces, sits the Central Park Tennis Center.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/CPTC1/CPTC1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/CPTC1/CPTC1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/CPTC1/CPTC1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 572, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/CPTC1/CPTC1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1145, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/CPTC1/CPTC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/CPTC1/CPTC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/CPTC1/CPTC1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Place for Passionate Tennis Players', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Place for the Passionate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Park Tennis Center', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corallo, Helene', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diarra, Yaya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T03:36:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isaac Eger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isaac', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed37f577-57b6-5c14-a2e8-6daad60f3bc7', 'word_count': 2629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed37f577-57b6-5c14-a2e8-6daad60f3bc7'}, {'abstract': 'Kevin Youkilis, who came into the game with .301 career average against the Yankees, hit a tiebreaking grand slam off Ivan Nova, who has won only one of his last eight starts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/sports/baseball/kevin-youkilis-continues-to-hurt-yankees-as-ivan-nova-keeps-struggling.html', 'snippet': 'Kevin Youkilis, who came into the game with .301 career average against the Yankees, hit a tiebreaking grand slam off Ivan Nova, who has won only one of his last eight starts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — Even as their lead in the American League East has shriveled in the last few weeks, the outward calm of the Yankees has never seemed shaken. But late Tuesday night, after another poor outing by Ivan Nova, Manager Joe Girardi acknowledged that Nova’s problems had now endured for a significant period of time. But he bristled at questions about how much longer the Yankees could stick with Nova, their struggling right-hander.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13',