Express and a Chipotle. At one end, a Perkins Family Restaurant flies a preposterously large Stars and Stripes in its front yard, as if it were a federal building or an aircraft carrier.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/magazine/26monkey1/26monkey1-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 732, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/magazine/26monkey1/26monkey1-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 732}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/magazine/26monkey1/mag-26Monkey-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 834, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/magazine/26monkey1/mag-26Monkey-t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1222, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/magazine/26monkey1/26monkey1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/magazine/26monkey1/26monkey1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/magazine/26monkey1/26monkey1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s a Monkey to Do in Tampa?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Swing State', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monkeys and Apes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Mooallem', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mooallem', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d7245e7-0cea-5250-b928-4de66d5debaf', 'word_count': 4676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d7245e7-0cea-5250-b928-4de66d5debaf'}, {'abstract': 'The Reuters staff photographer Goran Tomasevic was with the Free Syrian Army in Aleppo and elsewhere, photographing the intense street combat as government forces sought to tamp the rebellion.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/streetfighting-in-aleppo/', 'snippet': 'The Reuters staff photographer Goran Tomasevic was with the Free Syrian Army in Aleppo and elsewhere, photographing the intense street combat as government forces sought to tamp the rebellion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Goran Tomasevic, a staff photographer for Reuters, photographed the fighting in Aleppo, Syria, from Aug. 1 to 17. While he was there, his dramatic images ran on the front pages of newspapers throughout the world. Mr. Tomasevic, 43, has been covering armed conflicts since 1991. On Tuesday, James Estrin interviewed him via e-mail. The exchange has been edited.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Street Fighting in Aleppo', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T09:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e84b1350-2ee2-5fdc-b54a-802a9d08a7b9', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e84b1350-2ee2-5fdc-b54a-802a9d08a7b9'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers seek the most protection for the North Atlantic’s humpback whales at the least cost to the fishing and tourism industry.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/managing-the-ocean-for-humans-and-whales/', 'snippet': 'Researchers seek the most protection for the North Atlantic’s humpback whales at the least cost to the fishing and tourism industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I wrote this week in a story about the humpback whales that summer off New England, one of the main reasons researchers want to learn about the humpbacks is so that the whales can be better protected from human activities like fishing and boating.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Managing the Ocean for Humans and Whales', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whales and Whaling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stellwagen Bank National Marine Sanctuary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New England States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T10:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kelly Slivka', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kelly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Slivka', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role'