abstract': 'Four years later, Mike Michalowicz has decided he wants people to know his real name, so he’s trying to kill the brand he created.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/how-the-toilet-paper-entrepreneur-branded-himself-too-well/', 'snippet': 'Four years later, Mike Michalowicz has decided he wants people to know his real name, so he’s trying to kill the brand he created.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mike Michalowicz published a book in 2008, he was looking for a name that would stick. He chose: “The Toilet Paper Entrepreneur.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Toilet Paper Entrepreneur Branded Himself Too Well', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T11:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melinda F. Emerson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melinda', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Emerson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4cc2d78-08fb-54bd-a8e7-78142bcdcdb7', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4cc2d78-08fb-54bd-a8e7-78142bcdcdb7'}, {'abstract': 'The Bangladeshi government’s power grab for the world’s biggest microlender hurts millions of poor, and threatens the gains made by the women who run it.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/an-attack-on-grameen-bank-and-the-cause-of-women/', 'snippet': 'The Bangladeshi government’s power grab for the world’s biggest microlender hurts millions of poor, and threatens the gains made by the women who run it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This month, the Grameen Bank, the organization that won the Nobel Peace Prize for extending small loans to impoverished village women, has come under renewed attack from the government of Bangladesh. Last year, I reported that the government was attempting to forcibly remove the bank’s founder, Muhammad Yunus, from his position as managing director on the pretense that Yunus, then 70, was beyond the official retirement age. The government prevailed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Attack on Grameen Bank, and the Cause of Women', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microfinance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yunus, Muhammad', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grameen Bank', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T11:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afc28ea8-4c26-5f20-bb01-b745fc1de49f', 'word_count': 1471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afc28ea8-4c26-5f20-bb01-b745fc1de49f'}, {'abstract': 'What started as a lark for three pro photog