 of spinner dolphins before spotting a group of bottlenose dolphins and collecting a few genetic samples.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scott Baker, associate director of the Marine Mammal Institute at Oregon State University, writes from Samoa, where he studies the formation of local communities among dolphins and their genetic isolation from one another. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Parade of Spinning Dolphins', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dolphins and Porpoises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whales and Whaling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Samoa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T11:37:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f23c1113-ba00-57ad-85f5-65eeafa2fccd', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f23c1113-ba00-57ad-85f5-65eeafa2fccd'}, {'abstract': 'As talks resume on Greece’s financial crisis and its prime minister appeals for more time to meet bailout terms, the euro zone’s fiscal hardliners are hinting they could live with a Greek exit from the single currency.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/euro-zone-talks-revive-specter-of-greek-exit/', 'snippet': 'As talks resume on Greece’s financial crisis and its prime minister appeals for more time to meet bailout terms, the euro zone’s fiscal hardliners are hintin