ocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pussy Riot', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tolokonnikova, Nadezhda', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samutsevich, Yekaterina', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alyokhina, Maria', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T12:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/842aaf29-98e4-5dae-9760-56a509b498cf', 'word_count': 1307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/842aaf29-98e4-5dae-9760-56a509b498cf'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/morning-take-out-543/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Profits in G.M.A.C. Bailout to Benefit Financiers, Not U.S. \xa0|\xa0 Among the companies that were bailed out by the federal government during the financial crisis, perhaps the most intractable is proving to be the company formerly known as the General Motors Acceptance Corporation. It is a case study in how bailouts can linger and profits, when they do come, flow not to the government but to the Warren E. Buffetts of the world, the Deal Professor writes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T12:01:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c56518d-d7ce-5204-b404-1faa86a9f9c0', 'word_count': 2072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c56518d-d7ce-5204-b404-1faa86a9f9c0'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney has held the lead recently in quite a few swing state polls. That wasn’t the case in June or July, when Barack Obama held leads in those polls more often than Mr. Romney did.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/aug-21-romney-showing-improved-results-in-swing-state-polls/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney has held the lead recently in quite a few swing state polls. That wasn’t the case in June or July, when Barack Obama held leads in those polls more often than Mr. Romney did.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We can get pretty detail-oriented in our analysis of the polls here at FiveThirtyEight. But sometimes there is also value in applying a simpler approach.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 21: Romney Showing Improved Results in Swing State Polls', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T12:03:49+0000', 'document_type': 'a