 after the Fukushima disaster last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — For the first time since antinuclear rallies began months ago outside Prime Minister Yoshihiko Noda’s office, a dozen protesters were allowed inside on Wednesday for a half-hour meeting that the fledgling movement hailed as a victory. The meeting comes at a time of growing antinuclear sentiment in Japan, and with elections expected this year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japanese Leader Meets With Antinuclear Protesters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japanese Leader Meets With Antinuclear Protesters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Noda, Yoshihiko', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T12:24:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0013dd2b-71c3-5854-9781-e4fe62a0b3bc', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0013dd2b-71c3-5854-9781-e4fe62a0b3bc'}, {'abstract': 'On its anniversary, revisiting details of the crime, and its aftermath, that inspired the film “Dog Day Afternoon.”', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/a-botched-robbery-went-hollywood/', 'snippet': 'On its anniversary, revisiting details of the crime, and its aftermath, that inspired the film “Dog Day Afternoon.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Temperatures we