o, while the mirrors wear garlands of silk flowers, the soap bottles dispense fruit-scented hand cleanser and plastic ferns stand in the corner. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Public Bathroom, Transformed Into a Gem by the Beach', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Brighton Beach, a Public Restroom That’s Nice Enough for Company', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bathrooms and Toilets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parks and Recreation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brighton Beach (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T14:05:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Yee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d00a980-479f-5b0c-8302-8fcadd14d3f7', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d00a980-479f-5b0c-8302-8fcadd14d3f7'}, {'abstract': 'In “Every Love Story Is a Ghost Story” D. T. Max traces the career and truncated life of the novelist David Foster Wallace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/books/david-foster-wallace-biography-by-d-t-max.html', 'snippet': 'In “Every Love Story Is a Ghost Story” D. T. Max traces the career and truncated life of the novelist David Foster Wallace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Infinite Jest” David Foster Wallace  described  clinical depression as “the Great White Shark of pain,” “a level of psychic pain wholly incompatible with human life as we know it,” a “nausea of the cells and soul,” a sort of “double bind in which any/all of the alternatives we associate with human agency — sitting or standing, doing or resting, speaking or keeping silent, living or dying — are not just unpleasant but literally horrible,” a radical loneliness in which “everything is part of the problem, and there is no solution.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/books/23book/23book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 745, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/books/23book/23book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1489, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/books/23book/23book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/23/books/23book/23book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Searching Through the Ashes of an Exploded Life', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Searching Through the Ashes of an Exploded Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wallace, David Foster', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Max, D T', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T14:10:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported'