emens court proceedings put jurors to sleep, but his return to baseball — and softball — has people talking and scouts bringing their radar guns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are some sports stories you just couldn’t make up if you tried. For today’s example, Roger Clemens comes out of retirement at 50 to pitch for an independent minor league team and also take some hacks in an over-50 men’s softball league. Now, were the Atlantic League the kind of league that installs beer kegs at each base and requires someone with actual athletic talent to pitch with a small child perched on his shoulders, heads across the country might not be lolling with such fatigue. But no, the Sugar Land Skeeters (we couldn’t make that up either) are apparently enough of an actual organization to have an official team backdrop — with the team’s and its sponsor’s name, no less — for Clemens’s news conference Wednesday. Oh, and the Astros consider this serious enough to send a scout to contemplate a possible major league return.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/22leading-pic/22leading-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/22leading-pic/22leading-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1394, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/22leading-pic/22leading-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/22/sports/22leading-pic/22leading-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 