pounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bearded and blustery, with a kaffiyeh draped around his neck, Juan Manuel Sánchez Gordillo cuts a rakish profile. For the last 33 years he has been the mayor of the small Andalusian town of Marinaleda, a Communist enclave in southern Spain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Don Quixote of the Spanish Crisis', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez Gordillo, Juan Manuel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANDALUSIA (SPAIN)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cadiz (Spain)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seville (Spain)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T15:34:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Blitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbd7d553-8e29-5c16-887d-cc1a16e62f6d', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbd7d553-8e29-5c16-887d-cc1a16e62f6d'}, {'abstract': 'The Packard owner, 102, was treated to an audience with the Maharana of Udaipur and with de facto automotive royals like Edsel Ford II and Jay Leno.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/margaret-dunning-queen-for-a-weekend-at-pebble-beach/', 'snippet': 'The Packard owner, 102, was treated to an audience with the Maharana of Udaipur and with de facto automotive