', '_id': 'nyt://article/94bc0d1c-7267-57bc-aeaf-a571e6f216db', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94bc0d1c-7267-57bc-aeaf-a571e6f216db'}, {'abstract': 'Ethiopians may be mourning the death of Prime Minister Meles Zenawi, but they should worry about the legacy of his personality-centric development agenda.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/death-of-a-strongman/', 'snippet': 'Ethiopians may be mourning the death of Prime Minister Meles Zenawi, but they should worry about the legacy of his personality-centric development agenda.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI — After two months of mysterious absence, Meles Zenawi, Ethiopia’s prime minister, is finally accounted for: He’s dead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death of a Strongman', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zenawi, Meles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ethiopia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T16:20:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dayo Olopade', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dayo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olopade', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/356c3d3a-e306-5719-bd4c-ea469ef36442', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/356c3d3a-e306-5719-bd4c-ea469ef36442'}, {'abstract': 'Video: Two 4,000-pound adolescent southern white rhinos are the latest edition to the Bronx Zoo.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/the-rhinos-have-arrived/', 'snippet': 'Video: Two 4,000-pound adolescent southern white rhinos are the latest edition to the Bronx Zoo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'O.K., it’s August. But the arrival of two 4,000-pound adolescent southern white rhinos — brothers, no less — at the Bronx Zoo would be news any day. The surprisingly nimble-footed pair (see video above or here) were a gift from The Wilds, a conservation park in Cumberland, Ohio, where they were born three and a half years ago. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rhinos Have Arrived', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rhinoceroses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronx Zoo Wildlife Conservation Park', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T16:23:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b34f137-c00f-53df-8106-9a9aaf3c6241', 'word_count': 60, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b34f137-c00f-53df-8106-9a9aaf3c6241'}, {'abstract': 'An assessment of Ms. Diller’s comedy technique and career through the years. She died on Monday at 95.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/phyllis-diller-and-her-comic-craft/', 'snippet': 'An assessment of Ms. Diller’s comedy technique and career through the years. She died on Monday at 95.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early in her career Phyllis Diller, who died on Monday at 95, made fun of her legs and her figure. Later she took aim at her wrinkles and plastic surgery. “I’ve had so many things done to my body,” she began a joke, “that when I die, God won’t know me.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Phyllis Diller and Her Comic Craft', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Phyllis Diller and Her Comic Craft', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diller, Phyllis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T16:23:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6aa9dacb-1a93-5fbf-a9af-f46eee48da03', 'word_count': 980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6aa9dacb-1a93-5fbf-a9af-f46eee48da03'}, {'abstract': 'What, exactly, do Republicans find offensive about Todd Akin’s comments?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/ask-your-local-g-o-p-candidate-about-legitimate-rape/', 'snippet': 'What, exactly, do Republicans find offensive about Todd Akin’s comments?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A reporter for the Pittsburgh TV station KDKA asked Paul Ryan the other day what he thought of Rep. Todd Akin’s pronouncement that victims of “legitimate rape” can magically “shut down” pregnancy and so do not need the right to an abortion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ask Your Local G.O.P. Candidate About ‘Legitimate’ Rape', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akin, Todd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cornyn, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T16:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'r