ter/', 'snippet': 'A Twitter conversation with Pete Wells and others about the problems of sharing a meal made up of small plates meant for sharing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pete Wells’s blog post about the problems of sharing a meal made up of small plates sparked an exchange on Twitter with the writers Michele Humes and Francis Lam, the chef David Chang, the Bloomberg restaurant critic Ryan Sutton and others. about Chinese cuisine and American habits, the distinction between a family-style meal and the current small plates rage, and the advantage in serving small plates for the restaurant. Here are excerpts from the conversation. To be sure we see your tweet on the subject, cc @nytdining. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talk of Small Plates on Twitter', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T16:44:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/701b6cb0-9fe8-5c30-8624-c3f5f38ee292', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/701b6cb0-9fe8-5c30-8624-c3f5f38ee292'}, {'abstract': 'Jake Gyllenhaal’s new movie, in which he plays a cop in South Los Angeles, has a private screening and celebrity-filled party in East Hampton.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/fashion/end-of-watch-gets-an-east-hampton-screening.html', 'snippet': 'Jake Gyllenhaal’s new movie, in which he plays a cop in South Los Angeles, has a private screening and celebrity-filled party in East Hampton.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the new movie “End of Watch,” Jake Gyllenhaal plays a cop in South Central Los Angeles, working the neighborhood patrol and battling some seriously scary thugs from a Mexican drug cartel. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 's