erican oil and mining companies to disclose taxes and other fees they pay to foreign governments. The disclosures are aimed at curbing corruption, which is common in some major oil-producing nations. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/business/SEC/SEC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/business/SEC/SEC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Oil and Mining Companies Must Disclose Payments to Foreign Governments', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Oil and Mining Companies Must Disclose Payments to Foreign Governments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Metals and Minerals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflict Minerals and Resources', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T16:53:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb96d22a-c56f-566b-b0e3-cfc33b06c8aa', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb96d22a-c56f-566b-b0e3-cfc33b06c8aa'}, {'abstract': 'With estimates of the death toll varying, Kenyans were shocked by ethnic clashes in a coastal area that left around 50 people dead, mostly women and children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/world/africa/dozens-dead-in-kenya-clashes.html', 'snippet': 'With estimates of the death toll varying, Kenyans were shocked by ethnic clashes in a coastal area that left around 50 people dead, mostly women and children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — As many as 52 people, most of them women and children, were killed Wednesday in a coastal area of Kenya in attacks involving two rival communities, officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kenya Clashes Leave Dozens Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kenya Clashes Leave Dozens Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T16:53:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reuben Kyama', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reuben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kyama', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb071c09-5c8e-516a-a1a6-9beb29a48ec4', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb071c09-5c8e-516a-a1a6-9beb29a48ec4'}, {'abstract': 'A federal court clears denial of state money to Planned Parenthood-affiliated clinics in Texas despised by the Republican Party and Gov. Rick Perry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/opinion/in-texas-dont-even-mention-abortion.html', 'snippet': 'A federal court clears denial of state money to Planned Parenthood-affiliated clinics in Texas despised by the Republican Party and Gov. Rick Perry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republican-controlled State Legislature in Texas and Gov. Rick Perry are perfectly willing to endanger the general health and welfare of low-income women to further their agenda of eroding abortion rights. And, now, a federal appeals court has given them a green light to do that, at least temporarily.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Texas, Don’t Even Mention Abortion', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Texas, Don’t Even Mention Abortion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yeakel, Lee', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T16:53:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ad4eb9b-fd37-532a-95ec-93d1a4d13c24', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ad4eb9b-fd37-532a-95ec-93d1a4d13c24'}, {'abstract': 'The book, written under a pseudonym by a member of the Navy SEALs, will be published on Sept. 11 and offer a “blow-by-blow narrative” of the raid that ended in the death of the Qaeda leader.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/navy-seals-book-will-describe-raid-that-killed-bin-laden/', 'snippet': 'The book, written under a pseudonym by a member of the Navy SEALs, will be published on Sept. 11 and offer a “blow-by-blow narrative” of the raid that ended in the death of the Qaeda leader.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A detailed first-person account of the raid that killed Osama bin Laden, written by a member of the Navy SEALs who participated in the mission and was present at Bin Laden’s death, will be released next month, the publisher said on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Will Describe Raid That Killed Bin Laden', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Book to Give Commando’s Account of Bin Laden Raid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Navy Seals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Penguin Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Abbottabad (Pakistan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T16:53:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fae4b6cf-8dfd-5c78-8e2c-15c608ae4e35', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fae4b6cf-8dfd-5c78-8e2c-15c608ae4e35'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Champion, formerly the senior director of Consumer Reports’ auto test center, will work to ensure Nissan’s competitiveness and build quality.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/david-champion-director-of-automotive-testing-for-consumer-reports-joins-nissan/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Champion, formerly the senior director of Consumer Reports’ auto test center, will work to ensure Nissan’s competitiveness and build quality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To fill the newly created position of adviser for competitive assessment and quality, Nissan North America has hired David Champion, formerly the senior director of Consumer Reports’ auto test center. The appointment takes effect on Sept. 10, Nissan noted in a media release on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'David Champion, Director of Automotive Testing for Consumer Reports, Joins Nissan', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Reports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T16:57:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45727b66-06ce-5cce-95c7-165e0daed0a7', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45727b66-06ce-5cce-95c7-165e0daed0a7'}, {'abstract': 'Random genetic mutations in children that become more numerous with advancing paternal age may account for as many as 30 percent of autism cases, researchers reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/health/fathers-age-is-linked-to-risk-of-autism-and-schizophrenia.html', 'snippet': 'Random genetic mutations in children that become more numerous with advancing paternal age may account for as many as 30 percent of autism cases, researchers reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Older men are more likely than young ones to father a child who develops autism or schizophrenia, because of random mutations that become more numerous with advancing paternal age, scientists reported on Wednesday, in the first study to quantify the effect as it builds each year. The age of mothers had no bearing on the risk for these disorders, the study found. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Father’s Age Is Linked to Risk of Autism and Schizophrenia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study Finds Risk Of Autism Linked To Older Fathers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stefansson, Kari', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Schizophrenia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DeCode Genetics', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature (Journal)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T17:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benedict Carey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benedict', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c047f582-9443-5409-991f-623504169f90', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c047f582-9443-5409-991f-623504169f90'}, {'abstract': 'The vice presidential candidate suggests that the policy of Mitt Romney is the policy of the ticket.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/ryan-pressed-to-explain-position-on-rape-and-abortion/', 'snippet': 'The vice presidential candidate suggests that the policy of Mitt Romney is the policy of the ticket.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Paul D. Ryan sought to distance himself from Todd Akin, his House colleague, on Wednesday by condemning his comments about rape, even while deflecting questions about the meaning of “forcible rape.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryan Pressed to Explain Position on Rape and Abortion', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akin, Todd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh (Pa)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T17:01:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0debd802-295c-5750-a28a-5af6c54a4eff', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0debd802-295c-5750-a28a-5af6c54a4eff'}, {'abstract': 'The brand is out with three pretty-close-to-perfect boots this fall.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/the-get-chloes-boots/', 'snippet': 'The brand is out with three pretty-close-to-perfect boots this fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A fall boot is like a winter coat — so critical it can easily turn into a must-have of mythic proportions. Thankfully, Chloé’s Clare Waight Keller has designed three similar and pretty-close-to-perfect boot styles — the toe shape is the same on all; the heel size and height varies from pair to pair — that help make the best-ever boot something one cannot only attain but wear everyday. Available in three seasonally-appropriate colors — mustard-yellow, brick-red and rich burgundy (very important this season, take note) — the glossed-leather gives the shoes’ equestrian silhouettes a polished feel. The only hard part now? Picking which one to wear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Chloé’s Boots', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T17:01:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oona Haas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03ac1e0e-7059-55b1-a465-6aa0ea80b818', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03ac1e0e-7059-55b1-a465-6aa0ea80b818'}, {'abstract': 'Despite American-led efforts to marginalize Iran, Ban Ki-moon, the secretary general of the United Nations, plans to attend the annual meeting of the Nonaligned Movement being held there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/world/middleeast/ban-ki-moon-will-attend-iran-summit-over-american-and-israeli-objections.html', 'snippet': 'Despite American-led efforts to marginalize Iran, Ban Ki-moon, the secretary general of the United Nations, plans to attend the annual meeting of the Nonaligned Movement being held there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Efforts led by the United States and Israel to isolate Iran suffered a setback on Wednesday when the United Nations announced that Ban Ki-moon, the secretary general, would join officials from 120 countries in Tehran next week for a summit meeting that Iran has trumpeted as a vindication of its defiance and enduring importance in world affairs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/world/iran/iran-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/23/world/iran/iran-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/world/iran/iran-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/world/iran/iran-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/world/iran/iran-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/23/world/iran/iran-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/world/iran/iran-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Visit Will Set Back a Push to Isolate Iran', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Visit Will Set Back a Push to Isolate Iran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban Ki-moon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nonaligned Movement', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T17:06:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01ec2ff0-df65-53b4-a577-048fcb4ef388', 'word_count': 1220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01ec2ff0-df65-53b4-a577-048fcb4ef388'}, {'abstract': 'When someone hacks into a company’s computer system and wreaks havoc, and a former employee is suspected, how does the business rebuild?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/business/smallbusiness/struggling-to-recover-from-a-cyberattack.html', 'snippet': 'When someone hacks into a company’s computer system and wreaks havoc, and a former employee is suspected, how does the business rebuild?', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN 2006, Peter Justen, a serial entrepreneur, founded MyBizHomepage, an online service that connected to companies’ QuickBooks accounting software to help business owners monitor their financial metrics. When the site went live in 2008, it attracted significant media attention. It was free to use and the company planned to make money through advertising, a recipe that appealed to Mr. Justen’s investors, who valued the company at $100 million based on the vast potential they perceived.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/business/smallbusiness/23sbiz/23sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/23/business/smallbusiness/23sbiz/23sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/business/smallbusiness/23sbiz/23sbiz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/business/smallbusiness/23sbiz/23sbiz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1325, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/business/smallbusiness/23sbiz/23sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/23/business/smallbusiness/23sbiz/23sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/business/smallbusiness/23sbiz/23sbiz-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Struggling to Recover From a Cyberattack', 'kicker': 'Case Study', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Struggling to Recover From a Cyberattack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Justen, Peter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T17:11:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Darren Dahl', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Darren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dahl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c38ef4b1-1b05-5399-9e20-dbe3ea27300c', 'word_count': 1283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c38ef4b1-1b05-5399-9e20-dbe3ea27300c'}, {'abstract': 'A cavernous, loud German-style beer garden with an unintimidating and older Park Slope crowd.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/fashion/die-koelner-bierhalle-in-park-slope.html', 'snippet': 'A cavernous, loud German-style beer garden with an unintimidating and older Park Slope crowd.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the spirit of barbarian tribes, beer gardens with no-frills décor and heavyweight glassware have invaded New York’s bar scene. The latest is Die Koelner Bierhalle, which opened in early August in Park Slope, a few blocks from the Barclays Center. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/fashion/23BOITE2/0823STLBOITE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 805, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/fashion/23BOITE2/0823STLBOITE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1609, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/fashion/23BOITE2/23BOITE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/23/fashion/23BOITE2/23BOITE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/fashion/23BOITE2/23BOITE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Die Koelner Bierhalle', 'kicker': 'Boîte', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Die Koelner Bierhalle: Park Slope', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Slope (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Die Koelner Bierhalle (Brooklyn, NY, Bar)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T17:34:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original':