ther Player Receives 50-Game Ban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colon, Bartolo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oakland Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Drug Use)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Testosterone', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T18:09:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser and Serge F. Kovaleski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Serge', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Kovaleski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bcfd7a3-812c-55a9-a173-a3f61226a547', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bcfd7a3-812c-55a9-a173-a3f61226a547'}, {'abstract': 'Real-time genome sequencing helped a federal research hospital understand and end an outbreak of a drug-resistant bacterium, Klebsiella pneumoniae, that killed six patients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/health/genome-detectives-solve-mystery-of-hospitals-k-pneumoniae-outbreak.html', 'snippet': 'Real-time genome sequencing helped a federal research hospital understand and end an outbreak of a drug-resistant bacterium, Klebsiella pneumoniae, that killed six patients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ambulance sped up to the red brick federal research hospital on June 13, 2011, and paramedics rushed a gravely ill 43-year-old woman straight to intensive care. She had a rare lung disease and was gasping for breath. And, just hours before, the hospital learned she had been infected with a deadly strain of bacteria resistant to nearly all antibiotics. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Genome Detectives Solve a Hospital’s Deadly Outbreak', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Genome Detectives Solve a Hospital’s Deadly Outbreak', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institutes of Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Science Translational Medicine (Journal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T18:15:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94360cea-8a5f-5d2c-8418-1b480347c4ac', 'word_count': 1130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94360cea-8a5f-5d2c-8418-1b480347c4ac'}, {'abstract': 'The Steinberg award, the most generous prize in theater, will allow the creator of “Chinglish” and “M. Butterfly” to decline film and television work and concentrate on writing plays.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/david-henry-hwang-wins-200000-prize-for-playwriting/', 'snippet': 'The Steinberg award, the most generous prize in theater, will allow the creator of “Chinglish” and “M. Butterfly” to decline film and television work and concentrate on writing plays.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The $200,000 Steinberg award for playwriting, the most generous prize in theater, has been presented to Tony Award winner David Henry Hwang for 32 years of provocative satires and dramas (“Chinglish,” “M. Butterfly”) that brought more Asian and Asian-American characters to Broadway and other stages, the Harold and Mimi Steinberg Charitable Trust announced on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'David Henry Hwang Wins $200,000 Prize for Playwriting', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'David Henry Hwang Wins Big Playwriting Prize', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hwang, David Henry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Steinberg, Harold and Mimi, Charitable Trust', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T18:15:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/977bd8c1-a39d-5908-8024-665770a9cc2b', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/977bd8c1-a39d-5908-8024-665770a9cc2b'}, {'abstract': 'Missouri residents active in the Republican Party were divided over Representative Todd Akin’s decision to continue his campaign for the United States Senate, even as a chorus of party leaders urged him to throw in the towel.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/missouri-republicans-weigh-in-on-akin/', 'snippet': 'Missouri residents active in the Republican Party were divided over Representative Todd Akin’s decision to continue his campaign for the United States Senate, even as a chorus of party leaders urged him to throw in the towel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Missouri residents who are active in the Republican Party are divided over Representative Todd Akin’s decision to continue his campaign for the United States Senate, even as a chorus of party leaders urged him to throw in the towel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missouri Republicans Weigh In on Akin', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akin, Todd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCaskill, Claire', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T18:16:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Yaccino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3db90b4-6f90-5996-a36f-ccd7c5083cee', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3db90b4-6f90-5996-a36f-ccd7c5083cee'}, {'abstract': 'Minutes of the most recent policy meeting are likely to solidify expectations that the central bank will introduce new measures this fall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/business/economy/fed-members-saw-new-action-unless-recovery-quickens.html', 'snippet': 'Minutes of the most recent policy meeting are likely to solidify expectations that the central bank will introduce new measures this fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Many Federal Reserve officials at their most recent policy meeting pushed for further actions to support the economy if the recovery failed to strengthen over the summer, an official account released on Wednesday showed.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Many at Fed Ready to Act if Necessary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Many at Fed Ready to Act If Necessary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T18:17:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52ef3522-0b96-5023-a6df-1ac9ce63b303', 'word_count': 913, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52ef3522-0b96-5023-a6df-1ac9ce63b303'}, {'abstract': 'Thomas Jefferson’s farming and diet were ahead of their time.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/thomas-jefferson-founding-foodie/', 'snippet': 'Thomas Jefferson’s farming and diet were ahead of their time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thomas Jefferson’s take on agriculture sounds remarkably like the 1800s version of Wendell Berry, with a little bit of Alice Waters thrown in.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thomas Jefferson, ‘Founding Foodie’', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'cont