 through the air when explosives were set beneath it this week at the Second Avenue subway excavation site, a transit spokesman said Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steel Plate Above Subway Blast Site ‘Opened Up Like a Trapdoor’', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blast at 2nd Ave. Subway Project Blew Steel Plate Open ‘Like a Trapdoor’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Explosions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Second Avenue Subway (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T19:40:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f759ec97-4479-5322-876a-a384e6457cf5', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f759ec97-4479-5322-876a-a384e6457cf5'}, {'abstract': 'During a campaign stop in Iowa on Wednesday, Mitt Romney said President Obama had failed to deal with deficits and unemployment.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/romney-returns-to-his-mainstay-the-economy/', 'snippet': 'During a campaign stop in Iowa on Wednesday, Mitt Romney said President Obama had failed to deal with deficits and unemployment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BETTENDORF, Iowa — With the unwanted distractions of Representative Todd Akin’s “legitimate rape” comments still swirling in the background on Wednesday, Mitt Romney returned to his political mainstay during a campaign stop at LeClaire Manufacturing here — hitting President Obama over the economy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Returns to His Mainstay: The Economy', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T20:01:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b1a1036-2597-56c5-905d-d357b21f6ff3', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b1a1036-2597-56c5-905d-d357b21f6ff3'}, {'abstract': 'Frank Parker charged the beach at Dieppe in 1942. Seventy years later, his daughter stepped onto the same hard sand for the first time.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/in-a-little-known-wwii-battle-a-fathers-experience-becomes-a-daughters-journey/', 'snippet': 'Frank Parker charged the beach at Dieppe in 1942. Seventy years later, his daughter stepped onto the same hard sand for the first time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DIEPPE, France — Going to the 70th anniversary commemoration of the Dieppe raid in Normandy this past weekend was part of a journey I began when I was very small. It gathered steam in college, when I first saw footage at the Canadian War Museum in Ottawa that was shot at Dieppe by the Germans. I stood in a gallery watching it, looking for my father, Francis Stanley Parker, a private in the Black Watch Regiment of Canada, in the columns marching past the camera — an American in the sea of Canadian captives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Little-Known WWII Battle, a Father’s Experience Becomes a Daughter’s Journey', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dieppe (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T20:03:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diantha Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a029157-78be-59bb-9f19-08264a9e3bed', 'word_count': 1830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a029157-78be-59bb-9f19-08264a9e3bed'}, {'abstract': 'A slaughterhouse in Hanford, Calif., was forced to stop operations after an animal rights charity secretly filmed inhumane treatment.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/work-at-slaughterhouse-is-halted-after-graphic-undercover-videos/', 'snippet': 'A slaughterhouse in Hanford, Calif., was forced to stop operations after an animal rights charity secretly filmed inhumane treatment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal authorities have shut down a California slaughterhouse for investigation after an animal protection charity secretly filmed cows being electrically shocked, shot in the head, suffocated and undergoing other abuses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Work at Slaughterhouse Is Halted After Graphic Undercover Videos', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 