erson': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f19f6391-fc9c-5362-b5f8-f0a15d5a0de7', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f19f6391-fc9c-5362-b5f8-f0a15d5a0de7'}, {'abstract': 'At the Second World Mind Sports Games in Lille, France, the United States senior team failed in its bid to win the world title.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/crosswords/bridge/bridge-second-world-mind-sports-games-in-france.html', 'snippet': 'At the Second World Mind Sports Games in Lille, France, the United States senior team failed in its bid to win the world title.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LILLE, France — At the Second World Mind Sports Games here the United States senior team (Richie Schwartz, Lew Finkel, Neil Chambers, John Schermer, Steve Landen and Sam Lev; I was its nonplaying captain) failed in its bid to win the world title. In the 96-board final on Tuesday and Wednesday against Hungary (Mikos Dumbovich, Mihaly Kovacs, Peter Magyar and Geza Szappanos, with its nonplaying captain, Gyorgy Barany), the United States lost by 247 international match points to 166. France came in third.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/arts/card/card-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/arts/card/card-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Second World Mind Sports Games in France', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None,