 the Director of National Intelligence, expressing concern about a “loophole” in the law that permits the collection of United States data.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter to the Director of National Intelligence', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs | Documents', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T22:20:15+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Opinion', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/aa009f0f-db0a-5e4e-a991-987357280e14', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/aa009f0f-db0a-5e4e-a991-987357280e14'}, {'abstract': 'After months of anticipation, Facebook is now in the final stage of completing its takeover of Instagram, the popular photo-sharing application.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/f-t-c-ends-investigation-on-facebooks-instagram-deal/', 'snippet': 'After months of anticipation, Facebook is now in the final stage of completing its takeover of Instagram, the popular photo-sharing application.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After months of anticipation, Facebook is now closer to completing its takeover of Instagram, the popular photo-sharing application.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.T.C. Ends Investigation on Facebook’s Instagram Deal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value