ednesday chasing the bird, alongside agents from Animal Care & Control of New York City, which rounds up stray animals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As of late Wednesday afternoon, the captivating, if elusive, peacock flying around Kew Gardens Hills, Queens, had still not been apprehended.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hunt Continues for Escaped Peacock in Queens', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Peacocks and Peahens', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kew Gardens (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T22:46:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric P. Newcomer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Newcomer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f99b9e99-7585-57db-9e75-071f1b63055b', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f99b9e99-7585-57db-9e75-071f1b63055b'}, {'abstract': 'The artist James Welling’s photographs of the homes and studios of Andrew Wyeth will be on display at the David Zwirner Gallery in New York, starting Sept. 7.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/garden/images-from-wyeths-world-paint-splatters-and-all-qa.html', 'snippet': 'The artist James Welling’s photographs of the homes and studios of Andrew Wyeth will be on display at the David Zwirner Gallery in New York, starting Sept. 7.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Welling’s interest in Andrew Wyeth dates from his teenage years, when he took a drawing class at the Wadsworth Atheneum in Hartford, where some of the artist’s work was displayed. Flash forward four decades. Mr. Welling, 61, is a professor in the Art Department at U.C.L.A. (he will be a visiting professor at Princeton starting next month). During his prolific career, he has painted, sculptured and worked in video. At one point, he was John Baldessari’s teaching assistant.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23QNA1_SPAN/23QNA1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23QNA1_SPAN/23QNA1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23QNA1_SPAN/23QNA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23QNA1_SPAN/23QNA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23QNA1_SPAN/23QNA1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23QNA1_SPAN/23QNA1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23QNA1_SPAN/23QNA1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Images From Wyeth’s World, Paint Splatters and All', 'kicker': 'Currents | Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Images From Wyeth’s World, Paint Splatters and All', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Welling, James', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyeth, Andrew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T22:48:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea8bb1f9-0d7e-53c5-beaf-7dcacf72be5f', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea8bb1f9-0d7e-53c5-beaf-7dcacf72be5f'}, {'abstract': 'The Guild Hall of East Hampton holds its seventh annual lecture and garden tour with access to five private gardens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/garden/hamptons-havens-open-for-a-day.html', 'snippet': 'The Guild Hall of East Hampton holds its seventh annual lecture and garden tour with access to five private gardens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do hedge fund managers’ hedges grow any greener? Two of the impeccably tended Edens on view this weekend for charity may offer a clue. On Saturday, the Guild Hall of East Hampton will present its seventh annual lecture and garden tour, the Garden as Art, offering access to five private gardens.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23SUBEVENTS/23SUBCURR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23SUBEVENTS/23SUBCURR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23SUBEVENTS/23SUBCURR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23SUBEVENTS/23SUBCURR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23SUBEVENTS/23SUBCURR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23SUBEVENTS/23SUBCURR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hamptons Havens Open for a Day', 'kicker': 'Currents | Events', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hamptons Havens Open for a Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guild Hall', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Hampton (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T22:48:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Mason', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mason', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7de04c4f-8b4e-5332-8d8d-69569d11b975', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7de04c4f-8b4e-5332-8d8d-69569d11b975'}, {'abstract': 'The Shelving System was created by the architect Mogens Koch, an unsung hero of Danish design.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/garden/a-classic-bookcase-comes-to-america.html', 'snippet': 'The Shelving System was created by the architect Mogens Koch, an unsung hero of Danish design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The late Danish architect Mogens Koch, one of the lesser-known heroes of Scandinavian design, is perhaps best remembered for the shelving system he created in 1928 for his own home in Copenhagen. The system soon caught the interest of Rud. Rasmussen, a local company. Rasmussen put it into production in 1932 and has been making it ever since. Last year, Carl Hansen, another Danish manufacturer, acquired Rasmussen and is giving Mr. Koch’s design its American debut. The Shelving System (it features an extensive range of modular elements, including a CD/DVD unit) is exceptionally flexible. The sections for the basic six-piece unit can be installed horizontally or vertically, allowing lots of options. Made of solid oak with dovetail and rabbet joints to provide strength and stability, the basic unit measures about 30 by 30 by 10.6 inches and is $1,650. Information: (212) 242-6736 or carlhansen.com. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23FURNITURE/23CURR4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23FURNITURE/23CURR4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1539, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23FURNITURE/23CURR4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23FURNITURE/23CURR4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/garden/23FURNITURE/23CURR4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Classic Bookcase Comes to America', 'kicker': 'Currents | Furniture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Classic Bookcase Comes to America', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carl Hansen & Son', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, Mogens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-22T22:48:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arlene Hirst', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arlene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirst', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe1837ae-b0bd-5230-86ea-9c3497677ea5', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe1837ae-b0bd-5230-86ea-9c3497677ea5'}, {'abstract': 'The former editor of Architectural Digest is downsizing and selling her furnishings online.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/garden/help-paige-rense-noland-clear-her-closets.html', 'snippet': 'The former editor of Architectural Digest is downsizing and selling her furnishings online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the former editor of Architectural Digest, Paige Rense Noland spent 35 years influencing taste. On Saturday, at 11 a.m., Eastern time, many of the objects she collected during that time will go up for sale at the online retailer One Kings Lane.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page':