 you might think the NBC-Twitter Olympics partnership was a disaster. But the two companies say Twitter commentary actually drove more viewers to turn on their television sets.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/22/despite-nbcfail-nbc-and-twitter-say-partnership-was-success/', 'snippet': 'If you followed the griping by Twitter users about NBC’s handling of the Olympic Games, you might think the NBC-Twitter Olympics partnership was a disaster. But the two companies say Twitter commentary actually drove more viewers to turn on their ...', 'lead_paragraph': ' If you followed the griping by Twitter users  about NBC’s handling of the Olympic Games, you might think the NBC-Twitter Olympics partnership was an epic disaster. NBC’s decision to time-delay most events prompted angry kvetching on Twitter and quickly popularized the hashtag #NBCFail.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/blogs/olympics/olympics-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/blogs/olympics/olympics-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite #NBCFail, NBC and Twitter Say Partnership Was Success', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T00:05:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth and Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae012815-6db9-51d8-acc4-8b2e0df2a411', 'word_count': 591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae012815-6db9-51d8-acc4-8b2e0df2a411'}, {'abstract': 'Gary Contessa, who in 1981 walked the upset winner Willow Hour to the summer’s marquee event at the Saratoga Race Course, has entered Speightscity, a 30-1 dark horse, this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/sports/in-travers-stakes-trainer-gary-contessa-takes-a-shot.html', 'snippet': 'Gary Contessa, who in 1981 walked the upset winner Willow Hour to the summer’s marquee event at the Saratoga Race Course, has entered Speightscity, a 30-1 dark horse, this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SARATOGA SPRINGS, N.Y. — The pills rattled in the jar announcing that the post-position draw for the Travers Stakes was under way. On the edge of the paddock, the trainer Gary Contessa tried to explain why he had entered a horse named Speightscity that looked as if he had no chance to win the 143rd running of the Midsummer Derby on Saturday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/sports/Y-POSTCARDS/Y-POSTCARDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/sports/