+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/5449c0ff-86ed-527d-b152-3e58f72d9e2b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/5449c0ff-86ed-527d-b152-3e58f72d9e2b'}, {'abstract': 'The metropolitan commuter transportation mobility tax, passed by the State Legislature in 2009, required employers to set aside 34 cents for every $100 in payroll costs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/nyregion/judge-overturns-a-state-tax-meant-to-help-the-mta.html', 'snippet': 'The metropolitan commuter transportation mobility tax, passed by the State Legislature in 2009, required employers to set aside 34 cents for every $100 in payroll costs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A tariff meant to provide revenue for the Metropolitan Transportation Authority by taxing businesses in the New York City region was struck down as unconstitutional on Wednesday by a State Supreme Court justice in Nassau County. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Overturns a State Tax Meant to Assist the M.T.A.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Overturns a State Tax Meant to Assist the M.T.A.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T03:22:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': No