ey-will-stay-the-course-amid-focus-on-abortion.html', 'snippet': 'Campaign advisers say Mr. Romney’s economic message will still resonate with female voters after the controversy created by Todd Akin’s “legitimate rape” comment subsides.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Mitt Romney’s campaign advisers have concluded that they do not need any major adjustments in strategy to respond to the new focus on abortion and reproductive rights caused by Representative Todd Akin, betting that their candidate’s economic message will still resonate with female voters after the controversy over Mr. Akin’s remarks about “legitimate rape” subsides.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Strategists Say They’ll Stay the Course Amid Focus on Abortion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romney Strategists Say They’ll Stay the Course Amid Focus on Abortion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akin, Todd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T03:27:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear and Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qu