ght': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Add to Woes, Despite Solid Start by Harvey', 'kicker': 'Rockies 5, Mets 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Loss Of Santana, Mets Add To Woes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santana, Johan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Colorado Rockies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harvey, Matt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T03:35:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33731a4f-7bee-52a7-b5cf-e27a86b34e17', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33731a4f-7bee-52a7-b5cf-e27a86b34e17'}, {'abstract': 'Two of the four men who federal officials said plotted terrorist activities from a booth at a North Georgia Waffle House were sentenced to five years in prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/us/georgia-2-men-who-talked-of-terrorist-activities-at-a-waffle-house-are-sentenced.html', 'snippet': 'Two of the four men who federal officials said plotted terrorist activities from a booth at a North Georgia Waffle House were sentenced to five years in prison.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Two of the four men who federal officials said plotted terrorist activities from a booth at a North Georgia Waffle House were sentenced to five years in prison on Wednesday for conspiring to obtain an unregistered explosive device and silencer. Defense lawyers had argued that the men were egged on by an informant and that recordings of their plot showed nothing more than old men bragging. Prosecutors said the men were members of a loose-knit militia group that had scouted federal buildings in Atlanta to attack and had planned to kill people. Judge Richard W. Story of Federal District Court said that while people have the right to talk about what they want, “when they start buying bombs and silencers, I’m sorry, we have crossed the line.” Lawyers for the men, Frederick Thomas, 73, and Dan Roberts, 68, said the sentence was part of a plea deal that includes 100 hours of community service. The other men charged, Ray Adams and Samuel Crump, both in their 60s, plan to go to trial. They are charged with conspiracy and attempting to make the poison ricin from castor beans. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Georgia: 2 Waffle House Plotters Are Sentenced ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Georgia: 2 Waffle House Plotters Are Sentenced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, Dan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Frederick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T03:43:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Severson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/388327bd-bde6-5767-bbef-1e629