a, Discover to accept PayPal in stores, weight-loss surgery may prevent diabetes and other consumer focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/thursday-reading-fathers-age-linked-to-risk-of-autism-schizophrenia/', 'snippet': 'Father’s age linked to risk of autism and schizophrenia, Discover to accept PayPal in stores, weight-loss surgery may prevent diabetes and other consumer focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and on our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday Reading: Father’s Age Linked to Risk of Autism and Schizophrenia', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T12:40:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3bef837-ef42-5e1c-90f3-7e9e4cd8e4e2', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3bef837-ef42-5e1c-90f3-7e9e4cd8e4e2'}, {'abstract': 'Google’s efforts to recruit and promote more women have resulted in more hires, but not in the executive offices.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/daily-report-at-the-top-of-google-fewer-women/', 'snippet': 'Google’s efforts to recruit and promote more women have resulted in more hires, but not in the executive offices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senior women at Google are losing ground, reports Claire Cain Miller in The New York Times. Since Larry Page became chief executive and reorganized Google last year, women have been pushed out of his inner circle and passed over for promotions. They include Marissa Mayer, who left last month to run Yahoo after being sidelined at Google. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: At the Top of Google, Fewer Women', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T12:40:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aedb104a-2681-579e-939e-467c71842d0a', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aedb104a-2681-579e-939e-467c71842d0a'}, {'abstract': 'Walking in Scotland, wondering about Palestine.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/a-tale-of-two-territories/', 'snippet': 'Walking in Scotland, wondering about Palestine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORTREE, Scotland — Earlier this month, ahead of the Edinburgh International Book Festival, my wife Penny and I decided to go hiking on the Isle of Skye. We were staying outside Portree, the main town on the island, at the foot of Loch Sligachan. From the window of our room we could see the Black Cuillin Mountains, their towering summits silhouetted against the sky as if drawn by a mighty hand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tale of Two Territories', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Walking', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Edinburgh (Scotland)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Isle of Skye (Scotland)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T12:47:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raja Shehadeh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raja', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shehadeh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5d02edc-c03a-57a1-ad46-37b76f840252', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5d02edc-c03a-57a1-ad46-37b76f840252'}, {'abstract': 'What the CBO didn’t do.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/saving-serious-ryan/', 'snippet': 'What the CBO didn’t do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There has, of course, been some pushback against my column pointing out that the Very Serious Paul Ryan is not, in fact, serious at all. Some of this pushback takes the form of assertions that he must be serious, because the Congressional Budget Office scored his plan and found that it led to lower debt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saving Serious Ryan', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T12:47:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d45b5c7-6e7f-5682-bc2d-fee8911120b6', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d45b5c7-6e7f-5682-bc2d-fee8911120b6'}, {'abstract': 'A pilot airlifts sheep and deer among Hawaii’s islands.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/stupid-animal-trick-flying-sheep-and-deer-among-hawaiis-islands/', 'snippet': 'A pilot airlifts sheep and deer among Hawaii’s islands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Audrey McAvoy, an Associated Press reporter in Hawaii, has filed a fascinating piece chronicling one of the human activities that have created the global mashup of animals and plants that is ecology in the Anthropocene. Here’s a snippet (as you read, keep in mind that islands are particularly vulnerable to serious environmental disruption from introduced species): ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stupid Animal Trick: Flying Sheep and Deer Among Hawaii’s Islands', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Invasive Species', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sheep', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Associated Press', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii (The Big Island)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maui (Hawaii)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T12:54:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3b64e58-b30e-5c8e-b844-94f73761e10e', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3b64e58-b30e-5c8e-b844-94f73761e10e'}, {'abstract': 'Turning the clock back two centuries.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/francisco-danconia-on-money/', 'snippet': 'Turning the clock back two centuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dave Weigel made a great catch the other day: he notes that Paul Ryan has said that his views on monetary policy are based on Francisco d’Anconia’s speech in Atlas Shrugged.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Francisco d’Anconia on Money', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T12:59:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2128f216-1324-546f-8497-80f35a02c82b', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2128f216-1324-546f-8497-80f35a02c82b'}, {'abstract': 'More than 140 artists and celebrities are trying to persuade Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo to bar hydraulic fracturing in parts of New York State.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/coalition-of-celebrities-speak-out-against-gas-drilling/', 'snippet': 'More than 140 artists and celebrities are trying to persuade Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo to bar hydraulic fracturing in parts of New York State.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 140 artists and celebrities, including Lady Gaga and Paul McCartney, have signed on to a coalition to try to persuade Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo to ban the use of hydraulic fracturing — also known as hydrofracking or fracking — to extract natural gas in parts of New York State.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrities Join to Oppose Upstate Gas Drilling', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Celebrities Join to Oppose Upstate Gas Drilling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lennon, Sean', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ono, Yoko', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T13:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee55850a-f2d7-58c8-a3e0-adf1b4367279', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee55850a-f2d7-58c8-a3e0-adf1b4367279'}, {'abstract': 'During her concert tour of Europe, Madonna changed a video that once showed Marine Le Pen, the president of France’s far-right National Front party, with a swastika superimposed on her head. The new video shows a question mark instead of the Nazi symbol.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/madonna-alters-concert-video-that-had-angered-french-political-party/', 'snippet': 'During her concert tour of Europe, Madonna changed a video that once showed Marine Le Pen, the president of France’s far-right National Front party, with a swastika superimposed on her head. The new video shows a question mark instead of the Nazi ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Madonna appears to have conceded in a war of words (and pictures) with France’s National Front political party, and has toned down an image shown in her concerts that once depicted Marine Le Pen, the president of that far-right party, with a swastika on her head.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Madonna Alters Concert Video That Had Angered French Political Party', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Madonna Alters a Concert Video', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Le Pen, Marine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madonna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Front (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T13:02:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d87bc33-148d-5590-bd46-78263904c315', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d87bc33-148d-5590-bd46-78263904c315'}, {'abstract': 'One of the ironies of the 2012 election campaign is this: Mitt Romney is a Harvard-trained pragmatist, as is President Obama, and both of them alienate their bases by caring more about data and solutions than they do about emotion or partisanship.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/pragmatism-as-a-guiding-political-trait/', 'snippet': 'One of the ironies of the 2012 election campaign is this: Mitt Romney is a Harvard-trained pragmatist, as is President Obama, and both of them alienate their bases by caring more about data and solutions than they do about emotion or partisanship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — After to speaking this week to Glenn Hubbard, a top Romney advisor and the dean of the Columbia Business School, I decided to focus my column on the big economic choice that Americans face in this election. But Mr. Hubbard also had some interesting things to say about Mr. Romney as a person and as a politician.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pragmatism as a Guiding Political Trait', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hubbard, R Glenn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T13:15:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chrystia Freeland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chrystia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Freeland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6517885-d43d-5104-b968-edad191515c9', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6517885-d43d-5104-b968-edad191515c9'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/what-were-reading-507/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Insatiable Critic: A highly personal and heartbreaking celebration of the life of the photographer Steven Richter, Gael Greene’s partner and dining companion of 27 years, who recently died at the age of 74. Titled “Farewell Steven: Letting Go,” its last sentence reads: “Not yet ready to be alone.” – Glenn Collins', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T13:21:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bb858ea-dcb4-5989-862c-0b9771339e47', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bb858ea-dcb4-5989-862c-0b9771339e47'}, {'abstract': 'Also, a documentary critical of President Obama leads in advance ticket sales, and Ladbrokes sets its odds in the race for the Nobel Prize for Literature.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/the-breakfast-meeting-politics-bores-the-networks-and-harry-tempts-british-papers/', 'snippet': 'Also, a documentary critical of President Obama leads in advance ticket sales, and Ladbrokes sets its odds in the race for the Nobel Prize for Literature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Confident that the presidential election this year lacks the drama of 2008, ABC, CBS and NBC are cutting back coverage of the conventions, Jeremy W. Peters reports. This means, among other things, that the first night of the four-night Republican National Convention will be skipped entirely by the networks, including a speech by Ann Romney, Mitt Romney’s wife. The other three nights will get an hour each. (The Democratic convention is only three nights long, but NBC will offer two of its three hours of coverage on the final night so it can carry an N.F.L. football game earlier in the week.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Politics Bores the Networks, and Harry Tempts British Papers', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T13:22:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e63d16d4-5249-5e76-9b1f-3e052236c4fa', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e63d16d4-5249-5e76-9b1f-3e052236c4fa'}, {'abstract': 'A highly scripted TV appearance of Chávez’s goes wrong, exposing more than one crack in the system he’s created.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/power-failures-in-venezuela/', 'snippet': 'A highly scripted TV appearance of Chávez’s goes wrong, exposing more than one crack in the system he’s created.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Venezuelans are used to the routine. A computer-generated Venezuelan flag flutters on the screen, followed by a ponderous announcement: “This is a broadcast from the Ministry of People’s Power for Communication and Information of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela and by the national network of radio and television.” Forget about that baseball game. This is a cadena, or chain, meaning it’s a chained broadcast and every single channel has to show it. (And every radio station, too!)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Power Failures in Venezuela', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steel and Iron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T13:23:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francisco Toro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francisco', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b92433ce-0978-5a3b-bb47-004045959877', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b92433ce-0978-5a3b-bb47-004045959877'}, {'abstract': 'Paris Saint-Germain’s big-spending ways are drawing scrutiny in France at the start of the Ligue 1 season.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/in-france-all-eyes-on-p-g/', 'snippet': 'Paris Saint-Germain’s big-spending ways are drawing scrutiny in France at the start of the Ligue 1 season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — These days it seems any discussion about Paris Saint-Germain begins with a look at the money the club has spent since Qatar Sports Investment bought the team.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In France, All Eyes on P.$.G.', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA Champions League (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABRAMOVICH, ROMAN A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibrahimovic, Zlatan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paris St-Germain FC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T13:35:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ricardo Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ricardo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cec3039c-c3e2-5e5a-8dcb-de8862126906', 'word_count': 1027, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cec3039c-c3e2-5e5a-8dcb-de8862126906'}, {'abstract': 'The real importance of research showing that full-time work means better health for all mothers can too easily get lost in one segment of society defending such a choice.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/full-time-work-means-better-health-for-mothers/', 'snippet': 'The real importance of research showing that full-time work means better health for all mothers can too easily get lost in one segment of society defending such a choice.', 'lead_paragraph': '“This is not about advice for women,” the University of Akron sociologist Adrianne M. Frech said of her latest research, which showed that women who work steadily full-time after the birth of their first child report better physical health than women who don’t.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/style/motherlode-monopoly-card/motherlode-monopoly-card-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/22/style/motherlode-monopoly-card/motherlode-monopoly-card-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/style/motherlode-monopoly-card/motherlode-monopoly-card-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/22/style/motherlode-monopoly-car