ce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Handy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0ab3e56-5a72-5509-841a-b21976544889', 'word_count': 1063, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0ab3e56-5a72-5509-841a-b21976544889'}, {'abstract': 'In David Levithan’s novel, a teenage romance is put to the test.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/books/review/every-day-by-david-levithan.html', 'snippet': 'In David Levithan’s novel, a teenage romance is put to the test.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As surely as a gardener plants flowers or a mason lays stone, a writer puts obstacles in the path of love. Your families hate each other. Your cultures clash. One of you is rich and one of you is poor, or one of you is naïf and one of you is whore. Maybe there’s a prickly vampirism issue, maybe a pesky time-travel quirk. It’s always something.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bodies and Soul', 'kicker': "Children's Books", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bodies and Soul', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levithan, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T14:29:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3f586a1-ffe0-5123-ba2b-dfb4f661ad1e', 'word_count': 703, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3f586a1-ffe0-5123-ba2b-dfb4f661ad1e'}, {'abstract': 'New picture books offer creative approaches to coun