umane procedures to encourage illegal aliens to return home voluntarily,” a...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republicans have adopted a party platform on immigration that would require employers nationwide to verify workers’ legal status and deny federal financing to universities that allow illegal immigrant students to enroll at lower in-state tuition rates. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Immigration Platform Backs ‘Self-Deportation’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dream Act (Development, Relief and Education for Minors Act)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Students (in US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kobach, Kris W', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T14:46:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4f8a358-efc1-5031-a6ef-21a34651bca9', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4f8a358-efc1-5031-a6ef-21a34651bca9'}, {'abstract': 'Bartolo Colon’s suspension tells writers that the Bay Area is the capital of steroids and makes them wonder whether the sport’s testing system works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/sports/undeterred-by-drug-testing-in-baseball-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'Bartolo Colon’s suspension tells writers that the Bay Area is the capital of steroids and makes them wonder whether the sport’s testing system works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At first glance, the news that pitcher Bartolo Colon has tested positive for performance-enhancing drugs is about as surprising as the Cookie Monster testing positive for chocolate chips. He is 39, having resurrected his injury-plagued career with help from a fishy-sounding stem cell procedure last year and despite a physique that makes it clear his performance-enhancing drugs are hidden in double cheeseburgers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/sports/24leading-pic/24leading-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 722, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/sports/24leading-pic/24leading-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1444, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/sports/24leading-pic/24leading-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandar