: 'While President Obama and Mitt Romney crisscross the nation raising money for their campaigns, in battleground states Republican and Democratic organizations have been laying the groundwork for voter organization and turnout for the November elect...', 'lead_paragraph': 'While President Obama and Mitt Romney crisscross the nation raising money for their campaigns, in the battleground states Republican and Democratic organizations have been laying the groundwork for voter organization and turnout for the November election. Much of the money for those efforts comes from the national party organizations — the Democratic and Republican National Committees, plus several Congressional party arms — that has been sent to the states from Washington.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Key Democratic State Parties Have Financial Edge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T15:29:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Derek Willis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Willis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dacf2376-4c0b-5832-8996-2c02bb61ffbc', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dacf2376-4c0b-5832-8996-2c02bb61ffbc'}, {'abstract': 'William B. Harrison Jr., a primary architect of the modern-day JPMorgan Chase, writes in an op-ed in The Times that the breakup of big banks would not prevent risky behaviors.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/jpmorgans-former-leader-defends-behemoths/', 'snippet': 'William B. Harrison Jr., a primary architect of the modern-day JPMorgan Chase, writes in an op-ed in The Times that the breakup of big banks would not prevent risky behaviors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a decade ago, William B. Harrison Jr. and Sanford I. Weill pioneered the model of the financial behemoth from their perches atop JPMorgan Chase and Citigroup. But today, the two Wall Street veterans hardly see eye to eye.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan’s Former Leader Makes a Case for Big Banks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glass-Steagall Act (1933)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrison, William B Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T15:34:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e60fcb14-621a-56cd-8448-d79f9bf8f08b', 'word_count': 671, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e60fcb14-621a-56cd-8448-d79f9bf8f08b'}, {'abstract': 'Despite rising criticism at home, Mrs. Gandhi’s rank rises in Forbes’ annual list.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/sonia-gandhi-ranked-sixth-most-powerful-woman-in-the-world/', 'snippet': 'Despite rising criticism at home, Mrs. Gandhi’s rank rises in Forbes’ annual list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sonia Gandhi, the Congress party president and chairwoman of the coalition government running the country, is India’s most powerful woman and the sixth most powerful woman in the world, according to Forbes magazine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sonia Gandhi Ranked Sixth Most Powerful Woman in the World', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T15:35:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamposh Raina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamposh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f534499b-f2f4-56b4-92e5-e453ab5a1392', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f534499b-f2f4-56b4-92e5-e453ab5a1392'}, {'abstract': 'New surveys show the ratings for governors in Florida, Ohio and Wisconsin as well as the state of play in key Senate contests.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/polls-highlight-senate-races-in-swing-states/', 'snippet': 'New surveys show the ratings for governors in Florida, Ohio and Wisconsin as well as the state of play in key Senate contests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Democratic incumbents have an edge over their challengers in the Florida and Ohio Senate races, while in Wisconsin, fresh from winning the Republican primary, former Gov. Tommy Thompson has a six-point advantage over Representative Tammy Baldwin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Polls Highlight Senate Races in Swing States', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'valu