6d835-112a-5294-9671-30c197825122'}, {'abstract': 'The severity of the country’s inventory surplus has been masked by the blocking or adjusting of economic data by the government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/business/global/chinas-economy-besieged-by-buildup-of-unsold-goods.html', 'snippet': 'The severity of the country’s inventory surplus has been masked by the blocking or adjusting of economic data by the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GUANGZHOU, China — After three decades of torrid growth, China is encountering an unfamiliar problem with its newly struggling economy: a huge buildup of unsold goods that is cluttering shop floors, clogging car dealerships and filling factory warehouses.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/business/global/24inventory/24inventory-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/24/business/global/24inventory/24inventory-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/business/global/24inventory/24inventory-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/business/global/24inventory/24inventory-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/business/global/24inventory/24inventory-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/24/business/global/24inventory/24inventory-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/business/global/24inventory/24inventory-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China Confronts Mounting Piles of Unsold Goods', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Confronts Mounting Piles Of Unsold Goods', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T16:03:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca3e2a0c-1e3d-5c58-8bab-7f80e1c742f8', 'word_count': 1347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca3e2a0c-1e3d-5c58-8bab-7f80e1c742f8'}, {'abstract': 'The state parole board, while noting Mark David Chapman’s good conduct record in prison, told him that paroling him “would greatly undermine respect for the law and tend to trivialize the tragic loss of life which you caused.”', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/lennons-killer-denied-parole-again/', 'snippet': 'The state parole board, while noting Mark David Chapman’s good conduct record in prison, told him that paroling him “would greatly undermine respect for the law and tend to trivialize the tragic loss of life which you caused.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark David Chapman has been denied parole, for the seventh time, in the murder ofJohn Lennon, the New York State corrections department said Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lennon’s Killer Denied Parole a 7th Time', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chapman Loses Seventh Bid for Parole in Lennon’s Killing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chapman, Mark David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lennon, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T16:05:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45624e3d-15ea-581d-9af3-dffba8603fa4', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45624e3d-15ea-581d-9af3-dffba8603fa4'}, {'abstract': 'How a mother built a home out of two suitcases.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/california-dreams-iranian-decor/', 'snippet': 'How a mother built a home out of two suitcases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1978, my mother packed two maroon, leatherette suitcases, and she, my father and I boarded a plane for the United States. Just about everyone who could leave Iran had done so already; friends and relatives had been selling off their houses for months. But “revolution” and “exile” were not words my family applied to our circumstances. We left our apartment on Pahlavi Avenue completely intact. The two suitcases suggested, if not a vacation, at most a temporary absence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California Dreams, Iranian Décor', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T16:10:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jasmin Darznik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jasmin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Darznik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c52c973-be53-589c-ae37-1583effd2a07', 'word_count': 1301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c52c973-be53-589c-ae37-1583effd2a07'}, {'abstract': 'Gen. John R. Allen, the senior commander in Afghanistan, said that up to one-quarter of the attacks by Afghan security forces on Americans could be caused by Taliban infiltration or coercion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/world/asia/general-notes-taliban-coercion-in-some-attacks-on-troops-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Gen. John R. Allen, the senior commander in Afghanistan, said that up to one-quarter of the attacks by Afghan security forces on Americans could be caused by Taliban infiltration or coercion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The senior commander in Afghanistan made new allowances on Thursday that Taliban influence could play a large role in attacks by Afghan security forces on Americans, saying that up to one-quarter of the killings could be caused by Taliban infiltration or coercion. But he reiterated that most of such insider attacks have still been attributed to personal grievances and animosities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'General Notes Taliban Coercion in Some Attacks on Troops', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'General Notes Taliban Coercion in Some Attacks on Troops', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T16:12:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7500fd4-a034-5d1c-a89e-136d43968527', 'word_count': 634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7500fd4-a034-5d1c-a89e-136d43968527'}, {'abstract': 'Twitter parodies of the Prime Minister, bloggers who exposed false rumors among government targets.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/indian-government-casts-a-wide-puzzling-net-over-internet/', 'snippet': 'Twitter parodies of the Prime Minister, bloggers who exposed false rumors among government targets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this week, the Indian government acknowledged that it had asked internet service providers to block about 250 web pages in an effort to contain