 Patchett at Jazz at Lincoln Center on Oct. 16.', 'lead_paragraph': 'J.K. Rowling is coming to America to promote her first novel for adults, “The Casual Vacancy,” her publisher has announced. Ms. Rowling will appear at one public event, an onstage interview at Jazz at Lincoln Center with the author Ann Patchett on Oct. 16. She will also take questions from the audience and sign copies of her book for audience members. Tickets go on sale Sept. 10, starting at $37, a price that includes a copy of the book. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rowling to Make U.S Appearance to Promote Her First Novel for Adults', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rowling in New York Appearance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patchett, Ann', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowling, J K', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jazz at Lincoln Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LITTLE BROWN & CO', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T16:27:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed8c506e-c38d-5689-98e9-6087cb613e1b', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed8c506e-c38d-5689-98e9-6087cb613e1b'}, {'abstract': 'Proceeds from the “Love for Levon” concert will go to help his family retain ownership of his home and his famous studio, a converted barn in Woodstock, N.Y.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/levon-helm-tribute-is-planned-for-october/', 'snippet': 'Proceeds from the “Love for Levon” concert will go to help his family retain ownership of his home and his famous studio, a converted barn in Woodstock, N.Y.', 'lead_paragraph': ' John Mayer, Gregg Allman, Joe Walsh and other prominent musicians plan to hold a large benefit concert to raise money for Levon Helm’s estate on Oct. 3 at the Izod Center in East Rutherford, N.J., Mr. Helm’s family announced.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Levon Helm Tribute Is Planned for October', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Concert Tribute to Levon Helm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allman, Gregg', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bentley, Dierks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Church, Eric (1977- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griffin, Patty', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Helm, Levon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hornsby, Bruce', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaMontagne, Ray', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayer, John', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staples, Mavis', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Lucinda', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Izod Center (East Rutherford, NJ)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Rutherford (NJ)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Woodstock (NY)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T16:29:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51524f5c-ab2d-5372-b32e-64f2ad98ad56', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51524f5c-ab2d-5372-b32e-64f2ad98ad56'}, {'abstract': 'How the president used his famous response to Horace Greeley to explain his new policy on emancipation.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/lincolns-letter-to-the-editor/', 'snippet': 'How the president used his famous response to Horace Greeley to explain his new policy on emancipation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Aug. 19, 1862 Horace Greeley, the editor of The New York Tribune, published a long “open letter” to President Lincoln in his newspaper. Titled “The Prayer for Twenty Millions,” the letter demanded that Lincoln immediately move to end slavery, not only in the Confederacy, but also in the loyal slave states – Delaware, Maryland, Kentucky, and Missouri, as well as in those parts of Tennessee under control of the United States. The letter was noteworthy as a bold, widely read attack on the president by a major figure in his own party. Even more noteworthy, though, was Lincoln’s response.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lincoln’s Letter to the Editor', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Sumter (SC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T16:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Finkelman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finkelman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92d9d843-56a6-5de1-8879-10711292c8ab', 'word_count': 1244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92d9d843-56a6-5de1-8879-10711292c8ab'}, {'abstract': 'Written by Ido Bernstein, the show explores the culture of aggressive masculinity in contemporary Israel.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/new-york-fringe-festival-report-dogs/', 'snippet': 'Written by Ido Bernstein, the show explores the culture of aggressive masculinity in contemporary Israel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reviews of shows from the New York International Fringe Festival will appear on ArtsBeat through the festival’s close on Aug. 26. For more information, go to fringenyc.org.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Fringe Festival Report: ‘Dogs’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fringe Festival in Review: Dogs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York International Fringe Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Ohio Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T16:32:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 