/', 'snippet': 'The Federal Trade Commission announced a settlement with Fitness Brands Inc. and its marketing partners on Thursday, over deceptive advertising claims for an abdominal exercise machine called the Ab Circle Pro.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are few easy ways to lose weight quickly, but that has not stopped some marketers from making claims to the contrary, especially for products pitched on late-night infomercials.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.T.C. Settles With Marketers of Ab Circle Pro', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T16:54:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03edeed3-9ebc-58d4-94f1-d58a997b70fc', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03edeed3-9ebc-58d4-94f1-d58a997b70fc'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook released major upgrades for its iPhone and iPad apps. Those who have suffered from the sluggishness of the current apps can breathe a collective sigh of relief: these new versions are much faster.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/facebook-iphone-ipad/', 'snippet': 'Facebook released major upgrades for its iPhone and iPad apps. Those who have suffered from the sluggishness of the current apps can breathe a collective sigh of relief: these new versions are much faster.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Facebook on Thursday released major upgrades to its iPhone and iPad apps. Those who have suffered from the sluggishness of the current apps can breathe a collective sigh of relief: these new versions are much faster.', 'source': 'Th