f_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcbeb810-322e-5ea4-82e2-93162707164e', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcbeb810-322e-5ea4-82e2-93162707164e'}, {'abstract': 'The carrier will begin what it’s calling a “Winemaker Series” for business travelers.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/pairs-well-with-peanuts-wine-tasting-on-delta/', 'snippet': 'The carrier will begin what it’s calling a “Winemaker Series” for business travelers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In-flight food has gotten regular upgrades — this spring alone British Airways prepared a menu with the chef Simon Hulstone, and ANA enlisted the French pastry chef Pierre Hermé. Now, Delta has turned its attention to oenophiles, who know that a chewy wine doesn’t mean you’ll need a toothpick after a glass.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pairs Well With Peanuts? Wine Tasting on Delta', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Delta Air Lines, Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T17:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Drake', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drake', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e169997-c1de-5727-81e0-b1c6481a241a', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e169997-c1de-5727-81e0-b1c6481a241a'}, {'abstract': 'The classic hairstyle has been morphing from a Nordic, tight style into chic, messier plaits.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/vain-glorious-braid-not-frayed/', 'snippet': 'The classic hairstyle has been morphing from a Nordic, tight style into chic, messier plaits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Braids have been around forever, of course, but they are morphing from a Nordic, tight style into chic, messier plaits, thanks to modern-day heroines like Jennifer Lawrence (as Katniss Everdeen in “The Hunger Games”) and Emilia Clarke, who plays the warrior princess Daenerys Targaryen on “Game of Thrones.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Braid, Not Frayed!', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gallagher, Sean', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hershberger, Sally', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T17:01:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Earle-Levine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Earle-Levine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c5bcfcd-8a46-5029-91cc-b4cfeeb2b225', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c5bcfcd-8a46-5029-91cc-b4cfeeb2b225'}, {'abstract': 'The company is trying to find ways to show lucrative ads to mobile users without cluttering up their hand-held screens and driving them away in frustration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/technology/facebook-rewrites-its-code-for-a-small-screen-world.html', 'snippet': 'The company is trying to find ways to show lucrative ads to mobile users without cluttering up their hand-held screens and driving them away in frustration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MENLO PARK, Calif. — At Facebook’s headquarters here, mobile devices are everywhere. The first thing visitors do is sign in on iPads at the front desk. Employees at the campus coffee shop use iPads as cash registers. Instead of sending e-mails, Facebook employees prefer to use the company’s messaging system, which pops up new messages on both mobile devices and PCs. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/business/24facebook_337/24facebook_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/24/business/24facebook_337/24facebook_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/business/24facebook_337/24facebook_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/business/24facebook_337/24facebook_337-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/business/24facebook_337/24facebook_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/24/business/24facebook_337/24facebook_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/business/24facebook_337/24facebook_337-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook Reorients Itself for a Small-Screen World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Facebook Reorients Itself for a Small-Screen World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T17:05:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10964756-ef16-5e72-b89c-848f360cc73f', 'word_count': 1185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10964756-ef16-5e72-b89c-848f360cc73f'}, {'abstract': 'Sony has purchased a 20 percent equity stake in Scott Sanders Theatrical Productions as it seeks to mount stage versions of the studio’s films, with their first project being a musical adaptation of the 1982 Dustin Hoffman comedy “Tootsie.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/sony-pictures-the-latest-studio-to-make-broadway-push/', 'snippet': 'Sony has purchased a 20 percent equity stake in Scott Sanders Theatrical Productions as it seeks to mount stage versions of the studio’s films, with their first project being a musical adaptation of the 1982 Dustin Hoffman comedy “Tootsie.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sony Pictures Entertainment has signed a five-year deal with the Broadway producer Scott Sanders (“Evita,” “The Color Purple”) to mount stage versions of the studio’s films, with their first project being a musical adaptation of the 1982 Dustin Hoffman comedy “Tootsie.” The deal, which was announced on Thursday, represents the latest move by several Hollywood film studios to capitalize on theatergoers’ appetite – particularly tourists visiting New York – for musicals based on movies or books; most Broadway musicals these days are adaptations, like the top-grossing shows “Wicked” and “The Lion King” and new hits like the Tony Award winner “Once” and the Disney musical “Newsies.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sony Pictures the Latest Studio to Make Broadway Push', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sony Pictures on Broadway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Scott (1957- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Pictures Entertainment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T17:15:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/993f9301-032f-5175-9a2d-0f2e109d0ac5', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/993f9301-032f-5175-9a2d-0f2e109d0ac5'}, {'abstract': 'The anonymous Navy SEAL member who wrote the book remained anonymous for less than 24 hours.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/fox-news-purports-to-identify-author-of-book-on-bin-laden-raid/', 'snippet': 'The anonymous Navy SEAL member who wrote the book remained anonymous for less than 24 hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The anonymous Navy SEAL member who has written a book about the raid that killed Osama bin Laden remained anonymous for less than 24 hours.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Author of Book on Bin Laden Raid Is Identified', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Owen, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T17:20:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman and Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49cbb1e1-247f-570a-b2bf-069bce982482', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49cbb1e1-247f-570a-b2bf-069bce982482'}, {'abstract': 'A report from the Natural Resources Defense Council says that much of the food produced for Americans goes unused, wasting water and the other resources that go into producing it.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/report-finds-americans-wasteful-of-food/', 'snippet': 'A report from the Natural Resources Defense Council says that much of the food produced for Americans goes unused, wasting water and the other resources that go into producing it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forty percent of the food Americans have available to them goes uneaten, according to a report released this week by the Natural Resources Defense Council. Most of this nutrient-rich uneaten food ends up rotting in landfills.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Report Finds Americans Wasteful of Food', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None,