rganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52f455cf-f263-544d-9eca-0898769140ca', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52f455cf-f263-544d-9eca-0898769140ca'}, {'abstract': 'Another reason, besides the housing bust, that those nearing retirement age may have suffered most from the financial crisis: a nearly 10 percent decline in household income in three years.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/big-income-losses-for-those-near-retirement/', 'snippet': 'Another reason, besides the housing bust, that those nearing retirement age may have suffered most from the financial crisis: a nearly 10 percent decline in household income in three years.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:24 p.m. | Updated with additional details.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Income Losses for Those Near Retirement', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Income Losses Hit Those Near Retirement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T18:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/def92074-e8e0-5b77-b20a-52df18e0714f', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/def92074-e8e0-5b77-b20a-52df18e0714f'}, {'abstract': 'Along with their credits as film producers, Mr. Zadan and Mr. Meron have worked in television.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/craig-zadan-and-neil-meron-to-produce-academy-awards-show/', 'snippet': 'Along with their credits as film producers, Mr. Zadan and Mr. Meron have worked in television.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The next Oscar show has found its producers, and they are a very musical pair. Craig Zadan and Neil Meron, whose films include the musicals “Chicago” and “Hairspray,” have agreed to produce the 85th Academy Awards ceremony, set for Feb. 24, the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences said on Thursday. Along with their credits as film producers, Mr. Zadan and Mr. Meron have worked in television, where their series include “Drop Dead Diva” and “Smash,” and on Broadway, where they were producers of the revived “How to Succeed in Business Without Really Trying” and “Promises, Promises.” The recruiting of Mr. Zadan and Mr. Meron was the first major step by Hawk Koch, who was elected president of the Academy earlier this month.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Craig Zadan and Neil Meron to Produce Academy Awards Show', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Producers Named for Oscars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meron, Neil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zadan, Craig', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACADEMY OF MOTION PICTURE ARTS AND SCIENCES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T18:07:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc43848e-b8fc-5a53-b350-819532580f57', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc43848e-b8fc-5a53-b350-819532580f57'}, {'abstract': 'The critically-acclaimed play about wrongfully convicted inmates on death row will return to the theater where it ran 10 years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/the-exonerated-to-be-revived-at-the-culture-project/', 'snippet': 'The critically-acclaimed play about wrongfully convicted inmates on death row will return to the theater where it ran 10 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Exonerated,” a critically acclaimed play about wrongfully convicted survivors of death row, which had star-filled casts for its Off Broadway run from 2002 to 2004, will return for a seven-week run starting Sept. 15 at the Culture Project, its artistic director announced on Thursday. The production will once again feature a rotating cast of stars – including Stockard Channing, Brian Dennehy and Brooke Shields – who will read accounts by former death row inmates.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Exonerated’ to Be Revived at the Culture Project', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘The Exonerated’ To Be Revived', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Culture Project', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T18:11:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organizat