1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc9f7fac-885c-5fb0-b622-fba2721d5f8f', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc9f7fac-885c-5fb0-b622-fba2721d5f8f'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Reserve Bank of New York said on Thursday that it had wound down the final remnant of its rescue of the American International Group, generating a multibillion-dollar profit in the process.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/new-york-fed-sells-off-last-a-i-g-related-holdings/', 'snippet': 'The Federal Reserve Bank of New York said on Thursday that it had wound down the final remnant of its rescue of the American International Group, generating a multibillion-dollar profit in the process.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:31 p.m. | Updated The government is one step closer to shedding its burden from the financial crisis.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Fed Sells Off Last A.I.G.-Related Holdings', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York Fed Sells Last Of Its A.I.G. Bailout Bonds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN INTERNATIONAL GROUP INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve Bank of New York', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T19:03:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15bc4e0e-6a37-54e0-a474-d4e0830f6798', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15bc4e0e-6a37-54e0-a474-d4e0830f6798'}, {'abstract': 'The mushroom huntress gathers her friends for a 4-course morel-focused meal.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/edible-selby-the-big-morel-cookout-with-connie-green/', 'snippet': 'The mushroom huntress gathers her friends for a 4-course morel-focused meal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this sequel to The Selby’s last film, which follows the mushroom huntress Connie Green and the chef Sean O’Toole on a search for edible fungus in California’s high Sierras, Green gathers her friends — “the tribal members of this mushroom hunting cult,” she calls them — for a four-course morel-focused meal. Joining her and O’Toole at the outside table: Chef Hiro Sone of Terra Restaurant in Napa, Calif., who prepares a tartine of foie gras-stuffed morels in a crayfish sauce; the pastry chef and restaurateur Lissa Doumani, also of Terra, and Ame in San Francisco, who makes morels stuffed with lamb kibbe; the Kitchen Door‘s chef, Todd Humphries, who serves morels stuffed with bratwurst; and Chef Staffan Terje of Perbacco and Barbacco, cooking porcinis and peaches. Click here to see more of what’s on the menu.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Edible Selby | The Big Morel Cookout With Connie Green', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T19:03:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Selby', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Selby'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/426a944d-5d51-5982-9976-dfa4418c27d6', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/426a944d-5d51-5982-9976-dfa4418c27d6'}, {'abstract': 'Confirmed by the fiscal cliff stuff.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/nobody-cares-about-the-deficit/', 'snippet': 'Confirmed by the fiscal cliff stuff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dave Weigel makes a good point: there’s a huge inconsistency between the way Republicans are responding to the new CBO report on the fiscal cliff and everything they’ve been saying for the past two years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nobody Cares About the Deficit', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T19:08:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a17c5a1a-e28a-5059-ab5d-695d1fea8bae', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a17c5a1a-e28a-5059-ab5d-695d1fea8bae'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Murray was placed in Roger Federer’s half of the draw at the United States Open, meaning they could meet in the semifinals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/sports/tennis/at-us-open-federer-murray-rematch-could-come-earlier.html', 'snippet': 'Andy Murray was placed in Roger Federer’s half of the draw at the United States Open, meaning they could meet in the semifinals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before the United States Open draw on Thursday, Brad Gilbert, a coach and commentator, asked the same question as everyone else in tennis. The “big, $64,000 question,” he called it — five words that would produce an answer crucial to this tournament.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/sports/tennis/tennis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': 