l. In Gillian Flynn’s “Gone Girl” — at No. 1 in its 11th week on the hardcover fiction list — a young wife disappears from her home on the morning of her fifth anniversary. Paula Bomer’s “Nine Months,” published on Aug. 21, features a pregnant painter who abandons her family and takes off on a debauched cross-country trip. And new on the extended hardcover fiction list at No. 18 is Maria Semple’s “Where’d You Go, Bernadette,” in which a renowned, reclusive and very cranky architect vanishes, leaving her 15-year-old daughter to piece together the clues.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/books/review/26semple/26semple-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 228, 'width': 223, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/books/review/26semple/26semple-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 228, 'width': 223, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/books/review/26semple/26semple-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/books/review/26semple/26semple-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/books/review/26semple/26semple-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'TBR: Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books 