08/23/at-lambstock-2012-fire-bourbon-and-fat-back/', 'snippet': 'There were no tickets for this annual camping trip in Virginia for chefs and farmers. Just tents and R.V.’s, a huge bonfire, and a simple pavilion for cooking and gathering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What do you get when you blend a Southern revival and an episode of “Top Chef” with a pinch of summer camp and prison break, all dry rubbed and left to cook on the spit?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Lambstock 2012, Fire, Bourbon and Fat Back', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T19:43:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Tesauro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tesauro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b34b8527-6503-5a0d-9d91-decdf41b3e02', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b34b8527-6503-5a0d-9d91-decdf41b3e02'}, {'abstract': 'Last year, a number of private equity-owned businesses in Egypt, in sectors like health care and power, increased their earnings by 40 percent or more, driven by surprising consumer spending.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/private-equity-firms-stimulate-earnings-and-deals-in-post-revolution-egypt/', 'snippet': 'Last year, a number of private equity-owned businesses in Egypt, in sectors like health care and power, increased their earnings by 40 percent or more, driven by surprising consumer spending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBAI — After Abraaj Capital bought a stake in AlBorg Laboratories in May 2008, the Dubai-based private equity firm braced for a rough ride. Over the next four years, AlBorg, an Egyptian medical testing company, weathered the global financial crisis, the economic downturn and the revolutions that swept the Mideast.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Private Equity Firms Stimulate Earnings and Deals in Post-Revolution Egypt', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Private Equity Stimulates Sectors in Post-Revolution Egypt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T19:50:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Hamdan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamdan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bb61753-c4cc-5e62-aef3-38471f7c738a', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bb61753-c4cc-5e62-aef3-38471f7c738a'}, {'abstract': 'Up to half of practicing doctors say they experience emotional exhaustion, detachment or a low sense of accomplishment, putting patients and doctors at risk, a new study reports.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/the-widespread-problem-of-doctor-burnout/', 'snippet': 'Up to half of practicing doctors say they experience emotional exhaustion, detachment or a low sense of accomplishment, putting patients and doctors at risk, a new study reports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The patient, a powerfully built middle-aged restaurant worker, had awakened one morning with a tight pain in his shoulders that traveled down his right arm. At work, he could barely shrug his shoulders or turn his head. “My fingers were so weak,” he recalled, “that I couldn’t even get a good grip around a glass of water.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/23/health/23chen/23chen-articleLarge.jpg', 'heigh