'Chen', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b21610d3-b493-5681-a2ab-61e6f19522b2', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b21610d3-b493-5681-a2ab-61e6f19522b2'}, {'abstract': 'A block party and food festival this weekend features a balut-eating contest, so City Room got a lesson in how to eat this dish.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/sampling-a-filipino-dish-theyll-be-competing-to-gulp-down/', 'snippet': 'A block party and food festival this weekend features a balut-eating contest, so City Room got a lesson in how to eat this dish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Balut, a perennial contender on any Westerner’s list of extreme foods, is consumed in the Philippines as naturally as hamburgers are here. It’s a fertilized duck egg, a Franken-snack complete with partially developed bones, veins and eyes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sampling a Filipino Specialty They’ll Be Competing to Gulp Down', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filipino-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T19:57:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Vadukul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vadukul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/764b708c-8571-5928-afe2-3b5a298465a0', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/764b708c-8571-5928-afe2-3b5a298465a0'}, {'abstract': 'Why would Ban-Ki-moon attend an international gathering in Iran?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/baiting-the-anti-u-n-crowd/', 'snippet': 'Why would Ban-Ki-moon attend an international gathering in Iran?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have always been a supporter of the United Nations. Despite its shortcomings, it has proven its worth again and again, from its role in the creation of Israel, to keeping the peace in countless global hotspots, to intervening in humanitarian crises.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Baiting the Anti-U.N. Crowd', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban Ki-moon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T20:01:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1948b4dc-22fb-5a35-8a78-fb4533dd6a9c', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1948b4dc-22fb-5a35-8a78-fb4533dd6a9c'}, {'abstract': 'The authorities banned three neo-Nazi groups and raided homes and meeting places in an effort to break up an aggressive network of far-right extremists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/world/europe/germany-cracks-down-on-neo-nazis.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities banned three neo-Nazi groups and raided homes and meeting places in an effort to break up an aggressive network of far-right extremists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — The authorities in Germany banned three known neo-Nazi groups and raided dozens of members’ homes and meeting places in the western state of North Rhine-Westphalia on Thursday, in an effort to break up an aggressive network of far-right extremists.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'German Raid Cracks Down on Neo-Nazis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'German Raid Cracks Down On Neo-Nazis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Neo Nazi Groups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Democratic Party (Germany)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T20:09:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Eddy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f41fd97-7982-5273-b5af-efacf362a300', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f41fd97-7982-5273-b5af-efacf362a300'}, {'abstract': 'Jonathan Miller, who came to the company in 2009 to help manage the company’s tech investments and steer its brands into the digital age, had some tough assignments, including trying to turn around MySpace.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/news-corp-s-chief-digital-officer-to-step-down-as-company-prepares-to-split/', 'snippet': 'Jonathan Miller, who came to the company in 2009 to help manage the company’s tech investments and steer its brands into the digital age, had some tough assignments, including trying to turn around MySpace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'News Corporation’s chief digital officer, Jonathan Miller, will step down, the company announced on Thursday, in the latest example of an executive departing since News Corporation said it would split the publishing business from the rest of the company. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Corp.’s Chief Digital Officer to Step Down as Company Prepares to Split', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Jonathan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T20:13:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e211aaaa-244a-55d2-8aba-4f99a7e61738', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e211aaaa-244a-55d2-8aba-4f99a7e61738'}, {'abstract': 'Some people have wondered if my dog is a wolf, but he is just a quivering, clumsy pet whose response to human troubles is always the same.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/fashion/dog-anchors-man-facing-setbacks.html', 'snippet': 'Some people have wondered if my dog is a wolf, but he is just a quivering, clumsy pet whose response to human troubles is always the same.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN I met the dog, he was sitting in a cage to my left as I entered a local animal shelter near the running path I frequent in downtown Austin, Texas. I had no intention to adopt a dog. I only stopped for a drink of cold water. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image