izations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Colorado Rockies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T21:32:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ca64938-488c-5108-8749-f6ee21f60de6', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ca64938-488c-5108-8749-f6ee21f60de6'}, {'abstract': 'A new tool allows Facebook users to buy goods and services on their mobile phones — and allows Facebook to bypass sharing revenues with rivals like Apple and Google.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/deal-will-allow-one-tap-purchases-through-facebook/', 'snippet': 'A new tool allows Facebook users to buy goods and services on their mobile phones — and allows Facebook to bypass sharing revenues with rivals like Apple and Google.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bango, a British company that few will have heard of on this side of the Atlantic, wants to help Facebook make money on mobile devices — not by showing advertisements, but by making it easy to buy things when you log into Facebook on your phone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deal Will Allow One-Tap Purchases Through Facebook', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T21:33:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/289dd388-63f4-54fd-80f5-e02308c4ca08', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/289dd388-63f4-54fd-80f5-e02308c4ca08'}, {'abstract': 'In “Little White Lies” a group of friends journey to Cap Ferrat for their annual communal vacation despite a life-threatening accident that lands one of them in intensive care.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/movies/little-white-lies-from-guillaume-canet-with-jean-dujardin.html', 'snippet': 'In “Little White Lies” a group of friends journey to Cap Ferrat for their annual communal vacation despite a life-threatening accident that lands one of them in intensive care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Guillaume Canet’s “Little White Lies” delivers a two-and-a-half-hour scolding to so-called “bobos,” the term in France for affluent people who embrace a fusion of bourgeois and bohemian values. Although the word “bobo” has been used by David Brooks, a columnist for The New York Times, to describe “members of the new information elite,” in France it refers to overgrown Parisian yuppies in their 30s and 40s, like the group of bickering friends in “Little White Lies” who take a communal vacation every summer in Cap Ferrat. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24LITTLE_SPAN/24LITTLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24LITTLE_SPAN/24LITTLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24LITTLE_SPAN/24LITTLE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24LITTLE_SPAN/24LITTLE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24LITTLE_SPAN/24LITTLE_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24LITTLE_SPAN/24LITTLE_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24LITTLE_SPAN/24LITTLE_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'By the Sea, by the Sea, Rivalries and Conflicts', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'By the Sea, by the Sea, Rivalries and Conflicts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotillard, Marion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cluzet, Francois', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dujardin, Jean', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Little White Lies (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Canet, Guillaume', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T21:35:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastnam