: 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b590956-2586-50b3-8ef4-a828e1d55e7a', 'word_count': 1026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b590956-2586-50b3-8ef4-a828e1d55e7a'}, {'abstract': 'The buyer is Townsquare Media, which already owns 244 radio stations in small markets and a collection of music Web sites.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/mog-an-online-music-service-sells-its-ad-network-for-10-million/', 'snippet': 'The buyer is Townsquare Media, which already owns 244 radio stations in small markets and a collection of music Web sites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, half of the digital music company Mog was sold to Beats Electronics, the company behind the popular Beats by Dr. Dre headphones. Now the other half, an advertising network for music Web sites, has been sold as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mog, an Online Music Service, Sells Its Ad Network for $10 Million', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dre, Dr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iovine, Jimmy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beats Electronics', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mog', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations'