otels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Long before I’d actually visited one, I thought I knew what the ideal European town should look like. On snowy school-vacation afternoons in Westchester, N.Y., my grandmother would pull down from the shelves a beautifully illustrated German or English storybook she’d grown up with and suggest we get “cozy.” (This meant hot chocolate for my brother and me and a tumbler of sherry with rattling ice cubes for her.) In these Victorian volumes, there was always a castle on a mountain in the middle of the city, which would be cut in half by a swan-dotted river, and ham- or mustard-colored houses. Cobbled streets led to squares with four-spout stone fountains. Off-duty soldiers would be flirting with buxom barmaids, clergymen would be patting children on their heads (and not elsewhere), and housewives would be pinning hand-scrubbed sheets to lines run between old lilac bushes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eurofile | Loving Ljubljana', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T22:05:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Lobrano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lobrano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94b57d48-d282-5135-b79a-731d1f198917', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94b57d48-d282-5135-b79a-731d1f198917'}, {'abstract': 'Investing in student housing may not only help reduce room-and-board expenses, but also provide a revenue source, and in some cases a tax deduction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/realestate/mortgages-financing-student-housing.html', 'snippet': 'Investing in student housing may not only help reduce room-and-board expenses, but also provide a revenue source, and in some cases a tax deduction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS college students prepare for fall classes, some of their parents or grandparents will be studying up on the real estate markets near campus. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/realestate/26mort-graphic/26mort-graphic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 302, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/realestate/26mort-graphic/26mort-graphic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 302}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/realestate/26mort-graphic/26mort-graphic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 577, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/realestate/26mort-graphic/26mort-graphic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1154, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/realestate/26mort-graphic/26mort-graphic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/realestate/26mort-graphic/26mort-graphic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/realestate/26mort-graphic/26mort-graphic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Financing Student Housing', 'kicker': 'Mortgages'