ed-univision-turns-to-candidate-forums/', 'snippet': 'The Spanish language network said Thursday that it will broadcast separate “Meet the Candidate” forums with President Obama and Gov. Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Univision’s request for an official presidential debate may have been rejected, but the Spanish language network has succeeded in securing both candidates’ attendance at “Meet the Candidate” forums, the network said late Thursday afternoon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debates Denied, Univision Turns to Candidate Forums', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spanish Language', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Falco, Randy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramos, Jorge', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commission on Presidential Debates', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Hispanic Center', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Univision', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T22:32:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16c5f409-dcc3-55b4-886e-7ddc495f6432', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16c5f409-dcc3-55b4-886e-7ddc495f6432'}, {'abstract': 'The Harvard Club on West 44th Street is a holdout on what was once a block of clubs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/realestate/the-harvard-club-streetscapes-the-clubbiest-club-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'The Harvard Club on West 44th Street is a holdout on what was once a block of clubs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN July the prim neo-Georgian Harvard Club of 1894, on 44th Street between Fifth and the Avenue of the Americas, lifted its veil of construction netting. Newly spruced up, it’s the oldest club on what was once a block of such institutions, including New York Yacht and Yale. Most of the clubs are gone, but Harvard expanded twice, and in 2003 built a controversial third addition that has only recently lost its novelty. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/realestate/26STREETS2_SPAN/26STREETS2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/realestate/26STREETS2_SPAN/26STREETS2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/realestate/26STREETS2_SPAN/26STREETS2_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/realestate/26STREETS2_SPAN/26STREETS2_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/realestate/26STREETS2_SPAN/26STREETS2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/realestate/26STREETS2_SPAN/26STREETS2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/realestate/26STREETS2_SPAN/26STREETS2_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Clubbiest Club in New York’', 'kicker': 'Streetscapes/The Harvard Club', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘The Clubbiest Club in New York’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKim, Charles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard Club', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-23T22:37:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Gray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0eb1911-4305-5baa-9158-09c71c23cbf9', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0eb1911-4305-5baa-9158-09c71c23cbf9'}, {'abstract': 'In “Sleepwalk With Me,” a movie that the comic performer and writer Mike Birbiglia adapted from his one-man show, a slightly schlubby comedian takes his act on the road.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/movies/sleepwalk-with-me-by-the-comedian-mike-birbiglia.html', 'snippet': 'In “Sleepwalk With Me,” a movie that the comic performer and writer Mike Birbiglia adapted from his one-man show, a slightly schlubby comedian takes his act on the road.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It takes a kind of crazy tenacity for an aspiring stand-up comedian to endure the grubby humiliations of life on the bottom rung of the professional ladder. Watching Matt Pandamiglio, the jocular, slightly schlubby alter ego of the comic performer and writer Mike Birbiglia, take his act on the road in “Sleepwalk With Me” is like observing an out-of-shape military recruit stumbling through the first week of boot camp. Survival depends less on talent than on having a thick enough skin to recover after every setback and still maintain a facade of genial equanimity. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24SLEEP_SPAN/24SLEEP_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24SLEEP_SPAN/24SLEEP_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24SLEEP_SPAN/0824SLEEP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24SLEEP_SPAN/0824SLEEP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1303, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'im