in the number of refugees that Australia accepts yearly, part of an immigration reform package aimed at encouraging migrants to use official channels for asylum rather than long and dangerous boat journeys. The increase in the annual refugee intake — to 20,000 from 13,700, the biggest increase in 30 years — capped two weeks of debate that led Ms. Gillard’s governing Labor Party to reverse its longstanding opposition to reopening remote offshore detention centers. Those were closed in 2007. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Australia Increases Refugee Quota', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Australia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President Increases Refugee Quota', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillard, Julia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T00:05:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Siegel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siegel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a8714e2-5ca7-574f-a016-b317d05bdc3e', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a8714e2-5ca7-574f-a016-b317d05bdc3e'}, {'abstract': 'A good-time romp in the great outdoors goes very wrong in “The Victim.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/movies/the-victim-grind-house-film-directed-by-michael-biehn.html', 'snippet': 'A good-time romp in the great outdoors goes very wrong in “The Victim.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whenever anyone in a movie announces a desire for a quiet life, we know what follows will be 