Wayward Women, Menacing Men and a Cabin in the Woods', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Victim', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Victim (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biehn, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T00:13:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/217ffcb4-0fce-5aa3-b982-82972323bb1c', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/217ffcb4-0fce-5aa3-b982-82972323bb1c'}, {'abstract': 'Two polls of the Missouri Senate race since Representative Todd Akin’s remarks about rape showed a large number of Republicans who were not willing to declare their support for him or Claire McCaskill.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/republican-voters-could-sit-out-missouri-senate-race/', 'snippet': 'Two polls of the Missouri Senate race since Representative Todd Akin’s remarks about rape showed a large number of Republicans who were not willing to declare their support for him or Claire McCaskill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So far, we’ve had two polls of the Missouri Senate race since Representative Todd Akin made his remarks about rape on Sunday. The first survey, conducted by Public Policy Polling on Monday night, had Mr. Akin holding onto a one-point advantage in the race. But a second poll, conducted Wednesday night by Rasmussen Reports, had his opponent, the Democratic incumbent Claire McCaskill, up by 10 percentage points instead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Voters Could Sit Out Missouri Senate Race', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T00:19:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16b1bae3-4b5d-5205-9121-aa37a8d7d2bf', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16b1bae3-4b5d-5205-9121-aa37a8d7d2bf'}, {'abstract': 'In “Knight Knight” a pair of dim knights try to rescue an imprisoned princess, unfurling many droll anachronisms and comic observations on the medieval era in the process.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/movies/knight-knight-directed-by-christina-bucher.html', 'snippet': 'In “Knight Knight” a pair of dim knights try to rescue an imprisoned princess, unfurling many droll anachronisms and comic observations on the medieval era in the process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The castles look terrific in Christina Bucher’s “Knight Knight,” as do the costumes and the British sunlight. And certainly the actors deliver in this light satire of the Middle Ages, in which two dim knights of the post-Arthur period, Gilbert (David Wayman) and Edgar (Tom Eykelhof), attempt to rescue the hardheaded Princess Katrina (Ms. Bucher), a prisoner of the portly, blustery King Vince (Nick von Schlippe). The script, by Nicholas Horwood, is packed with droll anachronisms and comic observations on the medieval era, as well as amusing twists: Each hero successfully escapes the castle, only to have to return. When Edgar proposes to Rachael (Claira Watson Parr), half-sister of Katrina, she replies: “What? God, no. I mean, sorry, I’ve got a boyfriend.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24RDP_KNIGHT_SPAN/24RDP_KNIGHT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24RDP_KNIGHT_SPAN/24RDP_KNIGHT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24RDP_KNIGHT_SPAN/0824KNIGHT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24RDP_KNIGHT_SPAN/0824KNIGHT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24RDP_KNIGHT_SPAN/24RDP_KNIGHT_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24RDP_KNIGHT_SPAN/24RDP_KNIGHT_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/arts/24RDP_KNIGHT_SPAN/24RDP_KNIGHT_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Novice Knights: Now, What Was That Quest?', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knight Knight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bucher, Christina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'