idered/', 'snippet': 'Government regulators are considering invoking powers that were granted by the Dodd-Frank law to improve oversight of the money market fund industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the failure of one effort to overhaul a major part of the mutual fund industry, top government officials worked on Thursday to find alternative ways to rein in what they see as a systemic threat to the financial system.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Effort to Curb Money Market Funds, a Plan B Is Considered', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In an Effort to Curb Money Market Funds, a Plan B Is Considered', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Money Market Accounts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geithner, Timothy F', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schapiro, Mary L', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Stability Oversight Council', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T00:56:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis and Nathaniel Popper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None