istical and scheduling complications will prevent those involved with “Mies Julie” from bringing the show to New York in January.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/mies-julie-wins-best-of-edinburgh-fringe-award/', 'snippet': 'Logistical and scheduling complications will prevent those involved with “Mies Julie” from bringing the show to New York in January.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Mies Julie,” a smoldering South African stage adaptation of August Strindberg’s 1888 drama “Miss Julie,” won the ninth annual Carol Tambor Best of Edinburgh award, to be presented Friday in Scotland. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Mies Julie’ Wins Best of Edinburgh Fringe Award', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Edinburgh Winner(s) Announced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Edinburgh Festival Fringe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T02:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8c92c4c-9fc7-5fb2-87ae-4161995f2f85', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8c92c4c-9fc7-5fb2-87ae-4161995f2f85'}, {'abstract': 'After a loss on Wednesday, Borussia Mönchengladbach will soon be knocked out of the Champions League. Where the club goes from there will depend entirely on the lessons they take from the encounter.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/23/borussia-monchengladbach-learns-a-champions-league-lesson/', 'snippet': 'After a loss on Wednesday, Borussia Mönchengladbach will soon be knocked out of the Champions League. Where the club goes from there will depend entirely on the lessons they take from the encounter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Soccer, like any sport, is nothing more than emotional theater — demonstrated, in this case, through the physical act of 22 men chasing a round ball around a park. As such it often leads the typical fan down a bumpy path where turmoil and ecstasy go hand in hand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Borussia Monchengladbach Learns a Champions League Lesson', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA Champions League (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BORUSSIA MONCHENGLADBACH', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T02:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stefan Bienkowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stefan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bienkowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/315bd9b4-f899-5682-a660-ca17a31d4da0', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/315bd9b4-f899-5682-a660-ca17a31d4da0'}, {'abstract': 'A man who shot his wife to death in an I.C.U. in Akron has been charged with murder, but friends say he was acting out of compassion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/us/ohio-shooting-raises-questions-about-mercy-killings.html', 'snippet': 'A man who shot his wife to death in an I.C.U. in Akron has been charged with murder, but friends say he was acting out of compassion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MASSILLON, Ohio — John Wise tipped the taxi driver $25 that night, even though the driver had been late to pick him up and late getting him to Akron General hospital, about 30 miles north of this former steel town. Why he had to get there with such urgency the driver did not know, and did not ask, but before driving away, he wished Mr. Wise luck. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/us/MERCY-1/MERCY-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/us/MERCY-1/MERCY-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/us/MERCY-1/MERCY-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/24/us/MERCY-1/MERCY-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/us/MERCY-1/MERCY-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ohio Man’s Shooting of Ailing Wife Raises Questions About ‘Mercy Killings’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ohio Man’s Shooting of Ailing Wife Raises Questions About ‘Mercy Killings’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wise, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wise, Barbara', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Living Wills and Health Care Proxies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T02:11:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ray Rivera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rivera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c51e8dd-e894-59c1-b3a3-e7d4ddb48ac5', 'word_count': 1159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c51e8dd-e894-59c1-b3a3-e7d4ddb48ac5'}, {'abstract': 'Padraig Harrington, an Irishman who turns 41 next week, shot a seven-under-par 64 for a one-stroke lead at the Barclays, despite the attention focused on Tiger Woods and Rory McIlory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/sports/golf/at-barclays-tiger-woods-and-rory-mcilroy-get-attention-but-padraig-harrington-leads.html', 'snippet': 'Padraig Harrington, an Irishman who turns 41 next week, shot a seven-under-par 64 for a one-stroke lead at the Barclays, despite the attention focused on Tiger Woods and Rory McIlory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FARMINGDALE, N.Y. — Thousands of spectators fanned out on the back nine of the Black Course at Bethpage State Park on Thursday morning to watch the first PGA Tour pairing of Tiger Woods and his latest heir apparent, Rory McIlroy. They planted themselves along the gallery ropes and broke the birdsong with cries of “We love ya, baby!” for Woods and observations like “Rory’s much slighter than I thought” and “How can you not be a Rory fan?” ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/sports/sub-y-golf/sub-y-golf-jumbo.jpg', '