I. has redefined the crime of rape and is studying how to improve the way it collects data on sexual assaults.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Representative Todd Akin of Missouri said in an interview broadcast on Sunday that rape victims rarely get pregnant, he set off an outraged national discussion. Embedded, if unexamined, in all the talk is the rapidly shifting definition of rape, the history of the derided but longstanding term “forcible rape,” and the wildly varied databases on sexual assault.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/us/RAPE/RAPE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/us/RAPE/RAPE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Candidate’s Stumble on a Distressing Crime', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Candidate’s Stumble On a Distressing Crime', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akin, Todd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T02:26:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}]