pecially as the number of foreign forces in Afghanistan begins to decrease. The training program is a central part of America’s withdrawal strategy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Insider Attacks’ Target Afghans and Foreign Forces', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allen, John R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T03:53:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffery DelViscio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffery', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DelViscio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15f18f1f-e2e1-5b55-a850-f6f5987873b2', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15f18f1f-e2e1-5b55-a850-f6f5987873b2'}, {'abstract': 'Chinese state-controlled media acknowledged on Thursday that the country was actively developing mobile Dongfeng-41 intercontinental ballistic missiles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/world/asia/china-more-advanced-missiles-are-said-to-be-on-the-horizon.html', 'snippet': 'Chinese state-controlled media acknowledged on Thursday that the country was actively developing mobile Dongfeng-41 intercontinental ballistic missiles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chinese state-controlled media acknowledged on Thursday that the country was actively developing mobile Dongfeng-41 intercontinental ballistic missiles, and seemed to hint that they might have multiple warheads. But a Chinese military expert denied to The Global Times, a newspaper controlled by the Communist Party, that the missile had already been tested last month. Multiple re-entry vehicles on a ballistic missile, each of which can carry a nuclear warhead, make it much harder for missile defense systems to stop an attack. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: More Advanced Missiles Are Said to Be on the Horizon', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: More Advanced Missiles Are Said to Be on the Horizon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Missiles and Missile Defense Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T03:58:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b126ca0-5ef0-5532-ab92-756eb4eaf059', 'word_count': 81, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b126ca0-5ef0-5532-ab92-756eb4eaf059'}, {'abstract': 'The former Navy SEAL member who has written a firsthand account of the raid that killed Osama bin Laden has been identified as Matt Bissonnette.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/business/media/bin-laden-raids-firsthand-chronicler-is-unmasked.html', 'snippet': 'The former Navy SEAL member who has written a firsthand account of the raid that killed Osama bin Laden has been identified as Matt Bissonnette.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anonymity was short-lived for the former Navy SEAL member who has written a first-person account of the raid that killed Osama b