ecessarily excite in late August.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fire Meets Its Match: Spices', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T12:19:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19475822-3e29-5526-9640-c027aa5e0162', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19475822-3e29-5526-9640-c027aa5e0162'}, {'abstract': 'The prospect of a visit from Hillary Clinton puts a small Pacific island in a tizzy.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/cook-islands-is-in-a-tizzy-over-possible-visit-from-hillary/', 'snippet': 'The prospect of a visit from Hillary Clinton puts a small Pacific island in a tizzy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RAROTONGA, Cook Islands — Not since Queen Elizabeth II’s hello to this remote part of her realm four decades ago have the inhabitants of Rarotonga, the largest of the Cook Islands, made such a fuss for a visitor. Hillary Clinton is expected next week for the Pacific Island Forum.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guess Who’s Coming to Dinner', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cook Islands', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T12:22:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Luke Hunt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Luke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hunt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'o