, it’s likely that there will be calls for more radical steps.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/the-hard-choices-ahead-for-h-p/', 'snippet': 'Since February, the value of Hewlett-Packard has fallen by 40 percent, about one-quarter of that from Tuesday to Thursday of this week. If things don’t improve soon, though, it’s likely that there will be calls for more radical steps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How soon before the next big, tough decision at Hewlett-Packard? It could be as early as October.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/23/technology/bits/bitpix-hp-whitman/bitpix-hp-whitman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/23/technology/bits/bitpix-hp-whitman/bitpix-hp-whitman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/23/technology/bits/bitpix-hp-whitman/bitpix-hp-whitman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/04/23/technology/bits/bitpix-hp-whitman/bitpix-hp-whitman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/23/technology/bits/bitpix-hp-whitman/bitpix-hp-whitman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hard Choices Ahead for H.P.', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Stock Sputters, Hard Choices Ahead for H.P.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitman, Margaret C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hewlett-Packard Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T12:53:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa7d1124-4084-5fae-8862-a4abf0f0a78d', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa7d1124-4084-5fae-8862-a4abf0f0a78d'}, {'abstract': 'The Seattle restaurant’s annual board meeting is as much about bonding as it is business.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/at-canlis-dinner-with-a-side-of-camaraderie/', 'snippet': 'The Seattle restaurant’s annual board meeting is as much about bonding as it is business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last summer, Mark and Brian Canlis — the co-owners of the Seattle restaurant Canlis — mounted two horses near Pryor, Mont., and proceeded, on Day 1 of their annual board meeting, to chase off a couple of bears. They rode out of the barn on the 200,000-acre S Ranch, an hour south of Billings, with their board members, all close confidants of the family, including a tech entrepreneur (and childhood neighbor), a restaurant owner and hotelier (a college classmate), and a finance executive who introduced Mark to his wife and insisted on only being called “Big Steve.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Canlis, Dinner With a Side of Camaraderie', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headl