g mate, Mitt Romney tapped a congressman with a long and sometimes contentious legislative record.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/with-ryan-romney-loses-claim-to-outsider-status/', 'snippet': 'In choosing Paul D. Ryan to be his running mate, Mitt Romney tapped a congressman with a long and sometimes contentious legislative record.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:02 p.m. | Updated ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Ryan, Romney Loses Claim to Outsider Status', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Political Memo: By Adding Ryan as Running Mate, Romney Loses Outsider Status', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T13:02:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cf880e3-bb93-58c3-b078-e2e4d4b10391', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cf880e3-bb93-58c3-b078-e2e4d4b10391'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the writers and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/what-were-reading-252/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the writers and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': '@PressSec: As Brewgate continues to ferment, Jay Carney, the White House press secretary, promises to release the presidential beer recipe if enough people sign a petition asking for it. –Pete Wells', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T13:07:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/280afe8c-72ba-5b07-9a37-8d6903355f09', 'word_count': 448, 'uri': 'nyt://article/280afe8c-72ba-5b07-9a37-8d6903355f09'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook’s executives say the company is diving deep into mobile and trying to transform itself into a “mobile first” company. Developing mobile products has become a priority, they said, and every team inside the company has been reorganized with the goal of inserting mobile into its DNA.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/daily-report-facebook-tries-to-go-mobile-first/', 'snippet': 'Facebook’s executives say the company is diving deep into mobile and trying to transform itself into a “mobile first” company. Developing mobile products has become a priority, they said, and every team inside the company has been reorganized with...', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Facebook, mobile is on everyone’s mind, Brian X. Chen reports in Friday’s New York Times. People are now spending more time using Facebook through mobile apps than on computers. And on Wall Street, investors are putting pressure on Mark Zuckerberg’s social network to master the mobile world so it can speed up growth and lift its sagging stock.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlar