teps Out', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T13:31:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/928531d5-7ecd-5d24-bf80-3e868056c851', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/928531d5-7ecd-5d24-bf80-3e868056c851'}, {'abstract': 'Nathan Tinkler, an Australian coal magnate, has abandoned a $5.4 billion bid for the coal mining company, amid investor concern about Australia’s mining sector.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/australian-magnate-abandons-bid-for-whitehaven-coal/', 'snippet': 'Nathan Tinkler, an Australian coal magnate, has abandoned a $5.4 billion bid for the coal mining company, amid investor concern about Australia’s mining sector.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An effort to stage a buyout of Whitehaven Coal has fallen apart.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Australian Magnate Abandons Bid for Whitehaven Coal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitehaven Coal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T13:32:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b610e3a-b009-5130-9139-b19f428d485e', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b610e3a-b009-5130-9139-b19f428d485e'}, {'abstract': 'Minutes of the Fed’s latest policy meeting showed its members poised to cushion the economy if needed, while a letter from the Fed chairman, Ben Bernanke, said much the same thing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/business/shares-open-flat-on-wall-street.html', 'snippet': 'Minutes of the Fed’s latest policy meeting showed its members poised to cushion the economy if needed, while a letter from the Fed chairman, Ben Bernanke, said much the same thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stocks rose on Friday, paring the first weekly decline in almost two months for the Standard & Poor’s 500-stock index, as the Federal Reserve chairman, Ben S. Bernanke, said he saw “scope for further action,” increasing speculation that the central bank would act to stimulate economic growth.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shares Rise on Hopes for Further Fed Action', 'kicker': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shares Rise on Hopes For Further Fed Action', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Durable Goods (Economic Indicator)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T13:45:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bff2792f-47dc-5d4d-9dfc-11a9d4549883', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bff2792f-47dc-5d4d-9dfc-11a9d4549883'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Yoshihiko Noda threatened to scrap an agreement to provide support for the South Korean currency, and said he would appeal to the international community in Japan’s disputes with South Korea and China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/world/asia/japan-vows-to-press-claims-over-disputed-islands.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Yoshihiko Noda threatened to scrap an agreement to provide support for the South Korean currency, and said he would appeal to the international community in Japan’s disputes with South Korea and China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Japan stepped up the pressure on South Korea in a diplomatic dispute on Friday, condemning the South’s “illegal occupation” of islets that lie between the two countries and threatening to scrap an agreement to provide support for the South Korean currency. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan Places Pressure on South Korea Amid Islets Dispute', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan Places Pressure on South Korea Amid Islets Dispute', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East China Sea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee Myung-bak', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Noda, Yoshihiko', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea