 Sergio Gutiérrez-Ferrol of Spain on Friday for a spot in the United States Open main draw.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/team-tennis-player-vies-for-spot-in-u-s-open-draw/', 'snippet': 'Bobby Reynolds of the United States will play Sergio Gutiérrez-Ferrol of Spain on Friday for a spot in the United States Open main draw.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bobby Reynolds of the United States hopes to ride the wave of his excellent results this summer in World Team Tennis to advance through the last round of qualifying at the United States Open.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Team Tennis Player Vies for Spot in U.S. Open Draw', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reynolds, Bobby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World TeamTennis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T16:25:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': "By Craig O'Shannessy", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Shannessy", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cac443d5-fd7d-519f-915e-e87041ac494d', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cac443d5-fd7d-519f-915e-e87041ac494d'}, {'abstract': 'A year after the death of Agnes Varis, who financed the Met’s rush ticket program, the opera has found a way to continue it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/arts/music/met-opera-will-continue-to-offer-discounted-tickets.html', 'snippet': 'A year after the death of Agnes Varis, who financed the Met’s rush ticket program, the opera has found a way to continue it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Agnes Varis, a Metropolitan Opera board member and benefactor, died a year ago, the company lost the person who paid for its heavily discounted rush ticket program.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Met Opera to Preserve Rush Tickets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Met Opera To Preserve Rush Tickets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Varis, Agnes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T16:34:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1f5607f-1352-5d7b-b8e2-4e3c107533c8', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1f5607f-1352-5d7b-b8e2-4e3c107533c8'}, {'abstract': 'Facing realities about politics and the weather at a conservative conference days before the G.O.P. convention.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/conservative-forecasts-meteorological-and-political/', 'snippet': 'Facing realities about politics and the weather at a conservative conference days before the G.O.P. convention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — Along with fretting about the political fortunes of Representative Todd Akin, the Republican Senate candidate from Missouri whose comments about rape set off their own storm, the weather was a dominant topic of conversation at a pre-convention gathering of conservatives on Thursday evening.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conservative Forecasts, Meteorological and Political', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akin, Todd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council for National Policy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T16:46:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton and Andrew Siddons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siddons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcb7892f-f283-5355-900a-b63c1110e8d7', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcb7892f-f283-5355-900a-b63c1110e8d7'}, {'abstract': 'Chan Marshall, who performs as Cat Power, has recorded “Sun,” her first new original album in six years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/arts/music/cat-powers-new-album-is-sun.html', 'snippet': 'Chan Marshall, who performs as Cat Power, has recorded “Sun,” her first new original album in six years.', 'lead_paragraph': '“PEOPLE tend to think I’m insane,” Chan Marshall said, “and I’m really tired of it.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26PLAYLIST1/26PLAYLIST1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26PLAYLIST1/26PLAYLIST1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1466, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scraps of Joy and Inspiration Amid Struggle', 'kicker': 'Playlist | Cat Power', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scraps of Joy And Inspiration Amid Struggle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marshall, Chan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cat Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T16:48:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/13f3f7f2-5c00-5109-bce1-6a989550bcb3', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13f3f7f2-5c00-5109-bce1-6a989550bcb3'}, {'abstract': 'The men who first ran cable signals into TV sets — from poles, not underground — were a hardy breed. Like the writer’s father.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/arts/television/my-father-the-pioneering-cable-guy.html', 'snippet': 'The men who first ran cable signals into TV sets — from poles, not underground — were a hardy breed. Like the writer’s father.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YOU never know what sort of wish-I’d-dones are going to pop into your head while you’re at the bedside of a dying parent. A year ago this week, as I sat with my father during the last moments of his long life, this one came along unbidden: I sure wish I’d asked Dad, while he could still answer me, about the time he invented cable TV. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26CABLE1_SPAN/26CABLE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26CABLE1_SPAN/26CABLE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26CABLE1_SPAN/26CABLE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 825, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26CABLE1_SPAN/26CABLE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1649, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26CABLE1_SPAN/26CABLE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26CABLE1_SPAN/26CABLE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Father, the Cable Pioneer', 'kicker': 'Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Father, the Cable Pioneer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Genzlinger, Robert G', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T16:49:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfcd1ba6-bde9-5dc6-88be-ff2c1e49b9e4', 'word_count': 1685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfcd1ba6-bde9-5dc6-88be-ff2c1e49b9e4'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. McCarthy backs female performers with her organization Gorgeous Ladies of Comedy, which has grown from a blog to an informal society with open-mike nights and support services.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/arts/glennis-mccarthy-and-the-gorgeous-ladies-of-comedy.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. McCarthy backs female performers with her organization Gorgeous Ladies of Comedy, which has grown from a blog to an informal society with open-mike nights and support services.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LIKE most actresses in New York, Glennis McCarthy, 33, has to juggle callbacks and performances with her day job. But unlike most actresses Ms. McCarthy has a day job that involves keeping her peers united, inspired and working. She is the brains behind Gorgeous Ladies of Comedy, or GLOC. It began as a blog just under two years ago and, under Ms. McCarthy’s tireless hand, has bloomed into an informal society of New York’s brightest comediennes. Kristen Schaal, of “30 Rock” and “The Daily Show,” the actress Kristen Johnston and the stand-up star Tig Notaro have all performed at its events or lent advice on the blog.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26SNAPSHOT/26SNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26SNAPSHOT/26SNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1360, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26SNAPSHOT/26SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26SNAPSHOT/26SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Glennis McCarthy and the Gorgeous Ladies of Comedy', 'kicker': 'Snapshot | Glennis McCarthy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smelling Like Peonies And Networking for Laughs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gorgeous Ladies of Comedy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarthy, Glennis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T16:51:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Megan Angelo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Megan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Angelo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff214079-4862-5912-98b6-813257e9b6a8', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff214079-4862-5912-98b6-813257e9b6a8'}, {'abstract': 'Dani Vetere’s play is about an archaeologist whose professional and personal life is in disarray.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/new-york-fringe-festival-report-hadrians-wall/', 'snippet': 'Dani Vetere’s play is about an archaeologist whose professional and personal life is in disarray.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reviews of shows from the New York International Fringe Festival will appear on ArtsBeat through the festival’s close on Aug. 26. For more information, go to fringenyc.org.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Fringe Festival Report: ‘Hadrian’s Wall’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fringe Festival in Review: Hadrian’s Wall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York International Fringe Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T16:57:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08dd4a64-700a-5d8a-98f2-16f90e1329cf', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08dd4a64-700a-5d8a-98f2-16f90e1329cf'}, {'abstract': 'A graphic designer waxes poetic about the old days, when luxurious stationery was the social media of its time.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/the-complete-engraver/', 'snippet': 'A graphic designer waxes poetic about the old days, when luxurious stationery was the social media of its time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Complete Engraver', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T16:57:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8586053-1e70-56e2-9193-72e263a29100', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8586053-1e70-56e2-9193-72e263a29100'}, {'abstract': 'A comic-strip version of the writings of Frederich von Hayek, an economist whose antisocialist message influenced Paul Ryan.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/the-road-to-serfdom-the-graphic-version/', 'snippet': 'A comic-strip version of the writings of Frederich von Hayek, an economist whose antisocialist message influenced Paul Ryan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s magazine, Adam Davidson writes about Friedrich von Hayek, a shy, often misunderstood Austrian economist whose ideas are inspiring a new generation of Republican leaders, most notably Paul Ryan. Ryan has cited Hayek’s seminal work, “The Road to Serfdom,” which was published during World War II, as a major influence on his own thinking. (He also lists it, along with Ayn Rand’s “Atlas Shrugged,” as a favorite book on his Facebook page.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Road to Serfdom,’ the Graphic Version', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T17:03:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Kedmey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kedmey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/068c6b45-4ab6-54dd-810a-dfdaf1e7cadb', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/068c6b45-4ab6-54dd-810a-dfdaf1e7cadb'}, {'abstract': 'Two American service members, both with traumatic brain injuries, find therapy and each other in writing.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/writing-to-calm-and-compose-the-injured-brain/', 'snippet': 'Two American service members, both with traumatic brain injuries, find therapy and each other in writing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is an old “we.” We had near photographic memories, and school was easy. We found people’s faces familiar and daily tasks were easily remembered. We didn’t have any problems articulating his words. We maintained focus easily. We stood and walked without fear of stumbling. We didn’t fear debilitating headaches. Life was easier.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Writing to Calm and Compose the Injured Brain', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traumatic Brain Injury', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T17:05:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas James Brennan and Coban Shaw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'James', 'lastname': 'Brennan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Coban', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ef2d001-5da1-5006-af41-617b4fc4af89', 'word_count': 1076, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ef2d001-5da1-5006-af41-617b4fc4af89'}, {'abstract': 'Adm. William McRaven had in mind the recent news that a former member of the Navy SEALs team that killed Bin Laden had written a book, and also an effort by former Special Operations members to accuse President Obama of leaking information to enhance his reputation.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/u-s-special-operations-commander-cautions-against-exploiting-celebrity-status/', 'snippet': 'Adm. William McRaven had in mind the recent news that a former member of the Navy SEALs team that killed Bin Laden had written a book, and also an effort by former Special Operations members to accuse President Obama of leaking information to enha...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The news that Penguin would publish on Sept. 11 a book by a former member of the Navy SEALs team that killed Osama bin Laden has stirred an intense amount of interest — about what details will be revealed about the raid, but also about the protocol governing the release of information on military operations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Special Operations Commander Cautions Against Exploiting ‘Celebrity’ Status', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bissonnette, Matt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McRaven, William H', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Navy Seals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Special Operations Command', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T17:08:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name