seph-godla-vows.html', 'snippet': 'A couple weds about six years after being introduced by his wife, from whom he was separated at the time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON Aug. 1, an eclectic mix of New York and Los Angeles museum folk, Parisian friends and Western artists gathered at the Rainbow Ranch near Big Sky, Mont., to watch Charlotte Vignon, 37, an associate curator of decorative arts at the Frick Collection in Manhattan, and Joseph Godla, 56, the chief conservator there, exchange vows.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/fashion/26VOWS1_SPAN/26VOWS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/fashion/26VOWS1_SPAN/26VOWS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/fashion/26VOWS1_SPAN/VOWS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/fashion/26VOWS1_SPAN/VOWS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/fashion/26VOWS1_SPAN/26VOWS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/fashion/26VOWS1_SPAN/26VOWS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/fashion/26VOWS1_SPAN/26VOWS1_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Charlotte Vignon and Joseph Godla', 'kicker': 'Vows', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Charlotte Vignon and Joseph Godla', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vows (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T17:56:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toby Thompson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thompson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a31bf15-1b99-51c6-93f7-404759e731e6', 'word_count': 1302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a31bf15-1b99-51c6-93f7-404759e731e6'}, {'abstract': 'Ken Thomas broadcasts tennis matches on the Internet, including qualifying at the United States Open, reviving the lost art of tennis on the radio.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/at-the-u-s-open-and-beyond-a-radio-announcers-internet-odyssey/', 'snippet': 'Ken Thomas broadcasts tennis matches on the Internet, including qualifying at the United States Open, reviving the lost art of tennis on the radio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tennis fans will not see Ken Thomas at the 2012 United States Open. A tanned, gray-haired man wearing a headset and microphone and sitting on a scaffold platform above Court 13, Thomas has been a sideshow of his own during qualifying rounds at the Billie Jean King National Tennis Center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At the U.S. Open and Beyond, a Radio Announcer’s Internet Odyssey', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T17:59:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77fc936b-5448-5dd7-86b4-90f3f44b2348', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77fc936b-5448-5dd7-86b4-90f3f44b2348'}, {'abstract': 'The usual enticement for “deluxe” editions is behind-the-scenes features. In this area, the color edition of “Scott Pilgrim” does not disappoint.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/graphic-books-best-sellers-color-me-better/', 'snippet': 'The usual enticement for “deluxe” editions is behind-the-scenes features. In this area, the color edition of “Scott Pilgrim” does not disappoint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At No. 2 on the hardcover list this week is Volume 1 of the color edition of “Scott Pilgrim,” by Bryan Lee O’Malley. The original softcover version of the series was a regular presence on our sales chart in 2010 as fans counted down the days until the release of the film version starring Michael Cera. (The movie criminally underperformed at the box office.) In August of that year, the six volumes were in the top seven of the paperback list. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: Color Me Better', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T18:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cd8f5d3-9554-5ee2-b907-53d943bb35a2', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cd8f5d3-9554-5ee2-b907-53d943bb35a2'}, {'abstract': 'How to be frugal in a region where a fast-food meal for one goes for $23? Six lessons learned the hard way.', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/scandinavia-on-125-a-day/', 'snippet': 'How to be frugal in a region where a fast-food meal for one goes for $23? Six lessons learned the hard way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT was my first full day in Oslo and I thought that I had found a rare bargain: a six-pack of Carlsberg beer for under $5 (or 27.40 Norwegian kroner) at the Kiwi Minipris supermarket! Even for a mass-produced pilsner, it was a surprising deal for Norway, where just about everything costs more than you’d expect. And by more, I don’t mean by increments of 10 or 15 percent, but by multiples of two or three or four.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scandinavia on $125 a Day', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scandinavia On $125 a Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T18:02:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By SETH KUGEL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KUGEL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2dcf99e-6188-5433-a5b8-b801d174538a', 'word_count': 3088, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2dcf99e-6188-5433-a5b8-b801d174538a'}, {'abstract': 'Once, there were hundreds, if not thousands of Basque sheepmen in the American West. Meet one of the few who remain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/travel/herding-sheep-in-basque-country-idaho.html', 'snippet': 'Once, there were hundreds, if not thousands of Basque sheepmen in the American West. Meet one of the few who remain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHEEP, you may be surprised to learn, are not as dumb as they look. Some people might even describe them as shrewdly calculating, remarkably crafty animals with fierce independent streaks. Given the slightest opening, for example, they will quit a herd, striking out in small, enterprising bands for the high-desert plains — ungulate fugitives in a promised land of sagebrush and cactus — sometimes never to be seen again.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/travel/26-cultured-sheep/26-cultured-sheep-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/travel/26-cultured-sheep/26-cultured-sheep-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/travel/26-cultured-sheep/26-cultured-sheep-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/travel/26-cultured-sheep/26-cultured-sheep-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/travel/26-cultured-sheep/26-cultured-sheep-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/travel/26-cultured-sheep/26-cultured-sheep-thu