.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/big-ticket-sold-for-21-million/', 'snippet': 'A co-op in the landmark Verona with interiors designed by Gwathmey Siegel and sweeping views of Central Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A penthouse with sophisticated steamed-beech-dominated interiors by Charles Gwathmey and sweeping views of Central Park from its perch at the Verona, an Upper East Side co-op designed by William E. Mowbray in 1908, sold under the radar for $21 million, the biggest sale of the week according to city records.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Ticket |  Sold for $21 Million', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gwathmey, Charles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T18:47:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b026ba2b-cde1-5725-99fd-ea3870529118', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b026ba2b-cde1-5725-99fd-ea3870529118'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of events.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/arts/aug-26-sept-1.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE novelist Ian Fleming was not pleased when he learned that his greatest creation, James Bond, was played by Sean Connery in “Dr. No,” the first in the film series. “I’m looking for Cmdr. James Bond,” he said, “not an overgrown stuntman.” Moviegoers disagreed, and Fleming later came to his senses. Now, in honor of the franchise’s 50th anniversary, the complete Connery Bonds (including “Never Say Never Again,” from 1983), will be screened in IFC’s aptly named program JAMES BOND NO. 1: SEAN CONNERY’S 007, starting Friday (with an all-day, seven-film Bond-a-thon next Sunday.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26GUIDE1/26GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 841, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26GUIDE1/26GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1681, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 26 — Sept. 1', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T18:48:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e751058d-082e-58a2-b34f-a544528aa26a', 'word_count': 1158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e751058d-082e-58a2-b34f-a544528aa26a'}, {'abstract': 'For farmers, drought becomes a way of life. | Americans near retirement suffer big income losses. | James B. Stewart discusses Mitt Romney’s foreign tax credit.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/business-day-live-drought-disrupts-everyday-tasks-in-rural-midwest/', 'snippet': 'For farmers, drought becomes a way of life. | Americans near retirement suffer big income losses. | James B. Stewart discusses Mitt Romney’s foreign tax credit.', 'lead_paragraph': ' For farmers, drought becomes a way of life. | Americans near retirement suffer big income losses. | James B. Stewart discusses Mitt Romney’s foreign tax credit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Business Day Live: Drought Disrupts Everyday Tasks in Rural Midwest', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T18:53:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87ab63da-8fa2-5a6b-92c9-3130dac58bca', 'word_count': 27, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87ab63da-8fa2-5a6b-92c9-3130dac58bca'}, {'abstract': 'How do our feelings about risk affect our decisions about how much auto insurance to buy?', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/auto-insurance-scaredy-cats-and-the-rollers-of-the-dice/', 'snippet': 'How do our feelings about risk affect our decisions about how much auto insurance to buy?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this weekend’s Your Money column, I try to lay out the facts and odds that lay behind the question of whether any of us have enough auto insurance. Some people look at the long odds of a bad wreck and buy the minimum amount that their state requires. Others buy as much as they can, figuring that it’s better to be safe than to be sorry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Auto Insurance, Scaredy-Cats and the Rollers of the Dice', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Insurance and Liability', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T18:55:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b56fd2f0-920b-53c1-820f-c729c9a3015f', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b56fd2f0-920b-53c1-820f-c729c9a3015f'}, {'abstract': 'While it is true that a series of Greek governments bears a large share of the guilt for the euro crisis, for mismanaging their economy and finances, there are plenty of other culprits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/business/global/in-euro-crisis-plenty-of-blame-to-go-around.html', 'snippet': 'While it is true that a series of Greek governments bears a large share of the guilt for the euro crisis, for mismanaging their economy and finances, there are plenty of other culprits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — The debate about how to distribute the cost of preserving the euro often centers on a fundamental question that is unspoken but implicit: Who caused this crisis anyway?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/25/business/Blamejp/Blamejp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/25/business/Blamejp/Blamejp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/25/business/Blamejp/Blamejp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/25/business/Blamejp/Blamejp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/25/business/Blamejp/Blamejp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/25/business/Blamejp/Blamejp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/25/business/Blamejp/Blamejp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Euro Crisis, Fingers Can Point in All Directions', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Euro Crisis, Fingers Can Point in All Directions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T18:57:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f9ee8e6-30ca-596c-b287-bb863a7bf7a7', 'word_count': 1303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f9ee8e6-30ca-596c-b287-bb863a7bf7a7'}, {'abstract': 'A young chef serves up old-school Parisian fare in a former butcher shop.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/counter-intuitive-chez-aline-in-paris/', 'snippet': 'A young chef serves up old-school Parisian fare in a former butcher shop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was happenstance that the young chef Delphine Zampetti came to open the tiny Parisian eatery Chez Aline. Last May, Zampetti, who has worked at Café Caché and Le Verre Volé, was walking down Rue de la Roquette in the 11th Arrondissement when she noticed a butcher shop with a charmingly retro vibe. The next week, she passed the shop again, only this time there was a “for sale” sign in the window. It was “une petite idée, just like that,” she muses. And then she went for it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Counter Intuitive | Chez Aline in Paris', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T19:02:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Moroz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moroz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1c5d990-fb6e-5311-9f18-15f289cca10f', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1c5d990-fb6e-5311-9f18-15f289cca10f'}, {'abstract': 'A new financial tool is aimed at encouraging greater disclosure about greenhouse gas emissions from companies while, hopefully, also pushing investors to build more responsible portfolios.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/will-emissions-disclosure-mean-investor-pressure-on-polluters/', 'snippet': 'A new financial tool is aimed at encouraging greater disclosure about greenhouse gas emissions from companies while, hopefully, also pushing investors to build more responsible portfolios.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new financial tool developed by the investment firm South Pole Carbon, in partnership with the Swiss Federal Institute of Technology, provides greenhouse gas emissions profiles of more than 40,000 publicly listed companies. This index is aimed at encouraging greater disclosure from companies while, hopefully, also pushing investors to build more responsible portfolios.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Emissions Disclosure Mean Investor Pressure on Polluters?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Swiss Federal Institute of Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T19:08:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a645a73d-7ed2-558c-a9e1-0688d3dd9bef', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a645a73d-7ed2-558c-a9e1-0688d3dd9bef'}, {'abstract': 'The Blu-ray and DVD reissue of “Quadrophenia,” the film based on the Who rock opera, is part of a continued interest in the Mod culture and fashions the film revealed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/movies/quadrophenia-reissue-new-spark-for-enduring-mods.html', 'snippet': 'The Blu-ray and DVD reissue of “Quadrophenia,” the film based on the Who rock opera, is part of a continued interest in the Mod culture and fashions the film revealed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANY years after filming the climax to the 1979 film “Quadrophenia” in Brighton, England, the director Franc Roddam found himself back there for a screening. Though the town had long been famous as a beachfront resort, Mr. Roddam’s film adaptation of the Who’s rock opera has drawn fans there as well, particularly for its depiction of a 1964 gathering of the futurist Mods, which ended in a clash with their sworn enemies, the backward-gazing, leather-clad Rockers. New Mods continue to travel there for scooter rallies and “weekenders.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26QUADROPHENIA1_SPAN/26QUADROPHENIA1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26QUADROPHENIA1_SPAN/26QUADROPHENIA1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26QUADROPHENIA1_SPAN/26QUADROPHENIA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 988, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26QUADROPHENIA1_SPAN/26QUADROPHENIA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1834, 'width': 1900, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/arts/26QUADROPHENIA1_SPAN/26QUADROPHENIA1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 