n aren’t finding re-employment — and even when they do find new work, many are taking major pay cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/the-stranded-unemployed/', 'snippet': 'A new report finds that people who lost work between 2009 and 2011 often aren’t finding re-employment — and even when they do find new work, many are taking major pay cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday I wrote about how incomes have declined sharply in the last few years, particularly for people approaching retirement age. A new report from the Bureau of Labor Statistics sheds some light on why: People who lost work, especially if they’re older, often aren’t finding re-employment; even when they do find new work, they’re taking major pay cuts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Stranded Unemployed', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T21:06:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/926834e8-d1f1-5635-874b-48cdb1e88c07', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/926834e8-d1f1-5635-874b-48cdb1e88c07'}, {'abstract': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural events from this week.', 'w