ncing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T22:48:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3152f7c-8804-57a9-b10e-b9cc0d6babee', 'word_count': 1191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3152f7c-8804-57a9-b10e-b9cc0d6babee'}, {'abstract': 'At Lepri’s Grill, beef is from Charter Farms in nearby Ellington, vegetables are from Stafford and zucchini is from the garden out back.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/nyregion/a-review-of-lepris-grill-in-tolland.html', 'snippet': 'At Lepri’s Grill, beef is from Charter Farms in nearby Ellington, vegetables are from Stafford and zucchini is from the garden out back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANK LEPRI is known to Hartford-area diners from his years as chef at the late and lamented downtown bistro Pastis; when it closed, he and his wife, Debbie, opened an excellent trattoria called Da Lepri in Ellington, later adding a burger bar nearby. And last spring they opened a steak-and-seafood emporium in the 275-year-old Tolland farmhouse where the restaurant Zest had been.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26DINECT2_SPAN/26DINECT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26DINECT2_SPAN/26DINECT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26DINECT2_SPAN/26DINECT2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26DINECT2_SPAN/26DINECT2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26DINECT2_SPAN/26DINECT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26DINECT2_SPAN/26DINECT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26DINECT2_SPAN/26DINECT2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Kitchen Geared to a Locavore’s Tastes', 'kicker': 'Connecticut Dining | Tolland', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Kitchen Geared To a Locavore’s Tastes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lepri, Frank', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tolland (Conn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Lepri's Grill (Tolland, Conn, Restaurant)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T22:49:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rand Richards Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rand', 'middlename': 'Richards', 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b867ad9-9dd7-5d4b-880b-e5e071f070e1', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b867ad9-9dd7-5d4b-880b-e5e071f070e1'}, {'abstract': 'The new BBC/HBO show may share themes and a time period with “Downton Abbey,” but only one has, at its core, the mammoth tetralogy from Ford Madox Ford.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/will-tom-stoppard-side-with-graham-greene-on-the-last-book-of-parades-end/', 'snippet': 'The new BBC/HBO show may share themes and a time period with “Downton Abbey,” but only one has, at its core, the mammoth tetralogy from Ford Madox Ford.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Contributing to the One-Page Magazine is a fun and sometimes challenging exercise in compression and economy. For every 70 words I work into a column, there are often hundreds more I could have written on a subject. That’s never been more true than it is for Sunday’s edition, which focuses on the most exciting TV news in recent memory: Benedict Cumberbatch, best known as the lead in BBC’s “Sherlock,” stars in Tom Stoppard’s adaptation of Ford Madox Ford’s “Parade’s End.” The joint BBC and HBO production was directed by Susanna White and is positioned as the smart Edwardian-era alternative to “Downton Abbey,” a show Cumberbatch has ridiculed far and wide. Most notoriously, he denounced its cheap sentiment in an interview with Reader’s Digest and called the second season “atrocious,” preceded by an adverb that cannot be written here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Tom Stoppard Side With Graham Greene on the Last Book of ‘Parade’s End’?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumberbatch, Benedict', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greene, Graham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stoppard, Tom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T22:57:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maud Newton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maud', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c2db372-e4f8-55d8-a473-6244daf76603', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c2db372-e4f8-55d8-a473-6244daf76603'}, {'abstract': 'The designer who shot and killed a former colleague on Friday outside the Empire State Building had a Web site for his art work. Here is a selection of it.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/the-artwork-of-jeffrey-johnson/', 'snippet': 'The designer who shot and killed a former colleague on Friday outside the Empire State Building had a Web site for his art work. Here is a selection of it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeffrey T. Johnson, the designer who killed a former colleague near the Empire State Building on Friday, had a YouTube channel dedicated to showcasing the illustrations on his Web site, St. Jolly’s Art, most of which depict cars, motorcycles, women and combinations thereof. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Artwork of Jeffrey Johnson', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Jeffrey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-24T23:04:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7816730e-2b11-5f33-8c02-50fce64a5104', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/781