 people are good shots during a violent encounter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We had a shooting near the Empire State Building. An aggrieved ex-employee of an apparel company killed his former co-worker, and was himself killed by police. Except for the famous-landmark location, it was not actually a very big story. Remember the mass shooting at the lumberyard in North Carolina earlier this year, or the one last October at the California cement plant? No? Neither does anybody else except the grieving families.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Arms and the Duck', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arms And The Duck', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holmes, James Eagan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aurora, Colo, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Jeffrey T', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oak Creek, Wis, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Page, Wade Michael', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T01:11:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3aa53f11-e17f-56fe-9261-b3d0aa985b86', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3aa53f11-e17f-56fe-9261-b3d0aa985b86'}, {'abstract': 'Since a 1997 shooting on the Empire State Building’s observation deck, the Police Department has increased security measures in and around the building.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/nyregion/once-again-landmark-is-backdrop-to-violence.html', 'snippet': 'Since a 1997 shooting on the Empire State Building’s observation deck, the Police Department has increased security measures in and around the building.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On movie screens it has been besieged by aliens, tidal waves and an overgrown ape. But on Friday morning the horror at the Empire State Building was all too real. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Once Again, Landmark Is Backdrop to Violence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Once Again, Landmark Is Backdrop To Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ercolino, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Jeffrey T', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Empire State Building (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T01:13:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum and David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a11ac4a-89a3-5705-9843-510d77678a05', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a11ac4a-89a3-5705-9843-510d77678a05'}, {'abstract': '“Carousel,” by Richard Rodgers and Oscar Hammerstein II, runs at the Goodspeed Opera House in East Haddam, Conn., through Sept. 29.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/nyregion/a-review-of-carousel-at-the-goodspeed-opera-house-in-east-haddam-conn.html', 'snippet': '“Carousel,” by Richard Rodgers and Oscar Hammerstein II, runs at the Goodspeed Opera House in East Haddam, Conn., through Sept. 29.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Looked at objectively, the hero of “Carousel” isn’t very good hero material. Proud, vain and not just a little bit dumb, the carnival barker Billy Bigelow also possesses a violent streak and a hot temper. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26SUBARTSCT1_SPAN/26SUBARTSCT1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26SUBARTSCT1_SPAN/26SUBARTSCT1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26SUBARTSCT1_SPAN/26SUBARTSCT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26SUBARTSCT1_SPAN/26SUBARTSCT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26SUBARTSCT1_SPAN/26SUBARTSCT1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26SUBARTSCT1_SPAN/26SUBARTSCT1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At the Carnival, Love and Looming Clouds', 'kicker': 'Arts | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At the Carnival, Love And Looming Clouds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Haddam (Conn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hammerstein, Oscar II', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goodspeed Opera House', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snyder, James', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodgers, Richard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruggiero, Rob', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T01:13:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylviane Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylviane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa786e8c-5982-5038-a999-d6ca769cba41', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa786e8c-5982-5038-a999-d6ca769cba41'}, {'abstract': 'These five teams might be outside the Top 25 rankings, but they are not outside the conversation.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/24/college-football-preview-five-teams-to-watch/', 'snippet': 'These five teams might be outside the Top 25 rankings, but they are not outside the conversation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OHIO The last time the Bobcats won more games than any other Football Bowl Subdivision program in the state was 1962. That streak should end in 2012. Beyond the talent, experience and coaching, the Bobcats have a schedule that could not be more favorable. Ohio is simply a better team than every opponent on its schedule — and that includes Penn State, which hosts the Bobcats in the season opener.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'College Football Preview: Five Teams to Watch', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Around The Nation: Five Teams To Watch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louisiana Tech University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ohio University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Tennessee', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Utah', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T01:17:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Myerberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Myerberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eca490c8-d00e-56de-af76-97d57a26623d', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eca490c8-d00e-56de-af76-97d57a26623d'}, {'abstract': 'Even though the states can barely meet their core responsibilities now, Mitt Romney wants to increase their burdens by unloading several federal duties.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/opinion/romneys-plan-dump-it-on-the-states.html', 'snippet': 'Even though the states can barely meet their core responsibilities now, Mitt Romney wants to increase their burdens by unloading several federal duties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, Mitt Romney unveiled the latest in a series of bad ideas for taking government duties out of Washington and hiding them in the back rooms of state capitols. Mostly, Mr. Romney wants to allow states to quietly smother social programs the federal government has run for decades. In the case of his new energy policy, he wants to give states power to bypass Washington’s caution in burrowing for oil, gas and coal on federal lands. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dump It on the States', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dump It on the States', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal-State Relations (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Welfare (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T01:17:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/363e8613-f8fc-5e4c-8619-9163c7a2b408', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/363e8613-f8fc-5e4c-8619-9163c7a2b408'}, {'abstract': 'An animosity between the two men at the center of a fatal shooting outside the Empire State Building on Friday evolved over years in the workplace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/nyregion/in-empire-state-killing-a-grudge-boiled-over.html', 'snippet': 'An animosity between the two men at the center of a fatal shooting outside the Empire State Building on Friday evolved over years in the workplace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The two men at the center of a fatal shooting outside the Empire State Building on Friday had brushed shoulders for years — often literally, two large egos stuffed into a small office — and yet could hardly have been less alike.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26shoot_inline/26shoot_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26shoot_inline/26shoot_inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26shoot_inline/26shoot_inline-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Long Before Carnage, an Office Grudge Festered', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Long Before Carnage, an Office Grudge Festered', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ercolino, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Jeffrey T', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Empire State Building (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T01:18:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson, David M. Halbfinger and Sharon Otterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d78c75f-c4f1-5c27-9c44-8cbbc7b5ef22', 'word_count': 1583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d78c75f-c4f1-5c27-9c44-8cbbc7b5ef22'}, {'abstract': 'The parents of Tyler Clementi, the Rutgers student who jumped off the George Washington Bridge in 2010, continue to find many sources of blame.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/nyregion/after-tyler-clementis-suicide-his-parents-make-painful-changes-in-the-search-for-why.html', 'snippet': 'The parents of Tyler Clementi, the Rutgers student who jumped off the George Washington Bridge in 2010, continue to find many sources of blame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIDGEWOOD, N.J. — When Tyler Clementi told his parents he was gay, two days before he left for Rutgers University in the fall of 2010, he said he had known since middle school.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/25/nyregion/CLEMENTI/CLEMENTI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/25/nyregion/CLEMENTI/CLEMENTI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/25/nyregion/CLEMENTI/CLEMENTI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/25/nyregion/CLEMENTI/CLEMENTI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1274, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/25/nyregion/CLEMENTI/CLEMENTI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/25/nyregion/CLEMENTI/CLEMENTI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/25/nyregion/CLEMENTI/CLEMENTI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Gay Son’s Suicide, Mother Finds Blame in Herself and in Her Church', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Gay Son’s Suicide, Mother Finds Blame in Herself and in Her Church', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ravi, Dharun', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clementi, Tyler', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T01:25:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Zernike', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zernike', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15dd1a8a-d281-5a64-950e-4904e864a6e6', 'word_count': 1241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15dd1a8a-d281-5a64-950e-4904e864a6e6'}, {'abstract': 'By crushing dissent, Egypt’s new leader, Mohamed Morsi, is repeating the errors of his ousted predecessor, Hosni Mubarak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/opinion/president-morsi-and-his-critics.html', 'snippet': 'By crushing dissent, Egypt’s new leader, Mohamed Morsi, is repeating the errors of his ousted predecessor, Hosni Mubarak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was another street demonstration in Cairo on Friday. This time, instead of inveighing against former President Hosni Mubarak, or his generals, people were protesting against Egypt’s first freely elected president, Mohamed Morsi. It was one more sign that citizens in the new Egypt are determined to make their voices heard — and a sign, too, that Mr. Morsi and his party, the Muslim Brotherhood, are having a hard time hearing those voices. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'President Morsi and His Critics', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President Morsi and His Critics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Afifi, Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Okasha, Tawfik', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T01:29:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/157a58ff-33a5-5154-817d-1fdb662172bd', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/157a58ff-33a5-5154-817d-1fdb662172bd'}, {'abstract': 'Aruba Networks, a maker of components for mobile devices, surged 14 percent after reporting quarterly sales and profit that exceeded analysts’ estimates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/technology/aruba-shares-gain-on-strong-quarter.html', 'snippet': 'Aruba Networks, a maker of components for mobile devices, surged 14 percent after reporting quarterly sales and profit that exceeded analysts’ estimates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aruba Networks, a maker of components for mobile devices, surged 14 percent, to $19.36, after reporting quarterly sales and profit that exceeded analysts’ estimates. Revenue in the period, which ended July 31 and was the fourth quarter of Aruba’s fiscal year, rose 22 percent, to $139.2 million, and profit excluding some items was 18 cents a share, topping a company projection of 16 to 17 cents. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aruba Shares Gain on Strong Quarter', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | Technology', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aruba Shares Gain On Strong Quarter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aruba Networks Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T01:30:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f85b19cb-0270-5f99-be72-a162947adb27', 'word_count': 69, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f85b19cb-0270-5f99-be72-a162947adb27'}, {'abstract': 'Here are our recommendations in four Democratic judicial contests in Manhattan, Brooklyn and the Bronx.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/opinion/for-judgeships-in-new-york-city.html', 'snippet': 'Here are our recommendations in four Democratic judicial contests in Manhattan, Brooklyn and the Bronx.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Congressional primaries decided in a separate election in June and just a few state 