k Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Military Deaths in Afghanistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T03:51:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/88aa6c33-ad42-5a25-bdd3-9cc29ac4fa53', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88aa6c33-ad42-5a25-bdd3-9cc29ac4fa53'}, {'abstract': 'Books examining the legal affairs of Ira B. Arnstein, providing insider tidbits on Gov. Nelson A. Rockefeller, and celebrating George M. Steinbrenner and the Yankees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/nyregion/books-about-a-musical-plaintiff-rockefeller-and-the-yankees.html', 'snippet': 'Books examining the legal affairs of Ira B. Arnstein, providing insider tidbits on Gov. Nelson A. Rockefeller, and celebrating George M. Steinbrenner and the Yankees.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Music,” the composer Ira B. Arnstein once said, “is a language in sound like Latin or French. I’ll prove it.” He tried. But the perennial plaintiff, who argued in lawsuit after lawsuit that more popular composers had plagiarized his music, never won a case.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26BOOK_SPAN/26BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26BOOK_SPAN/26BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '