', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/hertz-said-to-be-close-to-buying-dollar-thrifty/', 'snippet': 'Talks between the two rental car leaders are expected to continue through the weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hertz Global Holdings is near a deal to acquire the Dollar Thrifty Automotive Group for nearly $2.5 billion, according to a person briefed on the transaction, ending a fierce and protracted merger battle among the nation’s largest car rental companies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hertz Said to Be Close to Buying Dollar Thrifty', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Renting and Leasing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dollar Thrifty Automotive Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hertz Global Holdings Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T04:08:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c78177e-2336-57bc-a59d-8dd03a4bd810', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c78177e-2336-57bc-a59d-8dd03a4bd810'}, {'abstract': 'Long before Bill O’Brien chose to lead the rebuilding of Penn State football, he had already been dealt a far greater challenge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/sports/ncaafootball/penn-states-bill-obrien-no-stranger-to-adversity.html', 'snippet': 'Long before Bill O’Brien chose to lead the rebuilding of Penn State football, he had already been dealt a far greater challenge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STATE COLLEGE, Pa. — Every morning, Bill and Colleen O’Brien know their older son, 10-year-old Jack, will have a seizure when he wakes up. It could last 30 seconds or go on for 30 minutes, necessitating an ambulance trip to the hospital. There may be more seizures during the day, depending on disparate factors like weather patterns and Jack’s growth spurts. And when they happen, the O’Briens can do little except to turn their son on his side and wait for the seizure to end.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/sports/OBRIEN/OBRIEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/24/sports/OBRIEN/OBRIEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/sports/OBRIEN/OBRIEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/sports/OBRIEN/OBRIEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/sports/OBRIEN/OBRIEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/24/sports/OBRIEN/OBRIEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/sports/OBRIEN/OBRIEN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Tough as His Task', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Tough as His Task', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belichick, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paterno, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandusky, Jerry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Brien, Bill (1969- )", 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T04:10:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/101aa7a8-dca2-530f-933e-cefe40326d8f', 'word_count': 2541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/101aa7a8-dca2-530f-933e-cefe40326d8f'}, {'abstract': 'Patrick McEnroe, the former tennis pro, goes to church, plays with his three girls in the park and has become an avid collector of ladybugs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/nyregion/sundays-with-patrick-mcenroe-and-his-family.html', 'snippet': 'Patrick McEnroe, the former tennis pro, goes to church, plays with his three girls in the park and has become an avid collector of ladybugs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Patrick McEnroe, 46, ESPN’s affably enlightening tennis commentator, will host and call matches at the United States Open, which starts Monday at the Billie Jean King National Tennis Center in Flushing, Queens. He also works at the site year-round, as the general manager of player development for the United States Tennis Association. Mr. McEnroe retired from professional tennis in 1998, though he and his older brother John won the over-45 legends doubles tournament at the French Open this year. He and his wife, the actress-singer  Melissa Errico, live in SoHo with their three daughters, Victoria, 6, and the twins Diana and Juliette, 3 ½. Sundays are family time, either in the city or at the house they rent in Sag Harbor, N.Y., in summer. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE_SPAN/26ROUTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE_SPAN/26ROUTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE_SPAN/26ROUTINE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE_SPAN/26ROUTINE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE_SPAN/26ROUTINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26ROUTINE_SPAN/26ROUTINE