75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/20120826LOCALSTOPss-slide-TJER/20120826LOCALSTOPss-slide-TJER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/20120826LOCALSTOPss-slide-TJER/20120826LOCALSTOPss-slide-TJER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Local Stop: Sutton Place', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SUTTON PLACE (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T04:30:38+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/83a2a29b-7d2f-524c-ad9e-dd4b458cf05d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/83a2a29b-7d2f-524c-ad9e-dd4b458cf05d'}, {'abstract': 'Sutton Place is a stately, if staid, enclave on the East Side, the sort of place where the butcher shop still delivers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/nyregion/more-parkland-and-privacy-in-sutton-place.html', 'snippet': 'Sutton Place is a stately, if staid, enclave on the East Side, the sort of place where the butcher shop still delivers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sutton Place is both a grand old residential avenue (originally known as “Avenue A”), running alongside the East River from 53rd to 59th Street, and a serviceable neighborhood extending west to Second Avenue. At the river’s edge, the cross streets end in little vest-pocket parks with wide views of boats navigating the river’s treacherous currents, of Roosevelt Island’s Southpoint Park and of the monumental Queensboro and Williamsburg Bridges. Like many of its residents, Sutton Place is sedate and well maintained. Once here, people and businesses tend to stay put. “Whenever people talk about assisted living, I say, ‘No way, I’d rather live in Sutton Place!’\xa0” said Vera Mayer, who moved there from Riverdale, in the Bronx, 38 years ago. “There’s the privacy of Sutton Place, and then you walk over one block and you have everything you need.”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26LOCAL1/26LOCAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26LOCAL1/26LOCAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26LOCAL1/26LOCAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 585, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26LOCAL1/26LOCAL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1171, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26LOCAL1/26LOCAL1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26LOCAL1/26LOCAL1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/nyregion/26LOCAL1/26LOCAL1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline