er’s maiden name.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eight Fantasy Football Sleepers in 2012', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T14:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Bales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8692f8d7-1254-545f-8295-6595d6055458', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8692f8d7-1254-545f-8295-6595d6055458'}, {'abstract': 'And the politicians who reject them.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/inflation-lessons/', 'snippet': 'And the politicians who reject them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the themes I’ve hit on many times is the fact that the crisis and slump have been a testing ground for economic doctrines. People came into this mess with very different views about how the economy works, and the crisis in effect provided natural experiments that tested those views.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inflation Lessons', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T14:32:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': N