d-back demeanor and a sensible, cooperative nature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The player representatives for every major league team were summoned to a conference call with the union’s executive director, Michael Weiner, at 1 p.m. Eastern on Tuesday. The players did not know the subject but had no reason to suspect anything unusual. Weiner wasted no time in telling them the news: the day before, he had begun treatment for a brain tumor.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Union Leader Works On Despite Brain Tumor', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Extra Bases: Union Leader Works On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Michael S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T15:25:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6993bfc-1225-5c9b-9d90-93ccd6f88b5d', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6993bfc-1225-5c9b-9d90-93ccd6f88b5d'}, {'abstract': 'The decorated American sprinter Sanya Richards-Ross has taken on Rule 40, an I.O.C. regulation that limits how athletes can promote their sponsors during the Olympics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/sports/olympics/sanya-richards-ross-fights-for-olympic-athletes-rights.html', 'snippet': 'The decorated American sprinter Sanya Richards-Ross has taken on Rule 40, an I.O.C. regulation that limits how athletes can promote their sponsors during the Olympics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Olympic sprinter Sanya Richards-Ross was at BET’s Midtown studios last Wednesday for an appearance on the hip-hop show “106 & Park.” Before stepping in front of the raucous studio audience, she put on her makeup with expert precision and helped a hair stylist fashion her characteristic “S. R. R. braid.” Later she joked with the rapper Bow Wow about his stealing the two gold medals she won at the recent London Games. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sports/dog-srr/dog-srr-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sports/dog-srr/dog-srr-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sports/dog-srr/dog-srr-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/sports/dog-srr/dog-srr-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sports/dog-srr/dog-srr-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Games Are Over; Battle Goes On', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Games Are Over; Battle Goes On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards-Ross, Sanya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Olympic Committee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T15:33:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Pilon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pilon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dff7af1-fe25-52fd-b342-22ed9ee1b55d', 'word_count': 1296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dff7af1-fe25-52fd-b342-22ed9ee1b55d'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney said he had re-read Mr. Obama’s Denver acceptance speech. “He says marvelous things,” Mr. Romney said. “He just hasn’t done them.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/romney-compares-protesters-to-a-greek-chorus/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney said he had re-read Mr. Obama’s Denver acceptance speech. “He says marvelous things,” Mr. Romney said. “He just hasn’t done them.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'POWELL, Ohio — Mitt Romney had a message for the protesters who greeted him and Representative Paul D. Ryan, along with 5,000 supporters, here on Saturday morning: “This is kind of like the Greek chorus in the background,” he said, in a reference to President Obama’s speech four years ago at the Democratic convention in Denver, which he delivered in front of large Greek columns. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Compares Protesters to a Greek Chorus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'