 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/e31d74d8-261d-59a8-9032-3ac4aaaddcb1', 'word_count': 958, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e31d74d8-261d-59a8-9032-3ac4aaaddcb1'}, {'abstract': 'Confusing language in the health care reform law could mean that millions of middle-class Americans are left without affordable coverage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/opinion/sunday/a-glitch-in-health-care-reform.html', 'snippet': 'Confusing language in the health care reform law could mean that millions of middle-class Americans are left without affordable coverage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Confusing language in the health care reform law has raised the possibility that millions of Americans living on modest incomes may be unable to afford their employers’ family policies and yet fail to qualify for government subsidies to buy their own insurance. This is a bizarre development that undercuts the basic goal of health care reform — to expand the number of insured people and make their coverage affordable.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Glitch in Health Care Reform', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Glitch in Health Care Reform', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T16:22:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bd2572c-e005-5175-bca7-b0ad96cb5ab5', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bd2572c-e005-5175-bca7-b0ad96cb5ab5'}, {'abstract': 'The West Nile virus should not be shrugged off, but it is important to put it in perspective.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/opinion/sunday/the-outbreak-of-west-nile-disease.html', 'snippet': 'The West Nile virus should not be shrugged off, but it is important to put it in perspective.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nation is in the midst of an outbreak of West Nile disease that could become the worst ever recorded since the virus was first detected in New York in 1999. The number of cases has risen sharply in recent weeks. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Outbreak of West Nile Disease', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Outbreak of West Nile Disease', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'West Nile Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mosquitoes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T16:26:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/368608b6-2a77-569b-a7a3-f7f196a96dda', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/368608b6-2a77-569b-a7a3-f7f196a96dda'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney’s plan would add trillions of dollars to projected military spending, yet there is no sense that this money would lead to a more effective security strategy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/opinion/sunday/how-mr-romney-would-force-feed-the-pentagon.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney’s plan would add trillions of dollars to projected military spending, yet there is no sense that this money would lead to a more effective security strategy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney and Paul Ryan are portraying themselves as lionhearted budget-cutters, ready to slice out profligate spending in all sorts of government programs and services and lead America to lower taxes and lower deficits. Many experts say their numbers don’t add up, even if they were to impose all the cuts they want.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sunday-review/26OBSERVER/26OBSERVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/sunday-review/26OBSERVER/26OBSERVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sunday-review/26OBSERVER/26OBSERVER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sunday-review/26OBSERVER/26OBSERVER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sunday-review/26OBSERVER/26OBSERVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/sunday-review/26OBSERVER/26OBSERVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty