ntly were clothed. Actually, he apologized for “any embarrassment I have caused for my colleagues and constituents.” ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sunday-review/26looseends/26looseends-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/sunday-review/26looseends/26looseends-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sunday-review/26looseends/26looseends-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sunday-review/26looseends/26looseends-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1468, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sunday-review/26looseends/26looseends-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/sunday-review/26looseends/26looseends-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sunday-review/26looseends/26looseends-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Would Jesus Do? Skinny-Dip', 'kicker': 'Loose Ends', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Would Jesus Do? Skinny-Dip', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sea of Galilee (Israel)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yoder, Kevin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nudism and Nudity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T17:32:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dani Renan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Renan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/077bec54-8a4e-575a-a75d-57e9662efd13', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/077bec54-8a4e-575a-a75d-57e9662efd13'}, {'abstract': 'Scott Radinsky has been introspective since the Indians fired him 111 games into the season, his first season as pitching coach.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/sports/baseball/pitching-coach-scott-radinsky-faces-whatever-is-next.html', 'snippet': 'Scott Radinsky has been introspective since the Indians fired him 111 games into the season, his first season as pitching coach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scott Radinsky pitched for four major league teams from 1990 to 2001. A left-handed reliever who appeared in 557 games, Radinsky compiled a 42-25 record, a 3.44 earned run average and 52 saves. In 2004, he began working his way up the coaching ranks for the Cleveland Indians, serving as a pitching coach for four of their minor league teams. In 2010, he became the Indians’ bullpen coach, and this year, he was put in charge of the pitchers. But six days after a reporter interviewed him in Cleveland, Radinsky was home in California, without a job and pondering his next move. And he was being Radinsky, which means being engagingly different, as this two-week account demonstrates. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sports/dogRADINSKY2/dogRADINSKY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/sports/dogRADINSKY2/dogRADINSKY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sports/dogRADINSKY2/dogRADINSKY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sports/dogRADINSKY2/dogRADINSKY2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sports/dogRADINSKY2/dogRADINSKY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/sports/dogRADINSKY2/dogRADINSKY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/sports/dogRADINSKY2/dogRADINSKY2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Out of a Job, but Not Missing a Beat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Out of a Job, but Not Missing a Beat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Indians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Radinsky, Scott', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T17:33:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hillel Kuttler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hillel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kuttler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/776d6ad5-fea7-5602-abf7-d06a09643cfb', 'word_count': 1630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/776d6ad5-fea7-5602-abf7-d06a09643cfb'}, {'abstract': 'Nearly a quarter of the 124 programs in the Football Bowl Subdivision will change their conference affiliation between 2011-13. A look at the 2012 and 2013 changes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/08/26/sports/ncaafootball/shifting-conference-alignments.html', 'snippet': 'Nearly a quarter of the 124 programs in the Football Bowl Subdivision will change their conference affiliation between 2011-13. A look at the 2012 and 2013 changes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly a quarter of the 124 programs in the Football Bowl Subdivision will change their conference affiliation between 2011-13. A look at the 2012 and 2013 changes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shifting Conference Alignments', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southeastern Conference', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big East Conference', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T17:36:12+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/76acf36e-1a0b-56ee-83fe-2bf2fc97c51a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/76acf36e-1a0b-56ee-83fe-2bf2fc97c51a'}, {'abstract': 'Cliff Lee has seven losses and two victories, the fewest wins for any pitcher with at least 20 starts this season.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/lees-losing-battle-on-the-mound/', 'snippet': 'Cliff Lee has seven losses and two victories, the fewest wins for any pitcher with at least 20 starts this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Tuesday, in the seventh inning against Cincinnati at Citizens Bank Park, Cliff Lee of the Philadelphia Phillies walked Todd Frazier. It is the only walk Lee has issued in four starts this month, compared with 32 strikeouts. Alas, he has no victories in August.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lee’s Losing Battle on the Mound', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Extra Bases: Lee's Losing Battle", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Cliff', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Phillies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T17:37:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0696448d-1d98-50cb-951a-6dbc6115c4c3', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0696448d-1d98-50cb-951a-6dbc6115c4c3'}, {'abstract': 'The very idea of a culture war over values clouds what’s really at stake: women’s economic freedom.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/the-antisocial-contract/', 'snippet': 'The very idea of a culture war over values clouds what’s really at stake: women’s economic freedom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN the Republican Party meets in Tampa, Fla., this week, Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey will deliver the keynote address. He promises “hard truths.” Twenty years ago, the Democrat-turned-Republican Phil Gramm had that job. Warning to Governor Christie: no one remembers anything Mr. Gramm said. What we do remember from the 1992 convention in Houston is the jeremiad delivered by Patrick J. Buchanan, the former speechwriter for Richard M. Nixon who won nearly a quarter of Republican primary votes that year. With his invocation of a “cultural war” for the “soul of America,” Mr. Buchanan brought down the house.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Antisocial Contract', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Antisocial Contract', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akin, Todd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T17:37:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert O. Self', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Self', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e54939d-63f2-5d12-84d0-46cb46a4de21', 'word_count': 1558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e54939d-63f2-5d12-84d0-46cb46a4de21'}, {'abstract': 'The sweat-drenched practice of Bikram yoga was my medicine for anxiety, but over time, it stopped working.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/drugs-sweat-and-fear/', 'snippet': 'The sweat-drenched practice of Bikram yoga was my medicine for anxiety, but over time, it stopped working.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the fall of 2007, I attended my first yoga class. For more than four years — ever since graduation had dumped me into adulthood — I’d been leveled by anxiety. My days were plagued with worry. Was I living correctly? What if I died? What if, like in that Twilight Zone episode, the rest of the world died and I lived? Innocuous things I said to people haunted me hours later— Was that dumb? Mean? Wildly inappropriate?—until I’d squirm with shame. Unable to sleep at night, I gobbled Tylenol PM, rationalizing that it was over-the-counter, as if “over-the-counter” meant “nutritious.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drugs, Sweat and Fear', 'kicker': 'Anxiety', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Anxiety: Drugs, Sweat and Fear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yoga', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_da