-55 record and an eight-and-a-half-game lead for a playoff spot, only to squander it by going 9-18 in September. A year later, they are embarking on another final sprint, with another wild-card lead but a sharper perspective.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'By Adding Pieces, Braves Are Hoping to Complete Puzzle', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Extra Bases: By Adding Pieces, Braves Are Hoping To Complete Puzzle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wren, Frank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Braves', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-25T18:47:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21631e05-7191-561b-9f35-88110f7f6e77', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21631e05-7191-561b-9f35-88110f7f6e77'}, {'abstract': 'Using magnetic sensors that can spot changes in brain waves, researchers are working on a new, relatively inexpensive way to spot injuries and monitor brain diseases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/business/sensors-for-brain-injuries-may-help-future-athletes.html', 'snippet': 'Using magnetic sensors that can spot changes in brain waves, researchers are working on a new, relatively inexpensive way to spot injuries and monitor brain diseases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOOTBALL teams of the future — even high school squads on limited budgets — may someday have a new tool to check players for brain injuries. It’s a special form 