cience', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/fc09390c-4797-5410-ab83-bdaf5d780964', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/fc09390c-4797-5410-ab83-bdaf5d780964'}, {'abstract': 'Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva, the former president of Brazil, is winning over onetime rivals for his allies, and is anything but shy when it comes to blasting Europe’s handling of its debt crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/world/americas/brazils-ex-president-lula-back-on-political-front-lines.html', 'snippet': 'Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva, the former president of Brazil, is winning over onetime rivals for his allies, and is anything but shy when it comes to blasting Europe’s handling of its debt crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SÃO PAULO, Brazil — The trademark beard, a symbol of former President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva’s defiant past as a trade union leader and leftist political icon, is still missing from his face. Managing a smile, he touches the barren skin with his fingers, wondering aloud if it will ever grow back after an exacting battle with throat cancer that involved months of radiation therapy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/world/bull-lula/bull-lula-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/world/bull-lula/bull-lula-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/world/bull-lula/bull-lula-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': N