rivate insurers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/us/private-medicare-plans-find-success-despite-democrats-warnings.html', 'snippet': 'Beneficiaries and both parties have been generally satisfied with private Medicare Advantage plans and Medicare’s drug benefits, which are delivered by private insurers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Even as President Obama accuses Mitt Romney and Representative Paul D. Ryan of trying to privatize and “voucherize” Medicare, his administration crows about the success of private health plans in delivering prescription drug benefits and other services to Medicare beneficiaries.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/us/MEDICARE/MEDICARE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/us/MEDICARE/MEDICARE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1227, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/us/MEDICARE/MEDICARE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/26/us/MEDICARE/MEDICARE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/us/MEDICARE/MEDICARE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Democrats’ Warnings, Private Medicare Plans Find Success', 'kicker': 'Election 2012', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite Democrats’ Warnings, Private Medicare Plans Find Success', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T03:50:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8289c966-34ee-562f-b38d-fd8ce7d47ff0', 'word_count': 1255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8289c966-34ee-562f-b38d-fd8ce7d47ff0'}, {'abstract': 'Usually a late-season buyer, Boston sends high-priced stars to Los Angeles.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/25/red-sox-deal-catches-yanks-by-surprise/', 'snippet': 'Usually a late-season buyer, Boston sends high-priced stars to Los Angeles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLEVELAND — The headline-grabbing trade between the Boston Red Sox and the Los Angeles Dodgers this weekend had repercussions all around baseball, but perhaps the most interested clubhouse may have been the Yankees’. Whenever a team makes a significant move that has wide-ranging implications in the division, it always captures the attention of its rivals, and no team is measured against the Yankees more than the Red Sox, and vice versa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Red Sox’ Deal Catches Yanks by Surprise', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beckett, Josh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crawford, Carl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzalez, Adrian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loney, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T03:52:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb2858fa-c04a-59f1-a77f-27d6f170a888', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb2858fa-c04a-59f1-a77f-27d6f170a888'}, {'abstract': 'On their way to Bull Run, General Jackson’s men capture a trove of Union supplies.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/stonewalls-bounty/', 'snippet': 'On their way to Bull Run, General Jackson’s men capture a trove of Union supplies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the most grueling of the forced marches for which Gen. Stonewall Jackson was justly famous — 56 miles in 36 hours across the rolling Virginia Piedmont. To move faster, at the beginning his men were ordered to “unsling knapsacks.” They were going to live off the land. But the land didn’t offer much to sustain 23,000 Confederates. On the second day, remembered a South Carolina soldier, Berry Benson, “My only food…was a handful of parched corn and three or four small sour green apples.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stonewall’s Bounty', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords