uch these days, not in a serious way, although it certainly applied to the astronaut Neil Armstrong. It might also apply to six Asians being honored this week for their civic efforts, which, while certainly more ter...', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The word isn’t often used in a serious or confident way anymore — hero — but it’s certainly being invoked, and appropriately so, in the obituaries about Neil Armstrong. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/blogs/mag-rdv/mag-rdv-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 110, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/26/blogs/mag-rdv/mag-rdv-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 110}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/blogs/mag-rdv/mag-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 187, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/26/blogs/mag-rdv/mag-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Down to Earth, But Heroic Nonetheless', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magsaysay, Ramon, Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Magsaysay, Ramon, Foundation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T05:10:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a753f1c-f3a2-5620-af4f-8420016b9eec', 'word_count': 1088, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a753f1c-f3a2-5620-af4f-8420016b9eec'}, {'abstract': 'A few service returns are the fondest memories for last year’s U.S. Open champions, Samantha Stosur and Novak Djokovic.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/returning-champs-remember-their-returns/', 'snippet': 'A few service returns are the fondest memories for last year’s U.S. Open champions, Samantha Stosur and Novak Djokovic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Samantha Stosur did not play a single match in Arthur Ashe Stadium during the 2011 United States Open until the final, when she stunningly and resoundingly defeated heavily-favored Serena Williams, 6-2, 6-3, to win her first Grand Slam singles crown. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Returning Champs Remember Their Returns', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stosur, Samantha', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T05:22:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6b0dd07-e365-5140-8b03-4eaf4c528c02', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6b0dd07-e365-5140-8b03-4eaf4c528c02'}, {'abstract': 'The roots of Assam violence, how the Mumbai police mishandled the Azad Maidan protests and a lost girl returns from the forest decades later.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/newswallah-long-reads-editions/', 'snippet': 'The roots of Assam violence, how the Mumbai police mishandled the Azad Maidan protests and a lost girl returns from the forest decades later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a well-researched piece in the Economic and Political Weekly, Jyoti Punwani analyzes the run-up to the Aug. 11 rally at Azad Maidan in Mumbai and the fallout from the violence that occurred. There were clear signs of upcoming trouble, which the Mumbai police should have noticed, she argues, including a weeklong promotion of the rally that\xa0involved the circulation of graphic video clips taken from the Internet and widespread discussion in the Urdu press. The Mumbai police suffer from a chronic lack of intelligence about the city’s Muslim community, she argues, caused by its lack of knowledge of Urdu, lack of Muslim recruits and biased attitude.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Long Reads Editions', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tehelka', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T06:14:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79637f76-fafb-52d9-b366-0e1be9dc9223', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79637f76-fafb-52d9-b366-0e1be9dc9223'}, {'abstract': 'With more than 200 bodies found over the weekend, the assault in Daraya, a suburb of Damascus has begun to look like one of the deadliest short-term raids of the uprising.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/world/middleeast/dozens-of-bodies-are-found-in-town-outside-damascus.html', 'snippet': 'With more than 200 bodies found over the weekend, the assault in Daraya, a suburb of Damascus has begun to look like one of the deadliest short-term raids of the uprising.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DARAYA, Syria — Mass burials in this Damascus suburb on Sunday showed the carnage of the past few days in gruesome detail: scores of bodies lined up on top of one another in long, thin graves moist with mud. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/world/27syria2/27syria2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/world/27syria2/27syria2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/world/27syria2/27syria2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': '