the Aeneid by Virgil, “Do not yield to evil,” is the official slogan of the Bronx, a borough, with its history of political malfeasance, that some say is in need of a more apt phrase.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/bronx-motto/', 'snippet': 'A quote from the Aeneid by Virgil, “Do not yield to evil,” is the official slogan of the Bronx, a borough, with its history of political malfeasance, that some say is in need of a more apt phrase.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Virgil never visited the Bronx, but his legacy endures there as the borough’s official slogan, a proverb that seems to have been honored lately more in the breach than in the observance. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bronx’s Motto is Fit for Aeneas, but Maybe Little Else', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bronx’s Motto Is Fit for Aeneas, Maybe Little Else', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slogans and Mottoes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bronck, Jonas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Virgil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T15:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee1336f5-1909-5cc4-b41f-f914f662c24b', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee1336f5-1909-5cc4-b41f-f914f662c24b'}, {'abstract': 'New Jersey, the heartburn state.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/eat-here-and-get-gas/', 'snippet': 'New Jersey, the heartburn state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wow. I knew that NJ gas taxes were low, but I hadn’t realized just how low compared with neighboring states:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eat Here And Get Gas', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T15:40:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/366de025-a337-56ae-9fdb-4b00068a8851', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/366de025-a337-56ae-9fdb-4b00068a8851'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my column about chemicals that are all around us and appear to be even more dangerous than previously thought.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/reader-comments-on-my-big-chem-column/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my column about chemicals that are all around us and appear to be even more dangerous than previously thought.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column is about chemicals that are all around us and appear to be even more dangerous than previously thought. I’ve written before about these endocrine disruptors, so called because they wreak havoc with the body’s endocrine system governing hormones. Now new research indicates that their effects may be passed down from generation to generation in humans. Using doses of the chemical BPA similar to what humans encounter, the study shows that exposure to the chemical in pregnant mice can affect the sociability of their children and their children’s children. This should be devastating for Big Chem, which has so far been able to block any meaningful national curbs on endocrine disruptors. This obviously isn’t regular fodder for op-ed columns, but it seems an issue of public health and public policy that deserves more attention. I’d welcome your comments on what should be done. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reader Comments on my Big Chem Column', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T15:51:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29f577a8-95bd-5f84-b32d-6b5517150806', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29f577a8-95bd-5f84-b32d-6b5517150806'}, {'abstract': 'Among the players who could impress at the U.S. Open are the Americans Sloane Stephens and Sam Querrey, who share a coach.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/players-to-watch-at-the-u-s-open/', 'snippet': 'Among the players who could impress at the U.S. Open are the Americans Sloane Stephens and Sam Querrey, who share a coach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sloane Stephens', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Open Preview: Players to Watch', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Building Momentum: Six Who Might Stand Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dolgopolov, Alexandr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li Na', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Querrey, Sam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shv