prise/', 'snippet': 'The political documentary, a cinematic extension of the best-selling book “The Roots of Obama’s Rage,” beat two new Hollywood releases at the weekend box office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The movie capital didn’t see this coming: The political documentary “2016: Obama’s America,” a cinematic extension of the best-selling book “The Roots of Obama’s Rage,” beat two new Hollywood releases at the weekend box office and came close to passing a third. “Obama’s America,” released by Rocky Mountain Pictures, took in an estimated $6.2 million at North American theaters, for a total of $9.1 million since opening in limited release last month. Two new movies — “Hit & Run” (Open Road Films) and “The Apparition” (Warner Brothers) — flopped, taking in less than $4.7 million each. Another new release, “Premium Rush” (Sony), managed to take in only $6.3 million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Obama’s America’ Is a Box-Office Surprise', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T16:40:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By BROOKS BARNES', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'BARNES', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eea0715c-e153-584c-845c-10b5b656405c', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eea0715c-e153-584c-845c-10b5b656405c'}, {'abstract': 'Max Eisenbud began representing Maria Sharapova when she was 12. She has since become the highest-paid female athlete in the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/sports/tennis/max-eisenbud-maria-sharapovas-agent-builds-her-brand.html', 'snippet': 'Max Eisenbud began representing Maria Sharapova when she was 12. She has since become the highest-paid female athlete in the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Maria Sharapova decided that she wanted to stay at a new hotel for this year’s United States Open, her agent, Max Eisenbud, embarked on a reconnaissance mission. He met with management and interviewed security officials. He toured suites and tested room service. He took a taxi from the lobby entrance to the Midtown Tunnel, mapping out the fastest route to the tennis center in Queens.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/AGENTtennis/AGENTtennis-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/AGENTtennis/AGENTtennis-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/AGENTtennis/AGENTtennis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/AGENTtennis/AGENTtennis-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1349, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/AGENTtennis/AGENTtennis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/AGENTtennis/AGENTtennis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/AGENTtennis/AGENTtennis-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subTy