ian nightclub in one day without leaving the five boroughs. When it comes to tennis, the city also provides local players the opportinuty to play on courts that replicate tennis’s four most prestigious tournaments. I call it the New York Grand Slam.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/SUB-COURTStennis/SUB-COURTStennis-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/SUB-COURTStennis/SUB-COURTStennis-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/SUB-COURTStennis/SUB-COURTStennis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/SUB-COURTStennis/SUB-COURTStennis-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/SUB-COURTStennis/SUB-COURTStennis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/SUB-COURTStennis/SUB-COURTStennis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/SUB-COURTStennis/SUB-COURTStennis-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One City, Four Surfaces', 'kicker': 'Building a Grand Slam Experience', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One City, Four Surfaces', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T18:09:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4a6f8e3-8471-5841-a6c7-c4d8b4cd676f', 'word_count': 2400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4a6f8e3-8471-5841-a6c7-c4d8b4cd676f'}, {'abstract': 'BBC America screened the premiere episode from the forthcoming season for a select audience of fans on Saturday night in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/a-warm-welcome-for-doctor-who-in-new-york/', 'snippet': 'BBC America screened the premiere episode from the forthcoming season for a select audience of fans on Saturday night in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You might have anticipated a minor riot on Saturday night at the Ziegfeld Theater on West 54th Street, where BBC America screened the premiere episode from the forthcoming season of “Doctor Who” for a select audience of lucky fans. BBC America had mounted similar events in New York for previous seasons of this long-running science-fiction franchise, filling an East Village theater with hard-core fans who had queued for hours in hopes of being among the chosen few.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Warm Welcome for ‘Doctor Who’ in New York', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Matt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BBC America', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T18:25:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/592371e7-fe80-5807-adec-921ac6017805', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/592371e7-fe80-5807-adec-921ac6017805'}, {'abstract': 'The perfect United States Open would start with the declaration that Arthur Ashe Stadium, acknowledged as the worst major tennis stadium in the world, will be replaced.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/sports/tennis/building-your-dream-us-open-start-with-a-roof.html', 'snippet': 'The perfect United States Open would start with the declaration that Arthur Ashe Stadium, acknowledged as the worst major tennis stadium in the world, will be replaced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The perfect United States Open would start with the declaration that Arthur Ashe Stadium, acknowledged as the worst major tennis stadium in the world, with upper deck seats so bad they might as well be in Rhode Island, will be replaced. If they want to get some use out of it, fine, use it to house the Yankees’ bank vault, store snowplows or Macy’s parade floats or spare La Guardia aircraft. Anything but tennis. And you’re off and running.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/DREAMsilence/DREAMsilence-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/DREAMsilence/DREAMsilence-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1481, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/DREAMsilence/DREAMsilence-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/DREAMsilence/DREAMsilence-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/DREAMsilence/DREAMsilence-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Start With a Roof', 'kicker': 'Building Your Dream Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Start With a Roof', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ashe, Arthur, Stadium', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T18:27:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/214d926f-4829-5dee-a1ac-d4a1ca260d8d', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/214d926f-4829-5dee-a1ac-d4a1ca260d8d'}, {'abstract': 'Party conventions typically cause the largest swings in the polls during the presidential campaign — but why, and how long-lasting are the effects?', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/how-will-party-conventions-affect-the-presidential-race/', 'snippet': 'Party conventions typically cause the largest swings in the polls during the presidential campaign — but why, and how long-lasting are the effects?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republican and Democratic national conventions bring the possibility of change to this static presidential race. \xa0But how will it change, and how much? \xa0Here is some of what we know.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Will Party Conventions Affect the Presidential Race?', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T18:29:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Sides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sides', 'qualifi