Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a913a1e-f3bc-5267-affe-3db9003c0cbf', 'word_count': 1014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a913a1e-f3bc-5267-affe-3db9003c0cbf'}, {'abstract': 'With Tropical Storm Isaac threatening to gain hurricane strength, organizers could decide to truncate the convention even more, scaling back the festivities and speeches out of deference to any damage on the Gulf Coast.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/storm-poses-risks-for-republican-convention-planners/', 'snippet': 'With Tropical Storm Isaac threatening to gain hurricane strength, organizers could decide to truncate the convention even more, scaling back the festivities and speeches out of deference to any damage on the Gulf Coast.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:05 p.m. | Updated TAMPA, Fla. — It looks to be one of the worst nightmares for planners of Mitt Romney’s coronation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Storm Poses Risks for Republican Convention Planners', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T19:11:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45cf7902-babb-52e1-bac8-eb94d721da41', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45cf7902-babb-52e1-bac8-eb94d721da41'}, {'abstract': 'A very bad, no good, truly awful idea.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/golden-instability/', 'snippet': 'A very bad, no good, truly awful idea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Say this for the GOP: by resurrecting the very bad, no good, truly awful idea of a gold standard, they’ve given us something to talk about.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Golden Instability', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T19:18:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc115455-f7b9-5beb-8ba4-226ef0a82f01', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc115455-f7b9-5beb-8ba4-226ef0a82f01'}, {'abstract': 'In her novel “NW,” Zadie Smith employs a stream-of-consciousness technique to trace her characters’ thoughts in a rapidly changing London.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/books/nw-by-zadie-smith.html', 'snippet': 'In her novel “NW,” Zadie Smith employs a stream-of-consciousness technique to trace her characters’ thoughts in a rapidly changing London.', 'lead_paragraph': '“NW,” the title of Zadie Smith’s clunky new novel, refers to northwest London, where she grew up — a multicultural corner of the city that will be familiar to readers of her dazzling debut, “White Teeth.” In that earlier book Ms. Smith took a contemporary London mapped by writers like Martin Amis, Salman Rushdie and Hanif Kureishi and claimed it decisively as her own. There are glimpses, here and there in “NW,” of that cacophonous metropolis — a city in constant flux as waves of immigrants and fierce youth reinvent it year by year, day by day — but “NW” is a much smaller, more meager book than “White Teeth.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/arts/jpbook/jpbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 921, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/arts/jpbook/jpbook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1843, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/27/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Navigating Tangled Narratives', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Navigating Tangled Narratives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Zadie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name'