 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/464fc791-de50-5106-9a4d-adbb0f6ba893'}, {'abstract': 'How about bringing the pop-up concept to Grand Slam tennis?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/sports/tennis/building-your-dream-us-open-qualifying-at-a-location-near-you.html', 'snippet': 'How about bringing the pop-up concept to Grand Slam tennis?', 'lead_paragraph': 'How about bringing the pop-up concept to Grand Slam tennis? ', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Qualifying at a Location Near You', 'kicker': 'Building Your Dream Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Qualifying At a Location Near You', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T20:19:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerald Marzorati', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerald', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marzorati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b1b0299-b6b3-5939-874b-faf1e5922ae0', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b1b0299-b6b3-5939-874b-faf1e5922ae0'}, {'abstract': 'The United States Open established equal prize money for women in 1973, maybe it is time to let the women join the men in playing best-of-five matches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/sports/tennis/building-your-dream-open-all-things-equal-lets-play-five.html', 'snippet': 'The United States Open established equal prize money for women in 1973, maybe it is time to let the women join the men in playing best-of-five matches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An expanded tennis center should equal more tennis. But that does not necessarily mean expanding the field. It should mean giving the world’s greatest tennis players more time on the sport’s largest stage.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/25/sports/DREAMfivesets/DREAMfivesets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 286, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/25/sports/DREAMfivesets/DREAMfivesets-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 286}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/25/sports/DREAMfivesets/DREAMfivesets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 489, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/25/sports/DREAMfivesets/DREAMfivesets-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 978, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/25/sports/DREAMfivesets/DREAMfivesets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/25/sports/DREAMfivesets/DREAMfivesets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/25/sports/DREAMfivesets/DREAMfivesets-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'All Things Equal: Let’s Play Five', 'kicker': 'Building Your Dream Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All Things Equal: Let’s Play Five', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T20:22:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ray Krueger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krueger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1d5823d-805a-51f4-b0dd-d6107e78a498', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1d5823d-805a-51f4-b0dd-d6107e78a498'}, {'abstract': 'With the increased physicality of the sport, best-of-five matches too often turn into seemingly interminable wars of attrition rather than the displays of finesse more befitting tennis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/sports/tennis/building-your-dream-open-get-to-the-point-in-fewer-sets.html', 'snippet': 'With the increased physicality of the sport, best-of-five matches too often turn into seemingly interminable wars of attrition rather than the displays of finesse more befitting tennis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is time to do away with the best-of-five format that is burdening the men’s game at Grand Slam events. With the increased physicality of the sport, best-of-five matches too often turn into seemingly interminable wars of attrition rather than the displays of finesse more befitting tennis. The men play best-of-five only at the majors and the Davis Cup, and there is little recent evidence that best-of-three makes for undeserving winners. Just as Roger Federer, Novak Djokovic, Rafael Nadal and Andy Murray have ruled the Grand Slams, they have also dominated the best-of-three Masters 1000 events, having swept the last 16 consecutive tournaments at that level.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/DREAMthreesets/DREAMthreesets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 295, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/DREAMthreesets/DREAMthreesets-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 295}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/DREAMthreesets/DREAMthreesets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 504, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/DREAMthreesets/DREAMthreesets-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1007, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/DREAMthreesets/DREAMthreesets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/DREAMthreesets/DREAMthreesets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/DREAMthreesets/DREAMthreesets-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Get to the Point, in Fewer Sets', 'kicker': 'Building Your Dream Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Get to the Point, in Fewer Sets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T20:26:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cca590d4-8efc-5c92-8350-ff73d8676b7d', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cca590d4-8efc-5c92-8350-ff73d8676b7d'}, {'abstract': 'The United States Tennis Association has a grand opportunity to reclaim some of the dignity it squandered with luxury boxes at Arthur Ashe Stadium.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/sports/tennis/building-your-dream-open-recalling-forest-hills.html', 'snippet': 'The United States Tennis Association has a grand opportunity to reclaim some of the dignity it squandered with luxury boxes at Arthur Ashe Stadium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Tennis Center is about to get another face-lift. Who runs tennis, anyway — Con Edison and its old Dig-We-Must slogan?', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/DREAMtudor/DREAMtudor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 875, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/DREAMtudor/DREAMtudor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1751, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/DREAMtudor/DREAMtu