cal convention organizers acknowledged that they were putting on reality shows, television networks and viewers might be more inclined to watch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the political conventions were managed like a typical television show that was losing audience, think of the meetings that would be held during the run-up.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/business/media/carr-new-headshot/carr-new-headshot-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/12/business/media/carr-new-headshot/carr-new-headshot-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/business/media/carr-new-headshot/carr-new-headshot-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/business/media/carr-new-headshot/carr-new-headshot-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/business/media/carr-new-headshot/carr-new-headshot-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/12/business/media/carr-new-headshot/carr-new-headshot-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/business/media/carr-new-headshot/carr-new-headshot-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Viewers Don’t Want Conventional', 'kicker': 'The Media Equation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Viewers Don’t Want Conventional', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T20:36:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a96c1e47-fbbf-52f7-8be3-433ffd89a153', 'word_count': 1125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a96c1e47-fbbf-52f7-8be3-433ffd89a153'}, {'abstract': 'During the Indians’ ceremony to commemorate the 50th anniversary of his orbiting Earth, John Glenn remembered Neil Armstrong for his accomplishments and patriotism.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/as-indians-honor-john-glenn-he-honors-neil-armstrong/', 'snippet': 'During the Indians’ ceremony to commemorate the 50th anniversary of his orbiting Earth, John Glenn remembered Neil Armstrong for his accomplishments and patriotism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLEVELAND — An event that was planned weeks in advance was altered Sunday after the death of Neil Armstrong, the first man to walk on the moon. John Glenn, the first American astronaut to orbit Earth and a good friend of Armstrong’s, threw out the ceremonial first pitch before the Cleveland Indians’ game against the Yankees at Progressive Field.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Indians Honor John Glenn, He Honors Neil Armstrong', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Armstrong, Neil Alden', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glenn, John Herschel Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T20:52:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbd0ad46-30c0-59ee-828a-391f0536f409', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbd0ad46-30c0-59ee-828a-391f0536f409'}, {'abstract': 'Solitary confinement does more than deprive an inmate of freedom; it violates the very structure of a person’s being.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/the-living-death-of-solitary-confinement/', 'snippet': 'Solitary confinement does more than deprive an inmate of freedom; it violates the very structure of a person’s being.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are many ways to destroy a person, but the simplest and most devastating might be solitary confinement.\xa0 Deprived of meaningful human contact, otherwise healthy prisoners often come unhinged. They experience intense anxiety, paranoia, depression, memory loss, hallucinations and other perceptual distortions. Psychiatrists call this cluster of symptoms SHU syndrome, named after the Security Housing Units of many supermax prisons. Prisoners have more direct ways of naming their experience.\xa0 They call it “living death,” the “gray box,” or “living in a black hole.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Living Death of Solitary Confinement', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T21:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Guenther', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Guenther', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/128f1d89-03de-5e5a-9b30-2e887d655412', 'word_count': 1280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/128f1d89-03de-5e5a-9b30-2e887d655412'}, {'abstract': 'Poulenc’s tragic 1957 work, “Dialogues des Carmélites,” was presented by Dell’Arte Opera company in repertory with “Carmen.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/arts/music/dialogues-des-carmelites-by-dellarte-opera-ensemble.html', 'snippet': 'Poulenc’s tragic 1957 work, “Dialogues des Carmélites,” was presented by Dell’Arte Opera company in repertory with “Carmen.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Poulenc’s solemn, shattering 1957 opera “Dialogues des Carmélites” is about a novice in an order of Carmelite nuns doomed by the anticlerical extremism of the French Revolution. The young woman, Blanche, struggles mightily with the rigors of the life to which she is committing herself before ultimately, joyously accepting them. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/arts/dialogue/dialogue-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 314, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/27/arts/dialogue/dialogue-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 