Campaign”) and Matt Jones (“Breaking Bad”) have been tapped to portray members of the Schrute clan at the family’s beet farm and bed-and-breakfast. No premiere date has been set.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Casting Developments for Spinoff of ‘The Office’', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Casting Developments For Spinoff of ‘The Office’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Middleditch, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Office (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Rainn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Delfino, Majandra', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Matt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T21:40:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/84b5985a-560b-5096-9f74-5e7c95063e7f', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84b5985a-560b-5096-9f74-5e7c95063e7f'}, {'abstract': 'The rookie Jeremy Hefner shut out the Astros for eight innings and Ike Davis hit his second solo home run of the game in the ninth inning to give the Mets the victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/sports/baseball/their-season-lost-mets-search-for-silver-linings.html', 'snippet': 'The rookie Jeremy Hefner shut out the Astros for eight innings and Ike Davis hit his second solo home run of the game in the ninth inning to give the Mets the victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here was their chance to interrogate a few of the men responsible for the Mets’ latest collapse. The manager, Terry Collins, and general manager, Sandy Alderson, entertained questions from about 1,500 season-ticket holders for about an hour Sunday morning at Citi Field, as did Mike Baxter, Jon Niese and the third base coach Tim Teufel. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/YMETS/YMETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/YMETS/YMETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/YMETS/YMETS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 641, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/YMETS/YMETS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1282, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/YMETS/YMETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/YMETS/YMETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/YMETS/YMETS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'While Front Office Addresses the Future, the Mets Enjoy an All-Too-Rare Moment', 'kicker': 'Mets 2, Astros 1', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'While Front Office Addresses the Future, the Mets Enjoy an All-Too-Rare Moment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hefner, Jeremy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Ike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Astros', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T21:46:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b71ae010-f6fe-5bff-ba2e-d6d8f3491776', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b71ae010-f6fe-5bff-ba2e-d6d8f3491776'}, {'abstract': 'The Times bought the expert site in 2005 but announced its intention to sell earlier this month.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/times-to-sell-about-group-to-iacinteractive-for-300-million/', 'snippet': 'The Times bought the expert site in 2005 but announced its intention to sell earlier this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times Company has agreed to sell the About Group, which includes the About.com network of topic sites, to Barry Diller’s IAC/InterActiveCorp for about $300 million in cash, the company said on Sunday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Times Agrees to Sell About to Diller’s IAC', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_h