nding home sales for July; companies reporting earnings will include Tiffany and Heinz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ECONOMIC REPORTS Data will include the Standard & Poor’s Case-Shiller home price index for June and consumer confidence for August (Tuesday); second-quarter gross domestic product (revised), pending home sales for July and the Federal Reserve’s so-called beige book report on current economic conditions (Wednesday); weekly jobless claims, and personal income and spending for July (Thursday); the Chicago purchasing managers index for August, the Thomson Reuters/University of Michigan consumer sentiment index for August and factory orders for July (Friday). ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economic Reports for the Week Ahead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking Ahead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HJ Heinz Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Standard & Poor's Case-Shiller Home Price Index", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Confidence (Economic Indicator)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T22:46:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/120dbe7f-381f-5242-a664-8b3c3f97a509', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/120dbe7f-381f-5242-a664-8b3c3f97a509'}, {'abstract': 'Officials for the United States Open said more definitively than ever Sunday that their main venue, Arthur Ashe Stadium, will one day have a roof. But they have yet to find a material that is lightweight enough.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/u-s-t-a-confirms-schedule-change-and-reaffirms-commitment-to-roof/', 'snippet': 'Officials for the United States Open said more definitively than ever Sunday that their main venue, Arthur Ashe Stadium, will one day have a roof. But they have yet to find a material that is lightweight enough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Officials for the United States Open said more definitively than ever Sunday that their main venue, Arthur Ashe Stadium, will one day have a roof.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S.T.A. Confirms Schedule Change and Reaffirms Commitment to Roof', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Getting Close’ To Chance at Roof', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Tennis Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T22:57:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c47d9b20-5d35-5284-8bfa-81bbe5a5f983', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c47d9b20-5d35-5284-8bfa-81bbe5a5f983'}, {'abstract': 'The United States passed new patent legislation last fall and key provisions are scheduled to take effect early next year. New research analyzing the experience in Canada, after it made a similar legal change, suggests that small inventors will be hurt. Patents awarded to individual inventors dropped by 15 percent after the legislative change in Canada.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/in-canada-the-impact-of-americas-new-patent-law-is-seen/', 'snippet': 'The United States passed new patent legislation last fall and key provisions are scheduled to take effect early next year. New research analyzing the experience in Canada, after it made a similar legal change, suggests that small inventors will be...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an article published in Monday’s New York Times and available now online, I wrote about a lawsuit that challenges the constitutionality of the nation’s new patent law, the America Invents Act. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Canada, the Impact of America’s New Patent Law Is Seen', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Pennsylvania', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T23:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5436b0ca-3acf-5a00-947d-ac0d838656c9', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5436b0ca-3acf-5a00-947d-ac0d838656c9'}, {'abstract': 'Tropical Storm Isaac was expected to gather strength, potentially making landfall as a hurricane somewhere along the Gulf Coast, late on Tuesday or early Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/us/tropical-storm-isaac-gains-strength-moving-toward-keys.html', 'snippet': 'Tropical Storm Isaac was expected to gather strength, potentially making landfall as a hurricane somewhere along the Gulf Coast, late on Tuesday or early Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — As Tropical Storm Isaac churned into the Gulf of Mexico on Sunday, South Florida managed to dodge the worst of it. But the fast-moving storm appeared poised to swell into a hurricane and hit land on Wednesday between the Florida Panhandle and New Orleans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/us/27storm1/27storm1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/27/us/27storm1/27storm1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/us/27storm1/27storm1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/us/27storm1/27storm1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1352, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/us/27storm1/27storm1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/27/us/27storm1/27storm1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/us/27storm1/27storm1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Storm Gains Strength Moving Toward Coast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Anniversary of Hurricane Katrina, New Storm Threatens the Gulf Coast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Isaac (2012)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf Coast (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HURRICANE KATRINA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-26T23:01:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9f6e735-605d-5199-ac42-5d857a556bbf', 'word_count': 961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9f6e735-605d-5199-ac42-5d857a556bbf'}, {'abstract': 'Many zoos are fearful of alienating visitors with tours or wall labels that dwell bleakly on damaged coral reefs, melting ice caps or dying trees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/science/earth/zoos-and-aquariums-struggle-with-ways-to-discuss-climate-change.html', 'snippet': 'Many zoos are fearful of alienating visitors with tours or wall labels that dwell bleakly on damaged coral reefs, melting ice caps or dying trees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Sitting on an artificial mangrove island in the middle of the ray and shark “touch tank,” Lindsay Jordan, a staff member at the New