/5ab77359-6c77-5283-9e7b-e639efb8ed94', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ab77359-6c77-5283-9e7b-e639efb8ed94'}, {'abstract': 'Three divisions away from their normal home in the Scottish Premier League, the first weeks of the 2012-13 season at Rangers have been either depressing or humorous, or both, depending on one’s point of view.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/sports/soccer/rangers-going-down-with-heads-held-high.html', 'snippet': 'Three divisions away from their normal home in the Scottish Premier League, the first weeks of the 2012-13 season at Rangers have been either depressing or humorous, or both, depending on one’s point of view.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GLASGOW — “Rangers then, Rangers now, Rangers forever,” shouted the Scottish soccer club’s new owner, Charles Green, in front of almost 50,000 fans on hand for the team’s home opener Aug. 18. “Today is just the start of the journey,” he went on defiantly.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Going Down With Heads Held High', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Going Down With Heads Held High', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scottish Premier League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rangers (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T00:20:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Ruthven', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruthven', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d773c4d7-33a6-5163-8058-a12eeeff6d3d', 'word_count': 1137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d77