-5cb0-ba19-7cd235e2d279'}, {'abstract': '“2016: Obama’s America,” a documentary critique of Barack Obama’s policies and ideological roots, ranked No. 8 at the box office over the weekend as it expanded to about 1,100 theaters across the country.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/film-critique-of-obama-takes-in-6-2-million-in-wider-release/', 'snippet': '“2016: Obama’s America,” a documentary critique of Barack Obama’s policies and ideological roots, ranked No. 8 at the box office over the weekend as it expanded to about 1,100 theaters across the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Love it or loathe it, “2016: Obama’s America” — the director Dinesh D’Souza’s documentary critique of Barack Obama’s policies and ideological roots — has arrived as a box-office event.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steep Climb to ‘Fahrenheit 9/11,’ but Anti-Obama Film Is a Hit', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Steep Climb to ‘Fahrenheit 9/11,’ But Anti-Obama Film Is a Hit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T00:42:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42b51b65-3edd-5066-a3dc-1e8cac1b48e2', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42b51b65-3edd-5066-a3dc-1e8cac1b48e2'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Murray endured a heartbreaking loss in the Wimbledon final and then won the Olympic gold medal at the All England Club.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/conversations-with-andy-murray-managing-the-olympic-aftermath/', 'snippet': 'Andy Murray endured a heartbreaking loss in the Wimbledon final and then won the Olympic gold medal at the All England Club.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Throughout the United States Open, Andy Murray will be sharing his observations on his matches and his time in New York on Straight Sets. It has already been a memorable summer for Murray, who endured a heartbreaking loss in the Wimbledon final and then won the Olympic gold medal at the All England Club. Murray, the No. 3 seed, opens his United States Open on Monday against Alex Bogomolov Jr. in the second match at Arthur Ashe Stadium.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Open Preview: Andy Murray Managing the Olympic Aftermath', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Managing Aftermath Of Summer In London', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T00:47:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f729460-b6a2-50fe-bafc-901b53eb5501', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f729460-b6a2-50fe-bafc-901b53eb5501'}, {'abstract': 'The story of Ron Wyden and Paul Ryan shows just how perilous lawmaking is in today’s Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/opinion/keller-the-last-bipartisan.html', 'snippet': 'The story of Ron Wyden and Paul Ryan shows just how perilous lawmaking is in today’s Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN I first encountered Ron Wyden in 1974, he was setting up the Oregon outpost of the Gray Panthers, a lobby group founded by the liberal activist Maggie Kuhn with a broad agenda but an emphasis on empowering the elderly. Wyden, who was 25, seemed improbably boyish to be a champion of senior citizens. But he radiated a winning, wonky exuberance. He was clearly bound for a life in politics. He won an insurgent campaign for a House seat in 1980, graduated to the Senate in 1996 — and now, at age 63, has spent almost exactly half his life on Capitol Hill. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 350, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/09/18/opinion/Keller_New/Keller_New-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subTyp