www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/sports/baseball/white-sox-though-winning-cant-outdraw-cubs-in-chicago.html', 'snippet': 'While a team that is more than 25 games out of first place in its division ranks 10th in attendance in the major leagues, its crosstown rival ranks 24th despite a 70-55 record.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — The first-place White Sox, in the thick of a pennant race, hosted the Seattle Mariners at U.S. Cellular Field on Saturday on a gorgeous 86-degree evening. A crowd announced at 27,562 was on hand as the home team won, 5-4. Earlier in the day, eight miles north at Wrigley Field, a crowd announced as 35,296 watched the fifth-place Cubs lose to the equally bad Colorado Rockies.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/CHICAGO1/CHICAGO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/CHICAGO1/CHICAGO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/CHICAGO1/CHICAGO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 603, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/CHICAGO1/CHICAGO1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1206, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/CHICAGO1/CHICAGO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/CHICAGO1/CHICAGO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight'