es', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Open Preview: Should Women Play Five Sets, or Should Men Play Three?', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T01:51:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1ad8e8c-af78-5ae7-847f-ed4f7189a242', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1ad8e8c-af78-5ae7-847f-ed4f7189a242'}, {'abstract': 'There have been only modest shifts back and forth in Mitt Romney’s polling numbers since he named Representative Paul D. Ryan of Wisconsin as his vice-presidential nominee.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/26/aug-26-little-momentum-in-polls-in-advance-of-conventions/', 'snippet': 'There have been only modest shifts back and forth in Mitt Romney’s polling numbers since he named Representative Paul D. Ryan of Wisconsin as his vice-presidential nominee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The FiveThirtyEight forecast for Sunday gives Barack Obama a 69.4 percent chance of winning the Electoral College on Nov. 6. That’s essentially unchanged from Saturday — although there have been some modest shifts back and forth in the numbers over the course of the past two weeks since Mitt Romney named Representative Paul D. Ryan of Wisconsin as his vice-presidential nominee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 26: Little Momentum in Polls in Advance of Conventions', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'v