ity Council passed a law to shed light on how much money was flowing into different parks across the city. Advocates were concerned that the parks system was splitting in two: in wealthy areas of the city, gleaming, innovative green spaces, buttressed by private financing sources; elsewhere, ailing parks with far fewer resources at their disposal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/nyregion/PARKS1/PARKS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/27/nyregion/PARKS1/PARKS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/nyregion/PARKS1/PARKS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/nyregion/PARKS1/PARKS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Law to Expose City Parks’ Inequalities Is Neglected', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Law to Expose City Parks’ Inequalities Is Neglected', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parks and Recreation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CENTRAL PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'PELHAM BAY PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Cou