8-8d51-5c49-9db9-060fdb405515', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44f83098-8d51-5c49-9db9-060fdb405515'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 26 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/word-of-the-day-saturate/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 26 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'saturate •\\ˈsa-chə-ˌrat\\• verb', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | saturate', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T04:02:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/061c80da-7cc3-57c5-be06-2d2aeabf6691', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/061c80da-7cc3-57c5-be06-2d2aeabf6691'}, {'abstract': 'The Scottish designer Jonathan Saunders loves splashing color and prints across his women’s wear, but for his men’s collection he toned it down.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/prints-regent/', 'snippet': 'The Scottish designer Jonathan Saunders loves splashing color and prints across his women’s wear, but for his men’s collection he toned it down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Scottish designer Jonathan Saunders loves splashing color and prints across his women’s wear, but for his men’s collection he toned it down. “With women, I think about how to configure prints on a female body,” he says. “For men, my approach is about the combination of textures and patterns in a more architectural and functional way.” He drew from the designs of Le Corbusier and Charlotte Perriand for the collection, which features waffle jacquard coats, sporty wool mélange suits and graphic printed shirts. The idea, Saunders says, was to create clothes that are casual and “not overly formal or sharp.” Available at matchesfashion.com. ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prints Regent', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prints Regent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T04:04:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Tudela', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tudela', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db404682-41d5-5ea0-8fac-e087f9b8c862', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db404682-41d5-5ea0-8fac-e087f9b8c862'}, {'abstract': 'When Maj. Dan Rooney saw a soldier’s remains taken off his flight, Rooney was inspired to provide help through golf.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/a-scorecard-filled-with-scholarships/', 'snippet': 'When Maj. Dan Rooney saw a soldier’s remains taken off his flight, Rooney was inspired to provide help through golf.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIAWAH ISLAND, S.C. — Wesley Bauguess still chokes up every time she tells the story of how her husband, Army Maj. Larry Bauguess, died at 36 during efforts to settle a border dispute. It was May 14, 2007, and her husband was participating in a peace meeting involving United States, Afghanistan and Pakistan forces in a tribal region of Pakistan. By all accounts, the meeting was successful. The participants shook hands, posed for photographs and exchanged coins.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Scorecard Filled With Scholarships', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Scorecard Filled with Scholarships', '