a walking, talking, handshaking, baby-hugging prototype of campaigning efficiency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/us/campaign-style-of-candidate-obama-is-relaxed-and-loose.html', 'snippet': 'In this re-election campaign, the president is a scheduler’s dream, a walking, talking, handshaking, baby-hugging prototype of campaigning efficiency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEXLEY, Ohio — During his three-minute chat on Tuesday with the man introducing him to 3,300 supporters at a campaign rally here, President Obama achieved four must-dos in every politician’s instruction manual.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/us/CANDIDATE-obama1/CANDIDATE-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/27/us/CANDIDATE-obama1/CANDIDATE-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/us/CANDIDATE-obama1/CANDIDATE-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/us/CANDIDATE-obama1/CANDIDATE-4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1300, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/us/CANDIDATE-obama1/CANDIDATE-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/27/us/CANDIDATE-obama1/CANDIDATE-4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/us/CANDIDATE-obama1/CANDIDATE-4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Relaxed and Loose, Candidate Obama Hits His Mark', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Campaigns With Styles as Similar as Red and Blue: Relaxed and Loose, Candidate Obama Hits His Mark', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T04:37:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26ceb5e4-5e87-537f-b1cf-e0ed7c215e61', 'word_count': 976, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26ceb5e4-5e87-537f-b1cf-e0ed7c215e61'}, {'abstract': 'Wonder Woman and Superman embrace and kiss in issue No. 12 of “Justice League,” published by DC Comics, which is to be available in comics stores on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/books/dc-comics-unveils-new-power-couple.html', 'snippet': 'Wonder Woman and Superman embrace and kiss in issue No. 12 of “Justice League,” published by DC Comics, which is to be available in comics stores on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Do you ever feel alone?” “Of course I ... do.” And with that exchange, Wonder Woman and Superman embrace and kiss in issue No. 12 of “Justice League,” published by DC Comics, which is to be available in comics stores on Wednesday. The cover of that issue — featuring the two heroes in flight canoodling — got comic book fans talking when it was released last week. Those strong reactions, good and bad, were exactly the goal of Geoff Johns, the writer of “Justice League,” and Jim Lee, the book’s artist. In 2011 Mr. Lee was named co-publisher at DC Comics along with Dan DiDio, and Mr. Johns was named chief creative officer of DC Entertainment. In an interview they said that the Superman-Wonder Woman romance had been one of the most exciting elements they had conceived of when DC’s heroes were given a reboot last fall. “When we thought about relaunching the entire DC universe, we considered not what we were going to remove, but what we could add to the mythology,” Mr. Lee said. Mr. Johns said the romance and how it affects the characters, their teammates and their supporting casts will affect the DC universe for years. Fans with longer memories will recall that in 1986, after a previous reboot, Superman and Wonder Woman had another flirtation but eventually decided they were not right for each other. That version of Superman eventually revealed his identity to Lois Lane. He proposed to her, and they were married. And that version of Wonder Woman later caught the eye of Aquaman and Batman.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DC Comics Unveils New Power Couple', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'DC Comics Unveils New Power Couple', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Superman (Fictional Character)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DC Comics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wonder Woman (Fictional Character)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T04:42:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e83b993-fac6-52e7-a4f3-b7e097ef7be0', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e83b993-fac6-52e7-a4f3-b7e097ef7be0'}, {'abstract': 'The latest ads for the Romney-Ryan ticket suggest that under President Obama money goes from the deserving to the undeserving.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/making-the-election-about-race/', 'snippet': 'The latest ads for the Romney-Ryan ticket suggest that under President Obama money goes from the deserving to the undeserving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republican ticket is flooding the airwaves with commercials that develop two themes designed to turn the presidential contest into a racially freighted resource competition pitting middle class white voters against the minority poor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making the Election About Race', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T04:43:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas B. Edsall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None