rricane threats to New Orleans.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:01 p.m. | Various updates below |With the tropical storm that will soon be Hurricane Isaac heading in the general direction of New Orleans seven years (possibly to the day) after Hurricane Katrina topped the flood protections there, I looked back at the archived track forecasts for the 2005 storm and posted the link on Twitter and Facebook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Katrina to Isaac – How Much Has Hurricane Forecasting Improved?', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HURRICANE KATRINA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T15:54:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e574535-32c5-52a5-943f-f6ea80214b92', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e574535-32c5-52a5-943f-f6ea80214b92'}, {'abstract': 'VMware, an early leader in the products that made cloud computing possible, is offering “cloud in a box,” or a complete system that should give small- and medium-sized businesses access to Amazon-style strength. It may demonstrate why VMware last month paid a stunning $1.26 billion for a single start-up.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/vmware-let-a-thousand-clouds-contend/', 'snippet': 'VMware, an early leader in the products that made cloud computing possible, is offering “cloud in a box,” or a complete system that should give small- and medi