nk': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Alexander', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kemp, Jack F', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Woodrow', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T17:01:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1ceb032-93a3-59ff-bf8e-f2168eea0bfd', 'word_count': 1127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1ceb032-93a3-59ff-bf8e-f2168eea0bfd'}, {'abstract': 'While they often differ on how to get there, there are several areas in which the two parties have common economic goals.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/what-do-democrats-and-republicans-agree-on/', 'snippet': 'While they often differ on how to get there, there are several areas in which the two parties have common economic goals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the next two weeks, during the Republican and Democratic conventions, we’ll hear a lot about the differences between the parties. How great we are. How terrible the other guy is. How we’re better on Medicare, on Social Security, on foreign policy, on defense, on education, on taxes. How they’re awful in policy realms you never even thought of.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Do Democrats and Republicans Agree On?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T17:02:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/206965cd-2c75-58c8-86ac-28b50d65dbb6', 'word_count': 669, 'uri': 'nyt://article/206965cd-2c75-58c8-86ac-28b50d65dbb6'}, {'abstract': 'Samantha Stosur of Australia beat Petra Martic of Croatia on Monday before rain delayed other early matches at the United States Open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/sports/tennis/day-one-us-open.html', 'snippet': 'Samantha Stosur of Australia beat Petra Martic of Croatia on Monday before rain delayed other early matches at the United States Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the first storm clouds of the United States Open bearing down on the Billie Jean King National Tennis Center on Monday, the biggest challenge for the defending champion Samantha Stosur of Australia was whether she could polish off Petra Martic of Croatia before the raindrops arrived. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/27usopen2_cnd/27usopen2_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 880, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/sports/27usopen2_cnd/27usopen2_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width