'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Voucherizing Medicare', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T19:14:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/937f17be-5b75-5191-b0e3-f168c790a689', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/937f17be-5b75-5191-b0e3-f168c790a689'}, {'abstract': 'Today’s protest was about preservation, not radicalism.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/march-on-the-r-n-c/', 'snippet': 'Today’s protest was about preservation, not radicalism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — When James Ingle of the International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers took the stage at this morning’s March on the R.N.C. protest, he paraphrased Dwight Eisenhower’s 1953 “Chance for Peace” address. “Every dollar spent on the military is a dollar not spent on the poor,” he said. Eisenhower’s exact words on the opportunity cost of defense spending were: “Every gun that is made, every warship launched, every rocket fired signifies, in the final sense, a theft from those who hunger and are not fed, those who are cold and are not clothed. This world in arms is not spending money alone.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'March on the R.N.C.', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eisenhower, Dwight David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Code Pink', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T19:15:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a11093a6-9296-5bb0-8c1e-8880f899e326', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a11093a6-9296-5bb0-8c1e-8880f899e326'}, {'abstract': 'The transportation authority noted that it lost revenue from shutting down several services and it incurred high costs in preparing for and recovering from the storm.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/mta-irene/', 'snippet': 'The transportation authority noted that it lost revenue from shutting down several services and it incurred high costs in preparing for and recovering from the storm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Transportation Authority said Monday that it had submitted claims to recover $65 million in losses resulting from Tropical Storm Irene, which\xa0a year ago\xa0 felled trees onto the tracks of its commuter rails, flooded train yards and prompted an unprecedented pre-emptive subway shutdown.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'M.T.A. Seeks $65 Million for Cost of Tropical Storm Irene Last Year', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'M.T.A. Says 2011 Storm Cost System $65 Million', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Irene (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metro-North Commuter Railroad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Port Jervis (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T19:23:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51c44335-2490-509d-9849-643d2c7d56f0', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51c44335-2490-509d-9849-643d2c7d56f0'}, {'abstract': 'Babies in a study who were exposed to antibiotics within six months of birth were 22 percent more likely than those given none to be overweight at age 3, researchers reported.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/weight-implications-for-infant-antibiotics/', 'snippet': 'Babies in a study who were exposed to antibiotics within six months of birth were 22 percent more likely than those given none to be overweight at age 3, researchers reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Young farm animals given antibiotics gain weight quickly. Now a new study suggests that the same thing may happen to human infants treated with antibiotics.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/health/well_risks/well_risks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/health/well_risks/well_risks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'sup