der both of Republican incompetence in handling Hurricane Katrina seven years ago, and the party’s no-less-disastrous plans to further cut emergency-related spending.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Storm, Again', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Storm, Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Isaac (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Emergency Management Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HURRICANE KATRINA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARMY CORPS OF ENGINEERS', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T21:15:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/01fa7aa0-8054-57fc-bb49-3d63bb579b23', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01fa7aa0-8054-57fc-bb49-3d63bb579b23'}, {'abstract': 'A vivid reminder of the nation’s growing debt as Republicans gather in Tampa.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/as-convention-opens-debt-clock-ticks/', 'snippet': 'A vivid reminder of the nation’s growing debt as Republicans gather in Tampa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Republicans gather in Tampa, Fla., for their convention, party leaders want to drive home a message to voters: The federal debt is hurtling toward $16 trillion, and it is President Obama’s fault.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Convention Opens, Debt Clock Ticks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Election 2012 | Debt Clock: A Reminder That Time Is Money', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Priebus, Reince R', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T21:16:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0046236-891a-5594-8424-eb56da3b00a4', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0046236-891a-5594-8424-eb56da3b00a4'}, {'abstract': 'The Republicans will attack Mr. Obama if he goes to Camp Lejeune next month, but they will also attack him if he does not go.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/would-presenting-a-marine-citation-help-president-obama/', 'snippet': 'The Republicans will attack Mr. Obama if he goes to Camp Lejeune next month, but they will also attack him if he does not go.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his Op-Ed column today, Roger Cohen quoted a letter from John Kael Weston to President Obama.\xa0 Mr. Weston, who served for the State Department in the city of Fallujah in Iraq and in Afghanistan’s Helmand Province, suggested that Mr. Obama appear in person at Camp Lejeune, in North Carolina, next month to present the Presidential Unit Citation to soldiers who fought under the Marine Expeditionary Brigade-Afghanistan from May 29, 2009, to April 12, 2010.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should the President Deliver a Marine Citation in Person?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T21:19:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7cbb90f-c192-51b4-a598-c3295548ecd3', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7cbb90f-c192-51b4-a598-c3295548ecd3'}, {'abstract': 'Recent studies on how some snakes and other animals detect infrared light provide striking examples of how new lifestyles can evolve when old genes learn new tricks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/science/animals-lifestyles-evolve-when-old-genes-learn-new-tricks.html', 'snippet': 'Recent studies on how some snakes and other animals detect infrared light provide striking examples of how new lifestyles can evolve when old genes learn new tricks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early one evening a few years ago, I took a short hike with my wife, Jamie, in the Cockscomb Basin Wildlife Sanctuary in Belize. The large, lush reserve is known for its healthy population of jaguars, so, following closely behind our guide, we kept our eyes peeled for the elusive cats. We saw a few tracks and some claw marks on trees, but elected to leave the jungle before nightfall. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/28/science/28CREA_SPAN/28JPCREA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/28/science/28CREA_SPAN/28JPCREA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/28/science/28CREA_SPAN/28JPCREA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/28/science/28CREA_SPAN/28JPCREA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/28/science/28CREA_SPAN/28JPCREA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStanda