 says Ben Benjamin Jr., the unlucky hero of “The Revised Fundamentals of Caregiving,” Jonathan Evison’s third and most stealthily powerful novel, “I had decent options. O.K., options.” Ben had a work history of painting parade floats and stacking scones in a bakery, then switched gears to become a doting father and husband. He gave his all to domesticity. He had no idea how evanescent his ordinary life would be. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/28/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 725, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/28/arts/book/book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1449, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/28/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/28/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/28/arts/book/book-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dented Souls, on the Road to Redemption', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dented Souls, On the Road To Redemption', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Evison, Jonathan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T21:27:51+0000', 'do