nt Obama to help Mitt Romney prepare for his debates.', 'lead_paragraph': ' TAMPA, Fla. – It’s time for Senator Rob Portman to dust off those old Obama audiobooks again. He has been tapped to reprise his role of playing President Obama to help Mitt Romney prepare for his debates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Portman to Reprise Obama Role for Romney Debate Preparation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T22:07:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f03ef8c9-6ce1-5ae7-96da-1f3e1922bda1', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f03ef8c9-6ce1-5ae7-96da-1f3e1922bda1'}, {'abstract': 'A Romney campaign attack ad accuses the president of gutting the welfare-to-work requirement.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/27/a-cynical-portrait-of-two-political-bases/', 'snippet': 'A Romney campaign attack ad accuses the president of gutting the welfare-to-work requirement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — The Romney campaign isn’t going to admit that its outrageous welfare ad, falsely accusing President Obama of gutting the welfare-to-work requirement, is a nakedly racial appeal to white working-class voters. (Tom Edsall’s expert dissection this morning makes that clear.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cynical Portrait of Two Political Bases', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Welfare (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-27T22:11:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d03a8c62-6dab-53e4-9aa6-87e76715fc4f', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d03a8c62-6dab-53e4-9aa6-87e76715fc4f'}, {'abstract': 'Pankaj Mishra’s new book, “From the Ruins of Empire: The Intellectuals Who Remade Asia,” is part of his tussle with Niall Ferguson and other writers over Western imperialism and capitalism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/books/pankaj-mishras-new-book-ruins-of-empire.html', 'snippet': 'Pankaj Mishra’s new book, “From the Ruins of Empire: The Intellectuals Who Remade Asia,” is part of his tussle with Niall Ferguson and other writers over Western imperialism and capitalism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1988 Pankaj Mishra was a recent university graduate in the northern Indian city of Benares with big literary ambitions he had little idea how to fulfill. But when he heard that a local library was going to be auctioning back issues of The New York Review of Books as waste paper, he knew exactly what to do. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/28/arts/mishra/mishra-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 815, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/28/arts/mishra/mishra-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 20