 States. Around 400,000 people die each year from smoking, which cuts lives short on average about 13 years. And that does not include the 50,000 who die from exposure to secondhand smoke or the 8.6 million whose illnesses are caused by smoking. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Warning: Smoking Can Kill You’', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Warning: Smoking Can Kill You’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T01:46:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/65128a05-e326-53a2-86fb-1386906a127f', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65128a05-e326-53a2-86fb-1386906a127f'}, {'abstract': 'Home rule, an obscure provision in the state constitution under which the state gives limited autonomy to local municipalities, has been cited twice this month in overturning state laws.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/nyregion/justices-cite-vague-rule-twice-this-month.html', 'snippet': 'Home rule, an obscure provision in the state constitution under which the state gives limited autonomy to local municipalities, has been cited twice this month in overturning state laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, opponents of a payroll tax to help finance the Metropolitan Transportation Authority argued that it unfairly made people in the suburbs underwrite a service that mostly benefited people in New York City.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 Courts Cite a Vague Rule in Rejecting State Laws', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Courts Cite A Vague Rule In Rejecting State Laws', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Payroll Tax', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Local Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T01:49:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Russ Buettner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Russ', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buettner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/707e49ad-e476-52b8-ae4a-a0f2b005b7d8', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/707e49ad-e476-52b8-ae4a-a0f2b005b7d8'}, {'abstract': 'The best approach to containing Tehran’s nuclear ambitions is still a diplomatic solution, despite growing pressure for military action from Israel and its supporters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/opinion/irans-nuclear-quest.html', 'snippet': 'The best approach to containing Tehran’s nuclear ambitions is still a diplomatic solution, despite growing pressure for military action from Israel and its supporters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Iran appears to have installed a few hundred more centrifuges at its deep underground site known as Fordow, thus enhancing its ability to produce uranium enriched to 20 percent, a purity that can be converted relatively quickly to bomb-grade fuel. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran’s Nuclear Quest', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran’s Nuclear Quest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nonaligned Movement', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T01:51:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f95c5d1c-689e-53f7-99a3-97a7f5040e21', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f95c5d1c-689e-53f7-99a3-97a7f5040e21'}, {'abstract': 'A deadly explosion at Venezuela’s largest oil refinery over the weekend has killed at least 41 people, leaving the neighboring town of Punto Fijo to cope with the destruction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/08/28/world/americas/20120828-venezuela.html', 'snippet': 'A deadly explosion at Venezuela’s largest oil refinery over the weekend has killed at least 41 people, leaving the neighboring town of Punto Fijo to cope with the destruction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A deadly explosion at Venezuela’s largest oil refinery over the weekend has killed at least 41 people, leaving the neighboring town of Punto Fijo to cope with the destruction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', '