rticle/40ca6478-e2d5-517f-8318-d1288607dcfd', 'word_count': 48, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40ca6478-e2d5-517f-8318-d1288607dcfd'}, {'abstract': 'Drug traffickers in Rio slums try to pacify the people caught in their cynical grasp by throwing them free block parties.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/brazilian-drug-traffickers-try-controlling-the-slums-with-parties/', 'snippet': 'Drug traffickers in Rio slums try to pacify the people caught in their cynical grasp by throwing them free block parties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIO DE JANEIRO — A Colt AR-15 rifle was aimed at my gut, an FMK-3 sub-machine gun a little lower. The men holding the weapons were barely that, and they shared a bottle of cheirinho da loló, passing the cheap chloroform-ether mix back and forth, sniffing it for a glossy high. This was a baile funk, Rio de Janeiro’s illegal block party of music, guns and narcotics — one of those all-night festas that exist in myth for those who cannot gain access to them or are too fearful to attend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Party Down, Favela Style', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gangs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rio de Janeiro (Brazil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T08:53:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brett Forrest', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brett', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Forrest', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93e37c3e-f213-5add-be49-773889a54b77', 'word_count': 868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93e37c3e-f213-5add-be49-773889a54b77'}, {'abstract': 'A preview of a new season of austerity threats, Greek bonds and the potential demise of the world’s most infuriating currency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/magazine/7-story-lines-to-watch-in-the-euro-crisis-this-fall.html', 'snippet': 'A preview of a new season of austerity threats, Greek bonds and the potential demise of the world’s most infuriating currency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In June, it seemed as if any day might bring about the collapse of the Greek economy and with it, the entire euro zone and its decade-old currency. Then in July and August, it seemed as if everyone was on vacation. Now they’re back — finance officials and political leaders have been flying all over Europe to meet with one another — and along with them the crisis that has been raging for the last two years. Here is a guide to the new season’s most intriguing (and terrifying) story lines.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02economy/02economy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02economy/02economy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 790}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02economy/02economy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02economy/02economy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non