4-5813-8244-eb16e3f8b53c', 'word_count': 1271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29199d36-8394-5813-8244-eb16e3f8b53c'}, {'abstract': 'Adál Maldonado’s work covers nearly 40 years and seeks — often weirdly, often humorously — to make sense of what it means to be Puerto Rican.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/an-artists-search-fo-puerto-rican-identity/', 'snippet': 'Adál Maldonado’s work covers nearly 40 years and seeks — often weirdly, often humorously — to make sense of what it means to be Puerto Rican.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adál Maldonado has been a photographic documentarian, a Dadaist visual satirist and a Nuyorican conceptual artist.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Puerto Rican Identity, In and Out of Focus', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puerto Ricans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Puerto Rico', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Juan (Puerto Rico)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T09:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ea7d2ad-59c2-57af-8349-3b11989abd85', 'word_count': 1247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ea7d2ad-59c2-57af-8349-3b11989abd85'}, {'abstract': 'When do you shop to get ready for the new school year?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/back-to-school-first-then-shop/', 'snippet': 'When do you shop to get ready for the new school year?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHO is Samantha Paradise?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Back-to-School Shopping, After the First Day', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T09:03:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d8f891a-14ac-5819-8591-3e6f27336eb5', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d8f891a-14ac-5819-8591-3e6f27336eb5'}, {'abstract': 'The Colts will certainly be better than they were last season, and they have Andrew Luck in place, but there is still a lot of work ahead.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/indianapolis-colts-2012-n-f-l-season-preview/', 'snippet': 'The Colts will certainly be better than they were last season, and they have Andrew Luck in place, but there is still a lot of work ahead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes the best thing to do is tap Control-Alt-Delete twice and move forward. There’s no shame in doing that after a disastrous 2-14 season when, for 12 years before that, you ran one of the sharpest programs in your industry. The Indianapolis Colts’ owner,\xa0Jim Irsay, can be proud of what his club accomplished during the Peyton Manning Era, and he can be proud of the all-in approach he has taken in starting what he hopes will one day come to be known as the Andrew Luck Era.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indianapolis Colts, 2012 N.F.L. Season Preview', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T09:18:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddb68620-9191-5bcc-9242-141f3d19c1b4', 'word_count': 2631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddb68620-9191-5bcc-9242-141f3d19c1b4'}, {'abstract': 'Ezra Dyer learns about the pleasures and pitfalls of mobile living with the Via, an R.V. based on the platform and powertrain of the Mercedes-Benz Sprinter van.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/driving-the-winnebago-via/', 'snippet': 'Ezra Dyer learns about the pleasures and pitfalls of mobile living with the Via, an R.V. based on the platform and powertrain of the Mercedes-Benz Sprinter van.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WILMINGTON, N.C. — After five minutes of wrestling with the electronic parking-meter station, I had my receipts to place beneath the windshield wiper. A roving meter maid would see that I had paid for my spot. And the spot next to it. And the one next to that, thus answering the question, “Where do you park a 25-foot Winnebago Via motor coach?” I’ll take spaces 113 through 115, thanks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Driving the Winnebago Via', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recreational Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Winnebago Industries Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ezra Dyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ezra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b700881d-b79a-5e4f-9ba6-93a7510206d2', 'word_count': 1223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b700881d-b79a-5e4f-9ba6-93a7510206d2'}, {'abstract': 'A scientist and her team kayak their way to daily measurements of the forests of the ABC islands of Alaska, pondering wilderness of the past and present.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/hunting-for-debris-and-answers-in-alaska/', 'snippet': 'A scientist and her team kayak their way to daily measurements of the forests of the ABC islands of Alaska, pondering wilderness of the past and present.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Throughout months of measuring trees, I carried the hope of finding a glass float on the outer coast of Southeast Alaska. Green and blue and made of hand-blown glass, they are remnants of the deep sea fishing industry, used long before plastic and other materials kept nets afloat. Most that remain today originated in Japan. Since I last wrote for the Green Blog, we’ve visited 24 sites in dead, dying and stressed yellow cedar forests in the West Chichagof-Yakobi Wilderness over the course of a three-week expedition.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hunting for Debris and Answers in Alaska', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wilderness Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Treinish, Gregg', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Land Management', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T10:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren E. Oakes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Oakes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebba88a7-2c81-5258-a16f-d4bb655ded5b', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebba88a7-2c81-5258-a16f-d4bb655ded5b'}, {'abstract': 'Will Packwood, who joined the club’s academy at 14, has made a good impression in his professional debut this season.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/19-year-old-american-flashes-potential-for-birmingham-city/', 'snippet': 'Will Packwood, who joined the club’s academy at 14, has made a good impression in his professional debut this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the season well under way in England, one of the more interesting American players is Will Packwood, a 19-year-old who looks to become a regular with Birmingham City. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '19-Year-Old American Flashes Potential for Birmingham City', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T10:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Sciaretta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sciaretta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d4e2316-7d50-51dc-bdb3-549c06d591d7', 'word_count': 789, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d4e2316-7d50-51dc-bdb3-549c06d591d7'}, {'abstract': 'Paul D. Ryan likes to cite the economist Friedrich von Hayek as an influence, but Hayek supported national health care and questioned Ronald Reagan’s policies, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/why-hayek-isnt-paul-ryans-guru/', 'snippet': 'Paul D. Ryan likes to cite the economist Friedrich von Hayek as an influence, but Hayek supported national health care and questioned Ronald Reagan’s policies, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul. He is the author of “The Benefit and the Burden: Tax Reform – Why We Need It and What It Will Take.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Hayek Isn’t Paul Ryan’s Guru', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'von Hayek, Friedrich', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T10:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01da7d68-957d-5e3c-bf22-a51d052ae5fd', 'word_count': 1016, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01da7d68-957d-5e3c-bf22-a51d052ae5fd'}, {'abstract': 'With Republicans cautiously proceeding to open their convention on Tuesday, Democrats have decided to move ahead with their no-holds-barred counterprogramming, including several aggressive ads aimed at Mitt Romney and a campaign swing by President Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/storms-potential-complicates-democratic-response-to-g-o-p-convention/', 'snippet': 'With Republicans cautiously proceeding to open their convention on Tuesday, Democrats have decided to move ahead with their no-holds-barred counterprogramming, including several aggressive ads aimed at Mitt Romney and a campaign swing by President...', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — With Republicans cautiously proceeding to open their convention on Tuesday, Democrats have decided to move ahead with their no-holds-barred counterprogramming, including a campaign swing by President Obama as Mitt Romney prepares to accept the nomination.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Storm’s Approach Complicates Democratic Response to G.O.P. Convention', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic National Committee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T10:12:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/140a3244-02a2-5d97-93b7-18628a90ae39', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/140a3244-02a2-5d97-93b7-18628a90ae39'}, {'abstract': 'Officer in New York City’s police department said he is focusing on Urdu and Bengali speakers in hunt for terrorists.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/speaking-urdu-or-bengali-a-cause-for-police-suspicion-in-nyc/', 'snippet': 'Officer in New York City’s police department said he is focusing on Urdu and Bengali speakers in hunt for terrorists.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Earlier this summer, Thomas P. Galati, commanding officer of the New York Police Department’s elite intelligence division, sat for an unusual legal interrogation, during which he talked of his keen interest in Urdu-speaking New Yorkers,” Michael Powell wrote in The New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Speaking Urdu or Bengali a Cause for Police Suspicion in NYC', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T10:28:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'perso