tup School is essentially a finishing school for employees.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/a-start-up-tries-to-prepare-students-to-work-in-start-ups/', 'snippet': 'Conceived at the Harvard Innovation Lab, Boston Startup School is essentially a finishing school for employees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For new graduates, shifting from college to a full-time job can deliver a jolt of culture shock. That’s doubly true for those who join start-ups, where teams are small and newcomers are often expected to acclimate quickly, finding their way without much formal training.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Start-Up Tries to Prepare Students to Work in Start-Ups', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Start-Up Prepares Students To Work With Start-Ups', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Startup School', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T11:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Bruder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50443f55-0eae-5b71-91a8-a50577f07f67', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50443f55-0eae-5b71-91a8-a50577f07f67'}, {'abstract': 'At Staten Island Mall we met Val Pacuku, whose peach sherbert-colored pants and tan wedges we