'nyt://article/16a7cc3a-d965-5789-8857-47da88f6682e', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16a7cc3a-d965-5789-8857-47da88f6682e'}, {'abstract': 'The police chief of Kandahar Province, Gen. Abdul Raziq, survived a powerful suicide car bombing by the Taliban late Monday, Afghan officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/world/asia/afghan-police-chief-escapes-attack-that-kills-4-civilians.html', 'snippet': 'The police chief of Kandahar Province, Gen. Abdul Raziq, survived a powerful suicide car bombing by the Taliban late Monday, Afghan officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANDAHAR, Afghanistan — The Taliban tried and failed to kill one of their most hated enemies late on Monday when the police chief of Kandahar Province, who is pursuing an aggressive campaign against the insurgents in their former southern homeland, survived a powerful suicide car bombing that killed four civilians and wounded 20 more, Afghan officials said Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/world/asia/29afghanistan/29afghanistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/29/world/asia/29afghanistan/29afghanistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/world/asia/29afghanistan/29afghanistan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/world/asia/29afghanistan/29afghanistan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'c