retto-first-look-at-the-new-coffee-collective-roastery-and-coffee-bar/', 'snippet': 'The small roaster’s distinctive coffees have always had a devoted following; now they have an elegant setting to match, in Copenhagen’s quiet Frederiksberg district.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ristretto | First Look at the New Coffee Collective Roastery and Coffee Bar', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T15:06:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oliver Strand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oliver', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d3b02f1-08c3-5c4a-8d71-cb4ab6e8ed55', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d3b02f1-08c3-5c4a-8d71-cb4ab6e8ed55'}, {'abstract': 'What was billed as a roving dance party attracts the attention of the police not far from the convention.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/a-more-lighthearted-protest-overnight/', 'snippet': 'What was billed as a roving dance party attracts the attention of the police not far from the convention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — The protesters began assembling just before 11 p.m. on Monday night, with people arriving in twos and threes at Centennial Park, in Ybor City, until there were about 100 of them gathered in the darkness a block away from one of the city’s main night life areas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A More Lighthearted Protest Overnight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T15:06:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67381428-50d4-5899-914e-0c33c8a2a83a', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67381428-50d4-5899-914e-0c33c8a2a83a'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Soul of It All,” Mr. Bolton will chronicle his rise to pop stardom (and perhaps his alleged obsession with the “Pirates of the Caribbean” movie franchise).', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/avast-ye-readers-memoir-coming-from-michael-bolton/', 'snippet': 'In “The Soul of It All,” Mr. Bolton will chronicle his rise to pop stardom (and perhaps his alleged obsession with the “Pirates of the Caribbean” movie franchise).', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is the tale of Captain Jack Sparrow, a pirate so brave on the seven seas — wait, sorry, scratch that: This is the tale of the singer Michael Bolton, the latter-day crooner with hair spun from gold, who’ll be unspooling his life story in a new memoir. The Center Street imprint of the Hachette Book Group said on Tuesday that it had acquired a book titled “The Soul of It All” from Mr. Bolton, the singer-songwriter (and devoted fan of the “Pirates of the Caribbean” movies, at least according to a recent Lonely Island/”Saturday Night Live” video). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Avast, Ye Readers! Memoir Coming From Michael Bolton', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolton, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hachette Book Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T15:14:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a33cc3e2-5fca-53ef-b17d-5543fd23053b', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a33cc3e2-5fca-53ef-b17d-5543fd23053b'}, {'abstract': 'The United Nations refugee agency said that 10,200 Syrians had crossed into Jordan last week, and Syrian activists reported deadly government airstrikes in Idlib, near Turkey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/world/middleeast/Syria.html', 'snippet': 'The United Nations refugee agency said that 10,200 Syrians had crossed into Jordan last week, and Syrian activists reported deadly government airstrikes in Idlib, near Turkey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — The United Nations refugee agency said on Tuesday that the number of Syrian refugees fleeing to Jordan last week had more than doubled from the previous week, raising further fears of a growing exodus from Syria that threatens to overwhelm international relief efforts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/world/middleeast/29syria/29syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy