ing a daily paper at The New Orleans Times-Picayune and its Alabama newspapers, said it would end the daily distribution of two more of its newspapers, The Post-Standard in Syracuse, and The Patriot-News in Harrisburg, Pa.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newspapers in Syracuse and Harrisburg, Pa., to End Daily Distribution', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Newhouse to Stop Printing Daily Newspapers in Syracuse and Harrisburg, Pa.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harrisburg (Pa)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syracuse (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T16:54:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc07cedb-d362-544e-bfcf-216bfcc7a64c', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc07cedb-d362-544e-bfcf-216bfcc7a64c'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama campaign is trying to expand its numbers and support among young voters, a group that tends to go to the polls at lower rates than older voters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/us/politics/obama-heads-to-campus-to-press-for-young-voters.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama campaign is trying to expand its numbers and support among young voters, a group that tends to go to the polls at lower rates than older voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT COLLINS, Colo. — Annie Hartnett was not old enough to vote in 2008 when she volunteered for the Obama campaign at the University of Iowa, where an older sister was a student. Now 21 and a leader of the Iowa State University Democrats, she said she was as excited as she was four years ago to be working for President Obama — yet she struggled to describe something that is missing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/us/YOUTH1/YOUTH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/29/us/YOUTH1/YOUTH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/us/YOUTH1/YOUTH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/us/YOUTH1/YOUTH1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/us/YOUTH1/YOUTH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/29/us/YOUTH1/YOUTH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/us/YOUTH1/YOUTH1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Courts the Votes of a Less-Engaged Youth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Visits to Campuses, Obama Keeps Campaigning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'sub