f bragging rights.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/world-class-underdogs/', 'snippet': 'When you’re an outcast of FIFA — like the soccer players from Darfur, Zanzibar and Northern Cyprus — you also get a certain amount of bragging rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How does it feel to be part of a soccer team that loses its first two games of an international tournament by a combined score of 33-0?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'World-Class Underdogs', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vice (Magazine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T17:21:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hugo Lindgren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hugo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindgren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8c20fda-f10f-522c-9837-dfb732f17509', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8c20fda-f10f-522c-9837-dfb732f17509'}, {'abstract': 'The United States Navy credited aggressive patrolling by international forces and increased vigilance by the shipping industry for a decrease in piracy in the waters around the Horn of Africa.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/world/africa/piracy-around-horn-of-africa-has-plunged-us-says.html', 'snippet': 'The United States Navy credited aggressive patrolling by international forces and increased vigilance by the shipping industry for a decrease in piracy in the waters around the Horn of Africa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Acts of piracy in the treacherous waters around the Horn of Africa have fallen sharply in 2012, according to statistics released by the United States Navy. The Navy credits aggressive patrolling by international forces and increased vigilance by the commercial shipping industry for the decrease.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/world/PIRATES/PIRATES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/29/world/PIRATES/PIRATES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/world/PIRATES/PIRATES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/world/PIRATES/PIRATES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/world/PIRATES/PIRATES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/29/world/PIRATES/PIRATES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/world/PIRATES/PIRATES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Reports That Piracy Off Africa Has Plunged', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Reports That Piracy Off Africa Has Plunged', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Piracy at Sea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARABIAN SEA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Red Sea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Aden', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T17:23:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f693e3ec-a2d3-5fc2-82c4-a5b704681868', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f693e3ec-a2d3-5fc2-82c4-a5b704681868'}, {'abstract': 'Chipotle Mexican Grill rounds change in some markets, to avoid handling coins that might slow down the checkout process.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/is-a-penny-rounded-a-penny-lost-ask-chipotle/', 'snippet': 'Chipotle Mexican Grill rounds change in some markets, to avoid handling coins that might slow down the checkout process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My children are fans of the food at Chipotle Mexican Grill. Soft, fresh tacos; black beans; melted cheese — what’s not to like? So I was intrigued when I read about a payment policy that the restaurant chain uses in some locations. It’s called “rounding” (which, by coincidence, my daughter is learning about at elementary school).', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is a Penny Rounded a Penny Lost? Ask Chipotle', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Penny Rounded, Penny Lost?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chipotle Mexican Grill Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T17:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b426efa-9d33-54d0-878f-fede28a09978', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b426efa-9d33-54d0-878f-fede28a09978'}, {'abstract': 'A look at what’s to come on Tuesday from the Republican National Convention in Tampa, Fla.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/timescast-politics-schedule-and-convention-day-at-a-glance/', 'snippet': 'A look at what’s to come on Tuesday from the Republican National Convention in Tampa, Fla.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Hurricane Isaac forced the cancellation of the first day of the Republican National Convention, events are getting under way on Tuesday, and The Times’s political unit will be broadcasting live with the latest from Tampa, Fla., beginning at 2 p.m. Here are a few of the highlights from the program:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast Politics Schedule and Convention Day at a Glance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T17:34:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbb93711-aa1a-539c-b281-a52515da7438', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbb93711-aa1a-539c-b281-a52515da7438'}, {'abstract': 'Though used to dislocation and stress, some military families are deeply anxious about the “what-ifs” of coming defense budget cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/amid-a-defense-budget-fight-military-families-plan-for-the-worst/', 'snippet': 'Though used to dislocation and stress, some military families are deeply anxious about the “what-ifs” of coming defense budget cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My husband doesn’t whisper. So when he leaned into me before his 2009 deployment and whispered that soldiers – many soldiers – were going to die where they were going in Afghanistan, I listened. Yet I am the kind of practical woman who could hear his fear and chalk it up to predeployment jitters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid a Defense Budget Fight, Military Families Plan for the Worst', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Lindsey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Joint Base Lewis-McChord (Wash)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T17:47:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Bushatz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bushatz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1