itle': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f289959f-be6b-562e-b2d7-89cba739396d', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f289959f-be6b-562e-b2d7-89cba739396d'}, {'abstract': 'With the start of football season, The Times is inviting readers to share their favorite tailgating recipes.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/serving-up-tailgate-recipes/', 'snippet': 'With the start of football season, The Times is inviting readers to share their favorite tailgating recipes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back-to-school sales should include deals on charcoal, propane, bratwurst and ribs, amid other cooking essentials, because it’s also tailgate time. As much as hard hits, long runs, cheerleaders and marching bands, the delicacies served in parking lots and living rooms before and during games are a huge part of football.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Serving Up Tailgate Recipes', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T19:51:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Luttrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Luttrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b59ee03-e533-54d0-96bb-97f9a6dfb6ed', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b59ee03-e533-54d0-96bb-97f9a6dfb6ed'}, {'abstract': 'For fall, a print shirt; Beth Ditto sunglasses by Mykita; Odyssey jeans From J Brand; and Coach and Frye co