; rigorous deconstruction, and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scientific American discusses the claim of a group of prominent researchers on consciousness recently convening at Cambridge: a neocortex is not a precondition of conscious experience. In fact, these researchers believe there are good reasons to suppose that the neural substrates of experiential states, and of emotive states as well, are present in creatures with brains structured very differently from our own. Most interestingly, even some invertebrates—specifically, octopuses—appear to show signs of being conscious. “That does not necessarily mean that you could have a distraught octopus or an elated cuttlefish on your hands,” Katherine Harmon writes. But it does mean we need to think of consciousness as being spread across a wide range of species, and being realizable by a number of different neurological structures. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stone Links: Consider the Octopus', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Critchley, Simon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scientific American', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T20:30:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark de Silva', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Silva', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4126d5a-d6dd-5e45-8910-98c105d8146b', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4126d5a-d6dd-5e45-8910-98c105d8146b'}, {'abstract': 'A second day of deadly unrest struck the Kenyan city of Mombassa after the death of the influential cleric, Sheik Aboud Rogo Mohammed, who had been accused of aiding a Somali militant group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/world/africa/grenade-attack-in-kenya-kills-police-officer-as-riots-rage.html', 'snippet': 'A second day of deadly unrest struck the Kenyan city of Mombassa after the death of the influential cleric, Sheik Aboud Rogo Mohammed, who had been accused of aiding a Somali militant group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — A Kenyan police officer died and 13 others were wounded late on Tuesday in a grenade attack during riots in Mombasa over the killing of a radical cleric, a senior police official said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/world/africa/29kenya2/29kenya2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/29/world/africa/29kenya2/29kenya2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/world/africa/29kenya2/29kenya2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/world/africa/29kenya2/29kenya2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1272, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/world/africa/29kenya2/29kenya2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/29/world/africa/29kenya2/29kenya2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLar