ce': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/28/technology/28bits-photos/28bits-photos-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 224, 'width': 352, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/28/technology/28bits-photos/28bits-photos-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 224, 'width': 352, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Facebook App That Aims to Keep Private Photos Private', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McAfee Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T20:41:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11351352-d612-5e08-a4d9-56b5f11c3993', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11351352-d612-5e08-a4d9-56b5f11c3993'}, {'abstract': 'Ron Paul supporters and other conservative activists object to what they call a power grab by the party establishment.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/over-loud-boos-romney-supporters-pass-new-rules/', 'snippet': 'Ron Paul supporters and other conservative activists object to what they call a power grab by the party establishment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — Mitt Romney’s supporters passed new rules governing future primaries over the loud boos of Ron Paul supporters and other conservative activists who had objected to what they said was a power grab by the party’s establishment leaders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Over Loud Boos, Romney Supporters Pass New Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T20:42:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccfa9275-df77-5b03-998f-8653d5373867', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccfa9275-df77-5b03-998f-8653d5373867'}, {'abstract': 'On Sept. 10, the Russian performance artists and punk activists known as Pussy Riot, three of whom were sentenced to prison in Moscow this month, will be the subject of a pop-up exhibition and fund-raiser at Lombard-Freid Projects, a Chelsea gallery.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/an-art-show-for-pussy-riot/', 'snippet': 'On Sept. 10, the Russian performance artists and punk activists known as Pussy Riot, three of whom were sentenced to prison in Moscow this month, will be the subject of a pop-up exhibition and fund-raiser at Lombard-Freid Projects, a Chelsea galle...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Russian performance artists and punk activists known as Pussy Riot, three of whom were sentenced to prison in Moscow this month, continue to garner international support, most recently from the art world. On Sept. 10, the group will be the subject of a pop-up exhibition and fund-raiser at Lombard-Freid Projects, a Chelsea gallery. The event is to be organized by Victoria Dushkina, a curator from Moscow, and Amnesty International, which has supported the cause of Pussy Riot for months. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Art Show for Pussy Riot', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pussy Riot Fund-Raiser At Chelsea Gallery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCartney, Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tolokonnikova, Nadezhda', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMNESTY INTERNATIONAL', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pussy Riot', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T20:43:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa5a466d-072b-5398-9e38-146ea728abdd', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa5a466d-072b-5398-9e38-146ea728abdd'}, {'abstract': 'In Scott Lasser’s novel, a lawyer returns to his blighted hometown and decides that he can’t leave it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/books/say-nice-things-about-detroit-scott-lassers-new-novel.html', 'snippet': 'In Scott Lasser’s novel, a lawyer returns to his blighted hometown and decides that he can’t leave it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the classic Motown song “Dancing in the Street,” Martha and the Vandellas sang, “Can’t forget the Motor City.” That’s easy enough to say when the topic is music: the MC5, the White Stripes, Bob Seger, Diana Ross, Smokey Robinson and countless other influential musicians have their roots there. But when it comes to literature, forgetting Detroit can be regrettably easy to do. The city may be one of our great, if crumbling, metropolises, yet contemporary fiction set there is sparse.  Dean Bakopoulos and Charles Baxter have written memorably about Detroit’s suburbs and nearby Ann Arbor. But fiction about present-day Detroit itself? Not so much lately; it’s almost as if novels themselves had had to flee the post-1960s urban blight. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/arts/book/book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2041, 'width': 1469, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/arts/book/book-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/29/arts/book/book-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/arts/book/book-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'About Black and White and a Great City’s Blight', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'About Black and White and a Great City’s Blight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lasser, Scott', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-28T20:47:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Langer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Langer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e231bb53-776a-5485-837c-2e7c4c1274d4', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e231bb53-776a-5485-837c-2e7c4c1274d4'}, {'abstract': 'The Times will be providing updates and analysis from the Republican National Convention in Tampa.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/live-updates-from-the-republican-national-convention/', 'snippet': 'The Times will be providing updates and analysis from the Republican National Convention in Tampa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney’s six-year quest for the Republican presidential nomination will culminate Tuesday afternoon when the 4,400 delegates gathered here officially make him their choice to reclaim the White House from President Obama and the Democrats. The roll call vote will be followed by an evening of speakers includi