in our own party.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/us/subPLATFORM/subPLATFORM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/29/us/subPLATFORM/subPLATFORM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/us/subPLATFORM/subPLATFORM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/us/subPLATFORM/subPLATFORM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1445, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Platform’s Sharp Turn to Right Has Conservatives Cheering', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Platform’s Sharp Turn to the Right Has Conservatives Cheering', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T01:10:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f094761-cab0-59fb-8e39-6c265b69e0ba', 'word_count': 1122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f094761-cab0-59fb-8e39-6c265b69e0ba'}, {'abstract': 'Unhappy teenage girls, seeking thrills, leave their homes for Los Angeles in this movie, which came out of a Sundance Film Festival workshop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/movies/little-birds-first-film-by-elgin-james.html', 'snippet': 'Unhappy teenage girls, seeking thrills, leave their homes for Los Angeles in this movie, which came out of a Sundance Film Festival workshop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lily and Alison are best friends, unhappy teenagers coming of age on the photogenically desolate shores of California’s storied Salton Sea. That salty, accidentally man-made body of water, with its shoals of calcified fish and bird bones under a relentless desert sun, supplies both a bleak atmosphere and some convenient metaphors for “Little Birds,” Elgin James’s Sundance-incubated debut feature, which follows Lily and Alison on a journey from boredom to danger.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/arts/29little/29little-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/29/arts/29little/29little-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/arts/29little/29little-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': N