aul delegates from several states protested what they said were new rules by the Republican leadership to squelch their movement’s rise within the party.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/us/subPAUL/subPAUL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/us/subPAUL/subPAUL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Paul Supporters’ Protest Signals Deeper Division', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paul Supporters’ Protest Signals Deeper Division', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T03:19:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57b20caa-0b23-5fef-a061-16442c774438', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57b20caa-0b23-5fef-a061-16442c774438'}, {'abstract': 'Mrs. Romney used her prime-time speech at the Republican National Convention to try to take some of the sheen off her husband’s glossy image.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/in-speech-ann-romney-plays-to-the-heart/', 'snippet': 'Mrs. Romney used her prime-time speech at the Republican National Convention to try to take some of the sheen off her husband’s glossy image.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ann Romney introduced her husband Tuesday night to the nation and to the Republican Party that had nominated him as president with a rousing speech that exhorted Americans, “You can trust Mitt.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Speech, Ann Romney Plays to the Heart', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T03:21:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c44c5a17-45ef-59e1-b920-c394b89a121e', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c44c5a17-45ef-59e1-b920-c394b89a121e'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Gunther spent 40 years in office as a state senator, making him the longest-serving member of the General Assembly in Hartford.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/nyregion/george-l-gunther-connecticut-legislator-dies-at-92.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Gunther spent 40 years in office as a state senator, making him the longest-serving member of the General Assembly in Hartford.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George L. Gunther, an iconoclastic Republican state senator from Connecticut who spent 40 years in office, making him the state’s longest-serving member of the General Assembly, died on Sunday in Branford, Conn. He was 92 and lived in Stratford.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': '