8:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/523dd26f-d365-5c75-8ab2-b2b2fbbd41f7', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/523dd26f-d365-5c75-8ab2-b2b2fbbd41f7'}, {'abstract': 'Over the past several days, there have been 15 national polls released, and they tell a pretty consistent story.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/28/aug-28-a-moment-of-polling-clarity/', 'snippet': 'Over the past several days, there have been 15 national polls released, and they tell a pretty consistent story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At FiveThirtyEight, we’re usually consumed by how much the polls disagree with one another, and where the race stands once you filter through all that noise. But every now and then, the pollsters make our job easy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 28: A Moment of Polling Clarity', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMahon, Linda E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Christopher Scott', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T03:44:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af83bb61-516e-5166-944e-d8007788e5b2', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af83bb61-516e-5166-944e-d8007788e5b2'}, {'abstract': 'Park officials have told 1,700 people they may have been exposed to a potentially lethal, rodent-borne disease while visiting one of Yosemite’s low-cost lodging areas this summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/us/rare-illness-has-killed-2-lodgers-at-yosemite.html', 'snippet': 'Park officials have told 1,700 people they may have been exposed to a potentially lethal, rodent-borne disease while visiting one of Yosemite’s low-cost lodging areas this summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — With its bears, slippery rock walls and waterfalls, Yosemite National Park, where at least 18 people died last year, is known as a particularly dangerous patch of America the beautiful.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/us/YOSEMITE/YOSIMITE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/us/YOSEMITE/YOSIMITE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1354, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rare Illness Has Killed 2 Lodgers at Yosemite', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rare Illness Has Killed 2 Lodgers At Yosemite', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hantavirus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'gloc