cles again Tuesday, extending its Major League Baseball rights for $5.6 billion from 2014 to 2021. At an average of $700 million annually, ESPN is doubling what it is now paying.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ESPN Extends M.L.B. Deal, Doubling What It Pays Yearly', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ESPN Extends M.L.B. Deal, Doubling What It Pays Yearly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T04:23:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d21ab7cf-ec3e-5923-a1fb-cfbebc8af028', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d21ab7cf-ec3e-5923-a1fb-cfbebc8af028'}, {'abstract': 'Promotions are just one way the new owner of the Yokohama BayStars baseball team is trying to shake up the old guard, with the hope of turning a profit within three years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/sports/baseball/new-owner-of-yokohama-baystars-seeks-to-revitalize-franchise-in-japan.html', 'snippet': 'Promotions are just one way the new owner of the Yokohama BayStars baseball team is trying to shake up the old guard, with the hope of turning a profit within three years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YOKOHAMA, Japan — It is fair to say that offering discounted tickets to men who come to the ballpark dressed in drag is an unconventional approach to filling seats. The same can be said