onvention in Tampa, Fla.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An interactive look at the most talked-about speeches from the Republican National Convention in Tampa, Fla.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Key Speeches From the Republican National Convention', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Ann', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T06:01:28+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/993258d0-c24e-5cad-b3ab-81311f823e44', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/993258d0-c24e-5cad-b3ab-81311f823e44'}, {'abstract': 'Ann Romney’s speech was most effective when it was confirming the impression that Mitt Romney is an unusual sort of throwback.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/the-case-for-noblesse-oblige/', 'snippet': 'Ann Romney’s speech was most effective when it was confirming the impression that Mitt Romney is an unusual sort of throwback.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One useful way to think about Mormon culture is to envision an outpost of old-fashioned Yankees dropped down in the Mountain West. The early Mormons were Anglo-Saxon Northeasterners who wended their way west, WASPs who dropped the Protestantism and added polygamy but otherwise kept many of the habits of their New York and New England forebears: a communitarian spirit and a flinty work ethic, and an attitude toward their own success that mixed self-effacement and noblesse oblige.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Case for Noblesse Oblige', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mormons (Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Ann', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T07:07:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f586b20a-bf20-554c-b36d-5dae0162c594', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f586b20a-bf20-554c-b36d-5dae0162c594'}, {'abstract': 'This question is about the varying amount of sleep people of different races get each night.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/test-yourself-math-aug-29-2012/', 'snippet': 'This question is about the varying amount of sleep people of different races get each night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Test your math skills with this question created by Pete Diamantis at Math for America from the article “How Well You Sleep May Hinge on Race.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | Math, Aug. 29, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T08:33:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/444f4e54-40de-5116-b8cb-740ed49b79fa', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/444f4e54-40de-5116-b8cb-740ed49b79fa'}, {'abstract': 'As an anti-government rally fizzles, the promise of Tahrir Square dies out.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/the-promise-of-egypts-revolution-dies-out/', 'snippet': 'As an anti-government rally fizzles, the promise of Tahrir Square dies out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — In the best of times the hotel touts and papyrus vendors of Talaat Harb Square are persistent and sly. They sidle up to tourists with a smile and chitchat, until they’ve bonded just enough to pitch a souvenir or a tour of the Pyramids. By then the tourist can’t walk away without being rude.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cairo, City of Fights', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T08:46:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graeme Wood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graeme', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7e63e37-cc42-5e7e-bde0-94127a69731c', 'word_count': 648, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7e63e37-cc42-5e7e-bde0-94127a69731c'}, {'abstract': 'India’s Supreme Court dismissed an appeal from the lone surviving terrorist in the 2008 Mumbai attacks.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/death-sentence-upheld-for-kasab/', 'snippet': 'India’s Supreme Court dismissed an appeal from the lone surviving terrorist in the 2008 Mumbai attacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Indian Supreme Court on Wednesday upheld the death sentence of Ajmal Kasab, the sole surviving gunman from the attacks that killed 166 people in Mumbai in November 2008.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death Sentence Upheld for Kasab', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kasab, Mohammed Ajmal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T08:47:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5be49a9d-41b4-5c84-9bb4-82ac90ce486b', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5be49a9d-41b4-5c84-9bb4-82ac90ce486b'}, {'abstract': 'The comedian turned the worst four months of her life into material.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/magazine/tig-notaro-has-cancer-go-ahead-laugh.html', 'snippet': 'The comedian turned the worst four months of her life into material.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, you went onstage at Largo in Los Angeles and did a very unusual set. You told the audience how four months ago you contracted a life-threatening infection. Days after your release from the hospital, your mother died after a freak fall in her house. Shortly after that, you were given a diagnosis of Stage 2 breast cancer. You opened your set saying, “Thank you, I have cancer, thank you.” The crowd laughed. Did they know?  I don’t think a lot did, no. People were laughing, and I remember being onstage thinking, We’re all standing on this bridge and only I know that it’s about to collapse. And it did.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02talk/mag-02Talk-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02talk/mag-02Talk-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02talk/02talk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02talk/02talk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02talk/02talk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tig Notaro Has Cancer. Go Ahead, Laugh.', 'kicker': 'Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Terribly Funny', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Notaro, Tig', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breast Cancer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Andrew Goldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Andrew', 'lastname': 'Goldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/2138c432-b114-5748-9153-a686e8ee7dfc', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2138c432-b114-5748-9153-a686e8ee7dfc'}, {'abstract': 'Angry moms, petty tweets and one reporter’s naïve dream of finding meaning in sauerkraut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/magazine/feel-the-loathing-on-the-campaign-trail.html', 'snippet': 'Angry moms, petty tweets and one reporter’s naïve dream of finding meaning in sauerkraut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometime early last May, I began to have this goofy notion, which turned into a daydream and eventually became a recurring fantasy. It went like this: One morning, I would wake up to the news that the previous evening, with no advance warning to the media, Mitt and Ann Romney stopped by the White House at the invitation of Barack and Michelle Obama. No one was certain what happened while they were there or what they talked about or how it came together, though eventually some details would trickle out. The couples told funny stories from the campaign trail and shared pictures of their families. Mitt drank lemonade, and Michelle led a moonlit tour of her garden. Everyone ate hot dogs loaded with toppings, which inspired a cable christening of the “Sauerkraut Summit.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02campaign1/02campaign1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 366, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02campaign1/02campaign1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 366}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02campaign1/mag-02campaign-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 623, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02campaign1/mag-02campaign-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 913, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02campaign1/02campaign1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02campaign1/02campaign1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02campaign1/02campaign1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Feel the Loathing on the Campaign Trail', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Feel the Loathing on the Campaign Trail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subj