, 'snippet': 'Are the Titans in a rebuilding mode? It’s hard to say, but Jake Locker’s development this season will go a long way to answering the question.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What are we to make of the Tennessee Titans? Midway through August, they announced that 24-year-old Jake Locker would be their starting quarterback in Week 1. Locker will be playing in a more open, advanced system than what offensive coordinator Chris Palmer was able to run last season, and he’ll be throwing to first-round rookie receiver Kendall Wright. These seem like the makings of a team in rebuilding mode – or at least of a team looking to begin a new chapter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tennessee Titans, 2012 N.F.L. Season Preview', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tennessee Titans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T10:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71549370-3c21-59d4-adbe-ca8d769a772e', 'word_count': 2566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71549370-3c21-59d4-adbe-ca8d769a772e'}, {'abstract': 'Highlight matches at the United States Open.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/what-to-watch-on-wednesday-at-the-us-open/', 'snippet': 'Highlight matches at the United States Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since joining the tour in 2007, John Isner has done nothing but surprise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Watch on 