 the outcome of Sunday’s episode of “Breaking Bad” if you haven’t already seen it. Also, it was recommended to us by Josh Groban, so caveat emptor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Very Different Ending for Sunday’s ‘Breaking Bad’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T13:28:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a026d57c-f35d-5532-8324-cd7dc24d325e', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a026d57c-f35d-5532-8324-cd7dc24d325e'}, {'abstract': 'It is hard to conceive of Mr. Romney winning in November but losing Florida, and the linchpin to winning Florida is usually found in and around Tampa’s Hillsborough County.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/in-florida-tampa-is-essential-to-romney-election-hopes/', 'snippet': 'It is hard to conceive of Mr. Romney winning in November but losing Florida, and the linchpin to winning Florida is usually found in and around Tampa’s Hillsborough County.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We continue our Presidential Geography series, a one-by-one examination of the peculiarities that drive the politics in all 50 states and the District of Columbia. Here, a look at Florida, the Sunshine State. FiveThirtyEight spoke with Lance deHaven-Smith, a professor of public administration and policy at Florida State University, and Daniel A. Smith, a professor in political science at the University of Florida.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Florida, Tampa Is Essential to Romney Election Hopes', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T13:38:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micah Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/657921a0-99ca-5126-a583-10a1fa6270fa', 'word_count': 1146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/657921a0-99ca-5126-a583-10a1fa6270fa'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the writers and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/what-were-reading-510/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the writers and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bloomberg Businessweek: It’s just so hot. There’s a D.J. And strobes. Dancing under black lights. There’s karaoke. Why, it’s — Applebee’s? The chain is doing an after-hours makeover at its restaurants, which will now offer a late-night bar-and-club scene for singles and 30-somethings. They’re calling it Club Applebee’s, or simply, “the bees.” — Glenn Collins ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T13:39:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dda826cc-5a59-550e-9280-5eccf18893d2', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dda826cc-5a59-550e-9280-5eccf18893d2'}, {'abstract': 'What I didn’t watch.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/unconventional/', 'snippet': 'What I didn’t watch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No, I didn’t watch it. In the immortal words of Barbara Bush, why should I waste my beautiful mind on that?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unconventional', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T13:40:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8ebdd40-33c0-596a-887e-43ae23c3daea', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8ebdd40-33c0-596a-887e-43ae23c3daea'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Aviation Administration will appoint a group to study air travel rules and make recommendations on changes, but in-flight cellphone calls will continue to be banned.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/daily-report-f-a-a-to-review-rules-restricting-electronic-devices/', 'snippet': 'The Federal Aviation Administration will appoint a group to study air travel rules and make recommendations on changes, but in-flight cellphone calls will continue to be banned.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Air travelers who carry smartphones, digital tablets and other electronic devices have long complained abou