potsdam-im-in-the-best-place/', 'snippet': 'The first Goal blog installment from Alex Singer, an American woman now playing for one of the top teams in Germany’s Bundesliga, 1.FFC Turbine Potsdam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'POTSDAM, Germany — I feel like I’m in the best place I can be.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turbine Potsdam: ‘I’m in the Best Place’', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA Champions League (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'German Bundesliga', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Freedom (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Potsdam (Germany)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T14:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ec0f886-98d0-57a1-992a-36892024ba8f', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ec0f886-98d0-57a1-992a-36892024ba8f'}, {'abstract': 'A senior fellow at the Council on Foreign Relations traces the evolution in economic thinking about the relationship between global trade and economic stagnation in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/changing-views-of-globalizations-impact/', 'snippet': 'A senior fellow at the Council on Foreign Relations traces the evolution in economic thinking about the relationship between global trade and economic stagnation in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a recent Economix post (as part of the election-year project called The Agenda) explaining that many economists see globalization as a major cause of the income slowdown in this country, Edward Alden of the Council on Foreign Relations noted on Twitter that this view was a new one. For years, economists argued that increased global trade did not have a large effect on wages or employment in the United States. The editors invited Mr. Alden — the director of the Renewing America initiative at the council, who previously helped run a council task force on trade and investment policy – to send along a more detailed version of his point.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the New View of Globalization', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Protectionism (Trade)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T14:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f52b8ad1-f6cb-5e92-bb75-83180770c7c3', 'word_count': 1124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f52b8ad1-f6cb-5e92-bb75-83180770c7c3'}, {'abstract': 'Amazon.com rarely talks about what it is doing with its cloud service, Amazon Web Services. But a look through the company’s help-wanted listings reveals a lot about where it is headed.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/amazons-a-w-s-job-openings-reveal-its-future/', 'snippet': 'Amazon.com rarely talks about what it is doing with its cloud service, Amazon Web Services. But a look through the company’s help-wanted listings reveals a lot about where it is headed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amazon.com does not talk much about what it does in operating the world’s largest publicly available computing cloud. But if you read between the lines you can get a sense of where it is going – global expansion, a new kind of Web browser, and spy work for the United States government.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/22/technology/bits/bitpix-amazon-bezos2/bitpix-amazon-bezos2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/22/technology/bits/bitpix-amazon-bezos2/bitpix-amazon-bezos2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1481, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/22/technology/bits/bitpix-amazon-bezos2/bitpix-amazon-bezos2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/04/22/technology/bits/bitpix-amazon-bezos2/bitpix-amazon-bezos2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/22/technology/bits/bitpix-amazon-bezos2/bitpix-amazon-bezos2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Job Openings at Amazon Web Services Reveal Its Future', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web Browsers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T14:02:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f12b122e-5d8e-5af2-b067-5ff53262f009', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f12b122e-5d8e-5af2-b067-5ff53262f009'}, {'abstract': 'Seth MacFarlane, the “Family Guy” creator and “Ted” director, will be joined by musical guest Frank Ocean when he hosts the “SNL” season premiere on Sept. 15.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/seth-macfarlane-joseph-gordon-levitt-and-daniel-craig-to-host-saturday-night-live/', 'snippet': 'Seth MacFarlane, the “Family Guy” creator and “Ted” director, will be joined by musical guest Frank Ocean when he hosts the “SNL” season premiere on Sept. 15.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Coming off a summer in which his directorial debut, “Ted,” was the season’s breakout hit comedy, Seth MacFarlane will take a victory lap as the host of “Saturday Night Live” for its premiere on Sept. 15, NBC said on Wednesday. Mr. MacFarlane, the creator and star of the Fox animated comedy “Family Guy” (who moonlights as a big-band singer), will be joined for the start of the 38th “SNL” season by musical guest Frank Ocean, and a cast that is still in flux but will include stalwarts like Bill Hader and Fred Armisen.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seth MacFarlane, Joseph Gordon-Levitt and Daniel Craig to Host ‘Saturday Night Live’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Saturday Night Live’ Names a Few Hosts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Craig, Daniel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon-Levitt, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MacFarlane, Seth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ocean, Frank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mumford & Sons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muse (Music Group)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T14:05:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cee43df-ec7e-5c93-adbc-a47d42e47a38', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cee43df-ec7e-5c93-adbc-a47d42e47a38'}, {'abstract': 'Daikin Industries may have finally gotten its wish by buying Goodman Global from the private equity firm Hellman & Friedman, but its shareholders do not seem as enthusiastic.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/daikin-shares-drop-after-goodman-deal-is-announced/', 'snippet': 'Daikin Industries may have finally gotten its wish by buying Goodman Global from the private equity firm Hellman & Friedman, but its shareholders do not seem as enthusiastic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daikin Industries may have finally gotten its wish by buying Goodman Global from the private equity firm Hellman & Friedman, but its shareholders do not seem as enthusiastic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daikin Shares Drop After Goodman Deal Is Announced', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Daikin Industries Ltd', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goodman Global, Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HELLMAN & FRIEDMAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T14:16:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1127c44-005c-5d30-9f2d-fc5879fd65b3', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1127c44-005c-5d30-9f2d-fc5879fd65b3'}, {'abstract': 'The Lede is following Hurricane Isaac on Wednesday, which has made landfall along the Gulf Coast. Updates will mix breaking news from our correspondents in the region with eyewitness accounts, photos and videos of the storm posted online.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/latest-updates-on-hurricane-isaac-2/', 'snippet': 'The Lede is following Hurricane Isaac on Wednesday, which has made landfall along the Gulf Coast. Updates will mix breaking news from our correspondents in the region with eyewitness accounts, photos and videos of the storm posted online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lede followed Hurricane Isaac on Wednesday, as it lashed the Gulf Coast with rain and high winds. Updates mixed breaking news from our correspondents in the region with eyewitness accounts, photos and videos of the storm posted online. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Latest Storm Updates on Isaac', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf Coast (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T14:16:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d91f162-8ca0-57f4-a97d-500ee50905d0', 'word_count': 1363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d91f162-8ca0-57f4-a97d-500ee50905d0'}, {'abstract': 'Dan Barber is collaborating with the International Culinary Center in Manhattan on a farm-to-table curriculum for students.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/for-culinary-students-a-new-kind-of-field-work/', 'snippet': 'Dan Barber is collaborating with the International Culinary Center in Manhattan on a farm-to-table curriculum for students.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Farm-to-table cooking is a phenomenon, it’s an obsession, and now it’s a curriculum. The chef Dan Barber is collaborating with the International Culinary Center in Manhattan on courses that will incorporate ecological agriculture and rural food production into a program in classic cooking techniques.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Culinary Students, a New Kind of Field Work', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T14:20:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92c389b2-89aa-549b-a221-8bb4e2fcfb7e', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92c389b2-89aa-549b-a221-8bb4e2fcfb7e'}, {'abstract': 'While the revised bankruptcy plan will give shareholders 1 percent of Dynegy, some shareholders (along with the United States government) are objecting to provisions that would release management, directors and shareholders from legal liability.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/in-exit-dynegy-shareholders-look-to-eke-out-something/', 'snippet': 'While the revised bankruptcy plan will give shareholders 1 percent of Dynegy, some shareholders (along with the United States government) are objecting to provisions that would release management, directors and shareholders from legal liability.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dynegy’s controlling shareholders, led by Carl C. Icahn, entered Chapter 11 with a roar, but they are about to leave rather meekly. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Exit, Dynegy Shareholders Look to Eke Out Something', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dynegy Inc.', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}]