verage.', 'lead_paragraph': ' What Hurricane Isaac might mean for energy prices. | Second-quarter growth revised upward. | How new media are dominating convention coverage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Business Day Live: Bracing for the Storm in Energy Prices', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T14:59:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c47e803a-6ee4-5c2e-9e3f-1df4f3f2f272', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c47e803a-6ee4-5c2e-9e3f-1df4f3f2f272'}, {'abstract': 'Mini-Unit 2 of our Election Unit is about researching the issues. The unit includes lesson activities, projects and useful handouts.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/election-unit-part-2-what-are-the-issues/', 'snippet': 'Mini-Unit 2 of our Election Unit is about researching the issues. The unit includes lesson activities, projects and useful handouts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All week long we are publishing sections of our Election Unit, each day’s post a new “mini-unit” based on an essential question. All five posts work together to take students through a series of hands-on research and presentation projects that will help them understand the candidates and the issues in this year’s presidential race.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Election Unit, Part 2: What Are the Issues?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T15:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/707b4efc-5a15-5d18-8a4a-416c5db52fa2', 'word_count': 1449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/707b4efc-5a15-5d18-8a4a-416c5db52fa2'}, {'abstract': 'Three picture books about the difficulties of sleep.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/books/lucy-cant-sleep-by-amy-schwartz-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Three picture books about the difficulties of sleep.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It starts with pregnancy, and it just doesn’t stop. Expectant women can’t sleep, and their bedmates probably can’t either. New parents can’t sleep. Newborns can’t sleep. Even young children, once they’re supposedly “sleeping through the night,” often can’t sleep either.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/books/29insomniacs/29insomniacs-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/29/books/29insomniacs/29insomniacs-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/books/29insomniacs/29insomniacs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/books/29insomniacs/29insomniacs-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1223, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/books/29insomniacs/29insomniacs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/29/books/29insomniacs/29insomniacs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/books/29insomniacs/29insomniacs-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Insomnia for Beginners', 'kicker': "Children's Books", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hilts, Sean', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hilts, Ben', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Amy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolf, Karina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T15:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamela Paul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a6c50e8-be07-5cbe-a371-7f349c7cdad1', 'word_count': 776, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a6c50e8-be07-5cbe-a371-7f349c7cdad1'}, {'abstract': 'Dan Peres, the editor in chief of Details, said the time was right for American designers to assert themselves here, especially since men’s wear has been growing in stature in recent years.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/a-push-for-american-mens-wear/', 'snippet': 'Dan Peres, the editor in chief of Details, said the time was right for American designers to assert themselves here, especially since men’s wear has been growing in stature in recent years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Men’s wear has long played second fiddle at New York Fashion Week, though a handful of respectable designers and labels like Duckie Brown, Nautica, Joseph Abboud, Tommy Hilfiger and Michael Bastian continue to show their clothes for guys amid a sea of competition for attention from women’s designers. A lot of big guns decamped for market weeks in Europe a while ago, so Calvin Klein and Tom Ford usually show in Milan and Scott Sternberg of Band of Outsiders took his collection to Paris this summer. Now London is putting a bigger focus on men’s wear shows and Mr. Ford has said he will show there in January.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Push for American Men’s Wear', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABBOUD, JOSEPH', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bartlett, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bastian, Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Tom', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hilfiger, Tommy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brown, Duckie', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nautica Enterprises', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T15:07:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bb4e87f-aa06-53b0-b201-955564990513', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bb4e87f-aa06-53b0-b201-955564990513'}, {'abstract': 'More than a third of “pre-retirees” say they don’t plan to retire.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/postponing-retirement-indefinitely/', 'snippet': 'More than a third of “pre-retirees” say they don’t plan to retire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a third of adults near retirement age — 35 percent — said last year that they simply don’t expect to retire. That was up from just 29 percent two years earlier.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Postponing Retirement Indefinitely', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not Retiring, Not by Choice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Savings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Society of Actuaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T15:07:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/309fc193-6a9d-515a-85f5-63dc15f6b98f', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/309fc193-6a9d-515a-85f5-63dc15f6b98f'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Dooley, a figment of the humorist Finley Peter Dunne’s imagination, is remembered 100 years later.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/he-skewered-politics-and-new-york-without-actually-existing/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Dooley, a figment of the humorist Finley Peter Dunne’s imagination, is remembered 100 years later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Henry James, Henry Adams and Theodore Roosevelt read him regularly. The historian Charles A. Beard said that given the toxic level of public controversies in the early 20th century, he “relaxed the tension of the ‘moral overstrain.’” The columnist Franklin P. Adams called his meditations “merely truth concealed in sugar-coated idiom and dialect” to conceal his loathing of injustice, sham and selfish stupidity. Through hundreds of columns beginning in 1893, he was a national sage and satirist laureate. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'He Skewered Politics and New York, Without Actually Existing', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunne, Finley Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T15:12:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ce16073-8d41-5b64-b20e-46def01c0a71', 'word_count': 1247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ce16073-8d41-5b64-b20e-46def01c0a71'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Fogle was imprisoned in Washington State in a life filled with true crimes, and used his experiences for fictional accounts in novels and an eventual movie.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/us/james-fogle-author-of-drugstore-cowboy-dies-at-75.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Fogle was imprisoned in Washington State in a life filled with true crimes, and used his experiences for fictional accounts in novels and an eventual movie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Fogle, a thief and addict who committed real crimes, then turned them into fiction in his novel “Drugstore Cowboy,” which became an acclaimed film, died Aug. 23 in the infirmary ward of the Washington State Reformatory in Monroe, Wash. He was 75.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/sports/fogle1/fogle1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/30/sports/fogle1/fogle1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/sports/fogle1/fogle1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/sports/fogle1/fogle1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 810, 'width': 1351, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/sports/fogle1/fogle1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/30/sports/fogle1/fogle1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/sports/fogle1/fogle1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'James Fogle, Author of ‘Drugstore Cowboy,’ Dies at 75', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'James Fogle, 75, ‘Drugstore Cowboy’ Author', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Drugstore Cowboy (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fogle, James', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T15:17:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/18e9de92-a7a8-5004-b5f7-63d5c1605717', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18e9de92-a7a8-5004-b5f7-63d5c1605717'}, {'abstract': 'Environmental advocates and community groups worry that a proposed natural gas pipeline in the Rockaways could damage fragile ecosystems, create safety hazards and compromise Brooklyn’s only piece of national parkland.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/proposed-gas-pipeline-endorsed-by-the-city-draws-criticism/', 'snippet': 'Environmental advocates and community groups worry that a proposed natural gas pipeline in the Rockaways could damage fragile ecosystems, create safety hazards and compromise Brooklyn’s only piece of national parkland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City needs cleaner, cheaper energy. That is the only thing everyone following a proposed natural gas pipeline in the Rockaways agrees upon. But the project — a conduit running from the Atlantic Ocean, under the Rockaways and Jamaica Bay, and then into southeast Brooklyn — has drawn concern and opposition since it became public this year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Proposed Gas Pipeline, Endorsed by the City, Draws Criticism', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brooklyn Pipeline Project Raises a Host of Worries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Williams Companies Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jamaica Bay (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockaway Beach (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T15:19:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a91b0a4-e862-5a72-bae0-eca99b3aafaf', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a91b0a4-e862-5a72-bae0-eca99b3aafaf'}, {'abstract': 'Serena Williams practices at the site of the U.S. Open in Flushing Meadows Corona Park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/nyregion/100000001748025/serena-williams-at-work.html', 'snippet': 'Serena Williams practices at the site of the U.S. Open in Flushing Meadows Corona Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Serena Williams practices at the site of the U.S. Open in Flushing Meadows Corona Park.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image