nezuela’s industrial history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Venezuelans are reeling this week from the deadliest accident in our nation’s industrial history. On Saturday a gas leak at the state-owned Amuay plant, the country’s largest refinery, set off a massive explosion, leaving at least 48 dead and hundreds injured, and leveling dozens of homes nearby.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Misrule of Law', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Explosions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PDVSA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T15:28:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francisco Toro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francisco', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9195dd34-913a-52ac-8ea5-30c2f8388ced', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9195dd34-913a-52ac-8ea5-30c2f8388ced'}, {'abstract': 'Reports that Kohlberg Kravis Roberts may ride in to help bolster the Japanese chip maker Renesas Electronics have given its shares a big boost.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/renesas-shares-leap-on-reports-of-a-pending-k-k-r-investment/', 'snippet': 'Reports that Kohlberg Kravis Roberts may ride in to help bolster the Japanese chip maker Renesas Electronics have given its shares a big boost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reports that Kohlberg Kravis Roberts may ride in to help bolster Renesas Electronics have given shares in the Japanese chip maker a big boost.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Renesas Shares Leap on Reports of a Pending K.K.R. Investment', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kohlberg Kravis Roberts & Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Renesas Electronics Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T15:29:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e36ba29a-4573-5511-8454-f3c6ec11e248', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e36ba29a-4573-5511-8454-f3c6ec11e248'}, {'abstract': 'Not all protesters in the areas around the Republican convention are from the left.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/ideological-diversity-adds-spice-to-protests/', 'snippet': 'Not all protesters in the areas around the Republican convention are from the left.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the speakers on the stage at the Republican convention have been largely on message, the protesters outside have not always been so united. At times during the protests over the last two days, the groups and individuals vying to use the same stretches of public space have been coming into conflict.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ideological Diversity Adds Spice to Protests', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Westboro Baptist Church', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T15:29:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe200c2f-4253-5a36-a69a-f0000d69ccf8', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe200c2f-4253-5a36-a69a-f0000d69ccf8'}, {'abstract': 'Why his supposed pivot to the right is arguably a play for undecideds.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/romneys-play-for-the-center/', 'snippet': 'Why his supposed pivot to the right is arguably a play for undecideds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The conventional wisdom going into this week’s Tampa festivities is that Mitt Romney has shifted, over the last few weeks, from a generic “economy economy economy” campaign to a harder-edged and more ideological attack on the incumbent’s record. The Paul Ryan pick, the wave of welfare-themed campaign ads, the “you didn’t build that” attacks and Romney’s “birther” joke have all been cited as evidence of this rightward shift. But this passage from a Josh Kraushaar column complicates this narrative in a useful way:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Play For the Center', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T15:31:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a68d7b35-c78d-50cb-908a-6a2f2d3316a0', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a68d7b35-c78d-50cb-908a-6a2f2d3316a0'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Chris Christie gave much higher prominence to Mitt Romney in a personal account of how Mr. Romney and his wife, Ann, visited the Christies’ New Jersey home last October and won his early endorsement.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/the-morning-after-his-big-speech-christie-mentions-romney-more/', 'snippet': 'Gov. Chris Christie gave much higher prominence to Mitt Romney in a personal account of how Mr. Romney and his wife, Ann, visited the Christies’ New Jersey home last October and won his early endorsement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — Some listeners thought Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey buried the lead in his keynote speech on Tuesday night at the Republican convention — only mentioning Mitt Romney toward the end of his remarks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Morning After His Big Speech, Christie Mentions Romney More', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}