urce': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Styles | Pretty Package', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T16:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/107fa396-1134-521c-bf2d-2378f8e0635e', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/107fa396-1134-521c-bf2d-2378f8e0635e'}, {'abstract': 'In Mr. LaValle’s new book, residents of a Queens psychiatric hospital battle bureaucracy and a monster.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/humor-and-horror-victor-lavalle-talks-about-his-novel-the-devil-in-silver/', 'snippet': 'In Mr. LaValle’s new book, residents of a Queens psychiatric hospital battle bureaucracy and a monster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Victor LaValle’s third novel, “The Devil in Silver,” a man called Pepper is taken to a psychiatric hospital in Queens by three cops who don’t want to be bothered with putting him in jail for assault. He’s told he will be there for 72 hours of observation, but the days stretch to months. Mr. LaValle is known for an approach that mixes various literary influences and tones, from humor to horror. While Pepper struggles to get decent treatment from an indifferent staff, he also forges alliances — some shakier than others — with his fellow patients and marshals them to fight a beast that has the withered body of an old man and the large head of a bison. In a recent e-mail interview, Mr. LaValle discussed “One Flew Over the Cuckoo’s Nest,” the art of making a monster, van Gogh’s kinship with his characters and more. Below are edited excerpts from the conversation:', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Humor and Horror: Victor LaValle Talks About His Novel ‘The Devil in Silver’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Hero in a Mental Hospital Finds Allies, Monsters and Some Humor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaValle, Victor D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T16:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5e04ff2-c59f-594d-8ba6-fcf32b279547', 'word_count': 1095, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5e04ff2-c59f-594d-8ba6-fcf32b279547'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Strauss said he was retiring from professional cricket after his team lost its series, and the No. 1 ranking, to South Africa. Alastair Cook will replace him as captain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/sports/cricket/30iht-cricket30.html', 'snippet': 'Andrew Strauss said he was retiring from professional cricket after his team lost its series, and the No. 1 ranking, to South Africa. Alastair Cook will replace him as captain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Not for nothing is Andrew Strauss a trained economist.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/sports/cricket/30iht-cricket30-andrew-strauss/30iht-cricket30-andrew-strauss-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'widt