 paid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The more researchers learn about delirium, the clearer it is that attention must be paid. For years, people thought of it as a transient condition: Patients, especially older ones, grow confused and irrational and sometimes even violent during hospital stays — then in a few days, the delirium passes and people return to themselves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Effects of Delirium Are Found to Linger', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARCHIVES OF INTERNAL MEDICINE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T16:13:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc555815-4e88-5bfc-812e-871eee4282c6', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc555815-4e88-5bfc-812e-871eee4282c6'}, {'abstract': 'A new proposal outlined on Wednesday by the Securities and Exchange Commission would remove a longtime restriction barring hedge funds from marketing themselves in public.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/hedge-funds-rules-allow-secretive-enclave-to-open-up/', 'snippet': 'A new proposal outlined on Wednesday by the Securities and Exchange Commission would remove a longtime restriction barring hedge funds from marketing themselves in public.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tight-lipped world of hedge funds might soon be able to speak more freely.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hedge Fund Proposal Would Allow Secretive Enclave to Open Up', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'S.E.C. Proposes Allowing Hedge Funds to Advertise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aguilar, Luis A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schapiro, Mary L', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T16:15:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/accbeca7-71b0-54a4-9607-acbf83ae926e', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/accbeca7-71b0-54a4-9607-acbf83ae926e'}, {'abstract': 'Amazon challenges Netflix in the streaming-movie arena with a free service. Well, it’s free with the purchase of an Amazon Prime membership.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/technology/personaltech/amazons-streaming-movie-service-offers-its-own-potluck-state-of-the-art.html', 'snippet': 'Amazon challenges Netflix in the streaming-movie arena with a free service. Well, it’s free with the purchase of an Amazon Prime membership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the olden days, bargains added spice to life. You’d get a free toaster with a new bank account, or a collectible drinking glass with a gas fill-up. Old-timers even claim that at one time, you got free meals on airplanes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/pogue-75/pogue-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/pogue-75/pogue-75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Potluck for the Eyeballs: Amazon’s Streaming Service', 'kicker': 'State of the Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amazon Takes On Netflix', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T16:19:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6818f7b6-352e-59ff-8d50-bbb47401bf1c', 'word_count': 1330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6818f7b6-352e-59ff-8d50-bbb47401bf1c'}, {'abstract': 'Who was James Reilly, and where is he today?', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/were-you-shot-at-the-1977-u-s-open/', 'snippet': 'Who was James Reilly, and where is he today?', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Michael Steinberger wrote in his recent magazine article about the 1977 U.S. Open, one of most startling moments during the tournament was the shooting of a spectator in the stands. James Reilly, a 33-year-old Manhattanite, was shot in the leg by — as police would later come to believe — someone in an apartment building near the stadium in Forest Hills, Queens. Whoever fired the gun was never found.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Were You Shot at the 1977 U.S. Open?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T16:26:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maya Lau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9b002b1-60a0-5db2-8df9-0f8978e02aec', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9b002b1-60a0-5db2-8df9-0f8978e02aec'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Myerberg of The Times is back this year hosting the best college watch party in the country and offering up his own analysis and insights on all of the big games and a lot of the not so big ones.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/a-football-watch-party-with-a-few-thousand-guests/', 'snippet': 'Paul Myerberg of The Times is back this year hosting the best college watch party in the country and offering up his own analysis and insights on all of the big games and a lot of the not so big ones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The only thing better than watching college football on Saturday is watching the games with your friends on a college football Saturday. Paul Myerberg of The Times is back this year to host the best college watch party in the country and offer up his own analysis and insights on all of the big games and a lot of the not so big ones. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Football Watch Party With a Few Thousand Guests', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T16:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0689b92f-d862-5ab3-a429-c2c6cbab59bf', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0689b92f-d862-5ab3-a429-c2c6cbab59bf'}, {'abstract': 'Thanks to tax-payer dollars and the Army Corps of Engineers, the flood-control pumps in New Orleans are working.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/we-built-it-flood-control-edition/', 'snippet': 'Thanks to tax-payer dollars and the Army Corps of Engineers, the flood-control pumps in New Orleans are working.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. – Someone from the Louisiana delegation ought to steal the “We Built It” sign from the convention hall and hang it on one of the giant flood-control pumps now protecting New Orleans, because that’s where it belongs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'We Built It: Flood-Control Edition', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HURRICANE KATRINA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARMY CORPS OF ENGINEERS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T16:34:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7d69e5e-ca63-533d-b59e-7a16a81d5bf1', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7d69e5e-ca63-533d-b59e-7a16a81d5bf1'}, {'abstract': 'Didier Drogba’s first achievement since joining Shanghai Shenhua has been bringing the team together and providing hope for its fans.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/drogba-provides-hope-for-fans-of-chinese-club/', 'snippet': 'Didier Drogba’s first achievement since joining Shanghai Shenhua has been bringing the team together and providing hope for its fans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first sight that Didier Drogba encountered on a Chinese soccer field was a familiar one. As Shanghai Shenhua’s newly introduced substitute waited for the second half to start, he shared a smile and a word with Aiyegbeni Yakubu, Guangzhou Fuli’s recently acquired striker.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drogba Provides Hope for Fans of Chinese Club', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anelka, Nicolas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drogba, Didier', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shanghai Shenhua (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T16:38:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Duerden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Duerden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6051ee62-92db-5273-8707-498c8c3810de', 'word_count': 973, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6051ee62-92db-5273-8707-498c8c3810de'}, {'abstract': 'The American Booksellers Association said Kobo, a Canadian e-book company, would join with independent bookstores to sell e-books, replacing a little-used Google service that ends in January.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/booksellers-group-partners-with-canadian-e-book-company/', 'snippet': 'The American Booksellers Association said Kobo, a Canadian e-book company, would join with independent bookstores to sell e-books, replacing a little-used Google service that ends in January.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly five months after Google said it would end a little-used program that allowed independent bookstores to sell its e-books, a Canadian e-reading company named Kobo has stepped in as a replacement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Booksellers Group Partners With Canadian E-Book Company', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BOOKSELLERS ASSN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kobo Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T16:42:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bde02f0-6b4b-5087-ba25-8c53e8b8e064', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bde02f0-6b4b-5087-ba25-8c53e8b8e064'}, {'abstract': 'Christoph Niemann and Mark Leibovich check in from Tampa.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/field-trip-the-magazine-at-the-r-n-c/', 'snippet': 'Christoph Niemann and Mark Leibovich check in from Tampa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christoph Niemann has filed another dispatch from Tampa, where he is live-illustrating tweets from the Republican National Convention:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Field Trip! The Magazine at the R.N.C.', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leibovich, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T16:45:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samantha Henig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Henig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6550d36a-3ce8-53d9-aae1-125550e22607', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6550d36a-3ce8-53d9-aae1-125550e22607'}, {'abstract': 'The National Park Foundation created a Web site with mobile devices in mind so travelers can find the nearest park and share park stories, photos or video.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/happy-birthday-parks-now-open-your-web-site/', 'snippet': 'The National Park Foundation created a Web site with mobile devices in mind so travelers can find the nearest park and share park stories, photos or video.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is safe to say that in 1916, when the National Park Service was created, no one could have imagined how the institution would be marking its 96th birthday: a Web site created with mobile devices in mind.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Happy Birthday, Parks. Now Open Your Web Site.', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Park Foundation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Park Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T17:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Drake', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drake', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3acc2745-ef64-5c28-b7e4-4b950abfc1de', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3acc2745-ef64-5c28-b7e4-4b950abfc1de'}, {'abstract': 'Entertaining advertising can create the impression of a retailer that has a sense of fun and that might have something unexpected in store for its customers.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/finding-effective-advertising-in-surprising-places/', 'snippet': 'Entertaining advertising can create the impression of a retailer that has a sense of fun and that might have something unexpected in store for its customers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recently, I heard that riff of music that I always hear when confronted with a piece of fine advertising. At the time, oddly enough, I was paused at an intersection in Austin, Tex., staring at the back end of a delivery truck for a local hardware store, Zinger Hardware. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding Effective Advertising in Surprising Places', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Effective Ad In Striking Place', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trucks and Trucking', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T17:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By MP Mueller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mp', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mueller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d018777c-7846-5d80-a497-4f58b793de7e', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d018777c-7846-5d80-a497-4f58b793de7e'}, {'abstract': 'Comedians following the Republican National Convention this week have taken to Twitter for what amounts to a running routine. Here’s a selection of the best (family-friendly) jokes.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/watching-the-convention-from-the-peanut-gallery/', 'snippet': 'Comedians following the Republican National Convention this week have taken to Twitter for what amounts to a running routine. Here’s a selection of the best (family-friendly) jokes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Chris Christie ever runs for president, America will continue to lead the world in fat jokes. That is abundantly clear to anyone who was paying close attention to the vast peanut gallery that is Twitter last night. Comedians, who have embraced the form as much as any other artist, were hard at work reacting to the Republican National Convention in Tampa, Fla., especially the major speeches of Mr. Christie, the New Jersey governor, and Ann Romney, wife of the\xa0 party’s nominee, Mitt Romney. Relying on Witstream, a Web site that collects Twitter postings from the comedy world, as well as some searching, I hereby offer a few of the best jokes suitable for a family newspaper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Peanut Gallery’s View of the Convention', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Albert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farley, Chris', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Houston, Whitney', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Ann', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T17:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e8fd752-9201-5412-a666-393f023717f1', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e8fd752-9201-5412-a666-393f023717f1'}, {'abstract': 'The public editor weighs in on a Times reporter’s decision to give a C.I.A. staffer an advance copy of Op-Ed Columnist Maureen Dowd’s print column.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/pre-publication-disclosure-of-dowd-column-a-breach-of-two-boundaries/', 'snippet': 'The public editor weighs in on a Times reporter’s decision to give a C.I.A. staffer an advance copy of Op-Ed Columnist Maureen Dowd’s print column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My final column as public editor was published in print on Sunday. However, I remain on duty through Friday and want to offer my take on the controversy this week over the pre-publication disclosure of a Maureen Dowd column. I see this as a problem of boundaries – the failure to maintain them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pre-Publication Disclosure of Dowd Column: A Breach of Two Boundaries', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T17:01:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arthur S. Brisbane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arthur', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Brisbane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c0bdc79-421a-562c-b0a2-e1122dafb5ec', 'word_count': 981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c0bdc79-421a-562c-b0a2-e1122dafb5ec'}, {'abstract': 'A look at what’s to come on Wednesday from the Republican National Convention in Tampa, Fla.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/day-2-timescast-politics-schedule-and-convention-day-at-a-glance/', 'snippet': 'A look at what’s to come on Wednesday from the Republican National Convention in Tampa, Fla.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:26 p.m. | Updated Tuesday’s Republican National Convention schedule featured nominations, protests, keynotes and 3 Doors Down, and that was only the beginning. The Times’s political unit is back in action in Tampa, Fla., broadcasting live with the latest from the convention hall. The next broadcast will be at 7 p.m. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Day 2: TimesCast Politics Schedule and Convention Day at a Glance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vice Presidents and Vice Presidency (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T17:09:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8f4b09e-bc51-595b-8113-66f902e13d70', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8f4b09e-bc51-595b-8113-66f902e13d70'}, {'abstract': 'Kirna Zabête and Odin commision pieces for Target; Otte opens a new store; and the Scoop NYC warehouse sale begins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/fashion/shopping-events-openings-and-sales-for-the-week-of-august-30.html', 'snippet': 'Kirna Zabête and Odin commision pieces for Target; Otte opens a new s