is Wednesday night address, Paul D. Ryan says he and Mitt Romney will tackle the tough issues, including job creation and repealing the health care law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. – Representative Paul D. Ryan, framing the presidential election as the “clearest choice possible,” intends to use his prime-time moment at the Republican National Convention on Wednesday night to assure Americans that he and Mitt Romney can oversee a strong economic recovery.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/us/30convention_span/30convention_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/30/us/30convention_span/30convention_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/us/30convention_span/30convention_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/us/30convention_span/30convention_span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/us/30convention_span/30convention_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/30/us/30convention_span/30convention_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/us/30convention_span/30convention_span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryan Speech to Focus on the Economy, With Shots at Obama', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ryan to Reassure Middle Class and Renew Attack on ‘Obamacare’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T17:18:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce674b00-94c8-5cb7-82e7-08d944aeff17', 'word_count': 1213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce674b00-94c8-5cb7-82e7-08d944aeff17'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Perry, known for songs like “California Gurls,” “Firework” and “Teenage Dream,” is becoming a minority investor in Popchips Inc. as well as a spokeswoman.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/katy-perry-wants-snackers-to-dream-of-popchips/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Perry, known for songs like “California Gurls,” “Firework” and “Teenage Dream,” is becoming a minority investor in Popchips Inc. as well as a spokeswoman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Popchips hopes to put more, well, pop in its chips by adding the pop singer Katy Perry to its roster of celebrity endorsers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Katy Perry Wants Snackers to ‘Dream’ of Popchips', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Katy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T17:18:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fec39eac-310a-5174-9b78-238bf0cfc6c3', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fec39eac-310a-5174-9b78-238bf0cfc6c3'}, {'abstract': 'Plaintiffs in the lawsuit, settled for $590 million, said the bank failed to disclose its huge holdings in collateralized debt obligations.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/citigroup-in-590-million-settlement-of-subprime-lawsuit/', 'snippet': 'Plaintiffs in the lawsuit, settled for $590 million, said the bank failed to disclose its huge holdings in collateralized debt obligations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Citigroup said on Wednesday that it had agreed to pay $590 million to settle a class-action lawsuit brought by shareholders who contended that they had been misled about the bank’s exposure to subprime mortgage debt on the eve of the financial crisis.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Citigroup in $590 Million Settlement of Subprime Lawsuit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Citigroup Settles Lawsuit Over Subprime Securities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T17:23:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Silver-Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a05562b6-c9d0-5e6d-bd12-04cec67ed834', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a05562b6-c9d0-5e6d-bd12-04cec67ed834'}, {'abstract': 'Former Senator Mel Martinez, Republican of Florida, said the immigration debate during the presidential primary season “did a lot of damage” to the party, and urged Mitt Romney to reach out to Hispanics.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/ex-senator-criticizes-republicans-tone-on-immigration/', 'snippet': 'Former Senator Mel Martinez, Republican of Florida, said the immigration debate during the presidential primary season “did a lot of damage” to the party, and urged Mitt Romney to reach out to Hispanics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. – Mel Martinez is a former United States Senator from Florida, served as chairman of the Republican Party under President George W. Bush, and is one of the highest-level Hispanic Republicans in public life. So it was striking on Wednesday morning to hear him speak starkly about his party’s problems with Latino voters after a primary season in which all the candidates stressed measures that would severely curb immigration', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Senator Criticizes Republicans’ Tone on Immigration', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martinez, Melquiades Rafael', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T17:25:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb506b7a-dad7-5108-9667-472230c63cc8', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb506b7a-dad7-5108-9667-472230c63cc8'}, {'abstract': 'The show is the first in a series of exhibitions that pay homage to Venice and its art of glass making.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/master-glass-carlo-scarpa-venini-1932-1947/', 'snippet': 'The show is the first in a series of exhibitions that pay homage to Venice and its art of glass making.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Master Glass | ‘Carlo Scarpa: Venini 1932-1947’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T17:30:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marco Velardi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marco', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Velardi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76cd429b-bb32-5fcc-b3da-f288f480bbe8', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76cd429b-bb32-5fcc-b3da-f288f480bbe8'}, {'abstract': 'Artists Against Fracking, a new coalition organized by Yoko Ono and Sean Lennon, will spread its message through social media.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/yoko-ono-and-sean-lennon-organize-artists-against-fracking/', 'snippet': 'Artists Against Fracking, a new coalition organized by Yoko Ono and Sean Lennon, will spread its message through social media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yoko Ono said it was not hard to recruit more than 180 artists to help convince Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo of New York not to allow natural gas drilling in the Marcellus Shale through the hydraulic fracturing process known as fracking.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yoko Ono and Sean Lennon Organize Artists Against Fracking', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lennon, Sean', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ono, Yoko', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T17:32:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf967a9c-2d6c-5e0c-8478-f9993f43a964', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf967a9c-2d6c-5e0c-8478-f9993f43a964'}, {'abstract': 'The network committed last year to show 90 additional episodes of the Charlie Sheen sitcom if the first 10 met ratings thresholds.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/fx-orders-more-episodes-of-anger-management/', 'snippet': 'The network committed last year to show 90 additional episodes of the Charlie Sheen sitcom if the first 10 met ratings thresholds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s something no one has been able to say about Charlie Sheen for a while: now he knows what he’ll be working on for the next two years, or, at least, where he’s supposed to go when he’s working. On Wednesday, FX said that it had committed to an additional 90 episodes of “Anger Management,” the sitcom that has served as Mr. Sheen’s comeback vehicle after his — didn’t you hear? — tumultuous departure from “Two and a Half Men.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'FX Orders 90 More Episodes of ‘Anger Management’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'FX Orders 90 More Episodes of Sheen Sitcom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheen, Charlie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX (TV Network)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lions Gate Entertainment Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T17:40:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43d604b4-8d2d-58ed-aa40-3db1bb9a79c4', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43d604b4-8d2d-58ed-aa40-3db1bb9a79c4'}, {'abstract': 'The Georgian authorities said they had engaged in a fierce gun battle to free five Georgian villagers being held by a band of militants who had crossed over the border from the Russian republic of Dagestan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/world/europe/georgian-forces-free-hostages-along-russian-border.html', 'snippet': 'The Georgian authorities said they had engaged in a fierce gun battle to free five Georgian villagers being held by a band of militants who had crossed over the border from the Russian republic of Dagestan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TBILISI, Georgia — The Georgian authorities said Wednesday that their forces had engaged in a fierce gun battle to free five Georgian villagers being held by a band of heavily armed militants who had crossed over the mountainous border from the Russian republic of Dagestan. Three Georgian officers and at least 10 militants were killed, officials said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/world/georgia/georgia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/world/georgia/georgia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1247, 'width': 2048, 's