ll out of Greece in the coming weeks, the latest large international business to abandon the country as it grapples with a debilitating recession and nagging questions about its future in the euro zone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'French Banks Prepare to Pull Out of Greece', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Credit Agricole SA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Societe Generale', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T17:42:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/580eb54a-a69e-5354-bb04-2a567a6c5e36', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/580eb54a-a69e-5354-bb04-2a567a6c5e36'}, {'abstract': 'The dollar value of mergers announced this summer was the lowest amount since financial markets began trembling in the summer of 2007. But the number of transactions was the second highest, reflecting a time of plentiful but small deals.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/two-views-of-this-summers-deal-making/', 'snippet': 'The dollar value of mergers announced this summer was the lowest amount since financial markets began trembling in the summer of 2007. But the number of transactions was the second highest, reflecting a time of plentiful but small deals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Looked at in one way, this summer was a dire time for deal-making. But from another perspective, it’s been a great one.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Views of This Summer’s Deal-Making', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T17:43:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d66651a-6f49-5dad-ad9a-90c79af99a80', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d66651a-6f49-5dad-ad9a-90c79af99a80'}, {'abstract': 'In a long-running study, rhesus monkeys whose caloric intake was restricted by 30 percent didn’t live any longer than their normal-weight peers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/science/low-calorie-diet-doesnt-prolong-life-study-of-monkeys-finds.html', 'snippet': 'In a long-running study, rhesus monkeys whose caloric intake was restricted by 30 percent didn’t live any longer than their normal-weight peers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For 25 years, the rhesus monkeys were kept semi-starved, lean and hungry. The males’ weights were so low they were the equivalent of a 6-foot-tall man who tipped the scales at just 120 to 133 pounds. The hope was that if the monkeys lived longer, healthier lives by eating a lot less, then maybe people, their evolutionary cousins, would, too. Some scientists, anticipating such benefits, began severely restricting their own diets. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 