om/2012/08/29/authenticity-and-ethnicity/', 'snippet': 'Why do Indian, African and Arab writers who are longtime legal citizens of Britain or the United States still identify themselves as Indian, African or Arab? And is there really such a thing as an authentic Indian, Arab or African novel?', 'lead_paragraph': 'EDINBURGH — Fifty writers from around the globe assembled in a large tent in Edinburgh in mid-August, and over five days they spoke about the relationship between literature and politics; about whether style and content are really opposites (as people who lack style often claim); and about censorship and the future of the novel. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Authenticity and Ethnicity', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T17:54:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manu Joseph', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Joseph', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b967a064-fd1d-599f-86a0-733fa8a2a9a5', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b967a064-fd1d-599f-86a0-733fa8a2a9a5'}, {'abstract': 'In his keynote, Mr. Christie mostly talked about himself.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/chris-christie-but-enough-about-mitt-lets-talk-about-me/', 'snippet': 'In his keynote, Mr. Christie mostly talked about himself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie is getting rave reviews today for his performance at the National Republican Convention, and there’s no doubt in my mind that he did a huge amount of good for the three most important people in his life – he, himself, and him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chris Christie: But Enough About Mitt, Let’s Talk About Me', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T18:02:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2646bbb-95b5-51f1-aea1-30b07212c229', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2646bbb-95b5-51f1-aea1-30b07212c229'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney left the Republican National Convention on Wednesday to address the American Legion in Indianapolis as Republicans tried to focus on national security.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/a-day-in-indianapolis-a-night-in-tampa/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney left the Republican National Convention on Wednesday to address the American Legion in Indianapolis as Republicans tried to focus on national security.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — A day after being formally nominated for president, Mitt Romney left the Republican National Convention on Wednesday to address the American Legion in Indianapolis as Republicans tried to focus on national security.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Day in Indianapolis, and a Night in Tampa', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T18:05:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f161e79f-4be2-5f9b-997a-35812c8adeee', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f161e79f-4be2-5f9b-997a-35812c8adeee'}, {'abstract': 'GOProud, which advocates for gay conservatives, says it is bringing unusual levels of gay support to Mitt Romney, but discordant notes rang through the dance music at a party near the Republican convention.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/bright-lights-small-tent-at-homocon-2012/', 'snippet': 'GOProud, which advocates for gay conservatives, says it is bringing unusual levels of gay support to Mitt Romney, but discordant notes rang through the dance music at a party near the Republican convention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — The go-go dancers at the party for gay Republicans on Tuesday night were, by go-go dancer standards, modestly dressed in T-shirts and jeans, baring only their midriffs and arms. Their choreography, set to dance remixes of “Call Me Maybe” and other Top 40 hits, conveyed enthusiasm more than sexual enticement. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gay Republicans Try to Join the Party', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican Na