irty spots ahead of the U.S. in math. Kristof praised the Chinese model and ended with a warning: “These latest test results should be our 21st-century Sputnik.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Questioning Kristof on Chinese Education', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T18:50:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Lew', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lew', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9593db18-c28d-56fc-b398-524de50e0a4d', 'word_count': 1513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9593db18-c28d-56fc-b398-524de50e0a4d'}, {'abstract': 'The United Nations secretary general, Ban Ki-moon, met with Iran’s leaders Wednesday to address his concerns about the country’s nuclear program, the Syria conflict and human rights issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/world/middleeast/united-nations-leader-ban-ki-moon-broaches-sensitive-topics-with-iran.html', 'snippet': 'The United Nations secretary general, Ban Ki-moon, met with Iran’s leaders Wednesday to address his concerns about the country’s nuclear program, the Syria conflict and human rights issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Making his first visit to Iran as United Nations secretary general, Ban Ki-moon met with four members of the country’s hierarchy on Wednesday, including the supreme leader, in sessions that Mr. Ban’s spokesman described as “very serious meetings” that addressed the disputed Iranian nuclear program, the Syria conflict, human rights problems and what he called the leadership’s objectionable comments about Israel.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Leader Broaches Delicate Topics in Meetings With Top Iranian Officials', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Leader Broaches Delicate Topics in Meetings With Top Iranian Officials', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban Ki-moon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T18:54:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9244b5e-175e-5516-bc59-8ccce1937690', 'word_count': 961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9244b5e-175e-5516-bc59-8ccce1937690'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Ford reimagines a classic pair of frames immortalized by Malcolm X.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/optical-allusion/', 'snippet': 'Tom Ford reimagines a classic pair of frames immortalized by Malcolm X.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like so many trappings of midcentury manliness, brow line eyeglasses — the kind favored by Malcolm X — have landed in the hipster bargain bin. Leave it to Tom Ford to rescue them with this exquisite version made of gold-plated metal and water buffalo horn, the way they used to be in the 1960s. (The horn component even comes with a certificate of authenticity, along with a special cleansing cream.) The only thing that’s not midcentury about these limited-edition frames is the $2,950 price tag. ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '56', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Optical Allusion', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Optical Allusion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T19:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Tudela', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tudela', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72626e12-ee0f-522b-adfc-722523f99b9e', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72626e12-ee0f-522b-adfc-722523f99b9e'}, {'abstract': 'At the Farm 2 Fork booth at the United States Open, the shortrib sandwich is definitely shareable.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/u-s-open-food-of-the-day-shortrib-sandwich/', 'snippet': 'At the Farm 2 Fork booth at the United States Open, the shortrib sandwich is definitely shareable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is our daily review of an item from the United States Open concession stands.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Open Food of the Day: Shortrib Sandwich', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sandwiches', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T19:00:48+0000', 'document_ty