ees-welcome-ugandan-little-league-team/', 'snippet': 'The Yankees rolled out the red carpet Wednesday for a visit from the Ugandan Little League team, the first African team to advance to a Little League World Series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees had special guests visit them on Wednesday: the Ugandan Little League team, the first African team to advance to a Little League World Series, was given a tour of the clubhouse by Manager Joe Girardi.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Welcome Ugandan Little League Team', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Little League World Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Little League Baseball and Softball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T19:14:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29e0bfef-57f8-58b1-a0ef-e3a910f63f40', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29e0bfef-57f8-58b1-a0ef-e3a910f63f40'}, {'abstract': 'Was the New Jersey governor’s speech on love and respect a “brain-switching” moment?', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/chris-christie-channels-oprah/', 'snippet': 'Was the New Jersey governor’s speech on love and respect a “brain-switching” moment?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Watching Gov. Chris Christie’s combative keynote speech last night reminded us of the cover piece I wrote about him last year. His mention of his mother teaching him the difference between love and respect, in particular, brought me back. “The greatest lesson Mom ever taught me,” Christie told the crowd in Tampa last night, “was this one: She told me there would be times in your life when you have to choose between being loved and being respected. She said to always pick being respected, that love without respect was always fleeting — but that respect could grow into real, lasting love.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chris Christie Channels Oprah', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T19:22:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Bai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e435bdb-77bf-5761-b698-0b1d8c50e8c5', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e435bdb-77bf-5761-b698-0b1d8c50e8c5'}, {'abstract': 'The latest CBS News poll takes stock of Americans’ views on abortion, the presidential candidates and the fallout from a Missouri congressman’s remarks.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/majority-in-poll-say-akins-remarks-dont-reflect-most-republicans-views/', 'snippet': 'The latest CBS News poll takes stock of Americans’ views on abortion, the presidential candidates and the fallout from a Missouri congressman’s remarks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the wake of the widespread outrage over a Missouri congressman’s remarks about rape and abortion, about 60 percent of Americans do not think his comments reflect the views of most Republicans, according to the latest CBS News