ng ire from animal right advocates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They may not rank with the Bridge of Sighs or gondolas as Venice’s top tourist attractions, but the pigeons of St. Mark’s Square definitely have their fans — and protectors. That has been amply demonstrated in recent days as the result of an art project undertaken as part of this year’s Architecture Biennale in Venice, in which two European artists have tinted some of the St. Mark’s flock in gaudy colors.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colorful Pigeons in St. Mark’s Square Stir Controversy', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pigeon Tinting in Venice Raises Hue and Cry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruelty to Animals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pigeons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Charriere, Julian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'von Bismarck, Julius', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venice (Italy)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T19:55:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09846d68-47fd-5c8d-a511-1a6b080e548c', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09846d68-47fd-5c8d-a511-1a6b080e548c'}, {'abstract': 'The jewelry designer Pamela Love is hosting a pop-up tattoo parlor during fashion week.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/tattoo-you/', 'snippet': 'The jewelry designer Pamela Love is hosting a pop-up tattoo parlor during fashion week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fashion Week may induce cravings for an “It” bag or a pair of shoes that last only a season, but the jewelry designer Pamela Love is hoping to leave showgoers with something a bit more permanent this time around. In the ultimate test of designer devotion, Love has nixed her usual presentation to host a pop-up tattoo parlor at Milk/Made’s Digital Bar from Sept. 8 to Sept. 9.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tattoo You', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tattoos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Love, Pamela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T20:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eliza Brooke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eliza', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3255c2c9-8895-5150-9019-e0d4cc88ded0', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3255c2c9-8895-5150-9019-e0d4cc88ded0'}, {'abstract': 'With his prime-time speech embracing the vice-presidential nomination approaching, Representative Paul D. Ryan made the customary walk-through of the convention hall stage on Wednesday afternoon.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/the-caucus-click-the-ryans-in-rehearsal/', 'snippet': 'With his prime-time speech embracing the vice-presidential nomination approaching, Representative Paul D. Ryan made the customary walk-through of the convention hall stage on Wednesday afternoon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — With the hours ticking down to his prime-time speech embracing the vice-president