al races.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — Paul D. Ryan will take the stage at the Republican National Convention here on Wednesday to accept his party’s nomination for vice president, but around the country, his plan for a sweeping remake of Medicare is shaking up Congressional campaigns, in some cases allowing Democrats to make inroads in races in which they were once seen as dead in the water.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryan Medicare Plan Is Already Shaking Up House Races', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benishek, Dan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hochul, Kathleen C', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matheson, Jim', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIntyre, Mike', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalise, Steve', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Republican Congressional Committee', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T21:19:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/442903e9-fd9d-56b4-91d7-55ded544bf24', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/442903e9-fd9d-56b4-91d7-55ded544bf24'}, {'abstract': 'The jazz singer Allan Harris performed songs from his CD “Convergence” at the Metropolitan Room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/arts/music/allan-harris-sings-at-the-metropolitan-room.html', 'snippet': 'The jazz singer Allan Harris performed songs from his CD “Convergence” at the Metropolitan Room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill Evans’s wistful, lightly skipping “Waltz for Debby” is a classic 1950s jazz composition that doesn’t really need words to conjure an evanescent childhood dream world. But its lyrics, added several years later by Gene Lees, about a little girl who will soon outgrow her “dolls and clowns and a big purple bear,” deepen the poignancy of a song that imagines those toys missing her once she abandons them.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/arts/HARRIS/HARRIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/arts/HARRIS/HARRIS-superJ