//slideshow/6c0c7423-de21-512f-a38e-a91d413a2d99'}, {'abstract': 'Mallory Burdette, a 21-year-old wild card, defeated Lucie Hradecka in the second round at the United States Open and is likely to face Maria Sharapova next.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/at-her-first-slam-burdette-reaches-the-third-round/', 'snippet': 'Mallory Burdette, a 21-year-old wild card, defeated Lucie Hradecka in the second round at the United States Open and is likely to face Maria Sharapova next.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mallory Burdette, a 21-year-old wild card from Jackson, Ga., has advanced to the third round of her first Grand Slam singles tournament, notching a 6-2, 6-4 win over 69th-ranked Lucie Hradecka at the United States Open on Wednesday afternoon. Hradecka, who won a silver medal in women’s doubles at the London Olympics, hit 13 winners, to Burdette’s 21.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Her First Slam, Burdette Reaches the Third Round', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hradecka, Lucie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharapova, Maria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T22:27:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfa89240-af91-5036-bad2-1486f076b62f', 'word_count': 593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfa89240-af91-5036-bad2-1486f076b62f'}, {'abstract': 'Which of today’s designs will stand the test of time?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/garden/the-classics-circa-2050.html', 'snippet': 'Which of today’s designs will stand the test of time?', 'lead_paragraph': 'DESIGNED by Philippe Starck in 2002 with an eye to the 18th century, the Louis Ghost chair pays homage to French baroque style. The chair has an oval back and twisted angular arms — fancy stuff for a piece of transparent plastic furniture.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/garden/30CLASSIC_SPAN/30DETAILS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/30/garden/30CLASSIC_SPAN/30DETAILS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/garden/30CLASSIC_SPAN/30DETAILS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/garden/30CLASSIC_SPAN/30DETAILS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1279, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/garden/30CLASSIC_SPAN/30DETAILS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/30/garden/30CLASSIC_SPAN/30DETAILS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Classics, Circa 2050', 'kicker': 'The Details', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Classics, Circa 2050', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Two Thousands (Decade)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T22:27:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Lasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a3fd8c3-5b79-57db-aeb7-b69590c7b815', 'word_count': 2250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a3fd8c3-5b79-57db-aeb7-b69590c7b815'}, {'abstract': 'Flat-screen TVs, matching linens — nothing is too luxurious for today’s college dorm room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/garden/the-well-decorated-dorm-room.html', 'snippet': 'Flat-screen TVs, matching linens — nothing is too luxurious for today’s college dorm room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I DON’T remember everything I took with me when I went to college, but do I know it all fit easily into the back seat of our family car. The twin-size sheets were new; nearly everything else (pillow, stereo, ugly green rug) had been scavenged from home or a thrift store. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/30/garden/30DORM_SPAN/30DORM_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/30/garden/30DORM_SPAN/30DORM_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't