, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4abf0f0-f776-533d-8aa6-f1278c605236', 'word_count': 1931, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4abf0f0-f776-533d-8aa6-f1278c605236'}, {'abstract': 'In two coming New York shows the Brazilian artist Saint Clair Cemin employs a variety of materials, subjects and sculpture traditions from around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/arts/design/saint-clair-cemin-on-broadway-and-at-paul-kasmin-gallery.html', 'snippet': 'In two coming New York shows the Brazilian artist Saint Clair Cemin employs a variety of materials, subjects and sculpture traditions from around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS a child the sculptor Saint Clair Cemin spent two years living on a 5,000-acre property in rural Brazil, where his father, an engineer, tried and failed to grow wheat. This was in the late 1950s, when the area surrounding the small city of Cruz Alta was, he said, “still known as gaucho land, as primitive as the American West in the 19th century.” There was no running water or electricity on the vast spread, which belonged to his mother, so his family depended on gas lamps for light.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02CEMIN1_SPAN/02CEMIN1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02CEMIN1_SPAN/02CEMIN1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02CEMIN1_SPAN/02CEMIN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/