bon dioxide as conventional coal plants. The builders, a consortium of municipal utilities and co-ops across eight states from Missouri to West Virginia, rushed to get it up and running before greenhouse rules could stop it, convinced that coal would be cheaper for the next few decades than alternative sources, like gas or nuclear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Late Bet on Coal May Not Pay Off', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-29T22:39:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6556f0c5-aab2-517d-b32f-9ede760647f8', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6556f0c5-aab2-517d-b32f-9ede760647f8'}, {'abstract': 'The novelist wrote the definitive work on interior design and used her own home as a laboratory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/garden/appreciating-edith-whartons-other-career.html', 'snippet': 'The novelist wrote the definitive work on interior design and used her own home as a laboratory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1911, her marriage in tatters, Edith Wharton sailed to Europe, where she 