', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Discriminatory Purpose’ in Texas', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Discriminatory Purpose’ in Texas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T01:22:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2b30ec9-06e9-5231-98e1-15994875c7f0', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2b30ec9-06e9-5231-98e1-15994875c7f0'}, {'abstract': 'In foreign policy, the relationship between what candidates say on the trail and what they do once elected can be tenuous.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/us/politics/romneys-foreign-policy-intentions-hard-to-gauge.html', 'snippet': 'In foreign policy, the relationship between what candidates say on the trail and what they do once elected can be tenuous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — Bill Clinton said he would crack down on China. George W. Bush said he would stay away from nation building. Barack Obama said he would restore civil liberties in the war on terror and sit down with rogue leaders.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Precise Foreign Policy Intentions Can Be Tough to Gauge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Precise Foreign Policy Intentions Can Be Tough to Gauge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T01:22:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f61746b-633c-5eb4-b798-57313f59255f', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f61746b-633c-5eb4-b798-57313f59255f'}, {'abstract': 'American citizens seem to do as good a job as government scientists in selecting candidates for federal protection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/opinion/the-public-role-in-species-protection.html', 'snippet': 'American citizens seem to do as good a job as government scientists in selecting candidates for federal protection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the virtues of the Endangered Species Act is its openness to citizen participation. The Fish and Wildlife Service can designate likely species for federal protection. But ordinary citizens and nongovernmental organizations can petition to have candidates of their own choosing considered for protection. Not everyone thinks this is a virtue. The enemies of the Endangered Species Act are legion, especially in the House of Representatives, and one of their major complaints has always been citizen petitions, which they claim are politically motivated and expensive, especially when they include litigation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Public Role in Species Protection', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Public Role in Species Protection', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fish and Wildlife Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T01:23:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3edca27a-1b49-5b5c-804f-a6f17bae2000', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3edca27a-1b49-5b5c-804f-a6f17bae2000'}, {'abstract': 'Pittsburgh’s three-game series this week against St. Louis was a crucial test as to whether it could remain a postseason contender into September or would retreat into irrelevancy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/sports/baseball/pittsburgh-pirates-playoff-dreams-in-peril.html', 'snippet': 'Pittsburgh’s three-game series this week against St. Louis was a crucial test as to whether it could remain a postseason contender into September or would retreat into irrelevancy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PITTSBURGH — Janice Martell directed an early-morning visitor Tuesday to a popular site at the hilly Jefferson Memorial Cemetery here: the grave of Honus Wagner, a shortstop who won eight National League batting titles and, in 19