China, India wants to send a mission to Mars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DELHI\xa0 — Let’s send a mission to Mars, Prime Minister Manmohan Singh announced a couple of weeks ago, just as his government was fending off corruption charges and the country was still recovering from the biggest blackout since the invention of electricity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BRICS in Space', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mars (Planet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Planets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singh, Manmohan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T10:43:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hartosh Singh Bal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hartosh', 'middlename': 'Singh', 'lastname': 'Bal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1150d3d1-e45d-5cf8-bc2c-73b0bbc9898c', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1150d3d1-e45d-5cf8-bc2c-73b0bbc9898c'}, {'abstract': 'Some browsers include typed commands for getting more information — and maybe a laugh — about the program.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/tip-of-the-week-learning-%e2%80%9cabout%e2%80%9d-your-browser/', 'snippet': 'Some browsers include typed commands for getting more information — and maybe a laugh — about the program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The wrench icon in the Google Chrome toolbar offers a menu of settings you can use to control and adjust how the browser looks and behaves. Chrome can also reveal more information on its internal pages with a series of commands typed directly into the address/search box (also known as the “omnibox”). While many of these commands are designed for programmers looking to debug Web-page code, some are helpful for quickly seeing what plug-ins and extensions are installed, or to see the browser’s bookmarks list.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Learning ‘About’ Your Browser', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T10:44:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.D. BIERSDORFER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d854f58-3487-575f-a98c-0c5bcdb10646', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d854f58-3487-575f-a98c-0c5bcdb10646'}, {'abstract': 'Juanjo López does “cooking like that of the gods.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/magazine/finding-the-divine-in-madrids-red-light-district.html', 'snippet': 'Juanjo López does “cooking like that of the gods.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Contemporary cooking in Spain is polarized in an odd way, from the avant-garde cuisine on the one hand and the wonderful menú del dia joints on the other. The center — talented chefs who are not necessarily trying to reinvent cuisine — is somewhat difficult to find.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02eat1/02eat1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 499, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02eat1/02eat1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 499}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02eat1/02eat1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 852, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02eat1/02eat1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1248, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02eat1/02eat1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02eat1/02eat1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02eat1/02eat1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding the Divine in Madrid’s Red-Light District', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Cooking Like That of the Gods’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T11:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a48138a-cf49-52a2-a099-b7392a35ade9', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a48138a-cf49-52a2-a099-b7392a35ade9'}, {'abstract': 'Welcome to the new middle-class matriarchy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/magazine/who-wears-the-pants-in-this-economy.html', 'snippet': 'Welcome to the new middle-class matriarchy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Patsy Prater’s office looks like something between an executive’s and a teacher’s, her large desk crowded with neat piles of grant applications and daily logs but also with dishes of candy and other freebies for the young and old who pass through. On the bulletin board behind her head are big, colorful signs designed to remind her public-housing clients of what they are eligible for: cellphones, computer classes or prescriptions that she makes sure they have even if she has to drive them to the pharmacy herself. At the front of her desk is a photo of her “grandbaby,” who lives in Madison, Ala., three hours away. She wishes she could be there, taking care of the infant now that her daughter is back at work. “I love this job,” she said. “I know it’s where I’m supposed to be. But I am not a women’s-rights-type person. My place is in the home, and I’m fine with that, so long as my husband is earning the bacon. ’Course, that hasn’t been happening so much lately.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02matriarchy1/02matriarchy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02matriarchy1/02matriarchy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 693}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02matriarchy1/mag-02matriarchy-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 811, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02matriarchy1/mag-02matriarchy-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1188, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02matriarchy1/02matriarchy1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02matriarchy1/02matriarchy1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/magazine/02matriarchy1/02matriarchy1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Wears the Pants in This Economy?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Wears the Pants in This Economy?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montgomery (Ala)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Alexander City (Ala)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Russell Brands LLC', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T11:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hanna Rosin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5522918a-21ae-546a-ab04-16da303404ae', 'word_count': 6755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5522918a-21ae-546a-ab04-16da303404ae'}, {'abstract': 'Hestia Tobacco positions itself as the first truly independent organic cigarette company, and there are a number of strong elements to the pitch.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/pitching-an-organic-cigarette-for-hipsters/', 'snippet': 'Hestia Tobacco positions itself as the first truly independent organic cigarette company, and there are a number of strong elements to the pitch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my last post, I reviewed a company focused on helping students find their passions. This week, I review a pitch for a product that may seem a bit contradictory in nature — an organic cigarette.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pitching an Organic Cigarette for Hipsters', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reynolds, R J, Tobacco Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T11:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qual