t_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaches', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T12:30:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Storm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Storm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc993266-dc4d-5e9c-a6c9-177793ff921b', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc993266-dc4d-5e9c-a6c9-177793ff921b'}, {'abstract': 'Pastries at Vergennes Laundry, the bakery located in a former laundromat in Vergennes, Vt., have gained a cult following.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/edible-selby-french-laundry/', 'snippet': 'Pastries at Vergennes Laundry, the bakery located in a former laundromat in Vergennes, Vt., have gained a cult following.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Everything starts out raw and goes straight on the tart,” says Julianne Jones, explaining why her pastries have gained a cult following. At Vergennes Laundry, the bakery Jones opened in 2010 with her French husband, Didier Murat, in a former laundromat in Vergennes, Vt., all tarts are made to order with the freshest seasonal ingredients. Summer brings berries or tomatoes; the spring months asparagus with goat cheese and mint. In fall and winter it’s Gilfeather turnips, potatoes, rosemary and crème fraîche. Jones won’t use glaze, and she insists on an open kitchen. “I prefer that somebody can see the tart as I’m making it,” she says. “They see the bag of potatoes or the crate of berries. They see the wheel of cheese.” Though Jones and Murat are also renowned for their slow-rise bread and nougat, a few locals have yet to register the boulangerie. “We still have people come in with their laundry bags from time to time,” Murat says. More…', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Edible Selby | French Laundry', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T13:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Todd Selby and Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Todd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Selby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6293592-344c-5832-b8f5-c1e71e8e8b9f', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6293592-344c-5832-b8f5-c1e71e8e8b9f'}, {'abstract': 'Few investors have ridden the recent Internet boomlet like the GSV Capital Corporation, Randall Smith reports for DealBook. After GSV announced in June 2011 that it was buying a stake in the privately held Facebook, the closed-end mutual fund surged 42 percent that day. Now, GSV is feeling the Facebook blues.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/daily-report-a-misplaced-bet-on-facebook/', 'snippet': 'Few investors have ridden the recent Internet boomlet like the GSV Capital Corporation, Randall Smith reports for DealBook. After GSV announced in June 2011 that it was buying a stake in the privately held Facebook, the closed-end mutual fund surg...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few investors have ridden the recent Internet boomlet like the GSV Capital Corporation, Randall Smith reports for DealBook. After GSV announced in June 2011 that it was buying a stake in the privately held Facebook, the closed-end mutual fund surged 42 percent that day. Capitalizing on the euphoria, GSV sold another $247 million of its shares, using the money to expand its portfolio of hot start-ups like Groupon and Zynga.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: A Misplaced Bet on Facebook', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T13:07:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a7cb39a-1461-5a79-8b0b-98a8dd9a91b8', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a7cb39a-1461-5a79-8b0b-98a8dd9a91b8'}, {'abstract': 'Richard C. Levin, 65, is currently the most senior president in the Ivy League and one of the longest-serving in the university’s history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/nyregion/yale-president-richard-levin-says-he-will-step-down.html', 'snippet': 'Richard C. Levin, 65, is currently the most senior president in the Ivy League and one of the longest-serving in the university’s history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard C. Levin, who has directed a vast expansion and modernization of Yale University while improving university finances and relations with the city of New Haven, announced on Thursday that he would retire as president at the end of the school year, after 20 years. Dr. Levin is currently the most senior president in the Ivy League and one of the longest-serving in Yale’s history. The university is expected to undertake a nationwide search for a successor, who will take the helm next summer at an elite institution with a global reputation and a $3 billion annual operating budget.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/nyregion/30yale-web/30yale-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 816, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/nyregion/30yale-web/30yale-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1632, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/nyregion/30yale-web/30yale-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/31/nyregion/30yale-web/30yale-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/nyregion/30yale-web/30yale-web-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Saying It’s Time to Move On, Yale President Will Retire', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saying It’s Time to Leave, Yale President Will Retire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Haven (Conn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levin, Richard C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T13:22:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a21ac0c2-2af3-52af-9f7c-7c12327061b5', 'word_count': 926, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a21ac0c2-2af3-52af-9f7c-7c12327061b5'}, {'abstract': 'The great annual global pulsing of fires — natural and human-made — is revealed in NASA imagery.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/a-12-year-view-of-the-global-pulse-of-fire/', 'snippet': 'The great annual global pulsing of fires — natural and human-made — is revealed in NASA imagery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A recent reader comment about this year’s season of heat and wildfire in Siberia prompted me to scan NASA Web pages for relevant data and images. I found this fascinating 12-year animation showing the annual shifts in frequency and distribution of fires — both wild and human-set — around the planet. Here’s some of the space agency’s explainer, with a link to the rest: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A 12-Year View of the Global Pulse of Fire', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forest and Brush Fires', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temperature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Siberia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South America', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T13:22:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b49c3c2d-8857-5b61-954f-7f32fa2956be', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b49c3c2d-8857-5b61-954f-7f32fa2956be'}, {'abstract': 'The Kingdom Trails offer adventure for downhill riders and gentler tracks for more leisurely cyclists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/travel/biking-in-vermont-body-armor-optional.html', 'snippet': 'The Kingdom Trails offer adventure for downhill riders and gentler tracks for more leisurely cyclists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT was an idyllic Vermont view from halfway up Burke Mountain. A patchwork of forest and pasture rolled westward to a distant mountain ridge. Puffy white clouds hung in a blue sky. But I was focused on a brown ribbon that plunged down the slope like a dirt bobsled track, nervously clenching the handlebars of a hulking bicycle that resembled a motocross motorcycle.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02EXPLORER1_SPAN/02EXPLORER1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02EXPLORER1_SPAN/02EXPLORER1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02EXPLORER1_SPAN/02EXPLORER1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02EXPLORER1_SPAN/02EXPLORER1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02EXPLORER1_SPAN/