cting indie rock albums: “American Weekend,” by Waxahatchee, and the self-titled debut album by Swearin’.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON YouTube there’s a brief documentary, made six years ago, about a teenage rock band in Alabama called the Ackleys. It’s a four-piece, anchored by an irrepressible set of apple-cheeked female twins, Allison and Katie Crutchfield. Seventeen years old, they name-check Fugazi, Guided By Voices and the Velvet Underground as influences and are shown playing accomplished, jangly indie rock in graffitied warehouse spaces.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02TWINS1_SPAN/02TWINS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02TWINS1_SPAN/02TWINS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02TWINS1_SPAN/02TWINS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02TWINS1_SPAN/02TWINS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02TWINS1_SPAN/02TWINS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02TWINS1_SPAN/02TWINS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02TWINS1_SPAN/02TWINS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Twin Rock Dreams Prevail', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Twin Rock Dreams Prevail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T13:34:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a570e79-77a1-5950-9f48-7b02df98605a', 'word_count': 1494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a570e79-77a1-5950-9f48-7b02df98605a'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: Cardinal Timothy M. Dolan, will offer a closing prayer for both the Republicans and the Democrats, and it will be interesting to hear how political he gets.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/at-the-political-conventions-stay-tuned-for-the-archbishop/', 'snippet': 'The Day: Cardinal Timothy M. Dolan, will offer a closing prayer for both the Republicans and the Democrats, and it will be interesting to hear how political he gets.', 'lead_paragraph': ' For the politically minded, the focus Thursday night will be on Mitt Romney’s acceptance speech at the Republican National Convention. But you may want to keep watching even after Mr. Romney is done and the last balloon has dropped. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Political Conventions, Stay Tuned for the Archbishop', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dolan, Timothy M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T13:38:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d579168a-0890-594b-b744-8342cca55293', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d579168a-0890-594b-b744-8342cca55293'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the writers and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/what-were-reading-511/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the writers and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eater: After 28 years at the helm of Gotham Bar and Grill, Alfred Portale hints that he has plans to open other places, and laments that today’s restaurant critics tend to focus on a single facet: “Now you can see restaurant reviews where it can be that the food is wonderful but everything else is lacking.” — Patrick Farrell', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T13:54:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95050930-3005-5045-bf48-7a8e75bc1396', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95050930-3005-5045-bf48-7a8e75bc1396'}, {'abstract': 'In this presidential election season, mum is the word on all issues related to climate change.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/what-will-it-take/', 'snippet': 'In this presidential election season, mum is the word on all issues related to climate change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two years ago, at a Washington symposium observing the 40th anniversary of the Clean Air Act, much of the discussion centered around the use of the landmark pollution law to try to address a problem its authors never anticipated – climate change caused by increasing concentrations of carbon dioxide and other heat-trapping gases in the atmosphere.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Will It Take?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T14:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56e58d54-04eb-5aac-90e8-91858e4e5095', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56e58d54-04eb-5aac-90e8-91858e4e5095'}, {'abstract': 'Stella Adler, the great acting teacher, is presented verbatim, discussing eminent American playwrights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/books/stella-adler-on-americas-master-playwrights-lectures.html', 'snippet': 'Stella Adler, the great acting teacher, is presented verbatim, discussing eminent American playwrights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Size mattered — really mattered — to Stella Adler. “Make it big,” she would say again and again to her students in the dramatic arts, whom she spent four decades training to be giants. “Be as large as the stage is,” she said. “Don’t be afraid of the size. You need it as actors — we need it in America.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/arts/31BOOK/31BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/arts/31BOOK/31BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1376, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/arts/31BOOK/31BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/31/arts/31BOOK/31BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/arts/31BOOK/31BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '... And in Eternal Stagecraft', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '... And in Eternal Stagecraft', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paris, Barry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ADLER, STELLA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major'