can National Convention.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/in-ryan-critique-of-obama-omissions-help-make-the-case/', 'snippet': 'A closer look at Representative Paul D. Ryan’s speech at the Republican National Convention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Interactive Feature: Anatomy of a Speech: Republican National Convention', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fact-Checking Ryan’s Convention Speech', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T14:26:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29f344f3-6b54-54a7-aa6d-1a24eb73dd1b', 'word_count': 1228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29f344f3-6b54-54a7-aa6d-1a24eb73dd1b'}, {'abstract': 'The Eugene Mirman Comedy Festival lineup this year will include Todd Barry and Sarah Silverman.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/eugene-mirman-comedy-festival-sets-lineup/', 'snippet': 'The Eugene Mirman Comedy Festival lineup this year will include Todd Barry and Sarah Silverman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brooklyn comedy is bustling. The Brooklyn Academy of Music recently started a stand-up series. Spaces like Littlefield and the Knitting Factory in Williamsburg have become reliable homes for great comedy. And Louis C.K. has made a habit of working out early versions of his annual stand-up specials at the Bell House. But the anchor of the Brooklyn scene is probably Eugene Mirman, the comic who runs a weekly Sunday show at Union Hall (where much of Mike Birbiglia’s movie “Sleepwalk With Me” was set) and curates and hosts the Eugene Mirman Comedy Festival. This freewheeling, talent-packed event has none of the stuffy air of more established festivals. It takes place Sept. 13-16 at the Bell House and Union Hall. Veteran comedians like Jon Glaser, Todd Barry and Sarah Silverman will appear. So will young, emerging comics like Michael Che and Brent Sullivan. You can also expect some special guests. The events include a Saturday show titled “Uh Oh: Dangerous, Inappropriate Comedy for Teenagers” and a film festival of short films on Sunday. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eugene Mirman Comedy Festival Sets Lineup', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brooklyn Comedy Festival Announces Its Lineup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barry, Todd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Birbiglia, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'C K, Louis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mirman, Eugene', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silverman, Sarah', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T14:28:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa224e46-5301-5b85-8cb4-275e3baafbc9', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa224e46-5301-5b85-8cb4-275e3baafbc9'}, {'abstract': 'Argentina’s official and grossly underestimated figures for inflation are a lie so big and so old, the government has to keep telling it.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/deflating-inflation-in-argentina/', 'snippet': 'Argentina’s official and grossly underestimated figures for inflation are a lie so big and so old, the government has to keep telling it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — Every month, when the official statistics agency INDEC releases estimates for inflation, the Argentine government lies to its people. Everyone knows the figures fall far short of reality, which is that Argentina has one of the world’s highest rates of inflation. INDEC’s July figure brought 12-month inflation to 9.9 percent, well below the 24.1 percent estimated by private analysts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deflating Inflation', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirchner, Cristina Fernandez de', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T14:31:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Politi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Politi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb82d411-e5e4-5120-8080-2b3668df369d', '