an outspread hand slowly creeping up a naked brick wall at 512 Rockaway Avenue in Brownsville, Brooklyn, was no exception. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Painted on the Walls, the Stories of New York Communities', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Court Innovation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brownsville (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T14:37:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Celia McGee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Celia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b4c6ddf-2893-524d-a4ee-543f6ce2acca', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b4c6ddf-2893-524d-a4ee-543f6ce2acca'}, {'abstract': 'Melissa Clark demonstrates how to make fig crostini with goat cheese and balsamic vinegar in a new video.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/the-sweetness-of-figs-the-crunch-of-toast/', 'snippet': 'Melissa Clark demonstrates how to make fig crostini with goat cheese and balsamic vinegar in a new video.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Crostini is one of my favorite things to make during fig season, especially with fruit from my backyard tree (for more about fig trees in Brooklyn, you can check out my column). I love the way the crunch of the toast echoes the fig seeds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sweetness of Figs, the Crunch of Toast', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T14:37:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c46248d-da0f-5500-88d1-8e215334ea36', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c46248d-da0f-5500-88d1-8e215334ea36'}, {'abstract': 'Some thoughts about companies that contractually forbid employees from telling anyone how much money they earn.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/employers-that-forbid-you-from-telling-others-what-you-make/', 'snippet': 'Some thoughts about companies that contractually forbid employees from telling anyone how much money they earn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was surprised earlier this month when I tuned in to a Marketplace report that noted that there are employers that contractually forbid employees from telling anyone how much money they make.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Employers That Forbid You From Telling Others What You Make', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T14:48:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9e18b72-b5b9-58af-b7b3-b3e4869fb69f', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9e18b72-b5b9-58af-b7b3-b3e4869fb69f'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican platform takes rhetorical aim at collective bargaining while calling for the nationwide adoption of a Right-to-Work law.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/g-o-p-platform-seeks-to-weaken-powers-of-unions/', 'snippet': 'The Republican platform takes rhetorical aim at collective bargaining while calling for the nationwide adoption of a Right-to-Work law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Unlike in the past, this year’s Republican platform in Tampa, Fla., does not contain any sympathetic nods to the nation’s labor unions, which have become among the Republicans’ most formidable political foes. Instead, the platform calls for numerous steps that could significantly weaken America’s labor unions — public-sector and private-sector ones — and help speed organized labor’s overall decline.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Platform Seeks to Weaken Powers of Unions', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF LABOR-CONGRESS OF INDUSTRIAL ORGANIZATIONS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Labor Relations Board', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], '