ntary filmmaker known for films like “The Kid Stays in the Picture” and “Chicago 10.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Rolling Stone Documentary Is Announced', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Rolling Stones Documentary Announced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgen, Brett', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rolling Stones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T15:54:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ea1072d-24f7-5e14-be0f-927beccfc8e3', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ea1072d-24f7-5e14-be0f-927beccfc8e3'}, {'abstract': 'Losing that $50 reminded me of my own, myriad unpaid debts.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/i-o-u-and-u-and-u/', 'snippet': 'Losing that $50 reminded me of my own, myriad unpaid debts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One cold day last November, Amy and I came home from work to a sickish young daughter and started to toy with just staying in for the night. Problem was, we had these tickets to see Miranda July, the performance artist, being interviewed by someone over at the Herbst Theater. Two tickets, $50 sunk into the situation. We hemmed and hawed, one of us made pasta, and finally I put a last-minute, Hail Mary ad on Craigslist. It was 7, and the event started at 8. No way. But five minutes later I had an e-mail from a guy named Joe. I picked up the phone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I.O.U., and U., and U.', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'July, Miranda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Craigslist', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T16:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Colin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Colin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51b233f2-a140-556f-80ad-28b19450a3c1', 'word_count': 1191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51b233f2-a140-556f-80ad-28b19450a3c1'}, {'abstract': 'The Chef’s Table at Brooklyn Fare doesn’t have a grade on display from the New York City Department of Health. Why?', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/why-are-some-city-restaurants-exempt-from-letter-grades/', 'snippet': 'The Chef’s Table at Brooklyn Fare doesn’t have a grade on display from the New York City Department of Health. Why?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chef’s Table at Brooklyn Fare, the eccentric 18-seat restaurant in downtown Brooklyn, has just about everything its customers could want, except more seats. The borough’s only three-star Michelin restaurant (one of seven in the city) has a three-star review from The New York Times and attracts a devoted clientele that reserves six weeks ahead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Are Some City Restaurants Exempt From Letter Grades?', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None,