home-at-columbia/', 'snippet': 'Jack Agüeros, an author and activist, will have his papers housed in an archive at Columbia, as part of the university’s effort to become a vital source of historical research on Latinos in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1996, Jack Agüeros, a Puerto Rican author and advocate who wrote sonnets about poor immigrants and Latino street life, would have seemed an unlikely candidate for inclusion in the library of New York City’s most prestigious university.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Papers of a Puerto Rican Poet Will Find a Home at Columbia', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Papers of Latino Writer Are Given to Columbia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puerto Ricans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AGUEROS, JACK', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'El Museo del Barrio', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T16:40:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Yee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d19ff1f4-5553-51d3-879d-2ac662575fad', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://art