tions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Associated Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T17:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dfec808-36b7-5bf1-9b79-7017f59401a6', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dfec808-36b7-5bf1-9b79-7017f59401a6'}, {'abstract': 'In a strange way, seeing-eye-to-eye with my husband about religion was making me feel very alone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/fashion/an-agnostics-guide-to-marriage.html', 'snippet': 'In a strange way, seeing-eye-to-eye with my husband about religion was making me feel very alone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN my husband, Fred, and I planned our wedding, he had two strong opinions: 1) brisket should be served, along with the fried chicken; and 2) we would recite the Lord’s Prayer in the ceremony.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/fashion/02MODERNLOVE_SPAN/02MODERNLOVE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/02/fashion/02MODERNLOVE_SPAN/02MODERNLOVE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/fashion/02MODERNLOVE_SPAN/02MODERNLOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/fashion/02MODERNLOVE_SPAN/02MODERNLOVE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1346, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/fashion/02MODERNLOVE_SPAN/02MODERNLOVE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/fashion/02MODERNLOVE_SPAN/02MODERNLOVE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Agnostic’s Guide to Marriage', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Agnostic’s Guide to Marriage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T17:01:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colleen Oakley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colleen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oakley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f72bf077-93d9-5200-a4e3-1278e3f920d7', 'word_count': 1457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f72bf077-93d9-5200-a4e3-1278e3f920d7'}, {'abstract': 'Sure Paul D. Ryan’s acceptance speech was a hit, but how much did it help Mitt Romney’s prospects of winning the White House?', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/with-speech-ryan-may-have-helped-himself-more-than-romney/', 'snippet': 'Sure Paul D. Ryan’s acceptance speech was a hit, but how much did it help Mitt Romney’s prospects of winning the White House?', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. – By every measure – the cheers in the hall, the praise from commentators across the country, the elation among aides to Mitt Romney – Representative Paul D. Ryan’s speech accepting the vice-presidential nomination was a hit. He aggressively framed the campaign against President Obama, signaled that he, unlike some previous vice-presidential candidates, had no compunctions about leading the attack, and anchored Mr. Romney in a conservative school of thought that has come to define the Republican Party.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Speech, Ryan May Have Helped Himself More Than Romney', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T17:05:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/027b42a0-5ce7-5377-9e7f-a4f78e175bc0', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/027b42a0-5ce7-5377-9e7f-a4f78e175bc0'}, {'abstract': 'No male upstream from Mike Huckabee finished high school. Ann Romney’s grandfather was a Welsh coal miner. Origin stories from the Republican convention.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/meet-the-parents/', 'snippet': 'No male upstream from Mike Huckabee finished high school. Ann Romney’s grandfather was a Welsh coal miner. Origin stories from the Republican convention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla.–In her convention speech last night, Condoleezza Rice said “the essence of America” is the idea that “you can come from humble circumstances and do great things. That it doesn’t matter where you came from but where you are going.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meet the Parents', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T17:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afa258b1-17f2-578e-a377-871bd7365355', 'word_count': 1498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afa258b1-17f2-578e-a377-871bd7365355'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Sullivan’s seventh book, “My American Revolution,” chronicles his quest through some of America’s chaotic birthplaces.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/revolutionary-inroads/', 'snippet': 'Robert Sullivan’s seventh book, “My American Revolution,” chronicles his quest through some of America’s chaotic birthplaces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To Robert Sullivan, history is not so much a collection of dates and facts but actual places you can revisit — layers of geography that can be excavated one by one. Sullivan’s seventh book, “My American Revolution” (Farrar, Straus & Giroux, $26), chronicles his quest through some of America’s chaotic birthplaces, parts of New Jersey and New York where forgotten battles still haunt the landscape. His journey begins at the top of the Empire State Building, where Sullivan looks into the distance and sees greater New York as a “palimpsest of the Revolution, a painted-over canvas of ancient routes walked smooth. . . . ”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '64', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Revolutionary Inroads', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Revolutionary Inroads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T17:32:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70220f9c-db37-5375-b507-91653c0ef202', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70220f9c-db37-5375-b507-91653c0ef202'}, {'abstract': 'But a shorter cycle this time.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/memories-of-the-bush-administration/', 'snippet': 'But a shorter cycle this time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Updike once wrote a novel titled Memories of the Ford Administration; it was largely about sex in the era “after the sexual revolution but before the microbes”.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Memories Of The Bush Administration', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T17:36:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24375e97-b588-57b2-98df-3738ab5e6d4c', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24375e97-b588-57b2-98df-3738ab5e6d4c'}, {'abstract': 'An elaborate marriage proposal on video goes viral and prompts questions about how it was done. Here are some answers.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/how-to-propose-the-pogue-way/', 'snippet': 'An elaborate marriage proposal on video goes viral and prompts questions about how it was done. Here are some answers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two weeks ago, I proposed. To the sweetest, funniest, wisest woman I’ve ever known.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Propose the Pogue Way', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T17:48:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c13f3c8f-19a4-59a4-baf3-71cf39b98410', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c13f3c8f-19a4-59a4-baf3-71cf39b98410'}, {'abstract': 'A small industrial-cozy restaurant whose pleasures are modest and familiar: grown-up drinks, rustic snacks and sound seasonal ingredients, approached without too much deference.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/dining/reviews/lulu-po-in-fort-greene-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'A small industrial-cozy restaurant whose pleasures are modest and familiar: grown-up drinks, rustic snacks and sound seasonal ingredients, approached without too much deference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LATE summer twilight on Carlton Avenue, faint hurrahs from the family reunion in the pastor’s backyard, firefighters lobbing a football outside Engine 210. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05HUNGRY2/05HUNGRY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05HUNGRY2/05HUNGRY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05HUNGRY2/05HUNGRY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 827, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05HUNGRY2/05HUNGRY2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1655, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05HUNGRY2/05HUNGRY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05HUNGRY2/05HUNGRY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05HUNGRY2/05HUNGRY2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Quiet, Modest Brooklynite', 'kicker': 'Hungry City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Modest Brooklynite Worth