a', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sofia (Bulgaria)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T18:10:36+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/5d5f599d-3868-568f-9ce3-e78b0705f222', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/5d5f599d-3868-568f-9ce3-e78b0705f222'}, {'abstract': 'Open dining strategy advice: head to the New Delhi Spice booth and avoid the crowd.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/u-s-open-food-of-the-day-vegetable-curry-combo/', 'snippet': 'Open dining strategy advice: head to the New Delhi Spice booth and avoid the crowd.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is another in the daily series of food reviews from the United States Open concession stands.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Open Food of the Day: Vegetable Curry Combo', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T18:15:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6f1cbd5-4da2-50f3-a623-87742cb74c87', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6f1cbd5-4da2-50f3-a623-87742cb74c87'}, {'abstract': 'At these spots, you can sit down for a meal and then shop for house-made goods to take home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/travel/chicagos-meal-market-hybrids.html', 'snippet': 'At these spots, you can sit down for a meal and then shop for house-made goods to take home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO’S culinary scene has in the last year and a half been enlivened by big-name chefs: Grant Achatz, Jean-Georges Vongerichten and Michael Shrader have all opened restaurants in that time. But you don’t have to make a reservation to sample the best in local cuisine. Lately, a number of hybrid restaurant-specialty markets have popped up, catering to customers who hope that, armed with the same spice rub, they can recreate a chef’s dishes at home.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02HEADSUP_SPAN/02HEADSUP-1345829540981-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02HEADSUP_SPAN/02HEADSUP-1345829540981-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02HEADSUP_SPAN/02HEADSUP_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02HEADSUP_SPAN/02HEADSUP_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1119, 'width': 1498, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02HEADSUP_SPAN/02HEADSUP_