sian energy company, has long presented the Shtokman field in the Barents Sea as the jewel in the crown of its natural gas reserves, a find that might hold enough gas to meet global demand for a year.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/business/Gasprom/Gasprom-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/business/Gasprom/Gasprom-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1258, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Gazprom, Views Conflict on Viability of Barents Sea Gas Project', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Gazprom, Views Conflict on Viability of Barents Sea Gas Project', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gazprom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Barents Sea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T19:01:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75c45757-6fb2-5125-a4ae-c699b253352b', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75c45757-6fb2-5125-a4ae-c699b253352b'}, {'abstract': 'The new rule will allow teams to bring back one player during the season.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/n-f-l-and-union-agree-to-change-in-injured-reserve-rule/', 'snippet': 'The new rule will allow teams to bring back one player during the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.F.L. and the players union agreed Thursday to a change to the injured reserve rules and a move of the trade deadline that owners first approved in the spring.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. and Union Agree to Change in Injured Reserve Rule', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Changes To Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T19:04:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87094c31-5b95-58c8-a4b0-36a8e8edd199', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87094c31-5b95-58c8-a4b0-36a8e8edd199'}, {'abstract': 'Mariano Rajoy said that Spain could meet the financial obligations of its troubled regions, despite word from Valencia that it would require more rescue money than it requested in July.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/business/global/daily-euro-zone-watch.html', 'snippet': 'Mariano Rajoy said that Spain could meet the financial obligations of its troubled regions, despite word from Valencia that it would require more rescue money than it requested in July.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — The Spanish prime minister, Mariano Rajoy, sought to reassure markets on Thursday that Spain could meet the financial obligations of its troubled regions despite word from Valencia that it would require 1 billion more euros in rescue money than it requested in July.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/business/Eurozone/Eurozone-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/business/Eurozone/Eurozone-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1418, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rescue Fund Is Sufficient, Spain’s Leader Asserts', 'kicker': 'Euro Watch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rescue Fund Is Sufficient, Spain’s Leader Asserts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajoy, Mariano', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T19:04:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a45a6546-78f4-5d00-8b7d-c0401e7f19e4', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a45a6546-78f4-5d00-8b7d-c0401e7f19e4'}, {'abstract': 'The Telluride Film Festival, which begins Friday, unveils a lineup that includes “Amour” and “Midnight’s Children.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/telluride-film-festival-announces-lineup/', 'snippet': 'The Telluride Film Festival, which begins Friday, unveils a lineup that includes “Amour” and “Midnight’s Children.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Telluride Film Festival, keeping with its practice, made a last-minute announcement of the program for its proceedings, which begin in Colorado on Friday and continue through Monday. The festival includes 25 documentary and narrative films, like the Cannes Palme d’Or winner “Amour,” from Michael Haneke; “Midnight’s Children,” based on the Salman Rushdie novel; and “The Act of Killing,” a nonfiction film in which former members of death squads in Indonesia re-enact their killings as if they were scenes from favorite films. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Telluride Film Festival Announces Lineup', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telluride Film Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toronto International Film Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cannes (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Telluride (Colo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venice (Italy)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T19:08:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ciep