t': '“House for Sale” follows Mr. Franzen’s experience selling a family house after the death of his mother.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/adaptation-of-jonathan-franzen-essay-heads-to-stage/', 'snippet': '“House for Sale” follows Mr. Franzen’s experience selling a family house after the death of his mother.', 'lead_paragraph': ' “House for Sale,” a play adapted from an essay by Jonathan Franzen, is coming to Off Broadway.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adaptation of Jonathan Franzen Essay Heads to Stage', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jonathan Franzen Essay Heads to the Stage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fish, Daniel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franzen, Jonathan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transport Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T19:18:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/260eaf7b-43b5-5ca2-8f47-e1a404d20a01', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/260eaf7b-43b5-5ca2-8f47-e1a404d20a01'}, {'abstract': 'When your partner spurns your boss’s dinner invitation; what to do when your dog bites a handler; and restraining from pointing out a fake diamond ring.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/fashion/the-honor-of-a-partners-presence.html', 'snippet': 'When your partner spurns your boss’s dinner invitation; what to do when your dog bites a handler; and restraining from pointing out a fake diamond ring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I received a promotion at work, and my boss proposed a celebratory dinner with my partner and me. I feel obliged to accept, but my partner does not care for my boss and has refused to go. I told my boss that I would be delighted to dine with him, but my partner could not attend. He then became insistent that my partner join us. I honor my partner’s wishes first, and am put off by my boss’s determination. How do I decline again, firmly and politely, and maintain good relations with him? Or is there another solution? Nadine, Washington', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Honor of a Partner’s Presence', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Honor of a Partner’s Presence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T19:23:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a939b778-dd36-55b2-b64b-5c7a1c41aa70', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a939b778-dd36-55b2-b64b-5c7a1c41aa70'}, {'abstract': 'A French company’s new pajama collection comes with a panda design – and a message.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/the-get-bonpoints-hi-panda-baby-pajamas/', 'snippet': 'A French company’s new pajama collection comes with a panda design – and a message.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I really imagined this collection as a dash of humor to start the school year,” says Christine Inammorato, the artistic director of Bonpoint. For fall, she’s brought the “insolent” creatures of the contemporary Chinese artist Ji-Ji’s Hi Panda collection to an exclusive series of cotton tees for children and moms, plus these pajamas for infants (available Sept. 1). His now famous Evil Pandas are made even cuter — if that’s possible — for the young and stylish with the addition of glasses, a book (how studious) and, of course, the\xa0French company’s signature cherries. Lest we forget, though, the bespectacled icons, which the fashion world fell in love with at the artist’s 2010 Palais de Tokyo show, aren’t there to just look adorable. Innamorato explains, “Ji-Ji gave them a true meaning: they reflect the passion, narcissism and endless search of identity of the Chinese generation born after 1980.” Lesson learned.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Bonpoint’s Hi Panda Baby Pajamas', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T19:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Kane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83de0281-c7c9-5edf-b2df-ceb6982c1d6f', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83de0281-c7c9-5edf-b2df-ceb6982c1d6f'}, {'abstract': 'Blatant falsehoods like those of the Romney-Ryan campaign are only possible because Americans no longer expect to hear the truth.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/speech-lies-and-apathy/', 'snippet': 'Blatant falsehoods like those of the Romney-Ryan campaign are only possible because Americans no longer expect to hear the truth.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Speech, Lies and Apathy', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'n