a': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pop Listings for Aug. 31-Sept. 6', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T22:16:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/df4c9acf-2765-5489-a87a-7d338242ab90', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df4c9acf-2765-5489-a87a-7d338242ab90'}, {'abstract': 'The Times will be providing updates and analysis from Tampa on our live dashboard. You can also follow along on Twitter @thecaucus, or follow our list of Times journalists covering the convention.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/live-updates-from-the-republican-national-convention-3/', 'snippet': 'The Times will be providing updates and analysis from Tampa on our live dashboard. You can also follow along on Twitter @thecaucus, or follow our list of Times journalists covering the convention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times will be providing updates and analysis from Tampa on our live dashboard. You can also follow along on Twitter @thecaucus, or follow our list of Times journalists covering the convention.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Updates From the Republican National Convention', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T22:17:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afb128ec-ca7f-5714-8091-71d0a162d617', 'word_count': 5710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afb128ec-ca7f-5714-8091-71d0a162d617'}, {'abstract': 'A risk for Mitt Romney is that even with favorable turnout, the Republican coalition may not be broad enough for a victory, given that the party is struggling among minority voters.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/30/base-turnout-strategy-may-be-too-narrow-for-romney/', 'snippet': 'A risk for Mitt Romney is that even with favorable turnout, the Republican coalition may not be broad enough for a victory, given that the party is struggling among minority voters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney’s strategy once seemed self-evident. First, skewer President Obama over the tepid economic recovery. Second, lean just enough to the center over the course of the fall campaign so you won’t lose because of social issues, temperament and tone, controversial proposals about the welfare state or other things that might distract voters from your economic message.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Base Turnout Strategy May Be Too Narrow for Romney', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T22:21:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93fd9240-3921-53f3-90e0-15a813f1715b', 'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93fd9240-3921-53f3-90e0-15a813f1715b'}, {'abstract': 'A selected guide to jazz performances and festivals in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/arts/music/jazz-listings-for-aug-31-sept-6.html', 'snippet': 'A selected guide to jazz performances and festivals in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jazz', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jazz Listings for Aug. 31-Sept. 6', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-30T22:21:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/58d9f87c-8af2-5cef-88af-9fb40da7edce', 'word_count': 2111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58d9f87c-8af2-5cef-88af-9fb40da7edce'}, {'abstract': '“For a Good Time, Call ...” is a phone sex comedy that does not try to be more than it really is.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/movies/for-a-good-time-call-is-a-romp-about-phone-sex.html', 'snippet': '“For a Good Time, Call ...” is a phone sex comedy that does not try to be more than it really is.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The enterprising New York women who establish a flourishing phone sex business in the boundary-breaking farce “For a Good Time, Call ...” know how to talk the talk. But can they walk the walk? The running joke of this fizzy, potty-mouthed comedy, directed by Jamie Travis, is that anyone with an erotic imagination — even the nicest of nice girls — can talk dirty and make money at it. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/arts/31FOR