rl': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/opinion/the-sexual-bully-in-albany.html', 'snippet': 'New York’s Assembly leader, comptroller and attorney general face questions about a growing harassment case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The stories about Assemblyman Vito Lopez groping and demeaning female staff members are flooding out of the back rooms in Albany. Female former employees told The Times this week that Mr. Lopez had asked them not to wear a bra to work. He routinely commented on their clothes — skirts not short enough — and their physique, preferring that they be “well endowed.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sexual Bully in Albany', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Sexual Bully in Albany', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Sheldon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Vito J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiNapoli, Thomas P', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T01:10:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/539283a5-0b46-59e1-83e7-f3cb3e40e6af', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/539283a5-0b46-59e1-83e7-f3cb3e40e6af'}, {'abstract': 'Federal courts are deciding that state laws that suppress minority votes cannot be allowed to stand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/opinion/justice-for-voters-in-texas-and-florida.html', 'snippet': 'Federal courts are deciding that state laws that suppress minority votes cannot be allowed to stand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republicans in Texas and Florida have been in the vanguard of the pernicious, widespread efforts to suppress voting by Hispanics and blacks. Fortunately, federal courts are seeing these efforts for what they are: a variation on the racist laws that disenfranchised millions before those tactics were outlawed by the Voting Rights Act. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justice for Voters in Texas and Florida', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justice for Voters in Texas and Florida', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'League of Women Voters', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T01:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/14fce239-f987-576b-b093-465bc453f8a7', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14fce239-f987-576b-b093-465bc453f8a7'}, {'abstract': 'The Metropolitan Transportation Authority, saying that conditions had improved at two subway stations after their trash cans were removed, implemented the program at eight more stations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/nyregion/mta-expands-an-effort-to-remove-trash-cans.html', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Transportation Authority, saying that conditions had improved at two subway stations after their trash cans were removed, implemented the program at eight more stations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The evidence has piled beside turnstiles and beneath benches, along subway platforms where riders found nowhere else to place their coffee cups or apple cores and on the tracks where tattered newspapers and crushed bottles seem to have taken up permanent residence.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/nyregion/GARBAGE1/GARBAGE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/08/31/nyregion/GARBAGE1/GARBAGE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/nyregion/GARBAGE1/GARBAGE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/nyregion/GARBAGE1/GARBAGE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_n