mmediate explanation for the message, which expressed support for three members of the Pussy Riot band who were convicted of hooliganism charges and sentenced to two years in prison for a protest against the Russian leader Vladimir V. Putin at a Moscow cathedral. Investigators said that the two women had been stabbed many times and that the murders occurred several days before the bodies were found. Supporters of Pussy Riot expressed dismay over the message at the scene; the band members’ lawyer called it “a horrendous provocation” or the work of a psychopath, according to news reports. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Crime-Scene Message About Convicted Band', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Crime-Scene Message About Convicted Band', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pussy Riot', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T03:44:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9ac6232-a3be-59c1-bcc8-aacea7763b51', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9ac6232-a3be-59c1-bcc8-aacea7763b51'}, {'abstract': 'Op-Ed columnists Frank Bruni and Charles M. Blow debate whether Republicans are waging a war on women.', 'web_url': 'http