onal', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2ca8636-9e83-5d7e-bae1-59619afa48e5', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2ca8636-9e83-5d7e-bae1-59619afa48e5'}, {'abstract': 'India’s race to space with China is “ludicrous,” the author argues.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/brics-in-space/', 'snippet': 'India’s race to space with China is “ludicrous,” the author argues.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Let’s send a mission to Mars, Prime Minister Manmohan Singh announced a couple of weeks ago, just as his government was fending off corruption charges and the country was still recovering from the biggest blackout since the invention of electricity,” Hartosh Singh Bal wrote in the New York Times’s Latitude blog. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BRICS in Space', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T05:28:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b51f8428-d4b0-56be-9a74-79242ed76c3a', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b51f8428-d4b0-56be-9a74-79242ed76c3a'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney’s and Paul D. Ryan’s speeches seemed to signal the arrival of a campaign in which fact-checking concerns have largely been set aside.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/us/politics/ryans-speech-contained-a-litany-of-falsehoods.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney’s and Paul D. Ryan’s speeches seemed to signal the arrival of a campaign in which fact-checking concerns have largely been set aside.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representative Paul D. Ryan used his convention speech on Wednesday to fault President Obama for failing to act on a deficit-reduction plan that he himself had helped kill. He chided Democrats for seeking $716 billion in Medicare cuts that he too had sought. And he lamented the nation’s credit rating — which was downgraded after a debt-ceiling standoff that he and other House Republicans helped instigate.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/us/FACT/FACT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 917, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/us/FACT/FACT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1949, 'width': 1746, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Facts Take a Beating in Acceptance Speeches', 'kicker': 'Check Point', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Facts Take a Beating In Acceptance Speeches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value