 are widely tapped to succeed them, Xi Jinping and Li Keqiang.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/global-home/31weiwei-rdv/31weiwei-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 625, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/global-home/31weiwei-rdv/31weiwei-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 625, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Merkel in China: A Dissenting View', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ai Weiwei', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T06:14:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37f929ab-1a1b-5e85-bd12-7c55e9ff4dae', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37f929ab-1a1b-5e85-bd12-7c55e9ff4dae'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Pawlenty, the former governor of Minnesota, walked through the convention hall, largely unnoticed.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/an-ex-governor-slips-by/', 'snippet': 'Tim Pawlenty, the former governor of Minnesota, walked through the convention hall, largely unnoticed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla.—Tim Pawlenty came close to being a star of the last two Republican conventions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Ex-Governor Slips By', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T06:33:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1aa38e0-28fa-54a6-9979-d3a5b54ba24c', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1aa38e0-28fa-54a6-9979-d3a5b54ba24c'}, {'abstract': 'Clint Eastwood’s rambling endorsement of Mitt Romney set off immediate questions and finger-pointing among Romney supporters.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/surprise-speaker-delivers-the-unexpected/', 'snippet': 'Clint Eastwood’s rambling endorsement of Mitt Romney set off immediate questions and finger-pointing among Romney supporters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla.—Clint Eastwood’s rambling, head-scratching endorsement of Mitt Romney on Thursday set off immediate questions and finger-pointing among Romney supporters: Who booked Mr. Eastwood? Did anyone have an idea of what he was going to say? Did anyone read his remarks before they were broadcast?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Surprise Speaker Delivers the Unexpected', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':