 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/the-ex-factor/', 'snippet': 'A variation on elder care: moving in with an ex.', 'lead_paragraph': 'She had recently moved to beautiful San Francisco from the East Coast. He was an artist living in the old Victorian house she was sketching. He came outside, looked over her shoulder and pointed out that she hadn’t drawn the correct number of pillars.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ex Factor', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sonoma County (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T10:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60543432-4d8c-5e28-9107-9b0a0c90c4c4', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60543432-4d8c-5e28-9107-9b0a0c90c4c4'}, {'abstract': 'After a year in the Maine woods with her family, the author finds the re-entry experience in New Jersey somewhat jarring.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/an-unlikely-welcome-wagon-back-in-suburbia/', 'snippet': 'After a year in the Maine woods with her family, the author finds the re-entry experience in New Jersey somewhat jarring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We returned from our year in the woods on Aug. 1 and are still in the thick of unpacking, resettling, registering the kids for public school, and catching up on doctor appointments. The big surprise was having to fix the myriad house problems that manifested in our absence, such as broken shower nozzles, a broken refrigerator shelf, a year’s worth of untrimmed hedges and mismatched touch-up paint unwittingly applied by our well-meaning tenants throughout the house. My shell of calm began to erode as I drove across the Piscataqua River Bridge — Maine’s southern border.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Unlikely Welcome Wagon, Back in Suburbia', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suburbs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T10:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susannah Hopkins Leisher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susannah', 'middlename': 'Hopkins', 'lastname': 'Leisher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/becb8e84-f848-5b4c-b2fc-3241950a257e', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/becb8e84-f848-5b4c-b2fc-3241950a257e'}, {'abstract': 'Manufacturing and mining showed almost no growth at all in the latest financial quarter.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/indias-economy-continues-to-be-weak/', 'snippet': 'Manufacturing and mining showed almost no growth at all in the latest financial quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Indian gross domestic product report released Friday for the April-June quarter showed that the economy was doing only marginally better than in the previous quarter. Growth was up 5.5 percent during the quarter from a year earlier, compared with 5.3 percent in the period ended in March, which was the weakest growth in nine years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India’s Economy Continues to Be Weak', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HSBC Holdings PLC.', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reserve Bank of India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T10:31:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fe1d05f-160a-57fe-b1c0-d044a775c104', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fe1d05f-160a-57fe-b1c0-d044a775c104'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Khosla has written a guide to understanding India’s constitution, the lengthiest in the world', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/a-conversation-with-constitution-expert-madhav-khosla/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Khosla has written a guide to understanding India’s constitution, the lengthiest in the world', 'lead_paragraph': 'Madhav Khosla, a doctoral student of political theory at Harvard University, is the author of “The Indian Constitution,” a short introduction to the world’s longest political text, which consists of 395 articles and 12 schedules. The book is a fascinating tour through the life of India’s supreme law, analyzing its central features like federalism, fundamental rights and the separation of power. In an interview with India Ink, Mr. Khosla explained why he sees the Constitution as more than a political text and how his book isn’t just for lawyers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With: Constitution Expert Madhav Khosla', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T10:50:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aayush Soni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aayush', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f59a88c1-bc76-58aa-9141-898ca8abfe5c', 'word_count': 1253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f59a88c1-bc76-58aa-9141-898ca8abfe5c'}, {'abstract': 'Doing your research before downloading freeware and shareware can help keep your computer safer.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/qa-be-cautious-with-free-software/', 'snippet': 'Doing your research before downloading freeware and shareware can help keep your computer safer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Be Cautious With Free Software', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Micr