llions of people languish in poverty, the governing party of more than three decades was expected to win the vote handily.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/world/africa/change-unlikely-from-angola-election-but-discontent-simmers.html', 'snippet': 'In a nation where Lamborghinis dot city streets, but where millions of people languish in poverty, the governing party of more than three decades was expected to win the vote handily.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LUANDA, Angola — From his doorstep, Paulo Silva can see emblems of his country’s transformation from war-addled basket case to petroleum powerhouse. A flock of cranes hovers over a skyline dotted with climbing skyscrapers, and dead center is a symbol of the country’s multiparty democracy: the half-built dome of the new home of Angola’s Parliament. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/world/sub-angola2/sub-angola2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/01/world/sub-angola2/sub-angola2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/world/sub-angola2/sub-angola2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/world/sub-angola2/sub-angola2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1268, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/world/sub-angola2/sub-angola2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/01/world/sub-angola2/sub-angola2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/world/sub-angola2/sub-angola2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Change Unlikely From Angolan Election, but Discontent Simmers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Discontent Simmers as Angolans Go to the Polls, but Change Is Unlikely', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANGOLA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dos Santos, Jose Eduardo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T11:02:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99424777-b699-543b-9a91-ba0b93aef661', 'word_count': 1161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99424777-b699-543b-9a91-ba0b93aef661'}, {'abstract': 'From the standpoint of our forecast model, the most important points on Thursday were economic rather than rhetorical. Two of the seven data series that make up the model’s economic index were updated on Thursday, and they both had somewhat better news about the condition of the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/aug-30-remember-the-economy/', 'snippet': 'From the standpoint of our forecast model, the most important points on Thursday were economic rather than rhetorical. Two of the seven data series that make up the model’s economic index were updated on Thursday, and they both had somewhat better...', 'lead_paragraph': 'We are in a holding pattern as we await polls that fully reflect the effects of the Republican National Convention.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aug. 30: Remember the Economy?', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T11:17:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fdabaab-2d99-5906-9e43-7b8e98718e75', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fdabaab-2d99-5906-9e43-7b8e98718e75'}, {'abstract': 'The spiritual leader of Lebanon’s Shiites disappeared 34 years ago on Friday. As the community faces a spillover from the conflict in Syria that threatens the rule of its traditional patron, Bashar al-Assad, some politicians may have an interest in maintaining the mystery surrounding the fate of Imam Musa Sadr.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/lebanon-syria-and-the-missing-imam/', 'snippet': 'The spiritual leader of Lebanon’s Shiites disappeared 34 years ago on Friday. As the community faces a spillover from the conflict in Syria that threatens the rule of its traditional patron, Bashar al-Assad, some politicians may have an interest i...', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The Shiite Muslim community of Lebanon was marking on Friday the 34th anniversary of the disappearance of its erstwhile spiritual leader, Imam Musa Sadr, after a reported claim by the country’s foreign minister that he was still alive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/blogs/rdv-mussadr/rdv-mussadr-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/blogs/rdv-mussadr/rdv-mussadr-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1411, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lebanon, Syria and the Missing Imam', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hezbollah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T11:29:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_ma