le/ce5d5f9c-dbae-5548-a7ee-59b7343837a5', 'word_count': 1094, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce5d5f9c-dbae-5548-a7ee-59b7343837a5'}, {'abstract': 'The reaction to an article about writers’ buying five-star reviews suggests several things: this sort of fakery has been going on for a long time, it is pervasive with books as well as other items, and there are few remedies in sight. Caveat emptor.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/reviewing-the-reviewers-story/', 'snippet': 'The reaction to an article about writers’ buying five-star reviews suggests several things: this sort of fakery has been going on for a long time, it is pervasive with books as well as other items, and there are few remedies in sight. Caveat empto...', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a large and energetic reaction to last Sunday’s article about a service that allowed writers to commission five-star reviews of their books. Some readers were shocked that the world of online reviews was pervaded by fakery and insincerity. “Sure puts a damper on online shopping,” wrote one. Said another: “This practice is the review equivalent of doping.” But just as with sports doping, others were not surprised and said it would be impossible to eradicate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing the Review Story', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T11:48:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname