rganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36da309b-2a93-5bbc-b5b5-da2ee79b1cb2', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36da309b-2a93-5bbc-b5b5-da2ee79b1cb2'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney’s speech at the Republican National Convention was the performance of someone who may not be a natural at politics, but had clearly spent time practicing for this appearance before the biggest audience of his life.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/romneys-performance-provided-a-smooth-ending-for-g-o-p-convention/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney’s speech at the Republican National Convention was the performance of someone who may not be a natural at politics, but had clearly spent time practicing for this appearance before the biggest audience of his life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA , Fla. — Just after 10:30 p.m. on Thursday, about 10 minutes behind schedule, Mitt Romney strode down on the red-carpeted floor of the Tampa Bay Times Forum, shaking hands on both sides of the aisle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Performance Provided a Smooth Ending for G.O.P. Convention', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T12:39:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44f0b8df-0f1a-57a5-b3c0-1d6bc11911fa', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44f0b8df-0f1a-57a5-b3c0-1d6bc11911fa'}, {'abstract': 'At a meeting of the Non-Aligned Movement, Ban Ki-Moon dispensed with the usual balanced language of U.N. chiefs.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/how-to-make-a-conference-matter/', 'snippet': 'At a meeting of the Non-Aligned Movement, Ban Ki-Moon dispensed with the usual balanced language of U.N. chiefs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At this week’s annual meeting of the Non-Aligned Movement in Tehran, the biggest international conference in Iran’s modern history, the country’s leaders made a case for their nuclear program and tried to demonstrate that Western efforts to ostracize it were failing. They envisioned the gathering as a diplomatic triumph — but they lost control of the script.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Make a Conference Matter', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban Ki-moon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T12:40:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Giacomo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Giacomo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92d8e4cc-790d-5b24-bab9-6cfc858d6ae3', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92d8e4cc-790d-5b24-bab9-6cfc858d6ae3'}, {'abstract': 'On a two-day trip to China, Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany concentrated on winning support from Prime Minister Wen Jiabao to help ease the sovereign debt crisis in Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/business/global/china-and-germany-promise-to-strengthen-ties.html', 'snippet': 'On a two-day trip to China, Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany concentrated on winning support from Prime Minister Wen Jiabao to help ease the sovereign debt crisis in Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI — Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany headed home on Friday from a two-day visit to China with a stack of newly signed business contracts and a pledge for Beijing’s backing in the euro crisis, but few promises from Beijing to improve human rights. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/world/chinamerkel/chinamerkel-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/world/chinamerkel/chinamerkel-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1277, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/world/chinamerkel/chinamerkel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/01/world/chinamerkel/chinamerkel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/world/chinamerkel/chinamerkel-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Merkel’s China Trip Focuses on Economy, Not Rights', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Merkel’s China Trip Focuses on Economy, Not Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wen Jiabao', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T12:45:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza and Melissa Eddy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c13d6f3-83ff-5493-8f5b-145751cfd839', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c13d6f3-83ff-5493-8f5b-145751cfd839'}, {'abstract': 'Detective work in Paris. David Byrne and music. Vintage menswear. Just some of the subjects in books T is reading this fall.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/bookshelf-23/', 'snippet': 'Detective work in Paris. David Byrne and music. Vintage menswear. Just some of the subjects in books T is reading this fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the early 1980s, the artist Sophie Calle found an address book on a Paris street and, after tracking down the people listed inside, composed a very controversial secondhand portrait of its owner, Pierre D. Her titillating detective work finally appears in English as “The Address Book” (Siglio, $30). In “How Music Works” (McSweeney’s, $32), David Byrne approaches his personal passion with the clear-minded intensity of a scholar. Antoine Wilson’s novel “Panorama City” (Houghton Mifflin Harcourt, $24) contains one of the season’s more endearing characters: a binoculars-wearing, soliloquizing doofus named Oppen Porter. And among the utilitarian rarities collected in “Vintage Menswear” (Laurence King, $50) are a fin de siècle firefighter jacket and a “walking suit” made specially for Alpine rambling.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bookshelf', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byrne, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calle, Sophie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "McSweeney's", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T13:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cffc4df-6124-5f94-952b-6c9969f0c803', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cffc4df-6124-5f94-952b-6c9969f0c803'}, {'abstract': 'Two researchers have spent the summer chasing an elusive surveillance tool from Bahrain across five continents, Nicole Perlroth reports on Friday in The New York Times. What they found was the widespread use of sophisticated, off-the-shelf computer espionage software by governments with questionable records on human rights.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/daily-report-a-surveillance-product-is-aimed-at-dissidents/', 'snippet': 'Two researchers have spent the summer chasing an elusive surveillance tool from Bahrain across five continents, Nicole Perlroth reports on Friday in The New York Times. What they found was the 