vard are trying to create films that reflect the messiness of life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/movies/harvard-filmmakers-messy-world.html', 'snippet': 'Faculty members and students at the Sensory Ethnography Lab at Harvard are trying to create films that reflect the messiness of life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUCKED within the syllabus for a class that the filmmaker and anthropologist Lucien Castaing-Taylor teaches at Harvard is a rhetorical question that sums up his view of nonfiction film: “If life is messy and unpredictable, and documentary is a reflection of life, should it not be digressive and open-ended too?”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02SUBHARVARD_SPAN/02HARVARDSUB_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 183, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02SUBHARVARD_SPAN/02HARVARDSUB_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 183}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02SUBHARVARD_SPAN/02HARVARDSUB_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 312, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02SUBHARVARD_SPAN/02HARVARDSUB_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02SUBHARVARD_SPAN/02SUBHARVARD_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02SUBHARVARD_SPAN/02SUBHARVARD_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 't