tein on the Beach (Opera)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glass, Philip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Childs, Lucinda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T14:06:47+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/095cc031-9cc7-5efa-86e6-f455cb86462f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/095cc031-9cc7-5efa-86e6-f455cb86462f'}, {'abstract': 'The opera “Einstein on the Beach” opens a 10-day run at the Brooklyn Academy of Music on Sept. 14, and it will be the first time New York has seen it in 20 years. Will it resonate?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/arts/music/einstein-on-the-beach-revival-at-bam-raises-questions.html', 'snippet': 'The opera “Einstein on the Beach” opens a 10-day run at the Brooklyn Academy of Music on Sept. 14, and it will be the first time New York has seen it in 20 years. Will it resonate?', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOME works of art become mythical, either because they are so important or because few people actually know them. “Einstein on the Beach,” the 1976 intermissionless four-and-a-half-hour opera by Robert Wilson and Philip Glass, qualifies on both counts. When “Einstein” opens a 10-day run at the Brooklyn Academy of Music on Sept. 14, it will be the first time New York has seen it in 20 years.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/02EINSTEIN1_SPAN/02EINSTEIN1_SPAN-ar