/09/02/books/review/double-cross-by-ben-macintyre.html', 'snippet': 'Ben Macintyre tells the story of five extraordinary spies at the center of a ruse to fool the Germans about D-Day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ben Macintyre is the leading practitioner of oddball-powered history. A connoisseur and celebrant of eccentricity, he specializes in often hilarious, sometimes tragic, but always fizzily exhilarating tales of madcap exploits and bizarre adventures.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/books/review/ROSE-2/ROSE-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 723, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/books/review/ROSE-2/ROSE-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1446, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/books/review/ROSE-2/ROSE-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/books/review/ROSE-2/ROSE-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/books/review/ROSE-2/ROSE-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'War Games', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'War Games', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Macintyre, Ben', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T15:12:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Rose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a6a4a7c-d162-536c-abf4-df983ef60e7f', 'word_count': 863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a6a4a7c-d162-536c-abf4-df983ef60e7f'}, {'abstract': 'After years of resisting exotic bazaars and stands selling trinkets, the author is done holding back. Her finds aren’t things, but memories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/travel/theyre-souvenirs-not-stuff.html', 'snippet': 'After years of resisting exotic bazaars and stands selling trinkets, the author is done holding back. Her finds aren’t things, but memories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOUVENIR. Even the word is beautiful. It has that gentle, whispery sound of memory brushing by. A wonderfully inclusive label, it can apply to anything, because anything can be a souvenir, any object whose real value lies in its association with a past journey — or, I suppose, a person. A souvenir of a city. A souvenir of a love affair. Something that may have started as an inconvenience (how will I find room in my suitcase?) but on arrival home makes its way onto the mantel as a keepsake of delight. If it is a souvenir, it can transcend kitsch, at least for your lifetime. You are the keeper of its value. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02SOUVENIR2/02SOUVENIR2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02SOUVENIR2/02SOUVENIR2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02SOUVENIR2/02JPSOUVENIR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 779, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02SOUVENIR2/02JPSOUVENIR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1141, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02SOUVENIR2/02SOUVENIR2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02SOUVENIR2/02SOUVENIR2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02SOUVENIR2/02SOUVENIR2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'They’re Souvenirs, Not Stuff!', 'kicker': 'Personal Journeys', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They’re Souvenirs, Not Stuff!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memorabilia and Souvenirs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T15:12:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dominique Browning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dominique', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': Non