on Top of Pasta', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T15:21:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71e85e18-d4c0-59e5-8460-8c45ddbc9978', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71e85e18-d4c0-59e5-8460-8c45ddbc9978'}, {'abstract': 'With Nomura announcing $1 billion in cost cuts on Friday, the Japanese firm formally and concretely revealed a retreat from the global financial player role it once sought.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/nomuras-failed-global-ambitions/', 'snippet': 'With Nomura announcing $1 billion in cost cuts on Friday, the Japanese firm formally and concretely revealed a retreat from the global financial player role it once sought.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Nomura announcing $1 billion in cost cuts on Friday, the Japanese firm formally and concretely revealed a retreat from the role it once sought at a global financial player.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nomura’s Failed Global Ambitions', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watanabe, Kenichi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nomura Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T15:24:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c70d5d0a-842f-541f-803f-33931cb2372c', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c70d5d0a-842f-541f-803f-33931cb2372c'}, {'abstract': 'A humorous image, made to look like it came from an episode of “The Simpsons,” overstates the predictive power of that satirical Fox cartoon series.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/doh-eastwoods-convention-speech-spawns-fake-simpsons-meme/', 'snippet': 'A humorous image, made to look like it came from an episode of “The Simpsons,” overstates the predictive power of that satirical Fox cartoon series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the words of that great animated philosopher Homer J. Simpson: “When are people going to learn? Democracy doesn’t work.” Sometimes the same can be said for social media.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'D’Oh! Eastwood’s Convention Speech Spawns Fake ‘Simpsons’ Meme', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Social Media: ‘The Simpsons’ Didn’t Do It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eastwood, Clint', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Simpsons (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T15:34:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f275b3df-892b-5e24-b473-a0b7f462866d', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f275b3df-892b-5e24-b473-a0b7f462866d'}, {'abstract': 'Worthwhile Canadian comparison.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/health-systems-and-health-costs/', 'snippet': 'Worthwhile Canadian comparison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Related to today’s column: Suppose that you were really, really concerned about the long-run federal budget, and understood correctly that rising health care costs are the biggest source of rising spending. What you might do in that case is look around the world to see what kinds of health care system appear to be best at containing costs. And you wouldn’t have to look far, because there’s a pretty dramatic contrast just north of the border:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Systems and Health Costs', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T15:54:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99ccc5e9-91aa-5ee3-85ee-77e82a979cc9', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99ccc5e9-91aa-5ee3-85ee-77e82a979cc9'}, {'abstract': 'Adrian Beltre hits for power and average, but the way he plays third base makes him one of the most underappreciated performers in baseball.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/sports/baseball/rangers-adrian-beltre-plays-third-base-like-no-one-else.html', 'snippet': 'Adrian Beltre hits for power and average, but the way he plays third base makes him one of the most underappreciated performers in baseball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARLINGTON, Tex. — The offense is obvious,