sclose the details of the operation; his identity; and any perceived political motives behind its publication.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Navy Seals Embark on a Hellish Literary Adventure', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fictional SEAL Team On a Hellish Adventure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Navy Seals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T16:53:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14c1053e-d9c9-5e53-865e-49b29376c7a5', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14c1053e-d9c9-5e53-865e-49b29376c7a5'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney had announced earlier that he will tour the bayou region south of New Orleans today. President Obama will travel there on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/obama-to-visit-gulf-coast-on-monday/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney had announced earlier that he will tour the bayou region south of New Orleans today. President Obama will travel there on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:22 p.m. | Updated  LAKELAND, Fla. — The two contenders for the White House announced Friday morning that they would both visit the Gulf Coast to tour the damage from Hurricane Isaac and meet with officials about the recovery efforts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama to Visit Gulf Coast on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf Coast (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T16:54:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear, Jeremy W. Peters and Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cce147c-c70d-594d-8275-21265656a7f8', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cce147c-c70d-594d-8275-21265656a7f8'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Lighty, one of the most powerful managers in hip-hop, helped knock down the wall that separated that culture from the mainstream.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/arts/music/chris-lighty-hip-hop-manager-changed-music.html', 'snippet': 'Chris Lighty, one of the most powerful managers in hip-hop, helped knock down the wall that separated that culture from the mainstream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When LL Cool J filmed his 1997 commercial for the Gap, it was a milestone: never before had a rapper been called on to endorse as mainstream an apparel company. The commercial was minimal and cool: LL Cool J, rapping a cappella in front of a white background, quick camera cuts matching the speed of his verse.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/arts/LIGHTY-jp/LIGHTY-jp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/arts/LIGHTY-jp/LIGHTY-jp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1509, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/arts/LIGHTY-jp/LIGHTY-jp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/01/arts/LIGHTY-jp/LIGHTY-jp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/arts/LIGHTY-jp/LIGHTY-jp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'He Took Hip-Hop From Gritty to Global', 'kicker': 'An Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'He Took Hip-Hop From Gritty To Global', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lighty, Chris', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T16:55:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename'