e': 'Author of Account of Bin Laden Raid May Face Legal Action', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bissonnette, Matt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Owen, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Navy Seals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T17:15:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Bumiller and Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bumiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28abd0a2-7b22-53d9-bdd6-aa591d8c3233', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28abd0a2-7b22-53d9-bdd6-aa591d8c3233'}, {'abstract': 'Environmental groups are pressing New York to conduct a study of the health effects of hydraulic fracturing before the state makes its final determination on whether to allow the drilling process.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/state-considering-studying-health-impacts-of-fracking/', 'snippet': 'Environmental groups are pressing New York to conduct a study of the health effects of hydraulic fracturing before the state makes its final determination on whether to allow the drilling process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late in its review process, New York state regulators are now considering an examination of the potential public health effects of hydraulic fracturing as part of its review of the controversial natural gas drilling process.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State Considering Studying Health Impacts of Fracking', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Department of Environmental Conservation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T17:15:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fd5d90f-5204-55ad-87c0-c45227c0b13f', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fd5d90f-5204-55ad-87c0-c45227c0b13f'}, {'abstract': 'At this spot, where cuisines collide, you can start with the pho before pivoting to a po’boy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/travel/restaurant-report-minh-hoa-restaurant-cajun-seafood-in-wichita.html', 'snippet': 'At this spot, where cuisines collide, you can start with the pho before pivoting to a po’boy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Along a dark stretch of western Wichita, past vacant buildings and dollar and liquor stores, is a restaurant that appears so foreboding that one might never think to enter.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02BITES/02BITES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02BITES/02BITES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1125, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02BITES/02BITES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/travel/02BITES/02BITES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Report: Minh Hoa Restaurant & Cajun Seafood in Wichita', 'kicker': 'Bites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wichita: Minh Hoa Restaurant & Cajun Seafood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wichita (Kan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T17:15:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cheryl Lu-Lien Tan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cheryl', 'middlename': 'Lu-lien', 'lastname': 'Tan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b970079a-69f2-576d-92c9-7772879cd58b', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b970079a-69f2-576d-92c9-7772879cd58b'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to recent articles in the Travel section.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/travel/letters-to-the-editor.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to recent articles in the Travel section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: Regarding “Can Travel Make the Child?” (Aug. 12): Families participating in service-abroad programs should be cautious of one of travel’s worst crimes: academic tourism. Sure, it’s tempting to expose your (upper-middle class) children to the “exotic,” but can such short programs with such hefty price tags adequately address a country’s pressing social issues? As a former participant on similar programs, I suspect not. Equipped with a tour guide and camera, travelers become poverty tourists, observing locals through an invisible but palpable barrier. Families who take such brief glimpses at “the other” are at risk of undermining these cultures or even perpetuating stereotypes against them, while giving themselves an ego or a college-application boost. JOSHUA PETIMAR Staten Island', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Editor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Letters: Volunteer Programs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T17:16:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff4bb4b7-27c3-5731-957d-b5d9611b74b8', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff4bb4b7-27c3-5731-957d-b5d9611b74b8'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Christopher Buckley talks about Christopher Hitchens’s “Mortality”; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; Barry Gewen discusses George Orwell’s diaries; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2012/08/31/books/review/31books_pod.html', 'snippet': 'This week, Christopher Buckley talks about Christopher Hitchens’s “Mortality”; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; Barry Gewen discusses George Orwell’s diaries; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'lea