2)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paralympic Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawking, Stephen W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pistorius, Oscar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC Sports Network', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Times of London', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T17:25:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua George', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'George', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d074c98f-f82d-560a-8f74-2870d5e0fe67', 'word_count': 1029, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d074c98f-f82d-560a-8f74-2870d5e0fe67'}, {'abstract': 'Delaware has undergone the same political realignments as larger states in the Northeast.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/delaware-a-small-example-of-a-larger-trend/', 'snippet': 'Delaware has undergone the same political realignments as larger states in the Northeast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We continue our Presidential Geography series, a one-by-one examination of the peculiarities that drive the politics in all 50 states and the District of Columbia. Here, a look at Delaware, the First State. FiveThirtyEight spoke with Dr. Joseph A. Pika, a professor in the Department of Political Science and International Relations at the University of Delaware.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Delaware: A Small Example of a Larger Trend', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T17:25:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micah Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0839c78e-8f6e-5d95-a36d-f8f4abb8a0b9', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0839c78e-8f6e-5d95-a36d-f8f4abb8a0b9'}, {'abstract': 'Even the most passionate boating enthusiast looks for ways to cut expenses, which is hard to do while burning 100 gallons of fuel an hour.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/your-money/how-to-keep-yachting-expenses-manageable-wealth-matters.html', 'snippet': 'Even the most passionate boating enthusiast looks for ways to cut expenses, which is hard to do while burning 100 gallons of fuel an hour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I HAVE spent many Labor Day weekends in Edgartown, Mass., on Martha’s Vineyard, and one of my favorite activities is looking at the yachts bobbing in the harbor while eating a lobster roll. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/your-money/01wealth/01wealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/01/your-money/01wealth/01wealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/your-money/01wealth/01wealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/your-money/01wealth/01wealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumb