ight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Cunningham | In Season', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T17:33:49+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'Joanna Nikas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nikas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/33961c5c-3059-5f28-a6ab-b745d7c8ffe0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/33961c5c-3059-5f28-a6ab-b745d7c8ffe0'}, {'abstract': 'At the Venice Film Festival, Michael Cimino discusses his painful history with “Heaven’s Gate.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/venice-film-festival-michael-cimino-revisits-heavens-gate/', 'snippet': 'At the Venice Film Festival, Michael Cimino discusses his painful history with “Heaven’s Gate.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'VENICE — Most box office flops rarely even attain the status of film-history footnote. But “Heaven’s Gate,” the 1980 epic by Michael Cimino, became a legend. Its notoriously troubled production and disastrous premiere turned it into a punch line, a cautionary tale, a symbol of all that was wrong with the Hollywood system and its excesses. In the popular telling at least, this sprawling western, which recounts the violent conflict between wealthy cattle barons and poor European settlers in 1890s Wyoming, is the film that derailed the career of its ambitious young director (who had won an Oscar for “The Deer Hunter”) and sank its studio, United Artists.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venice Film Festival: Michael Cimino Revisits ‘Heaven’s Gate’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 