land declared at the beginning of her 1984 memoir “D.V.” She meant nothing of the sort, as Christopher Lehmann-Haupt noted in his review in The Times, calling the book a “deceptively frothy meringue of a monologue.” Vreeland was an unconventional editor and an unconventional mother (though something of a traditional mate), and her slant on life was from an angle informed by beauty. She had, quite simply, an amazing eye. This was a very specialized story she was bound to tell. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vintage Fashion', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vreeland, Diana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IFC Center (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Versailles (France)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T17:51:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d4532f4-61f4-5671-9cd8-ac813537299b', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d4532f4-61f4-5671-9cd8-ac813537299b'}, {'abstract': 'Barclays moved to restore its reputation by overhauling its culture. We explained the trouble with closed-end mutual funds that invest in start-ups and provided analysis of a deal that helped one of the nation’s bigger regional banks catch up in capital. A look back on our reporting of last week’s highs and lows in finance.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/week-in-review-tracking-the-deal-makers-outside-of-tampa/', 'snippet': 'Barclays moved to restore its reputation by overhauling its culture. We explained the trouble with closed-end mutual funds that invest in start-ups and provided analysis of a deal that helped one of the nation’s bigger regional banks catch up in c...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Barclays is moving to restore its reputation by overhauling its culture. We explained the trouble with closed-end mutual funds that invest in start-ups and provided analysis of a deal that helped one of the nation’s bigger regional banks catch up in capital.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week in Review: Tracking Deal Makers Outside of Tampa', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T18:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Owles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Owles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c8346f6-a8cf-5e97-b5fe-55b00514265a', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c8346f6-a8cf-5e97-b5fe-55b00514265a'}, {'abstract': 'Talking about sex is a national pastime here in France. But when it comes down to actual carnal mechanics, the French can seem clueless.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/lumire-sex-and-savoir-faire/', 'snippet': 'Talking about sex is a national pastime here in France. But when it comes down to actual carnal mechanics, the French can seem clueless.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Summer this year came with special radio programs about a subject the French take very seriously: sex. On Saturday nights, Europe 1 focused on desire. In “Chaude Est la Nuit” (“Hot Is the Night”), famous actors with voices of velour read erotic literary texts about female pleasure. RTL, a competitor, took a more clinical approach. In a daily two-hour series throughout July, sexologists, psychiatrists and gynecologists explored such subjects as “the trouble with the erection,” “sex for seniors” and “perversions.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lumière | Sex and Savoir-Faire', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T18:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Sciolino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sciolino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1f5404a-a1a1-55cb-8dc4-d3ded03360cf', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1f5404a-a1a1-55cb-8dc4-d3ded03360cf'}, {'abstract': 'A paper by a Columbia economics professor says that to foster growth now, the Fed must promise to tolerate higher inflation later.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/a-critique-of-fed-policy/', 'snippet': 'A paper by a Columbia economics professor says that to foster growth now, the Fed must promise to tolerate higher inflation later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JACKSON HOLE, Wyo. — Many economists regard asset purchases as the most powerful tool the Federal Reserve could use to stimulate the economy. But Michael Woodford, an economics professor at Columbia University, argued Friday that a second option would actually be much more effective – both because it would have significant economic benefits, and because the benefits of asset purchases are significantly overstated.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Critique of Fed Policy', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T18:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d88ffb78-466c-5e37-9931-4d88cf2ec75d', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d88ffb78-466c-5e37-9931-4d88cf2ec75d'}, {'abstract': 'The decorated former Formula One driver will appear at the collector car and motorsports festival with Ferraris, Maseratis, Porsches and other cars he campaigned over his career.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/stirling-moss-reuniting-with-precious-metal-at-lime-rock/', 'snippet': 'The decorated former Formula One driver will appear at the collector car and motorsports festival with Ferraris, Maseratis, Porsches and other cars he campaigned over his career.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:03 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stirling Moss, Reuniting With Precious Metal at Lime Rock', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'