through.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/grilling-low-and-slow/', 'snippet': 'The indirect grilling technique is excellent for any large hunk of food that needs a long time to cook through.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s column and video are about indirect grilling. I grilled a marinated pork loin, but the technique is excellent for any large hunk of food that needs a long time to cook through. Indirect grilling is all about low and slow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grilling Low and Slow', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grilling (Cooking)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T20:20:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9cf3604-d3a7-5713-9640-05bec44279b8', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9cf3604-d3a7-5713-9640-05bec44279b8'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Duncan, an urban adventure guide who has run tours of New York’s sewers and train tunnels, has a new project.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/underground-tour-guide-pops-up-in-las-vegas/', 'snippet': 'Steve Duncan, an urban adventure guide who has run tours of New York’s sewers and train tunnels, has a new project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the urban adventure guides whose tours of New York’s sewers and train tunnels were featured in a Times article last year has popped up in Sin City. Steve Duncan’s new project is called “Undercity: Las Vegas.” The tunnels he finds there are nowhere near as cool and crumbly and aromatic as the ones beneath New York, but who doesn’t love a sewer? Mr. Duncan spoke to The Huffington Post about his explorations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Underground Tour Guide Pops Up in Las Vegas', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Steve', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T20:21:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d4125d7-3c26-53b1-850e-d13018375503', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d4125d7-3c26-53b1-850e-d13018375503'}, {'abstract': 'The Detroit-based automakers once created vehicles specifically for Canada, and usually built in Canada, based on models sold in United States. Once common on Canadian roads, such cars have become largely forgotten historical footnotes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/automobiles/collectibles/canadian-cousins-with-fleur-de-lis-and-mixed-genes.html', 'snippet': 'The Detroit-based automakers once created vehicles specifically for Canada, and usually built in Canada, based on models sold in United States. Once common on Canadian roads, such cars have become largely forgotten historical footnotes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA ', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/automobiles/02CANA2/02CANA2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/02/automobiles/02CANA2/02CANA2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'r