urselves, our movements and our views.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/one-womans-data-trail-diary/', 'snippet': 'It is impossible to live in urban, wired America without leaving everywhere clues about ourselves, our movements and our views.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As part of The Agenda, The Times’s look at major issues facing the next administration, we have been examining the trade-offs, more than a decade after the Sept. 11 attacks, between security and privacy and civil liberties. Some readers have written in about the electronic data trail that all of us leave as we go about our lives, using the Internet and carrying smartphones.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Woman’s Data Trail Diary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T21:16:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1b903d9-2cf7-58db-a0c5-c1661b397ddd', 'word_count': 955, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1b903d9-2cf7-58db-a0c5-c1661b397ddd'}, {'abstract': 'Cablevision workers in Brooklyn voted this year to unionize, and now they have released a video.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/a-union-spirited-labor-day-rap/', 'snippet': 'Cablevision workers in Brooklyn voted this year to unionize, and now they have released a video.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just in time for Labor Day, the Cablevision workers in Brooklyn who voted this year to unionize have released a rap video chronicling their struggle. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Union-Spirited Labor Day Rap', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cablevision Systems Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T21:18:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/379653fd-5f6c-5556-a6f2-d2623feb8ef3', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/379653fd-5f6c-5556-a6f2-d2623feb8ef3'}, {'abstract': 'In August 2010, as my husband and I approached our 50th birthdays, we were suddenly forced to move into my parents’ home in Michigan with our three teenage children and dog.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/fashion/the-waltons-meets-modern-family.html', 'snippet': 'In August 2010, as my husband and I approached our 50th birthdays, we were suddenly forced to move into my parents’ home in Michigan with our three teenage children and dog.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I AM now a statistic. Earlier this summer, the United States Census Bureau reported that the number of adult children living in their parents’ households had increased by 1.2 million between 2007 and 2010. Shared households accounted for 18.7 percent of all American households in 2010, up from 17 percent in 2007. Most of those children were between age 25 and 34, but I had suddenly joined their ranks at a considerably older age.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0,