 Confederate flag emblem from its roof.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/the-general-lee-of-the-dukes-of-hazzard-will-not-change-its-stripes-or-stars/', 'snippet': 'Contradicting reports that circulated this week, Warner Brothers said it had issued no directive to producers of licensed merchandise stipulating that the emblematic Dodge Charger must shed the Confederate flag emblem from its roof.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Contradicting rumors that circulated through fan forums, film Web sites and other corners of the Internet this week, the orange, incredibly air-worthy 1969 Dodge Charger from “The Dukes of Hazzard” television series, known as the General Lee, is not expected to lose the Confederate flag from its roof.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The General Lee of ‘The Dukes of Hazzard’ Will Keep Flying Its Flag', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Ben', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tomy Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T21:40:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Pearley Huffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Pearley', 'lastname': 'Huffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a12dc52-3597-5fd1-8678-2013e54fe61e', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a12dc52-3597-5fd1-8678-2013e54fe61e'}, {'abstract': 'Firestone plans to begin running a campaign on Sunday that urges car owners to “Drive a Firestone.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/firestone-shows-drive-in-new-ad-campaign/', 'snippet': 'Firestone plans to begin running a campaign on Sunday that urges car owners to “Drive a Firestone.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Decades ago, cars made by De Soto with model names like Fireflite, Firedome and Firesweep roamed American highways. That may have been as close as anyone could have come to driving a Firestone – until now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Firestone Shows ‘Drive’ in New Ad Campaign', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tires', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Burnett, Leo, Worldwide', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T21:41:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a29bb0b-75fe-5980-bfc8-92f8bd591b8d', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a29bb0b-75fe-5980-bfc8-92f8bd591b8d'}, {'abstract': 'In three days, six new cases were reported in city residents, bringing the number this year to 14, health officials report.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/city-has-sudden-jump-in-west-nile-cases/', 'snippet': 'In three days, six new cases were reported in city residents, bringing the number this year to 14, health officials report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Six new cases of West Nile virus were reported in city residents in the last three days, almost as many as in the whole rest of the summer so far, according to the city health department’s Web site. There has been one death, a man in his 80s who had recently traveled outside the city, the department said. The new cases bring the total to 14, three more cases than there were last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Has Sudden Jump in West Nile Cases', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'West Nile Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T21:42:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d29caa3-17c7-5515-a354-b6628859cdaa', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d29caa3-17c7-5515-a354-b6628859cdaa'}, {'abstract': 'For school reading purposes, do books listened to, as audio books, count as books read?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/does-reading-an-audio-book-count/', 'snippet': 'For school reading purposes, do books listened to, as audio books, count as books read?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Filling out the lists of “summer reading” their teachers required as the school year began, my children and I ran across a quandary of our own. For school reading purposes, do books listened to, as audio books, count as books read?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Does ‘Reading’ an Audio Book Count?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline':