ts the melding of two corporate cultures — one a staid but successful Japanese behemoth, the other, Tesla, a disruptive California start-up — into a single machine.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/reviewing-the-toyota-rav4-ev/', 'snippet': 'The story of the 2012 Toyota RAV4 EV represents the melding of two corporate cultures — one a staid but successful Japanese behemoth, the other, Tesla, a disruptive California start-up — into a single machine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Sunday’s Automobiles section, Bradley Berman reviews the 2012 Toyota RAV4 EV, a purely electric version of the compact crossover with a drivetrain sourced from Tesla Motors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing the Toyota RAV4 EV', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T22:03:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04bd71b0-ae1c-5c56-9974-b880b97b71ae', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04bd71b0-ae1c-5c56-9974-b880b97b71ae'}, {'abstract': 'London 2012, the countrywide cultural jamboree for Britain’s Olympic summer, has been a showcase for the country’s artistic talent and its eccentricity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/arts/london-2012-festival-shows-british-talent-and-eccentricity.html', 'snippet': 'London 2012, the countrywide cultural jamboree for Britain’s Olympic summer, has been a showcase for the country’s artistic talent and its eccentricity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The school holidays are in their final throes here, and this week the Natural History Museum was, as the British like to say, heaving. (Translation: a tightly packed situation in which elbows might be useful.) In the midst of the throng, a woman approached two children in the cavernous ground floor space. “I’m going to give you something,” she said. They looked mildly alarmed. Then she added, “Some Shakespeare.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/arts/01FESTIVAL/01FESTIVAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 276, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/01/arts/01FESTIVAL/01FESTIVAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 276}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/arts/01FESTIVAL/01FESTIVAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 471, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/arts/01FESTIVAL/01FESTIVAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 942, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/arts/01FESTIVAL/01FESTIVAL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/01/arts/01FESTIVAL/01FESTIVAL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/arts/01FESTIVAL/01FESTIVAL-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain’s Arts-Mad Summer, on an Olympic Scale', 'k