arge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Zynga’s Gambling Expert, and Workday’s I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T23:39:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d2cf66f-bccd-50ab-a19d-d74845406168', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d2cf66f-bccd-50ab-a19d-d74845406168'}, {'abstract': 'In keeping with the tradition of surprise screenings at the Telluride Film Festival, Ben Affleck brought his new film, “Argo,” to town unannounced.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/telluride-film-festival-a-sneak-peek-at-argo/', 'snippet': 'In keeping with the tradition of surprise screenings at the Telluride Film Festival, Ben Affleck brought his new film, “Argo,” to town unannounced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TELLURIDE, Colo. — Telluride is not exactly a secret film festival— there are enough journalists and publicists here in the San Juan Mountains to get the word out to the masses below — but discretion is among the local traditions. According to custom, the lineup for the 39th edition of the festival was announced only Thursday, 24 hours before the first screenings, and as usual a number of spaces on the schedule were left mysterious, marked TBA. Some of those slots are reserved for “sneaks”—movies that pop into town like sudden thunderstorms — and rumors immediately began to fly about what special extras might be in store this year. Would Clint Eastwood (or at least his new movie, “Trouble With the Curve”) stop by on his way home from Tampa? Would we get a peek at “Cloud Atlas” or “The Master”?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Telluride Film Festival: A Sneak Peek at ‘Argo’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telluride Film Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AFFLECK, BEN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T23:42:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23fb09d9-c8ae-577e-a44b-bed14934af53', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23fb09d9-c8ae-577e-a44b-bed14934af53'}, {'abstract': 'The Staten Island district attorney, Daniel M. Donovan Jr., was appointed on Friday to look into allegations of sexual harassment against Assemblyman Vito J. Lopez of Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/nyregion/special-prosecutor-to-investigate-vito-lopez-in-sexual-harassment-case.html', 'snippet': 'The Staten Island district attorney, Daniel M. Donovan Jr., was appointed on Friday to look into allegations of sexual harassment against Assemblyman Vito J. Lopez of Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — The Staten Island district attorney, Daniel M. Donovan Jr., was named on Friday as a special prosecutor to investigate Assemblyman Vito J. Lopez of Brooklyn in the wake of a sexual harassment scandal. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Special Prosecutor to Investigate Lawmaker in Harassment Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Special Prosecutor to Investigate Lawmaker in Harassment Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Prosecutors (Independent Counsel)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Vito J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donovan, Daniel M Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T23:51:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danny Hakim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hakim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7738e402-59ef-5513-bedb-b4a4fa46bf44', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7738e402-59ef-5513-bedb-b4a4fa46bf44'}, {'abstract': 'The state attorney general’s office declined to charge Sheriff Paul Babeu of Pinal County over accusations that he misused his authority to harass and intimidate an ex-boyfriend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/us/arizona-sheriff-will-not-face-criminal-charges.html', 'snippet': 'The state attorney general’s office declined to charge Sheriff Paul Babeu of Pinal County over accusations that he misused his authority to harass and intimidate an ex-boyfriend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The state attorney general’s office declined on Friday to charge Sheriff Paul Babeu of Pinal County, a former co-chairman of Mitt Romney’s presidential campaign in Arizona, over accusations that he misused his authority to harass and intimidate an ex-boyfriend, whom Sheriff Babeu later accused of stealing his online identity. The ex-boyfriend, Jose Orozco, a Mexican immigrant hired by Sheriff Babeu to run the Twitter account and the Web site for his Congressional campaign, also will not face charges over accusations that he improperly manipulated them. Mr. Orozco had accused Sheriff Babeu of threatening to deport him if he made their relationship public, but the authorities said the allegations could not be proved. Mr. Babeu dropped his bid for Congress and is running for re-election instead. He won the primary on Tuesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arizona: Sheriff Will Not Face Criminal Charges ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arizona: Sheriff Will Not Face Criminal Charges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Babeu, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T23:52:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a252043f-f7f7-5ba6-8066-278d91333477', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a252043f-f7f7-5ba6-8066-278d91333477'}, {'abstract': 'Every time you close your eyes.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/friday-night-music-lies-lies/', 'snippet': 'Every time you close your eyes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Ryan left me no choice:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: Lies! Lies!', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-08-31T23:52:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_